window.REPORT = {"updated":"2026-11-19","version":"0.1 — first assembly, research still landing","sections":[{"id":"good-definition","tab":"good","order":5,"kicker":"What this tab is for","kicker_zh":"這一頁是做什麼的","title":"Science for Good is a programme, not a judging category","title_zh":"Science for Good 是一個長期計畫，不是一個評審項目","lede":"At GEMS, Science for Good means a club-form programme with no competition deadline: a few well-chosen problems, worked continuously and from several directions, for as long as they take. iGEM's Human Practices criteria are evidence we can learn from. They are not the definition.","lede_zh":"在 GEMS，Science for Good 指的是一個沒有比賽截止日的社團式長期計畫：挑幾個夠好的題目，從多個方向持續投入，需要多久就做多久。iGEM 的人類實踐評審標準是我們可以學習的材料，但不是它的定義。","body":"A competition season is nine months long and ends in a rubric. That shape is useful — it forces a team to finish something — but it decides a great deal that nobody intended. It decides that a problem is worth working on if it can be closed by October. It decides that the output is a wiki. And it decides who you talk to, because a judge recognises a professor's authority faster than a farmer's.\n\n**The evidence on this page is the cost of that shape.** Of 21 award-winning software tools from 2026, 8 are still usable today, and across every repository checked there are zero stars and zero forks — nobody came. Not one team in the 106 ran an inter-lab measurement ring, the one form of collaboration that would have produced a number other people could reuse. Of 106 decorated teams, 71 closed a stakeholder-to-design loop, but only nine or ten closed it with someone who was not a credentialled expert. None of this is because the teams were careless. It is because the deadline rewards an artefact and a defensible story, and all three of those things take longer than a season.\n\n**And the clearest measurement of that shape is how rarely anyone carries anything forward.** Taken across iGEM's full accepted rosters rather than the winners — 423 teams in 2026, 413 in 2025, 391 in 2024 — **284 of the 423 had competed before**, and returning tracks with results: Gold at 59% against 42%, Top 10 twenty-four against six. But returning is not continuing. Of the 81 decorated 2026 teams that had entered before, **5 carried a project line forward**, and **none of the six returning Grand Prize teams did**. Only **3 of 106** credit their own predecessor with anything at all. The institution comes back every year; the problem almost never does. That is not a failure of effort — it is what a season-shaped container does to a problem, and it is the single strongest argument for keeping one outside it.\n\n**So Science for Good at GEMS is the container for the work the competition cannot hold.** It is open membership rather than a selected team, it carries problems across years rather than seasons, and it is allowed to arrive somewhere with no method in hand. The first visit is listening. The solution does not have to be a construct — it can be an instrument, a dataset, a protocol, a piece of software, or a way of organising something that already exists. Sometimes the honest finding is that synthetic biology is the wrong tool, and a programme that cannot reach that conclusion is not doing research.\n\niGEM still matters, but the direction of supply reverses. *The programme feeds the competition, not the other way round.* A problem that has been lived with for two years makes a far better nine-month project than a problem invented in January to fit a village.","body_zh":"一個比賽季是九個月，終點是一張評分表。這個形狀有它的用處——它逼團隊把東西做完——但它也替我們決定了很多沒有人打算決定的事。它決定了一個題目值不值得做，取決於能不能在十月前收掉。它決定了產出是一個 wiki。它也決定了你去跟誰談，因為評審認得出教授的權威，比認得出農民的快得多。\n\n**這一頁上的證據，就是這個形狀的代價。** 2026 年得獎的 21 個軟體工具裡，今天還能用的有 8 個；而所有檢查過的程式庫，星數與分支數全部是零——沒有人來。106 支隊伍中沒有任何一支做過跨實驗室量測環，那正是唯一一種能產出別人可以再利用的數字的合作形式。106 支得獎隊伍中有 71 支閉合了「利害關係人到設計」的迴路，但其中只有九到十支，是和沒有專業資格的人閉合的。這些都不是因為隊伍不用心，而是因為截止日獎勵的是一件作品和一套站得住腳的敘事，而上面這三件事，全都需要比一季更久。\n\n**而這個形狀最清楚的量測，就是幾乎沒有人把任何東西帶到下一年。** 把範圍拉到 iGEM 完整的正式參賽名單、而不只是得獎者——2026 年 423 支、2025 年 413 支、2024 年 391 支——**423 支之中有 284 支先前就參賽過**，而回鍋確實與成績相關：金牌率 59% 對 42%，Top 10 二十四比六。但「回來」不等於「延續」。在 81 支先前參賽過的2026 年得獎隊伍裡，**只有 5 支把一條題目線帶到今年**，而**六支回鍋的總冠軍級隊伍一支也沒有**。106 支之中只有 **3 支**對自己的前一屆表示過任何感謝。機構每年都回來，題目幾乎從不回來。這不是努力不足——這是一個以賽季為形狀的容器對題目做的事，也是把另一個容器留在它之外最強的理由。\n\n**所以 GEMS 的 Science for Good，是用來裝比賽裝不下的那些工作的容器。** 它是開放參與而不是遴選出來的隊伍，它讓題目跨年而不是跨季，而且它允許你到了現場手上還沒有方法。第一次去就是去聽。解方不一定要是一個基因構築——可以是一台儀器、一組資料、一份流程、一個軟體，或是把既有的東西重新組織起來的方式。有時候誠實的結論是：合成生物學是錯的工具；一個無法得出這個結論的計畫，就不算在做研究。\n\niGEM 仍然重要，但供應的方向要反過來。*是長期計畫餵養比賽，不是反過來。* 一個已經相處了兩年的題目，會比一月才為了塞進某個 village 而想出來的題目，成為好得多的九個月專案。","cards":[{"kicker":"Criterion 1","kicker_zh":"條件一","title":"It matters to someone who is not us","title_zh":"它對我們以外的人有意義","body":"A problem someone outside GEMS already has, and would still have if we never showed up. The test is whether a specific person can describe it to you in their own words, unprompted, before you offer anything.","body_zh":"一個 GEMS 以外的人已經有的問題——就算我們從未出現，它還是在那裡。檢驗方式是：在你提出任何東西之前，有沒有一個具體的人能用自己的話、不經提示地把它描述給你聽。","chips":["social meaning"],"chips_zh":["有社會意義"]},{"kicker":"Criterion 2","kicker_zh":"條件二","title":"It can actually be put somewhere","title_zh":"它真的放得進某個地方","body":"There is a real site, a real operator and a real route to getting it there. The analysis on this page found the loops that closed were closed where a non-specialist physically operates the thing — a stall, a hive, a field. Deployability is not a later phase; it selects the problem.","body_zh":"有真實的場域、真實的操作者，以及真實的送達路徑。本頁的分析發現，真正閉合的迴路，都發生在由非專業人士實際操作那個東西的地方——一個攤位、一個蜂箱、一塊田。可佈署性不是後面的階段，它是挑題目的條件。","chips":["deployable"],"chips_zh":["放得進現場"]},{"kicker":"Criterion 3","kicker_zh":"條件三","title":"The effect can be counted","title_zh":"效果數得出來","body":"Before starting, you can name the number that would move and say how you would measure it. If the only available outcome is that people felt positive about science, it belongs in education, which is good work but a different programme.","body_zh":"在開始之前，你就能說出哪一個數字會變，以及你要怎麼量它。如果唯一拿得出來的成果是「大家對科學感覺很好」，那它屬於教育——那是好事，但是另一個計畫。","chips":["quantifiable"],"chips_zh":["數得出來"]},{"kicker":"Criterion 4","kicker_zh":"條件四","title":"The second one is cheaper than the first","title_zh":"第二次要比第一次便宜","body":"Scaling is a property of the design, not an ambition stated at the end. If helping the tenth farm costs what the first one cost, it is a service, not a solution — and the programme should know which it is building.","body_zh":"可規模化是設計的性質，不是結尾處宣示的志向。如果幫第十個農場的成本和第一個一樣，那它是一項服務，不是一個解方——而計畫本身應該清楚自己在做哪一種。","chips":["scalable"],"chips_zh":["做得大"]},{"kicker":"What it is not","kicker_zh":"它不是什麼","title":"Not an iGEM incubator, and not outreach","title_zh":"不是 iGEM 孵化器，也不是科普推廣","body":"A problem does not enter because it would make a good project, and it does not stay because it photographs well. Outreach and education are separate, valuable, and measured differently. Confusing the two is how a programme ends up with a lot of activity and no result.","body_zh":"一個題目不會因為「可以做成不錯的專案」而進來，也不會因為「拍起來好看」而留下。科普與教育是另一回事，有其價值，衡量方式也不同。把兩者混在一起，就是一個計畫最後活動很多、卻沒有成果的原因。","chips":["not outreach"],"chips_zh":["不是科普推廣"]}],"checklist":["Write the four criteria down and score every candidate problem against them in public, inside the programme.","Give each live problem one owner and a dated file that anyone in GEMS can read.","Make the first visit to any new partner a listening visit with no method proposed.","Require a named number before work starts: what would move, and how it gets measured.","Review the pipeline twice a year and close problems deliberately, with a written reason.","Let iGEM teams draw from the pipeline; do not let the iGEM calendar decide what enters it."],"checklist_zh":["把四個條件寫下來，並在計畫內部公開地用它們替每一個候選題目評分。","每一個進行中的題目都要有一位負責人，和一份 GEMS 任何人都能讀的、標了日期的檔案。","任何新夥伴的第一次拜訪都是去聽的，不提出方法。","動工之前必須先講明一個數字：哪一項會變，以及要怎麼量。","每年檢視兩次題目清單，並且要有意識地結案，附上書面理由。","讓 iGEM 團隊從這個清單裡取題；但不要讓 iGEM 的行事曆決定什麼可以進來。"],"method":"This section states GEMS Research's own definition of its Science for Good programme; it is not a finding about iGEM. The figures quoted in support — 8 of 21 software tools still usable, zero stars or forks, no inter-lab measurement ring in 106 teams, 71 of 106 loops closed with nine or ten closed by non-experts — come from the analyses further down this page and on the dry-lab tab, each of which states its own method and limits. They are offered as evidence that a nine-month container has predictable costs, not as proof that a club-form programme avoids them. That part is untested, and GEMS is the test.","method_zh":"這一節陳述的是 GEMS Research 自己對 Science for Good 計畫的定義，不是關於 iGEM 的研究發現。用來佐證的數字——21 個軟體工具中 8 個仍可使用、星數與分支數為零、106 支隊伍中沒有跨實驗室量測環、106 支中 71 支閉合迴路而其中只有九到十支由非專業人士閉合——都來自本頁下方與乾實驗室頁的分析，各自都載明了方法與限制。它們是用來說明「九個月的容器有可預期的代價」，不是用來證明社團式的長期計畫就能避開這些代價。那一點還沒有被驗證過，而 GEMS 自己就是那個驗證。"},{"id":"judging-criteria","tab":"judging","order":5,"kicker":"The rubric","kicker_zh":"評分標準","title":"Special awards do not buy a podium — the finalist questions do","title_zh":"特別獎買不到頒獎臺，決賽那幾道問題才能","lede":"iGEM's own results data records a designation most reports never mention: **Finalist**. In the 2026 High School section, 147 teams entered, 10 reached the Top 10, and **exactly 2 were named Finalists** — Lambert-GA and HongKong-JSS. GEMS-Taiwan was one of the eight that were not, despite winning three section special awards, the same number of special wins as the Grand Prize winner, while HongKong-JSS won none. The eight questions below are the ones that make that cut. One qualification, because it changes what the word means: in all three seasons on record — 2024, 2025 and 2026 — the Finalist set and the podium are **identical**, seven teams a year, the Grand Prize winners and the runners-up. The designation names the podium, not a wider round in front of it. One fact belongs at the top rather than in a later section, because it changes the question: **GEMS-Taiwan won the 2024 High School Grand Prize** and was a Finalist that year, so what follows is not an account of a bar this team has never reached.","lede_zh":"iGEM 官方結果資料裡記著一個幾乎沒有報告提過的身分：**Finalist（決賽入選）**。2026 年高中組有 147 支隊伍參賽、10 支進入 Top 10，而**只有 2 支被列為 Finalist**——Lambert-GA 和 HongKong-JSS。GEMS-Taiwan 是沒進去的那八支之一，儘管它拿下三個組別特別獎，特別獎得獎數與總冠軍相同，而 HongKong-JSS 一個都沒有。下面那八道問題，就是做出這道切分的問題。有一點必須先說清楚，因為它會改變這個詞的意思：在有紀錄的三個賽季——2024、2025、2026——Finalist 集合與頒獎臺**完全相同**，每年七支，就是總冠軍與各名次的亞、季軍。這個身分命名的是頒獎臺，而不是它前面更大的一輪名單。有一件事應該放在最前面，而不是放在後面的小節裡，因為它改變了問題：**GEMS-Taiwan 贏過 2024 年高中組總冠軍**，那一年它也是 Finalist；所以接下來要誫的，並不是一道這支隊伍從未跨過的門檻。","body":"There are three separate decisions in an iGEM season and they are easy to collapse into one. A **medal** is a checklist: you meet the deliverables and you get it, which is why 135 of the 147 High School teams have one and 63 of them are Gold. A **special award** is scored by judges who look at a single dimension and ask who did it best. The **Top 10** and the **Finalist** slate are decided by judges looking at the whole project and asking nine questions, of which eight leave a public record. One thing that sentence should not be allowed to imply: the Finalist designation is **not** a wider round that the podium was then chosen from. In 2024, 2025 and 2026 alike it lands on exactly the seven podium teams, so reaching it and reaching the podium are the same event. That makes the gap this tab examines a podium gap, described in iGEM's own vocabulary.\n\nAnd the detail belongs here rather than in a footnote, because it changes what this tab is for. **GEMS-Taiwan won the 2024 High School Grand Prize**, and was a Finalist that year. Across 2024, 2025 and 2026 the team placed Top 10 in every season — it and Lambert-GA are the **only two High School teams to do that** — holding Gold each year, with a Grand Prize in 2024 and three section wins in 2026. So this is not an account of a bar GEMS has never reached. It is an account of a bar GEMS cleared in 2024 and has not cleared since, which is a different question and a far more answerable one. Note the shape as well: 2024's wins were **Best Wiki**, Best New Basic Part and the project promotion video, while 2026's were Measurement, Hardware and Integrated Human Practices — and in 2025 the team won nothing at all, on five nominations. The sections that follow take that comparison to the wikis themselves.\n\nThose are three different games, and GEMS played two of them extremely well. Of 147 accepted High School teams, only **17 won any section-level award at all** and GEMS holds three of them; only 47 got so much as a nomination. Any account of 2026 that treats this as a failure is not reading the field. But the third game selected two teams out of ten, and that is the one this tab is about.\n\nRead the special-wins column in the table and it plainly does not sort the field: the two teams with three special wins each finished **first and fifth**, and the team that finished second won nothing. Dimension strength and whole-project strength are measured by different people asking different questions, and a team can be near the top of one distribution and mid-table in the other.\n\nWhat the eight questions reward is narrower and harder than being strong in several places. Three of them — 1, 2 and 7 — converge on a single demand: **one legible result, finished, built on characterised biology.** Two more, 6 and 8, ask whether a stranger can verify what you claim. The cards below take each question in turn with what the 2026 High School evidence shows it rewarding; the sections after them put Lambert-GA, HongKong-JSS and GEMS-Taiwan against all eight from their own wikis and Registry pages, then read the whole Top 10 the same way.","body_zh":"一個 iGEM 賽季裡其實有三個互相獨立的決定，而它們很容易被當成一件事。**獎牌**是一張檢核表：做到交付項目就拿得到，所以 147 支高中隊伍裡有 135 支有獎牌，其中 63 支是金牌。**特別獎**由只看單一面向的評審評分，問「誰在這個面向做得最好」。而 **Top 10** 與 **Finalist** 名單，是由看整個專案的評審決定的，他們問九道問題，其中八道留下了公開紀錄。有一件事不能讓那句話被誤讀：Finalist 並**不是**一輪比頒獎臺更大、再從中選出名次的名單。2024、2025、2026 三年都一樣，它剛好落在頒獎臺上那七支隊伍，所以「進入 Finalist」與「站上頒獎臺」是同一件事。因此本頁檢視的那道落差，就是頒獎臺落差，只是用 iGEM 自己的詞彙來說。\n\n而細節應該寫在這裡，而不是寫在註腦裡，因為它改變了這個頁面存在的理由。**GEMS-Taiwan 贏過 2024 年高中組總冠軍**，那一年它也是 Finalist。2024、2025、2026 三季，這支隊伍每一季都進了 Top 10——全高中組**只有它和 Lambert-GA 做到**——每年都是金牌，2024 年拿下總冠軍，2026 年拿下三個組別獎。所以這並不是在說一道 GEMS 從未跨過的門檻，而是在說一道它在 2024 年跨過、之後沒再跨過的門檻；那是一個不同的問題，也是一個更有機會回答的問題。也請留意它的形狀：2024 年的得獎是**Best Wiki**、Best New Basic Part 與專案宣傳影片，而 2026 年的得獎是量測、硬體與整合式人類實踐——至於 2025 年，這支隊伍在五項入圍下什麽都沒有贏。後面幾節會把這個比較帶到 wiki 本身上。\n\n這是三個不同的遊戲，而 GEMS 把其中兩個玩得非常好。147 支正式參賽的高中隊伍中，**只有 17 支拿到任何一項組別層級的獎**，GEMS 一個人就佔了三項；連入圍都算進去也只有 47 支。任何把 2026 年說成「失敗」的說法，都沒有在讀這個賽場。但第三個遊戲是從十支裡選兩支，而這個頁面談的就是那一個。\n\n把表格裡「特別獎得獎」那一欄讀下來，它顯然不決定排序：各有三個特別獎的兩支隊伍，一支**第一名、一支第五名**，而第二名那一支什麼特別獎都沒拿。面向上的強度和整體專案的強度，是由不同的人問不同的問題量出來的；一支隊伍完全可以在其中一個分布的頂端，在另一個分布裡位居中段。\n\n那八道問題獎勵的東西，比「在好幾個地方都很強」更窄、也更難。其中三道——第 1、2、7 題——指向同一個要求：**一個清楚可讀、已經做完、建立在已表徵生物學之上的成果。** 另外兩道，第 6 和第 8 題，問的是陌生人能不能驗證你所聲稱的東西。下面的卡片逐題說明，以及 2026 年高中組的證據顯示它們各自在獎勵什麼；再往後的幾節，則用 Lambert-GA、HongKong-JSS 和 GEMS-Taiwan 自己的 wiki 與 Registry 頁面對照全部八題，然後用同一把尺讀完整個 Top 10。","cards":[{"kicker":"Question 1","kicker_zh":"第 1 題","title":"How impressive is this project?","title_zh":"這個專案有多令人印象深刻？","body":"Impressive is not the same as large. It rewards one result a judge can repeat back in a single sentence without looking at notes. Lambert-GA had one: the first reported minibinder confirmed to bind Deformed Wing Virus VP3. HongKong-JSS had one: a mercury limit of detection in water. A project with four strong components and no headline sentence reads as four projects.","body_zh":"「令人印象深刻」不等於「規模大」。它獎勵的是一個評審不用翻筆記、用一句話就能複述出來的成果。Lambert-GA 有這樣一句：首次有報告確認的 minibinder 能結合 Deformed Wing Virus 的 VP3。HongKong-JSS 也有：水中汞的偵測極限。一個有四個強組件、卻沒有一句標題句的專案，讀起來就像四個專案。","chips":["one sentence, no notes"],"chips_zh":["一句話，不用翻筆記"]},{"kicker":"Question 2","kicker_zh":"第 2 題","title":"Did the project work, or is it likely to work?","title_zh":"專案真的做出來了嗎，或看起來會成功嗎？","body":"This is where long chains die. A judge asks which links were shown **with data**, which were shown **in principle**, and which were only **designed**. A five-link chain with four demonstrated links scores as a chain that does not work yet, not as 80% of a working chain. Shortening the claim is usually worth more than lengthening the system.","body_zh":"這是長鏈條死掉的地方。評審會問：哪些環節是**有資料**證明的、哪些是**原理上**說得通的、哪些**只是設計**。一條五環的鏈條做出四環，評分上是「這條鏈還不會動」，而不是「一條會動的鏈的 80%」。把主張縮小，通常比把系統拉長更值錢。","chips":["with data / in principle / designed"],"chips_zh":["有資料 / 原理上 / 只是設計"]},{"kicker":"Question 3","kicker_zh":"第 3 題","title":"Is the project likely to have an impact?","title_zh":"這個專案可能產生影響嗎？","body":"Impact is judged on whether a named person outside the team would use the thing, not on the size of the problem. Every project addresses a large problem; that is table stakes. The separating evidence is a specific user, a specific site, and a number they care about.","body_zh":"影響力的評分依據是「團隊之外某個具名的人會不會真的用這個東西」，不是問題有多大。每個專案針對的問題都很大，那只是入場券。真正拉開差距的證據是：一個具體的使用者、一個具體的場地，以及一個他們在意的數字。","chips":["a named user, not a big problem"],"chips_zh":["具名的使用者，不是大問題"]},{"kicker":"Question 4","kicker_zh":"第 4 題","title":"How well were engineering principles used?","title_zh":"工程原則運用得好不好？","body":"Design-build-test, standards, modularity. The cheapest evidence in the whole rubric and the most often missing: **one documented failure and what you changed because of it.** A page of successful iterations reads as a report. A page with a failed iteration reads as engineering.","body_zh":"設計—build—測試、標準、模組化。這是整張評分表裡最便宜的證據，卻也最常缺席：**一個被記錄下來的失敗，以及你因為它改了什麼。** 一頁都是成功迭代，讀起來像報告；一頁裡有一次失敗的迭代，讀起來才像工程。","chips":["one documented failure"],"chips_zh":["一個被記錄的失敗"]},{"kicker":"Question 5","kicker_zh":"第 5 題","title":"How thoughtful and thorough was the human practices work?","title_zh":"團隊對人類實踐的思考有多周全深入？","body":"This report's own IHP analysis found that of 106 decorated teams, 71 can point at a stakeholder who visibly changed the design — and nine or ten of those stakeholders were not credentialled experts. The question is not how many meetings happened. It is which design decision is different because of one.","body_zh":"本報告自己的整合式人類實踐分析發現：106 支得獎隊伍中，有 71 支能指出一位明顯改變了設計的利害關係人——而其中只有九或十位不是有專業背景的專家。問題不是辦了幾場會議，而是有哪一個設計決定，因為某一場會議而不一樣了。","chips":["which decision changed"],"chips_zh":["哪一個決定被改了"]},{"kicker":"Question 6","kicker_zh":"第 6 題","title":"How much of the work did the team do themselves?","title_zh":"多少工作是團隊自己做的？","body":"A judge forms a view from the attributions page in about ninety seconds. The risk is asymmetric: a team that lists every collaborator in detail looks honest, and a team whose page is thin next to an ambitious result looks like it is hiding the answer. Under-disclosing is the more expensive mistake.","body_zh":"評審大約九十秒就會從 attributions 頁形成判斷。風險是不對稱的：把每一位合作者都詳細列出來的隊伍看起來誠實；而頁面單薄、成果卻很有野心的隊伍，看起來像在藏答案。少揭露是比較貴的那個錯。","chips":["ninety seconds on /attributions"],"chips_zh":["九十秒的 /attributions"]},{"kicker":"Question 7","kicker_zh":"第 7 題","title":"Is the project built on synthetic biology and standard components?","title_zh":"專案是否建立在合成生物學與標準元件之上？","body":"Explicitly BioBricks, software, standards. A project whose strongest parts are an instrument and a model has to show a characterised genetic core as well, or this question and the next one both answer themselves badly. Three of the ten High School Top 10 teams won a parts award in 2026.","body_zh":"這一題明確點名 BioBricks、軟體、標準。一個最強的部分是儀器和模型的專案，必須同時展示一個已表徵的基因核心，否則這一題和下一題都會自己給出難看的答案。2026 年高中組 Top 10 的十支隊伍中，有三支贏得了元件獎。","chips":["3 of 10 won a parts award"],"chips_zh":["10 支中 3 支贏得元件獎"]},{"kicker":"Question 8","kicker_zh":"第 8 題","title":"Are the components well documented on the Wiki and in the Registry?","title_zh":"各個組件在 Wiki 與 Registry 上的文件是否完整？","body":"The Registry half is the one teams forget. This report's parts census found 2026 parts-award winners carrying **10,388 to 83,030 characters** of registry documentation against nominees' **440 to 2,500**. Documentation length is not quality, but a part with 600 characters cannot be assessed by anyone who was not in the room.","body_zh":"Registry 那一半是隊伍最常忘記的。本報告的元件普查發現，2026 年元件獎得主的 registry 文件長度是 **10,388 到 83,030 字元**，入圍者是 **440 到 2,500 字元**。文件長度不等於品質，但一個只有 600 字元的元件，沒有在場的人根本無法評估它。","chips":["10,388–83,030 vs 440–2,500"],"chips_zh":["10,388–83,030 對 440–2,500"]}],"table":{"head":["Team","Placing","Finalist","Special wins","Nominations","Parts award","Best Wiki"],"head_zh":["隊伍","名次","Finalist","特別獎得獎","入圍","元件獎","最佳 Wiki"],"rows":[["Lambert-GA","Grand Prize winner","Yes","3","1","No","Winner"],["HongKong-JSS","1st Runner-up","Yes","0","4","Nominee (Composite)","—"],["GEMS-Taiwan","Top 10","No","3","3","No","Nominee"],["GHCIS","Top 10","No","2","2","Winner (Collection)","Nominee"],["HFI","Top 10","No","1","3","Nominee (Collection)","Nominee"],["GCGS","Top 10","No","1","3","Winner (Improved)","Nominee"],["HKSSC","Top 10","No","1","2","Winner (Basic)","—"],["HangzhouFourteenAP","Top 10","No","0","4","No","Nominee"],["Eton-College-UK","Top 10","No","0","3","No","—"],["HongKong-HS","Top 10","No","0","2","No","Nominee"]],"rows_zh":[["Lambert-GA","總冠軍","是","3","1","否","得獎"],["HongKong-JSS","亞軍","是","0","4","入圍（Composite）","—"],["GEMS-Taiwan","Top 10","否","3","3","否","入圍"],["GHCIS","Top 10","否","2","2","得獎（Collection）","入圍"],["HFI","Top 10","否","1","3","入圍（Collection）","入圍"],["GCGS","Top 10","否","1","3","得獎（Improved）","入圍"],["HKSSC","Top 10","否","1","2","得獎（Basic）","—"],["HangzhouFourteenAP","Top 10","否","0","4","否","入圍"],["Eton-College-UK","Top 10","否","0","3","否","—"],["HongKong-HS","Top 10","否","0","2","否","入圍"]]},"method":"Placings and awards are from the official 2026 results at competition.igem.org (research/results2026.json), cross-checked against iGEM's own API at api.igem.org/v1, which is open and unauthenticated and which is also where the Finalist designation and the medal distribution come from: of 147 accepted High School teams, 135 have a recorded medal (63 Gold, 68 Silver, 4 Bronze), 17 won at least one section-level or village award and 47 received at least one nomination. Two High School teams were named Finalists; the Undergraduate section had three and the Overgraduate section two. The special-wins column counts section-level special awards only, excluding the Top 10 placing, the Grand Prize placings and Best Village Project, which is a village award and is shown separately. The nine finalist questions are iGEM's published criteria, supplied by the report's own team. Question 9, on how competently a team answered judges' questions live, is excluded from this entire tab because it leaves no public record and nothing in a wiki can evidence it. That omission is material: the live session may be exactly where part of the gap described here was created, and no public analysis can see it. Everything on this tab is therefore an account of what a judge could learn from the published record, which is a real but incomplete share of what judges actually saw. The Finalist designation was checked against the 2024 and 2025 seasons as well: in all three, the finalist set and the podium set are identical — seven teams each year — so the designation names the podium rather than a wider round, and no intermediate slate is visible in the public record. GEMS-Taiwan's own three-season record was read from the same API: 2024 Grand Prize Winner, Finalist, Top 10 and Gold, with Best Wiki, Best New Basic Part and Best Project Promotion Video won and Best Model, Best Education and Best Presentation nominated; 2025 Top 10 and Gold with five nominations and no win; 2026 Top 10 and Gold with Measurement, Hardware and Integrated Human Practices won. Team ids are reissued every season, so the three seasons were joined on team name.","method_zh":"名次與獎項來自 competition.igem.org 的 2026 年官方結果（research/results2026.json），並與 iGEM 自己在 api.igem.org/v1 的 API 交叉核對；該 API 公開且不需驗證，Finalist 身分與獎牌分布也來自那裡：147 支正式參賽的高中隊伍中，135 支有獎牌紀錄（63 金、68 銀、4 銅），17 支至少拿下一項組別或 village 層級的獎，47 支至少獲得一次入圍。高中組有 2 支隊伍被列為 Finalist，大學組 3 支，研究生組 2 支。「特別獎得獎」一欄只計組別層級的特別獎，不含 Top 10 名次、不含總冠軍名次，也不含 Best Village Project（那是 village 層級的獎，另行標示）。那九道決賽問題是 iGEM 公布的標準，由本報告自己的團隊提供。第 9 題關於團隊現場回答評審問題的能力，在整個頁面中都被排除，因為它沒有留下任何公開紀錄，wiki 裡也沒有任何東西能證明它。這個排除很重要：這裡描述的落差，很可能有一部分正是在現場問答中產生的，而任何公開分析都看不到那一段。因此本頁所有內容，都只是「一位評審能從公開紀錄中讀到什麼」的說明；那是真實的一部分，但不是評審實際看到的全部。Finalist 身分也與 2024、2025 兩個賽季核對過：三年都一樣，Finalist 集合與頒獎臺集合完全相同——每年七支——所以這個身分指的就是頒獎臺，而不是更大的一輪名單；公開紀錄裡也看不到任何中間名單。GEMS-Taiwan 自己三季的紀錄也是從同一個 API 讀出來的：2024 年總冠軍、Finalist、Top 10 與金牌，贏下 Best Wiki、Best New Basic Part 與 Best Project Promotion Video，並入圍 Best Model、Best Education 與 Best Presentation；2025 年 Top 10 與金牌，五項入圍、零項得獎；2026 年 Top 10 與金牌，贏下量測、硬體與整合式人類實踐。隊伍的 id 每季都會重新發放，所以三季是以隊伍名稱作為鍵來對接的。"},{"id":"picks-gates","tab":"picks","order":5,"kicker":"Start here","kicker_zh":"從這裡開始","title":"Three piles: what the 2026 results say is a lever, what is only a floor, and what is a mirage","title_zh":"三堆東西：2026 年的結果說哪些是槓桿、哪些只是門檻、哪些是幻覺","lede":"Every measured finding in this report, sorted by whether it can change where GEMS places. The useful part is the second and third piles: most of what feels like effort in iGEM is either table stakes GEMS already clears, or measured at no effect. Spending 2027 on those is the most expensive mistake available.","lede_zh":"本報告每一條量測過的發現，依「能不能改變 GEMS 的名次」分類。真正有用的是第二堆和第三堆：iGEM 裡大部分感覺很費力的事，要麼是 GEMS 早就跨過的基本門檻，要麼量出來根本沒有效果。把 2027 年花在那些事情上，是能犯的最貴的錯。","body":"**One lever is supported from two directions, and it is the only one.** Across the 2026 High School Top 10, seven of the seven teams that missed the podium stop at a surrogate — a synthetic trigger RNA standing in for river water, a model ester, a reporter standing in for a therapy. Exactly one team in ten ran its assay on a real sample, and that team took 1st Runner-up. Inside GEMS's own three seasons the podium year is the real-target year: 2024 fed three toxins to live *Aedes albopictus* larvae and reported LC50 for all three, while 2026's strongest result, a plant rescue at p < 0.0001 with 40 seedlings a condition, sits on a preparation that was never assayed. Cross-sectional and longitudinal agreement is rare in this report; nothing else here has it.\n\n**The second pile is the dangerous one, because it is where good teams work hard for nothing.** Falsification controls are the clearest case. Reading all 30 Top 10 wikis, 26 of 30 ran an experiment designed expressly to kill a rival explanation for their own result, and 30 of 30 published a result unfavourable to their own headline. The practice is so near-universal that it cannot separate a podium from a Top 10 — podium teams average 4.29 of five control types against 3.61, which is a permutation p of 0.079 and not a result. **GEMS-Taiwan holds all five types, a perfect score, and still placed outside the podium**, as did four other perfect scorers. So controls are a floor this team cleared years ago. Write them in week one, then stop thinking about them.\n\n**The third pile is measured at nothing, and some of it is counter-intuitive enough to be worth saying twice.** Choosing a village is not a lever. Reporting more statistics is not a lever — the Top 10 team with the most statistical apparatus won nothing, and the Grand Prize winner names no test at all. A bigger team is not a lever. Rebuilding the wiki is not a lever, and the proof is GEMS's own: the 2024 site that won Best Wiki in the Grand Prize year is the weakest presented of its three seasons.","body_zh":"**只有一條槓桿從兩個獨立方向都站得住，而且也只有這一條。**在 2026 年高中組 Top 10 裡，七支沒上頒獎臺的隊伍，七支全部停在替代物上——用合成的觸發 RNA 代替河水、用模型酯類、用報導基因代替療法。十支裡剛好只有一支把檢測跑在真實樣本上，而那一支拿下亞軍。在 GEMS 自己的三個賽季裡，上頒獎臺的那一年就是打在真實標的上的那一年：2024 年把三種毒蛋白餵給活的 *Aedes albopictus* 幼蟲、三種都報告了 LC50；而 2026 年最強的結果，每組 40 棵苗、p < 0.0001 的植物救援，卻建立在一份從未被檢測活性的製備上。橫向與縱向同時成立，在這份報告裡很罕見；除此之外沒有任何一條做到。\n\n**第二堆才是危險的那一堆，因為好隊伍會在這裡白費力氣。**否證對照是最清楚的例子。把 30 支 Top 10 隊伍的 wiki 全部讀完：30 支中有 26 支做過刻意殺掉自家結果另一種解釋的實驗，30 支全部公開過一項對自己標題主張不利的結果。這個習慣普及到分不出頒獎臺與前十——頒獎臺隊伍平均擁有五類對照中的 4.29 類，其餘是 3.61 類，置換檢定 p 為 0.079，不構成結果。**GEMS-Taiwan 五類全有、滿分，卻仍然沒上頒獎臺**，另外四支滿分隊伍也一樣。所以對照是這支隊伍好幾年前就跨過的門檻。第一週就寫好，然後不要再想它。\n\n**第三堆是量出來等於零的，其中有幾項反直覺到值得講兩次。**選村落不是槓桿。報告更多統計不是槓桿——Top 10 裡統計工具用得最多的那一支什麼獎都沒拿，而總冠軍連一個檢定名稱都沒寫。隊伍更大不是槓桿。重做 wiki 不是槓桿，而證據來自 GEMS 自己：2024 年那個在總冠軍年拿下 Best Wiki 的網站，是三個賽季裡呈現最差的一個。","cards":[{"kicker":"Lever","kicker_zh":"槓桿","title":"Can you get the real thing, by week six?","title_zh":"你能不能在第六週之前拿到真實的那個東西？","body":"This is the only finding in the report supported both across the 2026 field and across GEMS's own three seasons. If a candidate topic's honest answer is \"we will use a surrogate and argue it is representative\", the topic is capped before the season starts — seven of seven non-podium High School teams did exactly that. Make sample access a selection criterion, not a logistics problem to solve later. The question is not whether the science is good; it is whether the thing you claim to act on is the thing you measured.","body_zh":"這是整份報告裡唯一同時在 2026 年全體與 GEMS 自己三個賽季都站得住的發現。如果一個候選題目誠實的答案是「我們會用替代物，然後論證它具代表性」，那這個題目在賽季開始前就被設了上限——七支沒上頒獎臺的高中隊伍，七支都正是這樣做。把「樣本取得」當成選題條件，而不是之後再解決的後勤問題。問題不在科學好不好，而在你聲稱要作用的那個東西，是不是你真正量到的那個東西。","chips":["7 of 7 non-podium used a surrogate","1 of 10 used a real sample","that one took 1st Runner-up"],"chips_zh":["七支非頒獎臺隊伍全用替代物","十支裡一支用真實樣本","那一支拿下亞軍"]},{"kicker":"Lever","kicker_zh":"槓桿","title":"Close the model-data loop, and hold data back before you look at it","title_zh":"把模型與資料的迴路閉合，而且在看資料之前就先留一部分起來","body":"Teams that both fitted a model to their own measured data **and** validated it against something held back reached a Top 10 at 53%, against 23% for those that did not. All nine teams that closed the loop without a Top 10 won or were nominated for a major special prize anyway, so this is close to a floor on the downside and a lever on the upside. It is also scarce where it counts: only 12 of the 30 Top 10 teams validated against held-back data at all. Best Model recognition in the High School section maps onto the finalist slate exactly — Lambert-GA won it, HongKong-JSS was nominated, and no other Top 10 team appears in the category.","body_zh":"同時把模型擬合到自己量到的資料**並且**拿留存資料做驗證的隊伍，進 Top 10 的比例是 53%，沒做的是 23%。九支閉合了迴路但沒進 Top 10 的隊伍，全部還是拿到或入圍了某個重要特別獎，所以這件事下有保底、上有槓桿。而它在關鍵處其實很稀少：30 支 Top 10 隊伍裡，只有 12 支真的拿留存資料做過驗證。高中組的 Best Model 入圍與得獎名單，正好疊合在決賽名單上——Lambert-GA 得獎、HongKong-JSS 入圍，其餘 Top 10 隊伍沒有任何一支出現在這個類別裡。","chips":["53% against 23%","only 12 of 30 held data back","Best Model maps onto the finalists"],"chips_zh":["53% 對 23%","30 支裡只有 12 支留存資料","Best Model 疊合決賽名單"]},{"kicker":"Lever, and rare","kicker_zh":"槓桿，而且稀少","title":"Remove a confound by design, then run it again","title_zh":"用設計移除一個混淆因子，然後重跑一次","body":"Of the five falsification-control types, four are saturated across the Top 10 and one pair is scarce: only 17 of 30 removed a confound by design and re-tested, and only 12 of 30 held data back. Those two are where the podium actually leans ahead. GEMS's own 2024 attractant work is the model — a position bias was found and the centre cup removed, then the beetroot colour was suspected and every cup covered with black paper \"so that the selection of oviposition sites is based on odorant factors only\", after which the preference still held at p = 0.0003. **Two confounds found and eliminated by the team itself, on its own target species.**","body_zh":"五類否證對照裡有四類在 Top 10 之中已經飽和，只有一對很稀少：30 支中只有 17 支以設計移除混淆因子後重測，只有 12 支留存資料做驗證。頒獎臺真正拉開距離的就是這兩類。GEMS 自己 2024 年的引誘劑實驗就是範本——先發現位置偏誤，拿掉中央那一杯；接著懷疑甜菜根的顏色，就把每一杯都用黑紙蓋住，「讓產卵位置的選擇只取決於氣味因素」，之後偏好仍然成立，p = 0.0003。**兩個混淆因子都由團隊自己找出來並排除，而且是在自己的標的物種上。**","chips":["17 of 30 redesigned and re-tested","12 of 30 held data back","GEMS 2024 did both"],"chips_zh":["30 支中 17 支重新設計並重測","30 支中 12 支留存資料","GEMS 2024 兩者都做到"]},{"kicker":"Floor — already cleared","kicker_zh":"門檻——已經跨過","title":"The experiment that could have broken your own claim","title_zh":"那個可能推翻你自己主張的實驗","body":"Write it in week one and then stop thinking about it, because **GEMS already scores a perfect five of five** on this and it did not place. 26 of 30 Top 10 teams ran an exclusion of a rival explanation; 30 of 30 published a result unfavourable to their own headline. The habit is a floor, not a ranking. The cheapest part is also the most visible: 23 of 30 teams named an arm they could not run, and that is 7 of 7 on the podium against 16 of 23 off it. Athens wrote the best version — \"Separating the two requires that buffer-only arm, and until it is run we describe the effect as attributable to the preparation\" — and scored only 3 of 5 while doing so. Naming the gap costs nothing and is the clearest evidence a judge can see that you know what your data does not show.","body_zh":"第一週就寫好，然後不要再想它，因為**GEMS 這一項已經是滿分五類全有**，卻沒有名次。30 支 Top 10 隊伍中有 26 支做過排除對手解釋的實驗，30 支全部公開過對自己標題不利的結果。這個習慣是門檻，不是名次表。其中最便宜的部分也最顯眼：30 支中有 23 支指名了自己沒能做的那一組對照，而這是頒獎臺 7 比 7、臺下 23 比 16。Athens 寫出了最好的版本——「要把這兩者分開需要那一組只有緩衝液的對照，在它被做出來之前，我們把這個效應描述為可歸因於該製備」——而它這樣寫卻只拿 3 分。指名缺口完全不花錢，而且是評審能看到的最清楚證據，證明你知道自己的資料沒有顯示什麼。","chips":["26 of 30 ran an exclusion","30 of 30 published bad news","GEMS scores 5 of 5"],"chips_zh":["30 支中 26 支做過排除","30 支全部登出壞消息","GEMS 五類全有"]},{"kicker":"Floor — already cleared","kicker_zh":"門檻——已經跨過","title":"Do not rebuild the wiki, and the proof is your own 2024 site","title_zh":"不要重做 wiki，而證據是你自己 2024 年的網站","body":"The tempting story is that presentation slipped since 2024. Read against all three seasons it breaks. The 2024 site that won **both** the Grand Prize and Best Wiki is a 577-byte script shell with the whole site in one 1,690,501-byte bundle, no results page at all because `/results` returns 404, one p-value, and the longest module inventory of the three. The 2026 site beats it on every presentation measure: server-rendered, five times the p-values, 67 uniquely numbered figures, and a page that scores its own stages. Every team in the 2026 Top 10 publishes a wet-lab protocol a stranger could follow, so that is table stakes too. The one presentation thing that is still worth fixing is not design, it is honesty — see the next pile.","body_zh":"誘人的說法是：自 2024 年以來，呈現退步了。拿三個賽季一起讀，這個說法就破了。2024 年那個**同時**拿下總冠軍與 Best Wiki 的網站，是一個 577 位元組的腳本外殼，整站裝在一個 1,690,501 位元組的套件裡，根本沒有結果頁，因為 `/results` 回傳 404，全站只有一個 p 值，而且模組清單是三年裡最長的。2026 年的網站在每一項呈現指標上都勝過它：伺服器端渲染、p 值多五倍、67 張不重複編號的圖，還有一頁為自己的階段評分。2026 年 Top 10 的每一支隊伍都公開了陌生人能照著做的濕實驗流程，所以那也是基本門檻。唯一還值得修的呈現問題不是設計，而是誠實——見下一堆。","chips":["2024: 577-byte shell, no results page","2026 wins on every measure","all 30 publish followable protocols"],"chips_zh":["2024：577 位元組外殼、沒有結果頁","2026 在每項指標上勝出","30 支全部公開可照做的流程"]},{"kicker":"Not a lever either — fix it anyway","kicker_zh":"也不是槓桿——但還是要修","title":"The honesty gap does not buy a placing, and GEMS is the joint-worst in the Top 10","title_zh":"誠實落差買不到名次，而 GEMS 在 Top 10 裡並列最差","body":"This was measured across all 30 Top 10 wikis and the result reversed the expectation. **Over-claiming is the norm, and the podium does it slightly more**: 21 of 29 scorable teams assert more on the landing page than their own evidence page supports, the podium averages 1.43 on a 0-to-3 gap scale against 1.00 for everyone else, and two of the four teams whose own pages contradict them are podium teams. The three Grand Prize winners score 0, 1 and 1 — mid-cohort.\n\nSo fixing this buys credibility, not placing. Fix it anyway, because **GEMS-Taiwan is joint-worst at 3**, tied with Princeton, Cornell and WageningenUR, and it is the only team in thirty whose contradiction spans three of its own pages. The home page sells \"On-demand — Green light switches production on when the environmental sensors and forecasts decide to\". The results page says the ELISA showed no change over time, that the amount did not rise with light, and that the medium remained colorless. The model page says \"The reactor therefore cannot be scheduled from the forecast\". 2024 did not make this mistake: it hedged in the same breath, writing that the work \"partially proved the chromosome-free system\".","body_zh":"這一項在 30 支 Top 10 隊伍的 wiki 上全部量過，而結果與預期相反。**誇大宣稱是常態，而且頒獎臺隊伍還稍微誇得更兇**：29 支可評分的隊伍中有 21 支，在首頁上主張的內容超過自己證據頁撐得住的範圍；在 0 到 3 的落差尺度上，頒獎臺平均 1.43，其餘隊伍 1.00；而四支被自己頁面反駁的隊伍裡，有兩支就在頒獎臺上。三支總冠軍的分數是 0、1、1——都在中段。\n\n所以修這件事買到的是可信度，不是名次。但還是要修，因為**GEMS-Taiwan 以 3 分並列最差**，和 Princeton、Cornell 與 WageningenUR 同分，而且是三十支裡唯一一支矛盾橫跨自己三個頁面的隊伍。首頁賣的是「On-demand——綠光在環境感測器與預報做出判斷時開啟生產」。結果頁說 ELISA 隨時間沒有變化、產量並未隨光照上升、培養基始終沒有顯色。模型頁寫著「因此反應器無法由預報來排程」。2024 年沒有犯這個錯：它把保留寫在同一句話裡——「**部分**證實了無染色體系統」。","chips":["21 of 29 over-claim","podium 1.43 vs 1.00","GEMS joint-worst at 3"],"chips_zh":["29 支中 21 支誇大","頒獎臺 1.43 對 1.00","GEMS 以 3 分並列最差"]},{"kicker":"Mirage","kicker_zh":"幻覺","title":"Choosing a village is not a lever, and neither is team size","title_zh":"選村落不是槓桿，隊伍大小也不是","body":"Of 147 accepted High School teams, 47 were decorated, which is 32.0%. The per-village spread runs from 2 of 17 in Agriculture up to 12 of 23 in Biomanufacturing — and that spread is **not distinguishable** from 147 teams decorated independently at 32% (chi-square 19.64 on 12 degrees of freedom, Monte-Carlo p = 0.088). Year to year, the only thing that carries is crowding (r = +0.91); what a village pays does not (Top 10 rate r = +0.17, p = 0.58). Team size is the same story: headcount against award count across 84 decorated teams correlates at 0.06 with p = 0.61, and the smallest Top 10 team was Princeton with nine undergraduates. Pick the village the problem lives in and move on.","body_zh":"147 支獲准參賽的高中隊伍中，有 47 支得獎，也就是 32.0%。各村落的得獎率從 Agriculture 的 17 取 2，到 Biomanufacturing 的 23 取 12——而這個分布**無法與**「147 支隊伍各自獨立以 32% 機率得獎」區分開來（卡方 19.64、自由度 12、蒙地卡羅 p = 0.088）。年與年之間唯一延續的是擁擠程度（r = +0.91）；村落「給多少獎」並不延續（Top 10 率 r = +0.17、p = 0.58）。隊伍大小是同一個故事：84 支得獎隊伍的人數與獲獎數相關係數 0.06、p = 0.61，而最小的 Top 10 隊伍是 Princeton，九位大學部學生。選題目所在的那個村落，然後別再想它。","chips":["32.0% base rate","chi-square p = 0.088","team size r = 0.06"],"chips_zh":["32.0% 基礎比率","卡方 p = 0.088","隊伍人數 r = 0.06"]},{"kicker":"Mirage","kicker_zh":"幻覺","title":"More statistics, more Registry pages and more measurement discipline all buy nothing","title_zh":"更多統計、更多 Registry 文件、更嚴的量測紀律，全都買不到名次","body":"Three separate nulls point the same way. In the High School Top 10, HongKong-HS reported ANOVA, a Dunnett post-hoc, a t-test, n = 3 and standard deviations — and won nothing at all, while the Grand Prize winner names no statistical test and gives no p-value. The Grand Prize winner also has the **shortest** Registry documentation of all ten. And measurement discipline, scored on seven checkable habits across all 106 files, runs 27% against 29% — *no effect*. None of this means be sloppy; it means these are hygiene, and hygiene is not a strategy. Nobody ran an inter-lab measurement ring in 2026 and nobody measured an escape rate, so those remain genuinely unclaimed ground rather than crowded ground.","body_zh":"三個互相獨立的虛無結果指向同一個方向。在高中組 Top 10 裡，HongKong-HS 報告了 ANOVA、Dunnett 事後檢定、t 檢定、n = 3 與標準差——結果一個獎都沒拿；而總冠軍連一個統計檢定名稱都沒寫，也沒有給出任何 p 值。總冠軍的 Registry 文件也是十支裡**最短**的。而量測紀律——以七項可檢核的習慣掃過全部 106 份檔案——是 27% 對 29%，*沒有效果*。這些都不是叫你草率，而是說這些屬於衛生習慣，而衛生習慣不是策略。2026 年沒有任何隊伍辦過實驗室間的量測環，也沒有任何隊伍量過逃逸率，所以那些仍然是真正沒人佔的地，而不是擠滿人的地。","chips":["most statistics won nothing","Grand Prize has shortest Registry docs","measurement discipline 27% vs 29%"],"chips_zh":["統計最多的什麼都沒拿","總冠軍 Registry 文件最短","量測紀律 27% 對 29%"]}],"table":{"head":["Finding","Pile","The measurement","What it means for choosing 2027"],"head_zh":["發現","分類","量測結果","對 2027 選題的意義"],"rows":[["Central claim measured on the real target","**Lever**","7 of 7 non-podium HS teams used a surrogate; 1 of 10 used a real sample and took 1st Runner-up; GEMS's podium year is its real-target year","Make sample access a selection criterion. If the honest answer is a surrogate, pick a different topic."],["Model fitted to own data and validated on held-back data","**Lever**","53% reached a Top 10 against 23%; all 9 who closed it without a Top 10 still won or were nominated for a major special prize","Choose a topic where you will generate enough of your own data to fit and still hold some back."],["Best Model recognition","**Lever**","In the HS section it maps onto the finalist slate exactly: Lambert-GA won, HongKong-JSS nominated, no other Top 10 team appears","Treat the modelling track as the one award-level signal that tracks the podium."],["Confound removed by design, then re-tested","**Lever, and rare**","Only 17 of 30 Top 10 teams did it","Plan the redesign-and-repeat before you start, not after a reviewer asks."],["Validation against held-back data","**Lever, and rare**","Only 12 of 30 Top 10 teams did it; exactly 4 of 10 in each section","Decide the split rule in week one and write down which rows you kept out."],["An experiment that could break your own claim","**Floor — cleared**","26 of 30 ran one; 30 of 30 published an unfavourable result; **GEMS scores 5 of 5** and still did not place","Write it in week one, then stop. It cannot buy a placing it has already given everyone."],["Naming the arm you could not run","**Floor — cheap and visible**","23 of 30 overall; 7 of 7 on the podium against 16 of 23 off it","Costs nothing. Say which condition you could not cover and what it would have settled."],["A wet-lab protocol a stranger could follow","**Floor**","All 30 of the 2026 Top 10 publish one","Table stakes. Budget the time, claim no credit."],["Wiki presentation quality","**Floor — cleared**","GEMS's 2024 Best Wiki winner is the weakest presented of its three seasons: 577-byte shell, no results page, 1 p-value","Do not spend 2027 rebuilding the wiki."],["Landing page claims matching the results page","**Not a lever — fix for credibility**","21 of 29 Top 10 teams over-claim; podium averages 1.43 against 1.00, so the podium is slightly worse; **GEMS is joint-worst at 3** and the only team contradicted across three of its own pages","Fix it because it is about whether your claims are true, not because it will move you up."],["Choosing a village","**Mirage**","Spread 2 of 17 to 12 of 23 not distinguishable from 32% independent (chi-square 19.64, 12 df, Monte-Carlo p = 0.088); year to year only crowding carries, r = +0.91","Pick the village the problem lives in. Do not optimise on it."],["Team size","**Mirage**","Headcount against award count r = 0.06, p = 0.61 across 84 teams; smallest Top 10 team had nine members","Choose a topic the team you have can finish."],["Volume of statistical reporting","**Mirage**","The HS Top 10 team with the most of it won nothing; the Grand Prize winner names no test and gives no p-value","Report statistics honestly, but do not mistake apparatus for evidence."],["Volume of Registry documentation","**Mirage**","The Grand Prize winner has the shortest of all ten","Document parts properly, expect no placing from length."],["Measurement discipline","**Mirage**","27% against 29% across all 106 files — no effect","Hygiene, not strategy."],["Dark mode, alt-text sweeps, mascot systems","**Mirage**","Correlate with nothing across the Best Wiki winners","Skip them."],["Inter-lab measurement ring; escape-rate measurement","**Unclaimed ground**","Nobody in 106 decorated teams did either","Genuinely open. Cheap for a team that already holds a Measurement award."]],"rows_zh":[["核心主張打在真實標的上","**槓桿**","七支非頒獎臺高中隊伍全用替代物；十支裡一支用真實樣本並拿下亞軍；GEMS 上頒獎臺的那年就是打在真實標的上的那年","把樣本取得當成選題條件。如果誠實的答案是替代物，就換一個題目。"],["模型擬合自家資料並以留存資料驗證","**槓桿**","53% 進 Top 10，對 23%；九支閉合迴路但沒進 Top 10 的隊伍，全部仍得獎或入圍重要特別獎","選一個你們會產出足夠自家資料、既能擬合又還留得出一部分的題目。"],["Best Model 的得獎與入圍","**槓桿**","在高中組，它正好疊合決賽名單：Lambert-GA 得獎、HongKong-JSS 入圍，其餘 Top 10 隊伍皆未出現","把建模這條線當成唯一一個與頒獎臺同步的獎項層級訊號。"],["以設計移除混淆因子後重測","**槓桿，而且稀少**","30 支 Top 10 隊伍裡只有 17 支做了","在開始之前就把「重新設計再重跑」排進計畫，而不是等評審問起才做。"],["以留存資料做驗證","**槓桿，而且稀少**","30 支 Top 10 隊伍裡只有 12 支做了；三個組別各剛好 4 支","第一週就決定切分規則，並寫下你們留了哪些資料在外面。"],["一個可能推翻自己主張的實驗","**門檻——已跨過**","30 支中 26 支做過；30 支全部登出不利結果；**GEMS 五類全有滿分**，卻仍沒有名次","第一週寫好，然後停手。它買不到一個早就給了所有人的名次。"],["指名自己沒能做的那一組對照","**門檻——便宜又顯眼**","整體 30 支中 23 支；頒獎臺 7 比 7，臺下 23 比 16","完全不花錢。寫明你們沒能涵蓋哪個條件，以及它本來能定案什麼。"],["陌生人能照著做的濕實驗流程","**門檻**","2026 年 Top 10 全部 30 支都公開了","基本門檻。時間要排，但別指望加分。"],["wiki 的呈現品質","**門檻——已跨過**","GEMS 2024 年的 Best Wiki 得主是三季裡呈現最差的：577 位元組外殼、沒有結果頁、1 個 p 值","2027 年不要花時間重做 wiki。"],["首頁主張與結果頁相符","**不是槓桿——為可信度而修**","29 支 Top 10 隊伍中 21 支誇大；頒獎臺平均 1.43 對 1.00，所以頒獎臺還稍差；**GEMS 以 3 分並列最差**，而且是唯一一支被自己三個頁面反駁的隊伍","要修，是因為它關乎你的主張是不是真的，不是因為它會讓你往上移。"],["選村落","**幻覺**","17 取 2 到 23 取 12 的分布，無法與「各自獨立 32%」區分（卡方 19.64、自由度 12、蒙地卡羅 p = 0.088）；年與年之間只有擁擠程度延續，r = +0.91","選題目所在的那個村落。不要為它做最佳化。"],["隊伍大小","**幻覺**","84 支隊伍的人數對獲獎數 r = 0.06、p = 0.61；最小的 Top 10 隊伍九人","選一個你們現有人力做得完的題目。"],["統計報告的數量","**幻覺**","高中組 Top 10 裡統計最多的那支什麼都沒拿；總冠軍不寫檢定名稱也不給 p 值","統計要誠實報告，但不要把工具當成證據。"],["Registry 文件的數量","**幻覺**","總冠軍的文件是十支裡最短的","元件要好好記錄，但別期待長度換名次。"],["量測紀律","**幻覺**","全部 106 份檔案中 27% 對 29%——沒有效果","衛生習慣，不是策略。"],["深色模式、替代文字補掃、吉祥物系統","**幻覺**","在 Best Wiki 得主之間與任何結果都不相關","跳過。"],["實驗室間量測環；逃逸率量測","**沒人佔的地**","106 支得獎隊伍裡沒有任何一支做過","真正空著。對一支已經握有 Measurement 獎的隊伍來說很便宜。"]]},"checklist":["Sort every 2027 idea into these three piles before arguing about which is most interesting. An idea that only scores in the floor and mirage piles is not a candidate.","Ask of each candidate: what is the real target, and can we hold it in our hands by week six? If the answer is a surrogate, the topic is capped.","Pick a topic that will generate enough of your own data to fit a model and still hold some back. Only 12 of 30 Top 10 teams managed that, so it is both a lever and scarce.","Write the rival explanation and the arm that kills it in week one, then stop thinking about controls. GEMS already scores a perfect five of five and it did not place.","Name the arm you could not run, every season. It is free, it is 7 of 7 on the podium, and GEMS has done it three years running.","Do not rebuild the wiki and do not add statistics for their own sake. Both are measured at no effect, and the wiki proof is GEMS's own 2024 site.","Write the landing-page sentence last, from the results page, and have someone check it against the model page. That is the one presentation failure of 2026.","Choose the village the problem lives in and stop optimising it. The spread between villages is not distinguishable from chance.","If two candidates tie, prefer the one that opens unclaimed ground — an inter-lab measurement ring or an escape-rate measurement, neither of which any of the 106 decorated teams of 2026 attempted."],"checklist_zh":["在爭論哪個題目最有趣之前，先把 2027 年的每個想法分進這三堆。一個只在門檻堆和幻覺堆得分的想法，不算候選。","對每個候選問一句：真實標的是什麼，我們能不能在第六週之前親手拿到它？如果答案是替代物，這個題目就被設了上限。","選一個會產出足夠自家資料、既能擬合模型又還留得出一部分的題目。30 支 Top 10 隊伍裡只有 12 支做到，所以它既是槓桿又稀少。","第一週就把對手解釋、以及殺掉它的那一組實驗寫下來，然後不要再想對照。GEMS 已經是滿分五類全有，而且沒有名次。","每一季都要指名自己沒能做的那一組對照。它免費、在頒獎臺上是 7 比 7，而 GEMS 已經連續三年都做到。","不要重做 wiki，也不要為了統計而加統計。兩者都量出沒有效果，而 wiki 的證據來自 GEMS 自己 2024 年的網站。","首頁那句話最後才寫，而且從結果頁往回寫，再請人拿模型頁對一次。那是 2026 年唯一的呈現失誤。","選題目所在的那個村落，然後停止最佳化它。村落之間的差距無法與隨機區分。","如果兩個候選打平，選那個打開沒人佔的地的——實驗室間的量測環，或是逃逸率量測；2026 年 106 支得獎隊伍裡，兩者都沒有任何一支嘗試過。"],"method":"This block is a synthesis rather than a new measurement: every figure in it is measured elsewhere in this report and each source block states its own limits where it is reported. The lever, floor and mirage labels are this report's judgement about what can change a placing, not iGEM's categories and not a statistical classification. Sources, in the order the table uses them: judging-top10 and gems-three-seasons for the real-target finding and the three-season GEMS record; the model-loop figure and the Best Model mapping from the dry-lab analyses and judging-top10; falsification-controls for the five control types, the 26 of 30, the 30 of 30, the 17 and 12 of 30, the 23 of 30 disclosure flag and the permutation test; village-baserates for the village null; team-resources for team size; measurement-discipline for the 27-against-29 null; protocol-reproducibility for the protocol floor; wiki-craft and gems-three-seasons for presentation. Two cautions carry over from those blocks and apply to everything here. First, the sample is decorated teams only -- every team file is a Top 10 or special-prize winner or nominee -- so no figure here describes the competition at large except where a base rate is explicitly drawn from iGEM's full accepted roster. Second, the Top 10 comparisons rest on 30 teams and seven podium places, which cannot carry a causal claim; read them as a description of which side of a line the podium happened to fall on.","method_zh":"本節是綜合整理，不是新的量測：裡面每一個數字都量測於本報告其他處，而各來源區塊都在該處載明了自己的限制。「槓桿」、「門檻」、「幻覺」這三個標籤是本報告對「什麼能改變名次」的判斷，不是 iGEM 的分類，也不是統計上的分類。來源依表格使用順序：真實標的發現與 GEMS 三季紀錄來自 judging-top10 與 gems-three-seasons；模型迴路數字與 Best Model 的疊合來自乾實驗室相關分析與 judging-top10；五類對照、30 支中 26 支、30 支全部、30 支中 17 與 12 支、23 支揭露旗標與置換檢定來自 falsification-controls；村落虛無結果來自 village-baserates；隊伍大小來自 team-resources；27 對 29 的虛無結果來自 measurement-discipline；流程門檻來自 protocol-reproducibility；呈現相關來自 wiki-craft 與 gems-three-seasons。有兩項警告從那些區塊延續下來，並適用於本節全部內容。第一，樣本僅限得獎隊伍——每一份團隊檔案都是 Top 10 或特別獎得主或入圍者——所以除了明確取自 iGEM 完整正式參賽名單的基礎比率之外，本節沒有任何數字在描述整個賽事。第二，Top 10 的各項比較建立在 30 支隊伍與七個頒獎臺名額上，撐不起因果主張；請把它們讀成「頒獎臺剛好落在某條線的哪一側」的描述。"},{"id":"proposals-how","tab":"proposals","order":5,"kicker":"Read this first","kicker_zh":"先讀這一段","title":"How to read these candidates — and the prize to chase is Best Model","title_zh":"這些候選題目該怎麼讀——而該追的獎是 Best Model","lede":"Every candidate on this tab is run through the ten questions on the 2027 selection guide, with the same two gates — a real target in hand by week six, and a readout on an instrument GEMS already owns — and then through a third screen that matters more than either: iGEM's White List, which for a high school team is a hard ceiling rather than a default. None of them guarantees a Finalist slot, because nothing in this report predicts one. What they do is put the team on the right side of the one line the podium actually sat on.","lede_zh":"本分頁上的每一個候選題目，都跑過 2027 選題指南上的十個問題，關卡一樣兩道——第六週之前真實標的要在手上，讀值要用 GEMS 已經有的儀器做得出來——然後再過第三道比前兩道都更要緊的篩查：iGEM 白名單；對高中組隊伍而言那是一道硬天花板，不是預設值。沒有任何一個能保證決賽席位，因為這份報告裡沒有任何東西預測得了那個。它們能做的，是讓團隊站到頒獎臺真正落在的那條線的正確一側。","body":"**What \"Finalist\" actually means, so the target is the right size.** Across 2024, 2025 and 2026 alike the Finalist set and the podium are identical: seven teams a year, the Grand Prize winner and the runners-up. In the 2026 High School section, 147 teams entered, 10 reached the Top 10 and 2 were named Finalists. So this is not a wider round in front of the podium — it is the podium. GEMS has stood on it once, in 2024.\n\n**The prize to chase is Best Model, and the reason is specific.** Pooled over three seasons, the share of a category's nominees who also took a Top 10 runs from Best Wiki at 60% and Best Presentation at 53% down to 0% for Safety, Alternative Platform and New Improved Part. Best Model sits at 50% — but in the High School section it does something sharper than that: **it maps onto the finalist slate exactly.** Lambert-GA won it, HongKong-JSS was nominated, and no other High School Top 10 team appears in the category at all. GEMS was nominated for Best Model in 2024 and again in 2025, and has never won it. That is the single most addressable gap in the team's record, and five of the six proposals below are built to attack it.\n\n**Read the percentages as a map, not a prediction.** The figure is near-circular and this report says so: Wiki and Presentation are judged on how the whole project is communicated, which is the same material a Top 10 judgement works on. Chasing Best Wiki to win a Top 10 is chasing the thermometer. The reason Best Model is different is that it rewards a thing you can decide to do in week one — fit a model to your own measured data and validate it against data you held back — and that habit is independently measured at 53% reaching a Top 10 against 23%.\n\n**One regression worth naming.** GEMS won Best New Basic Part in 2024 and had **zero parts nominations in 2026**. Taiwan's zero across all thirteen competing teams is shared. Every proposal below therefore states what it would deposit in the Registry, because that is a prize category the team has already proved it can win and then stopped entering.","body_zh":"**先把「決賽隊伍」的意思講準，才知道目標有多大。**2024、2025、2026 三季都一樣：決賽隊伍集合與頒獎臺完全相同，一年七支，總冠軍加上亞軍季軍。2026 年高中組有 147 支隊伍參賽，10 支進 Top 10，2 支被列為決賽隊伍。所以這不是頒獎臺前面的一個較寬的回合——它就是頒獎臺。GEMS 站上去過一次，在 2024 年。\n\n**該追的獎是 Best Model，理由很具體。**三季合計，各類別入圍者同時拿下 Top 10 的比例，從 Best Wiki 的 60%、Best Presentation 的 53%，一路到 Safety、Alternative Platform 與 New Improved Part 的 0%。Best Model 是 50%——但在高中組，它做到一件更尖銳的事：**它正好疊合在決賽名單上。**Lambert-GA 得獎、HongKong-JSS 入圍，其餘高中組 Top 10 隊伍沒有任何一支出現在這個類別裡。GEMS 在 2024 年與 2025 年都入圍過 Best Model，從來沒有得過。那是這支隊伍紀錄裡最可著手的一個缺口，而下面六個提案有五個就是為了攻它而設計的。\n\n**那些百分比要當地圖讀，不要當預測讀。**這個數字接近循環論證，本報告自己也說了：Wiki 與 Presentation 評的是整個專案怎麼被傳達出來，而那正是 Top 10 評審所依據的同一批材料。為了拿 Top 10 去追 Best Wiki，是去追溫度計。Best Model 之所以不同，是因為它獎勵的是一件你在第一週就能決定要做的事——把模型擬合到自己量到的資料，再用事先留存的資料驗證它——而這個習慣另外被獨立量到：進 Top 10 的比例是 53% 對 23%。\n\n**有一項退步值得點名。**GEMS 在 2024 年拿下 Best New Basic Part，而 2026 年**零個元件類入圍**。台灣十三支參賽隊伍的零也是共享的。所以下面每一個提案都寫明它會往 Registry 存進什麼，因為那是一個這支隊伍已經證明自己拿得到、然後就不再投的獎項。","cards":[{"kicker":"The target","kicker_zh":"目標","title":"Finalist is the podium: seven teams a year, and GEMS has been one","title_zh":"決賽就是頒獎臺：一年七支，而 GEMS 當過其中一支","body":"In all three seasons on record the Finalist designation and the podium are the same seven teams, so it names the Grand Prize winner and the runners-up rather than a wider round. In the 2026 High School section that was 2 teams out of 147 entered and 10 in the Top 10. **GEMS won the 2024 High School Grand Prize**, and it and Lambert-GA are the only two High School teams in the Top 10 in all three seasons. So the honest framing for 2027 is not \"reach a bar we have never reached\" but \"clear one we cleared in 2024 and have not cleared since\".","body_zh":"有紀錄的三個賽季裡，決賽隊伍的認定與頒獎臺是同一批七支隊伍，所以它指的是總冠軍與亞軍季軍，而不是前面一個比較寬的回合。在 2026 年高中組，那是 147 支參賽、10 支進 Top 10 之中的 2 支。**GEMS 拿過 2024 年高中組總冠軍**，而且它和 Lambert-GA 是三個賽季都進高中組 Top 10 的僅有兩支隊伍。所以 2027 年誠實的說法不是「去跨一道我們從沒跨過的門檻」，而是「把 2024 年跨過、之後就沒再跨過的那一道再跨一次」。","chips":["2 Finalists of 147 entered","Finalist equals podium","GEMS won it in 2024"],"chips_zh":["147 支參賽中 2 支決賽","決賽即頒獎臺","GEMS 2024 年拿過"]},{"kicker":"The prize to chase","kicker_zh":"該追的獎","title":"Best Model maps onto the High School finalist slate exactly, and GEMS has never won it","title_zh":"Best Model 正好疊合高中組決賽名單，而 GEMS 從沒得過","body":"Across the 2026 High School Top 10, Best Model recognition lands on the two finalists and nobody else: Lambert-GA won it, HongKong-JSS was nominated, and not one of the other eight Top 10 teams appears in the category. Pooled over three seasons its nominees take a Top 10 **50%** of the time. GEMS was nominated in 2024 and 2025 and has not won. The route is not a bigger model — Lambert won by **benchmarking its own confidence metrics** against 5,721 labelled designs, finding a 38-metric ensemble at ROC-AUC 0.541, and publishing that its own eventual hit did not carry the best score.","body_zh":"在 2026 年高中組 Top 10 裡，Best Model 的得獎與入圍落在兩支決賽隊伍身上，沒有別人：Lambert-GA 得獎、HongKong-JSS 入圍，另外八支 Top 10 隊伍沒有一支出現在這個類別。三季合計，這個類別的入圍者有 **50%** 同時拿下 Top 10。GEMS 在 2024 與 2025 年入圍，沒有得過。路徑不是做一個更大的模型——Lambert 之所以得獎，是因為**拿 5,721 筆有標籤的設計去檢驗自己的信賴度指標**，發現一個 38 指標的集成模型 ROC-AUC 只有 0.541，而且公開說自己最後真正結合的那一個分數並不是最高的。","chips":["50% of nominees take a Top 10","maps onto both HS finalists","GEMS nominated 2024 and 2025"],"chips_zh":["入圍者 50% 進 Top 10","疊合兩支高中決賽隊伍","GEMS 2024、2025 入圍"]},{"kicker":"The regression","kicker_zh":"退步之處","title":"A parts award GEMS has already won, and then stopped entering","title_zh":"一個 GEMS 已經拿過、然後就不再投的元件獎","body":"GEMS won **Best New Basic Part** in the 2024 Grand Prize year. In 2026 it had zero nominations in any parts category, and so did all thirteen competing Taiwanese teams. The co-occurrence with a Top 10 is low — Best New Basic Part sits at 9% and Best Part Collection at 35% — so this is not a placing lever. It is a credibility gap and a continuity gap: a characterised, documented part is the one deliverable that outlives the season, needs no server, and can be used by somebody else. Every proposal below names what it would deposit.","body_zh":"GEMS 在 2024 年那個總冠軍賽季拿下 **Best New Basic Part**。2026 年它在任何元件類別都是零入圍，而台灣十三支參賽隊伍全部也都是零。這類獎與 Top 10 的同時發生率很低——Best New Basic Part 是 9%，Best Part Collection 是 35%——所以它不是名次槓桿。它是可信度的缺口，也是延續性的缺口：一個特性描述完整、文件齊全的元件，是唯一一種能活過這個賽季、不需要伺服器、而且別人真的用得到的交付成果。下面每一個提案都寫明它會存進什麼。","chips":["2024 win, 2026 zero","Taiwan's zero is shared","9% and 35% co-occurrence"],"chips_zh":["2024 得獎，2026 掛零","台灣的零是共享的","同時發生率 9% 與 35%"]},{"kicker":"The circularity","kicker_zh":"循環論證","title":"Do not chase Best Wiki to win a Top 10 — that is chasing the thermometer","title_zh":"不要為了拿 Top 10 去追 Best Wiki——那是去追溫度計","body":"Best Wiki nominees take a Top 10 60% of the time and Best Presentation 53%, which looks like the strongest signal on the board. It is not a lever, because both categories are judged on **how the whole project is communicated**, which is the same material a Top 10 judgement works on. The report's own three-season test makes the point harder: the 2024 GEMS site that won Best Wiki in the Grand Prize year is the weakest presented of its three seasons — a 577-byte script shell, no results page at all, one p-value. Defend the wiki because the work deserves to be readable, and pick the project on the science.","body_zh":"Best Wiki 的入圍者有 60% 同時拿下 Top 10，Best Presentation 是 53%，看起來是整張表上最強的訊號。它不是槓桿，因為這兩個類別評的都是**整個專案怎麼被傳達出來**，而那正是 Top 10 評審所依據的同一批材料。本報告自己的三季檢驗把這一點說得更硬：2024 年那個在總冠軍賽季拿下 Best Wiki 的 GEMS 網站，是三個賽季裡呈現最差的一個——577 位元組的腳本外殼、根本沒有結果頁、全站一個 p 值。把 wiki 顧好，是因為這些工作值得被讀懂；而選題要靠科學來選。","chips":["60% and 53%","judged on the same material","2024's Best Wiki was the weakest site"],"chips_zh":["60% 與 53%","評的是同一批材料","2024 的 Best Wiki 是最差的網站"]},{"kicker":"How each one is scored","kicker_zh":"每個提案怎麼評分","title":"The same ten questions, and the first two are gates","title_zh":"同樣的十個問題，而前兩題是關卡","body":"Every proposal is answered against the selection guide's instrument, in order: the real target and whether it is in hand by week six; the readout and the instrument that already exists; the model and the rows held back; the rival explanation and the arm that kills it; the named outside person; the multiplying audience; the cost of the tenth against the first; the artefact that still works a year after the freeze; the one sentence a judge should repeat; and, newly added, what the paper would be and who has already written it. **Questions one and two are gates rather than scores** — a proposal that fails either is not a candidate however interesting the biology is, and one of the six below is marked down on exactly that basis. **A third screen then runs behind both gates and matters more than either:** iGEM's White List, which for a high school team is a hard ceiling rather than a default, because this division has no Check-In route at all.","body_zh":"每一個提案都依選題指南的工具逐題作答，順序一致：真實標的是什麼、第六週前在不在手上；讀值與已經存在的儀器；模型與留存的資料列；對手解釋與殺掉它的那一組實驗；具名的外部人士；會放大的對象；第十次相對第一次的成本；凍結一年後還能用的產出；希望評審重複的那一句話；以及新加入的一題：這篇論文會是什麼，而誰已經寫過了。**第一題和第二題是關卡而不是分數**——過不了任何一題的提案就不算候選，不管生物學多有趣；下面六個之中，就有一個正是因為這一點被扣分。**而在兩道關卡後面還有第三道篩查，它比前兩道都更要緊：**iGEM 的白名單——對高中組隊伍而言那是一道硬天花板，不是預設值，因為這個組別根本沒有 Check-In 管道。","chips":["nine questions, in order","two gates","and a White List ceiling behind them"],"chips_zh":["九個問題，依序","兩道關卡","後面還有一道白名單天花板"]},{"kicker":"What this page cannot do","kicker_zh":"這一頁做不到的事","title":"Nothing here predicts a placing, and the report is explicit about why","title_zh":"這裡沒有任何東西能預測名次，而報告很明確地說明了原因","body":"The comparisons behind these recommendations rest on 30 Top 10 teams and seven podium places, which cannot carry a causal claim, and on a sample made entirely of decorated teams, so no figure here describes the competition at large. Three of the report's recent analyses returned nulls or reversals: choosing a village is not a lever, falsification controls are a floor GEMS already clears at full marks, and over-claiming on the landing page is the Top 10 norm with the podium slightly worse. **Treat these six as structured bets with their reasoning exposed**, not as a ranking — and the eligibility register on this page matters more than the ranking does, because a rule, not a judge, is what usually ends a project.","body_zh":"支撐這些建議的比較，建立在 30 支 Top 10 隊伍與七個頒獎臺名額上，撐不起因果主張；而樣本全部由得獎隊伍構成，所以這裡沒有任何數字在描述整個賽事。本報告最近有三項分析得到虛無或反轉的結果：選村落不是槓桿；否證對照是 GEMS 早就以滿分跨過的門檻；而首頁誇大是 Top 10 的常態，頒獎臺還稍差一些。**請把這六個當成把推理攤開來的結構化下注**，而不是一張名次表——而且這一頁上的資格檢查比排名更重要，因為終結一個專案的通常是規則，不是評審。","chips":["n = 30, 7 podium places","decorated teams only","rules end projects, not judges"],"chips_zh":["n = 30，七個頒獎臺名額","僅限得獎隊伍","終結專案的是規則，不是評審"]}],"table":{"head":["Special prize","Nominees also Top 10","GEMS record 2024-26","Chase it in 2027?"],"head_zh":["特別獎","入圍者同時進 Top 10","GEMS 2024-26 紀錄","2027 要追嗎？"],"rows":[["**Best Model**","**50% (20/40)**","2024 nominee · 2025 nominee · never won","**Yes — the primary target.** In the High School section it maps onto the finalist slate exactly. It rewards a decision made in week one, not a bigger model."],["Best Wiki","**60% (49/81)**","**2024 win** · 2025 nom · 2026 nom","Defend, do not chase. Near-circular: judged on the same material as a Top 10, and GEMS's own Best Wiki year is its weakest-presented site."],["Best Presentation","53% (42/79)","2024 nom · 2026 nom","Defend. Same circularity as Best Wiki."],["Best Integrated Human Practices","45% (17/38)","**2026 win**","Defend. Already won; the proposals keep the named-stakeholder habit rather than rebuilding it."],["Best Part Collection","35% (11/31)","never cited","**Yes, secondary.** GEMS has never been cited in any parts category since 2024, and Taiwan's zero is shared."],["Best Education","33% (12/36)","2024 nom · 2025 nom","Yes, if the proposal carries a Traditional Chinese artefact with a reuse licence — 3 of 31 teams and 1 of 136 PDFs respectively."],["Best Measurement","22% (7/32)","2025 nom · **2026 win**","Defend, and it is cheap to defend here: four of the six proposals are measurement-led."],["Best Hardware","21% (6/29)","**2026 win**","Defend only. Low co-occurrence, and GEMS already owns the instruments these proposals need."],["Best New Basic Part","9% (3/35)","**2024 win**","Yes, as credibility rather than placing. It is the one deliverable that outlives the season and needs no server."],["Safety and Security Award","**0% (0/9)**","never cited","Only if the project genuinely earns it. Zero of nine nominees took a Top 10, so enter it for the work, not the odds."],["Best Sustainable Development Impact","10% (3/30)","never cited","Incidental. Claim it if the project fits; do not design for it."],["Best Software","24% (4/17)","never cited","Only if a tool is a real output. Of 21 award-winning 2026 tools, 8 still run — and every live one was hosted before freeze day."]],"rows_zh":[["**Best Model**","**50%（40 取 20）**","2024 入圍 · 2025 入圍 · 從未得獎","**要——首要目標。**在高中組它正好疊合決賽名單。它獎勵的是第一週就能做的決定，不是更大的模型。"],["Best Wiki","**60%（81 取 49）**","**2024 得獎** · 2025 入圍 · 2026 入圍","守成，不要追。接近循環：評的材料和 Top 10 一樣，而 GEMS 自己拿 Best Wiki 那年的網站，是三季裡呈現最差的。"],["Best Presentation","53%（79 取 42）","2024 入圍 · 2026 入圍","守成。與 Best Wiki 同樣的循環問題。"],["Best Integrated Human Practices","45%（38 取 17）","**2026 得獎**","守成。已經拿過；這些提案延續具名利害關係人的習慣，而不是重做一次。"],["Best Part Collection","35%（31 取 11）","從未被提及","**要，次要目標。**GEMS 自 2024 年後在任何元件類別都沒被提及過，而台灣的零是共享的。"],["Best Education","33%（36 取 12）","2024 入圍 · 2025 入圍","要——條件是提案帶一份附可重用授權的繁體中文產出；這兩件事分別只有 31 支中的 3 支、136 份中的 1 份做到。"],["Best Measurement","22%（32 取 7）","2025 入圍 · **2026 得獎**","守成，而且在這裡守成很便宜：六個提案裡有四個是以量測為主軸的。"],["Best Hardware","21%（29 取 6）","**2026 得獎**","只守成。同時發生率低，而且這些提案需要的儀器 GEMS 都已經有了。"],["Best New Basic Part","9%（35 取 3）","**2024 得獎**","要，但目的是可信度而不是名次。它是唯一能活過賽季、又不需要伺服器的交付成果。"],["Safety and Security Award","**0%（9 取 0）**","從未被提及","只有在專案真的配得上時才投。九位入圍者沒有一位進 Top 10，所以為了工作本身去投，不是為了機率。"],["Best Sustainable Development Impact","10%（30 取 3）","從未被提及","順帶拿。如果專案本來就符合就投，不要為它設計。"],["Best Software","24%（17 取 4）","從未被提及","只有在工具是真正的產出時才投。2026 年 21 個得獎工具中有 8 個還跑得動，而每一個還活著的都在凍結日之前就上線代管了。"]]},"checklist":["Make Best Model the primary prize target and decide in week one what model will be fitted and which rows are held back. It is the one category that maps onto the High School finalist slate.","Do not design the season around Best Wiki or Best Presentation. Both are judged on the same material as a Top 10, so they report the result rather than cause it.","Deposit a characterised part in every candidate. GEMS won Best New Basic Part in 2024 and had zero parts nominations in 2026, and all thirteen Taiwanese teams shared that zero.","Answer questions one and two before anything else. A proposal with no real target in hand by week six, or no readout on an instrument already owned, is not a candidate.","Check eligibility before the biology. The register on this page is the part that ends projects; a rule is cheaper to discover in November than in June.","Carry one Traditional Chinese artefact with an explicit reuse licence in whichever proposal wins. Only 3 of 31 decorated teams published anything in Traditional Chinese, and 1 of 136 education PDFs carried a licence.","Keep the named-stakeholder habit that won Best Integrated Human Practices in 2026 rather than rebuilding it from scratch.","Write down which proposals you rejected and which question killed each one. Only 3 of 106 decorated teams credit their own predecessor with anything."],"checklist_zh":["把 Best Model 當成首要獎項目標，並在第一週就決定要擬合什麼模型、以及哪些資料列要留存不用。它是唯一一個疊合高中組決賽名單的類別。","不要圍繞 Best Wiki 或 Best Presentation 來設計整個賽季。兩者評的材料與 Top 10 相同，所以它們是在回報結果，不是造成結果。","每一個候選題目都要存進一個特性描述完整的元件。GEMS 在 2024 年拿過 Best New Basic Part，2026 年元件類零入圍，而台灣十三支隊伍共享這個零。","在做別的事之前，先回答第一題和第二題。第六週之前沒有真實標的在手、或讀值做不在已有的儀器上，就不算候選。","先查資格，再談生物學。這一頁上的檢查表才是終結專案的那一部分；一條規則在十一月發現，比在六月發現便宜得多。","不管最後選上哪一個提案，都要帶一份附明確可重用授權的繁體中文產出。31 支得獎隊伍中只有 3 支發表過繁體中文內容，136 份教育 PDF 中只有 1 份附了授權。","延續 2026 年拿下 Best Integrated Human Practices 的具名利害關係人習慣，而不是從零重做一次。","把你否決掉的提案、以及是哪一題殺掉它的，都寫下來。106 支得獎隊伍裡只有 3 支對自己的前一屆表示過任何感謝。"],"method":"The special-prize percentages come from award-economics.json, which pooled the 2024, 2025 and 2026 award records from iGEM's public API across all divisions, and that block states its own limits: the figure is near-circular for Wiki and Presentation, Best Village Project is excluded because it is awarded inside villages rather than across the field, and the High-School-only rates are not tabulated because their denominators fall to 1 or 2. The Best Model mapping onto the High School finalist slate is from judging-top10.json and covers the ten 2026 High School Top 10 teams only. The 53-against-23 model-loop figure, the Finalist-equals-podium result, the three-season GEMS record and the parts-nomination gap come from the dry-lab analyses, judging-criteria.json, gems-three-seasons.json and gems-gap.json respectively. Everything on this page is a recommendation built on those measurements, not a new measurement, and none of it predicts a placing: the underlying comparisons rest on 30 Top 10 teams and seven podium places and on a sample of decorated teams only.","method_zh":"特別獎的百分比來自 award-economics.json，該區塊彙整了 iGEM 公開 API 上 2024、2025 與 2026 三季、跨全部組別的獎項紀錄，並在該處載明自己的限制：對 Wiki 與 Presentation 而言這個數字接近循環論證；Best Village Project 被排除，因為它是在各 village 內部頒發而不是跨全體頒發；而只算高中組的比率不列表，因為分母會掉到 1 或 2。Best Model 疊合高中組決賽名單的結果來自 judging-top10.json，涵蓋範圍僅限 2026 年高中組 Top 10 那十支隊伍。53 對 23 的模型迴路數字、決賽即頒獎臺的結果、GEMS 三季紀錄，以及元件類入圍的缺口，分別來自乾實驗室相關分析、judging-criteria.json、gems-three-seasons.json 與 gems-gap.json。本頁所有內容都是建立在那些量測之上的建議，不是新的量測，而且沒有任何一項能預測名次：底層的比較建立在 30 支 Top 10 隊伍與七個頒獎臺名額上，樣本也僅限得獎隊伍。"},{"id":"gems-three-seasons","tab":"judging","order":7,"kicker":"Three seasons, one team","kicker_zh":"三個賽季，同一支隊伍","title":"GEMS won the 2024 Grand Prize, and the 2024 wiki is the weakest of the three","title_zh":"GEMS 拿下 2024 年總冠軍，而 2024 年的 wiki 是三年之中最弱的一個","lede":"The judging analysis on this tab treats a Finalist slate as a bar GEMS-Taiwan has yet to clear. **It cleared it in 2024**, as Grand Prize winner and Finalist, with Best Wiki among three wins. The tempting story is that the whole-project communication layer slipped between then and now. Read against the three wikis themselves, **that story breaks.** The 2024 site is a 577-byte JavaScript shell with **no results page at all**, one p-value on the entire site and no named statistical test; the 2026 results page is server-rendered, carries five p-values and 67 uniquely numbered figures, and a separate page scores all five project stages against criteria written down before the runs. What separates them is narrower and harder: in 2024 both central claims were measured on the real target animal with the competing explanation excluded, and every claim on the summary list was hedged to the evidence behind it. In 2026 the claim that makes ReLEAF an optogenetics project is stated on the landing page and contradicted on its own results page.","lede_zh":"本頁的評審分析，把決賽席位當成 GEMS-Taiwan 還沒跨過的一道門檻。**它在 2024 年就跨過了**——總冠軍、決賽隊伍，三個獎項之中還包含 Best Wiki。誘人的說法是：從那時到現在，整體專案的溝通層退步了。但把三份 wiki 放在一起讀，**這個說法就破了。** 2024 年的網站是一個 577 位元組的 JavaScript 外殼，**完全沒有結果頁**，整站只有一個 p 值，也沒有寫出任何統計檢定名稱；2026 年的結果頁是伺服器端渲染，有五個 p 值、67 張編號不重複的圖，還有另外一頁把專案的五個階段逐一對照「實驗開跑前就寫下的成功標準」來評分。真正把兩者分開的東西更窄、也更難面對：2024 年的兩項核心主張都是在真實的標的生物上量到的，而且排除了競爭解釋，摘要清單上的每一條都緊貼著它背後的證據。2026 年那個讓 ReLEAF 成為光遺傳學專案的主張，寫在首頁上，卻被它自己的結果頁推翻。","body":"Three seasons were measured on the same six questions. The 2024 wiki is a single-page application: `https://2024.igem.wiki/gems-taiwan/` returns 200 and 577 bytes, `/results` is a 404, and the whole site lives in one 1.69 MB JavaScript bundle, so **nothing on it is readable before scripts run.** The 2025 and 2026 pages are server-rendered and fetch as text. On the criterion that the Best Wiki winners studied elsewhere in this report satisfy — text first, scripts later — the Best Wiki winner of 2024 is the only one of the three that fails it.\n\n**The one-headline-versus-inventory distinction does not separate these three seasons at all.** 2024's summary is a nine-item numbered list on its description page, introduced \"Hence, our team worked across Wetlab, Drylab, Human Practice, and Software, and together, we achieved the following:\". 2025 publishes thirteen bullets under four module headings. 2026 publishes five one-line key results. The Grand Prize year has the longest inventory of the three. Whatever the two 2026 finalists were rewarded for, GEMS did not have it in 2024 either.\n\nStatistical reporting moved the same way, upward. p-values across the pages read: **2024 one, 2025 none, 2026 five.** Named statistical tests: **zero in all three seasons** — no t-test, ANOVA, Tukey, Dunnett, Welch, Mann-Whitney, Wilcoxon or Kruskal anywhere, in any year. The single 2024 p-value is \"the p-value equal to 0.0003\" on the oviposition assay. Dispersion runs from one `± SE` column in 2024, through 23 mentions of standard error in 2025, to SEM plus R² of 0.992 to 0.9995 and a pre-registered 90% interval in 2026. **Neither statistics nor structure is what changed.**\n\nWhat changed is what the central claim was made about. In 2024 the toxins were fed to live *Aedes albopictus* larvae — the actual vector species, not a surrogate — ten larvae per cup in triplicate, LC50 reported for all three toxins, 98 dead larvae mounted and examined, and a qPCR immune-gene panel against a BL21(DE3) empty-vector control run specifically \"to rule out the effect of *E. coli* in the death of mosquito larvae\". The attractant was tested on live gravid females, and when the team spotted a position bias it removed the centre cup, then suspected the beetroot colour and covered every cup with black paper before repeating. In 2026 the green-light device was never demonstrated: \"The ELISA showed no change over time\", ACCD at 2.6 to 3.2 µg/mL at every time point under both colours, AmilCP's \"medium remained colorless\", and every biological result came from a constitutively expressing bypass module. The 2024 chain was never joined end to end either — and the page says so in the same breath, \"Integration of our sticky ovitrap and recombinant biolarvicidal proteins **will be** a powerful vector control tool\", \"**partially** proved the chromosome-free system\". **That hedging is the difference the wikis actually show.** 2026's home page states \"Green light switches production on\" as a feature of the machine, and the refutation sits three pages deeper.","body_zh":"三個賽季用同樣六個問題量過。2024 年的 wiki 是一個單頁式應用程式：`https://2024.igem.wiki/gems-taiwan/` 回傳 200、只有 577 位元組，`/results` 是 404，整個網站裝在一個 1.69 MB 的 JavaScript 套件裡，因此**在腳本跑起來之前，它上面沒有任何東西讀得到。** 2025 與 2026 的頁面是伺服器端渲染，直接當文字抓得下來。本報告別處研究過的 Best Wiki 得主都滿足一個條件——文字先到、腳本後到——而三者之中唯一不滿足它的，正是 2024 年的 Best Wiki 得主。\n\n**「單一招牌結果」對「模組清單」的區分，在這三個賽季之間完全分不開任何東西。** 2024 年的摘要是 description 頁上一份九條的編號清單，開頭寫著「因此，我們的團隊橫跨 Wetlab、Drylab、Human Practice 與 Software 工作，共同達成了以下成果：」。2025 年在四個模組標題底下列出十三條。2026 年列出五條一行的 Key results。清單最長的那一年，正是總冠軍那一年。2026 年那兩支決賽隊伍是因為什麼被獎勵的，GEMS 在 2024 年也同樣沒有。\n\n統計報告的方向也是往上。各頁的 p 值依序是：**2024 年一個、2025 年零個、2026 年五個。** 寫出名稱的統計檢定：**三個賽季都是零**——任何一年、任何地方都沒有 t-test、ANOVA、Tukey、Dunnett、Welch、Mann-Whitney、Wilcoxon 或 Kruskal。2024 年那唯一的 p 值，在產卵偏好試驗上寫的是「這個實驗得到的結果高度顯著，p 值等於 0.0003」。離散度的呈現，從 2024 年一欄 `± SE`，到 2025 年二十三次提到標準誤，再到 2026 年的 SEM 加上 0.992 至 0.9995 的 R²，以及一個事先登記的 90% 區間。**改變的既不是統計，也不是結構。**\n\n改變的是「核心主張是在講什麼東西」。2024 年，毒蛋白被餵給活的 *Aedes albopictus* 幼蟲——真正的病媒物種，不是替代物——每杯十隻、三重複，三種毒蛋白都報告了 LC50，98 隻死亡幼蟲被封片檢視，還有一組 qPCR 免疫基因試驗對照 BL21(DE3) 空載體，做的目的明寫是「排除 *E. coli* 在蚊子幼蟲死亡中的作用」。引誘劑是在活的受孕雌蚊身上測的；團隊發現位置偏誤之後拿掉了中央那一杯，接著懷疑甜菜根的顏色，就用黑紙把每一杯都蓋起來再重做一次。2026 年，綠光裝置從未被證明：「ELISA 顯示隨時間沒有變化」，ACCD 在兩種光色、每一個時間點都是 2.6 至 3.2 µg/mL，AmilCP 的「培養液始終無色」，而所有生物學成果都來自一個組成型表現的旁路模組。2024 年的鏈條同樣從未端到端接起來——而那一頁在同一句話裡就說了：「把我們的黏性產卵器與重組殺幼蟲毒蛋白整合起來，**將會**是一個強大的病媒防治工具」、「**部分**證明了 chromosome-free system」。**這種緊貼證據的保留，才是三份 wiki 真正顯示出來的差別。** 2026 年的首頁把「綠光開啟生產」當成機器的一項功能寫出來，而推翻它的證據，要再往裡走三頁才看到。","cards":[{"kicker":"Hypothesis broken","kicker_zh":"假設被推翻","title":"The Best Wiki winner is the only one of the three whose text needs JavaScript to appear","title_zh":"三者之中唯一必須靠 JavaScript 才顯示得出文字的，正是 Best Wiki 得主","body":"`https://2024.igem.wiki/gems-taiwan/` returns 200 and **577 bytes**: a `<div id=\"root\">`, a `<noscript>` reading \"You need to enable JavaScript to run this app\", and one script tag. The whole site — every page of prose, every figure caption, the route table — is inside `main.8a37e754.js`, **1,690,501 bytes**, with no code splitting and no data fetched at runtime. `/results` on that host is a 404; the 2024 wiki has no results page, and its route list runs `/description`, `/engineering`, `/experiment`, `/proofofconcept`, `/parts`, `/awards` and sixteen more.\n\nThe 2025 and 2026 results pages fetch as server-rendered text, 108 KB and 160 KB. The 2026 home page is fully readable with scripts off, farmer quote and all, and even writes out the content of each map as text. **The team's wiki got strictly more robust across the three seasons, and the robust years are the years it did not win the category.** Whatever Best Wiki rewarded in 2024, this was not it.","body_zh":"`https://2024.igem.wiki/gems-taiwan/` 回傳 200 與 **577 位元組**：一個 `<div id=\"root\">`、一段寫著「You need to enable JavaScript to run this app」的 `<noscript>`，以及一個 script 標籤。整個網站——每一頁文字、每一個圖說、路由表——都裝在 `main.8a37e754.js` 裡，**1,690,501 位元組**，沒有程式碼分割，執行期間也不抓取任何資料。那台主機上的 `/results` 是 404；2024 年的 wiki 沒有結果頁，它的路由清單是 `/description`、`/engineering`、`/experiment`、`/proofofconcept`、`/parts`、`/awards`，再加十六個。\n\n2025 與 2026 的結果頁都是伺服器端渲染的文字，108 KB 與 160 KB。2026 年的首頁在關掉腳本的情況下完全讀得到，連農民的引語都在，甚至把每一張地圖的內容也寫成文字。**這支隊伍的 wiki 在三個賽季裡嚴格地越來越穩固，而穩固的那兩年，正是它沒有拿下這個類別的年份。** 2024 年的 Best Wiki 獎勵的是別的東西，不是這個。","chips":["2024: 577-byte shell","no results page in 2024","2025 and 2026: server-rendered"],"chips_zh":["2024：577 位元組外殼","2024 沒有結果頁","2025 與 2026：伺服器端渲染"]},{"kicker":"Inventory, all three","kicker_zh":"三年都是清單","title":"The Grand Prize year has the longest module inventory of the three","title_zh":"總冠軍那一年，模組清單是三年中最長的","body":"The finding this section was built to test is that both 2026 finalists nominate one result while the eight non-finalists publish inventories. Against GEMS's own three seasons it does not sort anything. **2024 publishes nine numbered achievements**, introduced \"Hence, our team worked across Wetlab, Drylab, Human Practice, and Software, and together, we achieved the following:\" — twelve recombinant proteins, the potency of three toxins, a cloned chromosome-free system, the attractant, the trap, the egg counter, an epidemiological model, homology models, education tools. **2025 publishes thirteen bullets** under \"Key Findings:\" across four module headings. **2026 publishes five**, as \"Key results\": protectant secretion, light control, the photometer, plant rescue, containment and release.\n\nNine, thirteen, five — and the podium year is the nine. The distinction that separates the 2026 finalists from the 2026 field does not separate this team's Grand Prize from its Top 10s, which is a reason to hold it loosely as a rule about placings in general.","body_zh":"本節要檢驗的那個發現是：2026 年兩支決賽隊伍各自指定一個結果，而八支非決賽隊伍發表的是清單。拿到 GEMS 自己的三個賽季上，它分不開任何東西。**2024 年發表九條編號成果**，開頭是「因此，我們的團隊橫跨 Wetlab、Drylab、Human Practice 與 Software 工作，共同達成了以下成果：」——十二個重組蛋白、三種毒蛋白的效力、一個選殖出來的 chromosome-free system、引誘劑、捕蚊器、蟲卵計數器、一個流行病學模型、同源模型、教育工具。**2025 年在「Key Findings」底下、四個模組標題之中發表十三條。2026 年發表五條**，標題是「Key results」：保護蛋白分泌、光控制、光度計、植物救援、圍阻與釋出。\n\n九條、十三條、五條——而上頒獎臺的那一年是九條。把 2026 年兩支決賽隊伍與全場分開的那個區分，並沒有把這支隊伍的總冠軍與它的 Top 10 分開；這是一個理由，讓我們不要把它當成關於名次的一般性規則來緊握。","chips":["2024: nine items","2025: thirteen","2026: five"],"chips_zh":["2024：九條","2025：十三條","2026：五條"]},{"kicker":"Statistics","kicker_zh":"統計","title":"p-values went one, none, five — and no season ever names a statistical test","title_zh":"p 值依序是一個、零個、五個——而三個賽季都沒有寫出任何檢定名稱","body":"Counted the same way each year, after unescaping the HTML and matching on real test names with word boundaries: **2024 has exactly one p-value on its entire site**, \"The results obtained from this experiment were highly significant, with the p-value equal to 0.0003\", on the oviposition assay. **2025's results page has none.** **2026's has five**, all on the plant work, reported as asterisk markers — two for p < 0.01, three for p < 0.001, four for p < 0.0001 — with \"ns, not significant\" marked where it applies.\n\n**Named tests: zero, zero, zero.** No t-test, ANOVA, Tukey, Dunnett, Welch, Mann-Whitney, Wilcoxon or Kruskal appears in any season, so every \"significant\" and \"highly significant\" in 2024 and 2025 is unattributed. Dispersion improves monotonically too: one `Mortality ± SE (%)` column in 2024; standard error named 23 times in 2025; SEM throughout 2026 plus R² of 0.992, 0.9949, 0.9995 and a growth rate registered on 1 October as \"0.2986 h−1, 90% interval 0.2705 to 0.3300\" and later observed at 0.286 ± 0.010. Replicate disclosure is the one line that got worse: triplicates stated throughout 2024, against `n=1` and `n=3` in 2026.","body_zh":"每一年都用同樣方式計數，先把 HTML 的轉義還原，再以完整字詞比對真正的檢定名稱：**2024 年整站恰好只有一個 p 值**——產卵偏好試驗上寫著「這個實驗得到的結果高度顯著，p 值等於 0.0003」。**2025 年的結果頁一個也沒有。2026 年有五個**，全在植物工作上，以星號標記呈現——兩個星號代表 p < 0.01，三個代表 p < 0.001，四個代表 p < 0.0001——並在適用處標出「ns，不顯著」。\n\n**寫出名稱的檢定：零、零、零。** 任何賽季都沒有出現 t-test、ANOVA、Tukey、Dunnett、Welch、Mann-Whitney、Wilcoxon 或 Kruskal，因此 2024 與 2025 年每一個「顯著」與「高度顯著」都沒有依據可追。離散度的呈現也是單向改善：2024 年一欄 `Mortality ± SE (%)`；2025 年二十三次寫出標準誤；2026 年全頁使用 SEM，再加上 0.992、0.9949、0.9995 的 R²，以及 10 月 1 日事先登記的生長速率 0.2986 h⁻¹、90% 區間 0.2705 至 0.3300，其後實測 0.286 ± 0.010。唯一變差的一條是重複數的揭露：2024 年全程寫明三重複，2026 年則是 `n=1` 與 `n=3`。","chips":["1 / 0 / 5 p-values","0 named tests, all three years","triplicates to n=1"],"chips_zh":["p 值 1 / 0 / 5","三年都是 0 個檢定名稱","從三重複到 n=1"]},{"kicker":"The real difference","kicker_zh":"真正的差別","title":"In 2024 the claim was measured on the real animal, and the rival explanation was shut out","title_zh":"2024 年的主張是在真實的動物身上量到的，而且把對手解釋關在門外","body":"The 2024 toxins were assayed on live *Aedes albopictus* larvae — the vector itself, no surrogate — \"by exposing 10 stage 2 larvae in each cup to different concentrations of toxins. All assays were conducted in triplicates\", with LC50 reported for all three: Cyt2Ba 5.29 × 10⁶ CFU/mL, Xpp81Aa1 1.98 × 10⁷, BmK IT1 179 mg/mL. 98 dead larvae were mounted and examined. Then the obvious rival explanation was tested directly: a qPCR panel of *Gambicin*, *Rel1*, *Rel2* and *defensin* against a BL21(DE3) empty-vector arm, run because \"We want to rule out the effect of *E. coli* in the death of mosquito larvae\".\n\nThe panel reached a verdict and then disclosed its own gap. For the 37 °C induction the team wrote that \"This data indicated that the mortality observed in the larvicidal assay was not due to the introduction of BL21(DE3)\" — while also reporting that most immune-gene transcripts were not regulated at all. For the 20 °C arm they said plainly what they could not do: \"We acknowledge the limitation of this particular study because we did not compare it to BL21(DE3) ... Our team had a shortage of mosquito larvae to conduct additional groups during this period of time.\" **The exclusion is finished for one induction condition and declared unfinished for the other** — the same move as the LC50 series, whose own incomplete arm is disclosed on the same page. A reader can tell exactly how far the claim reaches.\n\nThe attractant work is the same discipline. Gravid females, three replicates, cups rotated by position; a position bias was spotted and the centre cup removed; then the beetroot colour was suspected and every cup covered with black paper, \"so that the selection of oviposition sites is based on odorant factors only\", after which the preference held at p = 0.0003. **Two confounds found and eliminated by the team itself, on its own target species.** That is the depth route the 1st Runner-up took in 2026, and GEMS had already walked it in 2024.","body_zh":"2024 年的毒蛋白是在活的 *Aedes albopictus* 幼蟲上試驗的——病媒本身，沒有替代物——方法寫明是「每一杯放入 10 隻第二齡幼蟲，暴露於不同濃度的毒蛋白。所有試驗都以三重複進行」，三種都報告了 LC50：Cyt2Ba 5.29 × 10⁶ CFU/mL、Xpp81Aa1 1.98 × 10⁷、BmK IT1 179 mg/mL。98 隻死亡幼蟲被封片檢視。接著，最明顯的對手解釋被直接檢驗：一組 *Gambicin*、*Rel1*、*Rel2* 與 *defensin* 的 qPCR 試驗，對照 BL21(DE3) 空載體組，做的理由是「我們想排除 *E. coli* 在蚊子幼蟲死亡中的作用」。\n\n這組試驗給出了結論，同時也自己交代了缺口。37 °C 誘導的那一組，團隊寫的是「這筆資料顯示，幼蟲致死試驗中觀察到的死亡並非由 BL21(DE3) 的導入所造成」——但同時也報告大多數免疫基因的轉錄其實完全沒有被調節。20 °C 的那一組，他們直接寫明自己做不到的事：「我們承認本研究的限制，因為我們沒有把 20 °C 隔夜生產的生物殺幼蟲毒蛋白拿去與 BL21(DE3) 比較……團隊在那段時間蚊子幼蟲數量不足，無法再增加實驗組。」**這個排除在其中一個誘導條件下做完了，在另一個條件下則被明白宣告沒做完**——這和 LC50 系列是同一個動作，那份不完整的實驗組也在同一頁上被揭露。讀者因此能確切知道這個主張延伸到哪裡為止。\n\n引誘劑那部分是同一套紀律。受孕雌蚊、三重複、各杯依位置輪換；發現位置偏誤後拿掉中央那一杯；接著懷疑甜菜根的顏色，於是把每一杯都用黑紙蓋住，「讓產卵位置的選擇只取決於氣味因素」，之後偏好仍然成立，p = 0.0003。**兩個混淆因子都由團隊自己找出來並排除，而且是在自己的標的物種上。** 那正是 2026 年亞軍走的深度路線，而 GEMS 在 2024 年就已經走過一次。","chips":["LC50 on the vector itself","empty-vector qPCR control","incomplete arm disclosed"],"chips_zh":["在病媒本身上測得 LC50","空載體 qPCR 對照","不完整的實驗組有揭露"]},{"kicker":"The headline gap","kicker_zh":"標題與內文的落差","title":"2026's landing page states the one thing its own results page withdraws","title_zh":"2026 年的首頁寫下了它自己的結果頁收回的那一件事","body":"The 2026 home page lists \"On-demand — Green light switches production on when the environmental sensors and forecasts decide to\" among five features of the machine, and the results page's second key result reads \"Light control — Green light switches ACCD on, and activity leads the protein by hours\". Three screens into the same page: **\"The ELISA showed no change over time.** ACCD was already present at the baseline (about 3.0 µg/mL before illumination) and measured 2.6 to 3.2 µg/mL at every time point under both colors ... indicating that the cultures produced ACCD but the amount did not rise with light\". The DNPH activity difference it falls back on has \"error bars overlapped at 3 h and 8 h\", and the explanation offered ends \"We have not tested this directly\". The reporter meant to make secretion visible failed outright: \"Despite repeated experiments, the medium remained colorless\".\n\n**The 2024 summary never does this.** Its nine items are hedged to their evidence in the sentence that makes them — \"**partially** proved the chromosome-free system\", and for the component that was never joined to the rest, \"Integration of our sticky ovitrap and recombinant biolarvicidal proteins **will be** a powerful vector control tool\". Both seasons left the chain unjoined. Only one of them put the unjoined link on the front page as a finished feature.","body_zh":"2026 年的首頁在機器的五項功能中列出「On-demand——當環境感測器與預測做出判斷時，綠光開啟生產」，而結果頁的第二條 Key results 寫的是「Light control——綠光開啟 ACCD，而活性比蛋白量早幾個小時出現」。往同一頁再走三個畫面：**「ELISA 顯示隨時間沒有變化。** ACCD 在基線就已經存在（照光前約 3.0 µg/mL），在兩種光色下的每一個時間點都量到 2.6 至 3.2 µg/mL……這表示菌液確實產生了 ACCD，但量並沒有隨光上升」。它退守的那個 DNPH 活性差異，「在 3 小時與 8 小時，誤差棒互相重疊」，而所提出的解釋結尾是「我們沒有直接檢驗過這一點」。原本要讓分泌看得見的報告子徹底失敗：「儘管反覆實驗，培養液始終無色」。\n\n**2024 年的摘要從來不這樣做。** 它那九條，在寫下它們的同一句話裡就緊貼著證據保留了空間——「**部分**證明了 chromosome-free system」；而對於從未與其他部分接起來的那個元件，寫的是「把我們的黏性產卵器與重組殺幼蟲毒蛋白整合起來，**將會**是一個強大的病媒防治工具」。兩個賽季都讓鏈條沒有接起來。但只有其中一個，把沒接起來的那一環當成完成的功能放上首頁。","chips":["front page: \"switches production on\"","results page: \"no change over time\""],"chips_zh":["首頁：「綠光開啟生產」","結果頁：「隨時間沒有變化」"]},{"kicker":"Where it does hold","kicker_zh":"它成立的地方","title":"2025 is the season the communication hypothesis actually fits, and it is the season with zero wins","title_zh":"溝通層假設真正吻合的是 2025 年，而那正是零獲獎的那一年","body":"2025 took a Top 10 place and a Gold medal, five nominations including Best Wiki, and **won nothing.** It is also the only season whose wiki still carries the iGEM template's own words. The home page headline reads \"Your iGEM Journey Begins Here! We wish you a successful and rewarding season!\", and the results page opens, above the team's own contents list, with \"Present the results of your project, along with a detailed analysis and discussion of their significance. Also outline future plans and reflections on the impact of your project.\" The home page's one big number renders as **\"The world generates 0 tons of textile waste every year\"** until a counter animation runs.\n\nThe results page carries 64 images but **restarts figure numbering in each of its six sections**, so \"Figure 3\" names four different figures on one page — \"Figure 3. Residual activity of (A) Variant 1\", \"Figure 3. The surface graph of the second high-throughput screening\", \"Figure 3. Comparison of enzymatic degradation of pure PET textiles\", \"Figure 3. Enzymatic degradation of PET from cotton-polyester blended fabrics\". And the awards page is gratitude prose with no number in it, as 2024's also is. **The presentation hypothesis survives for the trough, not for 2026.**","body_zh":"2025 年拿到 Top 10 名次與金牌、五項入圍（其中包含 Best Wiki），而**什麼都沒有拿到。** 它也是唯一一個 wiki 上還留著 iGEM 範本自己文字的賽季。首頁的標題寫著「你的 iGEM 旅程從這裡開始！祝你有一個成功而充實的賽季！」；而結果頁在團隊自己的目錄之上，開頭是「呈現你的專案結果，並附上對其意義的詳細分析與討論。也請列出未來計畫，以及對專案影響的反思。」首頁那個大數字，在計數動畫跑起來之前顯示為**「全世界每年產生 0 公噸紡織廢棄物」**。\n\n結果頁有 64 張圖，卻**在它的六個段落裡各自從 1 重新編號**，因此同一頁上「Figure 3」指的是四張不同的圖——一張是 Variant 1 的殘餘活性，一張是第二次高通量篩選的曲面圖，一張是純 PET 布料酵素降解的比較，還有一張是棉／聚酯混紡布料的 PET 酵素降解。而 awards 頁是一篇沒有任何數字的感謝文，2024 年那一頁也是。**呈現方式的假設在谷底那一年撐得住，在 2026 年撐不住。**","chips":["template text still on two pages","\"Figure 3\" names four figures","0 wins"],"chips_zh":["兩頁還留著範本文字","「Figure 3」指四張圖","0 個獲獎"]},{"kicker":"Real sample","kicker_zh":"真實樣本","title":"2024 ran a randomised household field trial, and published that the users disliked the trap","title_zh":"2024 年做了一次隨機分組的家戶實地試驗，並且公開使用者不喜歡那個捕蚊器","body":"Of 342 general-survey respondents, 84 volunteered, 58 were contactable, and 10 Taipei households were scheduled across two months from 3 August to 28 September, one week each, \"randomized into two different groups: those using only water and those that needed to add beetroot peel powder\". Returned sticky papers were sorted by species. The reporting is unflattering by choice: in one trial the paper \"caught 33 mosquitoes, but most of them were\" the wrong genus, \"only trial 12 caught 5\" *Aedes*, and on usefulness **\"only 6.7% of the users rated 5 out of 5\"** for effective and convenient. The team also states the limit plainly: \"There was no synthetic biology component involved throughout our field trial (we did not have them test our biolarvacides)\".\n\n2025's ladder is the same instinct in the lab, running from the model substrate pNPB up to commercial 35:65, 55:45 and 65:35 cotton-PET blended textiles, and reporting the reversal it found: \"the prior removal of cotton inhibited the most active enzymes\". **2026 reached real plants but not the reactor's own output** — the preparation sprayed was never assayed. Across the three seasons the thing that got further from the real target is the engineered component, not the wiki.","body_zh":"一般問卷 342 份回覆中，84 人願意參與，58 人聯絡得上，最後排定台北 10 個家戶，從 8 月 3 日到 9 月 28 日橫跨兩個月、每戶一週，「隨機分成兩組：一組只用水，另一組要加入甜菜根皮粉」。收回的黏紙按物種分類。這份報告是刻意不好看的：某一次試驗的黏紙「抓到 33 隻蚊子，但大多數是」錯的屬，「只有第 12 次試驗抓到 5 隻」*Aedes*；而在好用程度上，**「只有 6.7% 的使用者給了 5 分滿分」**，認為它有效又方便。團隊也明白寫出限制：「我們的實地試驗全程沒有涉及任何合成生物學成分（我們沒有讓他們測試殺幼蟲劑）」。\n\n2025 年那道階梯是同一種本能，只是在實驗室裡：從模型底物 pNPB 一路爬到市售 35:65、55:45 與 65:35 的棉／PET 混紡布料，並且報告了它找到的反轉：「先移除棉反而抑制了活性最強的那些酵素」。**2026 年碰到了真實植物，卻沒有碰到反應器自己的產物**——噴上去的那份製備從未被檢測活性。三個賽季下來，離真實標的越來越遠的是那個被工程化的元件，不是 wiki。","chips":["10 households, 2 months","randomised into two arms","6.7% rated it 5 of 5"],"chips_zh":["10 個家戶、2 個月","隨機分成兩組","6.7% 給 5 分滿分"]},{"kicker":"Executive layer","kicker_zh":"總覽層","title":"No season answers the award criteria one by one — and 2026 comes closest by a distance","title_zh":"沒有一個賽季逐條回答獎項標準——而 2026 年遠遠最接近","body":"The Best Wiki winners studied elsewhere in this report answer each medal and award criterion in a few sentences and deep-link the evidence. **None of the three GEMS seasons does that.** 2024's `/awards` and 2025's `/awards` are both gratitude prose and nothing else; 2026 has no awards page at all, with `/awards`, `/judging` and `/medals` all returning 404.\n\nBut 2026 publishes the nearest thing any of the three has: a `/development` page that names five stages, states the functional requirement and the evidence needed for each, and then grades them — \"Detect, Forecast & Activate — Detection and forecast met; activation waits on green light\", \"Produce — Five of six rows met\", \"Contain — All four met\", \"Protect — Three of four met\". Its results page opens with an abstract and five key results and then runs `Endpoint / Tested on / Result / State` tables marked \"Measured\" or \"Partial\". **If the executive layer is what judges reward, 2026 should have scored higher than 2024, and it did not.** Deep linking is the one gap left: the 2026 results page carries only three links to other pages in 14,762 words.","body_zh":"本報告別處研究過的 Best Wiki 得主，會用幾句話逐條回答每一項獎牌與獎項標準，並把證據以深層連結指過去。**GEMS 三個賽季都沒有這樣做。** 2024 年的 `/awards` 與 2025 年的 `/awards` 都只是感謝文，別無其他；2026 年完全沒有 awards 頁，`/awards`、`/judging` 與 `/medals` 全部回傳 404。\n\n但 2026 年發表了三者之中最接近的東西：一個 `/development` 頁，列出五個階段，逐一寫出功能要求與所需證據，然後為它們評分——偵測與預測達標、啟動仍等著綠光；生產六項達成五項；圍阻四項全數達成；保護四項達成三項。它的結果頁以摘要與五條 Key results 開場，接著是一連串 `Endpoint / Tested on / Result / State` 表格，標記為「Measured」或「Partial」。**如果評審獎勵的是總覽層，2026 年本該比 2024 年得分更高，而它沒有。** 深層連結是唯一還留著的缺口：2026 年的結果頁在 14,762 字之中，只有三個連到其他頁面的連結。","chips":["no criterion page in any season","2026: /development grades five stages","3 outbound links in 14,762 words"],"chips_zh":["三年都沒有標準對照頁","2026：/development 為五階段評分","14,762 字中 3 個外連"]}],"table":{"head":["Season","Placing and awards","Headline shape","p-values / named tests","Dispersion and replicates","Central mechanism evidenced?","Readable without scripts"],"head_zh":["賽季","名次與獎項","招牌形式","p 值／檢定名稱","離散度與重複數","核心機制有證據嗎？","無腳本可讀"],"rows":[["**2024**","**Grand Prize**, Finalist, Top 10, Gold; 3 wins (Wiki, New Basic Part, Promotion Video), 3 nominations","**Nine** numbered achievements on /description; **no results page exists**","**1** p-value (0.0003) / **none**","`Mortality ± SE (%)`; triplicates throughout, 10 larvae per cup, 98 larvae examined","**Yes** — LC50 for three toxins on live *Aedes albopictus* larvae, with an empty-vector qPCR arm run to exclude *E. coli*","**No** — 577-byte shell, whole site in one 1.69 MB bundle"],["**2025**","Top 10, Gold; **0 wins**, 5 nominations (Measurement, Model, Education, Wiki, Village)","**Thirteen** bullets under four module headings; iGEM template text still above them","**0** / **none**","Standard error named 23 times; triplicate, five replicates per RSM condition","Partly — activity shown on pNPB, then on real PET film, pure PET textile and commercial cotton-PET blends; the cotton-removal step reversed","Yes"],["**2026**","Top 10, Gold, **not a Finalist**; 3 wins (Measurement, Hardware, Integrated Human Practices), 3 nominations","**Five** key results plus an abstract; /development grades five stages against pre-stated criteria","**5** / **none**","SEM; R² 0.992-0.9995; a 90% interval registered 13 days ahead; `n=1` and `n=3`","**No** — ELISA flat at 2.6-3.2 µg/mL under both colours, AmilCP medium stayed colourless, all biology from the constitutive bypass","Yes"]],"rows_zh":[["**2024**","**總冠軍**、決賽隊伍、Top 10、金牌；3 個獲獎（Wiki、New Basic Part、Promotion Video）、3 項入圍","/description 上**九條**編號成果；**不存在結果頁**","**1** 個 p 值（0.0003）／**無**","`Mortality ± SE (%)`；全程三重複、每杯 10 隻幼蟲、檢視 98 隻","**有**——三種毒蛋白在活的 *Aedes albopictus* 幼蟲上測得 LC50，並以空載體 qPCR 組排除 *E. coli*","**否**——577 位元組外殼，整站裝在一個 1.69 MB 套件裡"],["**2025**","Top 10、金牌；**0 個獲獎**、5 項入圍（Measurement、Model、Education、Wiki、Village）","四個模組標題底下**十三條**；上方還留著 iGEM 範本文字","**0** ／**無**","二十三次寫出標準誤；三重複，RSM 每個條件五個重複","部分——先在 pNPB 上證明活性，再到真實 PET 薄膜、純 PET 布料與市售棉／PET 混紡；移除棉之後出現反轉","是"],["**2026**","Top 10、金牌、**非決賽隊伍**；3 個獲獎（Measurement、Hardware、Integrated Human Practices）、3 項入圍","**五條** key results 加一段摘要；/development 以事先寫下的標準為五個階段評分","**5** ／**無**","SEM；R² 0.992-0.9995；一個提早 13 天登記的 90% 區間；`n=1` 與 `n=3`","**沒有**——ELISA 在兩種光色下都平在 2.6-3.2 µg/mL，AmilCP 的培養液始終無色，所有生物學成果來自組成型旁路","是"]]},"checklist":["Stop treating a Finalist slate as unprecedented for this team. GEMS won the 2024 Grand Prize, and the honest question for 2027 is what the 2024 project had, not whether the bar is reachable.","Do not spend 2027 rebuilding the wiki. By every measure taken here the 2026 site already beats the Best Wiki winner of 2024: server-rendered, five times the p-values, uniquely numbered figures, and a page that grades its own stages.","Name the target organism or material in week one and plan every central assay on it. 2024 measured LC50 on live Aedes albopictus larvae; 2026 measured the sprayed preparation on plants but never assayed the preparation.","Write the rival explanation down and run the experiment that kills it. 2024 ran an empty-vector qPCR arm specifically to rule out E. coli; nothing in 2026 plays that role for the light-gated device.","Hunt your own confounds and publish the hunt. Position bias, then colour bias, eliminated one after the other is why the 2024 attractant claim survives at p = 0.0003.","Name a statistical test. Zero named tests in three seasons means every 'significant' the team has ever written is unattributed, and this is the cheapest fix on the list.","Hold the front page to the results page. Before anything ships, check that every claim on the home page and in the key-results block is one the body of the wiki still supports three screens later.","Delete every line of iGEM template text before August. In the zero-win season it was still sitting on both the home page and the top of the results page."],"checklist_zh":["不要再把決賽席位當成這支隊伍前所未有的事。GEMS 拿過 2024 年總冠軍，2027 年真正該問的是 2024 年那個專案擁有什麼，而不是這道門檻能不能跨過。","不要把 2027 年花在重做 wiki 上。依本頁採用的每一項量測，2026 年的網站已經勝過 2024 年的 Best Wiki 得主：伺服器端渲染、p 值多五倍、圖號不重複，還有一頁為自己的階段評分。","第一週就把標的生物或標的材料定下來，並且讓每一項核心試驗都做在它身上。2024 年在活的 Aedes albopictus 幼蟲上量到 LC50；2026 年把噴劑用在植物上，卻從未檢測那份噴劑。","把對手解釋寫下來，然後做掉它的那個實驗。2024 年刻意做了一組空載體 qPCR 來排除 E. coli；2026 年沒有任何東西為光控裝置扮演這個角色。","獵捕自己的混淆因子，並且把這場獵捕公開。先排除位置偏誤、再排除顏色偏誤，正是 2024 年引誘劑的主張能以 p = 0.0003 撐住的原因。","寫出統計檢定的名稱。三個賽季零個檢定名稱，意思是這支隊伍寫過的每一個「significant」都沒有依據可追，而這是清單上最便宜的一項修正。","讓首頁對結果頁負責。任何東西上線之前，確認首頁與 Key results 區塊上的每一個主張，在往下三個畫面之後，wiki 的內文仍然支持它。","八月之前把 iGEM 範本文字一行不留地刪掉。在零獲獎的那個賽季，它還同時留在首頁與結果頁的最上方。"],"method":"Fetched with curl and a browser User-Agent on 20 November 2026. 2025 and 2026 are server-rendered and were read directly: https://2025.igem.wiki/gems-taiwan/ and /results, /awards, /description, /experiments, /measurement; https://2026.igem.wiki/gems-taiwan/ and /results, /development, /description, /experiments, /measurement, plus static/assets/data/site-nav.js for the page list. 2026/awards, 2026/judging and 2026/medals all return 404. The 2024 wiki is a single-page application: https://2024.igem.wiki/gems-taiwan/ returns 577 bytes and /results is a 404, so the route table and all page text were extracted from the bundle at /gems-taiwan/static/js/main.8a37e754.js (1,690,501 bytes), which has no code splitting and fetches no data at runtime, meaning the bundle contains the whole site; the browser pane was not needed. All text was html.unescape-ed before matching, because pages write p &lt; 0.0001. Named tests were matched on t-test, ANOVA, Tukey, Dunnett, Welch, Mann-Whitney, Wilcoxon and Kruskal with word boundaries, never on a bare \"t test\", since every such hit in 2026 was the ordinary word tested. Counts are floors, not totals: a test named only inside a figure image, a PDF or a collapsed panel is invisible to this method, and the 2024 figures live in 488 images on static.igem.wiki that were not read. The scopes are not identical and cannot be: 2024 has no results page, so its counts are for the whole site, which makes them a generous bound, while 2025 and 2026 are counted on /results. This is one team with one data point per season. The cohort, the judges and the project change completely every year, a Best Wiki nomination rather than a win may only mean a stronger field, and nothing here supports a causal claim about what any award was given or withheld for. Question 9, the live judging session, leaves no public record and is excluded, as it is everywhere on this tab. GEMS-Taiwan is the report author's own team and the same six questions were put to it as to the other nine teams in the cohort section.","method_zh":"2026 年 11 月 20 日以 curl 搭配瀏覽器 User-Agent 取得。2025 與 2026 年是伺服器端渲染，直接讀取：https://2025.igem.wiki/gems-taiwan/ 以及 /results、/awards、/description、/experiments、/measurement；https://2026.igem.wiki/gems-taiwan/ 以及 /results、/development、/description、/experiments、/measurement，另外取 static/assets/data/site-nav.js 來得到頁面清單。2026/awards、2026/judging 與 2026/medals 全部回傳 404。2024 年的 wiki 是一個單頁式應用程式：https://2024.igem.wiki/gems-taiwan/ 回傳 577 位元組，/results 是 404，因此路由表與所有頁面文字都是從 /gems-taiwan/static/js/main.8a37e754.js（1,690,501 位元組）這個套件中抽出來的；該套件沒有程式碼分割，執行期間也不抓取資料，意即整個網站都在套件裡，因此不需要使用瀏覽器面板。所有文字在比對前都先做過 html.unescape，因為頁面會把小於號寫成轉義字元。檢定名稱是以 t-test、ANOVA、Tukey、Dunnett、Welch、Mann-Whitney、Wilcoxon 與 Kruskal 搭配完整字詞界線來比對，絕不以單純的「t test」比對，因為 2026 年所有這類命中都是普通字 tested。這些計數是下界，不是總數：若某個檢定名稱只出現在圖片、PDF 或折疊面板裡，這個方法就看不到它；而 2024 年的圖存放在 static.igem.wiki 上的 488 個影像檔中，並未讀取。各年的範圍並不一致，而且不可能一致：2024 年沒有結果頁，因此它的計數涵蓋整站，這對它是寬鬆的上限；2025 與 2026 年則只計 /results。這是一支隊伍、每個賽季一個資料點。群體、評審與專案每一年都完全改變，Best Wiki 是入圍而非獲獎，也可能只代表當年對手更強；本頁沒有任何內容足以支撐關於「某個獎為什麼頒出或為什麼沒頒」的因果主張。第 9 題現場問答沒有留下公開紀錄，在此排除，與本分頁其他各處一致。GEMS-Taiwan 是本報告作者自己的團隊，與群體那一節的其他九支隊伍一樣，被問了同樣六個問題。"},{"id":"findings-index","tab":"overview","kicker":"Start here","kicker_zh":"從這裡開始","title":"31 findings, and where to read each one","title_zh":"31 個發現，以及各自該讀哪一頁","lede":"The 2026 Best Wiki winners all build a layer like this — each claim in two sentences, with a link straight to the evidence. It works, so this report does it too.","lede_zh":"2026 年所有最佳 Wiki 得主都建了一層像這樣的東西——每個主張兩句話，附上直達證據的連結。它有效，所以這份報告也這麼做。","cards":[{"kicker":"Modelling","kicker_zh":"建模","title":"Closing the model–data loop is the single best predictor of a Top 10","title_zh":"閉合模型與資料的迴圈，是 Top 10 最強的單一預測因子","body":"Teams that both fit a model to their own measured data and validate it against something held back reached a Top 10 at **53%**; teams that did not, at **23%** — less than half the rate. All nine who closed the loop without a Top 10 won or were nominated for a major special prize anyway. It needs no GPU and no licence.","body_zh":"既以自身量測資料擬合模型、又用保留資料加以驗證的團隊，進入 Top 10 的比例是 **53%**；沒有這麼做的則是 **23%**，不到一半。閉合了迴圈卻未進 Top 10 的那九支，全都拿下或入圍了重要特別獎。這件事不需要 GPU，也不需要授權。","chips":["53% vs 23%"],"chips_zh":["53% 對 23%"],"link":"drylab"},{"kicker":"High school","kicker_zh":"高中組","title":"At high-school level the gap is evaluation discipline, not tools","title_zh":"在高中層級，差距在評估紀律，不在工具","body":"Eton-College-UK used logistic regression and a PSSM but ran cluster-aware cross-validation, a label-shuffle control and an ablation. Lambert-GA won Best Model for benchmarking the confidence metrics themselves and publishing that its own hit was not top-scoring. GCGS reached the Top 10 with no model page at all.","body_zh":"Eton-College-UK 用的是 logistic regression 與 PSSM，但做了分群感知的交叉驗證、標籤洗牌對照與消融測試。Lambert-GA 拿下最佳模型，是因為他們對信心指標本身做了基準測試，並公開自己成功的設計其實分數不是最高的。GCGS 則在完全沒有 model 頁的情況下進入 Top 10。","chips":["all free tools"],"chips_zh":["全是免費工具"],"link":"drylab"},{"kicker":"Falsification","kicker_zh":"否證","title":"Running the experiment that could break your own claim is a floor, not a ranking — and GEMS already clears it","title_zh":"做一個可能推翻自己主張的實驗，是一道門檻，不是一張名次表——而 GEMS 早就跨過了","body":"The real-target finding has a second half — the rival explanation experimentally excluded — and measuring it across all 30 Top 10 wikis broke it. **26 of 30** ran an experiment designed expressly to kill a rival explanation, and **30 of 30** published a result unfavourable to their own headline, so the practice cannot separate a podium from a Top 10. Podium teams average 4.29 of the five control types against 3.61 (gap 0.68, permutation p = 0.079 — not a result). What survives is a floor: no podium team scored below 4, while 10 of 23 others did. **And the counting is not the mechanism — of the seven teams with all five types, five missed the podium, GEMS-Taiwan among them with a perfect score.** The scarce habits are the harder two: 17 of 30 removed a confound by design and re-tested, 12 of 30 validated against held-back data.","body_zh":"「打在真實標的上」這項發現還有另一半——對手解釋有沒有被實驗排除掉——而把 30 支 Top 10 隊伍的 wiki 全部讀完之後，這一半不成立。**30 支中有 26 支**做過刻意設計來殺掉自家結果另一種解釋的實驗，**30 支全部**公開過一項對自己主張不利的結果，所以這個習慣分不出頒獎臺和前十。頒獎臺隊伍平均擁有五類對照中的 4.29 類，其餘是 3.61 類（差距 0.68，置換檢定 p = 0.079——不構成結果）。留下來的是一道門檻：沒有任何頒獎臺隊伍低於 4 類，而其餘 23 支中有 10 支低於 4 類。**而這個計數並不是機制——五類全有的七支隊伍裡，有五支沒上頒獎臺，GEMS-Taiwan 就是其中一支，而且是滿分。**真正稀少的是較難的兩類：30 支中只有 17 支以設計移除混淆因子後重測，只有 12 支拿留存資料做驗證。","chips":["26 of 30","30 of 30 unfavourable","GEMS scores 5 of 5"],"chips_zh":["30 支中 26 支","30 支全部登出不利結果","GEMS 五類全有"],"link":"drylab"},{"kicker":"Claim integrity","kicker_zh":"主張誠實度","title":"Over-claiming on the landing page is the Top 10 norm, and the podium does it slightly more","title_zh":"首頁誇大是 Top 10 的常態，而頒獎臺隊伍還稍微誇得更兇","body":"Every 2026 Top 10 landing page was read against the team's own evidence page and scored 0 to 3. **21 of 29 scorable teams assert more than their own results support.** The expectation was that the gap would track placing; it reversed — the podium averages **1.43** against **1.00** for everyone else, two of the four teams contradicted by their own pages are podium teams, and the three Grand Prize winners score 0, 1 and 1. Princeton's hero tile reads \"450 nm — LIGHT-TRIGGERED RELEASE\" while its experiments page says \"The phage version described above is the step we have not yet run\". **GEMS-Taiwan is joint-worst at 3** and the only team in thirty whose contradiction spans three of its own pages. So closing this buys credibility, not a placing — and one team reached the Top 10 with no results page at all.","body_zh":"2026 年每一支 Top 10 隊伍的首頁，都拿去對照該隊自己的證據頁，並以 0 到 3 評分。**29 支可評分的隊伍中有 21 支，主張超過自己結果撐得住的範圍。**原本的預期是落差會與名次相關；結果反轉了——頒獎臺平均 **1.43**，其餘隊伍 **1.00**；四支被自己頁面反駁的隊伍裡有兩支在頒獎臺上；三支總冠軍的分數是 0、1、1。Princeton 的首頁大字寫著「450 nm——光觸發釋放」，而它的實驗頁寫著「上述的噬菌體版本，是我們還沒做的那一步」。**GEMS-Taiwan 以 3 分並列最差**，而且是三十支裡唯一一支矛盾橫跨自己三個頁面的隊伍。所以補起這個落差買到的是可信度，不是名次——而且有一支隊伍根本沒有結果頁就進了 Top 10。","chips":["21 of 29 over-claim","podium 1.43 vs 1.00","GEMS joint-worst at 3"],"chips_zh":["29 支中 21 支誇大","頒獎臺 1.43 對 1.00","GEMS 以 3 分並列最差"],"link":"judging"},{"kicker":"Software","kicker_zh":"軟體","title":"8 of 21 award-winning tools are still usable, and the reason is hosting","title_zh":"21 個得獎工具中有 8 個仍可使用，原因是「有沒有架站」","body":"Every live tool was hosted on wiki-freeze day; every source-only tool's wiki lists localhost as its only address. Not a coding or budget decision — a hosting decision made months early. Two high-school teams out-shipped most of the universities. Stars and forks across every repo checked: zero.","body_zh":"每一個仍在線的工具，在 wiki 凍結當日就已經上線；每一個只有原始碼的工具，wiki 上唯一的位址都是 localhost。這不是寫程式或預算的決定，而是提前好幾個月做的架站決定。兩支高中隊伍交付得比多數大學還好。所有檢查過的 repository，star 與 fork 都是零。","chips":["hosted on freeze day"],"chips_zh":["凍結日當天已架站"],"link":"drylab"},{"kicker":"Visualisation","kicker_zh":"視覺化","title":"The best figures build the reader's doubt into the picture","title_zh":"最好的圖，把讀者的懷疑畫進圖裡","body":"GEMS-Taiwan's provenance rail turns amber exactly where measurement stops and modelling begins. DKU gives \"not assessed\" its own verdict so an unmeasured gate cannot read as a passed one. Mingdao's captions carry the instrument, the buffer, the replicate count and a link to the raw CSV. DTU shows which stakeholders never replied.","body_zh":"GEMS-Taiwan 的來源軌道，正好在量測結束、模擬開始之處轉為琥珀色。DKU 給「未評估」一個自己的判定，讓未量測的關卡不會被讀成通過。Mingdao 的圖說載明儀器、緩衝液、重複次數，並連結原始 CSV。DTU 則把從未回覆的利害關係人也顯示出來。","chips":["provenance visible","\"not assessed\" as a state"],"chips_zh":["來源看得見","「未評估」也是一種狀態"],"link":"drylab"},{"kicker":"Leverage","kicker_zh":"放大器","title":"Seven teams in 106 taught the people who teach for a living, and one team did the whole thing","title_zh":"106 支裡有 7 支把課上給以教學為業的人，而把整件事做完的只有一支","body":"The multiplier nobody used. Across 106 decorated teams, **7 taught an audience that teaches professionally** and **5 left equipment or a kit in somebody else's hands** — and **only HongKong-JSS did both**, pairing a two-day PCR and agarose-gel workshop for 30 local school teachers with a standing loan of DNA samples and lab equipment, then adding a civic tier on top. Its own wiki calls that the most durable of its four tiers, against the 1,600 pupils and 730 secondary peers it reached once. Both counts are upper bounds on rarity, since a move not written up is invisible. By contrast, standing in front of a stakeholder who can veto you is the house style of this field, not a rarity. The other transferable moves: Stanford converted a 5,000-application, 230-place mentorship into a free course; Princeton handed the public a real unsolved sub-problem and got 42 submissions of which 26 passed printability screening; NIS Almaty-Medeu trained teachers across a 70-school network until nine partner schools ran the activities themselves.","body_zh":"沒有人用的那個放大器。106 支得獎隊伍中，**有 7 支把課上給以教學為業的對象**，**有 5 支把器材或套件留在別人手上**——而**兩件都做的只有 HongKong-JSS**：為 30 位本地學校教師辦兩天 PCR 與瓊脂膠體電泳工作坊，再搭配 DNA 樣品與實驗設備的常設借用方案，然後在上面又加了一層公民參與。他們自己的 wiki 把這一層稱為四層之中最耐久的，相對於只接觸一次的 1,600 位小學生與 730 位中學同儕。這兩個數字都只是稀有度的上限，因為沒寫出來的做法就看不到。相對地，站到一位能否決你的關係人面前，是這個領域的標準做法，不是稀罕事。其他可以照搬的做法：Stanford 把 5,000 份申請、230 個名額的導師制轉成一門免費課程；Princeton 把一個真正未解的子問題交給大眾，收到 42 份投稿、其中 26 份通過可列印性篩選；NIS Almaty-Medeu 在 70 校網絡裡持續培訓教師，直到九所夥伴學校能自行開辦。","chips":["7 of 106 trained trainers","5 of 106 left equipment","only 1 did both"],"chips_zh":["106 支中 7 支訓練師資","106 支中 5 支留下器材","兩件都做的只有 1 支"],"link":"picks"},{"kicker":"Science for Good","kicker_zh":"Science for Good","title":"The deadline, not the people, is what limits Science for Good","title_zh":"限制 Science for Good 的是截止日，不是人","body":"8 of 21 award-winning software tools still run, every repository checked has zero stars and zero forks, no team in 106 ran an inter-lab measurement ring, and only nine or ten of 71 closed loops were closed by a non-expert. These are deadline artefacts. GEMS's answer is a **club-form programme with no deadline**, carrying a few problems across years — its definition, criteria and current pipeline are on this tab.","body_zh":"21 個得獎軟體工具中有 8 個還能跑，所有檢查過的程式庫星數與分支數皆為零，106 支隊伍沒有一支做過跨實驗室量測環，71 個閉合的迴路中只有九到十個是與非專業人士閉合的。這些都是截止日造成的。GEMS 的回應是一個**沒有截止日的社團式長期計畫**，讓幾個題目跨年走下去——它的定義、條件與目前的題目清單都在這一頁。","chips":["a programme, not a category"],"chips_zh":["是計畫，不是獎項類別"],"link":"good"},{"kicker":"Governance","kicker_zh":"治理","title":"The exit rule is the one a club never writes, and it is the one that decides whether the programme lives","title_zh":"退場規則是社團從來不會寫的那一條，而它決定了這個計畫活不活","body":"Entry rules are easy and everybody writes them. This report already measured what happens without an exit rule: of 78 readable returning teams, **5 carried a problem forward**, none of the six returning Grand Prize teams did, and only **3 of 106** credit their predecessor. A programme cannot learn whether carrying a problem works until it records the ones it dropped — and nobody in the field records those. So the Science for Good pipeline now has an entry bar (a named person outside GEMS who described the problem in their own words before anyone offered them anything, one number that would move, a named operator, and the cost of the tenth deployment against the first), **five named exits of which only one is success**, a cap of five live slots that binds entry to exit, a six-line handover, and a listening-visit instrument of fourteen questions that opens on \"walk me through yesterday\" rather than on the word problem.","body_zh":"入列規則很容易，每個社團都會寫。沒有退場規則會發生什麼事，這份報告已經量過了：78 支前一年專案查得到的回鍋隊伍裡，**只有 5 支把題目帶了下去**，六支回鍋的總冠軍級隊伍一支也沒有，而 106 支之中只有 **3 支**對自己的前一屆表示過感謝。一個計畫要學會「把題目帶下去到底有沒有用」，前提是它記錄了那些被放掉的題目——而這個領域裡沒有人在記錄。所以科學向善的清單現在有了入列門檻（一位 GEMS 以外的具名人士，在任何人向他提出任何東西之前用自己的話描述過這個問題；一個會動的數字；一位具名的操作者；以及第十次佈署相對第一次的成本），**五條具名的出路，其中只有一條叫成功**，五個名額的上限把入列綁在退場上，六行交接，以及一套十四題的傾聽訪談工具——它的第一題是「帶我走過昨天」，而不是「你有什麼問題」。","chips":["5 exits, 1 is success","5 live slots","14 questions"],"chips_zh":["五條出路，一條叫成功","五個名額","十四個問題"],"link":"good"},{"kicker":"Human practices","kicker_zh":"人類實踐","title":"The loops that closed were closed by experts, not by publics","title_zh":"真正閉合的迴圈，是專家閉合的，不是公眾","body":"Of all 106 decorated teams, **71** can point at a stakeholder who visibly changed the design. But almost every one of those stakeholders was a credentialled technical expert. The publics, patients and communities the criterion is rhetorically about changed the vocabulary and not the vector, with **nine or ten exceptions in 106**. (The first pass scored 93 files and found 64 and six-to-seven; the figures here are the recount on the closed set.)","body_zh":"在全部 106 支獲獎隊伍中，有 **71** 支能指出一位明顯改變了設計的利害關係人。但這些利害關係人幾乎全是具備專業資格的技術專家。這個評審標準修辭上所指向的公眾、病人與社群，改變的是詞彙而不是方向——**106 支中只有九到十個例外**。（第一輪評的是 93 份檔案，得到 64 支與六到七個例外；這裡的數字是集合封閉後的重算。）","chips":["71 of 106","9–10 exceptions"],"chips_zh":["71/106","9 至 10 個例外"],"link":"good"},{"kicker":"Engagement","kicker_zh":"公眾參與","title":"The best education work was designed from data and measured like an experiment","title_zh":"最好的教育工作，是從資料設計、像實驗一樣量測的","body":"UCAS-China made compliance the target after a 461-person questionnaire, not awareness. GU Frankfurt sent nineteen members to a professional science-communication course first. Oxford built a podcast that deliberately pairs stakeholders who disagree. And the sharpest teams publish the lesson that failed.","body_zh":"UCAS-China 在做完 461 人的問卷後，把目標設為服藥遵從性，而不是認知提升。GU Frankfurt 先送 19 位成員去上專業的科學傳播課程。Oxford 做了一個刻意把意見相左者配對的 podcast。而最犀利的團隊，會把失敗的那堂課也公布出來。","chips":["survey-designed","measured"],"chips_zh":["從問卷設計","量過成效"],"link":"good"},{"kicker":"Commercial","kicker_zh":"商業","title":"The credible commercial sections published a model showing their own product losing","title_zh":"可信的商業章節，都公開了顯示自家產品輸掉的模型","body":"Worldshaper-Shanghai reports a negative NPV for its own enzyme. DTU-Denmark's LCA finds cement co-processing beats its route on almost every indicator, then converts each loss into an engineering target. Stockholm dismantled its venture when the safety board killed open-water release — and won the Safety and Security Award.","body_zh":"Worldshaper-Shanghai 報告自家酵素得出負的 NPV。DTU-Denmark 的 LCA 發現水泥共處理在幾乎每項指標上都勝過他們的路線，接著把每一項落敗轉成工程目標。Stockholm 在安全委員會否決開放水域釋放後拆掉了自己的創業計畫——然後拿下安全與保安獎。","chips":["negative NPV, published"],"chips_zh":["NPV 為負，照樣公開"],"link":"good"},{"kicker":"Wiki craft","kicker_zh":"Wiki 工藝","title":"Best Wiki winners ship an executive layer, not better graphics","title_zh":"最佳 Wiki 得主交付的是一個導讀層，不是更漂亮的圖","body":"Three of the four serve text that is readable before any script runs; the fourth mirrors every page as Markdown. All four build a layer that answers each medal criterion in two or three sentences and deep-links the evidence, failures included. Dark mode, late alt-text sweeps and mascot systems correlate with nothing.","body_zh":"四位得主中有三位提供的文字在任何程式執行前就可閱讀；第四位則把每一頁都鏡像為 Markdown。四位都建了一層用兩三句話回答每項獎牌標準、並直接深連到證據（含失敗）的導讀層。深色模式、最後才補的替代文字、吉祥物系統，則與得獎毫無相關。","chips":["text before JS","/judging page"],"chips_zh":["先給文字，再跑 JS","/judging 頁"],"link":"teams"},{"kicker":"Taiwan","kicker_zh":"台灣","title":"Taiwan won well, but only in the high-school tier","title_zh":"台灣贏得不錯，但只贏在高中組","body":"Thirteen competing teams returned six award wins — more than any East Asian territory except China, and more than Hong Kong on fewer teams. But every technical award came from the high-school tier, there were zero nominations in any parts award and zero in Best Software, and Hong Kong tripled Taiwan's Top 10 count.","body_zh":"13 支參賽隊伍拿下 6 座獎項——多於中國以外的任何東亞地區，而且以更少的隊伍數超越香港。但所有技術類獎項都來自高中組，在任何元件獎與最佳軟體上都掛零，而香港的 Top 10 席次是台灣的三倍。","chips":["13 teams · 6 wins"],"chips_zh":["13 隊 · 6 項大獎"],"link":"teams"},{"kicker":"Human practices","kicker_zh":"人文實踐","title":"The divide is not medical versus agricultural — it is platform versus applied","title_zh":"分界不在醫療與農業之間，而在平台與應用之間","body":"Therapeutics teams close loops with non-experts about as often as bioremediation teams do. What actually separates the field is whether anyone outside a lab ever operates the thing: the five platform villages — Foundational Advance, Space, Software & AI, Biomanufacturing, Fashion & Cosmetics — closed **26 loops between them and only 2 involved a non-expert**, against **14 of 45** across the applied villages.","body_zh":"治療類團隊與生物復育類團隊，和非專業人士閉合迴路的頻率其實差不多。真正分開這個領域的，是有沒有實驗室以外的人實際操作這個東西：五個平台類賽道——Foundational Advance、Space、Software & AI、Biomanufacturing、Fashion & Cosmetics——合計閉合了 **26 條迴路，其中只有 2 條牽涉非專業者**，應用類賽道則是 **45 條之中有 14 條**。","chips":["2 of 26 loops vs 14 of 45"],"chips_zh":["迴路 2/26 對 14/45"],"link":"good"},{"kicker":"Collaboration","kicker_zh":"合作","title":"Nobody ran an inter-lab measurement ring — in a competition about measurement","title_zh":"沒有任何一支隊伍做過跨實驗室量測環——在一個以量測為核心的競賽裡","body":"69 of 106 decorated teams record working with another team, but almost all of it is meet-ups. **Not one** ran an inter-lab measurement ring, and collaboration does not predict placing: substantive collaborators reached a Top 10 at 29%, attendance-only teams at 48%. The one team that offered to do real shared work publicly got **zero replies** — and won Best Software and Best Wiki anyway.","body_zh":"106 支得獎隊伍中有 69 支記錄了與其他隊伍的合作，但幾乎全是 meet-up。**沒有任何一支**做過跨實驗室量測環；而且合作並不預測名次：有實質合作的隊伍進入 Top 10 的比例是 29%，只去參加聚會的反而是 48%。唯一公開提議要做真正共同工作的那支隊伍，**一封回覆都沒有收到**——卻仍拿下最佳軟體與最佳 Wiki。","chips":["69 of 106","0 measurement rings"],"chips_zh":["69/106","0 個量測環"],"link":"teams"},{"kicker":"Biosafety","kicker_zh":"生物安全","title":"Nobody measured an escape rate","title_zh":"沒有人量過逸出率","body":"19 of 106 decorated teams describe a genetic containment device. **Zero** report a measured escape frequency, and only two name a DNA-synthesis screening regime. The sharpest result in the category is a negative one: the Safety winner found that a published Addgene kill switch failed first, weeks before its own circuits.","body_zh":"106 支得獎隊伍中有 19 支描述了基因層級的圍堵裝置。**沒有一支**報告量測到的逸出頻率，只有兩支指名了 DNA 合成訂單的篩查機制。這個類別最銳利的結果是一個負面結果：安全獎得主發現，一個已發表的 Addgene 自殺開關比他們自己的電路更早失效，而且早了好幾週。","chips":["0 of 106","2 name a screening regime"],"chips_zh":["0/106","2 支寫出篩查機制"],"link":"good"},{"kicker":"Parts","kicker_zh":"元件","title":"Winning parts are won on documentation, not on novelty","title_zh":"得獎元件靠的是文件，不是新穎性","body":"Winners' headline parts carry **10,388 to 83,030 characters** of registry documentation across three to six typed documents; sampled nominee parts carry 440 to 2,500, usually Design only. The high-school basic-part winner is a 247 bp native promoter copied from GenBank. Both improved-part awards had **zero nominees** — the cheapest category in iGEM to enter.","body_zh":"得獎隊伍的代表元件在註冊庫上帶著 **10,388 到 83,030 個字元**的文件，分布在三到六份分類文件中；抽樣的入圍元件則是 440 到 2,500 字，通常只有 Design 一項。高中組基礎元件得主是一段從 GenBank 複製來的 247 bp 原生啟動子。兩個改良元件獎項都是**零入圍**——那是 iGEM 裡最便宜的參賽門檻。","chips":["83,030 vs 440 characters","improved part: 0 nominees"],"chips_zh":["83,030 對 440 字元","改良元件：0 入圍"],"link":"teams"},{"kicker":"Measurement","kicker_zh":"量測","title":"Measurement discipline does not win anything — do it anyway","title_zh":"量測紀律贏不到任何東西——但還是要做","body":"Across 39 wikis read directly: 97% show a blank control, 72% calibrate into an absolute unit, but only **15%** compute a limit of detection for their own assay and **5%** ever measure one sample twice. And it does not predict placing: over all 106 files, teams mentioning calibration reached a Top 10 at 27% against 29%. **No effect.** The Best Measurement winner's nine pages contain the words *error bar* and *standard deviation* zero times.","body_zh":"直接讀過的 39 個 wiki 中：97% 有空白對照，72% 校正到絕對單位，但只有 **15%** 替自己的分析法算出偵測極限，**5%** 曾經把同一個樣本量過兩次。而且它並不預測名次：在全部 106 份檔案中，提到校正的隊伍進入 Top 10 的比例是 27%，沒提的是 29%。**沒有效果。**最佳量測得主的九個頁面裡，*error bar* 與 *standard deviation* 這兩個詞出現了零次。","chips":["15% compute an LOD","5% measure twice"],"chips_zh":["15% 算了 LOD","5% 量過兩次"],"link":"drylab"},{"kicker":"Hardware","kicker_zh":"硬體","title":"Six of twenty instruments could be rebuilt by a stranger","title_zh":"二十台儀器中，只有六台陌生人重建得出來","body":"Across the 2026 Best Hardware, Best Measurement and Best Alternative Platform cohorts, 20 instruments were built and **6** publish enough — bill of materials, geometry files, firmware, assembly guide — for someone in another country to rebuild them. **Nine publish no geometry file at all.** Exactly one has ever been used by anyone outside the team that built it.","body_zh":"在 2026 年最佳硬體、最佳量測與最佳替代平台這三個群體中，共有 20 台儀器被做出來，其中 **6 台**公開的資料足夠——材料清單、幾何檔案、韌體、組裝指南——讓另一個國家的人重建它。**有九台完全沒有公開任何幾何檔案。**而曾經被製作團隊以外的人使用過的，剛好只有一台。","chips":["6 of 20 rebuildable","1 ever reused"],"chips_zh":["6/20 可重建","只有 1 台被再用"],"link":"drylab"},{"kicker":"AI","kicker_zh":"AI","title":"Everyone disclosed their AI use — the argument is over what counts as AI","title_zh":"每一支隊伍都揭露了 AI 使用——爭點在於什麼算 AI","body":"The expected finding was that almost nobody disclosed. The actual finding is **106 of 106**, because iGEM 2026 made AI Tool Use a required block of a Bronze medal deliverable — a requirement produced total compliance overnight. But only **4 of 106** state what AI did *not* do, and of the 40 teams using a foundation model, only 15 file it as AI at all. AlphaFold is filed as biology.","body_zh":"原本預期的結果是幾乎沒有人揭露。實際的結果是 **106 支中的 106 支**，因為 iGEM 2026 把「AI 工具使用」列為銅牌必繳項目中的一個必填區塊——一條規定在一夜之間換來百分之百的遵循。但只有 **106 支中的 4 支**寫出 AI *沒有*做什麼；而在使用基礎模型的 40 支隊伍裡，只有 15 支把它填進 AI 欄位。AlphaFold 被歸類成生物學。","chips":["106 of 106","only 4 state a boundary"],"chips_zh":["106/106","只有 4 支寫出界線"],"link":"drylab"},{"kicker":"The bet","kicker_zh":"這一賭","title":"One team in 106 shines light on B. subtilis, and it is this one","title_zh":"106 支隊伍裡只有 1 支把光打在 B. subtilis 上，而那支就是我們","body":"Both trend reviews independently named optogenetic control in *Bacillus subtilis* as the white space this roadmap should aim at — a twelve-paper literature in all of PubMed. The census tested that against the competition itself. **5 of 106** used light as a control input in any organism; **5 of 106** worked with *B. subtilis*; the two sets overlap in exactly **one** team, which is GEMS-Taiwan. Outside GEMS the intersection is **0 of 105**. The gap in the literature is mirrored precisely in iGEM, and nobody in this cohort is competing for it.","body_zh":"兩份趨勢回顧各自獨立地把「*Bacillus subtilis* 的光控」指為這份路線圖該瞄準的空白——整個 PubMed 只有十二篇文獻。這次普查拿這個說法去對照比賽本身。**106 支中有 5 支**在任何生物裡把光當成控制輸入；**106 支中有 5 支**碰過 *B. subtilis*；兩個集合恰好只重疊在**一支**隊伍上，就是 GEMS-Taiwan。把 GEMS 排除之後，交集是 **105 支中的 0 支**。文獻裡的那個缺口，在 iGEM 裡被原樣複製了一次，而這一屆沒有人在搶。","chips":["5 of 106 used light","intersection: 0 of 105"],"chips_zh":["5/106 用了光","交集：0/105"],"link":"teams"},{"kicker":"Continuity","kicker_zh":"延續","title":"The institution comes back every year; the problem almost never does","title_zh":"機構每年都回來，題目幾乎從不回來","body":"Measured across iGEM's full accepted rosters rather than the winners — **284 of 423** 2026 teams had competed before, and returning tracks with results (Gold 59% against 42%). But returning is not continuing. Of the 81 decorated teams that had entered before, 78 had a readable previous project, and **5 of those 78 carried a project line forward** — three could not be classified at all because their own earlier wikis are templates or empty shells. **None of the six returning Grand Prize teams did**, and only **3 of 106** credit their own predecessor with anything. The hypothesis that continuing pays could not be tested — not for want of a baseline, but for want of cases.","body_zh":"這次是用 iGEM 完整的正式參賽名單、而不是得獎名單來算——2026 年 **423 支中有 284 支**先前就參賽過，而回鍋確實與成績相關（金牌率 59% 對 42%）。但「回來」不等於「延續」。在 81 支先前參賽過的得獎隊伍裡，78 支查得到前一年的專案內容，而**這 78 支之中只有 5 支把一條題目線帶到今年**——另外三支根本無法判定，因為它們自己前幾年的 wiki 是未編輯的範本或空殼。**六支回鍋的總冠軍級隊伍一支也沒有**。106 支之中只有 **3 支**對自己的前一屆表示過任何感謝。「延續有沒有用」這個假說無法檢定——不是因為缺少對照組，而是因為缺少案例。","chips":["5 of 78 continued","3 of 106 credit last year"],"chips_zh":["78 支中 5 支延續","106 支中 3 支感謝前一屆"],"link":"good"},{"kicker":"Education","kicker_zh":"教育","title":"Education artefacts outlive software and hardware, by a wide margin","title_zh":"教育產出活得比軟體和硬體久，而且差距很大","body":"The suspicion going in was that outreach survives only as photographs of children holding things. It was wrong. Of **285 education files** linked from 31 decorated wikis, **284 download today** and one returns 403 — not a single 404. Against 8 of 21 software tools still running and 6 of 20 devices rebuildable, the reason is structural: a PDF on static.igem.wiki needs no server to stay alive. The failures are elsewhere — **1 licence statement in 136 PDFs**, and the Best Education winner publishes no downloadable file at all.","body_zh":"一開始的懷疑是：教育推廣最後只會以「孩子們拿著東西的照片」留下來。這個懷疑錯了。31 份得獎 wiki 連出的 **285 個教育檔案**中，**284 個今天仍下載得到**，一個回 403——一個 404 都沒有。對照軟體 21 個中 8 個還能跑、硬體 20 台中 6 台重建得出來，原因是結構性的：放在 static.igem.wiki 上的一份 PDF，不需要任何伺服器就能活著。真正的失敗在別處——**136 份 PDF 裡只有 1 份寫了授權條款**，而最佳教育獎得主根本沒有提供任何可下載的檔案。","chips":["284 of 285 download","1 licence in 136 PDFs"],"chips_zh":["285 個中 284 個下載得到","136 份 PDF 中 1 份有授權"],"link":"good"},{"kicker":"Resources","kicker_zh":"資源","title":"Size buys nothing — the smallest Top 10 team had nine students","title_zh":"人多買不到名次——最小的 Top 10 隊伍只有九名學生","body":"Across 84 decorated teams, headcount and award count correlate at **0.06** (Spearman, p = 0.61), and within every section the Top 10 teams are statistically indistinguishable in size. Medians: high school 17.5, undergraduate 17, overgraduate 12.5. **Princeton reached 2nd runner-up Grand Prize with nine undergraduates** — and four named scientists behind them, one chassis reused across three applications, and a binder pipeline that made a new target cost compute instead of hands. The substitution for people is scope, software and supervision.","body_zh":"在 84 支得獎隊伍中，人數與獎項數的相關係數是 **0.06**（Spearman，p = 0.61），而且在每一個組別裡，Top 10 隊伍的人數與其他得獎隊伍在統計上沒有差別。中位數：高中組 17.5、大學組 17、研究生組 12.5。**Princeton 以九名大學生拿下總冠軍季軍**——他們背後有四位具名的科學家、一個底盤重複用在三個應用上，以及一條結合子設計流程，讓換一個標的花的是算力而不是人手。能取代人的，是範圍、軟體與指導。","chips":["r = 0.06, p = 0.61","smallest Top 10: 9 students"],"chips_zh":["r = 0.06、p = 0.61","最小的 Top 10：9 名學生"],"link":"teams"},{"kicker":"Judging","kicker_zh":"評審","title":"GEMS has already won this, in 2024 — so the question is what changed","title_zh":"GEMS 已經贏過一次，就在 2024 年——所以問題是什麽改變了","body":"**GEMS-Taiwan won the 2024 High School Grand Prize** and was a Finalist that year. It placed Top 10 in 2024, 2025 and 2026, and it and Lambert-GA are the **only two High School teams to do that** — each winning exactly one Grand Prize in the span, GEMS in 2024 and Lambert in 2026. So the finalist analysis is not about a bar this team has never reached. Note the shape of the three records: 2024's wins were **Best Wiki**, Best New Basic Part and the promotion video; 2025 brought five nominations and **no win at all**; 2026's wins were Measurement, Hardware and Integrated Human Practices, with Best Wiki and Best Presentation only nominated. The obvious reading is that the whole-project communication layer slipped — 2024's Best Wiki win against 2026's mere nomination, and Best Wiki nominees take a Top 10 60% of the time against 22% for Measurement. **It was tested against all three wikis and it broke.** The 2024 Best Wiki winner is a 577-byte script shell with no results page at all and one p-value on the whole site. What separated 2024 is that both central claims were measured on the real target animal and the rival explanation was experimentally excluded.","body_zh":"**GEMS-Taiwan 贏過 2024 年高中組總冠軍**，那一年它也是 Finalist。它在 2024、2025、2026 三季都進了 Top 10，而全高中組**只有它和 Lambert-GA 做到**——這段期間兩支各贏一次總冠軍，GEMS 在 2024 年，Lambert 在 2026 年。所以整份決賽分析談的並不是一道這支隊伍從未跨過的門檻。請留意三年紀錄的形狀：2024 年的得獎是**Best Wiki**、Best New Basic Part 與宣傳影片；2025 年有五項入圍、**一項都沒贏**；2026 年的得獎是量測、硬體與整合式人類實踐，而 Best Wiki 與 Best Presentation 只是入圍。最直覺的讀法是整體專案的「傳達層」退步了——2024 年贏下 Best Wiki，2026 年只入圍，而 Best Wiki 入圍者有 60% 同時進 Top 10，量測只有 22%。**這個說法拿三年的 wiki 實際比對過，然後破了。**2024 年那個 Best Wiki 得主是一個 577 位元組的腳本外殼，整站連結果頁都沒有，全站只有一個 p 值。真正把 2024 年分出來的，是兩個核心主張都在真正的標的生物上量過，而且對手解釋被實驗排除掉了。","chips":["2024 Grand Prize winner","the communication story broke"],"chips_zh":["2024 年總冠軍","「傳達層」的說法破了"],"link":"judging"},{"kicker":"Judging","kicker_zh":"評審","title":"The podium years are the years the claim was measured on the real thing","title_zh":"站上頒獎臺的那幾年，正是核心主張在真實標的上被量過的那幾年","body":"This is the one line that now holds from two independent directions. **Across** the 2026 High School Top 10, seven of seven non-podium teams stop at a surrogate and exactly one team in ten ran its assay on a real sample — HongKong-JSS on a soil extract — and that team took 1st Runner-up. **Within** GEMS's own three seasons, the Grand Prize year is the real-target year: 2024 fed three toxins to live *Aedes albopictus* larvae, reported LC50 for all three, examined 98 dead larvae under the microscope, and ran a qPCR immune-gene panel against an empty-vector arm explicitly \"to rule out the effect of *E. coli* in the death of mosquito larvae\". In 2026 the plant rescue is strong at p < 0.0001 with 40 seedlings a condition, but **the preparation sprayed on the plants was never assayed** and the light-gated device never showed light dependence. Statistics went the other way entirely — p-values 1, then 0, then 5, and **no named statistical test in any of the three seasons.**","body_zh":"這是目前唯一從兩個獨立方向都站得住的一條線。**橫向看**2026 年高中組 Top 10：七支非頒獎臺隊伍全部停在替代物上，十支裡剛好只有一支把檢測跑在真實樣本上——HongKong-JSS 的土壤萃取液——而那一支拿下亞軍。**縱向看** GEMS 自己的三季：拿總冠軍的那一年，就是打在真實標的上的那一年。2024 年把三種毒蛋白餵給活的 *Aedes albopictus* 幼蟲，三種都報告了 LC50，以顯微鏡檢視 98 隻死亡幼蟲，還跑了一組 qPCR 免疫基因試驗對照空載體組，目的明寫是「排除 *E. coli* 在蚊蟲幼蟲死亡中的作用」。2026 年的植物救援很強，每組 40 棵苗、p < 0.0001，但**噴到植物上的那份製備從未被檢測活性**，而光控裝置也從未顯示出光依賴性。統計的方向則完全相反——p 值是 1 個、0 個、5 個，而且**三季之中沒有任何一季寫出檢定名稱**。","chips":["1 of 10 tested a real sample","p-values 1, 0, 5 — tests named: none"],"chips_zh":["十支裡一支測過真實樣本","p 值 1、0、5；檢定名稱：零"],"link":"judging"},{"kicker":"Judging","kicker_zh":"評審","title":"Two routes to the finalist slate, and GEMS took neither","title_zh":"通往決賽席位有兩條路，GEMS 兩條都沒走","body":"In the 2026 High School section 147 teams entered, 10 reached the Top 10 and **2 were named Finalists**. GEMS-Taiwan was not one, while holding three of the 17 section-level awards won across the whole section. Five explanations died on the evidence: not statistics (the Grand Prize winner's results page has no p-values and no named test), not completeness, not Registry documentation (**the Grand Prize winner has the shortest of all ten**), not candour, and not even having one clear claim — the clearest headline among the non-finalists placed nowhere. The finalists arrived by different routes: **novelty**, and **depth on a real sample**. Seven of seven non-podium teams stop at a surrogate; exactly one team in ten tested a real one.","body_zh":"2026 年高中組有 147 支隊伍參賽、10 支進入 Top 10，而**只有 2 支被列為 Finalist**。GEMS-Taiwan 不在其中，但它握有整個組別總共 17 項組別層級獎項中的三項。五個解釋都死在證據上：不是統計（總冠軍的結果頁沒有 p 值、也沒有檢定名稱）、不是完成度、不是 Registry 文件（**總冠軍的文件是十支裡最短的**）、不是坦白，甚至也不是「有一個清楚的主張」——非決賽隊伍中標題最清楚的那一支，什麼名次都沒有。兩支決賽隊伍是沿著不同的路抵達的：**新穎性**，以及**在真實樣本上的深度**。七支非頒獎臺隊伍全部停在替代物上；十支之中只有一支測過真實樣本。","chips":["2 finalists of 10","novelty, or depth on a real sample"],"chips_zh":["10 支中 2 席決賽","新穎性，或真實樣本上的深度"],"link":"judging"},{"kicker":"Rigour","kicker_zh":"嚴謹度","title":"In the High School Top 10, the most rigorous team won nothing","title_zh":"在高中組 Top 10 裡，最嚴謹的那支隊伍什麼都沒拿","body":"Every results page in the 2026 High School Top 10, scored on what a reader can check. **HongKong-HS reports ANOVA, Dunnett's post-hoc, a t-test, n=3 and standard deviations — and won no award at all.** The Grand Prize winner names no statistical test, reports no p-value and gives no replicate count; its one quantitative claim is a confidence interval produced by a commercial service. Five of the ten publish no p-value anywhere, and one team reached the Top 10 **with no results page**. This is the measurement-discipline null reproduced inside a cohort of ten: rigour makes a claim checkable, and it does not place.","body_zh":"把 2026 年高中組 Top 10 的每一份結果頁，依「讀者能核對什麼」評分。**HongKong-HS 報告了 ANOVA、Dunnett 事後檢定、t-test、n=3 與標準差——結果一個獎都沒拿。** 總冠軍沒有寫出任何統計檢定名稱、沒有給出任何 p 值、也沒有重複數；它唯一的量化主張是一個由商業服務做出來的信賴區間。十支隊伍中有五支完全沒有 p 值，而有一支**在沒有結果頁的情況下**進了 Top 10。這是「量測嚴謹度」的虛無結果在十支隊伍群體裡的再現：嚴謹讓主張可被核對，但它不決定名次。","chips":["most rigorous: 0 awards","5 of 10 report no p-value"],"chips_zh":["最嚴謹：0 個獎","10 支中 5 支沒有 p 值"],"link":"judging"},{"kicker":"Judging","kicker_zh":"評審","title":"Village choice is not a lever, and the high-school village award has four doors, not thirteen","title_zh":"選 village 不是一根槓桿，而高中組的 village 獎只有四道門，不是十三道","body":"Of 147 accepted High School teams across 13 villages, **47 were decorated (32.0%)** and 10 took a Top 10 place. The per-village spread looks dramatic, from 2 of 17 in Agriculture to 12 of 23 in Biomanufacturing, and it **is not distinguishable from 147 teams decorated independently at 32%** (chi-square 19.64 on 12 df, Monte-Carlo p = 0.088). Across years the only property that carries is how crowded a village is (r = +0.91); what it pays does not (Top 10 rate r = +0.17, p = 0.58). And the structure is not per village at all: high-school teams compete for **four award groups**, 20 citations in total, between 1 in 5.6 and 1 in 9.6 — **0.63× an undergraduate team's odds**. GEMS's own Biomanufacturing was the most crowded high-school field in the competition and also the most decorated, 12 of 23.","body_zh":"13 個 village 裡共 147 支獲接受的高中隊伍，其中**47 支獲得獎項列名（32.0%）**，10 支拿下 Top 10。各 village 之間的差距看起來很大，從 Agriculture 的 17 取 2 到 Biomanufacturing 的 23 取 12，但它**與「147 支隊伍各自以 32% 機率獲得列名」無法區別**（卡方 19.64，自由度 12，蒙地卡羅 p = 0.088）。跨年度唯一延續下來的性質是一個 village 有多擁擠（r = +0.91）；它給出多少回報則沒有延續（Top 10 比率 r = +0.17，p = 0.58）。而且這個結構根本不是按 village 走的：高中隊伍競爭的是**四個獎項群組**、合計 20 個席次，機率介於 1 比 5.6 與 1 比 9.6 之間——**只有大學組隊伍的 0.63 倍**。GEMS 自己所在的 Biomanufacturing 是全場高中隊伍最擁擠的 village，同時也是列名率最高的，23 支裡有 12 支。","chips":["spread indistinguishable from chance","four groups, 20 citations"],"chips_zh":["差距與隨機無法區別","四個群組、20 個席次"],"link":"judging"},{"kicker":"Judging","kicker_zh":"評審","title":"Four categories behave like a whole-project verdict, and the three GEMS won are not among them","title_zh":"有四個類別的行為像是整體專案的判決，而 GEMS 贏下的那三個不在其中","body":"Pooled over 2024-26, the 17 special categories nominate between 3 and 26 teams, and the share of each category's nominees who also took a Top 10 place runs from **60% down to 0%**. The top four are Best Wiki **60%**, Best Presentation **53%**, Best Model **50%** and Integrated Human Practices **45%**. GEMS's three 2026 wins sit at 45%, **22%** and **21%**. The figure is near-circular — Wiki and Presentation are judged on how the whole project is *communicated*, which is the same material a Top 10 judgement works on — so it is useless as a prediction and useful as a map of which categories proxy a whole-project verdict and which certify one isolated dimension. GEMS held 5 of the 82 high-school citation slots in 2026, the most of any team in the section, and has never been cited in **9 of the 17** categories.","body_zh":"把 2024 到 2026 三季合起來看，17 個特別獎類別的入圍人數介於 3 到 26 支之間，而各類別入圍者同時拿下 Top 10 的比例，從**60% 一路到 0%**。最高的四個是 Best Wiki **60%**、Best Presentation **53%**、Best Model **50%** 與整合式人類實踐 **45%**。GEMS 在 2026 年贏下的三個，分別落在 45%、**22%** 與 **21%**。這個數字接近循環論證——Wiki 與 Presentation 評的是整個專案「如何被傳達」，而那正是 Top 10 評審所依據的同一批材料——所以它拿來預測毫無用處，拿來當地圖卻很有用：它標出哪些類別是整體專案判決的替身，哪些只認證單一面向。GEMS 在 2026 年占住 82 個高中組列名席次中的 5 個，是整個組別最多的一支，而在**17 個類別裡有 9 個**從未被列名過。","chips":["60% down to 0%","GEMS's wins at 45, 22 and 21%"],"chips_zh":["從 60% 到 0%","GEMS 的得獎在 45、22、21%"],"link":"judging"}],"method":"Each card summarises an analysis published in full on the tab it links to, where the evidence, the named teams and the limits of the method are set out. Where a finding rests on a number, the analysis says how the number was computed and what it cannot see.","method_zh":"每一張卡片都是某篇完整分析的摘要，點進連結的頁面即可看到證據、具名的團隊，以及該方法的限制。凡是以數字為基礎的發現，分析中都會說明該數字如何計算，以及它看不到什麼。","order":10},{"id":"picks-macro","tab":"picks","order":10,"kicker":"2027 selection · macro","kicker_zh":"2027 選題 · 大勢","title":"What the 2026 shifts do to what is worth attempting","title_zh":"2026 年的轉變，如何改變「什麼值得做」","lede":"Twenty-four shifts from this report's own two trend reviews, read for one thing only: does each make a kind of project newly worth doing, newly pointless, or newly cheap for a team with one season, a school lab and no budget.","lede_zh":"本報告自己的兩份趨勢回顧共二十四項轉變，這裡只為一件事而讀：對一支只有一季、一間學校實驗室、沒有預算的隊伍來說，每一項轉變讓哪一類專案變得剛好值得做、剛好變得沒意義，或剛好變便宜了。","body":"The two trend tabs say what moved. This block asks one question of each movement and nothing else: does it make a kind of project newly worth attempting, newly pointless, or newly cheap for a team with one season, a school lab and no budget? A shift with no answer to that question is not an opportunity, and it appears below only as a table row saying why it can be ignored.\n\n**The split that matters is commoditised against still hard.** What went free in 2026 is almost entirely prediction and design. A protein-ligand complex now folds on open weights in minutes. Thirty-five binder designs cost a few hundred dollars of compute. A flux-balance model of *B. subtilis* comes out of a published genome-scale model and COBRApy for nothing. A literature-to-hypothesis pass runs on an open agent stack. A genome language model will write you a promoter. None of that can be the project any more, because the marginal cost of the step is an afternoon and a GPU, and a judge comparing two teams cannot separate them on it. What stayed hard is everything that touches a physical sample: a quantitative binding measurement, an off-state for a light-inducible promoter, a titre anyone can defend, a real sample rather than a surrogate, a cost model, a containment argument, a lead time you can plan a season around. Choose the 2027 project so that the hard half is the contribution and the free half is a line in the methods.\n\n**The worked example, checked.** The team file for Lambert-GA supports a sharper claim than the one we were handed, and a narrower one. Lambert did not win Best Model only: it took the High School Grand Prize plus Best Model, Best Wiki, Best Sustainable Development Impact and Best Village Project, and a Best Hardware nomination. Its stack is exactly the commoditised frontier — BindCraft, Boltz-2, Protenix, Mosaic — with the biolayer interferometry bought in from a commercial provider. On *the only high-school team at that frontier*, the evidence supports it for the tier that was actually read: across the ten High School Top 10 dry labs, this report's own ceiling analysis finds only Lambert-GA working at the frontier of the toolchain, while the rest reached the same tier on logistic regression, NetLogo, NUPACK, PyMOL, FoldX and one tool reused outright from a 2024 team. HKSSC used AlphaFold, so structure prediction itself was not unique — the 2026 co-folding and binder-design stack was. It does not support a claim about high-school teams in general, because only decorated teams were read.\n\nAnd the part worth copying is not the stack. Lambert benchmarked the confidence metrics against 5,721 labelled designs, found a 38-metric ensemble at ROC-AUC 0.541, barely above chance, noticed that its own eventual hit did not carry the best score, showed across 1,307 prior designs that choosing the epitope roughly doubles the hit rate, and published all thirty-five designs with the failures left in. One of thirty-five bound, at KD 603.6 nM, on under USD 400 of compute. That is the shape of a 2027 project: the free tool runs, and the contribution is the honest evaluation of what it produced.\n\n**The existing bet, re-tested.** The roadmap already points at optogenetic control in *B. subtilis*, and the 2026 evidence pulls in two directions at once — it strengthens the strategic half and weakens the readiness half. Strategically it strengthens: both trend reviews, run separately from different sources with no knowledge of each other, landed on the same gap, and the competition test is harder than the literature count. Of the 106 decorated teams of 2026, 5 used light as a control input in any organism, 5 worked with *B. subtilis*, and the two sets intersect in exactly one team, which is GEMS; excluding GEMS the intersection is 0 of 105. Four of the five light teams work in organisms where optogenetics is already routine, and four of the five *B. subtilis* teams induce with something other than light. Nobody in that cohort is competing for the line.\n\nOn readiness it weakens. The same report records that ReLEAF's own 2026 pages do not yet evidence light-dependence: the ELISA showed no change over time, the AmilCP reporter never coloured, and every biological result in the project came from a constitutive bypass. Two candidate explanations are named — well-to-well light crosstalk in the plate apparatus, and red LEDs emitting near 640 nm when CcaSR needs about 672 nm to switch off — and neither has been tested. So the honest verdict is that 2026 strengthens the bet as a direction and weakens it as a starting position. The 2027 pick should be the experiment that closes that gap, not a new application stacked on top of it. The chassis census adds the discipline: among decorated teams a non-model chassis neither helped nor hurt a Top 10 place, 9 of 27 against 21 of 79, Fisher exact p = 0.62. Hold this line because the field is empty and the capability compounds, not because it wins.\n\n**Two shifts that are specifically Taiwanese.** The first is positional. China holds roughly 70 percent of world fermentation capacity, and Taiwan's state-backed push is a contract-manufacturing play with no visible synthetic-biology design layer, while Singapore and Israel are funding exactly that layer. A school team cannot out-build a CDMO and gains nothing by miniaturising one. It can choose a project whose surviving output sits in the design layer — a characterised part set, a measurement protocol calibrated to absolute units, a small local dataset with a benchmark task attached, a tool with a URL and a licence — and name a Taiwanese end user before starting.\n\nThe second is procedural and has a date. The November 2026 National Policy for Nucleic Acid Synthesis Screening ties US federal funding to buying synthetic DNA only from certified providers that screen orders of 50 or more nucleotides with verified tools and keep records for eight years. A Taiwanese team ordering into that perimeter, collaborating with US-funded partners or sending students to US labs is inside it whether or not it has noticed. The selection consequence is that proximity to a pathogen or toxin list is now a real cost in days: it buys a review step, a supplier conversation and a delay a one-season team cannot absorb. Pick a target no screening desk has to think about, and write the one-page ordering policy before the first order rather than after the first question.\n\n**What to ignore, and why.** Autonomous cloud labs and the Genesis Mission's 97-robot facility are allocated by proposal to funded institutions, run on proprietary stacks, and carry a documented per-device integration tax; a school team gets one transferable habit from them, which is writing protocols in a machine-readable form. Genome-scale generative design needs synthesis budget at kilobase-to-genome scale and carries the sharpest dual-use profile in the field — read it, critique it, do not build it. Therapeutics needs BSL-2 or above, patients and a regulator. The cost-of-goods wall is capital engineering with government money behind it. The post-platform correction and the funding concentration are a reading skill and a careers signal, not project ideas. Six of the nineteen rows below should change nothing at all about what GEMS picks, and saying so is half the work of selection.","body_zh":"兩個趨勢頁已經說了什麼在動。這個區塊對每一項變動只問一個問題，別的都不問：對一支只有一季、一間學校實驗室、沒有預算的隊伍來說，它讓哪一類專案變得剛好值得嘗試、剛好變得沒意義，或剛好變便宜了？一項轉變若回答不了這個問題，它就不是機會；它在下面只會是表格裡的一列，說明為什麼可以不理它。\n\n**真正該分清的是「已成為廉價商品」與「仍然困難」。** 2026 年變成免費的，幾乎全都是預測與設計。蛋白質與配體的複合物現在用開放權重幾分鐘就摺好。三十五個結合蛋白設計只要幾百美元的運算費。用 COBRApy 加一個已發表的基因組尺度模型，*B. subtilis* 的通量平衡模型一毛錢都不用。文獻到假說的那一輪可以跑在開放的代理堆疊上。基因組語言模型會幫你寫啟動子。這些都不能再當成專案本身，因為這個步驟的邊際成本就是一個下午加一張 GPU，評審拿兩支隊伍來比，在這件事上分不出高下。仍然困難的，是所有會碰到實體樣本的東西：一個定量的結合量測、一個光誘導啟動子的關閉態、一個站得住腳的產量數字、一個真實樣本而不是替代品、一份成本模型、一套圍堵論述、一個能用來排整季進度的交期。2027 年的選題應該這樣挑：困難的那一半是貢獻，免費的那一半只是方法章節裡的一行字。\n\n**那個示範推理，查過了。** Lambert-GA 的團隊檔案支持的，是一個比我們拿到的版本更銳利、同時範圍更窄的說法。Lambert 不是只拿最佳建模：它拿下高中組總冠軍，外加最佳建模、最佳 Wiki、最佳永續發展影響與最佳 Village 專案，還入圍最佳硬體。它的工具組正是那個已成廉價商品的前沿——BindCraft、Boltz-2、Protenix、Mosaic——而生物層干涉量測是向商業服務商外購的。關於「唯一站在那個前沿的高中隊伍」，證據在真正被讀過的那一層成立：在十支高中組 Top 10 的乾實驗室之中，本報告自己的高中天花板分析發現只有 Lambert-GA 站在工具鏈的前沿，其餘幾支靠的是邏輯斯迴歸、NetLogo、NUPACK、PyMOL、FoldX，以及一個直接沿用 2024 年某隊的工具。HKSSC 用了 AlphaFold，所以結構預測本身並不獨特——獨特的是 2026 年的共摺疊與結合蛋白設計工具組。它不足以支持一個關於所有高中隊伍的說法，因為被讀過的只有得獎隊伍。\n\n而真正值得抄的不是那套工具。Lambert 拿 5,721 個有標註的設計去評測那些信賴度指標，發現一個 38 項指標的集成模型 ROC-AUC 只有 0.541，幾乎只比亂猜好一點，注意到自己最終成功的那個設計並不是分數最高的，又用 1,307 個先前的設計證明選對抗原決定位大約讓命中率翻倍，然後把全部三十五個設計連失敗一起公開。三十五個裡有一個結合，KD 為 603.6 nM，運算費用不到 400 美元。這就是 2027 年專案該有的形狀：免費的工具照跑，貢獻在於誠實評估它產出了什麼。\n\n**既有的那個賭注，重新檢驗。** 路線圖已經指向 *B. subtilis* 的光遺傳學控制，而 2026 年的證據同時往兩個方向拉——它加強了策略那一半，削弱了準備度那一半。策略上是加強的：兩份趨勢回顧分別從不同來源、互不知情地進行，卻落在同一個空白上，而競賽層面的檢驗比文獻數量更嚴格。2026 年 106 支得獎隊伍中，有 5 支在任何生物裡把光當成控制輸入，有 5 支用 *B. subtilis*，兩個集合的交集恰好只有一支隊伍，就是 GEMS；把 GEMS 排除，交集是 105 支中的 0 支。五支用光的隊伍中有四支工作的生物本來就把光遺傳學當成例行工具，五支用 *B. subtilis* 的隊伍中有四支是用光以外的方式誘導。這一批隊伍裡沒有人在跟你搶這塊地。\n\n準備度上則是削弱的。同一份報告記下：ReLEAF 自己 2026 年的頁面還無法證明光依賴性——ELISA 顯示隨時間沒有變化，AmilCP 報告基因從未顯色，而專案裡每一個生物學結果都來自組成型的旁路。團隊點出兩個可能解釋——培養板裝置內孔與孔之間的光串擾，以及紅光 LED 發光波長約 640 nm，而 CcaSR 需要約 672 nm 才會關閉——兩個都還沒被直接測試。所以誠實的判斷是：2026 年讓這個賭注作為「方向」更站得住，作為「起跑位置」更站不住。2027 年的選題應該就是補上那個缺口的實驗，而不是在它上面再疊一個新應用。底盤普查還補上一道紀律：在得獎隊伍之中，用非模式底盤對進 Top 10 既沒幫助也沒妨礙，27 支中 9 支對 79 支中 21 支，Fisher 精確檢定 p = 0.62。守住這條線，是因為這塊地還空著、而且能力會累積，不是因為它會贏。\n\n**兩項專屬於台灣的轉變。** 第一項是位置問題。中國掌握全球約 70% 的發酵量能，而台灣由國家主導的布局是一場代工製造的局，看不到合成生物學的設計層，新加坡與以色列卻正好在補助那一層。學校隊伍蓋不過 CDMO，把它縮小一號來做也得不到任何東西。但它可以挑一個「留下來的產出落在設計層」的專案——一組特性已完整描述的元件、一份校準到絕對單位的量測流程、一個附帶基準任務的小型本地資料集、一個有網址與授權的工具——並且在開始之前就先指名一個台灣的終端使用者。\n\n第二項是程序問題，而且有日期。2026 年 11 月的國家核酸合成篩查政策，把美國聯邦經費與「只能向認證供應商採購合成 DNA」綁在一起，這些供應商必須以驗證過的工具篩查 50 個核苷酸以上的訂單，並保留紀錄八年。一支台灣隊伍只要訂單進到那個範圍、與受美國經費支持的夥伴合作，或送學生去美國實驗室，就已經在裡面了，不管它有沒有注意到。對選題的後果是：靠近病原或毒素清單現在要用天數來計價——它會換來一道審查、一輪跟供應商的往返，以及一段只有一季的隊伍吸收不了的延誤。挑一個篩查窗口完全不需要多想的標的，並在第一筆訂單之前就把那一頁訂購政策寫好，而不是等第一個問題來了才寫。\n\n**該忽略什麼，以及為什麼。** 自主雲端實驗室與 Genesis Mission 那座 97 台機器人的設施，是以計畫申請的方式配給有經費的機構，跑在專有的技術堆疊上，而且有被記錄下來的「每台裝置都要手寫轉接程式」的整合成本；學校隊伍從它們身上只能帶走一個可移植的習慣，就是把實驗流程寫成機器可讀的格式。基因組尺度的生成式設計需要千鹼基到整個基因組級別的合成預算，而且帶著這個領域裡最尖銳的雙重用途風險——讀它、批判它，不要去做它。治療用途需要 BSL-2 以上、病人與主管機關。產品成本那道牆是有政府資金在後面推的資本工程。後平台時代的修正與資金集中，是一項閱讀能力與一個職涯訊號，不是專案題目。下面十九列裡有六列，對 GEMS 要選什麼完全不該有任何影響，而把這件事講明白，就是選題工作的一半。","cards":[{"kicker":"Co-folding","kicker_zh":"共摺疊","title":"Predicting a complex is a step in your methods, not your project","title_zh":"預測複合物是方法裡的一個步驟，不是你的專案","body":"AlphaFold3's architecture was reproduced and out-opened by Boltz-1 and Boltz-2, Chai-1, Protenix and OpenFold3, so the entire structural layer of a project now runs on one GPU in seconds to minutes. The consequence for selection is blunt: no 2027 project can rest on having produced a structure or a docked complex, because every other team can produce one too. What stayed scarce is judgement — knowing when pLDDT, PAE and ipTM are lying, and ranking affinity within a congeneric series, which these models do badly because they interpolate the PDB rather than learn physics. Make the confidence audit the deliverable, the way Lambert-GA did.","body_zh":"AlphaFold3 的架構已被 Boltz-1 與 Boltz-2、Chai-1、Protenix 與 OpenFold3 複現，並在開放程度上超越，於是一個專案的整個結構層現在只要一張 GPU、數秒到數分鐘就跑完。對選題的後果很直白：2027 年沒有任何專案能靠「做出了一個結構或一個對接複合物」站住，因為別的隊伍也做得出來。仍然稀缺的是判斷力——知道 pLDDT、PAE 與 ipTM 什麼時候在騙你，以及在同系列化合物之間排序親和力，而後者這些模型做得很差，因為它們是在 PDB 之間內插，不是學會物理。像 Lambert-GA 那樣，把信賴度的查核本身當成交付成果。","chips":["Free: a complex in minutes","Hard: knowing when it is wrong","Avoid: prediction as a result","Reachable: yes"],"chips_zh":["免費：幾分鐘一個複合物","困難：知道它何時錯了","避開：把預測當成果","做得到：可以"]},{"kicker":"Generative design","kicker_zh":"生成式設計","title":"A de novo binder is affordable; the binding assay is what you must secure first","title_zh":"從頭設計結合蛋白負擔得起，要先談定的是結合檢測","body":"BindCraft, LigandMPNN and RFdiffusion2 made de novo binders routine enough to benchmark honestly, and the honest number is a cross-target success rate nearer 25 percent than the 46.3 percent mean, with the hardest published single-target set under 10 percent. Lambert-GA's own campaign landed 1 confirmed binder out of 35 designs, at KD 603.6 nM, for under USD 400 of compute — and bought the biolayer interferometry in. So the design half is cheap and the measurement half carries the whole project risk. Do not open a design campaign in 2027 without a named, costed route to a quantitative binding number: a partner lab, a commercial run, or an assay GEMS already owns.","body_zh":"BindCraft、LigandMPNN 與 RFdiffusion2 讓從頭設計的結合蛋白普及到足以誠實做基準評測，而誠實的數字是：跨標的成功率更接近 25%，而不是 46.3% 的平均值，已發表中最困難的單一標的資料集甚至低於 10%。Lambert-GA 自己那一輪，三十五個設計中確認有一個結合，KD 為 603.6 nM，運算費用不到 400 美元——而生物層干涉量測是外購的。所以設計那一半很便宜，量測那一半承擔了整個專案的風險。2027 年要開設計戰役，必須先有一條指名、已估價的路徑可以拿到定量的結合數字：一間合作實驗室、一次商業委測，或 GEMS 本來就有的檢測。","chips":["Free: 20 to 35 designs","Hard: a defensible KD","Lambert: 1 of 35 bound","Secure the assay first"],"chips_zh":["免費：20 到 35 個設計","困難：站得住的 KD","Lambert：35 個中 1 個結合","先談定檢測"]},{"kicker":"Light as control","kicker_zh":"以光作為控制","title":"The light gap is real and uncontested, but GEMS has not yet shown its own switch works","title_zh":"光的空白是真的、也沒人搶，但 GEMS 還沒證明自己的開關能用","body":"Two independent reviews converged: light has become a real-time actuator for closed-loop fermentation control, with reported titre gains near 60 percent in a 1 L photobioreactor, and the cheapest retrofit past the capital wall — while optogenetics in *B. subtilis* is twelve papers in all of PubMed. The competition test is sharper than the literature: 5 of 106 decorated teams used light as a control input, 5 worked in *B. subtilis*, the intersection is one team, and it is GEMS; 0 of 105 without it. Against that, ReLEAF's own 2026 pages report no ELISA change over time, a reporter that never coloured, and every biological result from a constitutive bypass. So the pick is specific: spend 2027 on dose-response and the off-state, testing the suspected 640-against-672 nm mismatch and the plate crosstalk directly. In a twelve-paper field that is on its own a publishable contribution. A new application on an unevidenced switch is not.","body_zh":"兩份互不相關的回顧收斂到同一處：光已成為閉環發酵控制的即時致動器，1 L 光生物反應器中回報的產量提升接近 60%，也是繞過資本門檻最便宜的改裝途徑——而 *B. subtilis* 的光遺傳學在整個 PubMed 裡只有十二篇論文。競賽層面的檢驗比文獻更嚴格：106 支得獎隊伍中有 5 支把光當成控制輸入，有 5 支做 *B. subtilis*，交集只有一支，就是 GEMS；把它排除就是 105 支中的 0 支。但另一邊，ReLEAF 自己 2026 年的頁面記載 ELISA 隨時間沒有變化、報告基因從未顯色，而每一個生物學結果都來自組成型旁路。所以選題很具體：2027 年投入在劑量反應與關閉態，直接測試那個疑似 640 對 672 nm 的波長錯配，以及培養板的光串擾。在一個只有十二篇論文的領域裡，這件事本身就是可發表的貢獻。在一個還沒被證明的開關上疊新應用，則不是。","chips":["Free: LEDs and a plate reader","Hard: an off-state","0 of 105 compete for it","Pick: dose-response first"],"chips_zh":["免費：LED 與讀盤機","困難：關閉態","105 支中 0 支在搶","選題：先做劑量反應"]},{"kicker":"ML-guided DBTL","kicker_zh":"機器學習導引的 DBTL","title":"Two design cycles on a small library is a season; six cycles with robots is not","title_zh":"小型函式庫跑兩個設計循環是一季的事；靠機器人跑六個循環不是","body":"COBRApy, flux balance analysis and a published *B. subtilis* genome-scale model cost nothing, and the benchmarks are reproducible, so the dry half of ML-guided strain design is free. The results are real: a five-fold titre gain over six cycles in *P. putida*, and 2.37-fold over two cycles on p-coumaric acid in yeast against a design space of roughly 170 million. But the published gains ride on lab automation and high-throughput proteomics that a school lab does not have. For one season the honest scope is to reproduce the exploration-against-exploitation comparison in silico, then run one real cycle on a library small enough to assay by hand. Avoid putting a titre figure in the abstract before the assay exists.","body_zh":"COBRApy、通量平衡分析，加一個已發表的 *B. subtilis* 基因組尺度模型都不要錢，而那些基準測試可以重現，所以機器學習導引菌株設計的乾實驗那一半是免費的。成果也是真的：*P. putida* 在六個循環中產量提升五倍，酵母菌生產 p-coumaric acid 在兩個循環中提升 2.37 倍，而設計空間約有 1.7 億種。但那些已發表的提升，靠的是學校實驗室沒有的實驗室自動化與高通量蛋白質體學。一季的誠實範圍是：先在電腦上重現探索對利用的比較，再在一個小到可以手工檢測的函式庫上跑一個真實循環。在檢測方法還不存在之前，不要把產量數字寫進摘要。","chips":["Free: COBRApy and a published GEM","Hard: library build and titre assay","Scope: one real cycle"],"chips_zh":["免費：COBRApy 與已發表的 GEM","困難：建函式庫與產量檢測","範圍：一個真實循環"]},{"kicker":"Build and supply","kicker_zh":"建構與供應","title":"Prototype cell-free, order fragments, and plan the season around a quoted lead time","title_zh":"用無細胞做原型、訂片段，並依實際報價的交期排整季","body":"Cell-free TXTL is the one wet step that got genuinely cheaper for a school lab: it removes transformation, growth and most of the biosafety friction, and it is the right first test of any new circuit. The rest of the build industrialisation — one-pot hybridisation synthesis of a thousand fragments, droplet pooled assembly, long-read design-space mapping — needs equipment a school does not have and should not chase. On supply, the 2026 shift is not price: Ansa sells 50 kb clonal constructs from USD 0.13 per base pair and Twist fragments from USD 0.07, so the differentiator is length, turnaround and customs. A 2027 plan that assumes a 10 kb construct arrives in two weeks will fail in Taiwan. Design for synthesis, order fragments you can assemble locally, and build the calendar backwards from a real quote.","body_zh":"無細胞的 TXTL 是學校實驗室真正變便宜的那一個濕實驗步驟：它省去轉形、培養與大部分生物安全上的摩擦，而且是任何新電路最合適的第一輪測試。建構工業化的其餘部分——一鍋式雜交合成一千個片段、液滴混池組裝、長讀長設計空間繪製——需要學校沒有的設備，也不該去追。在供應端，2026 年的轉變不在價格：Ansa 的 50 kb 單株構築體每鹼基對 0.13 美元起，Twist 的片段每鹼基對 0.07 美元起，所以差異化在長度、交期與海關。一個假設 10 kb 構築體兩週就到貨的 2027 年計畫，在台灣一定會失敗。為合成而設計，訂可以自己在本地組裝的片段，並依實際報價往回推整季行程。","chips":["Free: TXTL prototyping","Hard: lead time and customs","Order fragments, not one long construct"],"chips_zh":["免費：TXTL 原型製作","困難：交期與海關","訂片段，不要訂一條長構築體"]},{"kicker":"Biosecurity","kicker_zh":"生物安全","title":"Screening policy now prices your choice of target","title_zh":"篩查政策現在替你的標的選擇標上價格","body":"The November 2026 National Policy for Nucleic Acid Synthesis Screening ties US federal funding to certified providers, a 50-nucleotide screening threshold, identity verification and eight-year record retention, and the defensive literature is now publishing algorithms against order-splitting evasion. None of this is technically hard; it is paperwork with a deadline, and it reaches any team that orders synthetic DNA, collaborates with US-funded partners or sends students to US labs. The selection consequence is that proximity to a pathogen or toxin list is now a cost measured in days: a review step, a supplier conversation, a delay a one-season team cannot absorb. Pick a target no screening desk has to think about. Then write the one-page ordering policy before the first order, and teach screening itself — sequence similarity and adversarial order splitting is a genuinely good dry-lab exercise.","body_zh":"2026 年 11 月的國家核酸合成篩查政策，把美國聯邦經費綁上認證供應商、50 個核苷酸的篩查門檻、身分查核與八年紀錄保存，而防禦端的文獻現在也在發表對付拆單規避的演算法。這些在技術上都不難；它是有期限的文書工作，而且管到任何會訂購合成 DNA、與受美國經費支持的夥伴合作，或送學生去美國實驗室的隊伍。對選題的後果是：靠近病原或毒素清單現在是一筆以天數計算的成本——一道審查、一輪跟供應商的往返，一段只有一季的隊伍吸收不了的延誤。挑一個篩查窗口完全不必多想的標的。然後在第一筆訂單之前把那一頁訂購政策寫好，並且把篩查本身當課程教——序列相似度與對抗式拆單是一個真正好的乾實驗練習。","chips":["Hard: nothing technical","Cost: days of delay","Pick far from any list","Cheapest credibility here"],"chips_zh":["困難：技術上沒有","代價：以天計的延誤","挑離清單遠的標的","這裡最便宜的信譽"]},{"kicker":"Taiwan","kicker_zh":"台灣","title":"Taiwan is building tanks and no design layer, so leave a design-layer artefact behind","title_zh":"台灣在蓋發酵槽、沒有設計層，所以要留下設計層的產出","body":"China holds about 70 percent of world fermentation capacity, and Taiwan's state-backed biomanufacturing push is a contract-development play with no visible synthetic-biology design layer, while Singapore's biological data centre and Israel's biological-AI infrastructure fund exactly that layer. A school team cannot out-build a CDMO and gains nothing by miniaturising one. The 2027 consequence is to choose a project whose surviving output sits in the design layer — a characterised part set, a measurement protocol calibrated to absolute units, a small local dataset with a benchmark task, a tool with a URL and a licence — and to name a Taiwanese end user before starting rather than after. TBMC in Hsinchu is physically close and ramping, and this report's roadmap already names three Taiwanese teams worth writing to.","body_zh":"中國掌握全球約 70% 的發酵量能，而台灣由國家主導的生物製造布局是一場代工開發的局，看不到合成生物學的設計層；新加坡的生物資料中心與以色列的生物 AI 基礎設施，補助的正好就是那一層。學校隊伍蓋不過 CDMO，把它縮小一號也得不到任何東西。2027 年的後果是：挑一個「留下來的產出落在設計層」的專案——一組特性已完整描述的元件、一份校準到絕對單位的量測流程、一個附帶基準任務的小型本地資料集、一個有網址與授權的工具——並且在開始之前、而不是結束之後，就先指名一個台灣的終端使用者。新竹的 TBMC 距離近、正在擴產，而本報告的路線圖已經指名三支值得寫信去聯絡的台灣隊伍。","chips":["Free: proximity and open doors","Hard: no local pipeline to join","Pick a design-layer deliverable"],"chips_zh":["免費：地理鄰近與已開的門","困難：沒有本地管道可加入","選設計層的交付物"]},{"kicker":"Agriculture","kicker_zh":"農業","title":"In an agricultural pick, the containment story is part of the science","title_zh":"農業題目裡，圍堵論述就是科學的一部分","body":"A Nature Biotechnology assessment of 77 agricultural biotechnologies found market viability and social acceptance, not technological readiness, to be the binding constraints, and USDA conditionally licensed an engineered gut microbe now in 35 million broilers on a feed-conversion argument rather than a welfare one. For a school team that is good news, because the missing deliverables are cheap: a readiness score across the published dimensions, a regulatory-pathway memo naming the responsible Taiwanese agency, and a cost per hectare or per bird. Light-dependence is itself a containment mechanism — no light, no function — which is a genuinely novel argument and free to make. The expensive half is the other one: this report's reading of the High School Top 10 found exactly one team in ten assayed a real sample, and that team took 1st Runner-up. Pick an agricultural target where a real sample is actually reachable inside one season.","body_zh":"Nature Biotechnology 對 77 項農業生技的評估發現，真正的限制是市場可行性與社會接受度，不是技術成熟度；而美國農業部有條件核准了一株工程化的腸道微生物，目前已用在 3,500 萬隻肉雞上，賣點是飼料轉換率，不是動物福利。對學校隊伍來說這是好消息，因為缺的交付物都很便宜：依已發表的面向打一份成熟度評分、一份指名台灣主責機關的法規路徑備忘錄，以及每公頃或每隻雞的成本。光依賴性本身就是一種圍堵機制——沒有光就沒有功能——這是一個真正新穎、而且免費就能提出的論點。貴的是另外那一半：本報告讀過高中組 Top 10 後發現，十支中恰好只有一支把檢測做在真實樣本上，而那一支拿下亞軍。挑一個在一季之內真的拿得到真實樣本的農業標的。","chips":["Free: readiness score and a regulator memo","Hard: a real sample","1 of 10 ran one","Containment as an argument"],"chips_zh":["免費：成熟度評分與法規備忘錄","困難：真實樣本","十支中只有一支做了","把圍堵當成論點"]},{"kicker":"Data and standards","kicker_zh":"資料與標準","title":"You cannot own a model, but a small Taiwanese dataset with a benchmark is yours for good","title_zh":"模型你擁有不了，但一個附帶基準的小型台灣資料集會一直是你的","body":"Evo 2 is free and in Nature while Basecamp raised USD 140M on the claim that its biodiversity data is what public databases cannot give you, which locates the value precisely. No school team will out-train Arc, and none needs to. A narrow, locally collected, well-labelled dataset with a public benchmark task attached is a durable asset that compounds across cohorts, and it is one of very few things a single season can actually finish: subtropical soil or coastal microbiomes, a local crop pathogen, a Taiwan rice-stress series, or the light dose-response series this line needs anyway. Adopt SBOL3 and calibrate fluorescence to absolute units from the start, because the field's self-identified weak link is that its data are not machine-readable enough to train the models it now depends on — and a new programme has nothing to retrofit.","body_zh":"Evo 2 免費而且登上 Nature，而 Basecamp 以「它的生物多樣性資料是公開資料庫給不了的」為說法募到 1.4 億美元，這就精準指出價值在哪。沒有學校隊伍會在訓練上贏過 Arc，也沒有誰需要。一個範圍窄、在本地採集、標註良好，並附上公開基準任務的資料集，是一項會跨屆累積的長期資產，而且是極少數一季真的做得完的東西：亞熱帶土壤或沿海微生物體、一種本地作物病原、一套台灣稻作逆境序列，或者這條主線本來就需要的光劑量反應序列。從一開始就採用 SBOL3，並把螢光校準到絕對單位，因為這個領域自己點出的弱點就是：它的資料機器可讀程度不足，餵不動它現在賴以為生的那些模型——而一個新的計畫沒有任何舊資料要回頭遷移。","chips":["Free: SBOL3, calibration, a repo","Hard: data nobody else has","The benchmark is the output"],"chips_zh":["免費：SBOL3、校準、一個程式庫","困難：別人沒有的資料","交付的是基準，不是模型"]}],"table":{"head":["Shift","What it makes cheap or free","What is still hard","What GEMS should pick or avoid","Reachable by a high-school team?"],"head_zh":["轉變","它讓什麼變便宜或免費","什麼仍然困難","GEMS 該選或該避開什麼","高中隊伍做得到嗎？"],"rows":[["Co-folding became free infrastructure","A protein-ligand complex on open weights, minutes on one GPU","Judging when pLDDT, PAE and ipTM are wrong; affinity ranking within a series","Pick: fold as a methods step and make the confidence audit the contribution. Avoid: a predicted structure as a result","Yes — Colab or one shared GPU"],["Generative binder and enzyme design crossed into function","20 to 35 designs for a few hundred dollars of compute; BindCraft and LigandMPNN are open","A quantitative binding number; cross-target hit rates near 25 percent, and 1 of 35 for Lambert-GA","Pick: a design campaign only with a named, costed assay. Avoid: natural-language design as a production tool","Yes, if the assay is outsourced or a partner lab is secured"],["Light became the control and cleaning layer of bioprocessing","LED hardware, a plate reader, published CcaSR, EL222 and LOV parts, and an empty field (12 papers, 0 of 105 teams)","An off-state, full dose-response at the right wavelength, and a closed loop rather than on-off induction","Pick: dose-response and the 640-against-672 nm off-state. Avoid: a new application on an unevidenced switch","Yes — the one frontier a school lab can hold"],["ML-guided DBTL beats intuition on real titres","COBRApy, flux balance analysis, a published B. subtilis model, scikit-learn, reproducible benchmarks","Library construction and a defensible titre assay; published gains need automation and six cycles","Pick: in-silico reproduction, then one real cycle on a hand-assayable library. Avoid: a titre promise in the abstract","Dry half yes; wet half one cycle at most"],["The Build step is being industrialised","Cell-free TXTL prototyping, with no transformation, growth or biosafety step","One-pot thousand-fragment synthesis, droplet pooled assembly, long-read design-space mapping","Pick: cell-free as the default first test of any circuit. Avoid: a build-throughput project","TXTL yes; pooled synthesis no"],["DNA synthesis competes on length and turnaround, not price","Nothing new — 0.07 to 0.13 USD per base pair is already the floor","Lead time, customs and tariff exposure; assembling long constructs locally","Pick: design for synthesis and order assemblable fragments. Avoid: a plan needing 10 kb in two weeks","Yes, as planning discipline"],["Nucleic-acid synthesis screening became binding policy","Nothing — this is a cost, not a saving","Nothing technical; it is paperwork with a deadline and a named contact","Pick: a target no screening desk has to think about. Avoid: anything near a pathogen or toxin list","Yes, and it is the cheapest credibility on this list"],["The centre of gravity moved to Asia; Taiwan sits on the manufacturing side","Proximity to fermentation capacity, TBMC in Hsinchu, three named Taiwanese teams","There is no Taiwanese design-layer pipeline to join, so GEMS has to be it","Pick: a design-layer deliverable with a named Taiwanese end user. Avoid: a scale-up demonstration","Yes"],["Agricultural synbio hit a market and acceptance wall, and got its regulatory unlock","Readiness scoring, a regulatory-pathway memo and a cost-per-hectare model — all afternoon work","A contained greenhouse trial, and a real sample rather than a surrogate","Pick: an agricultural target with a reachable real sample, using light-dependence as containment. Avoid: a surrogate-only readout","Yes, with a Taiwanese agricultural partner"],["The moat moved to proprietary data, and standards are the field's weak link","SBOL3, fluorescence calibrated to absolute units, a versioned repo, a public benchmark task","Collecting a dataset nobody else has, inside one season","Pick: one narrow Taiwanese dataset with a benchmark attached. Avoid: training a model from scratch","Yes — the cheapest durable asset here"],["Agentic AI became an experiment designer","A documented literature-to-hypothesis pass; Biomni is open source","Knowing when an agent is confidently wrong; only 4 of 106 teams stated what AI did not do","Pick: run the pass, then audit it and publish what it got wrong. Avoid: an AI assistant as the project","Yes"],["Biosensors are machine-designed, including the receptor","The design step, and published minimal binding domains to start from","Redesigning specificity and proving it; a lyophilised, field-ready cell-free format","Pick: port and properly characterise a sensor with a colorimetric or electrochemical readout. Avoid: promising a redesigned receptor","Partly — porting yes, receptor redesign no"],["Virtual cells and biological foundation models","The Virtual Cell Challenge is free and externally scored; Evo 2 weights are open","Generalisation to unseen contexts is unsolved; nothing predicts an engineered phenotype","Pick: enter as a separate dry-lab track. Avoid: making it the season's project — it has no wet-lab counterpart","Partly — as a side track only"],["Genome-scale generative design writes genomes that boot","Generating and critiquing sequences costs nothing; building them does not","Synthesis budget at kilobase-to-genome scale, and the sharpest dual-use profile in the field","Ignore as a build. Keep it as a reading-and-critique teaching unit with nothing synthesised","No — budget and dual-use both rule it out"],["Autonomous cloud labs and the Genesis Mission","Nothing — access is allocated by proposal to funded institutions","A 97-robot facility, proprietary closed stacks, and a per-device integration tax","Ignore, except for one habit worth keeping: write protocols in a machine-readable form","No — not available to a school team"],["The post-platform correction, Ginkgo against Twist","Nothing — filings are free to read, and that is the whole value here","Nothing; it is not a technical trend","Ignore as a topic. Keep the lesson: pitch one capability, never a platform","Not a project — a reading skill"],["The cost-of-goods wall","A one-page techno-economic model is free to write","Redesigning a fermentation tank is capital engineering with government money behind it","Ignore as a topic. Attach a one-page cost model to whatever is picked","No — the trend is for funded companies"],["Therapeutics is where the capital and the credibility gap both sit","Nothing — comparing a press release against a trial registry is a free exercise","BSL-2 or above, patients, a regulator and a clinical trial","Avoid any therapeutic framing for 2027, however small the model system","No — the facility requirement alone rules it out"],["Funding is up in dollars and down in companies","Nothing — it is a labour-market signal, not a capability","Nothing; it is not a technical trend","Ignore when choosing the topic. Use it when choosing what to teach","Not a project — a careers signal"]],"rows_zh":[["共摺疊成為免費的基礎設施","用開放權重算出蛋白質與配體的複合物，一張 GPU、幾分鐘","判斷 pLDDT、PAE 與 ipTM 何時出錯；同系列化合物之間的親和力排序","選：把摺疊當方法步驟，把信賴度查核當貢獻。避開：把預測出的結構當成果","可以——Colab 或一台共用 GPU"],["生成式結合蛋白與酵素設計跨進了功能層面","幾百美元運算費就能做 20 到 35 個設計；BindCraft 與 LigandMPNN 是開放的","一個定量的結合數字；跨標的命中率約 25%，Lambert-GA 是 35 個中 1 個","選：只在已指名、已估價的檢測到手時才開設計戰役。避開：把自然語言設計當生產工具","可以，前提是檢測外購或已談定合作實驗室"],["光成為生物製程的控制與清潔層","LED 硬體、讀盤機、已發表的 CcaSR、EL222 與 LOV 元件，加上一塊空地（12 篇論文、105 支中 0 支）","關閉態、在正確波長下的完整劑量反應，以及閉合迴路而非單純開關誘導","選：劑量反應與 640 對 672 nm 的關閉態。避開：在未被證明的開關上做新應用","可以——學校實驗室唯一守得住的前沿"],["機器學習導引的 DBTL 在真實產量上勝過直覺","COBRApy、通量平衡分析、一個已發表的 B. subtilis 模型、scikit-learn，以及可重現的基準","建函式庫與站得住的產量檢測；已發表的提升需要自動化與六個循環","選：先在電腦上重現，再在可手工檢測的函式庫上跑一個真實循環。避開：在摘要裡先承諾產量數字","乾實驗那一半可以；濕實驗最多一個循環"],["Build 環節正在工業化","無細胞 TXTL 原型製作，不需轉形、培養或生物安全步驟","一鍋式千片段合成、液滴混池組裝、長讀長設計空間繪製","選：把無細胞當成任何電路的預設第一輪測試。避開：以建構通量為題的專案","TXTL 可以；混池合成不行"],["DNA 合成的競爭在長度與交期，不在價格","沒有新的便宜——每鹼基對 0.07 到 0.13 美元已經是地板","交期、海關與關稅暴露；在本地把長構築體組起來","選：為合成而設計，訂可自行組裝的片段。避開：需要兩週拿到 10 kb 的計畫","可以，當成排程紀律"],["核酸合成篩查成為具約束力的政策","沒有——這是成本，不是省下來的錢","技術上沒有難處；它是有期限、要指名聯絡人的文書工作","選：一個篩查窗口完全不必多想的標的。避開：任何靠近病原或毒素清單的東西","可以，而且是這張清單上最便宜的信譽"],["重心移向亞洲，台灣站在製造這一邊","鄰近發酵量能、新竹的 TBMC、三支已指名的台灣隊伍","台灣沒有設計層的人才管道可加入，所以 GEMS 得自己當那個管道","選：一個有指名台灣終端使用者的設計層交付物。避開：放大量產的示範","可以"],["農業合成生物學撞上市場與接受度的牆，同時拿到法規解鎖","成熟度評分、法規路徑備忘錄與每公頃成本模型——都只是一個下午的事","一次有圍堵條件的溫室試驗，以及真實樣本而非替代品","選：真實樣本拿得到的農業標的，並以光依賴性作為圍堵論述。避開：只有替代品的讀出","可以，前提是有台灣的農業合作夥伴"],["護城河移到專有資料，而標準是這個領域的弱點","SBOL3、校準到絕對單位的螢光、版本控管的程式庫、一個公開基準任務","在一季之內收集到別人沒有的資料集","選：一個範圍窄、附帶基準的台灣資料集。避開：從頭訓練一個模型","可以——這裡最便宜的長期資產"],["代理式 AI 成為實驗設計者","一輪有記錄的文獻到假說流程；Biomni 是開放原始碼","知道代理什麼時候在自信地犯錯；106 支隊伍中只有 4 支寫出 AI 沒做什麼","選：跑那一輪，然後查核它，並公開它錯在哪裡。避開：把 AI 助手當成專案本身","可以"],["生物感測器改為機器設計，連受體本身也是","設計那一步，以及可當起點的已發表最小結合域","重新設計專一性並加以證明；做出凍乾、可下田的無細胞格式","選：移植並完整描述一個有比色或電化學讀出的感測器。避開：承諾重新設計受體","部分可以——移植可以，重新設計受體不行"],["虛擬細胞與生物基礎模型","Virtual Cell Challenge 免費而且由外部評分；Evo 2 的權重是開放的","推廣到未見過的情境尚未解決；沒有模型能預測新設計出的表現型","選：當成另一條獨立的乾實驗路線參加。避開：把它當成本季的專案——它沒有對應的濕實驗","部分可以——只能當副線"],["基因組尺度的生成式設計寫出能啟動的基因組","生成與批判序列不花錢；真的去做就花錢了","千鹼基到整個基因組級別的合成預算，以及這個領域最尖銳的雙重用途風險","當成建構專案就忽略它。保留成閱讀與批判的教學單元，完全不做合成","不行——預算與雙重用途各自都足以排除"],["自主雲端實驗室與 Genesis Mission","沒有——使用權是以計畫申請配給有經費的機構","一座 97 台機器人的設施、專有封閉的技術堆疊，以及每台裝置的整合成本","忽略，只留一個值得保留的習慣：把實驗流程寫成機器可讀的格式","不行——學校隊伍拿不到"],["後平台時代的修正：Ginkgo 對 Twist","沒有——財報免費可讀，而這裡的價值就只有這個","沒有；它不是一項技術趨勢","當題目就忽略它。保留那個教訓：推銷一項能力，絕不要推銷一個平台","不是專案——是一項閱讀能力"],["產品成本那道牆","寫一頁技術經濟分析是免費的","重新設計發酵槽是有政府資金在後面推的資本工程","當題目就忽略它。把一頁成本模型附在最後選定的任何題目上","不行——這項趨勢是給有經費的公司的"],["治療領域同時是資金所在與可信度落差所在","沒有——把新聞稿對照臨床試驗登錄比對，是免費的練習","BSL-2 以上、病人、主管機關與一場臨床試驗","2027 年避開任何治療用途的框架，不管模式系統多小","不行——光是設施要求就足以排除"],["資金總額上升、公司數量下降","沒有——它是勞動市場訊號，不是一項能力","沒有；它不是一項技術趨勢","選題時忽略它。決定教什麼的時候才用它","不是專案——是一個職涯訊號"]]},"checklist":["Write each candidate as a consequence, not a theme. Name the 2026 shift, then the one sentence saying what it makes newly worth attempting. If that sentence will not write, the idea is not a project yet.","Check that the hard half is the contribution. List every step that is now free — folding, binder design, flux balance, a literature pass — and confirm that none of them is what the project is being judged on.","Secure the measurement before the design. Name the assay, its cost, its provider and its lead time on the day the topic is chosen, not in month four.","Close the light-dependence gap before extending the line. Dose-response, an off-state at the right wavelength, and the plate-crosstalk test come before any new application built on the switch.","Pick a target no screening desk has to think about, and publish the one-page ordering and screening policy before the first order rather than after the first question.","Make a real sample a gate, not an extra. If the season can only reach a surrogate, change the target — exactly one team in ten in the High School Top 10 assayed a real sample, and that team took 1st Runner-up.","Choose a deliverable that sits in the design layer and name its Taiwanese end user: a characterised part set, a calibrated protocol, a benchmarked dataset, or a tool with a URL and a licence.","Refuse the four that are not available — an autonomous cloud lab, a genome-scale build, a therapeutic, and a scale-up economics demonstration — and write the refusal down so the discussion does not reopen in month three.","Do not justify the pick as a way to win. Chassis choice did not predict a Top 10 place among decorated teams (9 of 27 against 21 of 79, p = 0.62) and GEMS already holds a perfect controls score. Pick for the capability that survives the cohort."],"checklist_zh":["把每個候選題目寫成一個後果，而不是一個主題。先指名 2026 年的那項轉變，再寫出那一句話：它讓什麼變得剛好值得嘗試。如果那句話寫不出來，這個想法還不是一個專案。","確認困難的那一半才是貢獻。把現在已經免費的每個步驟列出來——摺疊、結合蛋白設計、通量平衡、文獻回合——然後確認專案被評審的點不是其中任何一個。","在設計之前先把量測談定。選定題目的那一天，就要指名檢測方法、它的費用、它的服務商與它的交期，而不是拖到第四個月。","在延伸這條主線之前先補上光依賴性的缺口。劑量反應、在正確波長下的關閉態，以及培養板光串擾的測試，都要排在任何建立在這個開關之上的新應用之前。","挑一個篩查窗口完全不必多想的標的，並在第一筆訂單之前、而不是第一個問題之後，就把那一頁訂購與篩查政策公開。","把真實樣本當成關卡，不是加分項。如果這一季只能做到替代品，就換標的——高中組 Top 10 裡恰好只有十分之一支隊伍把檢測做在真實樣本上，而那一支拿下亞軍。","選一個落在設計層的交付物，並指名它的台灣終端使用者：一組特性已完整描述的元件、一份校準過的流程、一個已附基準的資料集，或一個有網址與授權的工具。","拒絕那四個拿不到的東西——自主雲端實驗室、基因組尺度的建構、治療用途，以及放大量產的經濟性示範——並且把這個拒絕寫下來，讓討論不會在第三個月又被翻出來。","不要用「這樣比較會贏」來替選題找理由。在得獎隊伍之中，底盤選擇無法預測是否進 Top 10（27 支中 9 支對 79 支中 21 支，p = 0.62），而 GEMS 的對照組分數本來就已滿分。為那個能撐過這一屆學生的能力而選。"],"method":"The trend material in this block is not original. It comes from this report's own two trend reviews: the academic review, built from the Nature, Nature Biotechnology, Nature Methods and Nature Reviews Bioengineering subject listings, a bioRxiv synthetic-biology sweep from June to November 2026, PubMed, Consensus and targeted web searches across 25 recorded sources; and the industry review, built from 18 recorded sources covering company filings, funding announcements, policy documents and trade press. Both are published as their own tabs and every trend claim above can be traced there. What is original here is only the second step — the consequence. Those are judgements about what a one-season, school-lab, no-budget team should attempt, not measurements, and a reader is entitled to accept a trend and reject the inference drawn from it. Four things were verified against the report's own files rather than taken on trust. **Lambert-GA** was read from its team file, which records the High School Grand Prize plus Best Model, Best Wiki, Best Sustainable Development Impact and Best Village Project and a Best Hardware nomination, a BindCraft, Boltz-2, Protenix and Mosaic stack, biolayer interferometry bought in from Adaptyv Bio, the ROC-AUC 0.541 ensemble benchmark against 5,721 labelled designs, and 1 confirmed binder of 35 designs at KD 603.6 nM on under USD 400 of compute. The claim that it was *the only high-school team at that frontier* was narrowed using the high-school ceiling analysis, which reads the ten High School Top 10 dry labs and finds only Lambert-GA at the frontier of the toolchain; HKSSC used AlphaFold, so structure prediction was not unique, and nothing here extends to undecorated high-school teams. The light-and-*Bacillus* counts — 5 of 106, 5 of 106, intersecting in 1, and 0 of 105 excluding GEMS — and the Fisher exact null on non-model chassis (9 of 27 against 21 of 79, p = 0.62) come from the chassis census. ReLEAF's unevidenced light-dependence, the one-in-ten real-sample finding across the High School Top 10, and the 4-of-106 AI-disclosure figure come from the report's own roadmap and the blocks it cites. Nothing in this block was checked against a team's live wiki, and no new literature was read for it.","method_zh":"這個區塊的趨勢素材不是原創的。它來自本報告自己的兩份趨勢回顧：學術回顧建立在 Nature、Nature Biotechnology、Nature Methods 與 Nature Reviews Bioengineering 的主題清單、2026 年 6 月至 11 月的 bioRxiv 合成生物學掃讀、PubMed、Consensus，以及針對性的網路搜尋，共 25 筆記錄來源；產業回顧建立在 18 筆記錄來源，涵蓋公司財報、募資公告、政策文件與產業媒體。兩者都各自成頁發表，上面每一項趨勢主張都可以回溯到那裡。這裡原創的只有第二步——後果。那些是對「一支只有一季、一間學校實驗室、沒有預算的隊伍該嘗試什麼」所做的判斷，不是量測；讀者完全可以接受某項趨勢，同時否定由它推出的推論。有四件事是對照報告自己的檔案查核過的，不是信了就用。**Lambert-GA** 讀自它的團隊檔案，其中記載高中組總冠軍，外加最佳建模、最佳 Wiki、最佳永續發展影響與最佳 Village 專案，以及最佳硬體入圍；工具組為 BindCraft、Boltz-2、Protenix 與 Mosaic；生物層干涉量測向 Adaptyv Bio 外購；以 5,721 個有標註的設計所做的集成模型基準測試 ROC-AUC 為 0.541；三十五個設計中確認一個結合，KD 為 603.6 nM，運算費用不到 400 美元。至於「唯一站在那個前沿的高中隊伍」這個說法，是用高中天花板分析收窄過的：該分析讀了十支高中組 Top 10 的乾實驗室，發現只有 Lambert-GA 站在工具鏈前沿；HKSSC 用了 AlphaFold，所以結構預測本身並不獨特，而這裡的任何說法都不延伸到未得獎的高中隊伍。光與 *Bacillus* 的計數——106 支中 5 支、106 支中 5 支、交集 1 支、排除 GEMS 後 105 支中 0 支——以及非模式底盤的 Fisher 精確檢定虛無結果（27 支中 9 支對 79 支中 21 支，p = 0.62），來自底盤普查。ReLEAF 尚未被證明的光依賴性、高中組 Top 10 中「十支只有一支用真實樣本」的發現，以及 106 支中 4 支的 AI 揭露數字，來自報告自己的路線圖與它引用的區塊。這個區塊沒有任何內容是對照隊伍的現行 Wiki 查核的，也沒有為它額外讀任何新文獻。"},{"id":"proposals-rules","tab":"proposals","order":12,"kicker":"The register","kicker_zh":"資格檢查表","title":"The White List is a ceiling, not a default — a High School team has no Check-In route at all","title_zh":"白名單是天花板，不是預設值——高中組隊伍根本沒有 Check-In 管道","lede":"Read from iGEM's own 2026 rules pages. One sentence decides more about a 2027 project than anything else on this tab: work that would need a Check-In is simply not permitted in the High School section, so anything off the White List has no appeal, no exception and no collaborator workaround.","lede_zh":"直接讀自 iGEM 自己的 2026 年規則頁。有一句話對 2027 年選題的影響，比本分頁其他任何東西都大：需要 Check-In 的工作在高中組就是不被允許，所以任何不在白名單上的東西，沒有申訴、沒有例外，也沒有找合作者代勞這條路。","body":"**The operative sentence, from iGEM's live safety forms application.** *\"We are a High School team. Do we file Check In and Animal Use Forms? No. High School teams are required to conduct all their work with organisms, parts, and activities from the White List, so Check In Forms and Animal Use Forms are disabled for that section — you will not see them on the Submissions tab. Your team files the Project Safety Form only. Work that would require a Check In is not permitted in the High School section, so if your project seems to need one, email safety@igem.org before you build your plans around it.\"* The Rules and Policies page says the same thing more briefly: *\"High school teams must use organisms, parts and activities from the White List in their iGEM projects.\"* This restriction began in 2025 and was in force for 2026.\n\n**The collaborator loophole is closed in writing.** The White List page addresses it directly: a team that cannot get approval *\"by virtue of being a high school team (and therefore unable to seek approval via Check-In Forms)… should not engage collaborators to work beyond the White List.\"* A university partner does not widen the ceiling.\n\n**The White List has three axes and any one of them can end a project.** Organisms, parts and activities each have their own allowed column and their own Check-In column, so a project can be clean on the chassis and still blocked on the activity. Risk Group 1 microorganisms are in, with *E. coli* and *B. subtilis* named. Risk Group 2 is out. Risk Group 3 and 4 whole organisms, and parts from Risk Group 4 organisms, are banned outright for every team with or without a form.\n\n**The list only grows within a season.** *\"We might add things to the White List, but we will not remove things from the White List until after the Jamboree each year.\"* So a project that is clean in January stays clean — but 2027's list is not published yet, and all three of the things that matter most here have changed in the last two seasons.","body_zh":"**那句關鍵句，出自 iGEM 線上的安全表單系統。***「我們是高中隊伍，要交 Check In 與動物使用表嗎？不用。高中隊伍必須以白名單上的生物、零件與活動進行全部工作，所以該組別的 Check In Form 與 Animal Use Form 都被停用——你在繳交頁上根本看不到它們。你的團隊只需繳交 Project Safety Form。需要 Check In 的工作在高中組不被允許，所以如果你的專案看起來需要一份，請在圍繞它擬定計畫之前，先寫信到 safety@igem.org。」*規則與政策頁把同一件事說得更短：*「高中隊伍在 iGEM 專案中必須使用白名單上的生物、零件與活動。」*這項限制自 2025 年開始，2026 年仍然有效。\n\n**「找合作者代勞」這條路被白紙黑字堵死了。**白名單頁直接處理了這一點：一支因為*「身為高中隊伍（因而無法透過 Check-In Form 申請核准）」*而拿不到核准的隊伍，*「不應該找合作者去做超出白名單的工作。」*一位大學端的夥伴並不會把天花板撐高。\n\n**白名單有三個軸，任何一個都能終結一個專案。**生物、零件、活動各自有自己的允許欄與 Check-In 欄，所以一個專案可能底盤乾淨、卻被活動擋住。風險群 1 的微生物在名單上，並具名列出 *E. coli* 與 *B. subtilis*。風險群 2 不在。風險群 3 與 4 的整體生物、以及來自風險群 4 生物的零件，對所有隊伍都是直接禁止，有沒有表格都一樣。\n\n**名單在一個賽季內只會變多。***「我們可能會往白名單裡增加項目，但在每年 Jamboree 結束之前，我們不會從白名單移除任何項目。」*所以一月乾淨的專案會一直乾淨——但 2027 年的名單還沒公布，而這裡最要緊的三件事，在過去兩個賽季都變動過。","cards":[{"kicker":"Rule 1 · the ceiling","kicker_zh":"規則一 · 天花板","title":"No Check-In route means no appeal, no exception, and no partner workaround","title_zh":"沒有 Check-In 管道，就沒有申訴、沒有例外，也沒有夥伴代勞","body":"For a collegiate team the White List is a default that a Check-In can widen; the Safety and Security Committee replies to most within a few days. For a High School team the forms are **disabled in the submissions interface** and the rule is stated as a prohibition rather than a hurdle. The practical consequence for 2027 planning: eligibility is not a risk to manage during the season, it is a filter to apply before choosing. Email safety@igem.org in the design phase, not in June — and note that iGEM's own guidance says to do exactly that, *\"before you build your plans around it.\"*","body_zh":"對大學組隊伍而言，白名單是一個可以用 Check-In 撐開的預設值；安全與保安委員會對多數申請在數天內回覆。對高中組隊伍而言，那些表單在繳交介面上**直接被停用**，而規則的寫法是「禁止」，不是「門檻」。對 2027 年規劃的實際後果是：資格不是賽季中要管理的風險，而是選題前要套用的篩子。在設計階段就寫信給 safety@igem.org，不要等到六月——而且 iGEM 自己的指引講的正是這件事：*「在你圍繞它擬定計畫之前。」*","chips":["forms disabled, not just unlikely","no collaborator workaround","ask in the design phase"],"chips_zh":["表單被停用，不只是難通過","不能找合作者代勞","在設計階段就問"]},{"kicker":"Rule 2 · human anything","kicker_zh":"規則二 · 任何與人有關的","title":"Human samples need a Check-In, and testing on people is banned for everyone","title_zh":"人體檢體需要 Check-In，而在人身上測試對所有隊伍都是禁止的","body":"The White List puts *\"Conducting laboratory experiments using human samples, such as blood, DNA, other bodily specimens, and health or psychological outcomes, including from members of the team\"* in the Check-In column — so for this division it is simply unavailable. Separately, and for every team: *\"Testing your product on humans (including yourselves) is strictly prohibited. Engineered organisms you make should never come into direct contact with humans.\"* There is a double bind worth seeing: even where collegiate teams can apply, the committee is *\"unlikely to grant permission to use samples from vulnerable populations (such as minors/children…)\"* — and a high school team is largely made of minors. **What survives is surveys, interviews and public engagement**, which iGEM says do not need a Check-In, though they still require compliance with local law and institutional rules.","body_zh":"白名單把*「使用人體檢體進行實驗室實驗，例如血液、DNA、其他身體檢體，以及健康或心理結果，包括來自團隊成員的」*放在 Check-In 欄裡——所以對這個組別而言，它就是不可得。另外，對每一支隊伍都適用的是：*「在人身上（包括你們自己）測試你的產品是嚴格禁止的。你們製造的工程化生物，絕不應與人體直接接觸。」*還有一個值得看見的雙重束縛：即使在大學組可以申請的地方，委員會也*「不太可能核准使用來自弱勢族群（例如未成年人／兒童……）的檢體」*——而高中隊伍本身大多由未成年人組成。**還活得下來的是問卷、訪談與公眾參與**，iGEM 明說這些不需要 Check-In，但仍須遵守當地法律與機構規定。","chips":["unavailable to this division","banned outright for everyone","surveys and interviews survive"],"chips_zh":["這個組別不可得","對所有人都直接禁止","問卷與訪談還能做"]},{"kicker":"Rule 3 · nothing leaves the lab","kicker_zh":"規則三 · 沒有東西能離開實驗室","title":"Not the organism, not its product, not inside a containing device","title_zh":"生物不行，它的產物不行，裝在「密閉」裝置裡也不行","body":"*\"Teams cannot release or deploy their project outside of the laboratory at any time during the Competition or at the Grand Jamboree.\"* And the definition is wider than it first looks: *\"Taking the products of your GMOs outside of the lab… 'Products' includes any chemicals that your GMOs might synthesize, even if you purify them.\"* Also: *\"If you engineer an organism in the lab, you may not deliberately release it outside the lab, even inside a 'containing' device.\"* Every escape hatch in the policy is conditioned on advance permission from the committee, which this division cannot obtain. **Two things are explicitly exempt and they are the ones GEMS is strongest at:** releasing software or hardware is not release, and transporting an engineered organism between two labs in proper packaging for research or teaching is not release either — which is precisely what an inter-lab measurement ring needs.","body_zh":"*「隊伍不得在競賽期間或 Grand Jamboree 上的任何時刻，將其專案釋出或佈署到實驗室之外。」*而這個定義比乍看之下更寬：*「把你們基改生物的產物帶出實驗室……『產物』包括你們的基改生物可能合成的任何化學物質，即使你們已經純化了它。」*還有：*「如果你在實驗室裡工程改造了一個生物，你就不得刻意把它釋出到實驗室外，即使裝在一個『密閉』裝置裡也不行。」*政策裡每一個逃生口，都以委員會的事前許可為條件，而這個組別拿不到。**有兩件事是明文豁免的，而它們正好是 GEMS 最強的那兩項：**釋出軟體或硬體不算釋出；為研究或教學、以適當包裝在兩個實驗室之間運送工程化生物，也不算釋出——而那正是一個實驗室間量測環所需要的。","chips":["products count, even purified","containing devices do not help","software, hardware and lab-to-lab shipping are exempt"],"chips_zh":["產物也算，純化過也算","裝在密閉裝置裡也沒用","軟體、硬體與實驗室間運送豁免"]},{"kicker":"Rule 4 · environmental samples","kicker_zh":"規則四 · 環境樣本","title":"You may use the sample; you may not isolate anything from it","title_zh":"你可以用那個樣本；你不能從裡面分離出任何東西","body":"This is the rule that reshaped two proposals on this page, and it cuts a surprisingly fine line. Permitted: *\"As long as parts or organisms are not isolated from them, samples from the environment, the food industry, or other non-traditional suppliers may be used in your experiments.\"* Not permitted without a Check-In: *\"Isolation and sequencing of nucleic acids from environmental samples also require the submission of a Check In Form.\"* The White List reinforces it from the organism side, putting *\"All organisms isolated from an environmental sample\"* and *\"Any organisms obtained from outside the lab or from non-traditional / non-institutional suppliers\"* in the Check-In column. **So bulk field soil, river water or process water can be brought in and used as-is — but a metagenomics, bioprospecting or environmental-sequencing project is closed to this division.**","body_zh":"這就是把本頁兩個提案重新塑形的那條規則，而它切出的線比想像中細。允許的是：*「只要沒有從中分離出零件或生物，來自環境、食品工業或其他非傳統供應者的樣本，都可以用在你的實驗裡。」*沒有 Check-In 就不被允許的是：*「從環境樣本中分離與定序核酸，同樣需要提交 Check In Form。」*白名單從生物那一側再加固一次，把*「所有從環境樣本中分離出來的生物」*與*「任何取自實驗室外、或取自非傳統／非機構供應者的生物」*放進 Check-In 欄。**所以團體的田土、河水或製程水可以搬進實驗室照原樣使用——但總體基因體學、生物探勘或環境定序專案，對這個組別是關閉的。**","chips":["bulk sample in, nothing isolated out","metagenomics is closed","it reshaped two proposals here"],"chips_zh":["團體樣本進得來，分離不出去","總體基因體學關閉","它改寫了本頁兩個提案"]},{"kicker":"Rule 5 · parts and activities","kicker_zh":"規則五 · 零件與活動","title":"Where medical designs usually die, and it is not the chassis","title_zh":"醫療設計通常死在哪裡，而且不是死在底盤","body":"Protein-coding genes from animals, plants and Risk Group 1 or 2 microorganisms are white-listed **except** virulence factors, factors that help pathogens evade the immune system, and *\"factors that regulate the immune system, such as cytokines and interferons.\"* On the non-coding side, guide RNAs, microRNAs, siRNAs and shRNAs are white-listed only when they **do not** target human genes. That removes most RNA-therapeutic and immunomodulation designs in one stroke. On the activities axis, antimicrobial-resistance work has its own Check-In trigger, as does use of controlled chemicals, and so does anything that could make a hazardous agent more hazardous. **The chassis is rarely the problem. The part and the activity usually are.**","body_zh":"來自動物、植物與風險群 1 或 2 微生物的蛋白質編碼基因在白名單上，**除了**毒力因子、幫助病原逃避免疫系統的因子，以及*「調節免疫系統的因子，例如細胞激素與干擾素」*。在非編碼那一側，嚮導 RNA、microRNA、siRNA 與 shRNA 只有在**不**針對人類基因時才在白名單上。這一刀就移除了大部分 RNA 療法與免疫調節的設計。在活動軸上，抗藥性相關工作有自己的 Check-In 觸發條件，受管制化學品的使用也有，而任何可能讓危險因子變得更危險的事情同樣有。**底盤很少是問題。零件和活動通常才是。**","chips":["no cytokines or interferons","no human-gene-targeting RNA","AMR has its own trigger"],"chips_zh":["不能用細胞激素或干擾素","不能用針對人類基因的 RNA","抗藥性有自己的觸發條件"]},{"kicker":"Unresolved","kicker_zh":"未解","title":"Three things this screen could not settle, and none should be read as permission","title_zh":"這次篩查沒能定案的三件事，沒有一件該被讀成許可","body":"**The Registry Red Flag list could not be read.** The page sits behind a JavaScript challenge, so every Registry part a 2027 project plans to use must be checked by hand in a browser — red-flagged parts need a Check-In this division cannot file. **Human and primate cell lines are genuinely ambiguous.** The White List allows those *\"tested and certified free of known pathogens\"*, while iGEM's own Risk Groups table assigns *\"Most human and mammal cell lines\"* to Risk Group 2, which the organisms row routes to Check-In. No published page reconciles the two, and that single ambiguity decides whether any mammalian-cell project is available at all. **And no 2027 rules exist yet.** Everything here is the 2026 season read as a proxy; registration has historically opened in mid-January. The three items to re-verify first are the White List itself, the High School Check-In prohibition and the special award list — all three changed in the last two seasons.","body_zh":"**Registry 的 Red Flag 清單讀不到。**那個頁面擋在一道 JavaScript 驗證後面，所以 2027 年專案打算使用的每一個 Registry 元件，都必須在瀏覽器裡人工逐一確認——被標紅旗的元件需要這個組別無法提交的 Check-In。**人類與靈長類細胞株確實存在矛盾。**白名單允許那些*「經檢驗並證實不帶已知病原」*的細胞株，而 iGEM 自己的風險群表格卻把*「大多數人類與哺乳類細胞株」*列為風險群 2，而生物那一列又把風險群 2 導向 Check-In。沒有任何已發布頁面調和這兩者，而光是這一個模糊地帶，就決定了任何哺乳類細胞培養專案到底可不可行。**而且 2027 年的規則還不存在。**這裡的一切都是把 2026 賽季當成代理來讀的；報名在歷年上大約於一月中旬開放。最該優先重新確認的三件事是：白名單本身、高中組的 Check-In 禁令，以及特別獎清單——這三者在過去兩個賽季都變動過。","chips":["Red Flag list unread","cell lines genuinely ambiguous","2027 rules not published"],"chips_zh":["Red Flag 清單未讀到","細胞株確實模糊","2027 規則尚未公布"]}],"table":{"head":["Proposal","White List verdict","What triggers it","What to do"],"head_zh":["提案","白名單判定","觸發條件是什麼","該怎麼做"],"rows":[["**O1 · Characterise the switch**","**Clean**","*B. subtilis* is a named Risk Group 1 organism; Registry parts; all work in the lab; nothing leaves","Proceed. Check each Registry part against the Red Flag list by hand, since that list could not be read here"],["**O2 · What reaches the plant**","**Clean if re-scoped**","Only *Physcomitrella patens*, *Arabidopsis* spp. and *Nicotiana* spp. are white-listed plants; GMO products may not leave the lab","Use a white-listed plant, not rice. Bring bulk soil in and use it as-is. Keep the model about rice and say so"],["**M1 · Resistance genes in water**","**Not permitted**","Isolation and sequencing of nucleic acids from environmental samples; and antimicrobial-resistance experiments — two independent triggers","Drop the metagenomics. Sense a purchased analyte standard and a bulk matrix, and publish where the chain breaks"],["**M2 · Oral-pathogen biofilm**","**Unresolved — ask in writing**","Risk Group 2 organisms need a Check-In this division cannot file; organisms from non-traditional suppliers do too","Email safety@igem.org before designing. If the answer is no, fall back to a Risk Group 1 indicator and say why"],["**N1 · Inter-lab ring**","**Clean, and explicitly blessed**","Transporting an engineered organism between two labs in proper packaging for research or teaching is listed as NOT release","Proceed. Package properly and state the arrangement on the safety page"],["**N2 · Process-water sensor**","**Clean if lab-only**","Bringing a product of a GMO outside the lab needs permission; controlled chemicals have their own trigger","Bring the water to the lab, not the sensor to the plant. Confirm the contaminant is not a controlled chemical"],["*Any project using human samples*","**Not permitted**","Human samples, including from team members, sit in the Check-In column; testing on people is banned outright for every team","Use surveys, interviews and public engagement instead — iGEM states these need no Check-In"],["*Any project using a Risk Group 2 organism*","**Not permitted**","Risk Group 2 needs enhanced containment, which routes to Check-In","There is no route. Choose a Risk Group 1 chassis and state the substitution on the wiki"]],"rows_zh":[["**O1 · 把開關特性描述清楚**","**乾淨**","*B. subtilis* 是具名的風險群 1 生物；使用 Registry 元件；全部工作在實驗室內；沒有東西離開","可以進行。每一個 Registry 元件要人工到瀏覽器裡對 Red Flag 清單確認，因為那份清單這次讀不到"],["**O2 · 真正送到植物上的東西**","**改寫範圍後乾淨**","白名單植物只有 *Physcomitrella patens*、*Arabidopsis* spp. 與 *Nicotiana* spp.；基改產物不得離開實驗室","用白名單植物，不要用水稻。把團體田土搬進來照原樣使用。模型仍然可以是關於水稻的，而且要寫明"],["**M1 · 水中的抗藥性基因**","**不被允許**","從環境樣本分離與定序核酸；以及抗藥性相關實驗——兩條互相獨立的觸發條件","拿掉總體基因體學。改成感測一個買得到的分析物標準品與一個團體基質，並公開鏈條斷在哪裡"],["**M2 · 口腔致病菌生物膜**","**未解——先要到書面回覆**","風險群 2 的生物需要這個組別無法提交的 Check-In；來自非傳統供應者的生物同樣需要","設計之前先寫信給 safety@igem.org。如果答案是否定的，退回用風險群 1 的指示菌，並寫明原因"],["**N1 · 實驗室間量測環**","**乾淨，而且明文背書**","為研究或教學、以適當包裝在兩個實驗室之間運送工程化生物，被明列為「不算釋出」","可以進行。包裝要確實，並在安全頁上寫明這個安排"],["**N2 · 製程水感測器**","**只在實驗室內則乾淨**","把基改生物的產物帶出實驗室需要許可；受管制化學品有自己的觸發條件","把水送進實驗室，不要把感測器送到廠裡。確認該污染物不是受管制化學品"],["*任何使用人體檢體的專案*","**不被允許**","人體檢體，包括來自團隊成員的，都在 Check-In 欄裡；在人身上測試對所有隊伍都直接禁止","改用問卷、訪談與公眾參與——iGEM 明說這些不需要 Check-In"],["*任何使用風險群 2 生物的專案*","**不被允許**","風險群 2 需要加強圍堵，而那會導向 Check-In","沒有任何管道。改選風險群 1 的底盤，並在 wiki 上寫明這個替換"]]},"checklist":["Screen every candidate against all three White List axes before costing it: the organism, the part and the activity. A project can be clean on the chassis and dead on the activity.","Email safety@igem.org during the design phase, not in June. iGEM's own guidance says to ask before you build your plans around it, and the reply usually comes within days.","Ask iGEM in writing about the human and primate cell line contradiction before any mammalian-cell project is considered. The White List and the Risk Groups table disagree, and no published page reconciles them.","Check every planned Registry part against the Red Flag list by hand in a browser. That list sits behind a JavaScript challenge and could not be read here, and a red-flagged part needs a Check-In this division cannot file.","Do not plan on a university partner widening the ceiling. The White List page closes that door explicitly for high school teams.","Keep bulk environmental samples, drop anything that isolates or sequences from them. Using the sample is permitted; isolating from it is not.","Design the demonstration around software and hardware, which are exempt from the release rules, rather than around taking an engineered product anywhere.","Re-verify the White List, the High School Check-In prohibition and the special award list when the 2027 rules publish, historically mid-January. All three changed in the last two seasons.","File the Project Safety Form on time. It is the only safety form this division files, and missing a required form is grounds for disqualification rather than a lost point."],"checklist_zh":["在估算成本之前，先把每個候選題目對照白名單三個軸篩一遍：生物、零件、活動。一個專案可能底盤乾淨、卻死在活動上。","在設計階段就寫信到 safety@igem.org，不要等到六月。iGEM 自己的指引就說要在圍繞它擬定計畫之前先問，而回覆通常數天內就到。","在考慮任何哺乳類細胞專案之前，先就人類與靈長類細胞株的矛盾向 iGEM 取得書面答覆。白名單與風險群表格互相牴觸，而且沒有任何已發布頁面調和它們。","每一個預定使用的 Registry 元件，都要人工在瀏覽器裡對 Red Flag 清單確認。那份清單擋在 JavaScript 驗證後面，這次讀不到，而被標紅旗的元件需要這個組別無法提交的 Check-In。","不要指望大學端的夥伴能把天花板撐高。白名單頁針對高中隊伍明文堵死了這條路。","保留團體環境樣本，拿掉任何從中分離或定序的步驟。使用樣本是允許的；從中分離則不允許。","把成果展示設計在軟體與硬體上——它們豁免於釋出規則——而不是設計成把一個工程化產物帶到任何地方。","等 2027 年規則公布（歷年約在一月中旬）時，重新確認白名單、高中組 Check-In 禁令，以及特別獎清單。這三者在過去兩個賽季都變動過。","準時繳交 Project Safety Form。那是這個組別唯一要交的安全表單，而漏繳必繳表單的後果是取消資格，不是扣分。"],"method":"Read from iGEM's own published pages for the 2026 season, which is the most recent season published; no 2027 rules exist yet, so everything here is a 2026 proxy and is labelled as such. Primary sources: the White List guidance and policy pages and the Risk Groups, Human Experimentation, Release Beyond Containment and Environmental Samples policies on responsibility.igem.org; the Rules and Policies, Awards, Medals and Registration pages on competition.igem.org; and the live safety forms application at teams.igem.org, which turned out to state the high-school rule most explicitly. Every iGEM site is a client-rendered application that returns an empty shell to a plain fetch, so each page was read by downloading its compiled JavaScript content chunk from the same origin and extracting string literals with entities unescaped; those chunk hashes are tied to one release and will change on the next deploy. Operative sentences are quoted verbatim so a reader can check them. This is an eligibility screen and not legal or institutional advice: iGEM states plainly that its approval does not replace institutional or national approval, and that a team needs both. Three items could not be settled and are named on this page rather than guessed -- the Registry Red Flag list, the human and primate cell line contradiction, and whether any high-school-specific containment-level rule exists beyond what the White List implies. Anything marked unresolved here should be treated as unresolved rather than as permission.","method_zh":"直接讀自 iGEM 自己 2026 賽季的已發布頁面，那是目前最新已發布的賽季；2027 年規則尚不存在，所以本頁一切都是以 2026 年作為代理，並已如此標註。主要來源：responsibility.igem.org 上的白名單指引頁與政策頁，以及風險群、人體實驗、超出圍堵之釋出、環境樣本等政策；competition.igem.org 上的規則與政策、獎項、獎牌與報名頁；以及 teams.igem.org 上線上的安全表單系統——結果那裡才是把高中組規則講得最明確的地方。iGEM 所有網站都是用戶端渲染的應用程式，對一般抓取只會回傳空殼，所以每個頁面都是從同一來源下載其編譯後的 JavaScript 內容區塊、並將實體字元還原後擷取字串常數來閱讀的；那些區塊雜湊綁定於某一次發布，下次部署就會改變。關鍵句一律逐字引用，讓讀者可以自行查核。這是一份資格篩查，不是法律或機構層面的建議：iGEM 明白表示，它的核准不能取代機構或國家層級的核准，兩者都需要。有三件事無法定案，已在本頁具名列出而不是用猜的——Registry 的 Red Flag 清單、人類與靈長類細胞株的矛盾，以及除了白名單隱含之外、是否存在任何高中組專屬的圍堵等級規定。本頁任何標示為未解的事項，都應該當成未解，而不是當成許可。"},{"id":"gems-gap","tab":"roadmap","order":20,"kicker":"Original analysis","kicker_zh":"原創分析","title":"GEMS measured against its own report","title_zh":"用這份報告的標準衡量 GEMS 自己","lede":"Every finding in this report, turned back on the team that commissioned it. Some of it is flattering and some of it is not, and the roadmap only means anything if both are said plainly.","lede_zh":"把這份報告的每一項發現，轉回來檢視委託這份報告的團隊。有些結論好看，有些不好看，而路線圖只有在兩者都直說時才有意義。","body":"**Start with what already meets the standard, because it is more than expected.**\n\nThe report's central result is that teams which close the model–data loop reach a Top 10 at 53% against 23%. GEMS-Taiwan closes it, and in one respect goes beyond anything else in the 2026 field: the crop-stress index was *fitted* to Taiwan's own harvest record — 25 years of county rice yields against ERA5 reanalysis, all 32,767 combinations of fifteen candidate terms scored on held-out years — and then tested **prospectively**, frozen on 26 September before any county published. County error came in at 365 kg/ha against 419 for a plain trend line. Separately, a growth rate of 0.2986 h⁻¹ with a 90% interval was registered in writing on 1 October, before a single bioreactor run; run 6 landed inside it at 0.286 ± 0.010.\n\nNo other team in this report pre-registered a quantitative prediction and scored it afterwards. It is the single highest-credibility item on the wiki and it cost nothing but committing in writing before the data arrived.\n\nThe provenance discipline is likewise at the top of the field, alongside TU Delft's. The honesty is real too: run 7 was excluded from scoring with the reason given, the curve-shape endpoint was recorded as not scored, and a 68-year payback was published against a partner's 4.9-year figure with the disagreement named rather than resolved. The human-practices loop closes properly — Prof. Chen Wen-Liang said in April that the organism could not be contained and that biological temperature sensing was not precise enough, and both the hollow-fibre perfusion reactor and the entire electronic sensing layer came out of that one conversation. Education was measured with pre- and post-surveys and the failures published, including the 30% who got DNA base pairing wrong.\n\n**Now the gaps, each tied to a finding in this report.**\n\n*The software has no front door.* The report found that 8 of 21 award-winning tools survive, and that the one habit separating them is a hosting decision made months early — every live tool was up on wiki-freeze day, every source-only tool lists localhost. The digital twin is MIT-licensed on GitLab and genuinely substantial, but it is a reactor controller: there is nothing a stranger can open. A simulator mode running on recorded data, at a URL, would move it from the source-only column to the live one. Two **high-school** teams managed exactly this in 2026.\n\n*The structure-prediction stack is a generation behind.* The census found AlphaFold still dominates iGEM at roughly a third of teams while the research literature has moved to open models. GEMS used AlphaFold with a pre-set confidence gate, which is better practice than most — but Boltz-2, Chai-1 and the MPNN family are where Lambert-GA, Heidelberg and Princeton were working. This is the cheapest capability gap to close on the list.\n\n*No parts contribution.* Taiwan took zero nominations in any of the four parts awards across both tiers in 2026, and GEMS is part of that zero. The report found that teams with no venture at all — HBUT-China, WHU-China, Squirrel-Beijing, BASIS-China — still contributed infrastructure other teams can reuse, and that this has a longer half-life than a business plan. A characterised, documented *B. subtilis* optogenetic part is the obvious candidate, and it is the same work as the Phase 3 research line.\n\n*The model is not yet fitted at the scale it is used.* The CcaSR Hill transfer function is assumed to hold at 20 L when every induction run was at a single light intensity. By the report's own loop-closure test, that step is modelled rather than measured — and the wiki's amber rail says so, which is to its credit, but saying so is not the same as fixing it.\n\n*The integration gaps are stated and still open.* Green-light induction tested but not wired in; dissolved-oxygen calibration did not hold; the protectant amount cannot be measured. These are the honest limits of a nine-month competition, and they are exactly the work an institution — rather than a team — exists to finish.\n\n*No collaboration page.* GEMS appears on no other Taiwanese team's collaboration page and has none of its own, while NYCU-Taiwan's July meet-up drew 53 people from five teams. Being findable is a precondition for everything in Phase 4.\n\n**The summary, stated plainly.** GEMS-Taiwan's weakness is not rigour — on provenance, pre-registration and honest reporting it is at or near the top of the entire 2026 field, high school and collegiate alike. The weakness is **reach**: a tool nobody outside can open, a part nobody else can order, a page nobody can find. That is a different problem from the one most teams have, and it needs a different year.","body_zh":"**先談已經達標的部分，因為比預期多。**\n\n這份報告的核心結果是：閉合模型與資料迴圈的團隊，進入 Top 10 的比例是 53% 對 23%。GEMS-Taiwan 做到了，而且在一點上超越了 2026 年其他所有隊伍：作物逆境指數是*擬合*出來的——以台灣自己的收穫紀錄，25 年的各縣市稻作產量對上 ERA5 再分析資料，把十五個候選項的全部 32,767 種組合在保留年份上評分——然後做了**前瞻性**檢驗，在 9 月 26 日任何縣市公布前就凍結。縣市誤差為 365 kg/ha，而單純趨勢線為 419。另外，他們在 10 月 1 日、任何一次生物反應器實驗之前，就以書面登記了 0.2986 h⁻¹ 的生長速率與 90% 區間；第 6 批次落在區間內，為 0.286 ± 0.010。\n\n本報告中沒有第二支團隊預先登記一個量化預測並在事後評分。這是整個 wiki 上可信度最高的一項，而它的代價只是「在資料出現之前先白紙黑字承諾」。\n\n來源標註的紀律同樣位居領先群，與 TU Delft 並列。誠實也是真的：第 7 批次被排除計分並附上理由，曲線形狀的指標被記為未評分，而 68 年的回收期與合作夥伴的 4.9 年並陳，歧異被指名而非被抹平。人類實踐的迴圈確實閉合——陳文亮教授在四月指出該菌無法被圍堵、且生物性溫度感測不夠精準，而中空纖維灌流反應器與整個電子感測層都出自那一次對話。教育工作以課前課後問卷量測，並公布失敗，包括 DNA 鹼基配對只有 30% 答對。\n\n**接著是落差，每一項都對應本報告的一個發現。**\n\n*軟體沒有入口。* 報告發現 21 個得獎工具中只有 8 個存活，而唯一的區分習慣是提前幾個月做的架站決定——每個仍在線的工具在 wiki 凍結日就已上線，每個只有原始碼的工具都只列 localhost。數位孿生以 MIT 授權放在 GitLab 上，內容扎實，但它是反應器控制器：沒有任何東西是陌生人打得開的。一個以錄製資料運行的模擬模式，放上一個網址，就能把它從「僅有原始碼」移到「仍在線」。2026 年有兩支**高中**隊伍正是做到了這件事。\n\n*結構預測的工具鏈落後一個世代。* 普查發現 AlphaFold 在 iGEM 仍占約三分之一的團隊，而研究文獻早已轉向開源模型。GEMS 使用 AlphaFold 並設了預先訂定的信心門檻，這比多數團隊的做法更好——但 Boltz-2、Chai-1 與 MPNN 家族才是 Lambert-GA、Heidelberg 與 Princeton 工作的地方。這是清單上最便宜就能補起來的能力落差。\n\n*沒有元件貢獻。* 2026 年台灣在兩個層級的四項元件獎中全數掛零，GEMS 也是那個零的一部分。報告發現，完全沒有創業規劃的團隊——HBUT-China、WHU-China、Squirrel-Beijing、BASIS-China——仍然貢獻了其他隊伍可重用的基礎設施，而那東西的半衰期比商業計畫書長。一個經過表徵、文件完整的*枯草桿菌*光遺傳元件是最明顯的候選，而且它與階段三的研究路線是同一件工作。\n\n*模型尚未在它被使用的尺度上完成擬合。* CcaSR 的 Hill 轉移函數被假定在 20 公升仍然成立，但所有誘導實驗都只在單一光強度下進行。依本報告自己的迴圈閉合判準，那一步是模擬而非量測——wiki 的琥珀色軌道確實這麼標示了，這一點值得肯定，但標示出來不等於解決了它。\n\n*已載明的整合缺口仍然敞著。* 綠光誘導已測試但未整合；溶氧校正未能維持；保護劑用量無法量測。這些是九個月競賽的誠實極限，而它們也正是「機構」——而非「團隊」——存在的目的所在。\n\n*沒有 collaboration 頁面。* GEMS 沒有出現在任何其他台灣團隊的合作頁面上，自己也沒有一個；而 NYCU-Taiwan 七月的聚會吸引了來自五支隊伍的 53 人。能被找到，是階段四所有事情的前提。\n\n**直說結論。** GEMS-Taiwan 的弱點不是嚴謹度——在來源標註、預先登記與誠實報告上，它在整個 2026 年、無論高中組或大專組，都位居頂端或接近頂端。它的弱點是**觸及**：一個外人打不開的工具、一個別人訂不到的元件、一個沒有人找得到的頁面。那是一個與多數團隊不同的問題，也需要一個不同的年度。","cards":[{"kicker":"Already at the top of the field","kicker_zh":"已經位居領先","title":"The only pre-registered prediction in the report","title_zh":"本報告中唯一的預先登記預測","body":"A growth rate of 0.2986 h⁻¹ with a 90% interval, registered in writing on 1 October before any bioreactor run; run 6 landed inside it at 0.286 ± 0.010. The crop-stress index was frozen on 26 September and tested against county yields nobody had published yet. No other team in this report did either. Keep doing it, and make it a house rule rather than one person's idea.","body_zh":"0.2986 h⁻¹ 的生長速率與 90% 區間，在 10 月 1 日、任何生物反應器實驗之前就以書面登記；第 6 批次以 0.286 ± 0.010 落在區間內。作物逆境指數則在 9 月 26 日凍結，並對當時尚未公布的縣市產量進行檢驗。本報告中沒有第二支團隊做過其中任何一件。請繼續做，並把它變成全機構的規則，而不是某一個人的點子。","chips":["unique in 2026"],"chips_zh":["2026 年唯一一例"]},{"kicker":"Already at the top of the field","kicker_zh":"已經站在全體前列","title":"Five of five on the controls that could have broken its own claim, and it still did not place","title_zh":"五類「可能推翻自己主張」的對照全部做到，卻仍然沒有名次","body":"Scored against all 30 Top 10 teams of 2026 on five kinds of falsification control, **GEMS-Taiwan holds all five** — a chassis-only arm, an exclusion of a rival mechanism, a confound removed by design and re-tested, validation against held-back data, and an unfavourable result published against its own headline. Only six other teams in thirty did, and of those seven perfect scorers **five missed the podium, GEMS among them**. The disclosure is the striking part: GEMS published an ELISA in which the untransformed host read in the same range as its own constructs, and said plainly that the differences there cannot be attributed to expression level. That is the same habit as 2024, whose LC50 series disclosed its own incomplete arm and whose *E. coli* exclusion declared which induction condition it could not cover. **Three seasons of it.** So when this tab says the weakness is reach rather than rigour, this is the measurement behind it — and it also means adding controls is not a lever this team has left to pull.","body_zh":"把 2026 年 30 支 Top 10 隊伍放在五類否證對照上評分，**GEMS-Taiwan 五類全有**——只有底盤的對照組、排除對手機制、以設計移除混淆因子後重測、拿留存資料做驗證，以及公開一項對自己標題主張不利的結果。三十支裡只有另外六支做到，而這七支滿分隊伍中**有五支沒上頒獎臺，GEMS 就是其中一支**。真正值得一提的是那份揭露：GEMS 登出了一張 ELISA，其中未轉形宿主讀到和自家構築體同一個範圍，並且寫明那裡的差異不能歸因於表現量。這和 2024 年是同一個習慣——那一年的 LC50 系列揭露了自己不完整的實驗組，而 *E. coli* 的排除也明白宣告了它沒能涵蓋哪一個誘導條件。**三個賽季都是這樣。**所以當本頁說「弱的是觸及範圍，不是嚴謹度」，這就是背後的量測——而它同時也意味著，加對照已經不是這支隊伍還能拉的槓桿。","chips":["5 of 5 control types","7 perfect scorers, 5 unplaced","three seasons of disclosure"],"chips_zh":["五類對照全有","七支滿分，五支無名次","三季都有揭露"]},{"kicker":"The gap","kicker_zh":"落差","title":"The digital twin has no front door","title_zh":"數位孿生沒有入口","body":"MIT-licensed on GitLab and genuinely substantial — live OD600, pH, four pressure channels, an autoencoder alarm, a Kalman forecast, a hydraulic fouling model and the BLASTAM infection rule. But it is a reactor controller: there is nothing a stranger can open. A simulator mode running on recorded data, at a URL, moves it from source-only to live. Two high-school teams managed that in 2026.","body_zh":"以 MIT 授權放在 GitLab 上，內容扎實——即時 OD600、pH、四個壓力通道、自編碼器警報、Kalman 預測、水力積垢模型，以及 BLASTAM 感染規則。但它是反應器控制器：沒有任何東西是陌生人打得開的。一個以錄製資料運行、放在網址上的模擬模式，就能讓它從「僅有原始碼」變成「仍在線」。2026 年有兩支高中隊伍做到了。","chips":["source-only","a URL would fix it"],"chips_zh":["只有原始碼","給個網址就解決了"]},{"kicker":"The gap","kicker_zh":"落差","title":"Zero parts nominations, and Taiwan's zero is shared","title_zh":"元件獎掛零，而台灣的零是共同的","body":"Taiwan took no nomination in any of the four parts awards across both tiers in 2026. Teams with no venture at all still contributed parts other teams can reuse, and that outlives a business plan. A characterised, documented *B. subtilis* optogenetic part is the obvious candidate — and it is the same work as the Phase 3 research line, not extra work.","body_zh":"2026 年台灣在兩個層級的四項元件獎中全數未獲提名。完全沒有創業規劃的團隊，仍然貢獻了其他隊伍可重用的元件，而那比商業計畫書活得更久。一個經過表徵、文件完整的*枯草桿菌*光遺傳元件是最明顯的候選——而且它與階段三的研究路線是同一件工作，不是額外的工作。","chips":["same work as Phase 3"],"chips_zh":["與階段三同一件事"]},{"kicker":"The gap","kicker_zh":"落差","title":"The Hill curve is assumed at 20 L, not measured there","title_zh":"Hill 曲線在 20 公升是假設的，不是量出來的","body":"Every induction ran at a single light intensity, so the CcaSR transfer function is modelled rather than measured at the scale it is used. The wiki's amber rail says so, which is to its credit — but saying so is not fixing it. A dose–response series across intensities at working volume is a term's work and would close the loop at the step that currently carries the most weight.","body_zh":"所有誘導實驗都在單一光強度下進行，因此 CcaSR 轉移函數在它實際被使用的尺度上是模擬而非量測。wiki 的琥珀色軌道確實標示了這一點，值得肯定——但標示不等於修正。在工作體積下跨多個光強度做一組劑量反應曲線，是一個學期的工作量，並且能在目前承載最多重量的那一步閉合迴圈。","chips":["single intensity"],"chips_zh":["只有單一強度"]},{"kicker":"The verdict","kicker_zh":"結論","title":"The weakness is reach, not rigour","title_zh":"弱點是觸及，不是嚴謹","body":"On provenance, pre-registration and honest reporting, GEMS-Taiwan sits at or near the top of the entire 2026 field, high school and collegiate alike. What it lacks is a tool anybody outside can open, a part anybody else can order, and a page anybody can find. That is a different problem from the one most teams have, and it needs a different kind of year. The rigour half is no longer an impression: across the 2026 Top 10, GEMS holds all five falsification-control types and sits in the top seven of thirty, and across its own three seasons it has disclosed an incomplete arm every year. The reach half is where every remaining item on this roadmap lives.","body_zh":"在來源標註、預先登記與誠實報告上，GEMS-Taiwan 位居整個 2026 年——無論高中組或大專組——的頂端或接近頂端。它缺的是一個外人打得開的工具、一個別人訂得到的元件、一個有人找得到的頁面。那是一個與多數團隊不同的問題，也需要一個不同性質的年度。　「嚴謹度」這一半已經不再只是印象：在 2026 年 Top 10 之中，GEMS 五類否證對照全有，位居三十支裡的前七；而在自己的三個賽季裡，它每一年都揭露過一組不完整的實驗。剩下的這份路線圖，每一條都住在「觸及範圍」那一半。","chips":["rigour: top of field","reach: not yet"],"chips_zh":["嚴謹：全場頂尖","觸及：還沒到"]}],"method":"Compares the GEMS-Taiwan team file in this report against the findings of the other nine analyses. The file was researched from the team's own 2026 wiki on the same terms as every other team, and much of the critical material here is the team's own stated limits rather than our discovery — the wiki is unusually candid, which is what makes this comparison possible at all. Where we say a gap exists, it is a gap relative to practice elsewhere in the 2026 field, not a judgement that the work is poor.","method_zh":"本篇以本報告中的 GEMS-Taiwan 團隊檔案，對照其餘九篇分析的發現。該檔案與其他所有團隊採用相同標準，取自該隊自己的 2026 wiki；此處許多批評性的材料其實出自團隊自述的限制，而非我們的發現——那個 wiki 異常坦白，這也正是這項比較得以成立的原因。凡我們指出存在落差之處，都是相對於 2026 年其他團隊實作的落差，而非認定該工作做得不好。"},{"id":"good-pipeline","tab":"good","order":20,"kicker":"The pipeline","kicker_zh":"題目清單","title":"What is actually in the pipeline right now","title_zh":"目前清單上真正有什麼","lede":"Two live entries, both inherited from relationships the ReLEAF season happened to create, and three proposals that come from this report's evidence rather than from a person. That is an honest picture of a programme at the start, and the asymmetry is the most useful thing on this page.","lede_zh":"兩個進行中的題目，都是 ReLEAF 那一季碰巧建立起來的關係留下的；另外三個是提案，來自這份報告的證據而不是來自某一個人。這就是一個剛起步的計畫的真實樣貌，而這個不對稱，正是本頁最有用的東西。","body":"A pipeline is only worth keeping if it distinguishes between a problem **someone brought you** and a problem **you thought of**. The first kind already passes criterion one; the second kind has to earn it, and most never do. Both belong here, but they must be labelled, because a programme that forgets the difference quietly fills up with its own ideas.\n\nRight now GEMS has two of the first kind, and both arrived the same way: not through a search for projects, but because a team spent a season in a place and kept talking to the people there. That is worth noticing, because it is the actual mechanism by which this pipeline will fill. **Relationships generate problems; project searches generate topics.** The implication for 2027 is not to brainstorm harder but to go back, without a proposal in hand, to the places the 2026 season already reached.\n\nThe three proposals below come from the report and are marked as such. Each one passes the four criteria on paper, which is exactly their weakness: nobody outside GEMS has yet said they want any of them. They are candidates for a listening visit, not plans.\n\n*The partner behind both live entries is named here, at GEMS's decision: Chen Hui-wen (陳惠雯), who farms and teaches by natural-farming principles.* What is not written down here is what that farm's specific difficulties actually are — not out of discretion, but because nobody has asked yet. That is what the first entry below is for. When those constraints are finally recorded, they should be recorded in the farmer's own words and published only with their agreement.","body_zh":"一份題目清單要有價值，必須區分**別人帶來的**題目和**你自己想到的**題目。前者已經通過了條件一；後者必須自己掙到，而大多數永遠掙不到。兩種都該放進來，但一定要標示清楚，因為一個忘記這個差別的計畫，會不知不覺被自己的點子塞滿。\n\n目前 GEMS 有兩個屬於第一種，而且它們的來路一樣：不是靠找專案找到的，而是因為一支隊伍在一個地方待了一季，並且持續跟那裡的人說話。這一點值得注意，因為這正是這份清單日後會被填滿的真實機制。**關係會長出題目，找專案只會長出主題。** 對 2027 年的意義不是更用力腦力激盪，而是回到 2026 年那一季已經走到的地方，手上不帶提案地回去。\n\n下面三個提案來自這份報告，並且已經標示清楚。每一個在紙上都通過了四個條件，而這恰恰是它們的弱點：到目前為止，還沒有 GEMS 以外的任何人說過他們想要其中任何一個。它們是「該去聽一聽」的候選，不是計畫。\n\n*兩個進行中條目背後的夥伴，依 GEMS 的決定在此具名：陳惠雯老師，以自然農法耕作與教學。* 這裡沒有寫下來的，是那座農場的具體困難到底是什麼——不是出於保留，而是因為還沒有人去問。這正是下面第一個條目的用處。等到那些限制真的被記錄下來，應該用農場主人自己的話來記，也應該在取得同意之後才公開。","cards":[{"kicker":"Live · from a person","kicker_zh":"進行中 · 來自一個人","title":"Go back to Chen Hui-wen's farm without a method","title_zh":"回到陳惠雯老師的農場，手上不帶方法","body":"The ReLEAF season put the team in contact with Chen Hui-wen (陳惠雯), a teacher who farms by natural-farming principles. The next visit should carry **no synthetic-biology requirement at all** — the point is to hear what that farm's actual constraints are and write them down before anyone proposes anything. It is entirely possible the answer is not biology. That outcome is a result, not a failure, and the programme has to be able to publish it.","body_zh":"ReLEAF 那一季讓團隊認識了依自然農法耕作的陳惠雯老師。下一次的拜訪應該**完全不帶任何合成生物學的前提**——重點是聽清楚那座農場真正的限制是什麼，並且在任何人提出任何東西之前先把它們寫下來。答案完全有可能不是生物學。那是一個結果，不是失敗，而這個計畫必須能夠把它公開。","chips":["listening visit first","no method in hand"],"chips_zh":["先去聽一次","手上不帶方法"]},{"kicker":"Live · from a person","kicker_zh":"進行中 · 來自一個人","title":"A seed-exchange platform","title_zh":"種子交換平台","body":"Raised by Chen Hui-wen, the same partner. Worth taking seriously precisely because it is **probably not a synthetic-biology problem** — it looks like a matching, trust and record-keeping problem, which is to say software, logistics and governance. If GEMS can only work on things that need a construct, it is a competition team with a longer deadline. The first question is not how to build it but who else is already trying, and why seed savers would use a new one.","body_zh":"由同一位夥伴陳惠雯老師提出。值得認真看待，正因為它**大概不是一個合成生物學問題**——它看起來是配對、信任與紀錄保存的問題，也就是軟體、物流與治理。如果 GEMS 只能做需要基因構築的事，那它不過是一支截止日比較長的比賽隊伍。第一個問題不是怎麼做出來，而是還有誰已經在做、以及留種的人為什麼要改用一個新的。","chips":["probably not biology","that is the point"],"chips_zh":["大概不是生物學","這正是重點"]},{"kicker":"Proposal · from this report","kicker_zh":"提案 · 來自本報告","title":"The shared measurement standard nobody built","title_zh":"沒有人建立的共用量測標準","body":"Not one of the 106 decorated teams of 2026 ran an inter-lab measurement ring. GEMS holds Best Measurement and Best Hardware, so it can credibly ship a calibrated construct and a written protocol to other Taiwanese labs and publish the between-lab variance. Passes all four criteria on paper. Untested against a real person's stated need — nobody has asked for it.","body_zh":"2026 年 106 支得獎隊伍中，沒有一支做過跨實驗室量測環。GEMS 擁有最佳量測與最佳硬體，因此有資格把一個已校正的構築與一份書面流程寄給台灣其他實驗室，並公開實驗室之間的變異。紙上通過全部四個條件。但尚未對照任何真實的人所說出口的需求——沒有人開口要過。","chips":["0 of 106 did this","nobody asked yet"],"chips_zh":["0/106 做過","還沒有人開口要"]},{"kicker":"Proposal · from this report","kicker_zh":"提案 · 來自本報告","title":"An instrument a school can afford and rebuild","title_zh":"一台學校買得起、也修得好的儀器","body":"The hardware analysis on the dry-lab tab asks whether a stranger could rebuild any award-winning 2026 device. Taiwanese school labs are a real population with a real budget ceiling and a real operator who is not an engineer — which is the deployability condition the human-practices analysis found actually matters. Scales by documentation rather than by manufacturing.","body_zh":"乾實驗室頁的硬體分析問的是：陌生人能不能重建 2026 年任何一台得獎裝置。台灣的學校實驗室是一個真實的群體，有真實的預算上限，也有一位真實的、不是工程師的操作者——而那正是人文實踐分析發現真正重要的可佈署條件。它靠文件擴散，不靠製造。","chips":["real operator","scales by documentation"],"chips_zh":["真實的操作者","靠文件擴散"]},{"kicker":"Proposal · from this report","kicker_zh":"提案 · 來自本報告","title":"A characterised part someone else actually uses","title_zh":"一個真的被別人用到的、已表徵的元件","body":"Taiwan took zero parts nominations in 2026, and the registry is the one artefact designed to outlive a project. A well-documented part is small enough for a club to finish between seasons and is reused by definition if it is any good. Weakest of the three on criterion one: it serves the field rather than a named person, and the programme should be honest that this makes it a different kind of entry.","body_zh":"台灣在 2026 年的元件獎項中掛零，而註冊庫是唯一被設計成能比專案活得更久的產物。一個文件完整的元件，規模小到社團可以在兩季之間做完，而且只要夠好，按定義就會被重複使用。三個提案中它在條件一上最弱：它服務的是這個領域，而不是某一個具名的人，計畫應該誠實承認這讓它屬於另一類條目。","chips":["Taiwan: zero in 2026","weak on criterion one"],"chips_zh":["台灣 2026：零","第一條件偏弱"]}],"table":{"head":["Entry","Came from","Someone outside asked for it","Deployable","Countable","Scales","Next step"],"head_zh":["條目","來源","有外部的人開口要","可佈署","數得出來","可規模化","下一步"],"rows":[["Natural-farming farm","Chen Hui-wen","Yes","Yes — a working farm","Not yet defined","Unknown until the problem is named","Listening visit, no proposal"],["Seed-exchange platform","Chen Hui-wen","Yes","Yes","Exchanges completed; seed kept in circulation","Strongly — software","Find who already does this, and why it is not enough"],["Shared measurement standard","This report","No","Yes — other labs","Between-lab variance","Yes — protocol plus post","Offer it to one lab and see if anyone says yes"],["Affordable rebuildable instrument","This report","No","Yes — school labs","Cost, and whether a rebuild works","By documentation","Ask three teachers what they cannot currently measure"],["Characterised registry part","This report","No","Registry","Reuse by other teams","Yes","Pick the improved-part category and a parent part"]],"rows_zh":[["自然農法農場","陳惠雯老師","是","是——一座運作中的農場","尚未定義","題目講清楚之前還不知道","去聽，不提案"],["種子交換平台","陳惠雯老師","是","是","完成的交換次數；種子是否持續流通","強——軟體","找出已經有誰在做，以及為什麼還不夠"],["共用量測標準","本報告","否","是——其他實驗室","實驗室之間的變異","是——流程加上公開發表","先給一間實驗室，看看有沒有人說好"],["買得起又修得好的儀器","本報告","否","是——學校實驗室","成本，以及重建是否成功","靠文件","問三位老師：現在有什麼是量不到的"],["已表徵的註冊庫元件","本報告","否","註冊庫","被其他隊伍再利用","是","選定改良元件類別與一個母元件"]]},"checklist":["Keep the two columns separate forever: problems a person brought, and problems GEMS thought of.","Before any proposal is written for a partner, record their constraints in their own words, dated.","Return to every place the 2026 season reached, without a project in hand.","For each proposal, find one person outside GEMS who will say they want it — or close the entry.","Ask a partner before publishing what they told you — naming someone is one thing, publishing their difficulties is another.","Review twice a year; closing an entry with a written reason is a success, not an admission."],"checklist_zh":["永遠把兩欄分開：別人帶來的題目，和 GEMS 自己想到的題目。","在為任何夥伴寫下任何提案之前，先用他們自己的話、附上日期，記錄他們的限制。","回到 2026 年那一季走到過的每一個地方，手上不帶專案。","每一個提案，都要找到 GEMS 以外的一個人說出「我要這個」——否則就把它結案。","公開夥伴說過的話之前先問過他們——具名是一回事，公開他們的困難是另一回事。","每年檢視兩次；附上書面理由把一個條目結案，是成果，不是認錯。"],"method":"The two live entries come from GEMS Research's own 2026 season and are reported from the programme's account of them, not from any published source; the partner is named at GEMS's decision, and no specific difficulty of the farm is described here because none has been recorded yet. The three proposals are derived from analyses elsewhere in this report — the collaboration network, the hardware reproducibility census and the parts census — and each states there what it can and cannot see. No proposal here has been validated against a stated external need, which is recorded in the table as a No rather than smoothed over. This section is a plan, not a finding, and should be read as one.","method_zh":"兩個進行中的條目來自 GEMS Research 自己 2026 年的那一季，依據計畫本身的紀錄陳述，不是來自任何公開來源；夥伴依 GEMS 的決定具名，而此處沒有描述農場的任何具體困難，因為還沒有人記錄過。三個提案衍生自本報告其他處的分析——合作網絡、硬體可重建性普查，以及元件普查——各自在該處載明了看得到與看不到的範圍。此處沒有任何一個提案通過「外部確實說出口的需求」的檢驗，這一點在表格中如實記為「否」，而不是含糊帶過。這一節是計畫，不是研究發現，也應該這樣讀。"},{"id":"judging-three-teams","tab":"judging","order":20,"kicker":"Head to head","kicker_zh":"正面對照","title":"Lambert-GA, HongKong-JSS and GEMS-Taiwan against the eight questions","title_zh":"Lambert-GA、HongKong-JSS 與 GEMS-Taiwan 對照八道問題","lede":"Four theories for the gap died on the evidence, each killed by a team that placed **above** GEMS: it is not statistical rigour, not a finished chain, not Registry documentation, and not self-criticism — Lambert-GA and HongKong-JSS are each weaker than GEMS on at least one of those, and Lambert argues against itself harder than GEMS does. This section takes the three teams question by question. The conclusion it reaches — that the finalists' unfinished work sits at the periphery while ReLEAF's sits at the centre — holds for these three and is then **qualified by the full cohort in the next section**, where seven of seven non-podium teams turn out to stop at the centre too.","lede_zh":"關於這道落差的四個理論都死在證據上，而且每一個都被某支名次**高於** GEMS 的隊伍殺掉：不是統計嚴謹度、不是鏈條是否做完、不是 Registry 文件、也不是自我批評——Lambert-GA 與 HongKong-JSS 各自至少有一項比 GEMS 更弱，而 Lambert 自我批評的力道比 GEMS 更強。本節逐題檢視這三支隊伍。它得到的結論——決賽隊伍沒做完的部分位於邊緣，而 ReLEAF 沒做完的部分位於正中央——對這三支成立，但接著會**在下一節被整個群體修正**：七支非頒獎臺隊伍，結果每一支都同樣停在正中央。","body":"Four theories had to die before the answer was visible. Each died on the evidence of a team that finished above GEMS.\n\n**Not statistics.** Lambert-GA won the Grand Prize with a results page carrying no p-values and no named statistical test. Its one quantitative claim is a 603.6 nM binding affinity, 95% CI 497.1–733.3, n=2 — measured by Adaptyv Bio, not by the team. Its own bench work is called \"preliminary evidence\" on one page and disowned on another. GEMS's plant work, at p < 0.0001 with 40 seedlings per condition, is more statistically serious than anything on Lambert's results page.\n\n**Not completeness.** HongKong-JSS's extraction platform never once fed its biosensor. Lambert's RNAi arm — six siRNAs — has **no knockdown data at all**, twelve transfection conditions all inconclusive, and nothing was ever tested against intact virus, bee cells, or a bee. Lambert's own colony model concludes that RNAi supplies most of SWARM's predicted benefit while the minibinder adds \"a small further improvement\". The arm carrying the impact has no data.\n\n**Not Registry documentation, and here GEMS is ahead of both.** GEMS deposited 34 parts, median 7,369 characters of documentation, 269,653 across the collection, 14 inside the band this report measured for parts-award winners. HongKong-JSS's four parts carry 756, 643, 468 and 385 characters. Lambert's top out at 6,313 with descriptions as short as 19 characters and almost no characterisation sections anywhere. On question 8's Registry half, GEMS beat the Grand Prize winner and the runner-up, and still finished below both.\n\n**Not self-criticism — this is the theory worth killing loudest.** Lambert's Best Wiki pages argue against Lambert on Lambert's own award pages: the parts page contradicts the results page about the in-house pull-down and concludes the result \"does not establish binding by the registered candidate\"; the Best Model page states its gram-scale Sobol analysis \"did not pass its numerical checks\"; the Best Hardware page prints a protein table and then declares its own concentration columns \"unverified\". A downloadable CSV stamps every siRNA row \"biological efficacy not established by this file.\" **Candour did not cost Lambert the Grand Prize, and candour is therefore not what cost GEMS the finalist slate.**\n\nWhat is left is where the hole sits. Lambert is named for hitting the virus and the mite; the virus half produced a measured binder and the mite half produced nothing, and the measured half is the half the project leads with. HongKong-JSS is named for in-field mercury detection; the detection works and the in-field part does not. In both cases a judge can name the achievement in one clause and the gap is in the next clause, at the edge.\n\nReLEAF is named for a stress-responsive optogenetic bioreactor. The stress-responsive half is refuted by GEMS's own model — *\"The reactor therefore cannot be scheduled from the forecast\"* — and the optogenetic half did not show light dependence: ELISA read 2.6 to 3.2 µg/mL under both colours at every time point, the AmilCP reporter never coloured, the red LEDs sit at 640 nm where CcaSR needs about 672 nm to switch off, and **every biological result in the project came from a constitutive bypass module rather than the light-gated device.** What works — secreting an enzyme, pushing it through a membrane, rescuing a stressed plant — is real, quantified, and is not what the project is called.\n\nThat is the loss, stated as precisely as the public record allows. GEMS built a very good small fermenter, a very good optical density meter, and a genuinely excellent human-practices programme, and three category panels rewarded exactly those. The eight finalist questions ask what the project achieved, and the project's own pages answer that its central mechanism is undemonstrated and its scheduling premise does not hold. **None of the three fixes needs a bigger team or a better lab.**\n\n**One honest limit on the paragraph above, found by reading the other seven.** Every one of the eight non-podium teams also stops short of its intended target: GHCIS's field water tool has only ever seen its own synthetic trigger RNA at micromolar concentrations; HongKong-HS's home urine test has never touched urine and demonstrates a floor roughly a million-fold above urinary miRNA; HKSSC claims paraben removal and measures a tolerance shift instead; HFI's premise experiment is labelled \"ns, not significant\" in its own figure. **So \"the gap is at the centre\" describes the whole non-podium group, not GEMS uniquely** — and the finalists are not clean either, since Lambert never tested anything against intact virus, bee cells or a bee. The distinction is one of degree, and the next section reports the one award-level signal that does map onto the finalist slate exactly.","body_zh":"在答案浮現之前，有四個理論必須先死掉。每一個都死在某支名次高於 GEMS 的隊伍所提供的證據上。\n\n**不是統計。** Lambert-GA 拿下總冠軍，而它的結果頁上沒有 p 值，也沒有任何統計檢定名稱。它唯一的量化主張是 603.6 nM 的結合親和力，95% CI 497.1–733.3，n=2——由 Adaptyv Bio 量測，不是團隊自己做的。它自家的實驗工作在一個頁面上被稱為「初步證據」，在另一個頁面上被否認。GEMS 的植物工作，p < 0.0001、每組 40 棵幼苗，在統計上比 Lambert 結果頁上的任何東西都更嚴謹。\n\n**不是完成度。** HongKong-JSS 的萃取平台一次都沒有餵進它的生物感測器。Lambert 的 RNAi 這一支——六條 siRNA——**完全沒有任何剔除效率的資料**，十二種轉染條件全部無法判定，而且從未對完整病毒、蜜蜂細胞或一隻蜜蜂做過測試。Lambert 自己的蜂群模型結論是：RNAi 貢獻了 SWARM 預測效益的大部分，而 minibinder 只增加「小幅的進一步改善」。承載影響力的那一支，沒有資料。\n\n**不是 Registry 文件，而且在這一項 GEMS 領先兩者。** GEMS 存放了 34 個元件，文件長度中位數 7,369 字元，整個集合 269,653 字元，其中 14 個落在本報告為元件獎得主量到的區間內。HongKong-JSS 的四個元件是 756、643、468、385 字元。Lambert 的上限是 6,313 字元，說明短到只有 19 個字元，而且幾乎沒有任何地方有表徵段落。在第 8 題的 Registry 那一半，GEMS 贏過總冠軍、也贏過亞軍，名次卻在兩者之下。\n\n**不是自我批評——這個理論最值得大聲殺掉。** Lambert 那些拿下最佳 Wiki 的頁面，在自己的得獎頁面上反駁自己：元件頁與結果頁對於自家的 pull-down 實驗互相矛盾，並下結論說該結果「並未證實已註冊的候選分子有結合能力」；最佳模型頁寫明它的公克級 Sobol 分析「沒有通過自己的數值檢查」；最佳硬體頁印出一張蛋白濃度表，然後宣告自己那幾欄濃度「未經驗證」。一份可下載的 CSV 在每一列 siRNA 上蓋章寫著「本檔案並未建立生物效力」。**坦白並沒有讓 Lambert 失去總冠軍，因此坦白也不是讓 GEMS 失去決賽席位的原因。**\n\n剩下的是：那個洞長在哪裡。Lambert 的命名是「同時打病毒與打蟎」；病毒那一半做出了一個被量測到的結合分子，蟎那一半什麼也沒做出來，而專案開場用的正是被量測到的那一半。HongKong-JSS 的命名是「現地汞偵測」；偵測成功了，現地那部分沒有。在這兩個例子裡，評審都能用一個子句說出成就，而缺口在下一個子句，位於邊緣。\n\nReLEAF 的命名是「逆境響應式光控生物反應器」。逆境響應這一半，被 GEMS 自己的模型推翻——*「因此反應器無法由預報來排程」*；而光控這一半沒有顯示出光依賴性：ELISA 在每個時間點、兩種顏色下都讀到 2.6 到 3.2 µg/mL，AmilCP 報告子從未顯色，紅光 LED 在 640 nm 而 CcaSR 需要約 672 nm 才能關閉，而且**這個專案裡每一項生物學成果，都來自組成型的旁路模組，不是來自光控裝置。** 真正成功的部分——分泌一個酵素、讓它穿過膜、救援一棵受逆境的植物——是真實的、量化過的，但那不是這個專案的名字。\n\n這就是失分之處，以公開紀錄所能允許的精確度陳述。GEMS 做出了一台很好的小型發酵槽、一台很好的光密度計，以及一個真正出色的人類實踐計畫，而三個類別評審團獎勵的正是這些。那八道決賽問題問的是「這個專案達成了什麼」，而專案自己的頁面回答：它的核心機制尚未被證實，它的排程前提不成立。**這三件要修的事，沒有一件需要更大的團隊或更好的實驗室。**\n\n**上面那段有一個誠實的限制，是讀完其他七支之後才看到的。** 八支非頒獎臺隊伍，每一支都同樣停在距離目標還有一段的地方：GHCIS 的現地水質工具，至今只見過自己合成的觸發 RNA，而且是微莫耳濃度；HongKong-HS 的居家尿液檢測從未碰過尿液，所展示的下限大約比尿中 miRNA 高出一百萬倍；HKSSC 聲稱要移除對羥基苯甲酸酯，實際量到的是耐受度的位移；HFI 檢驗自身前提的那個實驗，在它自己的圖上被標成「ns，不顯著」。**所以「缺口在正中央」描述的是整個非頒獎臺群體，不是 GEMS 獨有的毛病**——而兩支決賽隊伍也並不乾淨，因為 Lambert 從未對完整病毒、蜜蜂細胞或一隻蜜蜂做過任何測試。這是程度上的差別；下一節會報告唯一真正與決賽名單完全對應的那個獎項層級訊號。","cards":[{"kicker":"Question 1","kicker_zh":"第 1 題","title":"Both finalists had one sentence. GEMS had five.","title_zh":"兩支決賽隊伍各有一句話。GEMS 有五句。","body":"GEMS's `/results` page opens with a **Key results** block, and it is excellent work: protectant secretion, light control, the photometer at R² 0.992 with 434 h unattended, plant rescue with a timing effect, and containment with active enzyme in the cell-free shell for 72 h. Five results, each real. Lambert-GA's whole project resolves into one claim about a minibinder binding Deformed Wing Virus VP3. HongKong-JSS's resolves into one number for mercury in water. **A judge on this question is looking for the sentence they can repeat back without notes, and five results do not average into one — they compete with each other.**\n\nWorth noting that Lambert's project is *also* two arms with one working, and HongKong-JSS's is also a three-part system. The difference is not how many pieces a project has. It is whether one of them has been nominated as the answer.","body_zh":"GEMS 的 `/results` 頁開頭是一個 **Key results** 區塊，而那是很好的工作：保護蛋白分泌、光控、光度計 R² 0.992 與 434 小時無人監測、具時序效應的植物救援，以及在無細胞殼側維持 72 小時活性酵素的生物圍堵。五個成果，每一個都是真的。Lambert-GA 的整個專案收斂成一個主張：一個 minibinder 結合 Deformed Wing Virus 的 VP3。HongKong-JSS 收斂成一個數字：水中的汞。**評審在這一題找的是「不用翻筆記就能複述出來的那一句話」，而五個成果不會平均成一個——它們會互相競爭。**\n\n值得注意的是，Lambert 的專案**同樣**是兩支其中一支成功，HongKong-JSS 的同樣是一個三段式系統。差別不在於一個專案有幾個部件，而在於其中有沒有一個被指定為「答案」。","chips":["5 key results vs 1 claim"],"chips_zh":["五個重點成果，對一個主張"]},{"kicker":"Question 2","kicker_zh":"第 2 題","title":"Every biological result came from the constitutive bypass, not the light-gated device","title_zh":"所有生物學成果都來自組成型的旁路模組，不是光控裝置","body":"GEMS's **plant biology is properly done**: measurable rescue of salinity- and heat-stressed *Arabidopsis* by fresh weight and chlorophyll at p < 0.0001, with 40 seedlings per condition and real dose thresholds, plus ACC deaminase secreted at about 16 µg/mL and crossing a 0.2 µm membrane to stay active at 5–8.4 U/mg for 72 hours. The middle of the chain works.\n\nBut ReLEAF is named for optogenetic control, and the light-gated device is the one thing that did not work. ELISA found **no light dependence at all** — 2.6 to 3.2 µg/mL under both colours at every time point. The AmilCP reporter never coloured. The red LEDs emit at 640 nm where CcaSR needs about 672 nm to switch off, so the off-state does not exist. And **every biological result above was produced by a constitutive bypass module**, not by the light-gated construct. The team documents all of this. The *Key results* line still reads \"Green light switches ACCD on\", resting on an activity assay while the team's own protein measurement shows no difference.","body_zh":"GEMS 的**植物生物學做得很紮實**：以鮮重與葉綠素量到對鹽逆境與熱逆境下 *Arabidopsis* 的救援效果，p < 0.0001，每組 40 棵幼苗，並有真實的劑量門檻；此外 ACC deaminase 分泌量約 16 µg/mL，能穿過 0.2 µm 膜並在無細胞側維持 5–8.4 U/mg 的活性達 72 小時。鏈條的中段是會動的。\n\n但 ReLEAF 是以光控命名的，而光控裝置正是唯一沒有成功的那一塊。ELISA **完全沒有測到光依賴性**——在每一個時間點，兩種顏色下都是 2.6 到 3.2 µg/mL。AmilCP 報告子從未顯色。紅光 LED 發的是 640 nm，而 CcaSR 需要約 672 nm 才能關閉，所以「關閉狀態」並不存在。而且**上面每一項生物學成果，都是由組成型的旁路模組做出來的**，不是由光控構築做出來的。團隊把這些全都記錄下來了。但 *Key results* 那一行仍然寫著「綠光開啟 ACCD」，其依據是活性測定，而團隊自己的蛋白量測顯示沒有差異。","chips":["ELISA: no light dependence","biology via constitutive bypass"],"chips_zh":["ELISA：無光依賴性","生物學成果來自組成型旁路"]},{"kicker":"Question 3","kicker_zh":"第 3 題","title":"GEMS's own model refutes the project's premise, and publishes the contradiction","title_zh":"GEMS 自己的模型推翻了專案的前提，並把矛盾公開","body":"This turned out to be the sharpest weakness of the eight, and it is self-reported. The model page's own *Key results* block states: **\"Payback 68 years on our loss figure; Geospatial Analysis says 4.9\"** — a fourteen-fold contradiction between two of GEMS's own pages, left standing. The same page works out that one hectare needs 5.4 days of brewing against a three-day forecast, so \"2.4 days of production precede any forecast that would justify it\", and concludes: **\"The reactor therefore cannot be scheduled from the forecast.\"** Forecast-triggered production is the premise of ReLEAF. The page also records that **\"The preparation sprayed on plants was never assayed.\"**\n\nHongKong-JSS and Lambert both benchmark against an external standard a judge recognises — WHO and EPA mercury limits, honeybee colony loss. GEMS benchmarks against itself and finds it does not add up. That is admirable and it is also, on question 3, the answer a judge takes away.\n\nIn fairness, Lambert's impact headline is not better evidenced: its 96.7% pollination-retention figure rests on a 93.6% mite-reproduction reduction lifted from an external study, which it states, and the arm supplying most of the modelled benefit has no efficacy data. The difference is that Lambert's economics do not contradict Lambert. GEMS publishes a refutation of its own premise and leaves it standing, which is more honest and, on this question, more expensive.","body_zh":"這一題最後成了八題中最鋒利的弱點，而且是自己報出來的。模型頁自己的 *Key results* 區塊寫著：**「Payback 68 years on our loss figure; Geospatial Analysis says 4.9」**——GEMS 自己兩個頁面之間十四倍的矛盾，就這樣擺著。同一頁算出一公頃需要 5.4 天的培養，而預報只有三天，因此「有 2.4 天的生產發生在任何能正當化它的預報之前」，並下結論：**「因此反應器無法由預報來排程。」** 而「由預報觸發生產」正是 ReLEAF 的前提。該頁也記下：**「噴到植物上的那份製備從未被檢測活性。」**\n\nHongKong-JSS 與 Lambert 都是對照評審認得的外部標準——WHO 與 EPA 的汞限值、蜂群損失率。GEMS 對照的是自己，而且發現算不過來。這很值得敬重，但在第 3 題上，這也就是評審帶走的那個答案。\n\n公平地說，Lambert 的影響力標題證據並不更好：它 96.7% 的授粉保留率，建立在一項外部研究的 93.6% 蟎繁殖抑制率之上（他們寫明了），而貢獻了大部分模型效益的那一支沒有任何效力資料。差別在於，Lambert 的經濟分析沒有反駁 Lambert。GEMS 公開了一份對自身前提的反駁，並且把它擺在那裡；那更誠實，但在這一題上也更昂貴。","chips":["68 years vs 4.9 years","cannot be scheduled from the forecast"],"chips_zh":["68 年 對 4.9 年","無法由預報排程"]},{"kicker":"Question 4","kicker_zh":"第 4 題","title":"The distinction is not whether a failure is documented. It is whether a fix followed.","title_zh":"差別不在於有沒有記錄失敗，而在於後面有沒有跟著一個修正。","body":"All three teams document failures, so presence is not the discriminator. What the finalists add is the next step.\n\nLambert ran **33 numbered DBTL iterations** and its first minibinder campaign submitted 15 designs and got **zero** binders — including one scoring ipSAE 0.927 that still came back negative. They changed the epitope from an unresolved C-terminal region to the QP/A-ridge, added two new design tools and agreement-across-predictions filtering, and campaign 2 returned 1 binder from 20. They then add that \"the improved outcome cannot be attributed to PRINCE or SolubleMPNN independently\". HongKong-JSS ran nine cycles, discovered its mercury aptamers were DNA rather than RNA and could not fold inside an mRNA, **abandoned the route** and published the sequences as a warning.\n\nGEMS documents its failures at least as thoroughly and then stops. On the central optogenetic result the wiki names two candidate explanations — neighbouring-well light crosstalk in the LPA, and red LEDs at 640 nm against the ~672 nm CcaSR needs — and says: \"**We have not tested either explanation directly.**\" Both would have been a week's work. A documented failure with a response reads as engineering; a documented failure with a hypothesis reads as a lab notebook.","body_zh":"HongKong-JSS 的工程頁跑了**九個編號的濕實驗循環，其中大多數記錄的是失敗**——包含一個被公開出來、用以警告其他隊伍的觀念錯誤：他們依據已發表的汞 aptamer 設計了四個構築，以為所有 aptamer 都是 RNA，後來發現 D3 與 D4 是 DNA aptamer，其篩選出的結構無法在 mRNA 內形成，於是放棄這條路線，並把序列標上「請勿重複使用」後公開。他們也承認缺少對照組、未誘導的次培養卻變紅、放大器在接觸任何汞之前就已經深紅。**一個被公開的失敗，是整張評分表上最便宜、也最有說服力的證據。**","chips":["Lambert: 15 designs, 0 binders, then a fix","GEMS: two explanations, neither tested"],"chips_zh":["Lambert：15 個設計、0 個結合，然後修正","GEMS：兩個解釋，都沒測"]},{"kicker":"Question 5","kicker_zh":"第 5 題","title":"Not the separator — GEMS beat both here","title_zh":"不是分水嶺——GEMS 在這裡贏過兩者","body":"HongKong-JSS ran 333- and 195-response surveys and worked with four government departments, six universities and four farms, with design changes traceable to specific conversations. It is excellent. GEMS still won the category against it. Anyone reading this analysis looking for the lost ground should not look here.","body_zh":"HongKong-JSS 做了 333 份與 195 份回覆的問卷，與四個政府部門、六所大學、四座農場合作，而且設計變更可以追溯到特定的對話。那非常好。GEMS 仍然在這個類別上贏過它。任何讀這份分析、想找出失分之處的人，不應該往這裡看。","chips":["category won head-to-head"],"chips_zh":["正面交鋒拿下該類別"]},{"kicker":"Question 6","kicker_zh":"第 6 題","title":"Nobody was punished for outside help, and the Grand Prize winner outsourced its headline number","title_zh":"沒有人因為外部協助被懲罰，而總冠軍把招牌數字外包了","body":"This question is the one most likely to be read backwards, and the evidence says it did not separate these three at all.\n\nLambert's headline affinity was produced end to end by **Adaptyv Bio**, which received the sequences, expressed the protein, ran the BLI and interpreted the result; an Adaptyv scientist also diagnosed the failed first campaign and supplied the numeric fix. The DWV coding sequence with its P-domain boundaries came from an external virologist, and a Georgia Tech lab \"helped shape our minibinder design strategy\" and \"guided the development of our predictive mathematical modeling\". All of it is disclosed in detail. HongKong-JSS **did no cloning at all**, had its mercury solutions prepared by its supervisor, and credits a Secondary PI with hardware, software and the wiki.\n\nGEMS discloses on the same scale — 31 students against 8 PIs and instructors and 10 advisors — and what it discloses is more exposed: an instructor credited with \"Designed and conducted experiments of the project\", and an advisor who was \"a core member of the hardware team, designing the bioreactor and photometer from idea generation and planning through CAD modeling\". That is an adult leading the work that won Best Hardware, in the team's own words. **But Lambert outsourced the measurement its Grand Prize rests on and won anyway. This question did not decide it.**","body_zh":"這是最容易被讀反的一題，而三支隊伍都大量揭露。HongKong-JSS 明說它**完全沒有做選殖**——「我們的團隊沒有進行選殖」，質體來自 IDT、GenScript 與 BGI Genomics；也說「所有汞溶液都由我們的指導老師配製」，以及一位 Secondary PI 負責了硬體設計、軟體開發**以及** wiki。Lambert 的招牌親和力數字由商業 BLI 服務 **Adaptyv** 量測，並且寫明了。兩者都沒有因此被懲罰。\n\nGEMS 的揭露規模相當：31 名學生，對 8 位 PI 與指導老師、10 位顧問。但它揭露出來的內容比較暴露。一位指導老師被記為「Designed and conducted experiments of the project」（設計並執行了專案的實驗），一位顧問被記為「a core member of the hardware team, designing the bioreactor and photometer from idea generation and planning through CAD modeling」（硬體團隊的核心成員，從構想、規劃到 CAD 建模設計了生物反應器與光度計）——用團隊自己的話說，那是一位成年人主導了拿下最佳硬體的那部分工作。**問題不在於有沒有揭露，而在於有什麼要揭露。**","chips":["Adaptyv ran the BLI","HongKong-JSS did no cloning","an advisor led GEMS hardware"],"chips_zh":["BLI 由 Adaptyv 執行","HongKong-JSS 沒做選殖","GEMS 硬體由顧問主導"]},{"kicker":"Question 7","kicker_zh":"第 7 題","title":"The synthetic-biology core has to be the validated part","title_zh":"合成生物學的核心，必須是被驗證的那一部分","body":"Questions 7 and 2 close on GEMS together. ReLEAF's claim to be synthetic biology rests on green-light control of *B. subtilis* through CcaSR — the one module that showed no light dependence, and whose published transfer function was never tested because \"every induction so far has been at one setting\". Worse, and this comes from GEMS's own parts page rather than from any outside reading: the page carries a **Documentation** column that the team states was read from the live Registry API, and **every one of its four regulatory parts shows \"—\"** — PcpcG2-veg (BBa_26GJIT8W, the green-light promoter itself), PtagC+RBS, RBS0 and EEBD-RBS0. The control elements that *are* the synthetic-biology contribution are the parts with no documentation at all.\n\nThe parts GEMS evidenced best, secreting a protein and applying it to a plant, are conventional protein work. Lambert's novelty and Lambert's evidence are the same object: the minibinder is the new thing and the measured thing. **GEMS's novelty and GEMS's evidence are in different places, and the novel one is the least documented part in the collection.** The fair hostile summary is the one the analysis arrived at independently: a very good small fermenter with a very good OD meter, and the optogenetics as decoration.","body_zh":"第 7 題與第 2 題在 GEMS 身上一起收口。ReLEAF 自稱合成生物學，倚靠的是透過 CcaSR 以綠光控制 *B. subtilis*——而那正是唯一沒有顯示光依賴性的模組，其已發表的轉移函數也從未被測試，因為「到目前為止每一次誘導都只用了一個設定」。更糟的是，這一點來自 GEMS 自己的元件頁，不是外部的解讀：該頁有一個 **Documentation** 欄，團隊自述其內容是從線上 Registry API 讀取的，而**它四個調控元件全部顯示「—」**——PcpcG2-veg（BBa_26GJIT8W，也就是綠光啟動子本身）、PtagC+RBS、RBS0 與 EEBD-RBS0。那些「本身就是合成生物學貢獻」的控制元件，正是完全沒有文件的那幾個。\n\nGEMS 證據最紮實的部分，也就是分泌一個蛋白並施用到植物上，是常規的蛋白工作。Lambert 的新穎性與證據是同一個物件：minibinder 既是新東西，也是被量測的東西。**GEMS 的新穎性與證據落在不同的地方，而新穎的那一個是整個元件集合裡文件最少的。** 最公允的敵意總結，就是這份分析獨立得到的那一句：一台很好的小型發酵槽配一台很好的 OD 計，而光遺傳學是裝飾。","chips":["4 of 4 regulatory parts undocumented","one induction setting only"],"chips_zh":["4 個調控元件全部無文件","只用過一個誘導設定"]},{"kicker":"Question 8","kicker_zh":"第 8 題","title":"The Registry documentation is long. Almost none of it is characterisation.","title_zh":"Registry 文件很長，但幾乎沒有一段是表徵資料。","body":"The obvious theory was that GEMS's Registry pages were thin. They are not, and this is the one place the comparison runs clearly in GEMS's favour. All 34 deposited accessions resolve with sequence and the documentation is substantial. Measured identically across the whole High School Top 10 — documentation payload for six headline parts per team — **the Grand Prize winner is last of ten at a median of 670 characters**, HongKong-JSS is eighth at 2,606, and GEMS is fourth at 8,644. The longest in the cohort belong to parts-prize winners who reached no podium: HKSSC at 23,116 and GCGS at 14,763.\n\nSo volume is not the problem. **Kind is, and GEMS publishes the proof itself.** Its parts page carries a Documentation column the team says was read from the live Registry API, and across the 35 parts it presents the column reads: **Experiment 18, Design 8, nothing at all 6, and Characterisation 3.** Three parts in thirty-five carry characterisation, about 3,300 characters between them. A judge on question 8 is asking whether a stranger can check the claim, and Design and Experiment prose describes what was intended and what was done — not what was measured. Separately, on the results page: five p-values, SEM and error bars throughout, R² to four decimals — and **no named statistical test anywhere.** Significance is carried by asterisks alone, while HongKong-JSS writes \"paired two-sided t-test p = 0.0080\". And five bioreactor figures are captioned \"redrawn from the team's chart\", with the wiki's own `growth-data.js` recording `csv: null` beside the note \"The owner, 15 Oct: 'ill give data later'\".","body_zh":"最直覺的理論是 GEMS 的 Registry 頁面太薄。並不是，而這也是整個比較中唯一明顯對 GEMS 有利的地方。34 個存放的編號全部解析成功且附序列，文件內容也相當充實。用同一套方式量過高中組 Top 10 全部十支——每隊六個招牌元件的文件內容總長——**總冠軍是十支中的最後一名，中位數 670 字元**，HongKong-JSS 第八名 2,606，GEMS 第四名 8,644。整組最長的屬於拿了元件獎卻沒上頒獎臺的隊伍：HKSSC 23,116、GCGS 14,763。\n\n所以問題不是量，**是種類，而且 GEMS 自己就公開了證據。** 它的元件頁有一個 Documentation 欄，團隊自述其內容讀自線上 Registry API，而在它所呈現的 35 個元件中，這一欄是：**Experiment 18 個、Design 8 個、完全沒有的 6 個、Characterisation 3 個。** 三十五個元件裡只有三個有表徵，三者合計約 3,300 字元。第 8 題問的是陌生人能不能核對這個主張，而 Design 與 Experiment 的敘述講的是「打算做什麼」和「做了什麼」——不是「量到了什麼」。此外在結果頁上：五個 p 值、全頁 SEM 與誤差棒、R² 寫到小數第四位——卻**沒有任何地方寫出統計檢定的名稱。** 顯著性只靠星號，而 HongKong-JSS 寫的是「paired two-sided t-test p = 0.0080」。還有五張生物反應器的圖，圖說是「redrawn from the team's chart」，而 wiki 自己的 `growth-data.js` 記著 `csv: null`，旁邊寫著「The owner, 15 Oct: 'ill give data later'」。","chips":["GEMS 4th of 10; Grand Prize last","Characterisation on 3 of 35","0 named tests"],"chips_zh":["GEMS 十支中第 4；總冠軍最後","35 個中 3 個有表徵","0 個檢定名稱"]}],"table":{"head":["Question","Lambert-GA · Grand Prize","HongKong-JSS · 1st Runner-up","GEMS-Taiwan · Top 10"],"head_zh":["問題","Lambert-GA · 總冠軍","HongKong-JSS · 亞軍","GEMS-Taiwan · Top 10"],"rows":[["1 Impressive","One claim: a minibinder binds DWV VP3","One number: mercury in water","Five key results, no single claim"],["2 Did it work","603.6 nM, 95% CI, n=2 — measured by Adaptyv; RNAi arm has no data","n=5 matched runs, paired t-test p=0.0080; chain incomplete and stated","Plant rescue p<0.0001; light-gated device showed no light dependence"],["3 Impact","Honeybee colony loss","WHO 6 µg/L and US EPA 2 ppb","Own model: payback 68 years vs its own 4.9; cannot be scheduled from the forecast"],["4 Engineering","33 iterations; 15 designs to 0 binders, then a fix","9 cycles, most documenting failure, incl. a published error","Failures documented; two explanations, neither tested"],["5 Human practices","SDI winner","4 departments, 6 universities, 4 farms","Best IHP winner — beat both"],["6 Own work","Adaptyv produced, ran and interpreted the BLI","No cloning at all, disclosed","31 students, 8 PIs, 10 advisors; an advisor led the hardware"],["7 Synbio and standards","Novel protein is the measured thing","MerR sensor is the measured thing","4 of 4 regulatory parts carry no documentation"],["8 Documentation","Best Wiki winner; shortest Registry documentation of all ten","8th of ten on Registry documentation","4th of ten on volume, but Characterisation on 3 of 35; 0 named tests"]],"rows_zh":[["1 印象深刻","一個主張：minibinder 結合 DWV VP3","一個數字：水中的汞","五個重點成果，沒有單一主張"],["2 是否成功","603.6 nM、95% CI、n=2——由 Adaptyv 量測；RNAi 那一支沒有資料","n=5 配對試驗，paired t-test p=0.0080；鏈條未完成且已說明","植物救援 p<0.0001；光控裝置未顯示光依賴性"],["3 影響力","蜂群損失","WHO 6 µg/L 與美國 EPA 2 ppb","自家模型：回本 68 年 對自家的 4.9 年；無法由預報排程"],["4 工程原則","33 次迭代；15 個設計得到 0 個結合，然後修正","9 個循環，多數記錄失敗，含一個公開的錯誤","有記錄失敗；兩個解釋，都沒有測試"],["5 人類實踐","永續發展影響獎得主","4 個部門、6 所大學、4 座農場","最佳 IHP 得主——贏過兩者"],["6 自主完成度","Adaptyv 製備、執行並解讀了 BLI","完全沒做選殖，已揭露","31 學生、8 PI、10 顧問；硬體由一位顧問主導"],["7 合成生物學與標準","新穎蛋白就是被量測的東西","MerR 感測器就是被量測的東西","4 個調控元件全部沒有文件"],["8 文件完整度","最佳 Wiki 得主；Registry 文件是十支中最短","Registry 文件在十支中排第八","文件量十支中第四，但 35 個中僅 3 個有表徵；0 個檢定名稱"]]},"checklist":["Pick the one sentence for 2027 before the wet lab starts, and make the novel link the one you validate hardest. In 2026 the novel link was the only one that failed.","If the light-gated device does not beat the constitutive control, the project is not an optogenetics project. Settle that in week six, not in October.","Name every statistical test beside its p-value. Asterisks alone cost nothing to fix and cannot be checked by a stranger.","Never ship a control arm at n=1. The LPA growth figure would have cost two more tubes.","Write a Characterisation section on every Registry part. GEMS's own parts table shows Characterisation on 3 of 35, and all four regulatory parts — the green-light promoter included — showing nothing at all.","Publish the numbers behind every figure as CSV. A chart traced from a picture of a chart is bounded by the tracing, not the experiment.","Reconcile the two payback figures, or retract one. A published 68-years-against-4.9 contradiction answers question 3 for the judge.","Keep the candour. It won three categories. Spend it bounding results that are clear, not only explaining results that are not."],"checklist_zh":["在濕實驗開始之前就選定 2027 年的那一句話，並且讓新穎的那一環成為你驗證得最用力的一環。2026 年新穎的那一環，正是唯一失敗的那一環。","如果光控裝置贏不過組成型對照組，這個專案就不是光遺傳學專案。這件事該在第六週就定案，不是等到十月。","每個 p 值旁邊都寫出檢定名稱。只放星號，修起來不花錢，但陌生人無法核對。","永遠不要讓對照組只有 n=1。那張 LPA 生長圖，差的只是兩支試管。","每一個 Registry 元件都寫出表徵段落。GEMS 自己的元件表顯示 35 個中只有 3 個有表徵，而四個調控元件——包含綠光啟動子——全部一片空白。","把每張圖背後的數字以 CSV 公開。用圖片描出來的圖表，其不確定度來自描圖，不是來自實驗。","把兩個回本年數調和，或撤回其中一個。公開的「68 年對 4.9 年」矛盾，會替評審把第 3 題回答掉。","保住那份坦白。它贏下了三個類別。把它用在為清楚的結果劃定邊界，而不只是解釋不清楚的結果。"],"method":"Every claim here was fetched first-hand from the three teams' live 2026 wikis and from api.registry.igem.org, and the specific figures were re-verified by the report's manager rather than taken on an analyst's word. GEMS's wiki is static HTML and was read with curl; Lambert's is server-rendered Astro and was read the same way; HongKong-JSS's needed a browser. Statistical-reporting counts come from stripping tags from the full results page and matching whole words, so a test named only inside a figure image would be invisible to the count. Question 9, on how competently a team answered judges' questions live, is excluded: it leaves no public record, and it is entirely possible that part of the gap described here was created in the room rather than on the wiki. GEMS-Taiwan is the report author's own team and is assessed on the same terms as the other two, which is the standing rule of this report. The analysis describes what a judge could learn from the published record; it is not a reconstruction of any judge's actual reasoning, and no judge has been consulted. The Registry comparison was re-measured consistently after a first pass mixed two different quantities: the figures quoted here are total documentation payload from /v1/parts/{uuid}/documentation for six headline parts per team, taken across all ten High School Top 10 teams, which is why they differ from an earlier draft of this section that compared GEMS's documentation payload against other teams' description fields. Description length and documentation payload differ by more than an order of magnitude on the same part, so the two must never be compared with each other. Lambert-GA's Registry figures are description and documentation-body lengths for the 21 of 38 accessions whose bodies were retrieved before api.registry.igem.org began returning HTTP 429 across the board for about fifty minutes; the remainder are recorded as not found with that reason rather than estimated, so Lambert's maximum is a floor on the sample and not a census. The Documentation-column tally for GEMS was read by the manager directly from the team's own published parts page, which states that the column was populated from the live Registry API on 21 October 2026; the per-part character counts come from the API and could not be re-verified at the time of writing because api.registry.igem.org was returning HTTP 429 to all requests.","method_zh":"此處每一項主張都是第一手從三支隊伍 2026 年的線上 wiki 以及 api.registry.igem.org 取得，具體數字由本報告的管理者重新查核，而不是採信分析員的轉述。GEMS 的 wiki 是靜態 HTML，用 curl 讀取；Lambert 的是 Astro 伺服器端渲染，也以同樣方式讀取；HongKong-JSS 的需要用瀏覽器。統計報告方式的計數，是把整個結果頁去除標籤後以完整字詞比對而得，因此若某個檢定名稱只寫在圖片裡，這個計數看不到它。第 9 題關於團隊現場回答評審問題的能力，在此排除：它沒有留下公開紀錄，而這裡描述的落差，完全有可能有一部分是在現場、而不是在 wiki 上產生的。GEMS-Taiwan 是本報告作者自己的團隊，與另外兩支以相同標準評估，這是本報告一貫的規則。本分析描述的是「一位評審能從公開紀錄中讀到什麼」，不是對任何評審實際推理過程的重建，也沒有徵詢過任何評審。 Registry 的比較在第一次量測混用了兩個不同的量之後重新量過：此處引用的數字，是每隊取六個招牌元件、以 /v1/parts/{uuid}/documentation 取得的文件內容總長，並且涵蓋高中組 Top 10 全部十支隊伍——這也是它與本節早先草稿不同的原因，那份草稿把 GEMS 的文件內容長度拿去和其他隊伍的 description 欄位比較。同一個元件上，description 長度與文件內容總長可以差一個數量級以上，因此兩者絕不可互相比較。 Lambert-GA 的 Registry 數字，是 38 個編號中在 api.registry.igem.org 開始全面回傳 HTTP 429（持續約五十分鐘）之前成功取得內文的那 21 個的說明與文件長度；其餘以「未取得」並註明該原因記錄，而非推估，因此 Lambert 的上限是這個樣本的下界，不是全面普查。 GEMS 的 Documentation 欄統計，由本報告管理者直接從該團隊自己公開的元件頁讀出；該頁自述這一欄是在 2026 年 10 月 21 日從線上 Registry API 取得。各元件的字元數來自 API，撰稿時無法重新核對，因為 api.registry.igem.org 當時對所有請求回傳 HTTP 429。"},{"id":"picks-leverage","tab":"picks","order":20,"kicker":"Original analysis","kicker_zh":"原創分析","title":"Find the audience that multiplies, not the one that counts","title_zh":"找會放大的對象，而不是能計數的對象","lede":"HongKong-JSS reached over 1,600 primary pupils and then spent two days teaching PCR and agarose gel electrophoresis to 30 local school teachers, and lent them the DNA samples and the equipment afterwards. Thirty teachers who each teach for years beat 1,600 children who each watch once, for the same hours. Across all 106 team files only 7 teams taught an audience that teaches professionally, and only 5 left equipment in somebody else's hands. One team did both.","lede_zh":"HongKong-JSS 的科普活動觸及超過 1,600 名小學生與家長，接著又用兩天時間，教 30 位本地學校教師做 PCR 與瓊脂膠體電泳，之後還把 DNA 樣本與實驗器材借給這些老師。同樣的工時，30 位會教好幾年的老師，勝過 1,600 個只看一次的孩子。翻遍 106 份團隊檔案，只有 7 支隊伍把課上給「以教學為業」的人，只有 5 支隊伍把器材留在別人手上。兩件都做的，只有一支。","body":"**Tier 3 is the one that matters.** HongKong-JSS, the High School 1st Runner-up, ran education in four tiers: over 1,600 primary pupils and parents with strawberry DNA extraction and live gel demonstrations, over 730 secondary peers, then a **two-day Teacher Biotech Training Workshop for 30 local school teachers covering PCR and agarose gel electrophoresis, combined with a standing loan programme letting those teachers borrow DNA samples and laboratory equipment from the team** — recorded in the team file as a deliberate attempt to leave teaching capacity behind after the competition ends. Tier 4 went into civic space: a stand at InnoEX 2026 and a joint announcement at the Drainage Services Department's annual media briefing, which put the project on an official government page and into local news.\n\nThe arithmetic is not subtle. A workshop for 30 teachers who each run a biology class for the next decade produces more teaching than a booth for 1,600 children who each see one gel, and it costs less. The same shape repeats everywhere once you look for it: the audience, the partner or the artefact that **multiplies** rather than the one that merely **counts**. It is worth saying plainly that the 1,600-pupil tier is not wasted — it is what made the teacher workshop credible and what filled it. The mistake is stopping there.\n\n**How rare is this?** Not uniformly. Standing in front of the stakeholder who can forbid your project is the house style of the decorated 2026 field, not a rarity: Oxford let four regulators overrule the beekeepers who preferred a living gut symbiont and switched to heat-inactivated dried yeast, stating the cost; HKSSC had its whole safety framing rebuilt by one professor's flat statement that engineered microbes cannot legally go into Hong Kong collection bins; Bist-China was told by a US state public-health educator that its prototype could hand a cancer-risk conclusion to an untrained user, and re-scoped it to a bench-side research instrument reporting only concentrations and quality-control status. That lever is available to anyone who asks the right person early enough.\n\nThe durable-capacity levers are the rare ones. **Of 106 teams, 7 taught people who teach for a living** — HongKong-JSS's 30 teachers, Muenster-University's grade 8 and 9 lesson concept built to North Rhine-Westphalia's school genetic-engineering rules and refined with partner-school teachers, UAlberta's Rural Teachers Synbiosium mapped to the Alberta curriculum with nine kits shipped in advance, MIT-MAHE walking teachers through every protocol step so the demonstration survives the team's departure, NIS Almaty-Medeu's teacher training across a 70-school network (nine partner schools were running the activities themselves by September), KAUST-KSA's course that trains youth volunteers who then teach rural farmers, and Marburg's curriculum-aligned toolbox tested with seven teachers at three schools. **And 5 left equipment or a kit in someone else's hands**: HongKong-JSS's standing loan, BAID-China's tactile magnetic genetic-circuit kit donated to a Beijing school for the visually impaired, UAlberta's nine shipped kits, NIS Almaty-Medeu's twelve individual hospital kits built because the volunteers and the shared LEGO had left with them, and Muenster-University's lending kit, which is designed rather than yet running. Only HongKong-JSS did both, and only HongKong-JSS added the civic tier on top.\n\n**Paper is the cheapest multiplier in the competition, and the report has already measured it.** Of 285 education files linked from the wikis of 31 decorated teams, 284 download today and one returns 403 — no dead links at all — against 8 of 21 software tools still running and 6 of 20 instruments rebuildable. Nothing has to be maintained: `static.igem.wiki` serves the file and the wiki freeze makes it permanent. Four teams took this further and served browser games from the frozen wiki itself, so even the interactive asset needs no hosting bill. But a file is not yet a capability. The census found that 33 of 64 artefacts ship an instruction layer for a second adult — a facilitator pack, a rulebook, a lesson plan with timings and materials — and the other 31 are the beautiful thing alone. Eton-College-UK ships its workshop as a facilitator pack and a student pack separately so somebody who was not there can rerun it. **That separation is the difference between an admirable artefact and a borrowable one.**\n\n**Build on what exists.** The cheapest multiplier of all is other people's finished work, and the strongest 2026 examples are explicit about it. Vilnius-Lithuania runs GelGenie's published, peer-reviewed U-Net weights for band segmentation and spends its own effort on the one step nobody had automated. Uni-Padua-IT forked and extended TISIGNER and validated the extension at the bench, with a 2.16-fold expression result and a failure rate cut from 52 percent to 2 percent. HongKong-HS built an entire high-school dry lab from NUPACK plus Wageningen iGEM 2024's miRADAR, and predicted its background-leakage failure mode before the gel showed it. Squirrel-Beijing met the Bronze contribution requirement by adding the characterisation an existing Registry part was missing rather than registering another new one. Eton-College-UK built on the open-source Biocoin wearable platform. In every case the borrowed base is named and cited, which is also what makes the team's own contribution legible.\n\n**Two more shapes worth stealing.** Princeton handed the public a genuine unsolved sub-problem from its own project — a 3D-printable gyroid biofilter, 20 mm by 25 mm, maximise contact surface area, with the team's real print parameters — ran it as a free asynchronous online competition, drew 42 submissions of which 26 passed dimensional and printability screening, ranked them computationally on total surface area, and then named the winners on the wiki and used their designs. Outreach became contributed engineering at almost no cost, and the task rewards spatial creativity rather than synthetic biology training, which is exactly why school students can win it. Stanford did the other move: its mentored bootcamp drew nearly 5,000 applications for 230 places, so instead of running it again at the same size the team converted the whole curriculum into SynBase, a free self-paced nine-module course with over 750 registered learners, and invited other teams to use it for their own onboarding. **When demand exceeds your hours, ship the course, not the cohort.**\n\n**Pool it.** HBUT-China initiated a five-school joint biosafety manual for anti-tumour synthetic biology with four other university teams, with internally unified but deliberately differentiable risk-assessment protocols, on the correct reasoning that one lab's risk-assessment competence is narrower than five labs'. HUST-China independently hosted a regional forum for 15 teams that replicated the Jamboree's own format — keynotes, a LiveStage block, judge commentary, a poster walk — and won the peer-voted iGEMers Prize. JLU-FBH coordinated a myth-busting handbook with submissions from more than 17 teams. None of these is expensive; all of them produce an artefact no single team could have afforded.\n\n**What this means for a Taiwanese high-school team.** Three multipliers are plainly available and under-used. First, teacher networks: a two-day PCR and gel workshop for in-service biology teachers is exactly the HongKong-JSS move, GEMS-Taiwan already owns instruments it built itself, and the loan shelf costs a sign-out sheet. Second, agricultural extension, which is Taiwan's strongest unexploited lever and the one the 2026 project already touched: farmers' associations and the district agricultural research and extension stations employ people whose job is to repeat advice to growers for years, and GEMS-Taiwan already knows one such body in the Lanyang River Friendly Farming Production Cooperative. Train the extension officers rather than the farmers. Third, the island's own cohort: Taiwan fielded thirteen competing teams in 2026 and Labi-Taiwan already runs TGEM, so HBUT's five-school manual and HUST's regional forum are both directly copyable. Add the free one: **3 of 31 decorated teams published any education material in Traditional Chinese, and all three already read it** — NCKU-Tainan, GEMS-Taiwan and HKSSC. Lambert-GA translated its children's book into thirteen languages including Simplified Chinese and not Traditional. A good artefact republished in Traditional Chinese with a reuse licence reaches a classroom nothing else in the 2026 census can reach, and only 1 of 136 education PDFs carried a reuse licence at all.\n\nScience museums are available but are a megaphone rather than a shelf: a weekend at a national science-education centre is attention, not capacity, unless something is left behind. Government departments are available for informational conversations, and GEMS-Taiwan has already had them, but a Taiwanese high-school team should not plan on a joint media briefing or a written regulatory determination — the one written determination that **is** free is iGEM's own, which BASIS-China obtained from the Director of Responsibility before collecting a single sample and then published. Not available: a federal science exhibition ship touring 33 cities, a national radio slot reaching a million listeners a day, and a deposit on a ministry-run open-educational-resources platform, which BOKU-Vienna could rely on in Austria and which nothing in this analysis verifies for Taiwan. Plan around what repeats, not what is photographed.","body_zh":"**真正關鍵的是第三層。** 高中組亞軍 HongKong-JSS 把科教活動分成四層：第一層用草莓 DNA 萃取與現場電泳，觸及超過 1,600 名小學生與家長；第二層觸及超過 730 名中學同儕；第三層是 **為 30 位本地學校教師辦的兩天「教師生物科技培訓工作坊」，內容涵蓋 PCR 與瓊脂膠體電泳，並搭配一個常設的借用方案，讓這些老師可以向團隊借 DNA 樣本與實驗器材** —— 團隊檔案記載，這是刻意要在競賽結束後把教學能量留下來。第四層則走進公共場域：在香港國際創科展 InnoEX 2026 設攤，並在渠務署年度記者會上共同發布，讓專案登上政府官方網頁與本地新聞。\n\n這筆算術並不精巧。為 30 位未來十年都會教生物課的老師辦一場工作坊，所產生的教學量超過讓 1,600 個孩子各看一塊膠體的攤位，而且成本更低。一旦開始找，這個形狀到處都在：挑**會放大**的對象、夥伴或產出，而不是只能**計數**的那一個。也要講清楚：1,600 人那一層並不是浪費——正是它讓教師工作坊有說服力，也是它把人招滿的。錯誤在於停在那裡。\n\n**這有多罕見？** 並不一致。站到那個有權否決你的關係人面前，是 2026 年獲獎群體的常態做法，而不是稀罕事：Oxford 讓四個主管與認證機構壓過偏好活體腸道共生菌的養蜂人，改用熱滅活乾酵母，並寫出這個選擇的代價；HKSSC 的整套安全論述，被一位教授一句「在香港，工程化微生物依法不能放進回收桶」徹底重建；Bist-China 被一位美國州衛生部門的醫檢教育者指出，原型機會把癌症風險結論直接交給未受訓練的使用者，於是重新定位為實驗桌旁的研究儀器，只回報濃度與品管狀態。只要夠早去問對的人，這個槓桿人人可用。\n\n稀有的是「留下能力」這一類槓桿。**106 支隊伍中，只有 7 支把課上給以教學為業的人**——HongKong-JSS 的 30 位老師；Muenster-University 依北萊茵-西發利亞邦校園基因工程實驗規定設計、並與夥伴學校教師共同修訂的八、九年級課程方案；UAlberta 對準亞伯達課綱、並事先寄出九份實作套件的「鄉村教師合成生物學研習」；MIT-MAHE 帶著老師把每個步驟走過一遍，讓示範在團隊離開後仍能繼續；NIS Almaty-Medeu 在 70 校網絡中同時培訓師生（到九月，已有九所夥伴學校自行開辦這些活動）；KAUST-KSA 訓練青年志工、再由志工去教偏鄉農民的課程；以及 Marburg 與三所學校七位教師一起試教的課綱對接教具箱。**另有 5 支把器材或套件留在別人手上**：HongKong-JSS 的常設借用方案；BAID-China 捐給北京一所視障學校、讓校內老師持續改用的觸覺磁性基因迴路套件；UAlberta 寄出的九份套件；NIS Almaty-Medeu 因為「志工和共用樂高都跟著離開」而做出的 12 份個人化病房套件；以及 Muenster-University 的外借套件——目前是設計完成，尚未實際運作。兩件都做的只有 HongKong-JSS，而且只有它再加上公共場域那一層。\n\n**紙本是全場最便宜的放大器，而本報告已經量過。** 31 支獲獎隊伍的 wiki 上共連出 285 份教育檔案，今天有 284 份下載得到，一份回傳 403，完全沒有死連結——相對地，21 個軟體工具只有 8 個還跑得動，20 件儀器只有 6 件重建得出來。什麼都不必維護：`static.igem.wiki` 負責供檔，wiki 凍結讓它永久存在。四支隊伍更進一步，把瀏覽器遊戲直接掛在凍結的 wiki 上，連互動產出都不需要有人付主機費。但「有檔案」還不等於「有能力」。普查發現，64 件產出中有 33 件附上給第二位大人看的操作層——帶領者手冊、遊戲規則、含時間與材料的教案——另外 31 件只有漂亮的東西本身。Eton-College-UK 把工作坊拆成帶領者包與學生包兩份，讓當天不在場的人也能重跑一次。**這個拆分，就是「令人佩服的產出」與「可被借走的產出」之間的差別。**\n\n**站在既有成果上。** 最便宜的放大器是別人已經做完的工作，而 2026 年最強的例子都把這件事說得很清楚。Vilnius-Lithuania 直接採用GelGenie 已發表、經同儕審查的 U-Net 權重做條帶切割，把自己的力氣花在唯一沒人自動化過的那一步。Uni-Padua-IT 分支並延伸了 TISIGNER，還在實驗端驗證延伸的部分：表現量提升 2.16 倍，失敗率由 52% 降到 2%。HongKong-HS 用 NUPACK 加上 Wageningen iGEM 2024 的 miRADAR，搭出一整個高中乾實驗室，並在膠體跑出來之前就先預測到背景洩漏這個失敗模式。Squirrel-Beijing 滿足銅牌貢獻要求的方式，是替一個既有 Registry 零件補上它缺少的特性數據，而不是再登錄一個新零件。Eton-College-UK 則建在開源穿戴式平台 Biocoin 之上。每一個案例都點名並引用了所借用的基礎，而這同時也讓團隊自己的貢獻看得清楚。\n\n**另外兩個值得照抄的形狀。** Princeton 把自己專案裡一個真正未解的子問題交給大眾——可 3D 列印的螺旋面生物濾材，直徑 20 公釐、高 25 公釐，目標是最大化接觸表面積，並附上團隊真正使用的列印參數——以免費、全非同步的線上競賽方式舉辦，收到 42 件投稿，其中 26 件通過尺寸與可列印性篩選，再以總表面積做電腦排序，最後在 wiki 上具名公布獲獎者並採用其設計。幾乎沒有成本，科普就變成了外部貢獻的工程；而且這個任務獎勵的是空間創造力而非合成生物學訓練，這正是中學生能夠獲勝的原因。Stanford 做的是另一手：它的導師制營隊收到近 5,000 份申請卻只有 230 個名額，於是團隊沒有照原規模再辦一次，而是把整套課程轉成 SynBase——一套免費、自主進度的九模組課程，註冊學習者超過 750 人——並邀請其他隊伍拿去訓練自己的新成員。**當需求超過你的工時，就交付課程，不要再交付一個班。**\n\n**把資源併起來。** HBUT-China 發起並主導了一份五校聯合生物安全手冊，與另外四支大學隊伍共同撰寫，內部統一卻刻意保留可區辨性的風險評估程序，理由很正確：一間實驗室的風險評估能力，比五間窄。HUST-China 自行舉辦區域論壇，接待 15 支隊伍，並刻意複製 Jamboree 本身的格式——主題演講、LiveStage 發表段、評審評論、海報走動交流——拿下同儕投票的 iGEMers Prize。JLU-FBH 統籌了一本破除迷思手冊，收錄超過 17 支隊伍的投稿。這些都不貴；而每一件都產出了單一隊伍負擔不起的成果。\n\n**這對台灣高中團隊意味著什麼。** 有三個放大器明顯可用，而且被用得太少。第一是教師網絡：為在職生物科教師辦一場兩天的 PCR 與電泳工作坊，就是 HongKong-JSS 那一手；GEMS-Taiwan 本來就擁有自己做出來的儀器，而一個借用架子只需要一張借還登記表。第二是農業推廣體系，這是台灣最被低估的槓桿，也是 2026 年專案已經碰到的一塊：農會與各區農業改良場裡，本來就有人以「年復一年把建議重複給農民」為職業，而 GEMS-Taiwan 已經認識蘭陽溪友善耕作生產合作社這樣一個組織。要訓練推廣人員，而不是只訓練農民。第三是島內自己的群體：台灣 2026 年有十三支隊伍參賽，Labi-Taiwan 已經在經營 TGEM，所以 HBUT 的五校手冊與 HUST 的區域論壇都可以直接照抄。再加上那個免費的：**31 支獲獎隊伍中，只有 3 支出版過任何繁體中文教育材料，而這三支本來就看得懂繁體**——NCKU-Tainan、GEMS-Taiwan 與 HKSSC。Lambert-GA 把童書譯成十三種語言，其中有簡體中文，沒有繁體中文。一份好的產出，用繁體中文重新出版並附上可重用授權，就能進到 2026 年普查中其他東西都到不了的教室；而 136 份教育 PDF 裡，只有 1 份真的附了可重用授權。\n\n科學博物館可用，但它是擴音器而不是架子：在國立科學教育場館待一個週末得到的是注意力，不是能力，除非有東西被留下來。政府部門可用於資訊性的對話，GEMS-Taiwan 也已經談過，但台灣高中團隊不該把計畫押在聯合記者會或書面法規認定上——唯一**真正**免費的書面認定來自 iGEM 自己：BASIS-China 在採集任何一份樣本之前，先向 iGEM 總部的 Director of Responsibility 取得書面同意，然後把那封信公開。不可得的是：巡迴 33 座城市的聯邦科學展覽船、每日百萬聽眾的全國廣播時段，以及在教育部層級的開放教育資源平台上存放材料——BOKU-Vienna 在奧地利能倚賴這一點，而本分析無法替台灣驗證同等管道。把計畫圍繞「會重複的東西」來排，而不是圍繞「會被拍照的東西」。","cards":[{"kicker":"Train the trainers","kicker_zh":"訓練訓練者","title":"HongKong-JSS taught 30 teachers, not 1,600 children","title_zh":"HongKong-JSS 教的是 30 位老師，不是 1,600 個孩子","body":"Two days of PCR and agarose gel electrophoresis for 30 local school teachers, recorded in the team file as a deliberate attempt to leave teaching capacity behind after the competition ends. Six other teams did something like it: Muenster-University built a lesson concept compliant with its state's school genetic-engineering rules and refined it with partner-school teachers; UAlberta mapped a half-day online event to the Alberta curriculum; MIT-MAHE walked teachers through every protocol step; NIS Almaty-Medeu trained teachers across a 70-school network until nine schools ran the activities themselves; KAUST-KSA trains youth volunteers who then teach rural farmers; Marburg tested its toolbox with seven teachers at three schools. **Seven of 106.**","body_zh":"兩天的 PCR 與瓊脂膠體電泳課程，對象是 30 位本地學校教師；團隊檔案明言，這是刻意要在競賽結束後留下教學能量。另有六支隊伍做了類似的事：Muenster-University 設計出符合所在邦校園基因工程規定的課程方案，並與夥伴學校教師共同修訂；UAlberta 把半天線上研習對準亞伯達課綱；MIT-MAHE 帶老師把每個步驟走過一遍；NIS Almaty-Medeu 在 70 校網絡裡持續培訓教師，直到九所學校能自行開辦；KAUST-KSA 訓練青年志工，再由志工去教偏鄉農民；Marburg 與三所學校的七位教師一起試教教具箱。**106 支中的 7 支。**","chips":["30 teachers, 2 days","PCR and gel electrophoresis","7 of 106 teams"],"chips_zh":["30 位教師、2 天","PCR 與膠體電泳","106 支中的 7 支"]},{"kicker":"Leave the capability behind","kicker_zh":"把能力留下來","title":"A loan shelf beats a demonstration","title_zh":"一個借用架，勝過一場示範","body":"The same team ran a standing loan programme letting the trained teachers borrow DNA samples and laboratory equipment. Four others left hardware in other hands: BAID-China donated its tactile magnetic genetic-circuit kit to a Beijing school for the visually impaired so its own teachers keep adapting it; UAlberta shipped nine hands-on kits before its teacher event; NIS Almaty-Medeu built twelve individual hospital kits after noticing that the volunteers and the shared LEGO left with them; Muenster-University designed a lending kit for schools with no thermocycler. The cheapest version is paper and needs no loan desk at all — 284 of 285 education files still download, against 8 of 21 software tools still running.","body_zh":"同一支隊伍還辦了常設借用方案，讓受訓教師可以借走 DNA 樣本與實驗器材。另有四支把硬體留在別人手上：BAID-China 把觸覺磁性基因迴路套件捐給北京一所視障學校，讓校內老師持續改用；UAlberta 在教師研習前先寄出九份實作套件；NIS Almaty-Medeu 發現「志工和共用樂高都跟著離開」後，做出 12 份個人化病房套件；Muenster-University 則為沒有 PCR 儀的學校設計了外借套件。最便宜的版本是紙本，連借還櫃台都不需要——285 份教育檔案有 284 份今天仍下載得到，而 21 個軟體工具只有 8 個還跑得動。","chips":["Standing loan of DNA and kit","5 of 106 left equipment","284 of 285 files survive"],"chips_zh":["DNA 與器材常設外借","106 支中 5 支留下器材","285 份檔案中 284 份存活"]},{"kicker":"Make the students the faculty","kicker_zh":"讓學生變師資","title":"HongKong-HS trained its own juniors to teach","title_zh":"HongKong-HS 把自己的學弟妹訓練成講師","body":"The Cascading Peer-Educator Model trained non-iGEM junior-form Science Team members as Student Facilitators in both content and facilitation skills, then had those facilitators independently run workshops for their schoolmates — and published the training guide for holding a secondary school workshop so the materials outlive the team. It multiplies in two directions at once: it buys delivery capacity the team does not have to staff, and it builds the next cohort's bench. HKSSC did the recruitment half of this with eight after-school workshops over seven months for 28 participants aged 11 to 16, described as a deliberate pipeline for future team members.","body_zh":"「階梯式同儕教育者模式」把非 iGEM 的低年級科學隊成員訓練成學生帶領者，內容與帶領技巧並重，再讓這些帶領者獨立為同校學生開辦工作坊——並公開了一份「如何辦一場中學工作坊」的培訓指引，讓材料活得比團隊更久。它同時往兩個方向放大：既買到團隊不必自己出人力的授課量，也養出下一屆的板凳深度。HKSSC 做了其中的招募那一半：七個月內八場課後工作坊，28 位 11 至 16 歲的參與者，團隊明言這是為未來成員刻意鋪的管道。","chips":["Juniors run the workshops","Training guide published","Also a recruitment pipeline"],"chips_zh":["由低年級學生主持工作坊","培訓指引已公開","同時是招募管道"]},{"kicker":"Borrow an institution's channel","kicker_zh":"借機構的通路","title":"BOKU deposited on the education ministry's platform","title_zh":"BOKU 把材料存進教育部的平台","body":"BOKU-Vienna published all its tested worksheets, workshop guides and experiment protocols as Open Educational Resources on eduvidual.at, the official learning platform of the Austrian federal education ministry, so teachers nationwide can reuse them. The same instinct, applied to attention rather than storage, produced HongKong-JSS's stand at InnoEX 2026 and its joint announcement at the Drainage Services Department's annual media briefing, which landed an official government page and local news; Muenster-University's stand on a federal research-ministry exhibition ship touring 33 cities; GU Frankfurt's slot on hr3, about a million daily listeners, and a political proposal the cross-party Bundestag group agreed to consider. **A shelf keeps paying out; a megaphone pays once.**","body_zh":"BOKU-Vienna 把所有經過試教的學習單、工作坊指引與實驗流程，全部以開放教育資源形式發布在 eduvidual.at——奧地利聯邦教育部的官方學習平台——讓全國教師都能重用。同樣的直覺若用在注意力而非儲存上，就產生了 HongKong-JSS 在 InnoEX 2026 的攤位，以及在渠務署年度記者會上的共同發布，換來政府官方網頁與本地新聞；Muenster-University 在聯邦研究部巡迴 33 座城市的科學展覽船上設攤；GU Frankfurt 上了每日約百萬聽眾的 hr3 電台，並提出一份跨黨派聯邦議院小組同意納入考慮的政策建議。**架子會持續產出，擴音器只響一次。**","chips":["Ministry platform deposit","Government media briefing","Shelf, not megaphone"],"chips_zh":["存進部會平台","政府記者會發布","要架子，不要擴音器"]},{"kicker":"Stand in front of the veto","kicker_zh":"站到否決權面前","title":"Oxford let regulators overrule its own users","title_zh":"Oxford 讓主管機關壓過自己的使用者","body":"Beekeepers preferred a persistent living engineered gut symbiont because it minimises their labour. Oxford took the question to four regulatory and certification bodies instead of simply obeying, switched the chassis to heat-inactivated dried yeast, and stated plainly what that cost: the persistence the beekeepers wanted, meaning repeat dosing and more labour. The lever is choosing the person whose objection changes the design rather than the person who compliments it. Bist-China's prototype was re-scoped to a bench-side research instrument after a state public-health educator found it could hand a cancer-risk conclusion to an untrained user. BASIS-China asked iGEM's own Director of Responsibility in writing before collecting a sample, and published the approval email.","body_zh":"養蜂人偏好一種持續存活的工程化腸道共生菌，因為那樣最省人力。Oxford 沒有照單全收，而是把問題帶去四個主管與認證機構，最後把底盤改成熱滅活乾酵母，並明白寫出代價：失去養蜂人想要的持續性，意思是必須重複投藥、更費人力。槓桿在於挑那個「反對意見會改變設計」的人，而不是那個會稱讚設計的人。Bist-China 的原型機在一位州衛生部門的醫檢教育者指出它會把癌症風險結論交給未受訓練的使用者之後，被重新定位為實驗桌旁的研究儀器。BASIS-China 則在採集任何樣本之前，先以書面向 iGEM 的 Director of Responsibility 請示，並把同意信公開。","chips":["Four regulators beat the users","Cost of the switch stated","Written determination, free"],"chips_zh":["四個主管機關勝過使用者","明寫改設計的代價","書面認定，免費"]},{"kicker":"Build on what exists","kicker_zh":"站在既有成果上","title":"Uni-Padua forked TISIGNER instead of rebuilding it","title_zh":"Uni-Padua 分支 TISIGNER，而不是重寫它","body":"ReTIsigner forks and extends a cited scientific tool and then validates the extension at the bench: a 2.16-fold wet-lab expression result and a failure rate cut from 52 percent to 2 percent. Three more examples are directly within high-school reach. Vilnius-Lithuania runs GelGenie's peer-reviewed U-Net weights for segmentation and spends its own effort on the one unautomated step. HongKong-HS built its whole dry lab from NUPACK plus Wageningen iGEM 2024's miRADAR. Squirrel-Beijing met the Bronze contribution requirement by adding the characterisation an existing Registry part was missing — a 15 to 37 degrees C gradient crossed with culture time — rather than registering another new part.","body_zh":"ReTIsigner 分支並延伸了一個有被引用的科學工具，然後在實驗端驗證延伸的部分：表現量提升 2.16 倍，失敗率由 52% 降到 2%。另有三個例子完全在高中能力範圍內。Vilnius-Lithuania 直接採用 GelGenie 經同儕審查的 U-Net 權重做切割，把力氣花在唯一沒被自動化的那一步。HongKong-HS 用 NUPACK 加上 Wageningen iGEM 2024 的 miRADAR 搭出整個乾實驗室。Squirrel-Beijing 滿足銅牌貢獻要求的方式，是替一個既有 Registry 零件補上缺少的特性數據——15 到 37 度的溫度梯度乘上培養時間——而不是再登錄一個新零件。","chips":["Fork, then validate at the bench","2.16-fold, 52% to 2%","Characterise, do not re-register"],"chips_zh":["先分支，再上實驗台驗證","2.16 倍、52% 降到 2%","補特性數據，別再登新零件"]},{"kicker":"Turn the audience into contributors","kicker_zh":"把觀眾變成貢獻者","title":"Princeton's PITCCH shipped a real unsolved part","title_zh":"Princeton 的 PITCCH 把真正未解的零件交出去","body":"Entrants were handed a genuine open engineering problem from the project — design a 3D-printable gyroid biofilter, 20 mm diameter by 25 mm height, maximising contact surface area — along with the team's actual print parameters. Free, fully asynchronous, online, with a junior division for grades 5 to 12. **42 submissions, 26 passed dimensional and printability screening, ranked computationally on total surface area, two winners named on the wiki and their designs used.** Outreach became contributed engineering at almost no cost, and because the task rewards spatial creativity rather than synthetic biology training, school students can genuinely win it.","body_zh":"參賽者拿到的是專案裡一個真正開放的工程問題——設計一個可 3D 列印的螺旋面生物濾材，直徑 20 公釐、高 25 公釐，目標是最大化接觸表面積——還附上團隊實際使用的列印參數。免費、全非同步、線上，並設有五到十二年級的少年組。**42 件投稿，26 件通過尺寸與可列印性篩選，以總表面積做電腦排序，兩位獲獎者在 wiki 上具名，其設計被採用。**幾乎零成本，科普就變成了外部貢獻的工程；而且這個任務獎勵的是空間創造力而非合成生物學訓練，中學生真的贏得到。","chips":["A real open sub-problem","42 entries, 26 screened","Winners named and used"],"chips_zh":["真正開放的子問題","42 件投稿、26 件過篩","獲獎者具名且設計被採用"]},{"kicker":"Ship the course, not the cohort","kicker_zh":"交付課程，不是交付一個班","title":"Stanford turned 5,000 applications into SynBase","title_zh":"Stanford 把 5,000 份申請變成 SynBase","body":"Stanford's free online bioengineering bootcamp drew nearly 5,000 applications from all 50 US states and over 100 countries for 230 places, two-thirds of applicants female and over 60 percent from low-income and first-generation backgrounds. Rather than run the same cohort again, the team converted the entire curriculum into SynBase: nine self-paced modules, saved progress, knowledge checks and discussion boards, no application and no deadline, free worldwide, **750 or more registered learners and 650 or more free-response contributions** — and an explicit invitation to other iGEM teams to use or adapt it for onboarding their own members. The teaching asset now outlives the cohort that could not be staffed.","body_zh":"Stanford 的免費線上生物工程密集營，收到來自全美 50 州與超過 100 個國家的近 5,000 份申請，名額只有 230 個；申請者中三分之二為女性，超過六成來自低收入或家族第一代大學生背景。團隊沒有照原規模再辦一屆，而是把整套課程轉成 SynBase：九個自主進度模組、進度保存、知識檢核與討論區，不需申請、沒有截止日、全球免費，**註冊學習者 750 人以上、開放式回應貢獻 650 則以上**——並公開邀請其他 iGEM 隊伍拿去訓練自己的新成員。那份教學資產，現在活得比那個排不出人力的班更久。","chips":["5,000 applications, 230 places","Nine self-paced modules","750+ learners, no deadline"],"chips_zh":["5,000 份申請、230 個名額","九個自主進度模組","750 人以上、無截止日"]},{"kicker":"Pool it across teams","kicker_zh":"跨隊共同承擔","title":"HBUT wrote one biosafety manual for five schools","title_zh":"HBUT 為五所學校寫了一份生物安全手冊","body":"HBUT-China initiated and led a five-school joint biosafety manual for anti-tumour synthetic biology with four other university teams, covering oncolytic-virus operating standards, GMO leakage hazards and waste disposal, published as a downloadable PDF with internally unified but deliberately differentiable risk-assessment protocols because the five teams use different carriers. The reasoning is the whole point: one lab's risk-assessment competence is narrower than five labs'. HUST-China hosted a regional forum for 15 teams replicating the Jamboree's own format and won the peer-voted iGEMers Prize; JLU-FBH coordinated a myth-busting handbook with more than 17 teams contributing.","body_zh":"HBUT-China 發起並主導一份抗腫瘤合成生物學的五校聯合生物安全手冊，與另外四支大學隊伍共同撰寫，涵蓋溶瘤病毒操作標準、基改生物洩漏風險與廢棄物處理，以可下載 PDF 發布；因為五隊使用不同載體，風險評估程序刻意做到內部統一卻可區辨。重點在那個理由：一間實驗室的風險評估能力，比五間窄。HUST-China 為 15 支隊伍舉辦區域論壇，複製 Jamboree 本身的格式，並拿下同儕投票的 iGEMers Prize；JLU-FBH 統籌一本破除迷思手冊，有超過 17 支隊伍投稿。","chips":["Five labs, one manual","Unified but differentiable","TGEM is the Taiwanese route"],"chips_zh":["五間實驗室、一份手冊","統一但可區辨","台灣的管道是 TGEM"]}],"table":{"head":["The move","Team","Multiplier type","The obvious version it beat","Open to a Taiwanese high-school team?"],"head_zh":["做法","團隊","放大類型","它勝過的明顯做法","台灣高中團隊可行嗎？"],"rows":[["Two-day Teacher Biotech Training Workshop in PCR and agarose gel electrophoresis for 30 local school teachers","HongKong-JSS (High School)","Train the trainers","A tenth strawberry-DNA booth for primary pupils","Yes"],["Standing loan programme letting those teachers borrow DNA samples and laboratory equipment from the team","HongKong-JSS (High School)","Leave the capability behind","Packing the kit away when the workshop ends","Yes, with a sign-out sheet"],["Exhibitor stand at InnoEX 2026 plus a joint announcement at the Drainage Services Department annual media briefing, landing an official government page and local news","HongKong-JSS (High School)","Borrow an institution's channel","A team Instagram post and a school assembly","Partly, a city agricultural office is reachable, a joint briefing is not assured"],["Drainage Services Department guidance replaced earlier chromoproteins with mRFP1e, giving a visible channel for non-specialists and a fluorescence channel for quantification","HongKong-JSS (High School)","Stand in front of the veto","Asking a professor who already liked the design","Yes"],["More Happy Farm said plainly that not every farmer wants to own a device, which moved the plan from instrument sales to a certification service","HongKong-JSS (High School)","Stand in front of the veto","A willingness-to-buy survey of farmers","Yes"],["Grade 8 and 9 protease lesson concept compliant with state school genetic-engineering rules, refined with partner-school teachers, plus a university module where master's students build and trial lesson plans","Muenster-University (Overgrad)","Train the trainers","One school visit with a borrowed demonstration","Partly, curriculum alignment yes, the university module needs a faculty partner"],["Lending experiment-kit designed because thermocyclers, electrophoresis chambers and photometers are not in every school","Muenster-University (Overgrad)","Leave the capability behind","Running the activity only where the equipment already is","Yes"],["All tested worksheets, workshop guides and experiment protocols deposited as Open Educational Resources on eduvidual.at, the Austrian federal education ministry platform","BOKU-Vienna (Overgrad)","Borrow an institution's channel","PDFs on the team wiki and nowhere else","Unverified, depends whether a Taiwanese teaching platform takes outside deposits"],["Cascading Peer-Educator Model: non-iGEM junior-form Science Team members trained as Student Facilitators who then ran workshops for schoolmates independently, with the training guide published","HongKong-HS (High School)","Make the students the faculty","Team members delivering every session themselves","Yes"],["Eight after-school workshops over seven months for 28 participants aged 11 to 16, described as a deliberate pipeline for future team members","HKSSC (High School)","Make the students the faculty","Recruiting next year's team from whoever volunteers","Yes"],["Rural Teachers Synbiosium, a half-day online professional-development event mapped to the Alberta middle and high school curriculum, with nine free hands-on kits shipped in advance","UAlberta (Undergrad)","Train the trainers","Helping rural schools found their own competition teams","Yes"],["Teachers walked through every protocol step so they could keep running the demonstration after the team left, and Vision Empower approved the tactile models for use across its associated schools","MIT-MAHE (Undergrad)","Train the trainers","Performing the demonstration for the class and leaving","Yes"],["Tactile magnetic genetic-circuit kit donated to a Beijing school for the visually impaired so its own teachers keep adapting it for different ages","BAID-China (High School)","Leave the capability behind","Taking the prototype home after the workshop","Yes"],["Teachers trained alongside students across a 70-school network, until by September teachers and older students at nine partner schools were delivering the activities themselves","NIS Almaty-Medeu (High School)","Train the trainers","Counting the 226 children reached in six school visits","Yes"],["Twelve individual hospital kits built after a paediatric oncology visit, because the volunteers and the shared LEGO left with them","NIS Almaty-Medeu (High School)","Leave the capability behind","Booking a second visit with the same shared equipment","Yes"],["A farmer-facing course that trains youth volunteers who then go and teach rural farmers","KAUST-KSA (Overgrad)","Train the trainers","Team members visiting farms themselves","Yes, through a farmers' association or extension station"],["Nearly 5,000 applications for 230 mentored bootcamp places converted into SynBase, a free self-paced nine-module course with 750 or more registered learners","Stanford University (Undergrad)","Ship the course, not the cohort","Running the same bootcamp again next summer at the same size","Yes"],["PITCCH handed the public a real unsolved sub-problem, a 3D-printable gyroid biofilter 20 mm by 25 mm maximising contact surface area, with the team's own print parameters; 42 submissions, 26 passed screening, two winners named and their designs used","Princeton (Undergrad)","Turn the audience into contributors","A poster session explaining the finished design","Yes"],["Five-school joint biosafety manual for anti-tumour synthetic biology co-authored with four other university teams, with internally unified but deliberately differentiable risk-assessment protocols","HBUT-China (Undergrad)","Pool it across teams","Writing your own laboratory risk assessment alone","Yes, through TGEM"],["First Central-China iGEM Forum, independently hosted for 15 teams and deliberately replicating the Jamboree format of keynotes, a LiveStage block, judge commentary and a poster walk","HUST-China (Undergrad)","Pool it across teams","Attending somebody else's regional meetup","Yes, through TGEM"],["Ladder Detector runs GelGenie's published peer-reviewed U-Net weights for band segmentation and spends the team's own effort on the one step nobody had automated","Vilnius-Lithuania (Undergrad)","Build on what exists","Training a segmentation network on gel images you do not have","Yes"],["ReTIsigner forks and extends TISIGNER, validated by a 2.16-fold wet-lab expression result and a failure rate cut from 52 percent to 2 percent","Uni-Padua-IT (Undergrad)","Build on what exists","Writing a new codon optimiser from scratch","Yes"],["A whole high-school dry lab built from NUPACK plus Wageningen iGEM 2024's miRADAR, ranking 16 candidate switches on explicit thermodynamic criteria and predicting the background-leakage failure before the gel showed it","HongKong-HS (High School)","Build on what exists","A bespoke script nobody outside the team can check","Yes"],["Bronze contribution met by adding the characterisation an existing Registry part was missing, a 15 to 37 degrees C gradient crossed with culture time, instead of registering another new part","Squirrel-Beijing (High School)","Build on what exists","Registering one more new and uncharacterised part","Yes"],["Wearable sensing built on the open-source Biocoin platform, with the substrate predictor released as a protease-agnostic package another team retrains on a basic laptop in a few hours","Eton-College-UK (High School)","Build on what exists","Designing a new potentiostat from first principles","Yes"],["Four regulatory and certification bodies overruled the beekeepers' preference for a living engineered gut symbiont; the chassis became heat-inactivated dried yeast and the cost of that switch was stated","Oxford (Undergrad)","Stand in front of the veto","Following the users who liked the original plan","Yes, a certification body is more reachable than a national regulator"],["A state public-health medical laboratory educator found the prototype could hand a cancer-risk conclusion to an untrained user, so it was re-scoped to a bench-side research instrument reporting only concentrations and quality-control status","Bist-China (High School)","Stand in front of the veto","A friendly clinician calling the idea promising","Yes"],["Asked iGEM's Safety and Regulatory Committee before collecting any samples, obtained written approval from the Director of Responsibility to collect shed cat hair without an Animal Use Form, and published the email","BASIS-China (High School)","Stand in front of the veto","Assuming an unavailable form means the work cannot be done","Yes, and free"],["Browser games served from the frozen wiki itself, so even the interactive teaching asset needs no server anyone must keep paying for","LYON, GU Frankfurt, HongKong-JSS, GEMS-Taiwan","Leave the capability behind","A hosted web app that goes dark when the hosting bill stops","Yes, and already done once"]],"rows_zh":[["為 30 位本地學校教師辦的兩天教師生物科技培訓工作坊，內容涵蓋 PCR 與瓊脂膠體電泳","HongKong-JSS（高中組）","訓練訓練者","再辦第十個給小學生的草莓 DNA 攤位","可行"],["常設借用方案，讓這些老師向團隊借用 DNA 樣本與實驗器材","HongKong-JSS（高中組）","把能力留下來","工作坊結束就把器材收回庫房","可行，只需一張借還登記表"],["在 InnoEX 2026 設攤，並在渠務署年度記者會上共同發布，換來政府官方網頁與本地新聞報導","HongKong-JSS（高中組）","借機構的通路","團隊發一則 Instagram 貼文加一場朝會","部分可行，地方農業局談得到，但聯合記者會不保證"],["渠務署的建議把先前使用的色素蛋白換成 mRFP1e，讓非專業者看得見顏色，也保留螢光通道做定量","HongKong-JSS（高中組）","站到否決權面前","去問一位本來就認同這個設計的教授","可行"],["More Happy Farm 直言並非每位農民都想擁有一台儀器，使計畫從賣儀器轉為提供認證服務","HongKong-JSS（高中組）","站到否決權面前","對農民做一份購買意願調查","可行"],["符合所在邦校園基因工程規定、並與夥伴學校教師共同修訂的八、九年級蛋白酶課程方案，外加一門由碩士生設計並試教課程的大學師培模組","Muenster-University（研究生組）","訓練訓練者","帶著借來的示範去學校跑一次","部分可行，課綱對接可以，大學師培模組需要大學端夥伴"],["因為並非每所學校都有 PCR 儀、電泳槽與分光光度計而設計的外借實驗套件","Muenster-University（研究生組）","把能力留下來","只在本來就有器材的地方做活動","可行"],["把所有經過試教的學習單、工作坊指引與實驗流程，以開放教育資源形式存入奧地利聯邦教育部的官方平台 eduvidual.at","BOKU-Vienna（研究生組）","借機構的通路","只把 PDF 放在團隊 wiki 上","尚未驗證，取決於台灣的教學平台是否接受外部投件"],["階梯式同儕教育者模式：把非 iGEM 的低年級科學隊成員訓練成學生帶領者，再讓他們獨立為同校學生開辦工作坊，並公開培訓指引","HongKong-HS（高中組）","讓學生變師資","每一場都由團隊成員親自上","可行"],["七個月內八場課後工作坊，28 位 11 至 16 歲參與者，團隊明言這是為未來成員刻意鋪的管道","HKSSC（高中組）","讓學生變師資","下一屆隊員等誰自己來報名就好","可行"],["鄉村教師合成生物學研習：半天線上師培，對準亞伯達中學課綱，並事先寄出九份免費實作套件","UAlberta（大學組）","訓練訓練者","協助偏鄉學校自己成立參賽隊","可行"],["帶著老師把每一個操作步驟走過一遍，讓示範在團隊離開後仍能繼續；Vision Empower 核可那套觸覺教具，將在其合作學校推廣使用","MIT-MAHE（大學組）","訓練訓練者","替全班做完示範然後離開","可行"],["把觸覺磁性基因迴路套件捐給北京一所視障學校，讓校內老師持續針對不同年齡改用","BAID-China（高中組）","把能力留下來","工作坊結束把原型帶回家","可行"],["在 70 校網絡中同時培訓教師與學生，到九月已有九所夥伴學校的教師與高年級學生自行開辦這些活動","NIS Almaty-Medeu（高中組）","訓練訓練者","統計六場校訪觸及的 226 名兒童","可行"],["在一次兒童腫瘤科探訪後製作 12 份個人化病房套件，因為志工和共用樂高都跟著離開了","NIS Almaty-Medeu（高中組）","把能力留下來","再安排一次帶同一批共用器材的探訪","可行"],["面向農民的課程，訓練青年志工，再由志工去教偏鄉農民","KAUST-KSA（研究生組）","訓練訓練者","團隊成員自己跑農場","可行，可透過農會或農業改良場"],["近 5,000 份申請爭取 230 個導師制營隊名額，於是整套課程被轉成 SynBase：免費、自主進度的九模組課程，註冊學習者 750 人以上","Stanford University（大學組）","交付課程，不是交付一個班","明年夏天照同樣規模再辦一屆","可行"],["PITCCH 把專案裡一個真正未解的子問題交給大眾：可 3D 列印、直徑 20 公釐高 25 公釐、最大化接觸表面積的螺旋面生物濾材，並附團隊實際列印參數；42 件投稿、26 件過篩，兩位獲獎者具名且設計被採用","Princeton（大學組）","把觀眾變成貢獻者","辦一場海報說明會解釋已完成的設計","可行"],["與另外四支大學隊伍共同撰寫的抗腫瘤合成生物學五校聯合生物安全手冊，風險評估程序內部統一卻刻意可區辨","HBUT-China（大學組）","跨隊共同承擔","自己一間實驗室寫自己的風險評估","可行，可透過 TGEM"],["自行舉辦第一屆華中 iGEM 論壇，接待 15 支隊伍，並刻意複製 Jamboree 的格式：主題演講、LiveStage 發表段、評審評論、海報走動交流","HUST-China（大學組）","跨隊共同承擔","去參加別人辦的區域聚會","可行，可透過 TGEM"],["Ladder Detector 直接採用 GelGenie 已發表、經同儕審查的 U-Net 權重做條帶切割，把自己的力氣花在唯一沒人自動化過的那一步","Vilnius-Lithuania（大學組）","站在既有成果上","用自己根本沒有的膠體影像去訓練切割模型","可行"],["ReTIsigner 分支並延伸 TISIGNER，並以實驗驗證：表現量提升 2.16 倍，失敗率由 52% 降到 2%","Uni-Padua-IT（大學組）","站在既有成果上","從零寫一個新的密碼子最佳化工具","可行"],["用 NUPACK 加上 Wageningen iGEM 2024 的 miRADAR 搭出一整個高中乾實驗室，以明確的熱力學標準排序 16 個候選開關，並在膠體跑出來之前就先預測到背景洩漏這個失敗模式","HongKong-HS（高中組）","站在既有成果上","寫一支外人完全無法檢驗的自製腳本","可行"],["以補上既有 Registry 零件缺少的特性數據來滿足銅牌貢獻要求：15 到 37 度的溫度梯度乘上培養時間，而不是再登錄一個新零件","Squirrel-Beijing（高中組）","站在既有成果上","再登錄一個新的、沒有特性數據的零件","可行"],["穿戴式感測建在開源 Biocoin 平台上，並把底物預測模型釋出為不綁特定蛋白酶的套件，別隊用一般筆電幾小時就能重新訓練","Eton-College-UK（高中組）","站在既有成果上","從基本原理重新設計一台恆電位儀","可行"],["四個主管與認證機構壓過養蜂人偏好的活體工程化腸道共生菌；底盤改為熱滅活乾酵母，並明寫這個改動的代價","Oxford（大學組）","站到否決權面前","聽從那些認同原方案的使用者","可行，認證機構比中央主管機關容易談到"],["一位州衛生部門的醫檢教育者發現原型機會把癌症風險結論交給未受訓練的使用者，於是重新定位為實驗桌旁的研究儀器，只回報濃度與品管狀態","Bist-China（高中組）","站到否決權面前","一位友善的臨床醫師說這想法很有潛力","可行"],["在採集任何樣本前先詢問 iGEM 安全與法規委員會，取得 Director of Responsibility 的書面同意，得以在無動物使用表的情況下收集自然掉落的貓毛，並公開該信件","BASIS-China（高中組）","站到否決權面前","以為表格申請不到就等於這件事不能做","可行，而且免費"],["把瀏覽器遊戲直接掛在凍結的 wiki 上，連互動教材都不需要有人持續付主機費","LYON、GU Frankfurt、HongKong-JSS、GEMS-Taiwan","把能力留下來","架一個雲端網頁應用，帳單一停就黑掉","可行，而且已經做過一次"]]},"checklist":["Choose a 2027 topic that has a professional repeater in Taiwan behind it, a teacher, an extension officer, an inspector or a technician, and name that person before you fix the biology.","Budget one two-day training session for adults who teach or advise for a living, and treat the pupil-facing events as the thing that recruits and legitimises it rather than as the goal.","Decide now what you will lend: list the equipment and consumables a school or a farm could borrow from you in 2028, and write the loan terms into the plan.","Ship every teaching artefact as a file on the frozen wiki with a facilitator sheet naming the time, the materials and the cost, because 31 of 64 artefacts in the 2026 census were the beautiful thing alone.","Publish at least one artefact in Traditional Chinese and state on the file itself that it may be reused, since 3 of 31 decorated teams reached Traditional Chinese and 1 of 136 education PDFs carried a reuse licence.","Before any design freezes, book the stakeholder who can forbid the project, a certification body, a procurement officer or a safety committee, and write down in advance what you would change if they said no.","Search for the published model, part or instrument you can fork before you write one, and say on the wiki why you did not rebuild it.","Hand the public one genuine unsolved sub-problem with real constraints, judge it on a single measurable criterion, and name the winners inside your own design.","Take one artefact to the other Taiwanese teams through TGEM and co-author it, so what survives the season is larger than one school's work."],"checklist_zh":["選一個 2027 題目，背後要有台灣的「職業重複者」：老師、農業推廣人員、稽查員或技術員；在定下生物學內容之前，先把這個人指名出來。","預算中排進一場兩天的培訓，對象是以教學或諮詢為業的大人；把面向學生的活動當成替它招人並建立正當性的手段，而不是目標本身。","現在就決定要借出什麼：列出 2028 年一所學校或一座農場可以向你借走的器材與耗材，並把借用條件寫進計畫。","每一份教材都要以檔案形式放上凍結的 wiki，並附一張帶領者說明，寫明所需時間、材料與費用；2026 年普查的 64 件產出中，有 31 件只有漂亮的東西本身。","至少出版一份繁體中文產出，並在檔案本身寫明可重用；31 支獲獎隊伍中只有 3 支觸及繁體中文，136 份教育 PDF 中只有 1 份附了可重用授權。","在任何設計定案之前，先約那個有權否決專案的關係人：認證機構、採購人員或安全委員會；並事先寫下如果對方說不，你會改什麼。","在自己動手寫之前，先去找可以分支的已發表模型、零件或儀器，並在 wiki 上寫出你為什麼沒有重做一遍。","把一個真正未解、帶有真實限制條件的子問題交給大眾，用單一可量測的標準評分，並在自己的設計中把獲獎者具名寫進去。","透過 TGEM 把一份產出帶給台灣其他隊伍共同撰寫，讓賽季結束後留下來的東西，大於一所學校自己的成果。"],"method":"What was read. All 106 team files in `research/teams/`, field by field: `good.publicEngagement`, `good.ihp`, `good.realWorld`, `good.partners`, `dry.software`, `dry.stack`, `gemsTakeaway`, `summary`, `awards`, `section` and `country`. The `gemsTakeaway` field was the most productive single source because it already records what a GEMS reader should steal. Three measured figures are quoted rather than re-derived and were read from the files that established them: 284 of 285 education files still downloading, 1 of 136 PDFs carrying a reuse licence, 3 of 31 teams reaching Traditional Chinese and 33 of 64 artefacts shipping facilitator instructions, all from `education-afterlife.json`; 8 of 21 software tools still running from `software-afterlife.json`; 6 of 20 instruments rebuildable from `hardware-afterlife.json`. The Taiwan cohort figures come from `taiwan-cohort.json`.\n\nThe inclusion rule. A move counted as a multiplier only if the team file named something checkable — a number, a named partner, or a named artefact — and the move bought reach, durability or credibility that the obvious version of the same activity would not have bought. A workshop for children counted only if it trained someone who teaches again, left an object behind, or produced an artefact a stranger could run. Reach alone never counted: a headcount is the thing this block is written against. Consultations counted only where the file records a design change or a documented reason for no change, which is why stakeholder entries here are tied to a specific reversal rather than to a meeting.\n\nWhat the team files cannot see. A technique used but not written up is invisible, so every count here is a count of documented practice, not of practice. Teams that trained teachers and did not say so are missing; so is any loan, donation or institutional deposit a team thought too ordinary to record. The direction of that error is one-sided: the rarity figures are upper bounds on rarity and the real numbers can only be higher. Nor can a file establish that a multiplier worked — 30 trained teachers is an input, and no team in this field followed up to show those teachers teaching the following year. The Austrian ministry deposit and the Muenster lending kit are reported as the files describe them, one unverified from this network and one designed rather than running.\n\nThe sample is decorated teams only. These 106 files cover award winners and nominees, so nothing here is a base rate for iGEM 2026 at large. When this block says 7 of 106 teams trained teachers, it means 7 of 106 decorated teams — among the field's strongest and best-documented programmes, which makes the scarcity more striking, not less.","method_zh":"讀了什麼。`research/teams/` 裡全部 106 份團隊檔案，逐欄閱讀：`good.publicEngagement`、`good.ihp`、`good.realWorld`、`good.partners`、`dry.software`、`dry.stack`、`gemsTakeaway`、`summary`、`awards`、`section` 與 `country`。單一來源中最有產出的是 `gemsTakeaway`，因為它本來就記錄了 GEMS 讀者該偷走什麼。有三組已量測數字是引用而非重新推導，直接取自建立它們的檔案：285 份教育檔案中 284 份仍可下載、136 份 PDF 中只有 1 份附可重用授權、31 支隊伍中只有 3 支觸及繁體中文、64 件產出中 33 件附帶領者說明，均出自 `education-afterlife.json`；21 個軟體工具中 8 個仍可運作，出自 `software-afterlife.json`；20 件儀器中 6 件可重建，出自 `hardware-afterlife.json`。台灣隊伍的統計數字取自 `taiwan-cohort.json`。\n\n納入規則。一個做法要算作放大器，必須在團隊檔案裡指名出可查核的東西——一個數字、一個具名夥伴，或一件具名產出——而且該做法換到的觸及、續存或可信度，是同一活動的明顯版本換不到的。給兒童辦的工作坊只有在它訓練了會再去教別人的人、留下了實體物件，或產出了外人能照著跑的成果時才算。純粹的觸及人數一律不算：這整個段落就是寫來反對人頭數的。關係人諮詢只有在檔案記錄了設計變更、或記錄了「不改的理由」時才算，這也是為什麼這裡的關係人條目都綁在某個具體的反轉上，而不是綁在一場會議上。\n\n團隊檔案看不見什麼。用了但沒寫下來的手法是隱形的，所以這裡每一個計數都是「有記錄的做法」的計數，不是「做法」的計數。訓練了老師卻沒寫出來的隊伍不會被算到；任何被團隊認為太平常而沒記錄的外借、捐贈或機構存放也一樣。這個誤差是單向的：罕見程度的數字是罕見程度的上界，真實數字只會更高。檔案也無法證明某個放大器真的奏效——30 位受訓教師是投入，而這個場上沒有任何隊伍回頭追蹤，證明那些老師隔年真的在教。奧地利部會平台的存放與 Muenster 的外借套件，都按檔案所述呈現：前者從本次網路環境無法驗證，後者是設計完成而非已在運作。\n\n樣本只有獲獎隊伍。這 106 份檔案涵蓋的是獎項得主與入圍者，所以這裡沒有任何數字可當作 iGEM 2026 全體的基準率。當本段說「106 支隊伍中有 7 支訓練教師」，意思是 106 支獲獎隊伍中有 7 支——這些是全場最強、記錄最完整的方案，這讓那份稀少更顯眼，而不是更不顯眼。"},{"id":"proposals-six","tab":"proposals","order":20,"kicker":"The first sweep","kicker_zh":"第一輪掃描","title":"The first sweep: six broader candidates, and what the rules did to them","title_zh":"第一輪掃描：六個範圍較寬的候選，以及規則對它們做了什麼","lede":"These six were the opening sweep across the whole space rather than one theme, and they are kept for two reasons: the eligibility screen applied to them is reusable for any candidate, and the pattern it exposed is the useful part. Two of the six came through the White List untouched and both are measurement work in a white-listed chassis. That is what the rules leave open to this division.","lede_zh":"這六個是跨整個空間的第一輪掃描，而不是針對單一主題，保留它們有兩個理由：套用在它們身上的資格篩查對任何候選題目都能重複使用，而那次篩查暴露出來的模式才是有用的部分。六個之中有兩個原封不動通過白名單，而且兩個都是在白名單底盤上的量測工作。那就是規則留給這個組別的空間。","body":"**The optogenetics pair is a sequence, not a choice.** The first characterises the switch and the second uses it on a real field sample; running the second without the first repeats 2026's mistake of stacking an application on a device that was never shown to work. If only one season is available, the first is the stronger candidate, because it passes both gates on day one and because closing a gap in a twelve-paper literature is publishable on its own.\n\n**The medical pair is designed around a rule, not around a disease.** The fastest way to kill a high-school medical project is to touch patients, clinical samples or human tissue. Both candidates here keep the medical motivation and move the sample: one targets a DNA sequence in environmental water, the other a live culture of the causative organism obtained from a collection. Neither requires a single human participant. The eligibility verdicts for both are in the register on this page and should be settled before the biology is designed.\n\n**The new pair claims ground the 2026 field left empty.** Nobody among 106 decorated teams ran an inter-lab measurement ring, and GEMS holds the Best Measurement credential that makes the invitation credible. And no team put a synthetic-biology design-layer artefact against Taiwan's own signature industry, which the industry review identified as the island's structural gap.\n\n**The eligibility screen mattered more than the scoring did, which is the point.** The resistance-gene proposal is not permitted in the High School section at all, blocked independently by the environmental-sample rule and by the antimicrobial-resistance rule. The oral-pathogen proposal is gated on a written answer from iGEM about one organism's risk group. The field proposal loses its field: the assay plant must be white-listed and the spray work must happen in the lab. The process-water proposal cannot put its sensor on site. **Two of the six came through untouched, and both are optogenetics or measurement work in a white-listed chassis.** That is not a coincidence — it is what the rules leave open to this division.","body_zh":"**光遺傳學這一對是一個順序，不是一個二選一。**第一個把開關特性描述清楚，第二個把它用在真實田間樣本上；沒做第一個就做第二個，等於重演 2026 年那個錯誤——在一個從未被證明有效的裝置上疊應用。如果只有一季可用，第一個是較強的候選，因為它第一天就通過兩道關卡，而且在一個十二篇論文的領域裡補上缺口，本身就可以發表。\n\n**醫療這一對是圍繞規則設計的，不是圍繞疾病設計的。**終結一個高中醫療題目最快的方式，就是碰到病人、臨床檢體或人體組織。這裡兩個候選都保留醫療動機，把樣本移開：一個以環境水體中的 DNA 序列為標的，另一個以來自菌種保存中心的致病菌活體培養為標的。兩者都不需要任何一位人類受試者。兩者的資格判定都在本頁的檢查表裡，而且應該在設計生物學之前就先定案。\n\n**新題目這一對，佔的是 2026 年全體留空的地。**106 支得獎隊伍裡沒有任何一支跑過實驗室間量測環，而 GEMS 握有讓這份邀請具可信度的 Best Measurement 資格。也沒有任何一支隊伍，把一個合成生物學的設計層產出放到台灣自己的招牌產業旁邊——而產業回顧正是把那一點指認為這座島的結構性缺口。\n\n**資格篩查比評分更要緊，而這正是重點。**抗藥性基因那個提案在高中組根本不被允許，被環境樣本規則與抗藥性規則各自獨立擋住。口腔致病菌那個提案卡在 iGEM 對某一種菌風險群的書面回覆上。田間那個提案失去了它的田：試驗植物必須在白名單上，而噴灑工作必須在實驗室裡進行。製程水那個提案的感測器不能放到現場。**六個裡只有兩個原封不動通過，而且兩個都是在白名單底盤上的光遺傳學或量測工作。**那不是巧合——那就是規則留給這個組別的空間。","cards":[{"kicker":"Optogenetics 1 · the strongest candidate","kicker_zh":"光遺傳學 1 · 最強候選","title":"Characterise the green-light switch itself, in absolute units, and publish the OFF state","title_zh":"把綠光開關本身特性描述清楚，用絕對單位，並且發表它的關閉態","body":"**The claim.** Green light switches ACC deaminase production on and off in *B. subtilis* WB800, and here is the dose-response, the OFF state, and how much it varies between plates.\n\n**Why this one.** The entire ReLEAF line rests on a switch the team's own 2026 pages do not evidence: the ELISA showed no change over time, the AmilCP reporter never coloured, and every biological result came from a constitutive bypass rather than the light-gated device. The team named two candidate explanations — well-to-well crosstalk in the light plate apparatus, and red LEDs near 640 nm when CcaSR needs about 672 nm to switch off — and tested neither. In a literature of twelve papers in all of PubMed, closing that gap is a publishable contribution on its own.\n\n**Gate 1, real target by week six:** the switch, in the team's own cells, on day one. **Gate 2, readout on an instrument already owned:** OD600, the reporter, ELISA for ACC deaminase, and the light plate apparatus GEMS built. Both gates pass more cleanly than any other candidate here.\n\n**The model, and this is the Best Model play.** In 2026 the control architecture rested on a published Hill transfer function assumed valid at 20 L, while every induction ran at a single light intensity — modelled rather than measured, by the report's own loop-closure test. Fit the Hill curve to your own dose-response across intensities and wavelengths, and hold back whole intensity levels, not scattered points, so the validation is honest.\n\n**The arm that could break it.** An apparent light response that is really temperature, growth phase or crosstalk. Run dark controls on the same plate at the same time, log temperature per well, map crosstalk by measuring each well with neighbours on and off, and run 672 nm against 640 nm as a named comparison.\n\n**Reach and durability.** Prof. Huang Chieh-Chen at National Chung Hsing University supplied WB800 and is already named; NTHU Taiwan runs engineered *B. subtilis* on the same island. Deposit a characterised part, publish the measurement protocol in absolute units, and publish the light plate geometry file — 9 of 20 award-winning 2026 instruments published none.","body_zh":"**主張。**綠光能讓 *B. subtilis* WB800 開啟與關閉 ACC deaminase 的生產，而這是它的劑量反應、關閉態，以及盤與盤之間的變異量。\n\n**為什麼是它。**整條 ReLEAF 路線建立在一個「團隊自己 2026 年頁面並未證實」的開關上：ELISA 顯示隨時間沒有變化、AmilCP 報告基因從未顯色，而每一個生物學結果都來自組成型旁路，不是光控裝置。團隊點出兩個可能解釋——光照盤裝置的孔間串擾，以及紅光 LED 約 640 nm 而 CcaSR 需要約 672 nm 才會關閉——兩個都沒測。在一個整個 PubMed 只有十二篇論文的領域裡，補上這個缺口本身就是可發表的貢獻。\n\n**關卡一，第六週前拿到真實標的：**開關本身，在團隊自己的細胞裡，第一天就有。**關卡二，讀值做在已有的儀器上：**OD600、報告基因、ACC deaminase 的 ELISA，以及 GEMS 自己做的光照盤裝置。兩道關卡都比這裡任何其他候選過得更乾淨。\n\n**模型，而這就是 Best Model 的著力點。**2026 年整套控制架構建立在一條「假設在 20 L 仍成立」的已發表 Hill 轉移函數上，而每一次誘導都只在單一光強度下進行——依本報告自己的迴路閉合檢驗，那是被建模而不是被量測。把 Hill 曲線擬合到你們自己跨強度、跨波長的劑量反應上，而且要整個強度層級地留存，不是零散地留幾個點，這樣驗證才誠實。\n\n**那個可能推翻它的實驗組。**一個看起來像光反應、實際上是溫度、生長期或串擾造成的結果。在同一塊盤、同一時間跑暗對照；逐孔記錄溫度；把鄰孔開與關分別量一次來畫出串擾圖；並把 672 nm 對 640 nm 當成具名的比較組來跑。\n\n**觸及範圍與耐久度。**中興大學黃介辰教授提供了 WB800，而且已經具名；清華大學的 NTHU Taiwan 隊在同一座島上就養著工程化的 *B. subtilis*。存進一個特性描述完整的元件、以絕對單位發表量測流程，並且發表光照盤的幾何檔案——2026 年 20 件得獎儀器裡有 9 件完全沒有發表幾何檔案。","chips":["both gates pass cleanly","the Best Model play","12-paper literature"],"chips_zh":["兩道關卡都乾淨通過","Best Model 的著力點","只有十二篇論文的領域"]},{"kicker":"Optogenetics 2 · closes the 2026 gap","kicker_zh":"光遺傳學 2 · 補上 2026 的缺口","title":"Assay the preparation that actually reaches the plant, on plants in real field soil","title_zh":"檢測真正噴到植物上的那份製備，而且用真實田土裡的植物","body":"**The claim.** A measured dose of ACC deaminase rescues stressed rice in soil from a named field, and here is the dose that was actually delivered.\n\n**Why this one.** 2026's strongest result — a plant rescue at p < 0.0001 with 40 seedlings a condition — sits on a preparation that was never assayed. That is precisely the gate-one failure this report found separating the podium from the rest: seven of seven non-podium High School teams stopped at a surrogate. The fix is not a new project; it is finishing this one.\n\n**Gate 1:** the real target is the spray preparation itself plus stressed plants in soil from the cooperative's field, and the relationship already exists — the team interviewed Mr. Chen Ke-Wei of the Lanyang River Friendly Farming Production Cooperative in 2026. **Gate 2:** ACC deaminase activity assay, ELISA and plant phenotype, all on instruments already owned.\n\n**The model.** Fit plant rescue against *measured* enzyme activity rather than nominal dose — that single change converts an assumed delivery into a measured one. Hold back a whole stress level or a whole field block.\n\n**The arm that could break it.** The rescue comes from something else in the preparation. Run a spent-medium-only arm, a heat-inactivated-enzyme arm and a buffer-only arm. Athens wrote the type specimen for naming this honestly: \"Separating the two requires that buffer-only arm, and until it is run we describe the effect as attributable to the preparation.\"\n\n**The constraint the team already found, and must keep saying.** A farmer at a 2026 forum asked whether the system breaks organic certification; the team researched the regulations and concluded **it cannot be used on organic farms**, then interviewed the cooperative to work out what that means commercially. That is an honest market cap and it belongs on the landing page, not in a footnote.\n\n**Reach.** The multiplier is agricultural extension: the district agricultural research and extension stations employ people whose job is to repeat advice to growers for years. Train the extension officers, not the growers.\n\n**Two rule constraints that change how this is built.** First, the White List names only *Physcomitrella patens*, *Arabidopsis* spp. and *Nicotiana* spp. as permitted multicellular plants; everything else is \"Other multicellular organisms\", which is Check-In work a high school team cannot file. GEMS's 2026 stress index was fitted to twenty-five years of Taiwanese county **rice** yields, so if the 2027 assay plant is rice, the assay is not available in this division — the model can still be about rice while the plant on the bench is a white-listed species, and the wiki should say so. Second, nothing engineered and no product of anything engineered may leave the lab without permission GEMS cannot obtain, so the spray assay happens **in the lab on bulk field soil brought in**, not in the field. Using the soil as-is is explicitly permitted; isolating anything from it is not.","body_zh":"**主張。**一個**被量到的** ACC deaminase 劑量，能讓長在具名田區土壤裡的逆境水稻恢復，而這就是真正送達的那個劑量。\n\n**為什麼是它。**2026 年最強的結果——每組 40 棵苗、p < 0.0001 的植物救援——建立在一份從未被檢測活性的製備上。那正是本報告找到的、把頒獎臺和其他人分開的那個關卡一失誤：七支沒上頒獎臺的高中隊伍，七支全部停在替代物上。解法不是一個新專案，而是把這一個做完。\n\n**關卡一：**真實標的就是噴劑製備本身，加上長在合作社田區土壤裡的逆境植物，而且關係已經存在——團隊在 2026 年訪談過蘭陽溪友善耕作生產合作社的陳科緯先生。**關卡二：**ACC deaminase 活性測定、ELISA 與植物表型，全部做在已經有的儀器上。\n\n**模型。**把植物救援對**實測的**酵素活性作擬合，而不是對名目劑量——光是這一個改變，就把「假設的送達」變成「量到的送達」。整個逆境層級或整個田區區塊地留存起來不用。\n\n**那個可能推翻它的實驗組。**救援其實來自製備裡的別的東西。跑一組只有用過培養基的、一組熱去活化酵素的、一組只有緩衝液的。Athens 寫出了誠實指名這件事的範本：「要把這兩者分開需要那一組只有緩衝液的對照，在它被做出來之前，我們把這個效應描述為可歸因於該製備。」\n\n**團隊已經找到、而且必須繼續講的那個限制。**2026 年一場論壇上，一位農民問這套系統會不會破壞有機認證；團隊去查了法規，結論是**它不能用在有機農場**，接著訪談合作社釐清這在商業上代表什麼。那是一個誠實的市場上限，它該出現在首頁，不是藏在註腳裡。\n\n**觸及範圍。**放大器是農業推廣：各區農業改良場僱用的人，工作就是年復一年把建議重複給農民聽。訓練推廣人員，不是訓練農民。\n\n**兩條會改變做法的規則限制。**第一，白名單上允許的多細胞植物只有 *Physcomitrella patens*、*Arabidopsis* spp. 與 *Nicotiana* spp.；其餘一律屬於「其他多細胞生物」，那是高中組隊伍無法提交的 Check-In 工作。GEMS 2026 年的逆境指數，是擬合到台灣各縣市二十五年的**水稻**產量上的，所以如果 2027 年的試驗植物是水稻，這個試驗在這個組別就做不成——模型仍然可以是關於水稻的，而實驗檯上那株是白名單物種，而且 wiki 應該把這件事寫出來。第二，任何工程化生物及其產物，都不得在沒有 GEMS 拿不到的許可下離開實驗室，所以噴灑試驗要**在實驗室裡、用搬進來的團體田土**進行，不是在田裡。照原樣使用那些土是明文允許的；從中分離任何東西則不允許。","chips":["fixes the 2026 gate-1 failure","white-listed plants only, not rice","in the lab, on soil brought in"],"chips_zh":["補上 2026 年關卡一的失誤","只能用白名單植物，不是水稻","在實驗室裡，用搬進來的土"]},{"kicker":"Medical 1 · blocked as designed, re-scoped","kicker_zh":"醫療 1 · 原設計不可行，已改寫","title":"The resistance-gene idea is not permitted in the High School section, and here is what survives","title_zh":"抗藥性基因那個構想在高中組不被允許，而這是還活得下來的版本","body":"**This one was killed by the rules, not by the science, and it was killed twice.** The original design was to detect antimicrobial-resistance genes in water from the cooperative's channel. Two independent White List triggers block it, and a high school team has no Check-In route to clear either.\n\nFirst, the environmental-sample rule: *\"Isolation and sequencing of nucleic acids from environmental samples also require the submission of a Check In Form.\"* Reading resistance genes out of river water is exactly that. Second, the activities column lists *\"Experiments making use of antimicrobial resistance factors not in common use in the host institution\"* as Check-In work in its own right. Either one ends it.\n\n**What survives, and it is a real project.** Keep the medical motivation, drop the metagenomics: build the sensor for an analyte you can buy as a standard, and characterise it on that standard and on a bulk matrix used as-is without isolating anything from it — which the same policy permits: *\"As long as parts or organisms are not isolated from them, samples from the environment, the food industry, or other non-traditional suppliers may be used in your experiments.\"*\n\n**Then say exactly where the chain breaks**, which is the habit this report found separating the podium: the real molecule is reachable, the real clinical sample is not, and the rule that forbids it should be quoted on the wiki rather than left as a silence. A project that names its own ceiling reads as rigour; the same project with the ceiling unmentioned reads as an over-claim, and GEMS is already joint-worst in the Top 10 on that measure.","body_zh":"**這一個是被規則殺掉的，不是被科學殺掉的，而且被殺了兩次。**原本的設計是偵測合作社水道裡的抗藥性基因。有兩條互相獨立的白名單觸發條件擋住它，而高中組隊伍沒有任何 Check-In 管道可以過關。\n\n第一，環境樣本規則：*「從環境樣本中分離與定序核酸，同樣需要提交 Check In Form。」*從河水裡讀出抗藥性基因，正是這件事。第二，活動欄本身就把*「使用該機構並非常規使用之抗藥性因子的實驗」*列為需要 Check-In 的工作。任何一條都足以終結它。\n\n**還活得下來的版本，而且它是個真專案。**保留醫療動機，拿掉總體基因體學：把感測器做給一個你買得到標準品的分析物，並且在那個標準品、以及一個「照原樣使用、不從中分離任何東西」的團體基質上做特性描述——而同一條政策正好允許這件事：*「只要沒有從中分離出零件或生物，來自環境、食品工業或其他非傳統供應者的樣本，都可以用在你的實驗裡。」*\n\n**然後把鏈條斷在哪裡講清楚**，那正是本報告找到的、把頒獎臺分出來的那個習慣：真實的分子拿得到，真實的臨床檢體拿不到，而禁止它的那條規則應該被引在 wiki 上，而不是留成一片沉默。一個指名自己上限的專案讀起來是嚴謹；同一個專案如果不提那個上限，讀起來就是誇大——而 GEMS 在這一項已經是 Top 10 裡並列最差。","chips":["blocked twice over","no Check-In route in High School","the re-scope is still a project"],"chips_zh":["兩條規則各自擋住","高中組沒有 Check-In 管道","改寫後仍然是個專案"]},{"kicker":"Medical 2 · eligibility decides it","kicker_zh":"醫療 2 · 由資格決定","title":"A live oral-pathogen biofilm as the real target, with no human sample anywhere","title_zh":"以活的口腔致病菌生物膜為真實標的，全程不碰任何人體檢體","body":"**The claim.** A peptide expressed from a whitelist chassis reduces biofilm formation by the actual caries organism in vitro, at this dose, with this effect size.\n\n**Why this shape.** This is the 2024 Grand Prize structure transplanted onto a health problem. In 2024 the real target was live *Aedes albopictus* larvae — the vector itself, not a surrogate — with LC50 reported for all three toxins and 98 dead larvae examined microscopically. Here the real target is a live biofilm of the organism that actually causes the disease, grown in the lab. **No patients, no saliva, no plaque, no human tissue, no clinical claim.** Childhood caries is a genuine and well-documented problem in Taiwan, so the medical motivation is real without the project ever entering a clinic.\n\n**Gate 1:** a live biofilm of the target organism, obtained from a culture collection rather than from a person — so the gate depends on a strain source and an eligibility verdict, not on recruiting anybody. **Gate 2:** biofilm quantification and growth curves on plate readers GEMS already owns.\n\n**The model.** Dose-response of biofilm inhibition with held-back concentrations, and an effect size with an interval rather than a bare p-value.\n\n**The arm that could break it.** The inhibition comes from the chassis or the medium rather than the peptide. Run an empty-vector arm, a heat-inactivated-peptide arm and a spent-medium arm — GEMS already scores a perfect five of five on exactly this habit, so it is cheap here.\n\n**Reach.** School nurses and dental hygienists repeat the lesson professionally, which is the HongKong-JSS shape. **The eligibility question is the whole risk, and the rules make it sharper than I first wrote it.** Only Risk Group 1 organisms are white-listed; anything needing enhanced containment is Check-In, and **a high school team has no Check-In route at all** — *\"Work that would require a Check In is not permitted in the High School section.\"* So if the target organism is Risk Group 2 under the sources iGEM names, this project does not exist for GEMS, full stop. A second gate sits behind it: *\"Any organisms obtained from outside the lab or from non-traditional / non-institutional suppliers\"* also require a Check-In, so the strain's provenance matters as much as its risk group. **Do not design a season around this until safety@igem.org has answered in writing.** The fallback, if the answer is no, is to run the same assay against a Risk Group 1 indicator organism and state plainly that the real pathogen was out of reach under the rules — which is a chain-break worth publishing, not a defeat worth hiding.","body_zh":"**主張。**一個由白名單底盤表現出來的胜肽，在體外能降低真正造成齲齒的那種菌所形成的生物膜，在這個劑量下、有這麼大的效應量。\n\n**為什麼是這個形狀。**這是把 2024 年總冠軍的結構，移植到一個健康問題上。2024 年的真實標的是活的 *Aedes albopictus* 幼蟲——病媒本身，不是替代物——三種毒蛋白都報告了 LC50，並以顯微鏡檢視 98 隻死亡幼蟲。這裡的真實標的，是真正造成該疾病的那種菌在實驗室裡長出來的活生物膜。**不碰病人、不採唾液、不取牙菌斑、不碰人體組織、不做臨床主張。**兒童齲齒在台灣是真實且有完整記載的問題，所以醫療動機是真的，而專案全程不必踏進診間。\n\n**關卡一：**標的菌的活生物膜，來源是菌種保存中心而不是人——所以關卡取決於菌株來源與資格判定，而不是取決於招募任何人。**關卡二：**生物膜定量與生長曲線，做在 GEMS 已經有的盤式讀取儀上。\n\n**模型。**生物膜抑制的劑量反應，並留存部分濃度不用；效應量要附區間，而不是只給一個裸的 p 值。\n\n**那個可能推翻它的實驗組。**抑制其實來自底盤或培養基，而不是胜肽。跑空載體組、熱去活化胜肽組與用過培養基組——GEMS 在這個習慣上已經是滿分五類全有，所以在這裡很便宜。\n\n**觸及範圍。**學校護理師與牙科衛生師會以職業身分重複這堂課，這正是 HongKong-JSS 的形狀。**資格問題就是全部的風險，而規則讓它比我原本寫的更尖銳。**白名單上只有風險群 1 的生物；任何需要加強圍堵的都要 Check-In，而**高中組隊伍根本沒有 Check-In 管道**——*「需要 Check In 的工作，在高中組不被允許。」*所以如果標的菌在 iGEM 指名的那些來源裡屬於風險群 2，這個專案對 GEMS 就不存在，沒有轉圜。它後面還有第二道關卡：*「任何取自實驗室外、或取自非傳統／非機構供應者的生物」*同樣需要 Check-In，所以菌株的來源和它的風險群一樣重要。**在 safety@igem.org 書面回覆之前，不要圍繞這個題目設計一整季。**如果答案是否定的，退路是把同一套試驗改用風險群 1 的指示菌來做，並且明白寫出真正的病原在規則下拿不到——那是一個值得發表的鏈條斷點，不是一個該藏起來的挫敗。","chips":["RG1 only, no Check-In route","strain provenance is a second gate","get it in writing first"],"chips_zh":["只能風險群 1，沒有 Check-In","菌株來源是第二道關卡","先拿到書面回覆"]},{"kicker":"New 1 · genuinely unclaimed ground","kicker_zh":"新題目 1 · 真正沒人佔的地","title":"The inter-lab measurement ring nobody in 106 teams ran","title_zh":"106 支隊伍裡沒有任何一支跑過的實驗室間量測環","body":"**The claim.** The same light-inducible part, measured in N labs to one protocol in absolute units, varies by this much — and here is how much of that is the lab, the plate and the instrument.\n\n**Why this one.** Across all 106 decorated teams of 2026 there was not one inter-lab measurement ring. The whole category of collaboration that produces a reusable result went unclaimed, in a competition about measurement, while the single team that publicly offered real shared work got zero replies. GEMS holds the 2026 High School Best Measurement award, which is the credential that makes an invitation credible.\n\n**Gate 1:** the real target is the between-lab variance itself, which exists as soon as two labs run the protocol — but it has to be set up in week one, because the gate here is partner commitment rather than sample access. **Gate 2:** OD600 and a reporter, with a shared calibrant, on instruments GEMS already owns and has already won an award for.\n\n**The model, and this is why it is a Best Model candidate.** The model *is* the result: a variance-components fit separating between-lab, between-plate and within-plate contributions, with one whole lab held out to test whether the model predicts a site it never saw. That is the loop-closure habit measured at 53% against 23%, in its purest form.\n\n**The arm that could break it.** The apparent between-lab differences are really instrument differences. Ship a shared calibrant, fix the protocol, collect instrument metadata, and report the null honestly if the labs agree — a ring that finds no difference is still the first ring.\n\n**Reach and risk.** Every participating team is a multiplier and the protocol outlives all of them. The risk is coordination: the result depends on other teams delivering on time, so recruit more labs than you need and publish who did not return data, the way DTU named the turbine makers who never replied.\n\n**Where this one came from, and the rule it has to clear.** This is not a new idea on this page: it is already an entry in the Science for Good pipeline, listed there as \"the shared measurement standard nobody built\" and marked as passing all four admission criteria on paper but **untested against a real person**. By the pipeline's own governance rule, an entry that comes from this report rather than from a person holds its slot on probation and must find somebody outside GEMS who will say they want it, in their own words, or it exits. That rule applies here too — and the coordination risk makes it sharper, because GEMS currently has no collaboration page and appears on no other team's.","body_zh":"**主張。**同一個光誘導元件，在 N 個實驗室依同一套流程、以絕對單位量測，變異有這麼大——而其中有多少來自實驗室、多少來自盤、多少來自儀器，在這裡。\n\n**為什麼是它。**2026 年全部 106 支得獎隊伍裡，沒有任何一支跑過實驗室間量測環。在一個以量測為名的競賽裡，整個「能產出可重複使用結果」的合作類別無人認領；而唯一公開提出真正共享工作的隊伍，收到零個回覆。GEMS 握有 2026 年高中組 Best Measurement，那正是讓一份邀請具有可信度的資格。\n\n**關卡一：**真實標的就是實驗室間變異本身，只要有兩個實驗室跑這套流程它就存在——但必須在第一週就架好，因為這裡的關卡是夥伴的承諾，不是樣本取得。**關卡二：**OD600 與報告基因，搭配共用校正品，做在 GEMS 已經有、而且已經靠它拿過獎的儀器上。\n\n**模型，而這正是它成為 Best Model 候選的原因。**模型**就是**結果：一個變異成分模型，把實驗室間、盤間與盤內的貢獻拆開，並留出整整一個實驗室，用來檢驗模型能不能預測一個它從沒見過的場址。那就是被量到 53% 對 23% 的迴路閉合習慣，而且是最純粹的形式。\n\n**那個可能推翻它的實驗組。**看起來的實驗室間差異，其實是儀器差異。寄出共用校正品、固定流程、收集儀器中繼資料，而且如果各實驗室其實一致，就誠實報告這個虛無結果——一個發現沒有差異的環，仍然是第一個環。\n\n**觸及範圍與風險。**每一個參與的隊伍都是放大器，而流程比它們全部都活得久。風險在協調：結果取決於別的隊伍準時交件，所以招募的實驗室要多於你需要的數量，並且公開誰沒有回傳資料——就像 DTU 把從未回覆的渦輪機製造商一一點名那樣。\n\n**這一個是從哪裡來的，以及它必須過的那條規則。**這不是本頁才出現的新想法：它已經是科學向善清單上的一個條目，在那裡被列為「沒有人建立的共用量測標準」，並註明四項入列條件在紙面上全部通過，但**從未對著一個真實的人檢驗過**。依該清單自己的治理規則，一個來自本報告而不是來自某個人的條目，只能以觀察期的身分佔住名額，而且必須找到一位 GEMS 以外的人，用他自己的話說他要這個，否則就退場。這條規則在這裡同樣適用——而協調風險讓它更尖銳，因為 GEMS 目前沒有合作頁面，也沒有出現在任何其他隊伍的頁面上。","chips":["0 of 106 ran one","already a pipeline entry, on probation","GEMS has no collaboration page"],"chips_zh":["106 支中 0 支跑過","已在清單上，觀察期中","GEMS 沒有合作頁面"]},{"kicker":"New 2 · Taiwan's signature industry","kicker_zh":"新題目 2 · 台灣的招牌產業","title":"A biosensor for one defined contaminant in Hsinchu process water, with real samples","title_zh":"針對新竹製程水中一種特定污染物的生物感測器，而且用真實水樣","body":"**The claim.** This sensor reports this contaminant at these concentrations in water from a real industrial process stream, with a limit of detection measured in that matrix rather than in buffer.\n\n**Why this one.** The industry review found that China holds about 70% of world fermentation capacity while Taiwan's state-backed biomanufacturing push is a contract-development play **with no visible synthetic-biology design layer** — Singapore and Israel are funding exactly that layer. A school team cannot out-build a contract manufacturer and gains nothing by miniaturising one. What it can do is put a design-layer artefact against the island's actual industry: a characterised sensing part, calibrated in absolute units, for a contaminant that a Hsinchu process stream really contains.\n\n**Gate 1 — and this is the honest risk.** Industrial sample access is harder than a farm. A water-treatment operator can hand over a sample in an afternoon, but only if the relationship exists; a company may also not want its effluent characterised by a school team. Name the route and the person before choosing this topic, and have a fallback stream. **Gate 2:** a colorimetric or fluorescent readout on plate readers already owned.\n\n**The model.** Calibration in the real matrix, inverse calibration, a computed limit of detection, and whole batches held back. The 2026 field gives a direct template: one team built a calibration curve per medium in micromolar fluoride and re-zeroed on that plate's own negative control.\n\n**The arm that could break it.** Matrix effects — the process water suppresses or mimics the signal. Spiked recovery in the real matrix, a matrix-only arm, and a buffer comparison published side by side.\n\n**Reach.** Water-treatment operators and environmental inspectors are professional repeaters, and Hsinchu is close enough for repeat visits. **Say what it is not:** a sensor is detection, not remediation, and the landing page must not promise cleanup the results page does not show.\n\n**One rule to build around.** The sensor cannot go to the plant: bringing a product of a genetically modified organism outside the lab requires permission a high school team cannot obtain. So the water comes to the lab, not the sensor to the water, and the wiki should say that plainly instead of implying an on-site device. Using the water as-is is permitted; isolating anything from it is not. Check separately that the target contaminant is not a controlled chemical, which is its own Check-In trigger.","body_zh":"**主張。**這個感測器在真實工業製程水流中，以這些濃度回報這種污染物，而偵測極限是在那個基質裡量出來的，不是在緩衝液裡。\n\n**為什麼是它。**產業回顧發現：中國掌握全球約 70% 的發酵量能，而台灣由國家主導的生物製造布局是一場代工開發的局，**看不到合成生物學的設計層**——新加坡與以色列補助的正好就是那一層。學校隊伍蓋不過代工廠，把它縮小一號也得不到任何東西。它能做的，是把一個設計層的產出放到這座島真實的產業旁邊：一個特性描述完整、以絕對單位校正過的感測元件，針對新竹某個製程水流裡真的含有的污染物。\n\n**關卡一——而這就是誠實的風險所在。**工業樣本的取得比農場難。一位水處理操作員一個下午就能給你一份樣本，但前提是關係已經存在；而且公司也可能不希望自己的放流水被一支學校隊伍做特性分析。在選這個題目之前先把路徑和人指名出來，並準備一個備援水流。**關卡二：**顯色或螢光讀值，做在已經有的盤式讀取儀上。\n\n**模型。**在真實基質中做校正、反向校正、算出偵測極限，並整批整批地留存。2026 年的全體資料給了一個直接的範本：有一支隊伍為每一種培養基各建一條以微莫耳濃度氟離子為單位的檢量線，並以該盤自己的陰性對照重新歸零。\n\n**那個可能推翻它的實驗組。**基質效應——製程水抑制或模擬了訊號。在真實基質中做加標回收、跑一組只有基質的對照，並把緩衝液的比較並排公開。\n\n**觸及範圍。**水處理操作員與環境稽查人員都是會重複的職業角色，而新竹近到可以重複拜訪。**也要講清楚它不是什麼：**感測器是偵測，不是整治；首頁不可以承諾結果頁沒有呈現的清除效果。\n\n**有一條規則要繞著它設計。**感測器不能送到廠裡：把基因改造生物的產物帶出實驗室，需要高中組隊伍拿不到的許可。所以是水送到實驗室，不是感測器送到水邊，而 wiki 應該把這點直說，而不是暗示那是一台現場裝置。照原樣使用那些水是允許的；從中分離任何東西則不允許。另外要分開確認：標的污染物不是受管制化學品，那本身是另一條 Check-In 觸發條件。","chips":["design layer against real industry","water comes to the lab, not the reverse","check it is not a controlled chemical"],"chips_zh":["把設計層放到真實產業旁","是水送進實驗室，不是反過來","確認它不是受管制化學品"]}],"table":{"head":["Proposal","Real target, in hand by week 6?","The model, and what is held back","Multiplying audience","Special prizes to enter","Verdict"],"head_zh":["提案","真實標的，第六週前在手上嗎？","模型，以及留存什麼","會放大的對象","該投的特別獎","判斷"],"rows":[["**O1 · Characterise the green-light switch**","**Yes, day one.** The switch in the team's own cells","Hill transfer function fitted to own dose-response across intensities and wavelengths; hold back whole intensity levels","Other iGEM teams via a shippable part and protocol; in-service biology teachers","**Best Model**, Best Measurement, Best New Basic Part, Best Part Collection","**Strongest, and now confirmed clean.** *B. subtilis* is named on the White List, the parts are Registry parts and nothing leaves the lab. No Check-In needed anywhere"],["**O2 · Assay what actually reaches the plant**","**Yes.** Spray preparation plus field soil; Mr. Chen Ke-Wei already interviewed","Rescue fitted against measured enzyme activity, not nominal dose; hold back a stress level or a field block","Agricultural extension officers at the district stations","**Best Model**, Best Measurement, Best IHP, Best Sustainable Development Impact, Best Education","**Strong, but re-scoped by the rules.** The assay plant must be *Arabidopsis* or *Nicotiana*, not rice, and the spray work happens in the lab on soil brought in"],["**M1 · Medical sensing, metagenomics dropped**","Yes for a purchased standard and a bulk matrix; **no** for any clinical or sequenced sample","Calibration per matrix, inverse calibration, computed limit of detection; hold back batches","Water-quality inspectors and extension officers","Best Measurement, Best Part Collection, Best Software, Diagnostics village","**Not permitted as designed.** Blocked twice: nucleic-acid isolation from environmental samples, and antimicrobial-resistance work. The re-scoped version drops the metagenomics and states the chain break"],["**M2 · Live oral-pathogen biofilm**","Depends on a strain source and an **eligibility verdict**, not on recruiting anyone","Dose-response of biofilm inhibition with held-back concentrations; effect size with an interval","School nurses and dental hygienists","**Best Model**, Best New Basic Part, Best Education, Therapeutics or Diagnostics village","**Gated on a written answer.** Risk Group 1 only and no Check-In route, so if the organism is RG2 the project does not exist. Strain provenance is a second gate. Ask safety@igem.org before designing"],["**N1 · The inter-lab measurement ring**","**Yes, if set up in week one.** The gate is partner commitment, not sample access","Variance components separating lab, plate and instrument; hold out a whole lab","Every participating team, and the protocol outlives them all","**Best Model**, Best Measurement, Best Part Collection, Best Software, Best Education","**Highest novelty, and the rules bless the mechanism.** Shipping an engineered organism between labs for research or teaching is explicitly not release. Still a pipeline entry on probation"],["**N2 · Hsinchu process-water biosensor**","**The honest risk.** Industrial access is harder than a farm; name the operator first","Calibration in the real matrix, inverse calibration, computed limit of detection; hold back batches","Water-treatment operators and environmental inspectors","Best Measurement, Best Part Collection, Best Sustainable Development Impact, Bioremediation village","**High upside, access-gated, lab-only.** The water comes to the lab, not the sensor to the water. Secure the sample route, and check the contaminant is not a controlled chemical"]],"rows_zh":[["**O1 · 把綠光開關特性描述清楚**","**是，第一天。**開關就在團隊自己的細胞裡","把 Hill 轉移函數擬合到自己跨強度、跨波長的劑量反應；整個強度層級地留存","透過可寄送的元件與流程觸及其他 iGEM 隊伍；以及在職生物教師","**Best Model**、Best Measurement、Best New Basic Part、Best Part Collection","**最強，而且現在確認資格乾淨。***B. subtilis* 明列於白名單上，元件是 Registry 元件，而且沒有任何東西離開實驗室。全程不需要任何 Check-In"],["**O2 · 檢測真正送到植物上的東西**","**是。**噴劑製備加田間土壤；已訪談過陳科緯先生","把救援效果對實測酵素活性擬合，而不是對名目劑量；整個逆境層級或整個田區區塊地留存","各區農業改良場的推廣人員","**Best Model**、Best Measurement、Best IHP、Best Sustainable Development Impact、Best Education","**強，但被規則改寫了範圍。**試驗植物必須是 *Arabidopsis* 或 *Nicotiana*，不是水稻，而噴灑工作要在實驗室裡、用搬進來的土進行"],["**M1 · 醫療感測，拿掉總體基因體學**","買得到的標準品與團體基質可以；任何臨床或需定序的樣本**不行**","每種基質各建檢量線、反向校正、算出偵測極限；整批留存","水質稽查人員與農業推廣人員","Best Measurement、Best Part Collection、Best Software、Diagnostics village","**原設計不被允許。**被兩條規則擋住：從環境樣本分離核酸，以及抗藥性相關工作。改寫版拿掉總體基因體學，並把鏈條斷點寫出來"],["**M2 · 活的口腔致病菌生物膜**","取決於菌株來源與**資格判定**，不取決於招募任何人","生物膜抑制的劑量反應並留存部分濃度；效應量附區間","學校護理師與牙科衛生師","**Best Model**、Best New Basic Part、Best Education、Therapeutics 或 Diagnostics village","**卡在一份書面回覆上。**只能用風險群 1 而且沒有 Check-In 管道，所以如果該菌屬於風險群 2，這個專案就不存在。菌株來源是第二道關卡。設計之前先問 safety@igem.org"],["**N1 · 實驗室間量測環**","**是，前提是第一週就架好。**關卡是夥伴承諾，不是樣本取得","變異成分模型拆開實驗室、盤與儀器；留出整整一個實驗室","每一支參與的隊伍，而流程比它們都活得久","**Best Model**、Best Measurement、Best Part Collection、Best Software、Best Education","**新穎度最高，而且規則正好為這個機制背書。**為研究或教學在實驗室之間運送工程化生物，明文不算釋出。但它仍是清單上觀察期中的條目"],["**N2 · 新竹製程水生物感測器**","**誠實的風險。**工業取得比農場難；先把操作員指名出來","在真實基質中校正、反向校正、算出偵測極限；整批留存","水處理操作員與環境稽查人員","Best Measurement、Best Part Collection、Best Sustainable Development Impact、Bioremediation village","**上檔大，卡在取得管道，而且只能在實驗室。**是水送進實驗室，不是感測器送到水邊。先確保樣本路徑，並確認污染物不是受管制化學品"]]},"checklist":["If only one season is available, run O1. It passes both gates on day one, it closes the gap the entire ReLEAF line rests on, and the literature it contributes to is twelve papers deep.","Do not run O2 before O1. Using the switch on a real field sample before showing the switch works repeats the 2026 mistake exactly.","Settle both medical eligibility verdicts before designing any biology. A rule discovered in June costs a season; the same rule discovered in November costs an afternoon.","Answer M1's readout question before choosing it. A nucleic-acid readout is a new capability for this team, and by this instrument's own rules that is a gate, not a detail.","For N1, recruit more labs than you need and publish who did not return data. The result survives a partner dropping out; it does not survive pretending they did not.","For N2, name the water-treatment operator and the fallback stream before committing. Industrial sample access is the one gate a relationship cannot be improvised into.","Whichever wins, decide in week one what model will be fitted and which rows are held back, because that is the Best Model play and Best Model is the category that maps onto the finalist slate.","Whichever wins, deposit a characterised part and publish one Traditional Chinese artefact with an explicit reuse licence. GEMS won a parts award in 2024 and entered none in 2026.","Write the landing-page sentence last, from the results page. GEMS is joint-worst in the 2026 Top 10 on the gap between what a home page claims and what its own evidence shows."],"checklist_zh":["如果只有一季可用，就做 O1。它第一天就通過兩道關卡，它補上整條 ReLEAF 路線所依賴的那個缺口，而它要貢獻的那個領域只有十二篇文獻。","不要在 O1 之前做 O2。在證明開關有效之前就把它用在真實田間樣本上，等於原封不動重演 2026 年的錯誤。","在設計任何生物學之前，先把兩個醫療提案的資格判定定案。六月才發現的規則要付一整季；十一月發現同一條規則，只要一個下午。","選 M1 之前先把讀值那一題回答掉。核酸讀值對這支隊伍是一項新能力，而依這套工具自己的規則，那是關卡，不是細節。","做 N1 要超額招募實驗室，並且公開誰沒有回傳資料。結果撐得住一個夥伴退出；撐不住假裝他沒退出。","做 N2 之前，先把水處理操作員和備援水流指名出來。工業樣本取得，是唯一一道沒辦法臨時用關係補上的關卡。","不管哪一個雀屏中選，都要在第一週就決定要擬合什麼模型、哪些資料列留存不用，因為那就是 Best Model 的著力點，而 Best Model 是那個疊合決賽名單的類別。","不管哪一個雀屏中選，都要存進一個特性描述完整的元件，並發表一份附明確可重用授權的繁體中文產出。GEMS 在 2024 年拿過元件獎，2026 年一個都沒投。","不管哪一個雀屏中選，首頁那句話都要最後才寫，而且從結果頁往回寫。在 2026 年 Top 10 裡，GEMS 在「首頁主張與自身證據的落差」這一項是並列最差。"],"method":"These six are proposals, not measurements. What is measured is the reasoning behind each criterion, and every figure cited is measured elsewhere in this report with its own limits stated where it is reported: the real-target finding and the seven-of-seven surrogate count from judging-top10.json; the GEMS three-season record, the 640-against-672 nm wavelength question and the constitutive-bypass finding from gems-three-seasons.json, judging-three-teams.json and report.json; the 53-against-23 model-loop figure from the dry-lab analyses; the falsification-control counts from falsification-controls.json; the inter-lab-ring and escape-rate gaps from collaboration-network.json and safety-practice.json; the multiplier counts from picks-leverage.json; the special-prize co-occurrence from award-economics.json; and Taiwan's position in the design layer from trends/industry.json. GEMS's own assets -- CcaSR in Bacillus subtilis WB800 supplied by Prof. Huang Chieh-Chen, the light plate apparatus, the hollow-fibre perfusion bioreactor, the ELISA and OD600 capability, the 2026 awards, the interview with Mr. Chen Ke-Wei of the Lanyang River Friendly Farming Production Cooperative, and the organic-certification conclusion -- are all read from research/teams/6072.json. The eligibility verdicts are NOT settled here: they are in the register block on this page, and anything it marks unverified should be treated as unverified rather than as permission.","method_zh":"這六個是提案，不是量測。被量測的是每一條判準背後的推理，而所引用的每一個數字都量測於本報告其他處，並在該處載明自己的限制：真實標的發現與「七支全停在替代物」的計數來自 judging-top10.json；GEMS 三季紀錄、640 對 672 nm 的波長問題與組成型旁路的發現，來自 gems-three-seasons.json、judging-three-teams.json 與 report.json；53 對 23 的模型迴路數字來自乾實驗室相關分析；否證對照的計數來自 falsification-controls.json；實驗室間量測環與逃逸率的空白來自 collaboration-network.json 與 safety-practice.json；放大器的計數來自 picks-leverage.json；特別獎的同時發生率來自 award-economics.json；台灣在設計層的位置來自 trends/industry.json。GEMS 自己的資產——由黃介辰教授提供的 Bacillus subtilis WB800 中的 CcaSR、光照盤裝置、中空纖維灌流反應器、ELISA 與 OD600 能力、2026 年的獎項、與蘭陽溪友善耕作生產合作社陳科緯先生的訪談，以及有機認證的結論——全部讀自 research/teams/6072.json。資格判定在此**並未**定案：它們在本頁的檢查表區塊裡，而任何被標示為未經查核的項目，都應該當成未經查核，而不是當成許可。"},{"id":"good-governance","tab":"good","order":22,"kicker":"The constitution","kicker_zh":"計畫章程","title":"How a problem enters the pipeline, and how it leaves","title_zh":"一個題目怎麼進清單，又怎麼離開","lede":"Entry rules are the easy half and every club writes them. The half that decides whether the programme survives is the exit rule, because this report already measured what happens without one: of 78 readable returning teams, 5 carried a problem forward.","lede_zh":"入列規則是容易的那一半，每個社團都寫得出來。真正決定這個計畫活不活下去的是退場規則，因為本報告已經量過沒有退場規則的後果：78 支可查的回鍋隊伍裡，只有 5 支把題目帶到下一年。","body":"The pipeline page says what is in the pipeline. It does not say how anything got there, and it says nothing at all about how anything gets out. **A problem that cannot be ended is never ended.** It stays on the list, unvisited and undiscussed, until the cohort that cared about it graduates and the whole list is quietly dropped. That is not a hypothetical failure mode; it is the one this report measured across an entire competition field.\n\n**The case for writing the exit rule first.** Of the 106 decorated 2026 teams, 81 had entered iGEM before and 78 of those had a previous project anyone could read. **5 of those 78 carried a project line forward.** None of the six returning Grand Prize teams did, and only **3 of 106** credit their own predecessor with anything at all. The institution comes back every year; the problem almost never does. And the analysis that produced those numbers refused to say whether carrying a problem across years is worth it, because five cases cannot be compared with anything and all five of them are survivors. That refusal is the argument. **A programme cannot learn whether carrying a problem works until it records the ones it drops**, and nobody in the field records those. GEMS can, at the price of one page per ending.\n\n**The entry bar comes from a different pair of numbers.** Of the 106 decorated teams, 71 closed a stakeholder-to-design loop, and nine or ten of those 71 closed one with somebody who was not a credentialled technical expert. The loops that closed were closed by experts, not by the people the projects were for. Where that gap is widest is not medicine against agriculture: across Foundational Advance, Space, Software & AI and Biomanufacturing, **2 of 26** closed loops involved a non-expert, against **14 of 45** in the applied villages. The separating condition was not the subject but whether a specific person physically operates the thing being changed. So the entry rule below asks for that person by name. Not a user group, not a sector, not a beneficiary: a name, and what they said before anyone offered them anything.\n\n**And the pipeline today fails its own entry rule three times out of five.** Three of the five entries came from this report rather than from a person. That is the honest figure and the rule does not forbid it; it gives that kind of entry a shorter tether. A report-origin entry holds a slot on probation, labelled as such, for two reviews. In that time its owner has to find one person outside GEMS who will say they want it, recorded in that person's own words. If nobody does, it leaves by one of the five named exits, and leaving is not a disgrace — it is the only way the sixth problem ever gets a slot, because **no new entry is admitted until one has left**.\n\n**The listening visit.** The pipeline's recorded next action is to go back to Chen Hui-wen's farm with no method in hand, and that has to mean more than arriving without a plan. The instrument is a notebook and two students. One asks and one writes, and the writer does not talk. Nothing is proposed, nothing is pitched, and synthetic biology is not mentioned; if asked what GEMS does, the answer is that we are learning. Quote verbatim wherever you can. Copy every number in the unit the person uses rather than the unit you would prefer, and write down any word you had to ask the meaning of, because that word is the best lead in the notebook. Ask to watch the thing done once instead of only being told about it. Leave at ninety minutes, before the welcome runs out.\n\n**The questions, in order.** They start from last week rather than from the word problem, because a person asked what their problems are will name the ones they think a visitor wants to hear. (1) Walk me through yesterday, or the last normal working day — what did you do first, and what last? (2) What took longer than it should have? (3) What did you do more than three times? (4) Show me the thing you use most — may I watch you use it once? (5) What work this year had to be done over again because something went wrong? (6) When something goes wrong here, how do you find out, and how long after it happened? (7) Who else is involved in this that we have not met? (8) What have you already tried for that, and what happened? (9) If you had one extra pair of hands for a day a week, what would you put them on? (10) What do people from outside usually get wrong about this place? (11) What would you rather we did not do? (12) Of everything we talked about, which one thing would you most want to be different a year from now? (13) May we write this down, and show it back to you before anyone else reads it? (14) Can we come back, and when is a bad time?\n\nQuestions 8 and 10 are there to break the visitor's expectations rather than confirm them: 8 stops the programme re-proposing something that already failed here, and 10 invites the person to correct the visitor, which is the only question in the set they are the sole authority on. Question 11 is a consent question and a design constraint at the same time.\n\n**The observations, written without asking.** What is already measured here, and with what — a gauge, a scale, a label, a logbook, a wall calendar, a note on a phone; copy one entry out exactly. What is written down, and where, or that nothing is. What is improvised: the thing held together with tape, the tool used for a job it was not made for. Improvisation marks a need the person stopped mentioning years ago. Who physically touches the thing — count the people and name their roles, and if nobody but a trained person touches it, write that down, because it predicts an expert-closed loop. What one go costs in money, minutes and trips, in the person's own unit. What gets thrown away, and what disposal costs.\n\n**The sentence, written the same evening.** The visit produces one filled-in sentence, so that the four admission criteria can be checked against it afterwards instead of argued about: `[named person]` at `[site]` loses or spends `[quantity, in their unit]` per `[week, season, batch]` because `[cause, in their words]`; they would know it was better if `[number]` changed; the person who would operate any fix is `[name and role]`; the tenth one costs `[more, the same, less]` than the first. Line one is criterion one, the operator is criterion two, the number is criterion three, the tenth is criterion four. **Any blank you cannot fill from quoted words is the agenda for the second visit, not a guess.** Then show the sentence to the person and write down what they corrected. Their correction is the evidence. That is how a non-expert's account becomes admissible in a process that otherwise only recognises credentials — verbatim words, a number in their unit, a named operator, and a correction on the record.\n\n**What is blank.** GEMS has not named a convener, has not fixed the two review dates, has not said where the dated files and exit notes will live, and has not counted how many members have a year left and will sign as owners. Those are the club's to fill in, and the rules below are written with the blanks visible rather than guessed at.","body_zh":"題目清單那一頁說了清單上有什麼。它沒有說任何一個題目是怎麼進來的，也完全沒有說任何一個題目要怎麼出去。**一個無法結束的題目，就永遠不會結束。** 它會一直留在清單上，沒有人去、也沒有人談，直到在意它的那一屆畢業，然後整份清單被安靜地整批丟掉。這不是假想的失效方式，這正是本報告在整個賽場上量到的那一種。\n\n**為什麼要先寫退場規則。** 106 支 2026 年得獎隊伍裡，有 81 支先前就參賽過，其中 78 支的前一個專案是任何人都查得到的。**那 78 支裡，只有 5 支把一條題目線帶到今年。** 六支回鍋的總冠軍級隊伍一支也沒有，而 106 支裡只有 **3 支**對自己的前一屆表示過任何感謝。機構每年都回來，題目幾乎從不回來。而且，產出這些數字的那份分析，拒絕回答「把題目跨年帶下去到底值不值得」，因為五個案例沒有東西可以拿來比較，而且這五個全都是倖存者。那個拒絕本身就是論證。**一個計畫要能學到「把題目帶下去有沒有用」，前提是它記錄了那些被放掉的題目**，而這個領域裡沒有人在記錄這些。GEMS 可以記，代價是每一次結束寫一頁。\n\n**入列的門檻來自另外兩個數字。** 106 支得獎隊伍裡，有 71 支閉合了「利害關係人到設計」的迴路，而這 71 支之中，只有九到十支是和沒有專業資格的人閉合的。真正閉合的迴路，是專家閉合的，不是專案所要服務的那些人閉合的。而這個落差最大的地方，不是醫療對農業：在 Foundational Advance、Space、Software & AI 與 Biomanufacturing 這幾個 village，閉合的迴路有 26 個，其中只有 **2 個**涉及非專業者；而在應用型的 village，45 個之中有 **14 個**。關鍵的分界不是題材，而是「有沒有一個具體的人，用自己的手去操作那個被改動的東西」。所以下面的入列規則要求把那個人具名寫出來。不是使用族群，不是產業，不是受益者：是一個名字，以及在任何人向他們提出任何東西之前，他們說過的話。\n\n**而今天的清單，五個條目裡有三個沒有通過自己的入列規則。** 五個條目裡有三個來自本報告，不是來自某一個人。這是誠實的數字，而規則並不禁止這種條目；規則只是給它一條比較短的繩子。來自報告的條目可以占一個名額，但要標示清楚，而且只能占兩次檢視的時間。在這段時間裡，負責人必須找到 GEMS 以外的一個人說出「我要這個」，並且用那個人自己的話記錄下來。如果沒有人說，它就從五條具名的出路之一離開——而離開不是丟臉，那是第六個題目唯一能拿到名額的方式，因為**在有人退場之前，不會有新的題目進來**。\n\n**去聽的那一次拜訪。** 清單上記錄的下一步，是回到陳惠雯老師的農場，手上不帶方法；而「不帶方法」必須比「不帶計畫」更有內容。這個工具就是一本筆記本和兩名學生。一個人問，一個人寫，寫的人不說話。不提出任何東西，不推銷任何東西，也不提合成生物學；如果被問到 GEMS 在做什麼，答案是我們是來學的。能逐字抄就逐字抄。每一個數字都用對方自己的單位抄下來，不要換成你習慣的單位；還要把你必須回頭問意思的每一個詞寫下來，因為那個詞是筆記本裡最好的線索。要求親眼看一次那件事怎麼做，而不是只聽人家講。九十分鐘就走，在對方的好意用完之前走。\n\n**問題，照這個順序問。** 它們從上個禮拜問起，而不是從「問題」這個字問起，因為一個被問「你有什麼問題」的人，講出來的會是他認為訪客想聽的那些。（1）帶我走一遍昨天，或者最近一個正常的工作日——你最先做什麼，最後做什麼？（2）有哪一件事花的時間比它該花的久？（3）有哪一件事你做了三次以上？（4）給我看你最常用的那個東西——我可以看你用一次嗎？（5）今年有哪些工作因為出了錯，必須整個重做？（6）這裡出狀況的時候，你是怎麼發現的？事情發生之後多久才發現？（7）這件事還牽涉到誰，是我們還沒見過的？（8）為了這件事你已經試過什麼？結果怎麼樣？（9）如果每個禮拜多一雙手、整天都歸你用，你會把它放在哪一件事上？（10）外面來的人，通常把這裡的什麼事情搞錯？（11）有什麼是你寧願我們不要做的？（12）我們今天談到的這些，你最希望一年之後哪一件變得不一樣？（13）我們可以把這些寫下來，並且在給任何其他人看之前，先拿回來給你看嗎？（14）我們可以再來嗎？什麼時候不方便？\n\n第 8 題和第 10 題的用處是打破訪客原本的預期，而不是確認它：第 8 題能阻止這個計畫重新提出一個在這裡已經失敗過的東西；第 10 題則邀請對方糾正訪客，而那是整組問題裡唯一一題，對方是唯一的權威。第 11 題同時是一個徵得同意的問題，和一條設計上的限制。\n\n**要觀察、但不用問的事。** 這裡已經在量什麼、用什麼量——一支量表、一台磅秤、一張標籤、一本紀錄簿、牆上的月曆、手機裡的備忘；照抄其中一筆。什麼被寫下來、寫在哪裡，或者根本沒有寫。什麼是臨時湊出來的：用膠帶纏著的那個東西，被拿去做它本來不是為了做的事的工具。臨時湊出來的東西，標示的是一個對方好幾年前就不再提起的需求。誰的手真的會碰到那個東西——數人數，記下角色；如果除了受過訓練的人沒有別人會碰它，把這件事寫下來，因為它預示一個由專家閉合的迴路。做一次要花多少錢、多少分鐘、跑幾趟，而且用對方自己的單位記。什麼被丟掉，以及丟掉要花多少。\n\n**當天晚上就要寫出來的那句話。** 一次拜訪的產出是一句填好空格的話，這樣四個入列條件事後可以拿來核對，而不是拿來爭論：`[具名的人]`在`[場域]`，因為`[原因，用他們自己的話]`，每`[一週、一季、一批]`損失或花掉`[數量，用他們的單位]`；他們會知道情況變好了，是因為`[哪一個數字]`改變了；真正會操作任何解方的人是`[姓名與角色]`；第十個的成本比第一個`[更高、一樣、更低]`。第一段對應條件一，操作者對應條件二，數字對應條件三，第十個對應條件四。**任何一個你無法用引述的話填滿的空格，都是第二次拜訪的題目，不是用猜的。**然後把這句話拿回去給對方看，並且寫下他們改了什麼。他們的更正就是證據。在一個原本只認得出資歷的流程裡，非專業者的說法就是這樣取得資格的——逐字的話、用他們的單位寫的數字、一位具名的操作者，以及一筆留在紀錄上的更正。\n\n**哪些地方是空白的。** GEMS 還沒有指定召集人，還沒有定下兩次檢視的日期，還沒有說有日期的檔案和退場紀錄要放在哪裡，也還沒有數過有多少成員還剩一年以上、並且願意簽名當負責人。那些是社團自己要填的，而下面的規則是把空白留著讓人看見，而不是用猜的補上。","cards":[{"kicker":"Rule 1 · Entry","kicker_zh":"規則一 · 入列","title":"A person, a number, an owner, and an empty slot","title_zh":"一個人、一個數字、一位負責人，和一個空出來的名額","body":"A problem is admissible when four things sit on one dated page: a named person outside GEMS who described it in their own words before anyone offered them anything; one number that would move, with the method for measuring it; a named site and a named operator, a person rather than a role; and one sentence on what the tenth deployment costs against the first. Anyone may propose, including the partner. Nothing enters without a member who signs as owner.","body_zh":"一個題目可以入列，條件是四件事寫在同一張標了日期的紙上：一位 GEMS 以外的具名人士，在任何人向他們提出任何東西之前，用自己的話描述了它；一個會改變的數字，以及測量它的方法；一個具名的場域和一位具名的操作者——是一個人，不是一個職稱；還有一句話說明第十次佈署相對第一次的成本。任何人都可以提案，夥伴本人也可以。沒有成員簽名當負責人，就沒有東西進得來。","chips":["four criteria, one page","anyone may propose","no owner, no entry"],"chips_zh":["四個條件，一張紙","任何人都能提案","沒有負責人就不入列"]},{"kicker":"Rule 2 · Entry","kicker_zh":"規則二 · 入列","title":"An entry GEMS thought of holds its slot on probation","title_zh":"GEMS 自己想到的題目，名額是試用的","body":"Three of the five entries in the pipeline today came from this report rather than from a person. Three-fifths is the honest figure and it is allowed, with a label and a tether: such an entry holds its slot for two reviews, and in that time its owner must find one person outside GEMS who will say they want it, recorded in that person's words. The label does not come off because the argument got better. It comes off when the person exists.","body_zh":"今天清單上的五個條目，有三個來自本報告而不是來自某一個人。五分之三是誠實的數字，而且這是允許的，只是要加上標籤和一條繩子：這樣的條目可以占住名額兩次檢視，在這段時間裡，負責人必須找到 GEMS 以外的一個人說出他要這個，並且用那個人的話記下來。標籤不會因為論證寫得更好而撕掉，只有在那個人真的出現時才撕掉。","chips":["3 of 5 today","two reviews","labelled until someone asks"],"chips_zh":["今天是 3/5","兩次檢視","沒人開口就一直標著"]},{"kicker":"Rule 3 · Exit","kicker_zh":"規則三 · 退場","title":"Five ways out, and only one of them is success","title_zh":"五條出路，只有一條是成功","body":"Handed on, solved and closed, merged, parked with a date, dropped. The table gives each one its trigger, its signatures and its record. Two of them are deliberately cheap: parking needs one signature and a real revisit date, dropping needs a criterion named and the evidence that failed it. Making the unglamorous exits cheap is the whole design, because an exit that costs face is never taken and the list grows instead.","body_zh":"交出去、做完結案、併入、暫停待議、放掉。表格給每一條出路寫明觸發條件、需要誰簽名、以及要留下什麼紀錄。其中兩條是刻意弄便宜的：暫停只需要一個簽名和一個真的日期，放掉只需要指出哪一個條件沒過、以及是什麼證據讓它沒過。把不光彩的那幾條出路弄便宜，就是整個設計的重點——一條要付出面子代價的出路沒有人會走，結果就是清單愈來愈長。","chips":["5 routes","1 is success","cheap to end"],"chips_zh":["五條出路","只有一條是成功","結束要很便宜"]},{"kicker":"Rule 4 · Exit","kicker_zh":"規則四 · 退場","title":"Silence is an exit, not a continuation","title_zh":"沉默是一種退場，不是延續","body":"At the first club meeting of each month every owner says one sentence about their entry, and it is written in the file with the date. Two silent roll-calls in a row put the entry on the next review's agenda for parking, and an entry with no dated activity for 180 days is parked at that review whether anyone argues for it or not. This is the rule that stops a list turning into a monument.","body_zh":"每個月社團的第一次聚會，每位負責人都要用一句話講自己的條目，並且連同日期寫進檔案。連續兩次點名都沉默，這個條目就會被排進下一次檢視的暫停議程；而任何一個 180 天內沒有任何標了日期的進展的條目，到那次檢視就暫停，不管有沒有人替它說話。這條規則是用來阻止一份清單變成一座紀念碑。","chips":["one sentence a month","two silences, then parked","180 days"],"chips_zh":["每月一句話","兩次沉默就暫停","180 天"]},{"kicker":"Rule 5 · Cadence","kicker_zh":"規則五 · 節奏","title":"Two reviews a year, on dates iGEM does not choose","title_zh":"一年兩次檢視，日期不由 iGEM 決定","body":"The programme has no competition deadline, so its calendar must not borrow one. Two reviews at least four months apart, neither falling in the eight weeks before an iGEM deadline, both fixed in writing a year ahead. Before each one every owner writes three lines: what changed, what the number did, what they want decided. The two dates are a blank the club fills in and then does not move.","body_zh":"這個計畫沒有比賽截止日，所以它的行事曆也不該去借一個。一年兩次檢視，相隔至少四個月，兩次都不能落在任何 iGEM 截止日前八週之內，而且都要提前一年以書面定下來。每次檢視之前，每位負責人寫三行：什麼變了、那個數字怎麼動、他們希望決定什麼。那兩個日期是社團要填的空白，填完以後就不要再動。","chips":["2 a year","4 months apart","dates are a blank"],"chips_zh":["一年兩次","相隔四個月","日期是空白"]},{"kicker":"Rule 6 · Limit","kicker_zh":"規則六 · 上限","title":"Five slots, and no new entry without an exit","title_zh":"五個名額，沒有人退場就沒有人進來","body":"Five is argued, not chosen. Each live entry needs an owner who will still be at GEMS next year, and a school club has few of those; each needs at least two contacts a year to stay alive, which is ten visits or calls across five entries, already a term's real work. And the field's failure is not a shortage of problems: 5 of 78 readable returning teams carried one forward, with nothing stopping the rest from listing more. So the cap binds entry to exit.","body_zh":"五這個數字是論證出來的，不是挑出來的。每一個進行中的條目都需要一位明年還在 GEMS 的負責人，而一個學校社團這樣的人不多；每一個條目一年至少要有兩次接觸才活得下去，五個條目就是十次拜訪或通話，這已經是一個學期實際的工作量。而這個領域的失敗不是題目不夠：78 支可查的回鍋隊伍裡只有 5 支把題目帶下去，而且沒有任何東西阻止其餘的人把清單列得更長。所以上限把入列綁在退場上。","chips":["5 live slots","at most 2 from this report","entry gated on exit"],"chips_zh":["五個進行中名額","最多兩個來自本報告","先退場才能入列"]},{"kicker":"Rule 7 · Handover","kicker_zh":"規則七 · 交接","title":"Six lines, because a long form does not get written","title_zh":"六行，因為太長的表格沒有人會寫","body":"Only 3 of 106 decorated teams credit their own predecessor with anything, so the fix cannot be a report. Before a student leaves they write six lines: the problem in the partner's own sentence; the person, how to reach them, what they last said and when, and what we promised; the number and its value today; one thing that was tried and did not work; what physically exists and where, with the year it came from; and what they would do next and what they would not do again.","body_zh":"106 支得獎隊伍裡只有 3 支對自己的前一屆表示過任何感謝，所以解法不可能是一份報告。學生離開之前寫六行：用夥伴自己的那句話寫下題目；那個人是誰、怎麼聯絡、最後一次說了什麼和什麼時候說的、我們答應了他們什麼；那個數字和它今天的值；一件試過而且沒有成功的事；有哪些實體的東西、放在哪裡、是哪一年留下來的；以及他們接下來會做什麼、以及不會再做什麼。","chips":["6 lines","3 of 106 credited anyone","next owner signs and dates"],"chips_zh":["六行","106 支裡只有 3 支致謝","下一位負責人簽名加日期"]},{"kicker":"Rule 8 · The instrument","kicker_zh":"規則八 · 工具","title":"Two students, one notebook, ninety minutes, no method","title_zh":"兩名學生、一本筆記、九十分鐘、不帶方法","body":"One asks, one writes, and the writer does not talk. Nothing is proposed, nothing is pitched, and synthetic biology is not mentioned; asked what GEMS does, the answer is that we are learning. Quote verbatim, copy numbers in the person's own unit, and write down any word you had to ask the meaning of, because that word is the best lead in the notebook. Ask to watch the thing done once rather than only be told about it.","body_zh":"一個人問，一個人寫，寫的人不說話。不提出任何東西，不推銷任何東西，也不提合成生物學；被問到 GEMS 在做什麼，答案是我們是來學的。逐字抄，數字用對方自己的單位抄，還要把你必須回頭問意思的每一個詞寫下來，因為那個詞是筆記本裡最好的線索。要求親眼看一次那件事怎麼做，不要只聽人家講。","chips":["one asks, one writes","nothing proposed","90 minutes"],"chips_zh":["一個問，一個寫","不提出任何方案","九十分鐘"]},{"kicker":"Rule 9 · The instrument","kicker_zh":"規則九 · 工具","title":"Write the sentence the same evening, then show it back","title_zh":"當天晚上就寫出那句話，然後拿回去給對方看","body":"The visit produces one filled-in sentence, so the four criteria can be checked against it afterwards instead of argued about. Any blank you cannot fill from quoted words is the agenda for the second visit, not a guess. Then show the sentence to the person and write down what they corrected. The correction is the evidence, and it is what makes a non-expert's account admissible in a process that otherwise only recognises credentials.","body_zh":"一次拜訪的產出是一句填好空格的話，這樣四個條件事後可以拿來核對，而不是拿來爭論。任何一個你無法用引述的話填滿的空格，都是第二次拜訪的題目，不是用猜的。然後把那句話拿回去給對方看，並且寫下他們改了什麼。那筆更正就是證據，也正是它讓非專業者的說法，在一個原本只認得出資歷的流程裡取得資格。","chips":["one sentence","blanks, not guesses","the correction is the evidence"],"chips_zh":["一句話","留空白，不要猜","更正就是證據"]}],"table":{"head":["Exit","What evidence triggers it","Who decides","What gets written down","Can it come back?"],"head_zh":["出路","什麼證據觸發它","誰決定","要寫下什麼","可以回來嗎"],"rows":[["Handed on","Someone outside GEMS agrees in writing to keep it and already has what they need to run it","Owner proposes; convener plus one member who never worked on it agree; the receiving party confirms in writing","Exit note: who took it, what went with them, what GEMS still owes them, and a date one year out to ask how it went","Only as a fresh entry, if they come back and ask"],["Solved and closed","The named number was measured before and after and moved, and the partner says it is finished","Owner proposes with both measurements attached; the partner's own words are quoted in the note","Exit note plus the before and after figures, the method, the cost, and what would be done differently","No, but the method joins the programme's reusable list"],["Merged","Two entries share a site, a partner or a number, and one owner can carry both","The two owners agree; the convener records which file survives","Both files linked, the merge date named, and the surviving file inherits the handover of the one that closed","Yes, split again at a review if the surviving owner asks"],["Parked","No dated activity for 180 days, or the owner cannot continue, or an outside condition blocks it for now","Owner or convener alone, no second signature needed","Exit note with the reason in one sentence and a revisit date that is an actual date, not a season","Yes, it returns to the agenda automatically on that date"],["Dropped","A criterion failed on evidence: nobody outside wants it, there is no operator, the number cannot be measured, or the tenth costs what the first did","Convener plus two members, one of them the owner","Exit note naming which criterion failed and the evidence that failed it, kept permanently and read aloud before any new entry is admitted","Only with new evidence from a named person, as a fresh entry"]],"rows_zh":[["交出去","GEMS 以外的人以書面同意接手，而且手上已經有運作它所需要的東西","負責人提出；召集人加上一位從未參與這個條目的成員同意；接手方以書面確認","退場紀錄：誰接走的、什麼一起交出去、GEMS 還欠他們什麼，以及一年後要去問進展的日期","只能以新條目回來，而且要由對方開口"],["做完結案","指定的那個數字前後都量過，而且真的動了，夥伴也說這件事做完了","負責人提出，並附上前後兩次量測；紀錄中引用夥伴自己的話","退場紀錄，加上前後數字、方法、成本，以及如果重做會怎麼做","不會回來，但方法進入計畫可重複使用的清單"],["併入","兩個條目共用同一個場域、同一位夥伴或同一個數字，而且一位負責人扛得起兩個","兩位負責人同意；召集人記下保留哪一份檔案","兩份檔案互相連結、寫明併入日期，保留下來的那份檔案承接被結掉那份的交接紀錄","可以，保留下來的負責人在檢視時提出就能拆開"],["暫停待議","180 天內沒有任何標了日期的進展，或負責人無法繼續，或有外部條件暫時擋住它","負責人或召集人單獨決定，不需要第二個簽名","退場紀錄，用一句話寫下理由，加上一個真的日期而不是一個季節的重啟日","可以，到那個日期自動回到議程上"],["放掉","有證據顯示某個條件沒過：外面沒有人要、沒有操作者、數字量不出來，或第十個的成本和第一個一樣","召集人加上兩位成員，其中一位是負責人","退場紀錄寫明哪一個條件沒過、是什麼證據讓它沒過，永久保存，並在接受任何新條目之前當場讀過","只有在拿到一位具名人士提供的新證據時，才能以新條目回來"]]},"checklist":["Admit a problem only when a named person outside GEMS has described it in their own words on a dated page, and one member has signed as its owner.","Hold five live slots and no more, at most two of them entries GEMS thought of, and admit nothing new until something has left by a named exit.","Give every report-origin entry two reviews to find one person outside GEMS who will say they want it, then exit it.","Fix the two review dates a year ahead, keep both out of the eight weeks before any iGEM deadline, and have every owner write three lines before each one.","Park any entry whose owner has nothing dated to show after 180 days, or who is silent at two monthly roll-calls in a row.","End every entry through one of the five named exits, with the reason, the date, the signatures and whether it can come back; keep the dropped ones forever and read them before admitting anything new.","Make the first visit to any partner a listening visit: two students, one notebook, ninety minutes, no method proposed and synthetic biology not mentioned.","Write the candidate problem statement the same evening in the partner's words and their units, show it back to them, and record what they corrected.","Have every departing owner leave the six-line handover, and have the next owner sign and date that they accepted it."],"checklist_zh":["只有在一位 GEMS 以外的具名人士用自己的話、在一張標了日期的紙上描述過它，而且有一位成員簽名當負責人時，才接受一個題目入列。","維持五個進行中名額、不多不少，其中最多兩個是 GEMS 自己想到的；在有東西從具名的出路離開之前，不接受任何新題目。","給每一個來自報告的條目兩次檢視的時間，去找到 GEMS 以外的一個人說出他要這個；找不到就讓它退場。","兩次檢視的日期提前一年定好，兩次都避開任何 iGEM 截止日前八週，而且每位負責人在每次檢視前寫三行。","任何負責人在 180 天後拿不出標了日期的進展、或連續兩次月點名沉默的條目，一律暫停。","每一個條目都要從五條具名出路之一結束，寫下理由、日期、簽名，以及能不能回來；被放掉的那些永久保存，並在接受任何新題目之前先讀過。","任何夥伴的第一次拜訪都是去聽的：兩名學生、一本筆記、九十分鐘，不提出方法，也不提合成生物學。","當天晚上就用夥伴的話和他們的單位寫出候選題目敘述，拿回去給他們看，並記下他們改了什麼。","每一位要離開的負責人都留下六行交接，並由下一位負責人簽名加日期表示已經接下。"],"method":"This section is a governance proposal, not a measurement. Nothing in it has been tested, because the programme it governs has not yet run a full cycle. It argues from three figures measured elsewhere in this report, each of which states its own limits where it is reported. First, 71 of the 106 decorated 2026 teams closed a stakeholder-to-design loop, and nine or ten of those closed one with somebody who was not a credentialled technical expert. Second, 81 of the 106 had entered iGEM before, 78 of those had a previous project that could be read, and 5 of those 78 carried a project line forward; none of the six returning Grand Prize teams did, and only 3 of 106 credit their own predecessor with anything. Three returning teams could not be classified at all, which is why the denominator is 78 rather than 81. Third, across the platform villages 2 of 26 closed loops involved a non-expert, against 14 of 45 in the applied villages. The source analysis of the second figure declines to say whether carrying a problem across years pays, because five cases are too few and all five are survivors; this note treats that refusal as its own argument for an exit rule rather than as support for the programme. Deliberately left blank for the club: the two review dates; who holds the convener role, which GEMS has not named; where the dated files and exit notes live; how many members have at least a year left and will sign as owners; how many visits a year the club can actually make; and who contacts Chen Hui-wen, and when. The five slots, the 180-day limit, the ninety-minute visit and the six handover lines are proposals with reasons attached, not measurements, and the club should change the numbers if it has better ones. Nothing here describes any difficulty of Chen Hui-wen's farm, because none has been recorded yet.","method_zh":"這一節是一份治理提案，不是一項量測。裡面沒有任何一條被驗證過，因為它所治理的計畫還沒有跑完一個完整的週期。它論證所依據的三個數字都量測於本報告其他處，各自在該處載明了自己的限制。第一，106 支 2026 年得獎隊伍中有 71 支閉合了「利害關係人到設計」的迴路，其中只有九到十支是和沒有專業資格的人閉合的。第二，106 支中有 81 支先前參賽過，其中 78 支的前一個專案是可以讀到的，而那 78 支裡有 5 支把一條題目線帶到今年；六支回鍋的總冠軍級隊伍一支也沒有，而 106 支中只有 3 支對自己的前一屆表示過任何感謝。有三支回鍋隊伍完全無法分類，這就是分母是 78 而不是 81 的原因。第三，在平台型的 village，26 個閉合的迴路中只有 2 個涉及非專業者，而應用型的 village 是 45 個中有 14 個。第二個數字的來源分析拒絕回答「把題目跨年帶下去划不划算」，因為五個案例太少，而且五個全都是倖存者；本節把那個拒絕當成「需要退場規則」的論證本身，而不是當成支持這個計畫的證據。刻意留給社團填的空白：兩次檢視的日期；召集人這個角色由誰擔任，GEMS 還沒有指定；有日期的檔案和退場紀錄放在哪裡；有多少成員還剩至少一年、並且願意簽名當負責人；社團一年實際上跑得了幾次拜訪；以及由誰、在什麼時候聯絡陳惠雯老師。五個名額、180 天的上限、九十分鐘的拜訪和六行交接，都是附了理由的提案，不是量測結果；如果社團有更好的數字，就該改掉。此處沒有描述陳惠雯老師農場的任何具體困難，因為還沒有人記錄過。"},{"id":"ihp-depth","tab":"good","kicker":"Original analysis","title":"Who actually let the outside world change the science","title_zh":"究竟是誰真的讓外界改變了科學","lede":"Across 93 teams, closing the loop has stopped being the distinction and become the norm — and almost every loop that closed was closed by a credentialled expert rather than by anybody the criterion is rhetorically about.","lede_zh":"在 93 支隊伍中，把回饋迴路閉合已經不再是區別所在，而成了常態——而幾乎每一個閉合的迴路，都是由一位有專業資歷的專家閉上的，不是由這條評審標準在修辭上所指的那些人。","body":"A score of four is a sentence, not a stakeholder list: a name, a specific thing said, and a design that is visibly different afterwards. Wageningen's Triton has three modules rather than one because Peter Fischer of Aqualab Zuid explained that trifluoroacetate can only be measured by LC-MS at a central lab, which forced an on-site biosensor, and because Bert van der Waal and Peyman Salehian showed that even tenfold reverse-osmosis concentration leaves it far too dilute, which forced a capture module. **GEMS-Taiwan** was releasing engineered Bacillus into soil until Prof. Chen Wen-Liang told them it could be neither contained nor made to sense temperature precisely; the hollow-fibre perfusion reactor and the electronic AIoT sensing layer both came out of that one April conversation. UCAS-China dropped NKX2-1 as a cargo and put SLPI in its place because Professor Huaiyong Chen said the first matters in development and barely in adulthood. RDFZ-China built bcsABCD in both BL21(DE3) and C41(DE3) and switched host after Professor Haibo Zhang warned that a working genetic module does not imply an efficient one; WUXI-DSAS excised gtdT on Dr Tengfei Hu's advice and recovered the linear dose-response its first-generation sensor could not give; IISER-Kolkata rebuilt its kill-switch trigger around the hypochlorite-sensing regulator RclR after a wastewater engineer pointed out that Indian plants disinfect with sodium hypochlorite rather than UV; and Oxford gave up a living Snodgrassella symbiont for heat-inactivated yeast because regulators pushed back against the beekeepers who had asked for it, then published what that cost its own users.\n\nThe three Best IHP winners share a method, and it is organisational rather than intellectual: the practice is wired into the engineering, not appended to it. **TU Delft** ran Value Sensitive Design in three declared passes and translated values into requirements, labelling the ones it could not meet as Future Perspectives rather than dropping them quietly; UCAS-China built its RCSF cycle as a deliberate parallel to DBTL and gave the human practices group the standing job of tracking every subteam's bottleneck; GEMS-Taiwan ran four thematic expert pipelines with five continuously engaged experts. What the winners do not have is a monopoly on depth. Oxford, Wageningen and UFABC-Brazil were nominees with chains at least as traceable, and UFABC declared its confirmation and refutation rules before seeing its survey results, then redrew its own SWOT when two assumptions failed. **Madrid-UCM**, which published the only genuine closure criterion in the cohort, got no human practices nomination at all.\n\nThe formats that changed designs are narrow and unglamorous. One of them is a single conversation with whoever operates the thing: Veolia's technical director for LYON, a sulfur-recovery engineer of thirty-three years for UOttawa, an optometrist for UAlberta, wet-market vendors for HongKong-JSS who demanded a number and got a wavelength-resolved spectrometer in place of a 14-channel colour sensor. Another is protocol-level consultation with whoever actually runs the technique, which is where chassis and construct changes come from: DTU to Komagataella phaffii, NFLSHS-CHINA from two plasmids to one, Heidelberg to a Serratia expression cassette. Add regulators contacted while the design is still open, peer teams handing over negative data as Darmstadt 2025 did to Padua on pcrABCD's oxygen sensitivity, and written-scorecard pitch events, which are cheap and work: Stanford's BIOME Shark Tank produced the microneedle segmentation pipeline. Against that, the school workshop, the museum stand, the carnival booth, the panel discussion and SDG mapping produced headcounts and nothing traceable, and the large public survey changed vocabulary with near-perfect reliability and hardware almost never.\n\nThe high-school tier is fully competitive wherever the work is user-facing and iterative. HongKong-JSS's farm-driven hardware revisions, measured as a drop from 7.41 to 1.95 per cent coefficient of variation, are better user-led engineering than most collegiate teams managed; **Hongwen School** struck three marketing claims on a gastroenterologist's evidence ladder and changed its selection antibiotic on a professor's re-annotation; HFI, NFLSHS-CHINA, RDFZ-China and WUXI-DSAS all changed circuits or hosts for a named reason; and QingdaoAcademy compressed twenty-two activities into thirteen numbered decisions that split a one-pot process in two and abandoned a planned pH-based function switch outright. Where the tier is not competitive is institutional reach: nothing in it approaches Oxford's EPA-FDA-USDA-CBD mapping, Wageningen's analysis of the non-viable-GMO approval route, UCL's Water UK discharge gap or DTU's correspondence with the European Environment Agency, and formal ethics infrastructure is rare, with Baltimore's community-lab board the main exception; the tier also almost never publishes failures of access the way DTU names the turbine makers who never replied.\n\nThe uncomfortable finding is who actually caused the changes. Of 64 teams that closed a loop, the loop was closed by a credentialled technical expert in nearly every case; the publics, patients and communities that the criterion is rhetorically about overwhelmingly changed the vocabulary and not the vector. Cornell's burn survivors changed what the team promises, Princeton's myeloma patients changed the word 'virus', HFI's 434 respondents changed 'genetically modified' to 'engineered' — all real, none of it touching a construct. Genuine counter-examples number six or seven in 93: LYON removed every living cell from its filter because the public objected, ICJFLS turned public fear into a four-layer containment design, HongKong-JSS re-specified a sensor because farmers wanted a number, UFABC-Brazil routed its seizure alert to a caregiver because a psychiatrist in the public system pointed out that patients who cannot recognise an aura cannot act on one, a beauty-salon manager's distrust of local seaweed put ultrafiltration desalting and endotoxin limits into QingdaoAcademy's plan, and a landfill worker of six years gave Hongwen School the handling cost that made local processing a hard constraint. Two further discomforts: the branded cycle acronym is now universal and predicts nothing, with Jilin-China's Social Shaping Loop and GreatBay-SCIE's five-stage framework scoring 2 while plain tables score 4; and awards track legibility rather than consequence, since **KIT** won Inclusivity and GreatBay-SCIE was nominated for Best IHP on evidence that scores 2, while Madrid-UCM, Hongwen School, GYHS and WUXI-DSAS closed loops nobody rewarded.","body_zh":"四分是一個句子，不是一張利害關係人名單：一個名字、一句具體說過的話，以及之後看得出不一樣的設計。Wageningen 的 Triton 有三個模組而不是一個，是因為 Aqualab Zuid 的 Peter Fischer 說明三氟乙酸只能把樣本送到中央實驗室用 LC-MS 量測，這迫使他們加上現場生物感測器；也因為 Bert van der Waal 和 Peyman Salehian 指出，即使經過十倍逆滲透濃縮，濃度還是稀得太多，這迫使他們加上捕捉模組。**GEMS-Taiwan** 原本要把工程化的 Bacillus 釋放到土壤裡，直到 Chen Wen-Liang 教授告訴他們，這既無法圍堵，也無法做到精確感測溫度；中空纖維灌流反應器和電子 AIoT 感測層，都出自四月那一場對話。UCAS-China 放棄 NKX2-1 作為載運基因、換上 SLPI，是因為 Huaiyong Chen 教授指出前者在發育期重要，在成年期幾乎不重要。RDFZ-China 把 bcsABCD 同時建在 BL21(DE3) 和 C41(DE3) 上，並在 Haibo Zhang 教授警告一個能運作的基因模組不代表它有效率之後換了宿主；WUXI-DSAS 依 Tengfei Hu 博士的建議切除 gtdT，救回第一代感測器給不出的線性劑量反應；IISER-Kolkata 在一位污水工程師指出印度的處理廠是用次氯酸鈉而不是紫外線消毒之後，圍繞次氯酸感測調控因子 RclR 重建了自殺開關的觸發機制；而 Oxford 放棄活的 Snodgrassella 共生菌、改用熱滅活酵母，是因為主管機關的意見與要求前者的養蜂人相反，之後他們也公開了這個選擇讓自己的使用者付出什麼代價。\n\n三支最佳整合式人類實踐得主共用一種方法，而且是組織上的而非思想上的：這套實踐被接進工程裡，不是附加在工程旁邊。**TU Delft** 以三個明確宣告的回合執行價值敏感設計，把價值轉譯成需求，並把做不到的那些標為 Future Perspectives，而不是悄悄刪掉；UCAS-China 刻意把自己的 RCSF 循環建成與 DBTL 平行的結構，並讓人類實踐組常態負責追蹤每一個分組的瓶頸；GEMS-Taiwan 跑了四條主題式專家管線，有五位持續參與的專家。得獎者沒有壟斷深度。Oxford、Wageningen 和 UFABC-Brazil 都只是入圍，但因果鏈至少同樣可追溯，而 UFABC 在看到問卷結果之前就先宣告自己的確認與反駁規則，之後在兩項假設失效時重畫了自己的 SWOT。**Madrid-UCM** 是全體隊伍中唯一提出真正閉環判準的隊伍，卻完全沒有拿到人類實踐的入圍。\n\n真正改變了設計的形式很窄，也不華麗。其中一種是和實際操作那個東西的人談一次話：LYON 談的是 Veolia 的技術總監，UOttawa 談的是一位有三十三年經驗的硫回收工程師，UAlberta 談的是一位驗光師，HongKong-JSS 談的是傳統市場的攤商，他們要的是一個數字，結果 14 通道的顏色感測器被換成了波長解析的光譜儀。另一種是和真正執行該技術的人做實驗流程層級的諮詢，這是底盤與構築體改變的來源：DTU 換成 Komagataella phaffii，NFLSHS-CHINA 從兩個質體變成一個，Heidelberg 換成 Serratia 表現卡匣。再加上在設計還沒定案時就接觸的主管機關、把負面資料交出來的同儕隊伍——例如 Darmstadt 2025 把 pcrABCD 對氧氣敏感的結果交給 Padua——以及有書面評分表的提案活動，這種活動便宜而且有效：Stanford 的 BIOME Shark Tank 催生了微針分割流程。相對地，校園工作坊、博物館攤位、園遊會攤位、座談會和 SDG 對照，產出的是參加人數，沒有任何可追溯的東西；而大型公眾問卷幾乎毫無例外地改變了用詞，卻幾乎從不改變硬體。\n\n只要工作是面對使用者而且會反覆迭代，高中組就完全有競爭力。HongKong-JSS 由農場驅動的硬體修改，量測結果是變異係數從 7.41% 降到 1.95%，這比多數大學隊伍做到的使用者導向工程更好；**Hongwen School** 依一位腸胃科醫師的證據階梯刪掉三項行銷聲稱，並依一位教授重新註解的結果更換了篩選用抗生素；HFI、NFLSHS-CHINA、RDFZ-China 和 WUXI-DSAS 都為了一個具名的理由改了迴路或宿主；QingdaoAcademy 則把二十二項活動壓縮成十三個編號的決定，其中把一鍋式製程拆成兩段，並且乾脆放棄原先計畫的 pH 功能切換。這一組不具競爭力的地方是制度性的觸及範圍：組內沒有任何案例接近 Oxford 的 EPA-FDA-USDA-CBD 對照、Wageningen 對非存活基改生物核可途徑的分析、UCL 找出的 Water UK 排放落差，或 DTU 與歐洲環境署的往來；正式的倫理機制也很少見，Baltimore 的社區實驗室審查委員會是主要的例外。這一組也幾乎從不公布接觸失敗的紀錄，像 DTU 那樣點名哪些渦輪機製造商從未回覆。\n\n令人不自在的發現是：究竟是誰造成了那些改變。64 支閉合了迴路的隊伍中，幾乎每一例都是由一位有專業資歷的技術專家閉上的；而這條標準在修辭上所指的公眾、病人和社群，絕大多數只改變了用詞，沒有改變載體。Cornell 的燒傷倖存者改變了隊伍承諾的內容，Princeton 的骨髓瘤病人改掉了「病毒」這個詞，HFI 的 434 位受訪者把「基因改造」改成「工程化」——全都真實，卻沒有一項碰到構築體。真正的反例在 93 支隊伍中有六、七個：LYON 因為公眾反對而把濾材裡所有活細胞都移除，ICJFLS 把公眾的恐懼轉成四層圍堵設計，HongKong-JSS 因為農民要一個數字而重新規格化感測器，UFABC-Brazil 因為公立體系的一位精神科醫師指出無法辨識前兆的病人也無法據以行動，而把癲癇警示改送到照顧者，一位美容院經理對本地海藻的不信任讓超過濾脫鹽與內毒素上限進了 QingdaoAcademy 的計畫，而一位做了六年的垃圾掩埋場工人則給了 Hongwen School 那筆搬運成本，使就地處理成為硬性限制。另有兩點令人不自在：掛上品牌的循環縮寫現在到處都有，而且什麼都預測不了——Jilin-China 的 Social Shaping Loop 和 GreatBay-SCIE 的五階段框架都只得 2 分，而樸素的表格得 4 分；獎項追蹤的是易讀性而不是後果，因為 **KIT** 以只得 2 分的證據拿下包容性獎、GreatBay-SCIE 也以這種等級的證據入圍最佳整合式人類實踐，而 Madrid-UCM、Hongwen School、GYHS 和 WUXI-DSAS 閉合的迴路沒有人獎勵。","cards":[{"kicker":"Worked example","title":"Two of three modules were somebody else's idea","title_zh":"三個模組中有兩個是別人的主意","body":"Wageningen set out only to degrade trifluoroacetate. Peter Fischer at Aqualab Zuid, one of six labs legally tasked with assessing Dutch drinking water, explained that the compound can only be measured by LC-MS on samples shipped to a central lab, so the bioreactor could not be operated at all without an on-site readout: that created the biosensor module. Bert van der Waal and Peyman Salehian then showed that tenfold reverse-osmosis concentration takes 2.2 micrograms per litre only to 22, against a milligram-per-litre target, which created the capture module. Frank Schoonenberg of Vitens moved the whole deployment target to reverse-osmosis concentrate, and Tue Kjaergaard Nielsen changed the readout to released fluoride because measuring TFA disappearance mistakes adsorption for degradation.","body_zh":"Wageningen 原本只打算分解三氟乙酸。Aqualab Zuid 的 Peter Fischer——該實驗室是荷蘭六家法定負責評估飲用水的機構之一——說明這個化合物只能把樣本送到中央實驗室用 LC-MS 量測，所以沒有現場讀出就根本無法操作這座生物反應器：這催生了生物感測模組。接著 Bert van der Waal 和 Peyman Salehian 指出，十倍逆滲透濃縮只能把每公升 2.2 微克提高到 22 微克，而目標是毫克每公升的量級，這催生了捕捉模組。Vitens 的 Frank Schoonenberg 把整個部署目標移到逆滲透濃縮液，而 Tue Kjaergaard Nielsen 把讀出改成釋出的氟離子，因為量測 TFA 的消失會把吸附誤認成分解。","chips":["WageningenUR","Overgrad","Score 4","Utility and lab engineers"],"chips_zh":["WageningenUR","研究生組","評分 4","水務與實驗室工程師"],"kicker_zh":"實例"},{"kicker":"Worked example","title":"The conversation that moved sensing out of the cell","title_zh":"把感測移出細胞之外的那場對話","body":"GEMS-Taiwan's original design put engineered Bacillus subtilis in the soil with a DesK-DesR system reading temperature directly. On 10 April, Prof. Chen Wen-Liang and bioprocess experts said two things were wrong: the bacteria could not be contained, and biological sensing was neither precise nor controllable enough. Sensing moved out of the cell into electronic sensors and an AIoT model, and a hollow-fibre perfusion bioreactor was built to hold the bacteria in while letting the protectants out. A later public forum with natural-farming advocates, who argued that a crop protected from every stress never builds tolerance, became the specification for the release threshold rather than an objection to be managed.","body_zh":"GEMS-Taiwan 最初的設計是把工程化的 Bacillus subtilis 放進土壤，用 DesK-DesR 系統直接讀取溫度。4 月 10 日，Chen Wen-Liang 教授和生物製程專家指出兩件事是錯的：細菌無法被圍堵，而生物感測既不夠精確也不夠可控。感測從細胞內移到電子感測器和一套 AIoT 模型，同時建了一座中空纖維灌流生物反應器，把細菌留在裡面、讓保護物質出去。後來一場與自然農法倡議者的公開論壇——他們主張一株被保護到完全沒有逆境的作物永遠不會建立耐受性——成了釋放閾值的規格依據，而不是一個要被處理掉的反對意見。","chips":["GEMS-Taiwan","High School","Score 4","Best IHP winner"],"chips_zh":["GEMS-Taiwan","高中組","評分 4","Best IHP 得主"],"kicker_zh":"實例"},{"kicker":"Worked example","title":"When the regulator overrules the user","title_zh":"當主管機關推翻使用者","body":"Danny Le Feuvre of the Australian Honey Bee Industry Council and Mike Allerton of Amateur Beekeepers Australia both wanted a persistent living Snodgrassella alvi gut symbiont because it minimises beekeeper labour. Oxford did not simply comply: it took the question to Scottish and Australian regulators and the Soil Association, who pushed the other way, and switched to heat-inactivated dried yeast. The team then stated plainly what that cost — the persistence the beekeepers valued, meaning repeat dosing and more labour. A joint meeting with EPA, FDA and USDA staff stopped them treating the inactivated route as a universal regulatory shortcut, forcing jurisdiction-by-jurisdiction mapping instead.","body_zh":"Australian Honey Bee Industry Council 的 Danny Le Feuvre 和 Amateur Beekeepers Australia 的 Mike Allerton 都想要一株能持續存在的活 Snodgrassella alvi 腸道共生菌，因為這能把養蜂人的工作量降到最低。Oxford 並沒有照辦：他們把這個問題帶到蘇格蘭與澳洲的主管機關以及 Soil Association，這些單位的意見正好相反，於是改用熱滅活的乾酵母。隊伍接著明白寫出這個選擇的代價——失去養蜂人所重視的持續性，意味著要重複投藥、工作量更大。一場與 EPA、FDA 和 USDA 人員的聯合會議，讓他們不再把滅活路線當成普遍適用的法規捷徑，而是改為逐一管轄區進行對照。","chips":["Oxford","Undergrad","Score 4","Best IHP nominee"],"chips_zh":["Oxford","大學組","評分 4","Best IHP 入圍"],"kicker_zh":"實例"},{"kicker":"Worked example","title":"A farmer asked for a number","title_zh":"一位農民要一個數字","body":"HongKong-JSS built a mercury biosensor with a visible colour readout. Koo's Farm and local wet-market vendors said they wanted numerical readings, not qualitative colour, which is the direct reason the AS7343 14-channel sensor was replaced by a wavelength-resolved Hamamatsu C12880 with a numerical display. Users then reported excessive syringe force on the V1 filter stack, so manual delivery became pump-driven dosing, improving the coefficient of variation from 7.41 to 1.95 per cent. More Happy Farm said plainly that not every farmer wants to own a device, which pushed them to a service model — and after a 195-person demonstration found high perceived confidence, the team separated device status from safety judgement in the interface because confidence is not accuracy.","body_zh":"HongKong-JSS 做了一個以可見顏色讀出的汞生物感測器。Koo's Farm 和本地傳統市場的攤商說他們要的是數值讀數，不是定性的顏色，這就是 AS7343 14 通道感測器被換成帶數值顯示的波長解析 Hamamatsu C12880 的直接原因。使用者接著回報 V1 濾材組需要過大的針筒推力，於是手動加樣改成泵驅動的定量加樣，變異係數從 7.41% 改善到 1.95%。More Happy Farm 直接說並不是每個農民都想擁有一台裝置，這把他們推向服務模式——而在一場 195 人的示範中發現使用者自覺的信心偏高之後，隊伍在介面上把裝置狀態與安全判斷分開，因為有信心不等於準確。","chips":["HongKong-JSS","High School","Score 4","Non-expert changed hardware"],"chips_zh":["HongKong-JSS","高中組","評分 4","非專家改了硬體"],"kicker_zh":"實例"},{"kicker":"Method that nobody rewarded","title":"The only team that defined what 'closed' means","title_zh":"唯一定義了「閉合」是什麼意思的隊伍","body":"Madrid-UCM built a five-rung integration ladder with an explicit closure criterion: a loop counts as closed only when the revised design goes back to the person whose input triggered it and their response produces a further change. They then demonstrated it on materials — Carmen Garcia Payo and Loreto Garcia Fernandez proposed core-shell capsules, the team built them but could not see the internal structure, took that problem back to the same researchers, and got magnetite as an optical tracer plus cryosectioning, which became a wall-thickness and leakage pipeline. Aurelio Hidalgo's point that a single-use biocatalyst is neither economical nor recoverable killed both placeholder designs and moved the enzyme panel onto a reusable solid support. They also document a change they chose not to make, on the grounds that not adding a pathway is a design decision too. No Best IHP nomination.","body_zh":"Madrid-UCM 建了一座五階的整合階梯，並有明確的閉環判準：一個迴路只有在修訂後的設計回到提供意見的那個人面前、而他的回應又帶來進一步的改變時，才算閉合。他們接著在材料上示範了這一點——Carmen Garcia Payo 和 Loreto Garcia Fernandez 提議核殼膠囊，隊伍做出來了卻看不到內部結構，於是把這個問題帶回同一批研究者，得到以磁鐵礦作為光學示蹤劑再加上冷凍切片的作法，這後來變成一條量測壁厚與滲漏的流程。Aurelio Hidalgo 指出單次使用的生物催化劑既不經濟也無法回收，這一句話殺掉了兩個暫用設計，並把酵素組移到可重複使用的固體支撐上。他們也記錄了一項選擇不做的改變，理由是不加進一條代謝途徑同樣是一個設計決定。沒有拿到最佳整合式人類實踐入圍。","chips":["Madrid-UCM","Undergrad","Score 4","Not nominated"],"chips_zh":["Madrid-UCM","大學組","評分 4","沒有入圍"],"kicker_zh":"沒有被獎勵的做法"},{"kicker":"Format that mostly did not work","title":"The survey that changes your vocabulary","title_zh":"只會改變你用詞的問卷","body":"Large public surveys are the most common instrument in the cohort and the least consequential for design. HFI's 434 responses replaced 'genetically modified' with 'engineered' across all materials and rebuilt the education from basics. Peking's 539 respondents named three priorities the team concedes already outlined the finished project. UCAS-China's 419 public respondents and HongKong-HS's 420 produced awareness statistics and workshop plans. The honest version is GHCIS, which found that its price and speed questions branched into samples too small to use and explicitly refused to convert 'within RMB 30' into a product requirement, carrying it forward as a question for frontline users instead.","body_zh":"大型公眾問卷是全體隊伍中最常見的工具，對設計的影響也最小。HFI 的 434 份回覆讓所有材料把「基因改造」換成「工程化」，並把教育內容從基礎重建。Peking 的 539 位受訪者點出三項優先事項，而隊伍自己承認這三項早就勾勒出了最終完成的專案。UCAS-China 的 419 位公眾受訪者和 HongKong-HS 的 420 位，產出的是認知度統計和工作坊計畫。誠實的版本是 GHCIS：他們發現價格與速度的題目分支之後樣本太小而無法使用，並明確拒絕把「人民幣 30 元以內」轉成產品需求，而是把它當成一個問題帶給第一線使用者。","chips":["HFI","Peking","GHCIS","UCAS-China","Vocabulary, not vector"],"chips_zh":["HFI","Peking","GHCIS","UCAS-China","改用詞，不改方向"],"kicker_zh":"大多無效的形式"}],"table":{"head":["Team","Section","Score","What changed"],"head_zh":["隊伍","組別","評分","改變了什麼"],"rows":[["ABOA","Overgrad","4","Purified enzymes dropped for whole cells on carriers; reactor moved to a side stream"],["Al-Nahrain-IRAQ","Undergrad","4","AI model abandoned for equation-based modelling; lab data entry page added"],["Athens","Overgrad","4","Delivery moved from spray to feed; live phage dropped for a non-replicating enzyme"],["BGCFullerton","High School","4","CIF peptides dropped; regolith mixture plan and model validation changed"],["CHINAGuangdongShimen","High School","4","Multivalent antibody replaced by a single monovalent nanobody"],["Cornell","Undergrad","4","Homemade high-voltage supply dropped; hypoxia AND gate added for specificity"],["DTU-Denmark","Overgrad","4","Enzyme step reframed as solvolysis complement; chassis to K. phaffii; docking filter dropped"],["ETH-Zurich","Overgrad","4","Pivot off the Drosophila biopesticide; split-cargo dual targeting invented"],["Eton-College-UK","High School","4","Plasmid backbone changed; reusable reader plus disposable cartridge fixed"],["GCGS","High School","4","VOC module de-scoped; temperature kill switch added, pH switch declined with a reason"],["GEMS-Taiwan","High School","4","Sensing moved out of the cell; perfusion reactor added; proline delivery abandoned"],["GYHS","High School","4","Bond strength replaced by a seven-part requirement set; V2 handling redesigned"],["HFI","High School","4","Lysine-responsive promoter abandoned for constitutive expression"],["HK-Joint-School","High School","4","Goal shifted from fire retardancy to non-toxic, low-smoke; benchmark added"],["HKSSC","High School","4","Kill switch and controlled use; MIC/growth-rate design; pH range from regulator data"],["HKU-HongKong","Unlisted","4","Hypothesis narrowed to partial inflammation modulation; M1/M2 framing dropped"],["HUST-China","Undergrad","4","Reflectin module abandoned entirely for a fashion-waste cellulose route"],["HangzhouFourteenAP","High School","4","Target moved from mineralised calculus to pre-mineralisation biofilm matrix"],["Heidelberg","Undergrad","4","Expression host swapped to a Serratia cassette; engineering retargeted onto GvpC"],["HongKong-HS","High School","4","Toehold switch replaced by HCR; ThT fluorescence replaced by G4/hemin colour"],["HongKong-JSS","High School","4","Colour sensor replaced by spectrometer; syringe replaced by pump dosing"],["Hongwen School","High School","4","IBS claims struck; selection marker changed; near-site processing made a hard constraint"],["ICJFLS","High School","4","Capsule killed for mouthwash/lozenge/gum set; plasmid dropped for chromosomal integration"],["IISER-Kolkata","Unlisted","4","Kill switch rebuilt around a hypochlorite sensor because plants do not use UV"],["KAUST-KSA","Overgrad","4","Dsup added to the chassis; payload reprioritised by real mission conditions"],["LYON","Undergrad","4","All living cells removed from the filter; households ruled out as customers"],["Lambert-GA","High School","4","Nanobodies abandoned for minibinders; target narrowed to the VP3 P-domain"],["MIT-MAHE","Undergrad","4","Target customer moved from fragrance houses to aroma compound manufacturers"],["Madrid-UCM","Undergrad","4","Secretion and consortium killed for immobilised enzymes; containment above performance"],["Marburg","Overgrad","4","5'UTR redesigned so the PPR site and RBS are disconnected; RBS testing dropped"],["McGill","Undergrad","4","Dropped ultra-purification; feedstock moved to fresh tailings; tolling business model"],["McMaster-Canada","Undergrad","4","Oncology and allergy concepts dropped for localised gut-associated systems"],["Muenster-University","Overgrad","4","Prediction pipeline rebuilt with a geometric scoring layer; NLR route dropped"],["NBJF","High School","4","DNA storage device abandoned for the enzymatic-writing bottleneck"],["NFLSHS-CHINA","High School","4","Two plasmids collapsed into one; aqueous formulation killed for oil and capsule"],["NJU-China","Undergrad","4","Recorded associations split from model predictions in every view"],["NUS-Singapore","Undergrad","4","Primary use moved from industrial monitoring to early-stage R&D"],["NYCU-Taiwan","Undergrad","4","Claimed advantages withdrawn after reading a competitor's documentation"],["Oxford","Undergrad","4","Living symbiont chassis dropped for heat-inactivated yeast, with the cost published"],["PSI Korea","High School","4","Auto-exposure disabled and imaging conditions fixed; instrument separated from material"],["Princeton","Undergrad","4","AlphaFold3 cut from the pipeline; IL-6 and amyloid-beta targets dropped"],["QingdaoAcademy","High School","4","One-pot process split in two; pH switch abandoned; desalting and endotoxin control added"],["RDFZ-China","High School","4","Host switched to C41(DE3); metal anchors replaced by on-site stone"],["SEHS","High School","4","Indication moved from liver to gastric cancer; binding re-tested per format"],["SMS-Shenzhen","High School","4","Target customer relocated from front-end recyclers to hydrometallurgical tail streams"],["SUIS-SFLS","High School","4","Deliverable rewritten from finished dressing to characterised protein plus QC records"],["Stanford University","Undergrad","4","Burns dropped for keloids; target moved from prevention to established scars"],["Stockholm","Overgrad","4","Open release abandoned for a sealed reactor sited at the membrane-bioreactor stage"],["TAU-Israel","Overgrad","4","Markers stratified across superficial and deep lesions; biosensor demoted to triage"],["TU Delft","Overgrad","4","Antibiotics dropped for AMPs; pre-coated implant instead of in-theatre paste"],["UAlberta","Undergrad","4","Binding-pocket release abandoned; yeast dropped for E. coli; GFP to mScarlet"],["UCAS-China","Undergrad","4","NKX2-1 cargo dropped for SLPI; repositioned to asthma maintenance"],["UCNZ","Undergrad","4","Distributed plants dropped for one central facility; sustainability claim narrowed"],["UFABC-Brazil","Overgrad","4","Pipetted cell-free reaction replaced by a paper strip; alert routed to a support network"],["UNILausanne","Overgrad","4","Defend strategy kept against the model's own advice; model scope declared the limit"],["UOttawa","Undergrad","4","Target stream moved from bitumen to diesel; pH loop added to the P&ID"],["UZurich","Overgrad","4","Machine-learning plan dropped for established software; root cohesion added to the model"],["Uni-Padua-IT","Undergrad","4","Cold-tolerance module cut; perchlorate genes compartmentalised in heterocysts"],["Vilnius-Lithuania","Undergrad","4","Gel software moved off image classification onto band-distance matching"],["WUXI-DSAS","High School","4","gtdT excised to restore linearity; output changed to a creatinine ratio"],["WageningenUR","Overgrad","4","Biosensor and capture modules created; readout changed to released fluoride"],["William-and-Mary","Undergrad","4","Readout replaced by CFU viability; seawater microcosm experiments added"],["Worldshaper-Shanghai","High School","4","Capacity-building dropped for licensing; sunlight-is-greener claims deleted"],["XJTLU-China","Undergrad","4","Success redefined as soluble protein, not total expression"],["ASIJ-Tokyo","High School","3","Positioning moved from replacement to extra source; patch route added"],["Baltimore","High School","3","Preservation study and patent strategy added; changes peripheral to the build"],["CalPolySLO","Undergrad","3","Survivability testing and a misuse framework added; the build itself unchanged"],["DKU","Undergrad","3","Per-application immunogenicity thresholds and clearer tool output; attribution collective"],["GHCIS","High School","3","Microfluidic format replaced by filter paper, on unnamed industry advice"],["GU Frankfurt","Overgrad","3","Binder accuracy made the governing constraint; biggest change was procedural"],["Kyoto","Undergrad","3","Food themes abandoned and the question reframed; specific changes not itemised"],["Peking","Undergrad","3","Broad-spectrum pesticide and crude biocontrol routes dropped; chain not attributed"],["SDU-Denmark","Overgrad","3","Target moved to reliable low-power generation; no named source"],["SJTU-BioX-Shanghai","Undergrad","3","Repositioned as a post-debridement dressing with physical containment; sources unnamed"],["Toronto","Overgrad","3","Contained bioreactor and close-homology enzymes preferred; stakeholders unnamed"],["UCL","Undergrad","3","Regulatory gap found and a techno-economic model built; the device did not change"],["UPF-Barcelona","Undergrad","3","Central claim shrunk from bulk soil water to a hydration shell at the root"],["ZJU-China","Undergrad","3","Cost weighted more heavily in material design; attribution aggregated"],["ZQT-Nanjing","High School","3","Narrowed from general skincare to barrier repair after a 397-person survey"],["BAID-China","High School","2","Communication depth differentiated by audience; accessibility artefacts revised"],["BNDS-China","High School","2","Workflow discipline borrowed from a peer team; rest is framing"],["BOKU-Vienna","Overgrad","2","Claims key design decisions changed but does not say which"],["CAU-China","Undergrad","2","Need reported from Malawi and Zambia; no design consequence recorded"],["GreatBay-SCIE","High School","2","Slogan changed on stigma grounds; design philosophy only loosely attributed"],["HBUT-China","Undergrad","2","Named virologist fed the risk assessment; no design consequence stated"],["Jilin-China","Undergrad","2","Double-loop reframing of what counts as success; consequences not shown"],["KIT","Overgrad","2","Survey converted into two inclusivity deliverables; science untouched"],["Labi-Taiwan","High School","2","Complements-not-replaces framing and a detects-not-diagnoses statement"],["Mingdao","High School","2","Five honest questions, including a no-project condition; no design change recorded"],["UMA Malaga","Undergrad","2","Question reframed around the diagnostic pathway, not the device"],["UOregon","Overgrad","2","Plant operators confirmed the gap; equity framing shaped, design did not"],["NIS Almaty-Medeu","High School","1","Questions published in advance; no answers or consequences recorded yet"],["Yucai-SZ","High School","1","A 719-response survey tested the premise; no consequence recorded"]],"rows_zh":[["ABOA","研究生組","4","放棄純化酵素，改用附著在載體上的全細胞；反應器移到側流"],["Al-Nahrain-IRAQ","大學組","4","放棄 AI 模型，改用方程式建模；新增實驗資料輸入頁面"],["Athens","研究生組","4","投遞方式從噴灑改為飼料；放棄活噬菌體，改用不複製的酵素"],["BGCFullerton","高中組","4","放棄 CIF 胜肽；風化層混合配方計畫與模型驗證方式改變"],["CHINAGuangdongShimen","高中組","4","多價抗體改成單一的單價 nanobody"],["Cornell","大學組","4","放棄自製高壓電源；為提高專一性加入缺氧 AND 閘"],["DTU-Denmark","研究生組","4","酵素步驟重新定位為溶劑分解的互補；底盤換成 K. phaffii；放棄對接篩選"],["ETH-Zurich","研究生組","4","放棄果蠅生物農藥方向；發明分割載運的雙標的策略"],["Eton-College-UK","高中組","4","更換質體骨架；定案為可重複使用的讀取器加一次性卡匣"],["GCGS","高中組","4","縮減 VOC 模組範圍；加入溫度自殺開關，並附理由否決 pH 開關"],["GEMS-Taiwan","高中組","4","感測移出細胞之外；加入灌流反應器；放棄脯胺酸投遞"],["GYHS","高中組","4","以一組七項需求取代單一黏結強度指標；V2 的操作方式重新設計"],["HFI","高中組","4","放棄離胺酸誘導型啟動子，改用組成型表現"],["HK-Joint-School","高中組","4","目標從阻燃改為無毒、低煙；加入基準比較"],["HKSSC","高中組","4","加入自殺開關與受控使用；以 MIC 與生長速率設計；pH 範圍取自主管機關資料"],["HKU-HongKong","未列組別","4","假設收斂為部分調節發炎；放棄 M1/M2 的框架"],["HUST-China","大學組","4","完全放棄 reflectin 模組，改走時尚廢棄物纖維素路線"],["HangzhouFourteenAP","高中組","4","標的從已礦化的牙結石移到礦化前的生物膜基質"],["Heidelberg","大學組","4","表現宿主換成 Serratia 卡匣；工程改造目標轉到 GvpC"],["HongKong-HS","高中組","4","toehold switch 改成 HCR；ThT 螢光改成 G4／hemin 顯色"],["HongKong-JSS","高中組","4","顏色感測器改成光譜儀；針筒改成泵驅動定量加樣"],["Hongwen School","高中組","4","刪除 IBS 相關聲稱；更換篩選標記；就近處理成為硬性限制"],["ICJFLS","高中組","4","放棄膠囊，改為漱口水／錠劑／口香糖組合；放棄質體，改為染色體嵌入"],["IISER-Kolkata","未列組別","4","因為處理廠不使用紫外線，自殺開關改以次氯酸感測器重建"],["KAUST-KSA","研究生組","4","底盤加入 Dsup；依真實任務條件重排酬載優先順序"],["LYON","大學組","4","濾材中所有活細胞全部移除；排除家庭用戶作為客戶"],["Lambert-GA","高中組","4","放棄 nanobody，改用 minibinder；標的收斂到 VP3 的 P-domain"],["MIT-MAHE","大學組","4","目標客戶從香水品牌商移到香料化合物製造商"],["Madrid-UCM","大學組","4","放棄分泌與菌群路線，改用固定化酵素；圍堵優先於效能"],["Marburg","研究生組","4","重新設計 5'UTR，使 PPR 位點與 RBS 不再連動；放棄 RBS 測試"],["McGill","大學組","4","放棄超純化；原料改為新鮮尾礦；改採代工收費的商業模式"],["McMaster-Canada","大學組","4","放棄腫瘤與過敏的構想，改為局部作用的腸道相關系統"],["Muenster-University","研究生組","4","預測流程以幾何評分層重建；放棄 NLR 路線"],["NBJF","高中組","4","放棄 DNA 儲存裝置，轉向酵素寫入的瓶頸"],["NFLSHS-CHINA","高中組","4","兩個質體併成一個；放棄水性配方，改為油劑與膠囊"],["NJU-China","大學組","4","在每一個檢視畫面中都把已記錄的關聯與模型預測分開"],["NUS-Singapore","大學組","4","主要用途從工業監測移到早期研發"],["NYCU-Taiwan","大學組","4","讀過競爭對手的文件後撤回原本宣稱的優勢"],["Oxford","大學組","4","放棄活體共生菌底盤，改用熱滅活酵母，並公開這個選擇的代價"],["PSI Korea","高中組","4","關閉自動曝光並固定影像條件；把儀器與材料分開處理"],["Princeton","大學組","4","從流程中移除 AlphaFold3；放棄 IL-6 與 amyloid-beta 標的"],["QingdaoAcademy","高中組","4","一鍋式製程拆成兩段；放棄 pH 開關；加入脫鹽與內毒素控制"],["RDFZ-China","高中組","4","宿主換成 C41(DE3)；金屬錨件改用現地石材"],["SEHS","高中組","4","適應症從肝癌移到胃癌；依每一種形式重新測試結合能力"],["SMS-Shenzhen","高中組","4","目標客戶從前端回收業者移到濕法冶金的尾端流程"],["SUIS-SFLS","高中組","4","交付成果從成品敷料改寫為完成特性分析的蛋白質加品管紀錄"],["Stanford University","大學組","4","放棄燒傷，改做蟹足腫；目標從預防移到已形成的疤痕"],["Stockholm","研究生組","4","放棄開放釋放，改為設置在膜生物反應器階段的密閉反應器"],["TAU-Israel","研究生組","4","標記依淺層與深層病灶分層；生物感測器降級為初步分流用"],["TU Delft","研究生組","4","放棄抗生素，改用 AMP；以預先塗層的植入物取代手術室現調的膏劑"],["UAlberta","大學組","4","放棄結合口袋釋放機制；放棄酵母改用 E. coli；GFP 換成 mScarlet"],["UCAS-China","大學組","4","放棄 NKX2-1 載運基因改用 SLPI；重新定位為氣喘的維持治療"],["UCNZ","大學組","4","放棄分散式廠房，改為單一中央設施；縮小永續性聲稱的範圍"],["UFABC-Brazil","研究生組","4","以試紙取代需要移液的無細胞反應；警示改送到支持網絡"],["UNILausanne","研究生組","4","在模型自身的建議之外仍保留防禦策略；明確宣告模型範圍就是其限制"],["UOttawa","大學組","4","目標物流從瀝青移到柴油；在 P&ID 中加入 pH 控制迴路"],["UZurich","研究生組","4","放棄機器學習計畫，改用成熟軟體；模型中加入根系團聚作用"],["Uni-Padua-IT","大學組","4","刪去耐寒模組；把高氯酸鹽相關基因區隔到異形細胞中"],["Vilnius-Lithuania","大學組","4","膠體軟體從影像分類改為條帶距離比對"],["WUXI-DSAS","高中組","4","切除 gtdT 以恢復線性；輸出改為肌酸酐比值"],["WageningenUR","研究生組","4","新增生物感測與捕捉模組；讀出改為釋出的氟離子"],["William-and-Mary","大學組","4","讀出改為 CFU 存活數；加入海水微宇宙實驗"],["Worldshaper-Shanghai","高中組","4","放棄能力建構路線改為技術授權；刪除日照更環保的聲稱"],["XJTLU-China","大學組","4","把成功重新定義為可溶性蛋白質，而不是總表現量"],["ASIJ-Tokyo","高中組","3","定位從替代品改為額外來源；加入貼片途徑"],["Baltimore","高中組","3","加入保存性研究與專利策略；這些改變與實際建置沒有直接關係"],["CalPolySLO","大學組","3","加入存活性測試與誤用評估框架；建置本身沒有改變"],["DKU","大學組","3","依應用場景設定免疫原性閾值，工具輸出更清楚；意見歸因是集體性的"],["GHCIS","高中組","3","依未具名的業界建議，微流體形式改為濾紙"],["GU Frankfurt","研究生組","3","以結合物準確度作為主要限制條件；最大的改變是流程上的"],["Kyoto","大學組","3","放棄食品主題並重新界定問題；具體改變沒有逐項列出"],["Peking","大學組","3","放棄廣效農藥與粗放生物防治路線；因果鏈沒有歸因"],["SDU-Denmark","研究生組","3","目標移向穩定的低功率發電；沒有具名來源"],["SJTU-BioX-Shanghai","大學組","3","重新定位為清創後使用、具物理圍堵的敷料；來源未具名"],["Toronto","研究生組","3","偏好密閉生物反應器與高同源性酵素；利害關係人未具名"],["UCL","大學組","3","找出法規落差並建立技術經濟分析模型；裝置本身沒有改變"],["UPF-Barcelona","大學組","3","核心主張從整體土壤水分縮小為根部的水合層"],["ZJU-China","大學組","3","材料設計中成本的權重提高；意見歸因是彙總的"],["ZQT-Nanjing","高中組","3","在一份 397 人的問卷之後，從一般護膚收斂到屏障修復"],["BAID-China","高中組","2","依受眾區分溝通深度；修訂無障礙相關產出"],["BNDS-China","高中組","2","從同儕隊伍借用工作流程紀律；其餘都是框架層面的"],["BOKU-Vienna","研究生組","2","聲稱關鍵設計決定有所改變，但沒有說是哪些"],["CAU-China","大學組","2","報告了來自馬拉威與尚比亞的需求；沒有記錄任何設計後果"],["GreatBay-SCIE","高中組","2","因汙名化的考量更改標語；設計理念的歸因很鬆散"],["HBUT-China","大學組","2","具名病毒學家提供意見納入風險評估；沒有陳述任何設計後果"],["Jilin-China","大學組","2","以雙迴路重新界定什麼算成功；沒有呈現後果"],["KIT","研究生組","2","把問卷轉成兩項包容性交付成果；科學本身沒有動"],["Labi-Taiwan","高中組","2","採用互補而非取代的定位，以及偵測而非診斷的聲明"],["Mingdao","高中組","2","五個誠實的問題，包括一個不做這個專案的條件；沒有記錄設計改變"],["UMA Malaga","大學組","2","問題重新圍繞診斷路徑而非裝置來界定"],["UOregon","研究生組","2","廠區操作人員確認了這個落差；公平性的框架被塑形，設計沒有"],["NIS Almaty-Medeu","高中組","1","事先公布了問題；還沒有記錄任何回答或後果"],["Yucai-SZ","高中組","1","一份 719 份回覆的問卷檢驗了前提；沒有記錄任何後果"]]},"method":"Every team in this report is a Top 10 or special-prize winner or nominee, so this is the most decorated tenth of the competition and not a representative sample. Read '64 of 93 closed the loop' as 'closing the loop is normal among teams that win things', not as a statement about iGEM at large. Every team file with any good.ihp content was scored on the four-point rubric from what the file itself states: a 4 required a named stakeholder, a specific thing said, and a change to the build, the deployment, the readout, the safety design or the business model that the file ties to that input. Teams whose only documented consequence was a change of framing, language, education material or evidence package scored 2 or 3 however elaborately the process was branded, and awards were ignored throughout. The rubric cannot verify that a change was made because of the advice rather than attributed to it afterwards, cannot see the wiki behind the summary, and cannot distinguish a thin causal chain from a thin write-up of a thick one. Files continued to land while the scoring ran; all 93 present at the end were read and scored, so the set is complete as of writing but not closed. Since this was written the set closed at 106 files. A later analysis on this page, Who the loop actually closes with, rescored the thirteen that landed late and recounts 71 of 106 closing a loop and nine or ten closing it with a non-expert, against the six or seven in 93 reported here. The extra non-expert loops are the late files plus two formulation and delivery-route changes this pass had read as framing. The shape of the finding is unchanged; the denominators there are the current ones.","method_zh":"本報告中的每一支隊伍都是 Top 10 或特別獎的得主或入圍者，所以這是整個競賽中獲獎最多的那十分之一，不是代表性樣本。「93 支中有 64 支閉合了迴路」要讀成「在會得獎的隊伍裡，閉合迴路是常態」，而不是關於 iGEM 整體的陳述。每一份有 good.ihp 內容的隊伍檔案，都依檔案本身的陳述用四分制評分：要拿 4 分，必須有具名的利害關係人、一句具體說過的話，以及檔案明確連回該意見的建置、部署、讀出、安全設計或商業模式上的改變。只記錄到框架、語言、教育材料或證據包有所改變的隊伍，不論流程被包裝得多華麗，都只得 2 或 3 分，而獎項在整個過程中都不納入考量。這套評分標準無法確認某項改變是因為那個建議而做，還是事後才歸因於它；看不到摘要背後的 wiki；也無法區分一條單薄的因果鏈，和一條厚實因果鏈的單薄書面紀錄。評分進行期間仍持續有檔案送進來；最後存在的 93 份全都讀過並評分，所以這個集合在撰寫時是完整的，但沒有封閉。　本文寫成之後，這個集合在 106 份檔案處封閉。本頁後面的另一項分析〈迴路實際上是跟誰閉合的〉重新評了晚到的那十三份，重新計得 106 份中有 71 份閉合迴路、其中九到十份是與非專業人士閉合，而非本文所報的「93 份中六到七份」。多出來的非專業迴路來自晚到的檔案，再加上兩項配方與投遞途徑的改變——這一輪把它們讀成了框架上的改變。結論的形狀沒有變；該處的分母是目前最新的。","scored":93,"kicker_zh":"原創分析","order":30},{"id":"judging-top10","tab":"judging","order":30,"kicker":"The whole cohort","kicker_zh":"整組十支","title":"The whole High School Top 10, and the three theories it destroys","title_zh":"整個高中組 Top 10，以及它推翻的三個理論","lede":"Reading all ten rather than three kills three tempting explanations, including one argued on this very page. Statistical reporting does not track placing — the team with the most of it won nothing. Registry documentation runs the other way: **the Grand Prize winner has the shortest of all ten.** And \"nominate one clear claim\" is not sufficient either, because the clearest headline among the non-finalists placed nowhere. What does hold is bleaker and more useful: **seven of seven non-podium teams stop at a surrogate for their own stated target, and exactly one team in the ten ever tested a real sample.**","lede_zh":"把十支隊伍一起讀，而不是只讀三支，會殺掉三個誘人的解釋，其中一個還是本頁自己主張過的。統計報告方式與名次無關——報告得最齊全的那支什麼都沒拿。Registry 文件的方向則是反的：**總冠軍的文件是十支裡最短的。** 而「指定一個清楚的主張」也不夠，因為非決賽隊伍中標題最清楚的那一支，什麼名次都沒有。真正撐得住的結論更冷峻，也更有用：**七支非頒獎臺隊伍全部停在自己所宣稱目標的替代物上，而這十支之中，只有一支真正測過真實樣本。**","body":"The three-team comparison above could be accused of fitting a story to one outcome, so the same questions were put to the whole cohort. Six of the ten results pages are server-rendered and were fetched directly; two are client-rendered and were read in a browser; one team has no results page at all. The table below is what a reader can actually check on each.\n\nThree explanations die here. **Statistical reporting**: HongKong-HS carries ANOVA, Dunnett's post-hoc, a t-test, n=3 and standard deviations, and won nothing; the Grand Prize winner names no test and reports no p-value. **Registry documentation**: measured consistently across all ten, the medians run from HKSSC's 23,116 characters per headline part down to Lambert-GA's 670 — the Grand Prize winner last, the runner-up eighth, and the three longest all belonging to parts-prize winners who reached no podium. **And the one-claim theory from the section above**: HangzhouFourteenAP states that a four-enzyme cocktail cut biofilm biomass 57.1% against control with ANOVA F(5,12) = 29.8, p < 0.001 — one sentence, quantified, test named — and took a village award and nothing more.\n\nTwo further sorting theories fail on structure alone. Eton-College-UK reached the Top 10 **with no results page and no parts page**, 24 of its 29 Registry entries being PCR primers. HKSSC placed **on a Silver medal** while the other nine hold Gold. And parts awards do not lead anywhere: GCGS, GHCIS and HKSSC each won one, all three finished outside the podium, and the two finalists won none between them.\n\nWhat survives is a wall rather than a formula. Every one of the seven non-podium teams examined in depth substitutes something convenient for the thing its project is actually about — synthetic trigger RNA for river water, a synthetic oligonucleotide for urine, a tolerance shift for paraben removal, *B. subtilis* for *S. mutans*, a reporter for a therapy — and stops there. **One team in the ten ran its sensor on a real sample, a soil extract, and that team is the 1st Runner-up.** With ten teams and two podium places this cannot carry a causal claim, and it is reported as the one line the podium sits on the right side of.\n\nThe two finalists then reached the slate by routes that do not resemble each other: Lambert-GA on **novelty** — a de novo binder reported as a first, measured by a commercial service, on a project whose other arm has no data — and HongKong-JSS on **depth**, five independent matched runs across 51 treatments with leave-one-run-out re-analyses and a selectivity panel. **GEMS took neither route.** Its novel element showed no light dependence in its own ELISA, with every biological result coming from the constitutive bypass; and its genuine depth, the plant work at p < 0.0001 with 40 seedlings per condition, sits on a protectant the reactor did not make, since the preparation sprayed on the plants was never assayed. That is a more precise and less comfortable answer than the one the section above reaches alone, and it is the one the full cohort supports.","body_zh":"上面那份三隊比較，可能會被質疑是「為一個結果編一個故事」，所以同樣的問題被拿去問整個群體。十份結果頁中有六份是伺服器端渲染、直接抓取；兩份是用戶端渲染，以瀏覽器讀取；還有一支隊伍完全沒有結果頁。下面的表格就是「讀者在每一支身上實際能核對什麼」。\n\n三個解釋在這裡死掉。**統計報告方式**：HongKong-HS 有 ANOVA、Dunnett 事後檢定、t-test、n=3 與標準差，什麼都沒拿；而總冠軍沒有寫出檢定名稱，也沒有 p 值。**Registry 文件**：用一致方式量過全部十支，每個招牌元件的中位數從 HKSSC 的 23,116 字元一路降到 Lambert-GA 的 670——總冠軍最後一名、亞軍第八名，而最長的三支全都是拿了元件獎卻沒上頒獎臺的隊伍。**還有上一節那個「一個主張」的理論**：HangzhouFourteenAP 寫出四酵素複方把生物膜量相對對照降低 57.1%，ANOVA F(5,12) = 29.8、p < 0.001——一句話、有量化、寫出檢定名稱——結果只拿到一個 village 獎，別無其他。\n\n另外兩個排序理論光從結構上就不成立。Eton-College-UK 在**沒有結果頁、也沒有元件頁**的情況下進了 Top 10，而它 29 個 Registry 條目中有 24 個是 PCR 引子。HKSSC 是**以銀牌**進榜，而其他九支都是金牌。元件獎也通不到任何地方：GCGS、GHCIS 與 HKSSC 各拿一個，三支全在頒獎臺之外，而兩支決賽隊伍加起來一個也沒有。\n\n撐下來的不是一個公式，而是一道牆。被深入檢視的七支非頒獎臺隊伍，每一支都用某個方便的東西替代了自己專案真正要處理的東西——用合成觸發 RNA 替代河水、用合成寡核苷酸替代尿液、用耐受度位移替代對羥基苯甲酸酯的移除、用 *B. subtilis* 替代 *S. mutans*、用報告子替代療法——然後就停在那裡。**十支隊伍中只有一支把自己的感測器用在真實樣本上，一份土壤萃取液，而那支隊伍是亞軍。** 十支隊伍、兩個席次，這無法承載因果論述，因此它只被當成「頒獎臺站在正確一側」的那一條線來報告。\n\n而兩支決賽隊伍進入名單的路徑，彼此並不相像：Lambert-GA 靠的是**新穎性**——一個從頭設計的結合分子，被報告為首例，量測由商業服務完成，而這個專案的另一支沒有任何資料；HongKong-JSS 靠的是**深度**——五組獨立配對試驗、涵蓋 51 個處理，附逐一剔除整組的重分析與選擇性測試。**GEMS 兩條路都沒走。** 它新穎的那個元素，在它自己的 ELISA 裡沒有顯示光依賴性，所有生物學成果都來自組成型旁路；而它真正的深度——每組 40 棵幼苗、p < 0.0001 的植物工作——建立在一份並非反應器做出來的保護蛋白上，因為噴到植物上的那份製備從未被檢測活性。這個答案比上一節單獨得到的更精確、也更不舒服，而它是整個群體的證據所支持的那一個。","cards":[{"kicker":"The wall","kicker_zh":"那道牆","title":"Seven of seven non-podium teams stop at a surrogate, and not one tested a real sample","title_zh":"七支非頒獎臺隊伍全部停在替代物上，沒有一支測過真實樣本","body":"This is the strongest pattern in the cohort, and it is not about the podium — it is about everyone else. GHCIS built a field water-monitoring tool whose only analyte has ever been its own synthetic trigger RNA at micromolar concentrations, three to six orders of magnitude from use. HongKong-HS built a home urine test that has never touched urine, demonstrating a floor of 100 nM synthetic oligonucleotide — roughly a million-fold above urinary miRNA. HKSSC claims paraben removal and measures a tolerance shift instead; its HPLC produced chromatograms and no quantification. GCGS built a sensor and an effector that both work and never joined them. HFI's premise experiment is labelled \"ns, not significant\" in its own figure legend. HangzhouFourteenAP used *B. subtilis* as a stand-in for *S. mutans*, one dose, once. Eton tested one protease at two concentrations, with no results page to gather it.\n\n**HongKong-JSS is the only team in the ten that ran its sensor on a real sample** — a soil extract — and it is on the podium. That is not proof of a mechanism, with ten teams and two podium places. But it is the one line on the table that the podium sits on the right side of.","body_zh":"這是整個群體裡最強的模式，而它談的不是頒獎臺，而是其他所有人。GHCIS 做了一個現地水質監測工具，而它的分析對象至今只有自己合成的觸發 RNA，濃度在微莫耳等級，距離實際使用相差三到六個數量級。HongKong-HS 做了一個居家尿液檢測，卻從未碰過尿液，所展示的下限是 100 nM 的合成寡核苷酸——大約比尿中 miRNA 高出一百萬倍。HKSSC 聲稱要移除對羥基苯甲酸酯，實際量到的卻是耐受度的位移；它的 HPLC 只產出層析圖，沒有定量。GCGS 做出了一個感測器和一個效應器，兩個都能動，卻從未接起來。HFI 檢驗自身前提的那個實驗，在它自己的圖說上被標成「ns，不顯著」。HangzhouFourteenAP 用 *B. subtilis* 代替 *S. mutans*，單一劑量、施用一次。Eton 測了一種蛋白酶的兩個濃度，而且沒有結果頁可以把它收攏起來。\n\n**HongKong-JSS 是這十支裡唯一把自己的感測器用在真實樣本上的隊伍**——一份土壤萃取液——而它在頒獎臺上。十支隊伍、兩個頒獎臺席次，這不足以證明因果。但它是這張表上唯一一條「頒獎臺站在正確一側」的線。","chips":["7 of 7 stop at a surrogate","1 of 10 tested a real sample"],"chips_zh":["7 支全部停在替代物","10 支中 1 支測過真實樣本"]},{"kicker":"Two routes","kicker_zh":"兩條路","title":"The two finalists got there by different routes, and GEMS took neither","title_zh":"兩支決賽隊伍走的是不同的路，而 GEMS 兩條都沒走","body":"There is no single podium formula in this cohort, because the two finalists do not resemble each other. **Lambert-GA's route is novelty**: a de novo designed minibinder reported as the first confirmed to bind its viral target, measured by a commercial service, on a project whose other arm has no data at all and whose results page carries no statistics. **HongKong-JSS's route is depth**: five independent matched runs across 51 treatments, paired statistics, two leave-one-run-out re-analyses, a selectivity panel against three competing metals, and the only real-sample trial in the ten — on a project that openly refuses to call its headline number a limit of detection.\n\nOne team was rewarded for doing something nobody had done; the other for proving a modest thing to a standard nobody else reached. **GEMS has neither.** Its novel element, green-light control of *B. subtilis*, showed no light dependence in its own ELISA, and every biological result came from the constitutive bypass. Its depth is real in the plant work but sits on an input the reactor did not make — the preparation sprayed on the plants was never assayed, and the chain was never run end to end. The two available routes to a finalist slate were novelty and depth, and ReLEAF's novelty is unevidenced while its depth is on the wrong link.","body_zh":"這個群體裡沒有單一的頒獎臺公式，因為兩支決賽隊伍彼此並不相像。**Lambert-GA 走的是新穎性**：一個從頭設計的 minibinder，被報告為首次確認能結合其病毒標的，量測由商業服務完成；而這個專案的另一支完全沒有資料，結果頁上也沒有任何統計。**HongKong-JSS 走的是深度**：五組獨立配對試驗、涵蓋 51 個處理、配對統計、兩次逐一剔除整組的重分析、對三種競爭金屬的選擇性測試，以及十支隊伍中唯一的真實樣本試驗——而這個專案公開拒絕把自己的招牌數字稱為偵測極限。\n\n一支隊伍因為做了沒人做過的事而被獎勵；另一支因為把一件樸素的事證明到沒人達到的標準而被獎勵。**GEMS 兩者都沒有。** 它新穎的那個元素，*B. subtilis* 的綠光控制，在它自己的 ELISA 裡沒有顯示光依賴性，而所有生物學成果都來自組成型旁路。它的深度在植物工作上是真的，但那建立在一個不是反應器做出來的投入上——噴到植物上的那份製備從未被檢測活性，鏈條也從未端到端跑過。通往決賽席位的兩條路是新穎性與深度，而 ReLEAF 的新穎性沒有證據，它的深度長在錯的那一環上。","chips":["Lambert: novelty","HongKong-JSS: depth","GEMS: neither"],"chips_zh":["Lambert：新穎性","HongKong-JSS：深度","GEMS：兩者皆無"]},{"kicker":"Theory killed","kicker_zh":"被推翻的理論","title":"\"Nominate one claim\" is not sufficient either — the clearest headline of the seven placed nowhere","title_zh":"「指定一個主張」也不夠——七支裡標題最清楚的那一支什麼名次都沒有","body":"The three-team comparison on this page argues that the finalists each resolve into one repeatable sentence while GEMS publishes five key results. That holds for those three. **It does not survive the other seven.** HangzhouFourteenAP has the single clearest headline in the non-podium group: a four-enzyme cocktail cut residual biofilm biomass by **57.1%** against a PBS control, with ANOVA F(5,12) = 29.8, p < 0.001, n = 3, and each single-enzyme omission significantly worse. That is one sentence, quantified, with a statistical test named. It won a village award and nothing else. GCGS states a limit of detection of **53.1 nM** C4-HSL with a fitted line and R² = 0.894. HKSSC reports its enzyme beating a commercial esterase by **2.09×** at equal mass, defended through a cascade from two-way ANOVA to Brown-Forsythe to Welch with Holm correction.\n\nSo having one legible claim is not what buys a placing. **What those three claims have in common is that each is a claim about a surrogate** — an artificial calculus model, a synthetic signalling molecule, a model ester. The sentence was clear; the thing it was about was not the thing the project was for.","body_zh":"本頁的三隊比較主張：兩支決賽隊伍各自收斂成一句可複述的話，而 GEMS 發表了五個重點成果。對那三支來說成立。**但它撐不過其他七支的檢驗。** HangzhouFourteenAP 在非頒獎臺群體裡擁有最清楚的單一標題：四酵素複方把殘餘生物膜量相對 PBS 對照降低了 **57.1%**，ANOVA F(5,12) = 29.8、p < 0.001、n = 3，而且每一個單酵素缺項的表現都顯著更差。那就是一句話、有量化、還寫出了檢定名稱。它拿到一個 village 獎，其他什麼都沒有。GCGS 寫出 C4-HSL 的偵測極限 **53.1 nM**，附擬合直線與 R² = 0.894。HKSSC 報告它的酵素在等質量下比商用酯酶高 **2.09 倍**，並以 two-way ANOVA 到 Brown-Forsythe 再到 Welch 加 Holm 校正的一整串檢定來防守。\n\n所以「有一個清楚可讀的主張」並不是換到名次的東西。**那三個主張的共同點是：每一個都是關於替代物的主張**——一個人工牙垢模型、一個合成訊號分子、一個模型酯類。句子是清楚的；但句子講的那個東西，不是這個專案存在的理由。","chips":["57.1%, F(5,12)=29.8, p<0.001","clear sentence, surrogate subject"],"chips_zh":["57.1%、F(5,12)=29.8、p<0.001","句子清楚，主詞是替代物"]},{"kicker":"Documentation","kicker_zh":"文件","title":"The Grand Prize winner has the shortest Registry documentation of all ten","title_zh":"總冠軍的 Registry 文件是十支裡最短的","body":"Measured consistently — total documentation payload across design, experiment, characterisation and discussion sections, six headline parts per team — the medians run: **HKSSC 23,116 · HFI 17,493 · GCGS 14,763 · GEMS-Taiwan 8,644 · HangzhouFourteenAP 7,786 · HongKong-HS 4,944 · HongKong-JSS 2,606 · GHCIS 1,969 · Eton 1,903 · Lambert-GA 670.** The Grand Prize winner is last; the 1st Runner-up is eighth. The longest belong to the three teams that won parts prizes and reached no podium — HKSSC's Best New Basic Part alone carries 50,189 characters.\n\n**Long Registry documentation buys a parts prize, not a placing.** It is still the right thing to write, because it is the one artefact that outlives the season and the only way a stranger can reuse the work. But it should be budgeted as a contribution rather than as a bid for the podium. One warning for anyone repeating this measurement: the short `description` field is a different quantity from the documentation payload and is not a proxy for it — HKSSC's best part has a 265-character description and 50,189 characters of documentation.","body_zh":"用一致的方式量測——每隊取六個招牌元件，把 design、experiment、characterisation、discussion 各段落的文件內容加總——中位數依序是：**HKSSC 23,116 · HFI 17,493 · GCGS 14,763 · GEMS-Taiwan 8,644 · HangzhouFourteenAP 7,786 · HongKong-HS 4,944 · HongKong-JSS 2,606 · GHCIS 1,969 · Eton 1,903 · Lambert-GA 670。** 總冠軍是最後一名；亞軍第八。最長的屬於那三支拿了元件獎、卻沒上頒獎臺的隊伍——HKSSC 的 Best New Basic Part 單一元件就有 50,189 字元。\n\n**長篇的 Registry 文件換得的是元件獎，不是名次。** 它仍然該寫，因為那是唯一比賽季活得更久的產物，也是陌生人能重複利用這份工作的唯一途徑。但它應該被當成一項貢獻來編列預算，不是當成爭取頒獎臺的投注。給任何想重複這個量測的人一個警告：簡短的 `description` 欄位與文件內容總長是兩個不同的量，不能互相代用——HKSSC 最好的那個元件，description 只有 265 字元，文件內容卻有 50,189 字元。","chips":["Lambert last of ten: 670","HKSSC first: 23,116"],"chips_zh":["Lambert 十支中最後：670","HKSSC 第一：23,116"]},{"kicker":"The inversion","kicker_zh":"反轉","title":"Statistical reporting does not track placing either","title_zh":"統計報告方式同樣與名次無關","body":"**HongKong-HS reports ANOVA, Dunnett's post-hoc, a t-test, n=3 and standard deviations — and won nothing at all.** HKSSC defends its headline through two-way ANOVA, a Brown-Forsythe test and Welch with Holm correction, and won one parts award on a Silver medal. The **Grand Prize winner names no statistical test, reports no p-value and gives no replicate count**; its single quantitative claim is a confidence interval produced by a commercial service. Five of the ten publish no p-value anywhere, and only four name any test.\n\nThis reproduces the measurement-discipline null from elsewhere in this report (27% against 29% across all 106 decorated teams) inside a cohort of ten. The distinction worth keeping is between **reporting machinery and replication depth**: HongKong-HS has the machinery on n=3 in buffer, while HongKong-JSS has five independent matched runs on a real extract. **Only the second kind appears to travel.**","body_zh":"**HongKong-HS 報告了 ANOVA、Dunnett 事後檢定、t-test、n=3 與標準差——結果什麼都沒拿。** HKSSC 用 two-way ANOVA、Brown-Forsythe 檢定，以及加上 Holm 校正的 Welch 來防守它的招牌結果，以銀牌拿下一個元件獎。而**總冠軍沒有寫出任何統計檢定名稱、沒有任何 p 值、也沒有任何重複數**；它唯一的量化主張是一個由商業服務做出來的信賴區間。十支隊伍中有五支完全沒有 p 值，只有四支寫出任何檢定名稱。\n\n這把本報告別處那個「量測嚴謹度」的虛無結果（全部 106 支得獎隊伍中 27% 對 29%）在十支隊伍的群體裡再現了一次。值得保留的區分是**報告的機械裝置**與**重複的深度**之間的差別：HongKong-HS 在緩衝液裡用 n=3 配上整套裝置，而 HongKong-JSS 是在真實萃取液上做了五組獨立配對試驗。**看起來只有後面那一種會傳遞出去。**","chips":["most machinery, 0 awards","Grand Prize: 0 tests"],"chips_zh":["裝置最齊全，0 個獎","總冠軍：0 個檢定"]},{"kicker":"Best Model","kicker_zh":"最佳模型","title":"One award maps onto the finalist slate exactly, and it is Best Model","title_zh":"有一個獎項與決賽名單完全對應，而那是最佳模型","body":"Across the ten, Best Model recognition lands on exactly the two finalists and nobody else: Lambert-GA won Best Model (High School), HongKong-JSS was nominated, and no other team in the Top 10 appears in that category. By contrast Best Hardware and Best Measurement both went to a team that did not reach the podium.\n\nThe caveat is real and should be read before the finding: **this is an award predicting an award**, judged partly by the same kind of panel, so it is close to circular, and with ten teams and two slots a clean binary split can arise by luck. Still, it is the only award-level signal in the cohort that lines up 2 for 2, and it points somewhere plausible — a model is where a team has to state what it predicts and then be held to it. Two of the seven non-podium teams examined have **no modelling page at all**; both `/gcgs/model` and `/hongkong-hs/model` return 404. GEMS has a substantial model page, and it is the page that publishes the 68-year payback beside its own 4.9-year figure.","body_zh":"在這十支隊伍中，最佳模型的肯定恰好落在兩支決賽隊伍身上，其他人都沒有：Lambert-GA 拿下最佳模型（高中組），HongKong-JSS 入圍，而 Top 10 裡沒有其他隊伍出現在這個類別。相對地，最佳硬體與最佳量測都頒給了一支沒有進頒獎臺的隊伍。\n\n這裡有一個真實的保留，而且應該先讀它再讀結論：**這是「用一個獎預測另一個獎」**，評審組成部分相近，所以接近循環論證；而十支隊伍、兩個席次，一個乾淨的二分完全可能是運氣。但它仍是這個群體裡唯一 2 比 2 完全對上的獎項層級訊號，而它指向的地方是說得通的——模型正是一支隊伍必須寫下「我預測什麼」並為此負責的地方。被檢視的七支非頒獎臺隊伍中，有兩支**完全沒有模型頁**；`/gcgs/model` 與 `/hongkong-hs/model` 都回傳 404。GEMS 有一個紮實的模型頁，而那正是公開「68 年回本期」與自家「4.9 年」並列的那一頁。","chips":["2 of 2 finalists","an award predicting an award"],"chips_zh":["2 席決賽全中","用獎預測獎"]},{"kicker":"No results page","kicker_zh":"沒有結果頁","title":"Eton-College-UK reached the Top 10 without a results page","title_zh":"Eton-College-UK 在沒有結果頁的情況下進了 Top 10","body":"Eton's wiki has description, contribution, implementation, engineering, protocols, notebook, model, three modelling sub-pages, hardware, human practices, education, a game, team and attributions. **It has no results page**, and no parts page either, while 24 of its 29 Registry submissions are PCR primers. Its device claim rests on one protease at two concentrations, and its own text reports failed self-assembled-monolayer formation on some runs and large sensor-to-sensor variation.\n\nIt is also **the most transparent team of the ten** on criterion 6, stating plainly that it had no access to suitable labs and secured two weeks of bought time at the University of Greenwich and King's College London, and publishing a named adult's follow-up gel as a figure. Neither the missing pages nor the candour moved it. Alongside GCGS reaching the Top 10 with no model page, the lesson is that **the Top 10 is not a documentation score** — but a missing claim is not survivable in the way a missing page is.","body_zh":"Eton 的 wiki 有 description、contribution、implementation、engineering、protocols、notebook、model、三個模型子頁、hardware、human practices、education、一個遊戲、team 與 attributions。**它沒有結果頁**，也沒有元件頁，而它 29 個 Registry 送交項目中有 24 個是 PCR 引子。它的裝置主張建立在一種蛋白酶的兩個濃度上，而它自己的文字也記載了某些批次自組裝單層形成失敗，以及感測器之間差異很大。\n\n它同時是這十支隊伍中**在第 6 題上最透明的一支**，明白寫出自己沒有合適的實驗室可用，因而在 University of Greenwich 與 King's College London 買了兩週的實驗室時間，並把一位具名成年人後續補做的膠體圖當成一張圖發表。缺少的頁面沒有拖累它，坦白也沒有幫到它。再加上 GCGS 在沒有模型頁的情況下進了 Top 10，這裡的教訓是：**Top 10 不是一個文件評分**——但「缺少一個主張」不像「缺少一個頁面」那樣活得下去。","chips":["no results page, still Top 10","24 of 29 parts are primers"],"chips_zh":["沒有結果頁，照樣 Top 10","29 個元件中 24 個是引子"]},{"kicker":"Attributions","kicker_zh":"貢獻揭露","title":"Six of seven non-podium teams disclose nothing usable about who did the work","title_zh":"七支非頒獎臺隊伍中有六支，對「誰做了這些工作」沒有提供任何可用的揭露","body":"HangzhouFourteenAP's attributions page is the **unedited iGEM template**. GCGS, GHCIS and HongKong-HS have no attributions page at all. HKSSC's points off-wiki. HFI's is an empty iframe. Only Eton gives a reader anything to work with, and Eton is the most forthcoming team in the cohort.\n\nThis matters because question 6 asks how much of the work the team did itself, and a judge can only answer from what is published. **Both finalists published detailed, in some places unflattering, attributions** — HongKong-JSS disclosing that it did no cloning at all and that its supervisor prepared every mercury solution, Lambert disclosing that a commercial service produced, ran and interpreted the measurement its Grand Prize rests on. Neither was punished. **The pattern across the ten is that disclosure is free and silence is not obviously rewarded** — and for GEMS, whose own attributions page credits an advisor with designing the bioreactor and photometer from idea generation through CAD modelling, the lesson is that the exposure comes from what there is to disclose, not from disclosing it.","body_zh":"HangzhouFourteenAP 的 attributions 頁是**未經編輯的 iGEM 範本**。GCGS、GHCIS 與 HongKong-HS 完全沒有 attributions 頁。HKSSC 的連到站外。HFI 的是一個空的 iframe。只有 Eton 給了讀者一些可用的東西，而 Eton 是這個群體裡最坦白的隊伍。\n\n這件事重要，因為第 6 題問的是「多少工作是團隊自己做的」，而評審只能依據已公開的內容回答。**兩支決賽隊伍都發表了詳細、在某些地方並不好看的 attributions**——HongKong-JSS 揭露它完全沒有做選殖、所有汞溶液都由指導老師配製；Lambert 揭露那個支撐其總冠軍的量測，是由一家商業服務製備、執行並解讀的。兩者都沒有因此被懲罰。**十支隊伍的模式是：揭露是免費的，而沉默也沒有明顯被獎勵**——而對 GEMS 來說，它自己的 attributions 頁把生物反應器與光度計「從構想到 CAD 建模」的設計記在一位顧問名下；這裡的教訓是，暴露來自「有什麼要揭露」，不是來自「去揭露它」。","chips":["6 of 7 unusable","both finalists disclosed in detail"],"chips_zh":["7 支中 6 支無法使用","兩支決賽隊伍都詳細揭露"]}],"table":{"head":["Team","Placing","Named test","p-values","Replicates","Real sample?","Stops at"],"head_zh":["隊伍","名次","檢定名稱","p 值","重複數","真實樣本？","停在哪裡"],"rows":[["Lambert-GA","Grand Prize","none","none","n=2 (outsourced)","No","Nothing tested against intact virus, bee cells or a bee; RNAi arm has no knockdown data"],["HongKong-JSS","1st Runner-up","paired two-sided t-test","0.0080, 0.0346","5 matched runs, 51 treatments","**Yes** — soil extract","Extraction platform never fed the biosensor"],["GEMS-Taiwan","Top 10","none","five","n=1 and n=3","Plants, not the reactor's output","Chain never run end to end; the preparation sprayed on plants was never assayed"],["HKSSC","Top 10","two-way ANOVA, Brown-Forsythe, Welch/Holm","five, incl. exact","not stated","No","Claims paraben removal and never measures it; HPLC gave chromatograms, no quantification"],["HongKong-HS","Top 10","ANOVA, Dunnett, t-test","three","n=3","No","100 nM synthetic oligo in buffer; never touched urine"],["HFI","Top 10","none","four","not stated","No","Premise experiment labelled \"ns, not significant\" in its own figure"],["GCGS","Top 10","none","none","not stated","No","Sensor and effector both work and were never joined"],["GHCIS","Top 10","none","none","not stated","No","Only ever its own synthetic trigger RNA, at micromolar"],["HangzhouFourteenAP","Top 10","ANOVA F(5,12)=29.8","p<0.001","n=3","No","Surrogate organism, single application, no mineral-phase measurement"],["Eton-College-UK","Top 10","none","none","not stated","No","One protease at two concentrations; no results page at all"]],"rows_zh":[["Lambert-GA","總冠軍","無","無","n=2（外部代做）","否","從未對完整病毒、蜜蜂細胞或一隻蜜蜂做測試；RNAi 那一支沒有剔除資料"],["HongKong-JSS","亞軍","paired two-sided t-test","0.0080、0.0346","5 組配對試驗、51 個處理","**是**——土壤萃取液","萃取平台從未餵進生物感測器"],["GEMS-Taiwan","Top 10","無","五個","n=1 與 n=3","有植物，但不是反應器的產物","鏈條從未端到端跑過；噴到植物上的那份製備從未被檢測活性"],["HKSSC","Top 10","two-way ANOVA、Brown-Forsythe、Welch/Holm","五個，含精確值","未說明","否","聲稱移除對羥基苯甲酸酯卻從未量過；HPLC 只給了層析圖，沒有定量"],["HongKong-HS","Top 10","ANOVA、Dunnett、t-test","三個","n=3","否","緩衝液中 100 nM 合成寡核苷酸；從未碰過尿液"],["HFI","Top 10","無","四個","未說明","否","檢驗自身前提的那個實驗，在它自己的圖說上被標成「ns，不顯著」"],["GCGS","Top 10","無","無","未說明","否","感測器與效應器都能動，但從未接起來"],["GHCIS","Top 10","無","無","未說明","否","至今只見過自己合成的觸發 RNA，而且是微莫耳濃度"],["HangzhouFourteenAP","Top 10","ANOVA F(5,12)=29.8","p<0.001","n=3","否","替代生物、單次施用、沒有礦物相的量測"],["Eton-College-UK","Top 10","無","無","未說明","否","一種蛋白酶、兩個濃度；完全沒有結果頁"]]},"checklist":["Before anything else in 2027, decide what the real sample is and get hold of it early. One team in ten tested one, and it is the only team on the right side of that line.","Pick a route deliberately: novelty, or depth on something modest. Lambert took the first, HongKong-JSS the second, and trying for both without finishing either is how GEMS spent 2026.","Make the novel element the one you validate hardest. If the light-gated device cannot beat the constitutive control, the project is not an optogenetics project, and that should be settled in week six.","Do not build the plan around out-rigouring the field. The team with the most statistical machinery in this section won nothing; depth of replication on a real matrix is the kind that appears to travel.","Budget Registry documentation as a contribution that outlives the season, not as a bid for a placing. The Grand Prize winner has the shortest in the cohort.","Write a real attributions page. Six of seven non-podium teams publish nothing usable, both finalists disclosed heavily and neither was punished for it.","Then ask one stranger the only question that matters: after two minutes on this wiki, what did this project achieve, and on what?"],"checklist_zh":["2027 年在做任何其他事之前，先決定「真實樣本」是什麼，並且及早把它弄到手。十支隊伍裡只有一支測過真實樣本，而那是唯一站在這條線正確一側的隊伍。","刻意選一條路：新穎性，或是在一件樸素的事上做到深度。Lambert 選了前者，HongKong-JSS 選了後者；兩邊都想要、兩邊都沒做完，正是 GEMS 2026 年的過法。","讓新穎的那個元素成為你驗證得最用力的一個。如果光控裝置贏不過組成型對照組，這個專案就不是光遺傳學專案，而這件事應該在第六週就定案。","不要把計畫建立在「比全場更嚴謹」上。這一組統計裝置最齊全的隊伍什麼都沒拿；真正會傳遞出去的，是在真實基質上的重複深度。","把 Registry 文件當成一項比賽季活得更久的貢獻來編預算，不是當成爭取名次的投注。總冠軍的文件是整組最短的。","寫一份真正的 attributions 頁。七支非頒獎臺隊伍中有六支沒有提供任何可用的內容，而兩支決賽隊伍都大量揭露，也都沒有因此被懲罰。","然後去問一個陌生人唯一重要的那個問題：在這個 wiki 上待兩分鐘之後，這個專案達成了什麼，又是在什麼東西上達成的？"],"method":"Results pages for GCGS, GHCIS, HFI, HKSSC, HongKong-HS and Lambert-GA are server-rendered and were fetched directly with curl and a browser User-Agent; Eton-College-UK's and HangzhouFourteenAP's wikis are client-rendered and were read in a browser; Eton has no results page, so its row describes an absence. Counts of named tests, p-values, replicate counts and dispersion measures come from stripping tags from each page and matching whole words, so a test named only inside a figure image, a PDF or a collapsed panel is invisible to this method, and roughly a third of 2026 wikis do hide content in click-to-open panels — these are floors, not totals. Registry figures are total documentation payload from /v1/parts/{uuid}/documentation, summed across design, experiment, characterisation and discussion sections, for six headline parts per team, 58 parts in all; the short description field is a separate quantity and is not a proxy for it, so the two are never compared here. The API throttles to HTTP 429 with retry-after values up to about 500 seconds, so the remaining accessions are recorded as unresolved rather than estimated. \"Stops at\" is each team's own account of its limit wherever one is published, and otherwise the furthest point its results actually reach; it is a reading of the published record, not a judgement of the science. The Best Model observation is an award predicting an award and is close to circular; with ten teams and two podium places, any binary split has a fair chance of lining up by luck, and no causal claim is made from it. Question 9, on the live judging session, is excluded throughout this tab because it leaves no public record, and part of what separated these teams may well have happened there. GEMS-Taiwan is the report author's own team and is scored on the same lines as the other nine.","method_zh":"GCGS、GHCIS、HFI、HKSSC、HongKong-HS 與 Lambert-GA 的結果頁是伺服器端渲染，以 curl 搭配瀏覽器 User-Agent 直接取得；Eton-College-UK 與 HangzhouFourteenAP 的 wiki 是用戶端渲染，以瀏覽器讀取；Eton 沒有結果頁，因此它那一列描述的是「缺少」。檢定名稱、p 值、重複數與離散度的計數，是把每一頁去除標籤後以完整字詞比對而得，因此若某個檢定名稱只出現在圖片、PDF 或折疊面板裡，這個方法就看不到它；而 2026 年大約三分之一的 wiki 確實把內容藏在點擊展開的面板中——這些是下界，不是總數。Registry 的數字是 /v1/parts/{uuid}/documentation 的文件內容總長，涵蓋 design、experiment、characterisation、discussion 各段落，每隊取六個招牌元件，共 58 個元件；簡短的 description 欄位是另一個量，不能代用，因此本頁從不把兩者相比。該 API 會節流到 HTTP 429，retry-after 可達約 500 秒，因此其餘編號記為未取得，而非推估。「停在哪裡」一欄，凡團隊自己公開寫明其限制者即採用其說法，否則採用其結果實際達到的最遠點；這是對公開紀錄的閱讀，不是對科學本身的評判。最佳模型那項觀察是「用一個獎預測另一個獎」，接近循環論證；十支隊伍、兩個頒獎臺席次，任何二分都有相當機率是運氣對上的，因此不由它導出任何因果主張。第 9 題關於現場問答，在本頁全程排除，因為它沒有留下公開紀錄，而把這些隊伍分開的因素，很可能有一部分正發生在那裡。GEMS-Taiwan 是本報告作者自己的團隊，與其他九支以相同標準評分。"},{"id":"taiwan-cohort","tab":"teams","kicker":"Original analysis","title":"Taiwan at iGEM 2026","title_zh":"台灣在 2026 年 iGEM","lede":"Taiwan fielded thirteen competing teams in 2026 and won six awards, more than any territory in East Asia except China, but every technical award came from the high-school tier and the island is invisible in parts, software and collegiate modelling.","lede_zh":"台灣在 2026 年派出十三支參賽隊伍，拿下六項得獎，是東亞除中國之外最多的，但每一項技術類獎項都來自高中組，而台灣在零件、軟體和大專組建模這三塊完全看不到身影。","body":"Taiwan registered fifteen entries with iGEM in 2026 and thirteen of them competed — eight high-school, four undergraduate, one overgraduate — returning **eight golds, five silvers and no bronzes**, one Top 10 place, six outright award wins and seven further nominations. The wins were GEMS-Taiwan's Best Measurement, Best Hardware and Best Integrated Human Practices, Labi-Taiwan's peer-voted iGEMers Prize, NYCU-Taiwan's Best Project Promotion Video and NCKU-Tainan's Best Infectious Diseases Project; the nominations added Mingdao for Model, NCKU-Tainan for Hardware, NTHU for Food & Nutrition, Labi-Taiwan for Measurement, and GEMS-Taiwan for Presentation, Wiki and Best Village Project. Against the region that is strong in volume and weak in altitude: China fielded 176 competing teams for 24 wins and five Top 10 places, Hong Kong 16 for three wins, three Top 10 places and the high-school Grand Prize first runner-up in HongKong-JSS, Japan seven for nine nominations and no wins, Korea six for none and Singapore four for none. Taiwan therefore out-won Hong Kong six to three on fewer teams and was the only territory outside China to win more than once, but it took a single Top 10 and placed nothing in any Grand Prize at any tier.\n\nThe strength is **instrumentation**: six of the thirteen teams built and documented a device — GEMS-Taiwan's hollow-fibre perfusion bioreactor and two in-line photometers, NCKU-Tainan's CAPTURE-Screen fluorescence reader at US$54–161 against the US$3,500 open-source plate reader it substitutes, NTHU's four-channel frequency-tagged reader with digital lock-in detection, NTHU Taiwan's open-source moving-bed biofilm reactor, Mingdao's single-frame fermentor and Labi-Taiwan's portable electrochemical reader — with human practices and communication a clear second, carrying three of the six wins. The weakness is just as sharply defined: **not one Taiwanese nomination in any of the four parts awards, and none in Best Software**, where even Hong Kong managed one through HK-Joint-School, despite GEMS-Taiwan, NCKU-Tainan and NYCU-Taiwan all releasing licensed code; Best Model appears once, at high-school level, for Mingdao; and the collegiate tier produced no technical special award at all, NYCU-Taiwan's win being a video and NCKU-Tainan's a village category. The clearest symptom is NTHU Taiwan's CatharSys, whose four models dropped a screening factor on a predicted 6% separation, reversed an enzyme-engineering plan when formaldehyde was projected to five times chassis tolerance, stated a falsifiable prediction before the build and reversed a nozzle geometry on first-principles hydraulics — and which won a gold medal and nothing else.\n\nGEMS-Taiwan's three wins and Top 10 place are the island's best result of the year, and they were earned on provenance rather than biology: an input ledger marking every number measured, cited or modelled, a growth rate pre-registered on 1 October and later scored at 0.286 ± 0.010 h⁻¹, and an autoencoder that named a failing photometer 26.7 hours before the channel died. Measured against the collegiate Top 10 sections the dry lab is thin in four named places — there is no inferential statistics, the central secreted-activity figure standing at **n = 1, 7.25 mU/mL, below quantitation** with two induction runs disagreeing on the sign, where NCKU-Tainan a tier up fits mixed models with plate as a random intercept and holds out a treatment to predict; the entire control architecture rests on a published CcaSR Hill curve assumed valid at 20 L although every induction ran at a single light intensity, so nothing in the project tests its own transfer function; the digital twin is an admitted digital shadow, replaying recorded runs with a person making every decision and green-light induction not integrated; and the economics are negative on the team's own numbers, 68 years to payback at perfect efficacy against a partner's 4.9. The step up needs depth in three places rather than more scope: replication and intervals on the central claim with a pre-registered **effect size** rather than a pre-registered growth rate; an in-house CcaSR dose–response across light intensities and scales in absolute fluorescein-calibrated units, which would simultaneously turn 35 contributed SubtiToolKit parts into a collection with the transfer curves a parts award actually rewards; and a twin that controls a run instead of replaying one, with one external software user whose complaints are written down.\n\nThe collaboration map begins with an uncomfortable fact: **GEMS-Taiwan is not in the island's network**. NYCU-Taiwan hosted the 2026 Taiwan iGEMers Meet-Up at its Bo-Ai campus on 27 July for 53 students and advisors from NYCU-Taiwan, NCKU-Tainan, HIA-Taiwan, VIS and WIST, and NCKU-Tainan's collaboration page adds Mingdao, CCU-Taiwan and NTHU — while neither GEMS-Taiwan nor Labi-Taiwan appears on either list and the GEMS wiki carries no collaboration page at all. The partners therefore follow from complementarity, not goodwill: NTHU Taiwan shares the *Bacillus subtilis* chassis and the open-hardware habit, NCKU-Tainan holds the statistics and the cheap reader, CCU-Taiwan works the rice leafroller on the same crop and the same island, NTHU's AeroSense group has the cohort's deepest computation and admits its decoder was validated on external metal-oxide sensor datasets rather than its own cells, Labi-Taiwan is the only other high-school programme with a real computational stack, and NYCU-Taiwan convenes.\n\nTaiwan's state-backed push is manufacturing-led — the Taiwan Bio-Manufacturing Corporation broke ground on a 15,000 m² GMP facility in Hsinchu Biomedical Science Park in June 2025 with operations from Q2 2026 including Taiwan's first GMP mRNA capability, biomedicine sits inside the 5+2 Innovative Industries Plan, a 33-company delegation went to BIO 2026, and this research found no Taiwan-specific synthetic-biology design programme or funding figure at all. Singapore and Israel are funding precisely that missing layer, with DayOne launching Singapore's first biological data centre prototype in August 2026 and Israel's Innovation Authority committing roughly NIS 70 million in July 2026 to national infrastructure for AI models built on biological data. The 2026 cohort is both the evidence of the gap and the evidence that it can be filled: thirteen teams, six instruments built, zero parts nominations, zero software nominations. GEMS should position itself as Taiwan's dry-lab pipeline rather than as a smaller wet lab, and say so to the Biotechnology and Pharmaceutical Industries Promotion Office and the Ministry of Economic Affairs with Singapore and Israel named as the comparison, to TBMC in Hsinchu as it ramps twenty minutes from NYCU and both NTHU teams, and to the Industrial Technology Research Institute, where NTHU Taiwan already holds a working relationship GEMS would not have to build from scratch.","body_zh":"台灣在 2026 年向 iGEM 註冊了十五個隊伍，其中十三支實際參賽——八支高中、四支大學、一支研究生——拿回**八金、五銀、零銅**、一個 Top 10 席次、六項正式得獎和另外七項入圍。得獎的是 GEMS-Taiwan 的最佳量測、最佳硬體和最佳整合式人類實踐，Labi-Taiwan 由各隊互投的 iGEMers Prize，NYCU-Taiwan 的最佳專案推廣影片，以及 NCKU-Tainan 的最佳傳染病專案；入圍再加上 Mingdao 的模型、NCKU-Tainan 的硬體、NTHU 的食品與營養、Labi-Taiwan 的量測，以及 GEMS-Taiwan 的簡報、Wiki 和最佳 Village 專案。對比這個量大但高度不足的區域：中國派出 176 支參賽隊伍，換得 24 項得獎和五個 Top 10 席次；香港 16 支，換得三項得獎、三個 Top 10 席次，以及 HongKong-JSS 的高中組總冠軍第一亞軍；日本七支，換得九項入圍、零得獎；韓國六支和新加坡四支都掛零。因此台灣以較少的隊伍數，在得獎數上以六比三勝過香港，也是中國以外唯一贏超過一次的地區，但只拿到一個 Top 10，在任何組別的總冠軍都沒有名次。\n\n強項是**儀器**：十三支隊伍中有六支做出並記錄了一台裝置——GEMS-Taiwan 的中空纖維灌流生物反應器和兩台在線光度計、NCKU-Tainan 售價 54 到 161 美元的 CAPTURE-Screen 螢光讀取器（它取代的開放原始碼盤式讀取器要 3,500 美元）、NTHU 帶數位鎖相偵測的四通道頻率標記讀取器、NTHU Taiwan 的開放原始碼移動床生物膜反應器、Mingdao 的單機架發酵槽，以及 Labi-Taiwan 的攜帶式電化學讀取器——人類實踐與溝通明顯是第二強項，拿下六項得獎中的三項。弱項同樣界線分明：**四個零件類獎項沒有任何一項有台灣隊伍入圍，最佳軟體也沒有**，而連香港都靠 HK-Joint-School 拿到一個入圍，儘管 GEMS-Taiwan、NCKU-Tainan 和 NYCU-Taiwan 都釋出了附授權的程式碼；最佳模型只出現一次，在高中組，由 Mingdao 拿下；大專組則完全沒有產生任何技術類特別獎，NYCU-Taiwan 的得獎是一支影片，NCKU-Tainan 的是一個 village 類別。最清楚的症狀是 NTHU Taiwan 的 CatharSys：它的四個模型因為預測的分離度只有 6% 而從篩選中剔除一個因子、在甲醛被推估到底盤耐受度五倍時推翻了一項酵素工程計畫、在建置之前就提出一個可否證的預測，並依第一原理的流體力學推翻了一個噴嘴幾何設計——而它拿到一面金牌，其他什麼都沒有。\n\nGEMS-Taiwan 的三項得獎和 Top 10 席次是台灣今年最好的成績，而且靠的是來源可追溯性，不是生物學：一份把每個數字標明為量測、引用或建模的輸入帳本，一個在 10 月 1 日預先登錄、後來評定為 0.286 ± 0.010 h⁻¹ 的生長速率，以及一個在通道死亡前 26.7 小時就點出光度計即將失效的自動編碼器。但若以大專組 Top 10 的水準來衡量，這個乾實驗室在四個明確的地方偏薄——沒有推論統計，核心的分泌活性數據停在 **n = 1、7.25 mU/mL、低於定量極限**，而兩次誘導實驗連正負號都不一致，相對地高一個層級的 NCKU-Tainan 以盤為隨機截距配適混合模型，還保留一個處理組來做預測；整套控制架構建立在一條已發表的 CcaSR Hill 曲線上，並假設它在 20 L 仍然成立，儘管每一次誘導都只在單一光強度下進行，所以整個專案沒有任何一處檢驗自己的轉換函數；數位孿生被自己承認是數位影子，重播錄下的運轉過程，每一個決定都由人做，綠光誘導也沒有整合進去；而經濟分析用隊伍自己的數字算是負的，在效力完美的前提下回收期是 68 年，對比合作夥伴的 4.9 年。要往上走一階，需要的是三處深度而不是更多範圍：對核心主張做重複實驗與區間估計，並預先登錄**效應量**而不是預先登錄生長速率；在不同光強度與規模下自己做一條 CcaSR 劑量反應曲線，以絕對的螢光素校正單位表示，這同時會把 35 個貢獻出去的 SubtiToolKit 零件變成一套附有轉換曲線的集合，而那正是零件類獎項真正會獎勵的東西；以及一個能控制運轉而不只是重播運轉的孿生，加上一位會把抱怨寫下來的外部軟體使用者。\n\n合作地圖要從一個不太舒服的事實開始：**GEMS-Taiwan 不在台灣這個網絡裡**。NYCU-Taiwan 於 7 月 27 日在博愛校區主辦 2026 Taiwan iGEMers Meet-Up，共有來自 NYCU-Taiwan、NCKU-Tainan、HIA-Taiwan、VIS 和 WIST 的 53 位學生與指導老師參加，而 NCKU-Tainan 的合作頁面還加上 Mingdao、CCU-Taiwan 和 NTHU——GEMS-Taiwan 和 Labi-Taiwan 都沒有出現在任何一份名單上，GEMS 的 wiki 更完全沒有合作頁面。因此這些合作對象是從互補性推出來的，不是從善意推出來的：NTHU Taiwan 共用 *Bacillus subtilis* 底盤和開放硬體的習慣，NCKU-Tainan 握有統計方法和便宜的讀取器，CCU-Taiwan 在同一種作物、同一座島上研究稻縱捲葉螟，NTHU 的 AeroSense 組擁有這群隊伍中最深的計算能力，並承認它的解碼器是在外部金屬氧化物感測器資料集上驗證，而不是在自己的細胞上，Labi-Taiwan 是唯一另一個有真正計算堆疊的高中計畫，而 NYCU-Taiwan 負責召集。\n\n台灣由國家支持的推動以製造為主——台灣生物醫藥製造公司（TBMC）於 2025 年 6 月在新竹生醫園區為一座 15,000 m² 的 GMP 廠動土，2026 年第二季起營運，其中包括台灣第一條 GMP mRNA 產能；生醫被放在 5+2 產業創新計畫裡；一個 33 家公司的代表團前往 BIO 2026；而這份研究完全沒有找到任何台灣專屬的合成生物學設計計畫或經費數字。新加坡和以色列正好在資助這一層缺口：DayOne 於 2026 年 8 月啟動新加坡第一座生物資料中心原型，以色列創新署則在 2026 年 7 月投入約 7,000 萬新謝克爾，建設以生物資料訓練 AI 模型的國家級基礎設施。2026 這一屆既是缺口的證據，也是缺口可以被填上的證據：十三支隊伍、六台做出來的儀器、零零件入圍、零軟體入圍。GEMS 應該把自己定位為台灣的乾實驗室人才管線，而不是一個比較小的濕實驗室，並且把這件事說給生技醫藥產業發展推動小組和經濟部聽，以新加坡和以色列作為對照；說給正在擴產、距離 NYCU 和兩支 NTHU 隊伍只有二十分鐘的新竹 TBMC 聽；也說給工業技術研究院聽，NTHU Taiwan 在那裡已經有現成的合作關係，GEMS 不必從零開始建。","cards":[{"kicker":"High School · Taipei · id 6072","title":"GEMS-Taiwan — ReLEAF","title_zh":"GEMS-Taiwan — ReLEAF","body":"An optogenetic Bacillus subtilis WB800 bioreactor that reads field sensors and weather forecasts, sets a green-light dose through the CcaSR two-component system and secretes plant-protective proteins beside a Taiwanese paddy. Taiwan's only Top 10 place in 2026 and the island's only triple winner: Best Measurement, Best Hardware and Best Integrated Human Practices, plus nominations for Presentation, Wiki and Best Village Project. The award case rests on provenance rather than biology — a pre-registered growth rate scored after the fact, an autoencoder that named a failing photometer 26.7 hours early, an input ledger marking every number measured, cited or modelled, and a wiki that withdraws its own claims. The hole is that the published CcaSR transfer function the whole control architecture depends on was assumed, never measured, and the central activity figure is n = 1 below quantitation.","body_zh":"一座光遺傳學的 Bacillus subtilis WB800 生物反應器，讀取田間感測器與天氣預報，透過 CcaSR 雙組分系統設定綠光劑量，在台灣的稻田旁分泌植物保護蛋白。這是台灣在 2026 年唯一的 Top 10 席次，也是台灣唯一的三冠得主：最佳量測、最佳硬體和最佳整合式人類實踐，另外入圍簡報、Wiki 和最佳 Village 專案。得獎的理由建立在來源可追溯性上，而不是生物學——一個事後評定的預先登錄生長速率、一個提早 26.7 小時點出光度計失效的自動編碼器、一份把每個數字標明為量測、引用或建模的輸入帳本，以及一個會撤回自己主張的 wiki。缺口在於整套控制架構所依賴的那條已發表 CcaSR 轉換函數是假設來的，從來沒有量測過，而核心的活性數據是 n = 1 且低於定量極限。","chips":["Gold","Top 10","3 wins","Hardware","Measurement","IHP","B. subtilis"],"chips_zh":["金牌","Top 10","3 項得獎","Hardware","Measurement","IHP","B. subtilis"],"kicker_zh":"高中組 · Taipei · id 6072"},{"kicker":"High School · Taoyuan · id 6511","title":"Labi-Taiwan — BlueCatcher","title_zh":"Labi-Taiwan — BlueCatcher","body":"A nucleic-acid biosensor for major depressive disorder, built by Labi Education, the programme formerly entered as Taipei-KCISLK. The dry lab is the most data-heavy of any Taiwanese high-school team: differential expression, miRNA–mRNA networks, GSEA and WGCNA narrowed 2,656 mature miRNAs to sixteen candidates and then to miR-124-3p as the first engineering target, with machine learning used to prioritise three-way-junction probes and toehold switches, and thermodynamic and kinetic modelling behind the readout. It won the iGEMers Prize, the award the other teams vote for, and was nominated for Best Measurement on a portable electrochemical reader. Like GEMS, it is a Taipei-area commercial-organiser programme and appears on no other Taiwanese team's collaboration page.","body_zh":"一個針對重度憂鬱症的核酸生物感測器，由 Labi Education 製作，這個計畫過去以 Taipei-KCISLK 的名義參賽。它的乾實驗室是台灣所有高中隊伍中資料量最大的：差異表現分析、miRNA–mRNA 網路、GSEA 和 WGCNA 把 2,656 個成熟 miRNA 收斂到十六個候選，再收斂到 miR-124-3p 作為第一個工程標的，並用機器學習排序三向接合探針與 toehold switch，讀出背後還有熱力學與動力學建模。它拿下 iGEMers Prize，也就是由其他隊伍投票選出的獎，並以一台攜帶式電化學讀取器入圍最佳量測。和 GEMS 一樣，它是臺北地區由商業機構營運的計畫，而且沒有出現在任何其他台灣隊伍的合作頁面上。","chips":["Gold","iGEMers Prize","Measurement nominee","miRNA","ML","electrochemical"],"chips_zh":["金牌","iGEMers Prize","Measurement 入圍","miRNA","機器學習","電化學"],"kicker_zh":"高中組 · Taoyuan · id 6511"},{"kicker":"Undergrad · Hsinchu · id 6306","title":"NYCU-Taiwan — BITE","title_zh":"NYCU-Taiwan — BITE","body":"A modular food-safety biosensor combining magnetic-bead DNA enrichment, CRISPR-Cas12a recognition and G4–hemin colorimetric readout against synthetic DNA from the Salmonella enterica invA region. The dry lab is organised as SeekProbe_Designer for capture-probe design plus a four-layer model stack from bead capture through Cas12a activation and hairpin-G4 colour to end-to-end prediction, with a Y-shaped multi-chamber device concept. It won Best Project Promotion Video — the island's only collegiate win outside a village category — on a silver medal, which is the gap between communication and technical recognition in one team. NYCU is also the convening institution: it hosted the 2026 Taiwan iGEMers Meet-Up for 53 people from five teams and built the exchange website behind it.","body_zh":"一個模組化的食品安全生物感測器，結合磁珠 DNA 富集、CRISPR-Cas12a 辨識和 G4–hemin 比色讀出，針對 Salmonella enterica invA 區域的合成 DNA。乾實驗室分成 SeekProbe_Designer 負責捕捉探針設計，加上一套四層模型堆疊，從磁珠捕捉、Cas12a 活化、髮夾-G4 顯色一路到端到端預測，另有一個 Y 形多室裝置的構想。它以銀牌拿下最佳專案推廣影片——這是台灣大專組在 village 類別之外唯一的得獎——而這一支隊伍本身就是溝通能力與技術肯定之間落差的縮影。NYCU 也是召集機構：它主辦了 2026 Taiwan iGEMers Meet-Up，有來自五支隊伍的 53 人參加，並建立了背後的交流網站。","chips":["Silver","Best Promotion Video","Cas12a","Meet-Up host","food safety"],"chips_zh":["銀牌","Best Promotion Video","Cas12a","Meet-Up 主辦","食品安全"],"kicker_zh":"大學組 · Hsinchu · id 6306"},{"kicker":"Undergrad · Tainan · id 6379","title":"NCKU-Tainan — Capture","title_zh":"NCKU-Tainan — Capture","body":"Two engineered E. coli systems reading the same Pseudomonas aeruginosa quorum-sensing signal: one reports AHL as fluorescence, one deploys aptamers to sponge it out of circulation, aimed at healthcare-associated infection in Taiwanese intensive care. It won Best Infectious Diseases Project and was nominated for Best Hardware for CAPTURE-Screen, a single-cuvette fluorescence reader at US$54–161 against US$3,500 for the plate reader it substitutes, paired with LasReader for 4PL calibration with approximate 95% intervals. The statistics are the best in the Taiwanese cohort — mixed models with plate as a random intercept, geometric-mean ratio effect sizes, and the Cb-2 treatment held out and then predicted. It is also the island's mentoring spine, having run a session for Mingdao in March with three of its own members as Mingdao alumni.","body_zh":"兩套工程化的 E. coli 系統讀取同一個 Pseudomonas aeruginosa 的群體感應訊號：一套把 AHL 以螢光回報，另一套用核酸適體把它從環境中吸走，目標是台灣加護病房的醫療照護相關感染。它拿下最佳傳染病專案，並以 CAPTURE-Screen 入圍最佳硬體——這是一台單一比色管的螢光讀取器，售價 54 到 161 美元，而它取代的盤式讀取器要 3,500 美元——並搭配 LasReader 做 4PL 校正與近似 95% 區間。它的統計是台灣這群隊伍中最好的——以盤為隨機截距的混合模型、幾何平均比的效應量，以及把 Cb-2 處理組保留下來再進行預測。它也是台灣的師徒骨幹，3 月為 Mingdao 辦了一場指導課，自己隊上有三位成員是 Mingdao 的校友。","chips":["Gold","Infectious Diseases win","Hardware nominee","US$54 reader","mixed models"],"chips_zh":["金牌","Infectious Diseases 得獎","Hardware 入圍","US$54 讀取儀","混合模型"],"kicker_zh":"大學組 · Tainan · id 6379"},{"kicker":"Overgrad · Hsinchu · id 6460","title":"NTHU — AeroSense","title_zh":"NTHU — AeroSense","body":"A biohybrid olfactory platform: Drosophila odorant receptors with ORCO in HEK293 cells, GCaMP6f fluorescence reporting, a four-channel frequency-tagged optical reader with digital lock-in processing, and a fly-inspired network for decoding odour patterns, aimed at early fungal-risk screening in stored bananas. This is the deepest computational work in the Taiwanese cohort — PCA and projection-neuron coding, measured infrared and quantum-vibration features, an OpenPOM comparison, mutation-robustness and cross-species transfer tests, and molecular-dynamics pocket-entry studies. Nominated for Best Food & Nutrition Project and nothing else. The team states its own limit plainly: the decoder was evaluated on external metal-oxide sensor datasets, not on its own cells.","body_zh":"一個生物混合嗅覺平台：在 HEK293 細胞中表現 Drosophila 嗅覺受體與 ORCO，用 GCaMP6f 螢光回報，搭配一台帶數位鎖相處理的四通道頻率標記光學讀取器，以及一個模仿果蠅的網路來解碼氣味樣態，目標是儲運香蕉的早期真菌風險篩檢。這是台灣這群隊伍中最深的計算工作——PCA 與投射神經元編碼、實測的紅外與量子振動特徵、與 OpenPOM 的比較、突變穩健性與跨物種轉移測試，以及分子動力學的口袋進入研究。入圍最佳食品與營養專案，其他什麼都沒有。隊伍自己明白寫出它的限制：解碼器是在外部金屬氧化物感測器資料集上評估，不是在自己的細胞上。","chips":["Gold","Food & Nutrition nominee","GCaMP6f","neural decoder","lock-in optics"],"chips_zh":["金牌","Food & Nutrition 入圍","GCaMP6f","神經解碼器","鎖相光學"],"kicker_zh":"研究生組 · Hsinchu · id 6460"},{"kicker":"High School · Taichung · id 6105","title":"Mingdao — Waste-to-Watt","title_zh":"Mingdao — Waste-to-Watt","body":"Laminated paper food containers from a 7,000-student campus turned into bioethanol by simultaneous saccharification and fermentation, with Zymomonas mobilis acting as a glucose sink so that BglA β-glucosidase never becomes product-inhibited and cellulase never sees accumulating cellobiose. Nominated for Best Model on three stacked models — enzyme-inhibition kinetics characterised under fermentation-compatible conditions rather than the thermophilic optimum, Monod growth for Z. mobilis, and a coupled ODE comparing closed and open systems. The hardware is a single 45 × 45 × 60 cm frame carrying shredding, hydrolysis, fermentation and distillation with the vessel riding to the distillation station on its own hotplate, so the mixture is never transferred. The clearest high-school modelling case in Taiwan after GEMS, and the only Taiwanese Best Model nomination at any tier.","body_zh":"把一所 7,000 名學生校園產生的淋膜紙食品容器，透過同步糖化發酵轉成生質乙醇，並讓 Zymomonas mobilis 充當葡萄糖的吸收端，使 BglA 這個 beta-葡萄糖苷酶永遠不會被產物抑制，纖維素酶也不會遇到累積的纖維二糖。以三個疊起來的模型入圍最佳模型——在符合發酵條件而非嗜熱最佳條件下描述的酵素抑制動力學、Z. mobilis 的 Monod 生長模型，以及一組比較密閉與開放系統的耦合 ODE。硬體是一個 45 × 45 × 60 cm 的單一機架，承載粉碎、水解、發酵和蒸餾，反應槽連同自己的加熱板一起移到蒸餾站，所以混合物從頭到尾不需要轉移。這是台灣在 GEMS 之後最清楚的高中建模案例，也是台灣在任何組別唯一的最佳模型入圍。","chips":["Gold","Best Model nominee","SSF","coupled ODE","fermentor"],"chips_zh":["金牌","Best Model 入圍","SSF","耦合 ODE","發酵槽"],"kicker_zh":"高中組 · Taichung · id 6105"},{"kicker":"Undergrad · Hsinchu · id 6416 — not on the briefed list","title":"NTHU Taiwan — CatharSys","title_zh":"NTHU Taiwan — CatharSys","body":"A second, separate National Tsing Hua University team, distinct from the overgraduate NTHU entry: engineered Bacillus subtilis forming biofilms on suspended carriers in a moving-bed reactor to treat TMAH and trimethylamine waste from Hsinchu's semiconductor lithography lines. Four models, and each one changed a decision — dissolved oxygen was dropped from the screen at a predicted 6% separation below flask noise, strengthening the bottleneck enzyme alone was shown to drive formaldehyde to five times chassis tolerance so a matched hxlAB upregulation was carried instead, a biofilm model stated a falsifiable prediction before the build, and first-principles hydraulics reversed a nozzle geometry for the pump already bought. CathaBench, its three-tank open-source benchtop MBBR with ESP32 control and an offline Wi-Fi dashboard, was iterated on feedback from ITRI and industry. Gold medal, zero nominations — on this evidence the most under-recognised dry lab in Taiwan in 2026, and the closest technical match to GEMS.","body_zh":"第二支獨立的國立清華大學隊伍，與研究生組的 NTHU 不同：工程化的 Bacillus subtilis 在移動床反應器的懸浮載體上形成生物膜，處理新竹半導體微影產線排出的 TMAH 與三甲胺廢水。四個模型，而且每一個都改變了一項決定——溶氧在預測的分離度只有 6%、低於搖瓶雜訊的情況下被從篩選中剔除；只強化瓶頸酵素被證明會把甲醛推到底盤耐受度的五倍，因此改為同步上調 hxlAB；一個生物膜模型在建置之前就提出可否證的預測；而第一原理的流體力學推翻了一個噴嘴幾何設計，泵都已經買好了。CathaBench 是它的三槽開放原始碼桌上型 MBBR，以 ESP32 控制並配上離線 Wi-Fi 儀表板，是依 ITRI 與業界的意見迭代出來的。金牌，零入圍——以這些證據來看，是台灣 2026 年最被低估的乾實驗室，也是技術上與 GEMS 最接近的隊伍。","chips":["Gold","no awards","B. subtilis","MBBR","ITRI","semiconductor waste"],"chips_zh":["金牌","沒有得獎","B. subtilis","MBBR","ITRI","半導體廢水"],"kicker_zh":"大學組 · Hsinchu · id 6416 — 不在原清單中"},{"kicker":"Undergrad · Chiayi · id 6408 — not on the briefed list","title":"CCU-Taiwan — NoFold","title_zh":"CCU-Taiwan — NoFold","body":"National Chung Cheng University against the rice leafroller, Cnaphalocrocis medinalis, which folds a rice leaf and eats it from inside and is described as a predominant foliage feeder across Asian rice ecosystems. The framing is the same economic argument GEMS makes: only about 12% of world rice crosses a border, so an Asian yield loss cannot be covered by imports, and the moths arrive on spring winds from overwintering areas such as Hanoi and Nanning with Taiwan on the route. Gold medal, no awards or nominations. Same crop, same island, same pest-pressure problem as ReLEAF, approached from entomology rather than abiotic stress — the most obvious untapped adjacency in the cohort.","body_zh":"國立中正大學對抗稻縱捲葉螟 Cnaphalocrocis medinalis，這種害蟲把稻葉捲起來從裡面吃，文獻描述它是整個亞洲稻作生態系中的主要食葉害蟲。它的切入角度和 GEMS 的經濟論點相同：全世界只有大約 12% 的稻米跨越國界，所以亞洲的減產無法靠進口補上，而這些蛾會隨春季的風從河內、南寧等越冬地北上，台灣就在路線上。金牌，沒有任何得獎或入圍。同一種作物、同一座島、同一個蟲害壓力問題，和 ReLEAF 一樣，只是從昆蟲學而不是非生物逆境切入——這是這群隊伍中最明顯尚未利用的鄰接機會。","chips":["Gold","no awards","rice","crop protection","Chiayi"],"chips_zh":["金牌","沒有得獎","水稻","作物防治","嘉義"],"kicker_zh":"大學組 · Chiayi · id 6408 — 不在原清單中"},{"kicker":"High School · Taichung · id 6062 — not on the briefed list","title":"WIST — ultrasound-reporting probiotic","title_zh":"WIST — 以超音波回報的益生菌","body":"Washington International School, Taichung: an engineered E. coli that answers two chemical clues at once, lactate and nitrate, and reports the AND condition by filling with gas vesicles and becoming visible to ultrasound, as a swallowable early screen for colorectal cancer. The acoustic-reporter approach is the same gas-vesicle technology Heidelberg built its collegiate Top 10 project on this year, which makes it an ambitious choice for a high-school team. It carries both a Model and a Software page and declares every figure on the home page a diagram of method rather than acquired data. Gold medal, no awards; it attended the NYCU Meet-Up and appears on NCKU-Tainan's collaboration list.","body_zh":"臺中的 Washington International School：一株工程化的 E. coli 同時回答兩個化學線索——乳酸和硝酸鹽——並以充滿氣囊、在超音波下變得可見的方式回報這個 AND 條件，作為可吞服的大腸癌早期篩檢。這種聲學報告子的作法，和 Heidelberg 今年拿下大專組 Top 10 的專案所用的氣囊技術相同，這讓它對一支高中隊伍來說是個野心很大的選擇。它同時有 Model 和 Software 頁面，並聲明首頁上的每一張圖都是方法示意圖，不是實際取得的資料。金牌，沒有得獎；它出席了 NYCU 的 Meet-Up，也出現在 NCKU-Tainan 的合作名單上。","chips":["Gold","no awards","gas vesicles","ultrasound","AND gate"],"chips_zh":["金牌","沒有得獎","氣體囊泡","超音波","AND 閘"],"kicker_zh":"高中組 · Taichung · id 6062 — 不在原清單中"},{"kicker":"High School · Taipei · id 6200 — not on the briefed list","title":"AEI Prep-Taiwan — SynPETic","title_zh":"AEI Prep-Taiwan — SynPETic","body":"Engineered E. coli making PETase and MHETase side by side on one scaffold — a 'PETosome' — to depolymerise PET in water at 37 °C with no extruder and no metal catalyst, framed around the roughly 2,500 kg of plastic waste the ISS generates a year and the up-to-US$20,000 cost of lifting a kilogram to orbit. One of only two commercially organised Taiwanese high-school programmes besides GEMS and Labi, and it carries Model, Software and Hardware pages. Silver medal, no awards or nominations. The Space village framing makes it the nearest cohort neighbour to GEMS's own village placement.","body_zh":"工程化的 E. coli 把 PETase 和 MHETase 並排接在同一個支架上——一個「PETosome」——在 37 °C 的水中分解 PET，不需要擠出機也不需要金屬催化劑，整個論述圍繞 ISS 每年產生約 2,500 kg 塑膠廢棄物，以及把一公斤物資送上軌道最高可達 20,000 美元的成本。這是除了 GEMS 和 Labi 之外，僅有兩個由商業機構營運的台灣高中計畫之一，而且有 Model、Software 和 Hardware 頁面。銀牌，沒有得獎或入圍。Space village 的定位讓它成為這群隊伍中與 GEMS 自己的 village 歸屬最接近的鄰居。","chips":["Silver","no awards","PETase","Space village","Taipei"],"chips_zh":["銀牌","沒有得獎","PETase","太空 village","臺北"],"kicker_zh":"高中組 · Taipei · id 6200 — 不在原清單中"},{"kicker":"High School · Taipei · id 6423 — not on the briefed list","title":"VIS — Cadture","title_zh":"VIS — Cadture","body":"VIS@betterworld Lab, testing whether engineered metallothioneins can capture cadmium from industrial wastewater, with a modelling page on cadmium removal. The notable feature is epistemic honesty of the kind GEMS also practises: the home page states that current work measures bacterial growth and GFP response and that direct cadmium removal remains to be tested, rather than implying a result it does not have. Silver medal, no awards or nominations. It attended the NYCU Meet-Up and is on NCKU-Tainan's collaboration list, so it is inside the island network that the Taipei commercial programmes are outside.","body_zh":"VIS@betterworld Lab 測試工程化的金屬硫蛋白能否從工業廢水中捕捉鎘，並有一個關於除鎘的建模頁面。值得注意的是它那種 GEMS 也在實踐的知識論誠實：首頁寫明目前的工作量測的是細菌生長與 GFP 反應，直接除鎘仍有待測試，而不是暗示一個它並不擁有的結果。銀牌，沒有得獎或入圍。它出席了 NYCU 的 Meet-Up，也在 NCKU-Tainan 的合作名單上，所以它在島內網絡之內，而臺北那兩個商業計畫在這個網絡之外。","chips":["Silver","no awards","metallothionein","cadmium","honest scoping"],"chips_zh":["銀牌","沒有得獎","金屬硫蛋白","鎘","誠實界定範圍"],"kicker_zh":"高中組 · Taipei · id 6423 — 不在原清單中"},{"kicker":"High School · Zhubei · id 6156 — not on the briefed list","title":"HIA-Taiwan — Aiy-U-Ready","title_zh":"HIA-Taiwan — Aiy-U-Ready","body":"Hsinchu International Academy in Zhubei, working on aiyu, Ficus pumila var. awkeotsang, a fig endemic to Taiwan that yields hundreds of tonnes a year and is almost unknown outside it. The project is built around that asymmetry — a locally owned crop nobody else is characterising — which is precisely the 'own a dataset nobody else has' logic the industry trend research identifies as a small institution's only durable asset. Silver medal, no awards or nominations, with a Dry Lab model page. It attended the NYCU Meet-Up and is on NCKU-Tainan's collaboration list.","body_zh":"位於竹北的 Hsinchu International Academy，研究愛玉 Ficus pumila var. awkeotsang，這是一種台灣特有的榕屬植物，年產量達數百公噸，在台灣以外幾乎沒人知道。整個專案就建立在這個不對稱上——一種本地擁有、沒有別人在做特性分析的作物——而這正是產業趨勢研究指出的「擁有一份別人沒有的資料集」邏輯，也是小型機構唯一能長久持有的資產。銀牌，沒有得獎或入圍，有一個 Dry Lab 模型頁面。它出席了 NYCU 的 Meet-Up，也在 NCKU-Tainan 的合作名單上。","chips":["Silver","no awards","aiyu","endemic crop","Hsinchu County"],"chips_zh":["銀牌","沒有得獎","愛玉","特有作物","新竹縣"],"kicker_zh":"高中組 · Zhubei · id 6156 — 不在原清單中"},{"kicker":"High School · New Taipei · id 6103 — not on the briefed list","title":"KCIS-Xiugang-Taipei — Herculyeast","title_zh":"KCIS-Xiugang-Taipei — Herculyeast","body":"Kang Chiao International School's Xiugang campus, running a yeast project with both Model and Software pages under its Dry Lab, plus Entrepreneurship, Inclusivity and Sustainability sections. Silver medal, no awards or nominations. Its sibling campus at Linkou entered separately as Taipei-TWN and was recorded as not eligible, so the Kang Chiao group fielded two high-school entries in 2026 and converted neither — and Labi-Taiwan, the iGEMers Prize winner, is the same Linkou programme's earlier lineage under a new organiser.","body_zh":"康橋國際學校秀崗校區，進行一個酵母專案，Dry Lab 下同時有 Model 和 Software 頁面，另有創業、包容性和永續性章節。銀牌，沒有得獎或入圍。它在林口的姊妹校區以 Taipei-TWN 另外註冊，並被記為不符資格，所以康橋集團在 2026 年派出兩支高中隊伍，兩支都沒有轉換成成績——而 iGEMers Prize 得主 Labi-Taiwan，正是同一個林口計畫在新營運單位之下的前身。","chips":["Silver","no awards","yeast","New Taipei","Kang Chiao"],"chips_zh":["銀牌","沒有得獎","酵母","新北","康橋"],"kicker_zh":"高中組 · New Taipei · id 6103 — 不在原清單中"},{"kicker":"Did not compete · ids 6142, 6543 — not on the briefed list","title":"Taipei-TWN and Oros Biotech","title_zh":"Taipei-TWN 與 Oros Biotech","body":"Two Taiwanese registrations that never reached the competition floor and so are missing from every results table. Taipei-TWN (Kang Chiao International School, Linkou campus, high school, Taipei) carries the status 'not eligible' with no medal and no wiki content. Oros Biotech of Taichung entered the venture-foundry track rather than the competition, has no section, no medal and a 404 wiki — meaning Taiwan's only 2026 entry into iGEM's startup pathway left no public record. Both matter for the denominator: fifteen Taiwanese registrations, thirteen competing teams, and an entrepreneurship route the island used once and did not document.","body_zh":"兩個從未站上競賽場的台灣註冊隊伍，因此在每一份成績表上都看不到。Taipei-TWN（康橋國際學校林口校區，高中，臺北）的狀態是「不符資格」，沒有獎牌也沒有 wiki 內容。臺中的 Oros Biotech 進入的是創投育成路線而不是競賽，沒有組別、沒有獎牌，wiki 回傳 404——也就是說，台灣 2026 年唯一進入 iGEM 新創路徑的隊伍沒有留下任何公開紀錄。兩者對分母都有意義：十五個台灣註冊隊伍、十三支參賽隊伍，以及一條台灣用過一次卻沒有記錄下來的創業路線。","chips":["Not eligible","venture foundry","no wiki","Taipei","Taichung"],"chips_zh":["不符資格","創投育成路線","沒有 wiki","臺北","臺中"],"kicker_zh":"未參賽 · ids 6142, 6543 — 不在原清單中"},{"kicker":"Regional comparison","title":"Taiwan against China, Hong Kong, Japan, Korea and Singapore","title_zh":"台灣對比中國、香港、日本、韓國與新加坡","body":"On accepted competing teams: China 176, Hong Kong 16, Taiwan 13, Japan 7, Korea 6, Singapore 4. On outright wins Taiwan placed second in the region with six, behind China's 24 and ahead of Hong Kong's three, with Japan, Korea and Singapore returning none at all — so Taiwan was the only territory outside China to win more than once. On altitude the ranking inverts: China took five Top 10 places and a Grand Prize first runner-up, Hong Kong three Top 10 places and the high-school Grand Prize first runner-up through HongKong-JSS, Singapore one through NUS-Singapore, and Taiwan one through GEMS-Taiwan, with no Taiwanese Grand Prize placing at any tier. In kind the regions differ sharply: China dominates the parts awards and the Registry layer, Hong Kong spreads thirteen nominations across parts, model, software, hardware, education, presentation and wiki, Japan accumulates nominations without converting any, and Taiwan concentrates in hardware, measurement and human practices while taking zero parts and zero software nominations.","body_zh":"以獲受理的參賽隊伍數計算：中國 176、香港 16、台灣 13、日本 7、韓國 6、新加坡 4。以正式得獎數計算，台灣以六項居區域第二，落在中國的 24 項之後、香港的三項之前，而日本、韓國和新加坡完全掛零——所以台灣是中國以外唯一贏超過一次的地區。但以高度來排，順序就反轉了：中國拿下五個 Top 10 席次和一個總冠軍第一亞軍，香港三個 Top 10 席次並透過 HongKong-JSS 拿到高中組總冠軍第一亞軍，新加坡透過 NUS-Singapore 拿到一個，台灣透過 GEMS-Taiwan 拿到一個，而台灣在任何組別的總冠軍都沒有名次。在類型上各區域差異很大：中國主導零件類獎項和 Registry 這一層，香港把十三項入圍分散在零件、模型、軟體、硬體、教育、簡報和 wiki，日本累積入圍卻一項都沒有轉換，而台灣集中在硬體、量測和人類實踐，零件和軟體的入圍數都是零。","chips":["TWN 13 teams","6 wins","1 Top 10","0 parts","0 software","HKG 3 Top 10"],"chips_zh":["TWN 13 隊","6 項得獎","1 個 Top 10","零件入圍 0","軟體入圍 0","HKG 3 個 Top 10"],"kicker_zh":"區域比較"}],"table":{"head":["Team","Tier","2026 result","Strength"],"head_zh":["隊伍","組別","2026 年成績","強項"],"rows":[["GEMS-Taiwan (6072)","High School","Gold; Top 10; wins in Measurement, Hardware, Integrated HP; nominees Presentation, Wiki, Village Project","Provenance discipline, pre-registration, four built devices"],["Labi-Taiwan (6511)","High School","Gold; iGEMers Prize winner; Best Measurement nominee","Sequencing-to-target evidence integration; portable electrochemical readout"],["Mingdao (6105)","High School","Gold; Best Model nominee","Enzyme-kinetic and coupled-ODE modelling; integrated single-frame fermentor"],["WIST (6062)","High School","Gold; no awards","Gas-vesicle ultrasound reporting; two-input AND logic"],["AEI Prep-Taiwan (6200)","High School","Silver; no awards","Scaffolded dual-enzyme PET depolymerisation; Space village framing"],["VIS (6423)","High School","Silver; no awards","Metallothionein cadmium capture; honest scoping of untested claims"],["HIA-Taiwan (6156)","High School","Silver; no awards","Taiwan-endemic aiyu crop nobody else is characterising"],["KCIS-Xiugang-Taipei (6103)","High School","Silver; no awards","Yeast chassis with both model and software pages"],["NYCU-Taiwan (6306)","Undergrad","Silver; Best Project Promotion Video winner","Communication, convening; four-layer Cas12a model stack and probe-design software"],["NCKU-Tainan (6379)","Undergrad","Gold; Best Infectious Diseases Project winner; Best Hardware nominee","Inferential statistics with held-out prediction; US$54-161 fluorescence reader"],["NTHU Taiwan (6416)","Undergrad","Gold; no awards","Four models that each reversed or changed a build decision; open-source MBBR"],["CCU-Taiwan (6408)","Undergrad","Gold; no awards","Rice leafroller entomology and rice-trade economics"],["NTHU (6460)","Overgrad","Gold; Best Food & Nutrition Project nominee","Deepest computation in the cohort: receptor prediction, odour decoding, lock-in optics"],["Taipei-TWN (6142)","High School","Not eligible; no medal","No public record"],["Oros Biotech (6543)","Venture foundry","No section, no medal, 404 wiki","Taiwan's only 2026 entry to iGEM's startup pathway"]],"rows_zh":[["GEMS-Taiwan (6072)","高中組","金牌；Top 10；量測、硬體、整合式人類實踐得獎；簡報、Wiki、Village 專案入圍","來源可追溯性的紀律、預先登錄、四台做出來的裝置"],["Labi-Taiwan (6511)","高中組","金牌；iGEMers Prize 得主；最佳量測入圍","從定序到標的的證據整合；攜帶式電化學讀出"],["Mingdao (6105)","高中組","金牌；最佳模型入圍","酵素動力學與耦合 ODE 建模；整合在單一機架上的發酵槽"],["WIST (6062)","高中組","金牌；無得獎","氣囊超音波回報；雙輸入 AND 邏輯"],["AEI Prep-Taiwan (6200)","高中組","銀牌；無得獎","支架化的雙酵素 PET 解聚；太空 village 的定位"],["VIS (6423)","高中組","銀牌；無得獎","金屬硫蛋白捕捉鎘；對未經測試的主張誠實界定範圍"],["HIA-Taiwan (6156)","高中組","銀牌；無得獎","台灣特有的愛玉作物，沒有別人在做特性分析"],["KCIS-Xiugang-Taipei (6103)","高中組","銀牌；無得獎","酵母底盤，同時有模型與軟體頁面"],["NYCU-Taiwan (6306)","大學組","銀牌；最佳專案推廣影片得主","溝通與召集；四層 Cas12a 模型堆疊與探針設計軟體"],["NCKU-Tainan (6379)","大學組","金牌；最佳傳染病專案得主；最佳硬體入圍","附保留樣本預測的推論統計；54 到 161 美元的螢光讀取器"],["NTHU Taiwan (6416)","大學組","金牌；無得獎","四個模型各自推翻或改變了一項建置決定；開放原始碼 MBBR"],["CCU-Taiwan (6408)","大學組","金牌；無得獎","稻縱捲葉螟的昆蟲學與稻米貿易經濟"],["NTHU (6460)","研究生組","金牌；最佳食品與營養專案入圍","這群隊伍中最深的計算：受體預測、氣味解碼、鎖相光學"],["Taipei-TWN (6142)","高中組","不符資格；無獎牌","沒有公開紀錄"],["Oros Biotech (6543)","創投育成","無組別、無獎牌、wiki 回傳 404","台灣 2026 年唯一進入 iGEM 新創路徑的隊伍"]]},"partners":[{"name":"NTHU Taiwan (National Tsing Hua University, Hsinchu) — team 6416","why":"The closest technical match to GEMS on the island and the one GEMS has no relationship with. Same chassis (engineered Bacillus subtilis), same commitment to open-source reactor hardware (CathaBench, a three-tank MBBR on ESP32 with an offline dashboard), and a modelling culture that demonstrably changed the build rather than decorating it — it dropped dissolved oxygen from a screen on a predicted 6% separation, reversed an enzyme-engineering plan when formaldehyde was projected to five times chassis tolerance, and reversed a nozzle geometry after first-principles hydraulics. It also already holds the ITRI and industry relationships GEMS would otherwise have to build from nothing. It won gold and nothing else, so it needs legibility as much as GEMS needs rigour.","why_zh":"島上技術上與 GEMS 最接近的隊伍，也是 GEMS 唯一完全沒有關係的那一支。相同的底盤（工程化的 Bacillus subtilis）、同樣投入開放原始碼反應器硬體（CathaBench，一套以 ESP32 控制、配離線儀表板的三槽 MBBR），以及一種確實改變了建置而不只是裝飾的建模文化——它因為預測的分離度只有 6% 而把溶氧從篩選中剔除、在甲醛被推估到底盤耐受度五倍時推翻了一項酵素工程計畫，並在第一原理的流體力學之後推翻了一個噴嘴幾何設計。它也已經握有 GEMS 原本得從零建立的 ITRI 與業界關係。它拿了金牌、其他什麼都沒有，所以它需要易讀性的程度，就跟 GEMS 需要嚴謹度一樣。","firstProject":"A joint Bacillus subtilis measurement standard. Co-characterise the CcaSR green-light transfer function and a suspension-versus-biofilm growth model across both teams' reactors in absolute fluorescein-calibrated units, then release it as a SubtiToolKit-compatible part collection with full transfer curves and a shared SBOL3 record. This closes GEMS's single largest hole — a control architecture resting on a Hill curve it never measured — and gives NTHU Taiwan the Registry-visible artefact its modelling earned and did not get.","firstProject_zh":"一套共同的 Bacillus subtilis 量測標準。在兩支隊伍的反應器上，以絕對的螢光素校正單位共同描述 CcaSR 綠光轉換函數，以及懸浮態與生物膜態的生長模型，然後把它作為相容於 SubtiToolKit 的零件集合釋出，附上完整的轉換曲線和一份共用的 SBOL3 紀錄。這補上了 GEMS 最大的單一缺口——一套建立在從未量測過的 Hill 曲線上的控制架構——同時也給 NTHU Taiwan 一件在 Registry 上看得見的成果，那是它的建模應得卻沒有拿到的。"},{"name":"NCKU-Tainan (National Cheng Kung University, Tainan) — team 6379","why":"The only Taiwanese collegiate team to win a technical-domain award in 2026, and the holder of the exact competence GEMS lacks: mixed models with plate as a random intercept, geometric-mean-ratio effect sizes with 95% intervals, and a held-out treatment used as a genuine prediction test. It is also an instrumentation peer — CAPTURE-Screen reads GFP at US$54-161 against US$3,500 for the open-source plate reader it replaces, and LasReader wraps 4PL calibration with confidence intervals around any reader's output. It is the de facto mentoring spine of Taiwanese iGEM, having run a session for Mingdao with three of its own members as Mingdao alumni, so a GEMS link here also buys entry to the network GEMS skipped.","why_zh":"2026 年唯一拿下技術領域獎項的台灣大專隊伍，也正好握有 GEMS 缺乏的能力：以盤為隨機截距的混合模型、帶 95% 區間的幾何平均比效應量，以及把保留的處理組當成真正的預測檢驗。它同時是儀器上的同儕——CAPTURE-Screen 以 54 到 161 美元讀取 GFP，而它取代的開放原始碼盤式讀取器要 3,500 美元，LasReader 則為任何讀取器的輸出包上帶信賴區間的 4PL 校正。它實質上是台灣 iGEM 的師徒骨幹，曾為 Mingdao 辦過一場指導課，自己隊上有三位成員是 Mingdao 校友，所以在這裡建立連結，也等於買到 GEMS 當初跳過的那個網絡的入場券。","firstProject":"A cross-instrument calibration round-robin. Run GEMS's in-line photometer, NCKU's CAPTURE-Screen and a benchtop plate reader against the same fluorescein and silica standards and the same sfGFP culture series, analyse everything through LasReader so the analysis path is identical, and publish a Taiwan measurement note reporting agreement, disagreement and the limits of each instrument's linear range. It is a Best Measurement-grade artefact for both teams and it imports NCKU's statistics into GEMS's practice by doing rather than by telling.","firstProject_zh":"一場跨儀器的校正循環比對。讓 GEMS 的在線光度計、NCKU 的 CAPTURE-Screen 和一台桌上型盤式讀取器，跑同一組螢光素與二氧化矽標準品和同一系列 sfGFP 培養液，全部透過 LasReader 分析，使分析路徑完全一致，然後發表一份台灣量測報告，說明一致之處、不一致之處，以及每台儀器線性範圍的極限。這對兩支隊伍都是最佳量測等級的成果，而且它是用做的方式、不是用講的方式，把 NCKU 的統計帶進 GEMS 的實務。"},{"name":"CCU-Taiwan (National Chung Cheng University, Chiayi) — team 6408","why":"Working the same crop, the same island and the same problem from the other side: rice under pest pressure rather than rice under abiotic stress. Its framing already matches GEMS's economic argument — that only about 12% of world rice crosses a border, so an Asian yield loss cannot be imported away — and it brings entomology and migration data (spring leafroller flights north from Hanoi and Nanning with Taiwan on the route) that GEMS's stress index does not contain. Gold medal, no awards, no obvious outlet for the work. Geographically it sits between Tainan and Taichung, inside the rice belt both projects target.","why_zh":"從另一側處理同一種作物、同一座島、同一個問題：稻米面對的是蟲害壓力，而不是非生物逆境。它的切入角度已經和 GEMS 的經濟論點一致——全世界只有大約 12% 的稻米跨越國界，所以亞洲的減產無法靠進口補上——而它帶來 GEMS 的逆境指數裡沒有的昆蟲學與遷移資料（春季捲葉螟從河內與南寧往北飛，台灣就在路線上）。金牌，沒有得獎，這些成果也沒有明顯的出口。地理上它位在臺南與臺中之間，就在兩個專案共同指向的稻作帶裡。","firstProject":"A shared Taiwan rice-stress dataset with a published benchmark. Extend GEMS's fitted stress index — 25 years of county rice yields against ERA5 daily reanalysis, scored across 32,767 candidate term combinations — with CCU's leafroller pressure and arrival data, release it as a versioned, licensed dataset with a defined forecasting benchmark task and a public leaderboard, and have both teams state a trigger rule against it in advance. One hectare, two trigger rules, one open benchmark that other teams can beat.","firstProject_zh":"一份共享的台灣稻作逆境資料集，並附上公開的基準測試。把 GEMS 配適出的逆境指數——25 年的縣級稻米產量對 ERA5 每日再分析資料，在 32,767 種候選項組合中評分——擴充進 CCU 的捲葉螟壓力與到達資料，以有版本控制、附授權的資料集釋出，定義一項預測基準任務和一個公開排行榜，並讓兩支隊伍各自事先針對它宣告一條觸發規則。一公頃、兩條觸發規則、一個其他隊伍可以來挑戰的開放基準。"},{"name":"NTHU (National Tsing Hua University, Hsinchu, overgrad AeroSense group) — team 6460","why":"The deepest computational work in the Taiwanese cohort and the natural counterpart to GEMS's protein-design pipeline. It runs receptor-response prediction with measured infrared and quantum-vibration features, an OpenPOM comparison, mutation-robustness and cross-species transfer tests, and molecular-dynamics pocket-entry studies — and it says openly that its decoder was evaluated on external metal-oxide sensor datasets rather than on its own cells. GEMS has the opposite problem: a GRAFT design workflow with docking, all-atom MD and a pre-set AlphaFold confidence gate, and almost no measured validation of what it designs. Each team is the other's missing half.","why_zh":"台灣這群隊伍中最深的計算工作，也是 GEMS 蛋白質設計流程天然的對應方。它做的是受體反應預測，使用實測的紅外與量子振動特徵、與 OpenPOM 的比較、突變穩健性與跨物種轉移測試，以及分子動力學的口袋進入研究——而它公開說明自己的解碼器是在外部金屬氧化物感測器資料集上評估，不是在自己的細胞上。GEMS 的問題正好相反：一套有對接、全原子分子動力學和預先設定 AlphaFold 信賴度門檻的 GRAFT 設計流程，卻幾乎沒有對設計結果做過實測驗證。兩支隊伍各自是對方缺的那一半。","firstProject":"A design-to-measurement validation loop. GEMS proposes a small, pre-registered panel of receptor or binder variants through GRAFT with the confidence gate and acceptance criteria fixed in writing beforehand; NTHU expresses and measures them on its HEK293/GCaMP6f assay and four-channel lock-in reader; both publish the hit rate including every failure, with the predictions timestamped before the measurements. The deliverable is a hit-rate number on a named pipeline, which is the one thing neither team can currently produce alone.","firstProject_zh":"一個從設計到量測的驗證迴路。GEMS 透過 GRAFT 提出一小組預先登錄的受體或結合物變異體，信賴度門檻與通過標準都事先以書面固定；NTHU 在它的 HEK293/GCaMP6f 分析和四通道鎖相讀取器上表現並量測這些變異體；兩隊共同發表命中率，包含每一次失敗，而預測都在量測之前標上時間。交付成果是一條具名流程的命中率數字，而這正是兩支隊伍目前各自都做不出來的東西。"},{"name":"Labi-Taiwan (Labi Education, Taoyuan) — team 6511","why":"The only other Taiwanese high-school programme with a genuine computational stack, and GEMS's structural twin: both are Taipei-area programmes run by commercial organisers, both are absent from NYCU's and NCKU's collaboration lists, and between them they hold four of Taiwan's six 2026 wins. Their skills barely overlap — Labi runs sequencing-to-target evidence integration (2,656 miRNAs narrowed to miR-124-3p through differential expression, miRNA-mRNA networks, GSEA and WGCNA), ML-prioritised nucleic-acid probe design and electrochemical readout, where GEMS runs sensor metrology, reactor control and provenance auditing. Labi's iGEMers Prize also proves it can carry a room, which is the reputational asset a teaching programme needs.","why_zh":"唯一另一個擁有真正計算堆疊的台灣高中計畫，也是 GEMS 結構上的孿生：兩者都是臺北地區由商業機構營運的計畫，都不在 NYCU 和 NCKU 的合作名單上，而台灣 2026 年六項得獎中有四項由它們兩家拿下。他們的技能幾乎不重疊——Labi 做的是從定序到標的的證據整合（2,656 個 miRNA 透過差異表現、miRNA-mRNA 網路、GSEA 和 WGCNA 收斂到 miR-124-3p）、以機器學習排序的核酸探針設計和電化學讀出，而 GEMS 做的是感測器計量、反應器控制和來源稽核。Labi 的 iGEMers Prize 也證明它撐得住一個場子，而那正是一個教學計畫需要的聲譽資產。","firstProject":"A two-module Taiwan high-school dry-lab school, co-taught and open to any Taiwanese team. GEMS teaches provenance ledgers, assumption registers, pre-registration with written pass criteria and instrument cross-calibration; Labi teaches target selection from public sequencing cohorts, probe design and electrochemical quantification. Every participating team leaves with one pre-registered prediction, scored publicly after their next experiment. Teaching is also how GEMS joins the island network it currently sits outside.","firstProject_zh":"一所兩個模組、共同授課、對任何台灣隊伍開放的高中乾實驗室學校。GEMS 教來源帳本、假設登記表、附書面通過標準的預先登錄，以及儀器交叉校正；Labi 教如何從公開定序世代資料中選標的、探針設計和電化學定量。每一支參加的隊伍離開時都帶著一個預先登錄的預測，在他們下一次實驗之後公開評分。教學也是 GEMS 加入目前被排除在外的島內網絡的方式。"},{"name":"NYCU-Taiwan (National Yang Ming Chiao Tung University, Hsinchu) — team 6306","why":"The island's convening institution and its best communicators. It hosted the 2026 Taiwan iGEMers Meet-Up at its Bo-Ai campus on 27 July for 53 students and advisors from five teams, built a dedicated Taiwan iGEMers exchange website as the public record, and won Best Project Promotion Video. It also sits in Hsinchu alongside both NTHU teams, TBMC's new GMP facility and ITRI, which makes it the right physical venue for anything recurring. What its meet-up lacked was technical content: the roundtables covered team cohesion, leadership and Jamboree preparation, not modelling or measurement.","why_zh":"台灣的召集機構，也是最好的溝通者。它於 7 月 27 日在博愛校區主辦 2026 Taiwan iGEMers Meet-Up，有來自五支隊伍的 53 位學生與指導老師參加，建立了專屬的 Taiwan iGEMers 交流網站作為公開紀錄，並拿下最佳專案推廣影片。它也位在新竹，與兩支 NTHU 隊伍、TBMC 的新 GMP 廠和 ITRI 同在一地，這讓它成為任何週期性活動最合適的實體場地。它的聚會缺的是技術內容：圓桌討論談的是團隊凝聚、領導和 Jamboree 準備，不是建模或量測。","firstProject":"Co-host the 2027 Taiwan iGEMers Meet-Up with a dry-lab track, and stand up a permanent Taiwan iGEM dry-lab repository behind it. NYCU supplies the venue, the convening and the website; GEMS supplies a half-day curriculum on modelling, calibration and reproducibility plus the repository's founding contents — shared calibration protocols, fluorescein standards, model code, SBOL3 construct records and a template pre-registration form. The test of success is that a 2027 team other than GEMS publishes a calibrated measurement using it.","firstProject_zh":"共同主辦 2027 Taiwan iGEMers Meet-Up，加開一條乾實驗室議程，並在它背後建立一個常設的台灣 iGEM 乾實驗室資料庫。NYCU 提供場地、召集能力和網站；GEMS 提供半天的建模、校正與可重現性課程，以及資料庫的創始內容——共用的校正協議、螢光素標準品、模型程式碼、SBOL3 構築體紀錄和一份預先登錄表單範本。成功的檢驗標準是：2027 年有一支不是 GEMS 的隊伍用它發表一份經過校正的量測。"}],"method":"The tally is built from research/results2026.json (captured from competition.igem.org/results/2026 on 19 November 2026) cross-checked team by team against iGEM's own public API — api.igem.org/v1/teams?year=2026 for the full 463-team roster with countries, cities, sections and acceptance status, and api.igem.org/v1/teams/<id>/awards for each team's medals, nominations and wins — which is how nine Taiwanese registrations absent from the results table were found, including NTHU Taiwan (6416), CCU-Taiwan (6408), WIST (6062) and AEI Prep-Taiwan (6200). Project detail comes from the teams' own 2026 wikis, read directly where server-rendered and through a browser for the client-rendered single-page sites (Labi-Taiwan, CCU-Taiwan), plus the existing researched file at research/teams/6072.json for GEMS-Taiwan and research/trends/industry.json for the TBMC, DayOne and Israel Innovation Authority figures. Two Taiwanese registrations could not be verified beyond their API records: Taipei-TWN (6142) is marked not eligible and has no wiki content, and Oros Biotech (6543) returns a 404 wiki, so nothing is claimed about either project; KCIS-Xiugang-Taipei's project could only be identified by name and navigation structure because its wiki ships a largely unmodified template, and Mingdao's medal-level claims rest on the API rather than on a wiki statement.","method_zh":"這份統計以 research/results2026.json 為基礎（於 2026 年 11 月 19 日從 competition.igem.org/results/2026 擷取），並逐隊與 iGEM 自己的公開 API 交叉核對——api.igem.org/v1/teams?year=2026 取得完整 463 支隊伍的名冊，含國家、城市、組別與受理狀態，api.igem.org/v1/teams/<id>/awards 取得每支隊伍的獎牌、入圍與得獎——這也是找到九個未出現在成績表上的台灣註冊隊伍的方法，包括 NTHU Taiwan（6416）、CCU-Taiwan（6408）、WIST（6062）和 AEI Prep-Taiwan（6200）。專案細節來自各隊自己的 2026 wiki，伺服器端渲染的直接讀取，客戶端渲染的單頁網站（Labi-Taiwan、CCU-Taiwan）則透過瀏覽器讀取，另外加上 GEMS-Taiwan 既有的研究檔案 research/teams/6072.json，以及 research/trends/industry.json 中 TBMC、DayOne 和以色列創新署的數字。有兩個台灣註冊隊伍除了 API 紀錄之外無法再驗證：Taipei-TWN（6142）被標記為不符資格，也沒有 wiki 內容；Oros Biotech（6543）的 wiki 回傳 404，所以本文對這兩個專案不做任何主張。KCIS-Xiugang-Taipei 的專案只能靠名稱和導覽結構辨識，因為它的 wiki 用的幾乎是未經修改的樣板；而 Mingdao 的獎牌層級說法是依據 API，不是依據 wiki 上的陳述。","kicker_zh":"原創分析","order":30},{"id":"technique-census","tab":"drylab","kicker":"Original analysis","title":"What 2026's best teams actually reached for","title_zh":"2026 年最強的團隊，實際上用了什麼","lede":"A census of the computational tools named across all 106 team files in this report — and the one habit that separates the podium from everybody else.","lede_zh":"對本報告全部 106 份團隊檔案中提及的運算工具所做的普查——以及把頒獎臺和其他人分開的那一個習慣。","body":"Across the 106 team files gathered here, **AlphaFold is still the default**: it is named by 32 teams, more than any other modelling tool and four times as often as Boltz. ProteinMPNN appears in 14 files, Rosetta in 12, ESMFold and RFdiffusion in 8 each. The academic literature has already moved past this — open models now match or beat the gated flagship — but iGEM has not caught up. That lag is an opportunity: a team that works fluently with the current open stack is doing something most of the competition is not.\n\nThe second pattern is that **the dedicated systems-biology tools have quietly lost**. COPASI, once the standard way an iGEM team built a kinetic model, appears in **one** file out of 106. Tellurium appears in one. MATLAB holds on in five. Everything else is Python — named by 44 teams, more than any other single item in the census, usually SciPy integrating an ODE system written by hand, with scikit-learn behind it in 12 files for anything statistical. Teaching COPASI as the entry point to modelling now teaches a tool the field has left behind.\n\nThe third pattern is the surprise. **Techno-economic analysis — costing the thing, modelling unit economics — is done by more high-school teams than undergraduate ones**: 11 against 8, and a far higher share of a smaller tier. High-school teams are being pushed hard on implementation and business thinking, and they are delivering it. Meanwhile GROMACS, full molecular dynamics, appears in 7 undergraduate files, 1 overgraduate file and **never once** in a high-school one. The two tiers are not weaker and stronger versions of each other; they are differently shaped.\n\n**Then the finding that matters.** We checked which teams do both halves of modelling properly: fit the model to their own measured data (parameter estimation, regression, R², RMSE, confidence intervals, error bars) *and* validate it against something held back (held-out data, cross-validation, a separate experimental test). Only **19 of 106** teams do both.\n\nOf those 19, **10 are Top 10 teams — 53%**. Of the 87 that do not close the loop, 20 are Top 10 — **23%**. A team that closes the model–data loop is more than twice as likely to place. And of the nine who closed it without reaching a Top 10, every one still won or was nominated for a major special prize: XJTLU-China and Jilin-China in Best Model, NJU-China took Best Software & AI Project, UBC-Vancouver took Best Diagnostics, CAU-China took Best Food & Nutrition.\n\nThis is the single most actionable number in the report. Not which model you use — whether you close the loop between the model and your own data. It is also, conveniently, the cheapest capability to build: it needs no GPU, no licence and no collaboration. It needs a student who knows what a residual is.","body_zh":"在本報告蒐集的 106 份團隊檔案中，**AlphaFold 仍然是預設選項**：共 32 支團隊提到它，多於任何其他建模工具，是 Boltz 的四倍。ProteinMPNN 出現在 14 份檔案中，Rosetta 12 份，ESMFold 與 RFdiffusion 各 8 份。學術文獻早已走過這一步——開源模型現已可匹敵甚至超越封閉的旗艦模型——但 iGEM 還沒跟上。這個時間差就是機會：能熟練運用當前開源工具鏈的團隊，正在做大多數競爭者沒做的事。\n\n第二個型態是，**專用的系統生物學工具已悄悄落敗**。COPASI 曾經是 iGEM 團隊建立動力學模型的標準做法，如今在 106 份檔案中只出現**一次**。Tellurium 一次。MATLAB 勉強守住五份。其餘全是 Python——共 44 支團隊提及，多於普查中任何其他單一項目，通常是用 SciPy 積分一組手寫的 ODE 系統，統計部分則由 scikit-learn 在 12 份檔案中接手。現在把 COPASI 當作建模的入門，等於是在教一個領域已經放下的工具。\n\n第三個型態令人意外。**做技術經濟分析——計算成本、建立單位經濟模型——的高中隊伍比大學部隊伍還多**：11 對 8，而且在一個規模更小的組別中占比高出許多。高中組被大力要求落實應用與商業思考，而他們做到了。相對地，完整的分子動力學（GROMACS）出現在 7 份大學部檔案、1 份研究生組檔案，在高中組則**一次也沒有**。這兩個層級不是同一件事的強弱版本，它們的形狀本來就不同。\n\n**接著是真正重要的發現。** 我們檢查了哪些團隊把建模的兩半都做完：以自己量到的資料擬合模型（參數估計、回歸、R²、RMSE、信賴區間、誤差棒），*並且*用保留的資料驗證它（held-out 資料、交叉驗證、獨立的實驗測試）。106 支團隊中只有 **19 支**兩者皆備。\n\n這 19 支裡，**有 10 支是 Top 10 團隊——53%**。而在沒有閉合迴圈的 87 支中，只有 20 支進入 Top 10——**23%**。閉合模型與資料迴圈的團隊，進榜機率是兩倍以上。而閉合了迴圈卻未進 Top 10 的那九支，無一例外都拿下或入圍了重要特別獎：XJTLU-China 與 Jilin-China 在最佳模型，NJU-China 拿下最佳軟體與 AI 專案，UBC-Vancouver 拿下最佳診斷，CAU-China 拿下最佳食品與營養。\n\n這是整份報告中最可執行的一個數字。重點不是你用哪個模型，而是你有沒有把模型與自己的資料之間的迴圈閉合起來。而且它恰好也是最便宜的能力：不需要 GPU、不需要授權、不需要合作對象。它需要的是一位知道什麼叫殘差的學生。","cards":[{"kicker":"The headline number","title":"53% versus 23%","title_zh":"53% 對 23%","body":"Teams that both fit their model to their own data and validated it against something held back reached a Top 10 at 53%. Teams that did not reached it at 23% — less than half the rate. Note the sample is already decorated: every team here is a Top 10 or special-prize winner or nominee, so this is loop-closure separating winners from other winners, not from the general field.","body_zh":"既以自身資料擬合模型、又用保留資料加以驗證的團隊，進入 Top 10 的比例是 53%；沒有這麼做的則是 23%，不到一半。請注意樣本本身已經過篩選：這裡每一支團隊都是 Top 10 或特別獎得主／入圍者，因此這是「閉合迴圈」把贏家從其他贏家中分出來，而不是從一般參賽者中分出來。","chips":["19 of 106 closed the loop","10 of those 19 made Top 10"],"chips_zh":["106 支中 19 支閉合迴圈","這 19 支中 10 支進 Top 10"],"kicker_zh":"關鍵數字"},{"kicker":"Still the default","title":"AlphaFold has not been displaced inside iGEM","title_zh":"在 iGEM 裡，AlphaFold 還沒被取代","body":"32 of 106 teams name AlphaFold, four times the rate of Boltz. The research literature moved to the open stack over the past year; the competition has not. The teams already working in Boltz and the MPNN family — Lambert-GA, Heidelberg, GU Frankfurt, DTU-Denmark, Princeton — are visibly ahead of the curve rather than merely current.","body_zh":"106 支團隊中有 32 支提到 AlphaFold，是 Boltz 的四倍。研究文獻在過去一年已轉向開源工具鏈，競賽卻還沒。已經在用 Boltz 與 MPNN 家族的隊伍——Lambert-GA、Heidelberg、GU Frankfurt、DTU-Denmark、Princeton——明顯走在前面，而不只是跟上。","chips":["AlphaFold ×32","ProteinMPNN ×14","Boltz ×8","RFdiffusion ×8"],"chips_zh":["AlphaFold ×32","ProteinMPNN ×14","Boltz ×8","RFdiffusion ×8"],"kicker_zh":"仍是預設選項"},{"kicker":"A tool generation ended","title":"Python ate the modelling stack","title_zh":"Python 吃掉了整個建模工具鏈","body":"COPASI appears once in 106 files. Tellurium once. MATLAB five times. Python appears in 44 team files, more than any other item in the census, usually SciPy integrating a hand-written ODE system, with scikit-learn behind it for anything statistical. For a programme deciding what to teach, this settles the question: teach Python and the numerical stack, and treat SBML-based tools as an interchange format rather than a starting point.","body_zh":"COPASI 在 106 份檔案中出現一次，Tellurium 一次，MATLAB 五次。Python 出現在 44 份團隊檔案中，多於普查中任何其他項目，通常是用 SciPy 積分手寫的 ODE 系統，統計部分交給 scikit-learn。對一個正在決定要教什麼的課程而言，這已經定案：教 Python 與數值運算工具鏈，把以 SBML 為基礎的工具當作交換格式，而不是起點。","chips":["Python ×44","scikit-learn ×12","COPASI ×1","Tellurium ×1"],"chips_zh":["Python ×44","scikit-learn ×12","COPASI ×1","Tellurium ×1"],"kicker_zh":"一個工具世代的終結"},{"kicker":"The inversion","title":"High-school teams cost their projects; undergraduates often don't","title_zh":"高中隊伍會算成本，大學部常常不算","body":"Techno-economic analysis appears in 11 high-school files against 8 undergraduate ones, and in a far higher share of the smaller tier. Full molecular dynamics runs the other way: 7 undergraduate files, 1 overgraduate, and never once in a high-school file. The tiers are differently shaped rather than simply further apart, and a high-school programme that assumes it must catch up on everything is aiming at the wrong gap.","body_zh":"技術經濟分析出現在 11 份高中組檔案中，對比大學部的 8 份，而且在規模較小的組別裡占比高出許多。完整的分子動力學則完全相反：7 份大學部、1 份研究生組，高中組一次也沒有。兩個層級的形狀不同，而不只是距離遠近的差別。一個假定自己必須在所有面向上追趕的高中課程，瞄錯了缺口。","chips":["Techno-economic: 11 HS vs 8 UG","GROMACS: 7 UG, 0 HS"],"chips_zh":["技術經濟分析：高中 11 對大學部 8","GROMACS：大學部 7，高中 0"],"kicker_zh":"反轉"},{"kicker":"A weaker result, reported anyway","title":"Publishing your failures: an effect that shrank when we added data","title_zh":"公開失敗：加入更多資料後，效果反而縮小了","body":"Several analysts noticed the same thing independently — Toronto, WageningenUR and UZurich each put a prominent negative result on the wiki, and two won the award in that exact category. On the first 54 files the pattern looked real: 54% against 41%. Re-run across all 106 it collapses to **33% against 27%**, and the measurement was always partly circular — it detects how candid *our own summary* of a team was, not reliably how candid the team was. We are leaving it in because reporting the finding that weakened is the same discipline the rest of this page is about. Publish the negative result because it is honest, not because it wins prizes.","body_zh":"好幾位分析員各自獨立注意到同一件事——Toronto、WageningenUR 與 UZurich 都在 wiki 上放了顯著的負面結果，其中兩隊正是在對應類別中獲獎。在最初的 54 份檔案上，這個型態看起來是真的：54% 對 41%。但擴及全部 106 份重跑之後，它塌縮為 **33% 對 27%**；而且這個量測本來就帶有循環性——它偵測到的是*我們自己的摘要*有多坦白，而未必能可靠反映團隊有多坦白。我們把它留下來，是因為「報告那個變弱的發現」正是本頁其餘部分所談的同一種紀律。公開負面結果，是因為那樣才誠實，而不是因為那樣會得獎。","chips":["first 54 files: 54% vs 41%","all 106 files: 33% vs 27%"],"chips_zh":["前 54 份：54% 對 41%","全部 106 份：33% 對 27%"],"kicker_zh":"較弱的結果，照樣報告"},{"kicker":"What this means for GEMS","title":"The cheapest capability is the one that correlates with winning","title_zh":"最便宜的能力，正好就是和得獎相關的那一個","body":"Closing the model-data loop needs no GPU, no licence, no partner lab and no new chassis. It needs a student who can fit a curve, report an uncertainty and hold data back for a test. That is a term's teaching, and on this evidence it moves the result more than any tool choice. It is Phase 2 of the roadmap for exactly this reason.","body_zh":"閉合模型與資料之間的迴圈，不需要 GPU、不需要授權、不需要合作實驗室、也不需要新的底盤。它需要的是一位會擬合曲線、會報告不確定度、並且懂得保留資料做測試的學生。那是一個學期的教學量，而根據這些證據，它對結果的影響大於任何工具選擇。這正是它成為路線圖階段二的原因。","chips":["No GPU required","One term of teaching"],"chips_zh":["不需要 GPU","一學期就教得完"],"kicker_zh":"這對 GEMS 的意義"}],"method":"Counts come from pattern-matching the dry-lab and science-for-good fields of all 106 team files in this report, not from reading the wikis a second time, so a technique a team used but did not write up is invisible here. The sample is decorated teams only — every file is a Top 10 or special-prize winner or nominee — so the baselines are not the whole competition. The loop-closure test looks for explicit language about fitting, uncertainty and validation; a team that did the work but described it loosely will be undercounted. An earlier version of this page reported 71% against 40% from a 54-file snapshot taken while research was still landing; the figures above supersede it. Read the numbers as a ranking, not a measurement.","method_zh":"計數方式是對本報告全部 106 份團隊檔案的乾實驗室與科學向善欄位做樣式比對，而非重新閱讀 wiki，因此團隊做了卻沒寫下來的技術在這裡是看不見的。樣本僅限獲獎隊伍——每一份檔案都是 Top 10 或特別獎得主／入圍者——所以基準值並不代表整個競賽。迴圈閉合的判準是尋找明確描述擬合、不確定度與驗證的文字；做了卻寫得含糊的團隊會被低估。本頁較早的版本依據研究仍在進行時的 54 份檔案快照，報告了 71% 對 40%；上述數字取代該版本。請把這些數字當成排序，而不是量測。","kicker_zh":"原創分析","order":30},{"id":"good-patterns","tab":"good","kicker":"Original analysis","title":"What separated real engagement from outreach theatre","title_zh":"真正的參與，和表演式推廣，差別在哪裡","lede":"Across the 2026 field, the teams whose Science for Good work counted did four things the rest did not.","lede_zh":"綜觀 2026 年的參賽團隊，那些「科學向善」真正有份量的隊伍，做了另外四件其他人沒做的事。","body":"**They designed education from data, then measured it like an experiment.** UCAS-China did not start from \"raise awareness\". It ran clinician interviews and a 461-person questionnaire, found that patients stop medication once they feel better and that parents refuse to start it for children out of fear of side effects, and made *compliance* the target instead of awareness. UOregon wrote three separate curricula for three audiences with different prior knowledge and ran them as three DBTL iterations across June, July and October, carrying each round's lessons forward. HFI ran everything through a five-step cycle it named CLEAR, in which **every activity had to report a measured outcome and a change for the next iteration**.\n\nThe sharpest version of this is publishing the results when they are bad. GEMS-Taiwan ran pre- and post-lesson surveys with 140 students across five schools and published per-question accuracy charts including the failures — only 30% of students got DNA base pairing right. That number is worth more to the next teacher than any photograph of a full classroom.\n\n**They trained themselves before training anybody else.** Nineteen GU Frankfurt members took the \"Basics of Science Communication\" workshop run by NaWik, Germany's national institute for science communication, and used its core-message and cloverleaf tools as the basis of everything that followed. Most teams treat communication as something you already know how to do because you can talk.\n\n**They put disagreeing people in the same room.** Oxford's *Buzz In* podcast is the most quietly radical format in the 2026 field: rather than interviewing stakeholders separately and summarising, it deliberately paired people who disagree — a Varroa-resistance academic with a commercial beekeeper on whether to treat at all, then an industry council CEO with amateur beekeepers. Disagreement is the thing most human-practices pages are built to smooth over; Oxford made it the content.\n\nKIT won Inclusivity by turning the same honesty inward. It read the iGEM Diversity and Inclusion Committee's own writing, surveyed five previous iGEM gender-equity projects, and noticed that nearly all of them face **outward** — role models, outreach to girls, awareness — and almost none examine the team itself. So KIT examined the team itself.\n\n**They quantified the need, and built a business model that was not \"sell the product\".** Oxford states the problem in numbers rather than adjectives: Australia's failed Varroa eradication cost A$101 million and destroyed about 30,000 hives; surveyed US commercial operations lost roughly 62% of colonies in 2024–25. DTU-Denmark anchors on a date and a measurement: the Danish wind industry's voluntary landfill ban took effect on 1 January 2026, and a Danish EPA screening detected bisphenol A in every tank leaching test on blade material.\n\nThen the models themselves. HongKong-JSS sells **Certification-as-a-Service** — farmers subscribe annually, the team tests soil on site, passing farms get a \"Heavy Metal-Free\" logo for supermarket packaging that earns a premium, and surprise re-tests throughout the year are affordable precisely because the test is cheap. GEMS-Taiwan deploys through farmer collectives rather than direct sales, because its own fleet analysis shows a reactor owned by a single farm sits idle most of the season. GU Frankfurt chose exclusive licensing over a start-up because an autologous cell therapy's facility and specialist-salary costs cannot be carried by a spin-out, and has a letter of support from Miltenyi Biotec to show for it. XJTLU-China gives catmaOS away, on the argument that accessibility *is* the commercial thesis.\n\nUAlberta's case is the most evidentially careful: demand is tabulated by customer role **with the strength of each piece of evidence named** — two clinician letters of support, a signed letter of intent from one clinic, 86% of 38 surveyed dry eye patients interested, an application at interview stage with Nucleate Canada. And UCAS-China opens its commercial section by stating outright that the case must rest on a defined unmet need rather than on technological novelty, then tabulates the strengths of the existing drugs it would have to displace. A team willing to argue against itself is a team worth believing.","body_zh":"**他們從資料出發設計教育，再像做實驗一樣去量測它。** UCAS-China 的起點不是「提升認知」。他們訪談臨床醫師、做了 461 人的問卷，發現病人一感覺好轉就停藥、家長因為害怕副作用而不願意讓孩子開始用藥，於是把目標從「認知」改成*服藥遵從性*。UOregon 為三種先備知識不同的對象寫了三套獨立課程，並在六月、七月與十月以三次 DBTL 迭代執行，把每一輪的教訓帶進下一輪。HFI 則讓所有活動都跑一個他們命名為 CLEAR 的五步驟循環，其中**每一項活動都必須回報一個量測到的結果，以及下一次要改什麼**。\n\n這件事最鋒利的版本，是在結果難看的時候照樣公布。GEMS-Taiwan 在五所學校對 140 名學生做了課前課後問卷，並公布逐題正確率圖表，包含失敗的部分——DNA 鹼基配對只有 30% 的學生答對。對下一位老師而言，這個數字比任何一張坐滿學生的照片都有價值。\n\n**他們先訓練自己，再去訓練別人。** GU Frankfurt 有 19 位成員上了德國國家科學傳播研究所 NaWik 的「科學傳播基礎」工作坊，並以其核心訊息與四葉草等工具作為後續一切的基礎。多數團隊把傳播當成「反正我會說話就會做」的事。\n\n**他們把意見不合的人放進同一個房間。** Oxford 的 *Buzz In* podcast 是 2026 年最安靜地激進的形式：它不是分別訪談各方再做摘要，而是刻意把意見相左的人配成一對——讓研究 Varroa 抗性的學者與商業養蜂人辯論「到底該不該用藥」，再讓產業公會執行長與業餘養蜂人對談。多數人類實踐頁面的設計目的就是把分歧抹平；Oxford 直接把分歧當成內容。\n\nKIT 則把同樣的誠實轉向內部，因而拿下包容性獎。他們讀了 iGEM 多元與包容委員會自己的文章，檢視了五個過去的 iGEM 性別平等專案，注意到它們幾乎全部朝**外**——榜樣、對女孩的推廣、意識提升——而幾乎沒有一個檢視團隊自身。於是 KIT 檢視了團隊自身。\n\n**他們把需求量化，而且做出來的商業模式不是「把產品賣掉」。** Oxford 用數字而非形容詞陳述問題：澳洲失敗的 Varroa 根除行動花了 1.01 億澳元、摧毀約 3 萬個蜂箱；受調查的美國商業蜂場在 2024–25 年損失了約 62% 的蜂群。DTU-Denmark 則錨定在一個日期與一次量測上：丹麥風電產業的自願掩埋禁令自 2026 年 1 月 1 日生效，而丹麥環保署的篩檢在葉片材料的每一次槽式溶出試驗中都測到雙酚 A。\n\n接著是商業模式本身。HongKong-JSS 賣的是**認證即服務**——農民年度訂閱，團隊到場檢測土壤，通過的農場取得「無重金屬」標章可用於超市包裝並賣出溢價，而全年不定期的突擊複檢之所以負擔得起，正是因為檢測又便宜又快。GEMS-Taiwan 透過農民合作社而非直接銷售來部署，因為他們自己的機隊分析顯示：單一農場自有的反應器一整季大部分時間都閒置。GU Frankfurt 選擇獨家授權而非自行創業，因為自體細胞治療的廠房與專業人力成本不是一間新創扛得起的，而他們手上有 Miltenyi Biotec 的支持信。XJTLU-China 則把 catmaOS 免費釋出，理由是可及性*本身*就是商業論點。\n\nUAlberta 的案例在證據上最為嚴謹：需求依客戶角色列表，而且**每一項證據的強度都被標明**——兩封臨床醫師支持信、一間診所簽署的意向書、38 位乾眼症受訪患者中 86% 有興趣、一件已進入面試階段的 Nucleate Canada 申請。UCAS-China 則在商業章節的開頭直接寫明：這個案子必須建立在明確的未滿足需求上，而不是技術新穎性，接著列表說明它必須取代的既有藥物有哪些優點。一支願意對自己提出反方論證的團隊，才值得相信。","cards":[{"kicker":"The format worth stealing","title":"Oxford's Buzz In: put the disagreement on the record","title_zh":"Oxford 的 Buzz In：把分歧記錄下來","body":"A three-episode podcast that deliberately paired stakeholders who disagree, rather than interviewing them separately and summarising. Episode one put a Varroa-resistance academic opposite a commercial beekeeper on whether to treat at all. Most human-practices pages exist to smooth disagreement away; this one makes it the content, and it is far harder to fake than a list of meetings.","body_zh":"一個三集的 podcast，刻意把意見相左的利害關係人配對，而不是分別訪談後再做摘要。第一集讓研究 Varroa 抗性的學者，與商業養蜂人正面交鋒「到底該不該用藥」。多數人類實踐頁面的存在目的是把分歧抹平；這一個把分歧變成內容，而且它比一份會議清單難假造得多。","chips":["3 episodes","paired opponents"],"chips_zh":["3 集","讓對立方同場"],"kicker_zh":"值得借用的形式"},{"kicker":"The habit worth stealing","title":"Publish the question your students got wrong","title_zh":"公布學生答錯的那一題","body":"GEMS-Taiwan surveyed 140 students across five schools before and after each lesson and published per-question accuracy — including DNA base pairing, where only 30% answered correctly. Reporting the failure makes the whole dataset credible and hands the next teacher something actionable. A photograph of a full classroom does neither.","body_zh":"GEMS-Taiwan 在五所學校對 140 名學生做課前課後問卷，並公布逐題正確率——包括 DNA 鹼基配對，只有 30% 答對。報告失敗讓整份資料變得可信，也交給下一位老師一個可以採取行動的東西。一張坐滿學生的照片兩者都做不到。","chips":["140 students · 5 schools","30% on base pairing"],"chips_zh":["140 名學生 · 5 所學校","鹼基配對只對 30%"],"kicker_zh":"值得借用的習慣"},{"kicker":"The habit worth stealing","title":"Train the team before training the public","title_zh":"先訓練團隊，再去教公眾","body":"Nineteen GU Frankfurt members took the Basics of Science Communication workshop from NaWik, Germany's national science-communication institute, and built everything afterwards on its core-message and cloverleaf tools. Science communication is a craft with a literature; almost every other team treats it as something you can already do because you can talk.","body_zh":"GU Frankfurt 有 19 位成員上了德國國家科學傳播研究所 NaWik 的「科學傳播基礎」工作坊，並以其核心訊息與四葉草工具為基礎建構後續所有內容。科學傳播是一門有文獻的技藝；幾乎其他所有團隊都把它當成「我會說話所以我就會」。","chips":["19 members trained","NaWik"],"chips_zh":["19 名成員受訓","NaWik"],"kicker_zh":"值得借用的習慣"},{"kicker":"The business model worth stealing","title":"Sell the certificate, not the instrument","title_zh":"賣證書，不要賣儀器","body":"HongKong-JSS does not sell its mercury assay. Farmers subscribe annually, the team tests on site, passing farms get a 'Heavy Metal-Free' logo for supermarket packaging that commands a premium, and surprise re-tests through the year keep the certificate honest — affordable precisely because the test itself is cheap. The cheapness of the science becomes the business model rather than a weakness.","body_zh":"HongKong-JSS 不賣他們的汞檢測。農民年度訂閱，團隊到場檢測，通過的農場取得可用於超市包裝的「無重金屬」標章並賣出溢價，而全年不定期的突擊複檢維持證書的公信力——之所以負擔得起，正因為檢測本身很便宜。科學的廉價在這裡變成商業模式，而不是弱點。","chips":["Certification-as-a-Service","surprise re-tests"],"chips_zh":["認證即服務","不預告複檢"],"kicker_zh":"值得借用的商業模式"},{"kicker":"The business model worth stealing","title":"Name the strength of each piece of evidence","title_zh":"標明每一項證據的強度","body":"UAlberta tabulates demand by customer role and says how strong each item is: two clinician letters of support, one signed letter of intent, 86% of 38 surveyed patients interested, one application at interview stage with Nucleate Canada. A letter of intent and a survey response are not the same kind of evidence, and saying so is what makes the table worth reading.","body_zh":"UAlberta 依客戶角色把需求列表，並說明每一項證據有多強：兩封臨床醫師支持信、一封已簽署的意向書、38 位受訪患者中 86% 有興趣、一件進入面試階段的 Nucleate Canada 申請。一封意向書和一份問卷回覆不是同一種證據，而把這件事講清楚，正是這張表值得讀的原因。","chips":["evidence graded by strength"],"chips_zh":["證據依強度分級"],"kicker_zh":"值得借用的商業模式"},{"kicker":"For GEMS","title":"Argue against yourself in public","title_zh":"公開地為自己提出反方論證","body":"UCAS-China opens its commercial section by saying the case must rest on unmet need rather than technological novelty, then lists what the existing drugs do well. GEMS-Taiwan publishes a 68-year payback against a partner's 4.9-year figure and names the disagreement instead of resolving it. This is the practice that most distinguishes the 2026 podium, and it costs nothing but nerve.","body_zh":"UCAS-China 在商業章節的開頭就說：這個案子必須建立在未滿足需求上，而非技術新穎性，接著列出既有藥物的優點。GEMS-Taiwan 公布了 68 年的回收期，對照合作夥伴算出的 4.9 年，並指名這個歧異而不去解決它。這是 2026 年頒獎臺上最顯著的共同做法，而它唯一的代價是膽識。","chips":["no budget required"],"chips_zh":["不需要預算"],"kicker_zh":"給 GEMS"}],"method":"Drawn from the Science for Good fields of the team files in this report, each researched from the team's own 2026 wiki. Audience numbers and survey sizes are the teams' own figures and are not independently verified. The judgement about what 'counted' is ours; the team files and the wikis behind them are linked so a reader can disagree. GEMS-Taiwan is the report author's own team and appears here on the same terms as the rest.","method_zh":"資料取自本報告團隊檔案中的「科學向善」欄位，每一份都來自該隊自己的 2026 wiki。參與人數與問卷樣本數為各隊自報數字，未經獨立查證。關於「什麼才算數」的判斷出自我們；團隊檔案與其背後的 wiki 都附有連結，讀者可以自行判斷是否同意。GEMS-Taiwan 是本報告作者自己的團隊，在此與其他隊伍適用相同標準。","kicker_zh":"原創分析","order":32},{"id":"highschool-ceiling","tab":"drylab","kicker":"Original analysis","title":"The high-school ceiling, measured honestly","title_zh":"誠實地量一次高中組的天花板","lede":"What a high-school dry lab can actually reach in one season — and the finding that the gap is not about tools.","lede_zh":"一個高中乾實驗室在一季之內真正能做到什麼——以及那個發現：差距不在工具。","body":"Read the ten High School Top 10 dry labs side by side and the first surprise is how ordinary the software is. **Eton-College-UK** built its protease substrate predictor out of L2-regularised logistic regression and a BLOSUM62-smoothed position-specific scoring matrix — techniques older than the students using them. **HFI** used NetLogo, which is free and was designed for schools. **GHCIS** used a local install of NUPACK. **HangzhouFourteenAP** used PyMOL and FoldX. **HKSSC** used AlphaFold, UCSF Chimera and HotSpot Wizard. **HongKong-HS** reused another team's tool outright — miRADAR, released by Wageningen's 2024 team — rather than rebuilding it. Almost none of this costs money, and none of it requires a cluster.\n\nOnly **Lambert-GA**, the Grand Prize winner, works at the frontier of the toolchain: BindCraft, Boltz-2, Protenix, Mosaic. And even there the thing that earned Best Model was not the tools. It was that they **benchmarked the confidence metrics themselves** — ipSAE, ipTM and a 38-metric ensemble, against 5,721 labelled experimental designs — found the ensemble barely beat chance at ROC-AUC 0.541, noticed that their own eventual hit did not have the best score, and published all of that rather than quietly reporting the hit.\n\nThat is the pattern, and it holds across the whole tier. **The differentiator at high-school level is evaluation discipline, not tool sophistication.**\n\nThe evidence is specific. Eton clustered near-duplicate sequences by Hamming distance and split whole clusters across folds, then ran a label-shuffle control and a composition-only ablation — three cheap steps that separate a real classifier from a leaky one. **HongKong-JSS** split runs into calibration and validation *before* fitting anything, subtracted a matched control from the same run and timepoint, and reported RMSE on held-out runs with the failures left in. HKSSC could not measure molar enzyme concentration, so rather than report an invalid *k*cat/*K*m they defined and justified a mass-normalised metric valid only below *K*m, then ran a two-way ANOVA, found unequal variances, and moved to a median-based test. GHCIS specified its colour-classification algorithm down to the equation and the threshold, including an explicit **\"unresolved, and must not be read as Negative\"** state, and shipped it with one-command Docker deployment. HangzhouFourteenAP reported the prediction that lost: FoldX ranked Y166Q first, the bench preferred Q172P, and the wiki revises its own ranking while using BCA normalisation to rule out protein load as the explanation.\n\n**GEMS-Taiwan** belongs on that list and is worth reading closely, because the wiki is unusually candid about its own weaknesses. The strengths are real: a genuinely pre-registered growth-rate forecast, registered on 1 October and scored on run 6, which landed inside its stated interval; an autoencoder that flagged a failing photometer 26.7 hours before it died; and a crop-stress index fitted to 25 years of county rice yields rather than to expert judgement. The weaknesses are stated by the team itself: secreted activity at n=1 and below the limit of quantitation; two induction runs that disagree on the *sign* of the change; a Hill curve assumed to hold at 20 L when every induction ran at a single light intensity; a 2.44× rice canopy correction that is modelled, not measured; an efficacy coefficient of 0.58 explicitly withdrawn; and a payback period of 68 years on the team's own loss figure against a partner's 4.9 years, with the disagreement named rather than resolved. Naming the disagreement instead of picking the flattering number is the practice worth keeping.\n\n**And the control case.** **GCGS** reached the High School Top 10 with no model page and no software page at all — both routes return 404. Its one modelling claim is an undocumented circuit-level simulation with no parameters, equations or tooling named. A team can still place in the top ten of its section with essentially no dry lab. What GCGS could not do is win a modelling, measurement or software prize, and that is the precise shape of the opportunity.","body_zh":"把高中組 Top 10 的十個乾實驗室並排來讀，第一個意外是：他們用的軟體有多麼普通。**Eton-College-UK** 的蛋白酶受質預測器，是用 L2 正規化的 logistic regression 加上以 BLOSUM62 平滑的位置特異性計分矩陣（PSSM）做出來的——這些技術比使用它們的學生還老。**HFI** 用的是 NetLogo，免費，而且本來就是為學校設計的。**GHCIS** 用本機安裝的 NUPACK。**HangzhouFourteenAP** 用 PyMOL 與 FoldX。**HKSSC** 用 AlphaFold、UCSF Chimera 與 HotSpot Wizard。**HongKong-HS** 則直接沿用別隊的工具——Wageningen 2024 年釋出的 miRADAR——而不是重做一個。這些幾乎都不花錢，也都不需要叢集運算。\n\n只有總冠軍 **Lambert-GA** 站在工具鏈的前沿：BindCraft、Boltz-2、Protenix、Mosaic。但即使在那裡，替他們贏得最佳模型的也不是工具，而是他們**對信心指標本身做了基準測試**——拿 ipSAE、ipTM 與一組 38 項指標的集成，去對照 5,721 個有實驗標註的設計——發現該集成的 ROC-AUC 只有 0.541，幾乎只比亂猜好一點，還注意到自己最後成功的那個設計分數並不是最高的，然後把這一切全部公開，而不是安靜地只報成功的那一個。\n\n這就是整個型態，而且在整個層級中都成立。**高中層級的差異來自評估的紀律，而不是工具的精密度。**\n\n證據很具體。Eton 以 Hamming 距離把近似重複的序列分群，再把整群一起分到同一個 fold，接著跑標籤洗牌對照與僅用胺基酸組成的消融測試——三個便宜的步驟，就把一個真正的分類器和一個資料外洩的分類器分開了。**HongKong-JSS** 在擬合任何東西*之前*就把實驗批次分成校正組與驗證組，扣除同一批次、同一時間點的對照，並在保留批次上報告 RMSE，而且把失敗的資料留在裡面。HKSSC 無法量到酵素的莫耳濃度，於是沒有去報一個無效的 *k*cat/*K*m，而是定義並論證了一個只在低於 *K*m 時有效的質量標準化指標，接著做雙因子 ANOVA，發現變異數不齊，再改用以中位數為基礎的檢定。GHCIS 把顏色判讀演算法寫到方程式與閾值的層級，包含一個明確的**「無法判定，且不得視為陰性」**狀態，並以一行指令的 Docker 部署出貨。HangzhouFourteenAP 報告了那個輸掉的預測：FoldX 把 Y166Q 排第一，實驗卻偏好 Q172P，而 wiki 修正了自己的排序，同時用 BCA 標準化排除「蛋白質上樣量不同」這個解釋。\n\n**GEMS-Taiwan** 也屬於這份名單，而且值得仔細讀，因為這個 wiki 對自身弱點的坦白程度相當罕見。強項是真的：一個貨真價實的預先登記成長率預測，10 月 1 日登記、在第 6 批次評分，結果落在所宣告的區間內；一個在光度計故障前 26.7 小時就示警的自編碼器；以及一個以 25 年各縣市稻作產量擬合、而非靠專家判斷加權的作物逆境指數。弱點則由團隊自己寫出來：分泌活性 n=1 且低於定量極限；兩次誘導實驗對變化的*正負號*彼此矛盾；Hill 曲線被假定在 20 公升仍然成立，但所有誘導都只在單一光強度下進行；2.44 倍的水稻冠層修正是模擬出來而非量出來的；一個 0.58 的效能係數被明確撤回；以及以團隊自己的損失數字計算出 68 年的回收期，對比合作夥伴算出的 4.9 年，而這個歧異被指名寫出，而不是被解決掉。把歧異寫出來、而不是挑一個好看的數字，正是值得保留的做法。\n\n**還有對照組。** **GCGS** 在完全沒有 model 頁也沒有 software 頁的情況下進入高中組 Top 10——兩個路徑都回傳 404。它唯一的建模主張，是一個沒有記載參數、方程式或工具名稱的電路層級模擬。一支隊伍確實可以幾乎沒有乾實驗室，仍然進入該組前十名。但 GCGS 做不到的是拿下建模、測量或軟體獎項——而那正是機會的確切形狀。","cards":[{"kicker":"The ceiling","title":"Lambert-GA, and what the frontier costs","title_zh":"Lambert-GA，以及站上前沿的代價","body":"Four linked models: protein-design metric benchmarking on 5,721 labelled designs, a Sobol-analysed oral pharmacokinetic model, a 13-ODE SimBiology RNAi network, and an individual-based six-year, 800-run colony epidemiology. They produced the first reported DWV VP3 minibinder for under $400 of compute, released the open-source PRINCE site ranker (45.8% top-3 hit rate against 23.8% random on a no-homolog subset), and an $80 dryer externally validated at two universities. This is the ceiling, and it is reachable.","body_zh":"四個彼此連動的模型：在 5,721 個有標註的設計上做蛋白質設計指標的基準測試、一個經 Sobol 分析的口服藥物動力學模型、一個 13 條 ODE 的 SimBiology RNAi 網路，以及一個為期六年、跑 800 次的個體導向族群流行病學模擬。他們以不到 400 美元的運算成本做出第一個被報導的 DWV VP3 minibinder，釋出開源的 PRINCE 位點排序工具（在無同源子集上，前三名命中率 45.8%，對照隨機的 23.8%），以及一台 80 美元、經兩所大學外部驗證的乾燥裝置。這就是天花板，而且搆得到。","chips":["Boltz-2 · BindCraft · Protenix","under $400 of compute"],"chips_zh":["Boltz-2 · BindCraft · Protenix","運算不到 400 美元"],"kicker_zh":"天花板"},{"kicker":"The floor","title":"GCGS: Top 10 with no dry lab at all","title_zh":"GCGS：完全沒有乾實驗室也能進 Top 10","body":"Both /model and /software return 404. The single modelling claim is an undocumented circuit-level simulation with no parameters, equations or tooling named. GCGS still reached the High School Top 10 on the strength of a clean two-cycle DBTL and its Best New Improved Part. Read it as the honest floor: the dry lab is not what gets you into the top ten — it is what gets you a prize.","body_zh":"/model 與 /software 都回傳 404。唯一的建模主張是一個沒有記載參數、方程式或工具名稱的電路層級模擬。GCGS 仍然憑著乾淨的兩輪 DBTL 與最佳改良基因元件獎進入高中組 Top 10。請把它讀成誠實的底線：乾實驗室不是讓你擠進前十名的東西——它是讓你拿到獎項的東西。","chips":["no model page","still Top 10"],"chips_zh":["沒有模型頁","照樣進 Top 10"],"kicker_zh":"地板"},{"kicker":"The pattern","title":"Three cheap controls that separate real from leaky","title_zh":"三個便宜的對照，分開真實與外洩","body":"From Eton-College-UK, and transferable to any student machine-learning project: cluster near-duplicate sequences by Hamming distance and split whole clusters across folds, so the model cannot memorise a near-copy; run a label-shuffle control, which must collapse to chance; run an ablation that strips the information you claim to be using. None of these needs a GPU. Together they turn a high-school classifier into something a reviewer can believe.","body_zh":"來自 Eton-College-UK，可移植到任何學生的機器學習專案：以 Hamming 距離把近似重複的序列分群，並把整群分到同一個 fold，讓模型無法記住近似副本；跑標籤洗牌對照，其表現必須塌回隨機水準；跑一個消融測試，剝除你宣稱正在使用的那項資訊。這些都不需要 GPU。合起來，它們能把一個高中生的分類器變成審閱者願意相信的東西。","chips":["cluster-aware CV","label shuffle","ablation"],"chips_zh":["分群式交叉驗證","標籤洗牌","消融測試"],"kicker_zh":"共同型態"},{"kicker":"The pattern","title":"Split before you fit","title_zh":"先切分，再擬合","body":"HongKong-JSS divided its runs into calibration and validation before fitting anything, subtracted a matched control from the same run and timepoint, inverted the fit to predict unknowns, and reported RMSE on the held-out runs with the failures left in — then published a list of the statistics they had not yet done. That last habit is rarer and more valuable than the first.","body_zh":"HongKong-JSS 在擬合任何東西之前就把實驗批次分成校正組與驗證組，扣除同一批次、同一時間點的對照，反解擬合式來預測未知樣本，並在保留批次上報告 RMSE、把失敗的資料留在裡面——接著公布了一份他們還沒做的統計分析清單。最後這個習慣比第一個更罕見，也更有價值。","chips":["held-out RMSE","published what is not yet done"],"chips_zh":["留存集 RMSE","公布還沒做的部分"],"kicker_zh":"共同型態"},{"kicker":"The pattern","title":"Publish the prediction that lost","title_zh":"公開那個輸掉的預測","body":"HangzhouFourteenAP's FoldX pipeline ranked Y166Q first; the bench preferred Q172P. Rather than bury it, the wiki revises its own ranking, demotes the failed candidate to a mechanistic probe, and uses BCA normalisation to rule out protein load as the confound. Lambert-GA did the same at a larger scale by showing its own hit was not the top-scoring design. A dry lab earns more credibility from one well-controlled loss than from three unexamined wins.","body_zh":"HangzhouFourteenAP 的 FoldX 流程把 Y166Q 排第一，實驗卻偏好 Q172P。他們沒有把它埋掉，而是在 wiki 上修正自己的排序，把失敗的候選降級為機制探針，並以 BCA 標準化排除「蛋白質上樣量」這個干擾因子。Lambert-GA 在更大的尺度上做了同樣的事：證明自己成功的那個設計並不是分數最高的。一個乾實驗室從一次控制良好的失敗中得到的可信度，大於三次未經檢驗的成功。","chips":["FoldX said Y166Q","the bench said Q172P"],"chips_zh":["FoldX 說是 Y166Q","實驗台說是 Q172P"],"kicker_zh":"共同型態"},{"kicker":"For GEMS","title":"The gap is one term of teaching, not a budget line","title_zh":"差距是一個學期的教學，不是一筆預算","body":"Every practice above — cluster-aware splits, label-shuffle controls, calibration/validation separation, provenance tagging, publishing the loss — costs nothing but attention and can be taught in a term. The tools the 2026 high-school field actually used are free: NetLogo, NUPACK, PyMOL, FoldX, scikit-learn, ImageJ, Chimera, the AlphaFold server. GEMS does not need to buy its way to the ceiling. It needs to make evaluation discipline the house style.","body_zh":"上述每一項做法——分群感知的資料切分、標籤洗牌對照、校正與驗證分離、來源標註、公開失敗——都不花錢，只花注意力，而且一個學期就能教完。2026 年高中組實際用到的工具都是免費的：NetLogo、NUPACK、PyMOL、FoldX、scikit-learn、ImageJ、Chimera、AlphaFold server。GEMS 不需要靠花錢爬上天花板，它需要的是把評估紀律變成自己的風格。","chips":["all free tools","one term"],"chips_zh":["全是免費工具","一個學期"],"kicker_zh":"給 GEMS"}],"table":{"head":["Team","Headline dry-lab work","Main tools","The discipline that stands out"],"head_zh":["團隊","乾實驗室重點工作","主要工具","最突出的紀律"],"rows":[["Lambert-GA","Four linked models: de novo minibinder design, oral PK, 13-ODE RNAi network, colony epidemiology","BindCraft, Boltz-2, Protenix, Mosaic","Benchmarked the confidence metrics themselves and published that its own hit was not top-scoring"],["Eton-College-UK","Seven-protease substrate predictor on 10,472 cleavage windows","scikit-learn, PSSM, BLOSUM62, VHSE","Hamming-cluster-aware cross-validation, label-shuffle and ablation controls"],["GEMS-Taiwan","Crop-stress index fitted to 25 years of county rice yields; optogenetic circuit; anomaly detection","Python, autoencoder, Kalman filter, ERA5, QGIS, AlphaFold","A pre-registered forecast scored after the fact, and a published disagreement between its own runs"],["GHCIS","Toehold design pipeline, plus ARGUS, a deployable colour-classification platform","NUPACK 4.1.0.1, Node.js, Docker, SQLite","Algorithm specified to the threshold, with an explicit 'unresolved' state"],["HongKong-JSS","Calibration and inverse prediction for an in-field mercury assay","ImageJ, log-linear calibration, Onshape, ESP32","Calibration/validation split before fitting; RMSE on held-out runs with failures left in"],["HKSSC","Structure-guided mutagenesis and enzyme kinetics for a paraben-degrading esterase","AlphaFold, UCSF Chimera, HotSpot Wizard, CB-Dock2","Invented a justified mass-normalised metric rather than report an invalid kcat/Km"],["HFI","Agent-based contact model and a 13-variable ODE system, both as wet-lab gatekeepers","NetLogo 3D, Runge-Kutta, interactive HTML front-ends","Screened seven RBS parts computationally before a single plasmid was built"],["HangzhouFourteenAP","Mutation prioritisation pipeline for CoGH66","PyMOL, FoldX, MAFFT, AlphaFold Server","Reported the computational prediction the bench overturned, with the confound controlled"],["HongKong-HS","Toehold switch thermodynamics for a urinary miRNA screening kit","NUPACK, miRADAR (Wageningen iGEM 2024)","Reused another team's released tool instead of rebuilding it"],["GCGS","No model or software page exists","—","The control case: Top 10 without a dry lab, but no modelling prize"]],"rows_zh":[["Lambert-GA","四個連動模型：de novo minibinder 設計、口服藥物動力學、13 條 ODE 的 RNAi 網路、族群流行病學","BindCraft, Boltz-2, Protenix, Mosaic","對信心指標本身做基準測試，並公開自己成功的設計其實不是分數最高的"],["Eton-College-UK","在 10,472 個切割視窗上建立七種蛋白酶的受質預測器","scikit-learn, PSSM, BLOSUM62, VHSE","以 Hamming 距離分群的交叉驗證，加上標籤洗牌與消融對照"],["GEMS-Taiwan","以 25 年各縣市稻作產量擬合的作物逆境指數；光遺傳電路；異常偵測","Python, autoencoder, Kalman filter, ERA5, QGIS, AlphaFold","一個事後評分的預先登記預測，以及公開自己兩次實驗之間的矛盾"],["GHCIS","Toehold 設計流程，外加可部署的顏色判讀平台 ARGUS","NUPACK 4.1.0.1, Node.js, Docker, SQLite","演算法明確寫到閾值，並設有明確的「無法判定」狀態"],["HongKong-JSS","現場汞檢測的校正與反解預測","ImageJ, 對數線性校正, Onshape, ESP32","擬合前先切分校正組與驗證組；在保留批次上報告 RMSE 並保留失敗資料"],["HKSSC","對羥苯甲酸酯分解酯酶的結構導向突變與酵素動力學","AlphaFold, UCSF Chimera, HotSpot Wizard, CB-Dock2","沒有報告無效的 kcat/Km，而是提出並論證一個質量標準化指標"],["HFI","代理人基礎接觸模型與 13 變數 ODE 系統，兩者都作為濕實驗的守門員","NetLogo 3D, Runge-Kutta, 互動式 HTML 前端","在建出任何一個質體之前，先以運算篩選七個 RBS 元件"],["HangzhouFourteenAP","CoGH66 的突變優先排序流程","PyMOL, FoldX, MAFFT, AlphaFold Server","公開那個被實驗推翻的運算預測，並控制了干擾因子"],["HongKong-HS","尿液 miRNA 篩檢套組的 toehold switch 熱力學","NUPACK, miRADAR（Wageningen iGEM 2024）","沿用別隊已釋出的工具，而不是重做一個"],["GCGS","沒有 model 頁，也沒有 software 頁","—","對照組：沒有乾實驗室也能進 Top 10，但拿不到建模類獎項"]]},"method":"Drawn from the ten High School Top 10 team files in this report, each researched from the team's own 2026 wiki. Tool lists are what each team names; a team may have used more than it wrote down. The judgement about what 'stands out' is ours, and a reader who disagrees should open the team file and the wiki behind it — both are linked. GEMS-Taiwan is the report author's own team and has been assessed on the same terms as the rest.","method_zh":"資料來自本報告中高中組 Top 10 的十份團隊檔案，每一份都取自該隊自己的 2026 wiki。工具清單是各隊自己寫出來的；團隊實際用到的可能多於其所記載。關於「什麼最突出」的判斷出自我們，不同意的讀者可以直接打開團隊檔案與其背後的 wiki——兩者都有連結。GEMS-Taiwan 是本報告作者自己的團隊，評判標準與其他隊伍相同。","kicker_zh":"原創分析","order":32},{"id":"wiki-craft","tab":"teams","kicker":"Original analysis","title":"What the Best Wiki winners did differently","title_zh":"最佳 Wiki 得獎隊伍做了哪些不一樣的事","lede":"The four 2026 Best Wiki winners did not win on visual polish or page weight; they won by building an executive layer that tells a judge where the evidence is, and then by being unusually specific and unusually honest underneath it.","lede_zh":"2026 年四組最佳 Wiki 得獎隊伍並不是靠視覺精緻度或頁面重量取勝；他們靠的是建立一層明確的摘要層，直接告訴評審證據在哪裡，然後在這層底下做到異常具體、異常誠實。","body":"Three of the four winners ship pages whose text exists in the HTML before any JavaScript runs: **Heidelberg** writes static HTML by hand, **Uni-Padua-IT** prerenders SvelteKit, **Lambert-GA** builds with Astro. TU Delft is the exception, a Vite single-page app behind a 3.4 MB bundle, and it compensates deliberately with an `llms.txt` at the wiki root and a plain-Markdown mirror of every page at `/tu-delft/<page>.md`. Against that, the control group — Princeton, Cornell, LYON, UAlberta, UCNZ, Athens, GU Frankfurt and Eton-College-UK, all winners of serious 2026 science prizes — serves near-empty shells of 486 bytes to 15 kB, as little as seven characters of text without JS.\n\nThe real differentiator is an explicit executive layer. Uni-Padua-IT and Lambert-GA both ship a `/judging` page that walks medal criterion by criterion, summarises each in two or three sentences and deep-links the evidence — Padua pointing straight at its own negative results, Lambert stating in the summary that fifteen minibinder designs produced no confirmed hits before a second campaign of twenty produced one binder at roughly 604 nM. TU Delft reaches the same place with an illustrated module map on Results where hovering highlights a module and clicking jumps to it, over the same five modules that organise the project; Heidelberg puts three summary cards above the fold and gives every nav link a one-line subtitle, so \"Results\" reads \"Where data tells the story\".\n\nUnderneath, the winners are simply more specific. **Heidelberg**'s captions carry panel letters, 547 ng and 433 ng transfection masses, 18,000 × g, and an effect size quoted with its range — 5.6×, 4.3 to 6.4× depending on the haze setting — while Padua photographs the plate that grew nothing, numbers it as a figure, and explains why an earlier transformation failed. **TU Delft** built a content system rather than a set of pages: 1,604 reference tags over 735 unique DOIs, 724 glossary calls against 102 definitions, 307 auto-numbered figures, and one unvarying Background → Results → Discussion → Future Perspective spine. Its decision matrix tags every cell as Factual, Inferred, Estimated or Speculative, with a legend saying the tag records the strength of the evidence behind the cell rather than the judgement — epistemic honesty rendered as a UI component, and I saw nothing like it elsewhere.\n\nWhat did not decide it is as instructive. Page weight spans two orders of magnitude inside the winners' circle, from Lambert-GA's 78 kB homepage to TU Delft's 3.4 MB. None of Heidelberg, Uni-Padua, Lambert-GA, Stanford, UCAS-China or Toronto declares a `prefers-color-scheme` rule, and meaningful alt text ran at 27 to 48 per cent across the winners while HongKong-JSS, ProFuture-China and WageningenUR hit 90, 86 and 81 per cent and won nothing for it. The winners do all honour `prefers-reduced-motion` — thirteen blocks in Heidelberg's stylesheet, eleven in TU Delft's bundle — and Heidelberg goes further, sniffing for a software WebGL renderer and dropping to a lite mode automatically, with `?lite=0` and `?perf=1` for anyone who wants to look: the motion budget goes to figure interactions and graceful degradation, not to hero spectacle.","body_zh":"四組得獎隊伍中有三組，頁面文字在任何 JavaScript 執行之前就已經存在於 HTML 裡：**Heidelberg** 手寫靜態 HTML，**Uni-Padua-IT** 以 SvelteKit 預先渲染，**Lambert-GA** 用 Astro 建置。TU Delft 是例外，它是一個 3.4 MB bundle 的 Vite 單頁應用，而它刻意用 wiki 根目錄的 `llms.txt`，以及每一頁在 `/tu-delft/<page>.md` 的純 Markdown 鏡像來補償。相對地，對照組——Princeton、Cornell、LYON、UAlberta、UCNZ、Athens、GU Frankfurt 和 Eton-College-UK，全都是 2026 年重量級科學獎項的得主——送出的是 486 位元組到 15 kB 的近乎空殼，在沒有 JS 的情況下最少只有七個字元的文字。\n\n真正的分水嶺是一層明確的摘要層。Uni-Padua-IT 和 Lambert-GA 都提供 `/judging` 頁面，逐條走過每一項獎牌標準，每一項用兩三句話摘要，並深層連結到證據——Padua 直接指向自己的負面結果，Lambert 在摘要裡寫明十五個 minibinder 設計沒有產生任何確認的命中，第二輪二十個設計才做出一個親和力約 604 nM 的 binder。TU Delft 以另一種方式到達同一處：Results 頁上一張插圖式的模組地圖，滑鼠移過會凸顯某個模組，點擊則跳到該模組，涵蓋的正是組織整個專案的那五個模組；Heidelberg 把三張摘要卡放在首屏之上，並給每個導覽連結一行副標，於是「Results」讀起來是「Where data tells the story」。\n\n再往下看，得獎隊伍就只是更具體。**Heidelberg** 的圖說帶有分圖編號、547 ng 與 433 ng 的轉染量、18,000 × g，以及附上範圍的效應量——5.6 倍，依 haze 設定落在 4.3 到 6.4 倍之間——而 Padua 把什麼都沒長出來的培養盤拍下來、編上圖號，並解釋早先一次轉形為何失敗。**TU Delft** 建的是一套內容系統，而不是一疊頁面：1,604 個引用標記對應 735 個不重複的 DOI、724 次詞彙表呼叫對應 102 條定義、307 張自動編號的圖，以及一條從不變動的 Background → Results → Discussion → Future Perspective 骨幹。它的決策矩陣為每一格標上 Factual、Inferred、Estimated 或 Speculative，圖例並說明這個標記記錄的是該格背後證據的強度，而不是判斷本身——把知識論上的誠實做成一個介面元件，這種作法我在別處沒有看到。\n\n沒有決定勝負的因素同樣值得一看。得獎圈內的頁面重量橫跨兩個數量級，從 Lambert-GA 78 kB 的首頁到 TU Delft 的 3.4 MB。Heidelberg、Uni-Padua、Lambert-GA、Stanford、UCAS-China 和 Toronto 都沒有宣告任何 `prefers-color-scheme` 規則；有意義的替代文字在得獎隊伍之間只有 27% 到 48%，而 HongKong-JSS、ProFuture-China 和 WageningenUR 分別達到 90%、86% 和 81%，卻沒有因此得到任何獎。得獎隊伍確實全都尊重 `prefers-reduced-motion`——Heidelberg 的樣式表裡有十三段，TU Delft 的 bundle 裡有十一段——而 Heidelberg 走得更遠，它會偵測軟體 WebGL 轉譯器並自動降為輕量模式，還留了 `?lite=0` 和 `?perf=1` 給想細看的人：動態效果的預算花在圖表互動和優雅降級上，而不是首頁的視覺奇觀。","cards":[{"kicker":"Information architecture","title":"Build a judging page and make it the front door","title_zh":"做一個 judging 頁面，並讓它成為正門","body":"Uni-Padua-IT and Lambert-GA each ship a `/judging` route that indexes every medal criterion and every award they apply for. Each entry is two or three sentences of plain summary followed by a deep link into the page that holds the evidence. Padua links directly to its own failed Design-Build-Test-Learn cycles under Silver; Lambert quotes the binding affinity and the two failed design campaigns in the Gold section. It costs one page and it converts a pile of required sections into a reading order.","body_zh":"Uni-Padua-IT 和 Lambert-GA 各自提供一個 `/judging` 路徑，索引每一條獎牌標準和每一個申請的獎項。每一則是兩三句樸素的摘要，後面接一個深層連結，直通存放證據的頁面。Padua 在銀牌項下直接連到自己失敗的 Design-Build-Test-Learn 循環；Lambert 在金牌段落引用結合親和力和兩次失敗的設計輪次。代價是一頁，換來的是把一堆規定章節轉成一條閱讀動線。","chips":["Uni-Padua-IT","Lambert-GA","2 clicks to evidence","One page"],"chips_zh":["Uni-Padua-IT","Lambert-GA","2 次點擊到證據","一頁到底"],"kicker_zh":"資訊架構"},{"kicker":"Data presentation","title":"Label the provenance of every number you did not measure","title_zh":"為每一個不是你量出來的數字標註來源","body":"TU Delft's entrepreneurship page scores four candidate applications against eleven weighted parameters. Every single cell carries a bracketed tag — [F]actual, [I]nferred, [E]stimated or [S]peculative — and the legend states that the tag records how strong the evidence behind the cell is, not the score, because every score is a judgement applied to sourced facts. The weights sum to 100 per cent and the weighted total is given to two decimals. It is the single most copyable device I found in 2026.","body_zh":"TU Delft 的創業頁面用十一個加權參數為四個候選應用評分。每一格都帶一個方括號標記——[F]actual、[I]nferred、[E]stimated 或 [S]peculative——圖例說明這個標記記錄的是該格背後證據有多強，而不是分數本身，因為每個分數都是對有來源的事實所做的判斷。權重加總為 100%，加權總分給到小數第二位。這是我在 2026 年找到最值得照抄的一項設計。","chips":["TU Delft","F / I / E / S","Weighted matrix","Shows its working"],"chips_zh":["TU Delft","F / I / E / S","加權矩陣","推導全攤開"],"kicker_zh":"資料呈現"},{"kicker":"Human practices","title":"Date every pivot and name who caused it","title_zh":"為每一次轉向標上日期，並指名是誰造成的","body":"Lambert-GA applies one named framework, H.I.V.E. — Hear, Inquire, Validate, Evolve — identically to every stakeholder, then closes with a Project Pivots timeline. Five entries, each with a date, the named expert whose feedback caused it, and a literal before-and-after: nanobody changed to minibinder, P-domain in general changed to specific hotspots. The caption says every change shown came directly from stakeholder feedback rather than internal decisions. It makes integration auditable instead of asserted.","body_zh":"Lambert-GA 對每一位利害關係人都套用同一個具名框架 H.I.V.E.——Hear、Inquire、Validate、Evolve——最後以一條 Project Pivots 時間軸收尾。五則記錄，每一則都有日期、意見造成這次轉向的具名專家，以及字面上的前後對照：nanobody 改成 minibinder，整個 P-domain 改成特定的熱點。圖說寫明所列的每一項改變都直接來自利害關係人的意見，而不是團隊內部的決定。這讓整合變成可查核的，而不是宣稱的。","chips":["Lambert-GA","H.I.V.E.","Dated timeline","Before → after"],"chips_zh":["Lambert-GA","H.I.V.E.","附日期的時間軸","前 → 後"],"kicker_zh":"人類實踐"},{"kicker":"Technical build","title":"Mirror the wiki as plain Markdown","title_zh":"把 wiki 鏡像成純 Markdown","body":"TU Delft's wiki is a Vite single-page app and the heaviest I measured, yet it publishes an `llms.txt` at the wiki root listing twelve pages, each mirrored as plain Markdown at `/tu-delft/<page>.md`. That gives a JS-free fallback, a machine-readable corpus, and a diffable source of truth for the content, all from one build step. If you insist on a client-rendered framework, this is the tax you should pay for it.","body_zh":"TU Delft 的 wiki 是 Vite 單頁應用，也是我量過最重的一個，但它在 wiki 根目錄發布 `llms.txt`，列出十二個頁面，每一頁都在 `/tu-delft/<page>.md` 鏡像成純 Markdown。這一個建置步驟同時換來不需要 JS 的替代方案、一份機器可讀的語料，以及一份可以做 diff 的內容真實來源。如果你堅持要用客戶端渲染的框架，這就是你該付的稅。","chips":["TU Delft","llms.txt","/page.md","JS-free fallback"],"chips_zh":["TU Delft","llms.txt","/page.md","沒有 JS 也能看"],"kicker_zh":"技術實作"},{"kicker":"Figures","title":"Write captions that stand alone, and number the negative control","title_zh":"寫能獨立成立的圖說，並為陰性對照編上圖號","body":"Heidelberg's captions carry panel letters, exact reagent masses, exact centrifugation and pressure conditions, and effect sizes quoted with a range across settings — a reader can take the figure out of the page and still understand it. Uni-Padua-IT goes one better on controls: the plate that grew nothing gets its own numbered figure with the full condition in the caption, sitting beside the plate that grew two colonies. Showing the control is cheap and it is the fastest way to look like you know what you are doing.","body_zh":"Heidelberg 的圖說帶有分圖編號、確切的試劑用量、確切的離心與壓力條件，以及跨設定給出範圍的效應量——讀者把圖從頁面裡拿出來也看得懂。Uni-Padua-IT 在對照組上更進一步：什麼都沒長出來的培養盤有自己的圖號，圖說裡寫出完整條件，就放在長出兩個菌落的培養盤旁邊。把對照組放出來很便宜，而且這是讓人看起來知道自己在做什麼的最快方法。","chips":["Heidelberg","Uni-Padua-IT","Units + n + conditions","Show the control"],"chips_zh":["Heidelberg","Uni-Padua-IT","單位 + n + 條件","把對照組秀出來"],"kicker_zh":"圖表"},{"kicker":"Build discipline","title":"Keep content out of components","title_zh":"別把內容寫進元件裡","body":"Stanford University — Grand Prize winner and a Best Wiki nominee, though not a winner — stores each page as a single hand-written JavaScript object with a documented block grammar of p, sh, gal, list, table, steps, math and quotes, plus a per-page accent colour and icon. TU Delft does the equivalent in MDX with a fixed component vocabulary. Either way the layout is written once and the copy is written by people who are not touching layout, which is why neither wiki drifts between pages.","body_zh":"Stanford University——總冠軍得主，也是最佳 Wiki 入圍者，但沒有得獎——把每一頁存成一個手寫的 JavaScript 物件，配上一套文件化的區塊語法：p、sh、gal、list、table、steps、math 和 quotes，再加上每頁自己的強調色與圖示。TU Delft 則用 MDX 搭配固定的元件詞彙做到同一件事。不論哪一種，版面只寫一次，文字由不碰版面的人來寫，這就是這兩個 wiki 不會在頁與頁之間走樣的原因。","chips":["Stanford University","TU Delft","One file per page","Block grammar"],"chips_zh":["Stanford University","TU Delft","一頁一個檔案","區塊語法"],"kicker_zh":"建置紀律"},{"kicker":"Craft","title":"Degrade on purpose, not by accident","title_zh":"刻意降級，而不是意外降級","body":"Heidelberg's wiki detects a software WebGL renderer on load and automatically switches to a lite mode, with `?lite=0` and `?lite=1` to force it either way and `?perf=1` to load a performance reporter. Its stylesheet carries thirteen `prefers-reduced-motion` blocks; TU Delft's bundle carries eleven. The winners treat a judge on a tired laptop as a real user. Nobody built a dark mode, and nobody needed one.","body_zh":"Heidelberg 的 wiki 在載入時偵測軟體 WebGL 轉譯器，並自動切換到輕量模式，另有 `?lite=0` 和 `?lite=1` 可以強制切換，`?perf=1` 則載入效能回報器。它的樣式表裡有十三段 `prefers-reduced-motion`；TU Delft 的 bundle 裡有十一段。得獎隊伍把用著一台老舊筆電的評審當成真實使用者。沒有人做深色模式，也沒有人需要。","chips":["Heidelberg","?lite=1","prefers-reduced-motion","Hardware sniffing"],"chips_zh":["Heidelberg","?lite=1","prefers-reduced-motion","偵測硬體"],"kicker_zh":"工藝"}],"table":{"head":["Wiki","Section","Framework / build","The one thing it does best"],"head_zh":["Wiki","組別","框架／建置","它做得最好的一件事"],"rows":[["Heidelberg","Undergrad — winner","Hand-written static HTML, Bootstrap plus a 77 kB token layer; ~1 MB of HTML, CSS and JS","Journal-grade figure captions, and an automatic lite mode for weak GPUs"],["Uni-Padua-IT","Undergrad — winner","SvelteKit, prerendered; 266 kB across 17 code-split files","A /judging page that links each medal criterion straight at the evidence, failures included"],["TU Delft","Overgrad — winner","Vite SPA, one 3.4 MB bundle, 16 flat routes; MDX content with a fixed component vocabulary","Per-cell evidence-provenance labels, plus every page mirrored as Markdown behind llms.txt"],["Lambert-GA","High School — winner","Astro, fully static; 78 kB of HTML, CSS and JS on the homepage","A dated pivot timeline that attributes each project change to a named stakeholder"],["Stanford University","Undergrad — nominee","Client-rendered template app; 15 hand-written content files with a documented block grammar","Content fully separated from layout, so nothing drifts between pages"],["UCAS-China","Undergrad — nominee","Static HTML, 18 pages including a /medal index","An odometer-style opening statistic that lands the problem in one screen"]],"rows_zh":[["Heidelberg","大學組——得獎","手寫靜態 HTML，Bootstrap 加一層 77 kB 的 token 層；HTML、CSS 與 JS 合計約 1 MB","期刊級的圖說，以及針對弱 GPU 的自動輕量模式"],["Uni-Padua-IT","大學組——得獎","SvelteKit，預先渲染；17 個程式碼分割檔案共 266 kB","/judging 頁面把每一條獎牌標準直接連到證據，失敗的部分也包含在內"],["TU Delft","研究生組——得獎","Vite 單頁應用，單一 3.4 MB bundle，16 條扁平路由；MDX 內容搭配固定的元件詞彙","逐格標註證據來源，並把每一頁鏡像成 Markdown 放在 llms.txt 後面"],["Lambert-GA","高中組——得獎","Astro，完全靜態；首頁的 HTML、CSS 與 JS 合計 78 kB","一條標了日期的轉向時間軸，把每次專案變更歸因到具名的利害關係人"],["Stanford University","大學組——入圍","客戶端渲染的樣板應用；15 個手寫內容檔，搭配文件化的區塊語法","內容與版面完全分離，所以頁與頁之間不會走樣"],["UCAS-China","大學組——入圍","靜態 HTML，18 個頁面，含一個 /medal 索引","里程表式的開場統計數字，一個畫面就把問題講清楚"]]},"checklist":["Ship HTML that already contains your words — prerender, or mirror every page as Markdown with an llms.txt, as TU Delft did.","Build a /judging page that answers each medal criterion in two or three sentences and deep-links the evidence.","State the controlling question on the first screen and repeat it in the same words on every summary layer.","Put a three-card or five-module summary above the detail on every long page, before any subsection.","Fix one spine for every results subsection — Background, Results, Discussion, Future Perspective — and never vary it.","Write captions that stand alone: panel letters, exact conditions, units, n, and the effect size with its range.","Photograph the negative control and give it a figure number of its own.","Name your failures with numbers, and name them in the executive layer rather than burying them.","Tag the provenance of every number you did not measure yourself — factual, inferred, estimated or speculative.","Keep content in one data file per page with a documented block grammar; let layout be written once.","Date every human-practices pivot, name the person whose feedback caused it, and show before and after.","Honour prefers-reduced-motion and spend the motion budget on figure interactions, not on the hero."],"checklist_zh":["送出已經包含你文字的 HTML——預先渲染，或像 TU Delft 那樣把每一頁鏡像成 Markdown 並配上 llms.txt。","做一個 /judging 頁面，用兩三句話回答每一條獎牌標準，並深層連結到證據。","在第一個畫面就寫出主導問題，並在每一層摘要用一模一樣的字重複它。","在每一個長頁面的細節之前，放上三張卡片或五個模組的摘要，排在任何子章節之前。","為每一個結果子章節固定同一條骨幹——Background、Results、Discussion、Future Perspective——而且絕不變動。","寫能獨立成立的圖說：分圖編號、確切條件、單位、n，以及附上範圍的效應量。","把陰性對照拍下來，並給它自己的圖號。","用數字說出你的失敗，而且要說在摘要層裡，不要埋起來。","為每一個不是你自己量出來的數字標註來源——事實、推論、估計或推測。","把內容放在每頁一個資料檔裡，搭配文件化的區塊語法；版面只寫一次。","為每一次人類實踐的轉向標上日期、指名是誰的意見造成的，並呈現前後對照。","尊重 prefers-reduced-motion，把動態效果的預算花在圖表互動上，而不是首頁主視覺。"],"antipatterns":["Dark mode and theme toggles. Not one of Heidelberg, Uni-Padua-IT, Lambert-GA, Stanford, UCAS-China or Toronto declares a prefers-color-scheme rule, and all of them placed well.","A late alt-text compliance sweep. The four winners ran 27 to 48 per cent meaningful alt text while HongKong-JSS (90 per cent), ProFuture-China (86) and WageningenUR (81) all beat them and none was a Best Wiki winner — it is a floor, not a differentiator, so do it early and cheaply.","Huge homepage media galleries. Toronto pulls 214 images and 252 .avif references on the homepage alone and ETH-Zurich serves a single 1.9 MB HTML page; neither won Best Wiki.","A client-rendered SPA with no text fallback. This is the default in the control group — Princeton, Cornell, LYON, UAlberta, UCNZ, Athens, GU Frankfurt and Eton-College-UK all serve near-empty shells despite winning major science prizes.","Per-page mascots, bespoke icon sets and per-page accent colours. Stanford invested in all three and placed as a nominee; none of the four winners has a mascot system.","Treating the mandatory section list as the information architecture. A deep-linked judging index does the same job in one page and reads as an argument rather than a form."],"antipatterns_zh":["深色模式與主題切換。Heidelberg、Uni-Padua-IT、Lambert-GA、Stanford、UCAS-China 和 Toronto 沒有一個宣告 prefers-color-scheme 規則，而他們的名次全都不錯。","最後才做一輪替代文字合規清查。四組得獎隊伍有意義的替代文字只有 27% 到 48%，而 HongKong-JSS（90%）、ProFuture-China（86%）和 WageningenUR（81%）都勝過他們，卻沒有一個是最佳 Wiki 得主——這是底線，不是差異點，所以早做、便宜做就好。","首頁放巨大的媒體圖庫。Toronto 光首頁就拉了 214 張圖和 252 個 .avif 參照，ETH-Zurich 送出單一 1.9 MB 的 HTML 頁面；兩者都沒有拿到最佳 Wiki。","客戶端渲染的單頁應用，而且沒有任何文字替代方案。這是對照組的預設做法——Princeton、Cornell、LYON、UAlberta、UCNZ、Athens、GU Frankfurt 和 Eton-College-UK 全都送出近乎空殼的頁面，儘管他們都拿下了重要的科學獎項。","每頁一隻吉祥物、客製圖示組和每頁不同的強調色。Stanford 三者都投資了，結果只是入圍；四組得獎隊伍沒有一個有吉祥物系統。","把規定的章節清單當成資訊架構。一個深層連結的 judging 索引用一頁就做到同一件事，而且讀起來像論證，不像表格。"],"method":"I rendered and read the four winners in full — Heidelberg, Uni-Padua-IT, TU Delft and Lambert-GA — by fetching their page HTML directly where it is server-rendered, by reading TU Delft's Markdown mirrors, and by loading the client-rendered pages in a browser; counts of references, figures, components, image formats, alt attributes and prefers-reduced-motion rules were taken from the shipped source. I sampled around thirty nominees and controls more shallowly, measuring framework, rendered text length, asset weight and alt-text coverage for all of them, and reading Stanford's and UCAS-China's content in detail as the closest nominees. I could not render several Vite single-page nominees deeply — Oxford, UCSC, NUS-Singapore, KAUST-KSA, Muenster-University, IISER-Kolkata and UOttawa among them — because a shared browser pane kept being navigated away mid-session, so they are excluded from the table and their design is not characterised here; I also did not measure real-world load time, mobile layout or screen-reader behaviour beyond the markup.","method_zh":"我完整渲染並讀過四組得獎隊伍——Heidelberg、Uni-Padua-IT、TU Delft 和 Lambert-GA：伺服器端渲染的部分直接抓取頁面 HTML，TU Delft 的部分讀它的 Markdown 鏡像，客戶端渲染的頁面則在瀏覽器中載入；引用、圖、元件、影像格式、alt 屬性和 prefers-reduced-motion 規則的數量，都取自實際送出的原始碼。我以較淺的方式抽樣約三十組入圍隊伍與對照隊伍，為全部這些隊伍量測框架、渲染後文字長度、資產重量和替代文字覆蓋率，並把 Stanford 與 UCAS-China 的內容當成最接近的入圍者細讀。有幾組 Vite 單頁應用的入圍隊伍我無法深入渲染——包括 Oxford、UCSC、NUS-Singapore、KAUST-KSA、Muenster-University、IISER-Kolkata 和 UOttawa——因為共用的瀏覽器面板在過程中一直被導向其他頁面，所以它們不列入表格，本文也不描述它們的設計；此外，除了標記語言本身之外，我沒有量測真實的載入時間、行動版版面或螢幕閱讀器行為。","kicker_zh":"原創分析","order":32},{"id":"collaboration-network","tab":"teams","order":34,"kicker":"Original analysis","kicker_zh":"原創分析","title":"Who worked with whom in 2026","title_zh":"2026 年誰和誰合作","lede":"Sixty-nine of the 106 decorated teams record working with at least one other iGEM team; thirty-seven record none. Almost all of it is meet-ups. Not one team in the cohort ran an inter-lab measurement ring, and the team that offered to run the nearest thing got no replies. GEMS-Taiwan has no collaboration page and appears on nobody else's — and still took Top 10 and three wins, which is the uncomfortable part.","lede_zh":"106 支得獎隊伍中有 69 支記錄了與至少一支其他 iGEM 隊伍的合作，37 支完全沒有。這些合作幾乎都是聚會。整個群體裡沒有任何一支隊伍跑過跨實驗室的量測環（inter-lab measurement ring），而唯一提出最接近做法的隊伍，一封回覆都沒收到。GEMS-Taiwan 沒有合作頁面，也沒出現在任何其他隊伍的頁面上——卻仍然拿下 Top 10 與三項大獎，而這正是尷尬的地方。","body":"Across the 106 researched team files, **69 teams document working with at least one other iGEM team and 37 document none**. The forms are not equally weighted. The dominant one by a wide margin is the **regional meet-up**: BFH's European Meet-Up in Hamburg on 15–17 May (third edition, co-run by Bielefeld, Frankfurt and Hamburg), KIT's first iGEM Baden-Württemberg Meetup on 13 June with eight German teams, HUST-China's First Central-China iGEM Forum on 12 July with fifteen teams, Uni-Padua-IT's Italian Meet-Up in the Botanical Garden of Padua on 25 July with Bologna and Milan, NYCU-Taiwan's Taiwan iGEMers Meet-Up on 27 July, Labi-Taiwan's TGEM at National Taiwan University on 22 August, Grand APiC at SUSTech and the University of Hong Kong on 16–19 August, ETH-Zurich's Swiss iGEM Meetup for five teams, Baltimore's Mid-Atlantic Meetup with nine regional teams, TAU-Israel's online Mini-Jamboree with eight. Below that sit mentorship of school teams by university teams, co-authored community publications, peer review, and a long tail of poster boards and podcast guest slots.\n\nSort them by whether a third party can use the output and the list gets short. **What survives contact with a stranger**: JLU-FBH's myth-busting handbook *Together with iGEM: Across Villages, From Myths to Facts*, chief-edited across submissions from 17-plus teams; HBUT-China's five-school joint biosafety manual for anti-tumour projects, written with ZJU-China, BNU-China, JLU-FBH and ZJUT-China and released as a downloadable PDF with deliberately differentiable risk protocols because the five teams use different carriers; SJTU-BioX-Shanghai's cross-team Education Activity Handbook, where they took responsibility for Part 7; the MSP Vector peer-reviewed iGEM journal run from Maastricht, where Madrid-UCM refereed three other teams' papers and Stockholm contributed a literature review and reviewed in turn; McGill's BIOME Book, to which NYCU-Taiwan supplied the text and concept for an LbCas12a entry and McGill supplied the artwork; and KCIS-Xiugang-Taipei and HKSSC splitting the central dogma between them into two physical teaching models over two planning calls on 20 August and 19 September, sharing prototypes through a common Drive, then each adapting to its own audience — KCIS rebuilding HKSSC's flat felt translation framework as a 3D tactile box with slotted E, P and A sites for seven students at the Taipei School for the Visually Impaired. **What does not**: icebreakers, rock stacking, beanbag toss, community blackboards, 'we met other teams and exchanged ideas'. NYCU-Taiwan says the quiet part itself on its own wiki: documenting an event does not by itself demonstrate its long-term impact.\n\nThe biggest hole in 2026 is technical. **Not one of the 106 teams ran an inter-lab measurement ring** — the same construct or sample measured by several teams on several instruments, with the between-lab spread published. The closest anyone came was negative. Uni-Padua-IT, who went on to win Best Software Tool and Best Wiki in the Undergraduate section, wrote on their software page: *\"On 9 August 2026 we published an open call for collaboration to validate the software and shared it in the two ways that actually reach people: on our social media channels and directly with other iGEM teams. The offer was simple: tell us your chassis, and we will optimise a sequence for it and send the result back. Unfortunately, we did not receive any replies.\"* The only genuine independent replications in the cohort came from outside iGEM — four mechanical engineering students at Hanyang University rebuilt PSI Korea's reader from the released documentation alone — or across years, where HongKong-HS generated its toehold candidates with miRADAR, the tool Wageningen released in 2024, and Mingdao re-characterised the cenA part lineage (Edinburgh 2008, CAU_China 2019, XMU-China 2019, SYSU-CHINA 2021) at 34 °C in Bis-Tris pH 6.4 instead of the standard 50 °C acidic assay. Live part or sample exchange between two 2026 teams: essentially absent.\n\n**Does it correlate with placing? Honestly, no.** Coding the 106 files three ways — substantive co-production (S, n = 48), attendance or visibility only (A, n = 21), nothing documented (N, n = 37) — gives Top 10 rates of 14/48 (29%), 10/21 (48%) and 6/37 (16%), and at-least-one-win rates of 29/48 (60%), 10/21 (48%) and 15/37 (41%). The hypothesis that substantive beats attendance runs the wrong way and is not significant (Fisher exact p = 0.17). The only thing with any signal is the crude contrast — any documented inter-team work, 24/69 Top 10, against none, 6/37 — and that is p = 0.069, suggestive at best, and confounded by the fact that teams who write more win more. The two biggest connectors in the whole network, Bielefeld-CeBiTec, which ran the European Meet-Up and the Community Blackboard that roughly 37 teams passed through, and JLU-FBH, which chief-edited the 17-team handbook, each took a Gold medal and nothing else. **One award does correlate, and it is the one other teams vote for.** Both 2026 iGEMers Prizes went to the most documented community builders in their tier: HUST-China, which hosted a fifteen-team forum and wrote entries into two other teams' publications, and Labi-Taiwan, which runs TGEM. Judges did not reward collaboration in 2026. Peers did.\n\nTaiwan ran **two** national events and GEMS-Taiwan was at neither. NYCU-Taiwan hosted the 2026 Taiwan iGEMers Meet-Up at Xian-Qi Hall on the Bo-Ai Campus on 27 July: 53 students and advisors, five Taiwanese teams (NYCU-Taiwan, HIA-Taiwan, NCKU-Tainan, VIS, WIST) plus Okinawa joining online, four icebreakers, five roundtable themes, two guest speakers, five fifteen-minute mock presentations, and — the part that matters — an iGEM Team Operations Guide compiled from the roundtable notes plus published preparation SOPs, registration templates and schedules for future organisers. Labi-Taiwan ran the fourth TGEM on 22 August at the Boya Building, National Taiwan University, co-hosted with NTU's Department of Biochemical Science and Technology: a mock competition of five-minute pitches and twenty-minute interrogation by professors, PIs and industry judges. TGEM has run annually since 2023, founded by Kang Chiao International School Linkou, Labi-Taiwan's own predecessor. Its named 2026 participants include NTHU Taiwan, Claremont CA, AEI Prep-Taiwan and KCIS-Xiugang-Taipei. NCKU-Tainan is the busiest Taiwanese partner on record: Mingdao mentorship on 7 March, the NYCU meet-up in July, a full online session with WIST on 17 September covering wet-lab bottlenecks and a dry-lab model comparison, CCU-Taiwan on 19 September, HIA-Taiwan on 20 September, and TAU-Israel's eight-team Mini-Jamboree on 8 October alongside NTHU. **GEMS-Taiwan has no /collaborations page, no /partnership page, and no other iGEM team named anywhere on its wiki.** Its one listed 'partner team' is Geospatial Analysis, an internal sub-team.\n\nA closing warning about the evidence. **Collaboration claims in 2026 are frequently one-sided.** NCKU-Tainan documents mentoring Mingdao in March and a detailed technical session with WIST in September; neither Mingdao's nor WIST's wiki mentions NCKU-Tainan. ASIJ-Tokyo lists KCIS Xiugang among eight partner teams; KCIS-Xiugang-Taipei's collaboration page names only HKSSC. NYCU-Taiwan lists WIST as a meet-up attendee; WIST's pages do not mention the event. Where a claim appears on one wiki and not the other, the collaboration was usually real and the documentation was unilateral — which is itself the lesson. The partner who writes it up gets the credit and the reusable artefact; the partner who does not gets a photograph.","body_zh":"在 106 份隊伍研究檔案中，**69 支隊伍記錄了與至少一支其他 iGEM 隊伍的合作，37 支完全沒有**。但各種形式的份量並不相等。遙遙領先的主流形式是**區域聚會**：BFH 於 5 月 15 至 17 日在 Hamburg 舉辦的 European Meet-Up（第三屆，由 Bielefeld、Frankfurt 與 Hamburg 三隊合辦）、KIT 於 6 月 13 日舉辦的第一屆 iGEM Baden-Württemberg Meetup（八支德國隊伍）、HUST-China 於 7 月 12 日舉辦的第一屆華中 iGEM 論壇（15 支隊伍）、Uni-Padua-IT 於 7 月 25 日在 Botanical Garden of Padua 舉辦的 Italian Meet-Up（與 Bologna、Milan）、NYCU-Taiwan 於 7 月 27 日的 Taiwan iGEMers Meet-Up、Labi-Taiwan 於 8 月 22 日在台灣大學舉辦的 TGEM、8 月 16 至 19 日在 SUSTech 與香港大學舉行的 Grand APiC、ETH-Zurich 為五支隊伍合辦的 Swiss iGEM Meetup、Baltimore 參加的九隊 Mid-Atlantic Meetup，以及 TAU-Israel 八隊的線上 Mini-Jamboree。再往下才是大學隊伍對中學隊伍的指導、跨隊共同著作、同儕審查，以及一長串海報牆與播客客座。\n\n若以「第三方能不能拿去用」來篩選，清單立刻變短。**能通過陌生人檢驗的**：由 JLU-FBH 擔任主編、彙整 17 支以上隊伍投稿的破除迷思手冊《Together with iGEM: Across Villages, From Myths to Facts》；HBUT-China 與 ZJU-China、BNU-China、JLU-FBH、ZJUT-China 合寫的五校抗腫瘤專案聯合生物安全手冊，以 PDF 公開，並因五隊載體不同而刻意設計成可區分的風險評估流程；SJTU-BioX-Shanghai 參與的跨隊教育活動手冊，他們負責第 7 部分；由 Maastricht 營運的同儕審查期刊 MSP Vector，Madrid-UCM 在其中審了三支隊伍的論文，Stockholm 投了一篇文獻回顧並參與審查；McGill 的 BIOME Book，NYCU-Taiwan 提供 LbCas12a 條目的文字與概念、McGill 負責繪圖；以及 KCIS-Xiugang-Taipei 與 HKSSC 把中心法則一分為二做成兩套實體教具——8 月 20 日與 9 月 19 日兩次線上規劃會議、以共用 Google Drive 交換原型，然後各自針對自己的受眾改編：KCIS 把 HKSSC 的平面不織布轉譯框架重做成帶有 E、P、A 位點凹槽的立體觸覺盒，給台北啟明學校的七名學生使用。**通不過的**：破冰遊戲、疊疊樂、沙包投擲、社群佈告欄、「我們和其他隊伍交換了想法」。NYCU-Taiwan 自己在 wiki 上就把話說破了：把活動記錄下來，本身並不能證明它的長期影響。\n\n2026 年最大的缺口在技術面。**106 支隊伍中沒有任何一支跑過跨實驗室量測環**——也就是同一個構築體或樣本由數支隊伍在各自儀器上量測，並公布實驗室之間的差異。最接近的一次，結果是零。後來拿下大專組 Best Software Tool 與 Best Wiki 的 Uni-Padua-IT 在軟體頁上寫道：*「2026 年 8 月 9 日，我們發出一份公開的合作邀請，希望有人協助驗證這個軟體，並用兩種真的能觸及到人的管道發布：我們的社群媒體，以及直接寄給其他 iGEM 隊伍。條件很簡單：告訴我們你的宿主，我們幫你最佳化一條序列再寄回去。可惜的是，我們沒有收到任何回覆。」* 這個群體裡唯一真正的獨立重現來自 iGEM 之外——四名 Hanyang University 的機械工程系學生，僅憑公開文件就重建了 PSI Korea 的判讀器——或是跨年度的：HongKong-HS 用 Wageningen 2024 年釋出的 miRADAR 產生 toehold 候選序列，Mingdao 則在 34 °C、Bis-Tris pH 6.4 的條件下重新表徵 cenA 這條零件血脈（Edinburgh 2008、CAU_China 2019、XMU-China 2019、SYSU-CHINA 2021），而不是沿用標準的 50 °C 酸性條件。至於兩支 2026 年隊伍之間真正的零件或樣本交換：基本上不存在。\n\n**那合作和名次有關嗎？老實說，沒有。** 把 106 份檔案分成三類——實質共同產出（S，n = 48）、僅出席或露臉（A，n = 21）、沒有任何記錄（N，n = 37）——Top 10 的比例分別是 14/48（29%）、10/21（48%）與 6/37（16%）；至少拿下一項大獎的比例是 29/48（60%）、10/21（48%）與 15/37（41%）。「實質合作勝過單純出席」這個假設方向是反的，而且不顯著（Fisher 精確檢定 p = 0.17）。唯一還有點訊號的是最粗的對比——有任何跨隊記錄者 24/69 進 Top 10，對上完全沒有的 6/37——但 p = 0.069，最多只能說有暗示，而且還被一個事實干擾：寫得多的隊伍本來就得獎得多。整個網路裡兩個最大的連結點，辦了 European Meet-Up 與大約 37 隊經手的 Community Blackboard 的 Bielefeld-CeBiTec，以及主編 17 隊手冊的 JLU-FBH，各自只拿到一面金牌，別無其他。**只有一個獎項真的相關，而那個獎是其他隊伍投出來的。** 2026 年兩座 iGEMers Prize 都落在各自組別中社群建設記錄最完整的隊伍：主辦 15 隊論壇並為另外兩隊的出版品撰稿的 HUST-China，以及營運 TGEM 的 Labi-Taiwan。2026 年評審沒有獎勵合作，同儕有。\n\n台灣辦了**兩場**全國性活動，而 GEMS-Taiwan 兩場都不在。NYCU-Taiwan 於 7 月 27 日在博愛校區賢齊廳舉辦 2026 Taiwan iGEMers Meet-Up：53 名學生與指導老師、五支台灣隊伍（NYCU-Taiwan、HIA-Taiwan、NCKU-Tainan、VIS、WIST）外加線上參與的 Okinawa、四項破冰活動、五個圓桌主題、兩位講者、五場十五分鐘的模擬簡報，以及真正重要的那一項——把圓桌便利貼整理成一份 iGEM Team Operations Guide，並公開籌備 SOP、報名表單範本與議程，供未來的主辦者沿用。Labi-Taiwan 則於 8 月 22 日在台灣大學博雅教學館舉辦第四屆 TGEM，與台大生化科技學系合辦：模擬競賽採五分鐘簡報加二十分鐘由教授、PI 與業界評審提問的形式。TGEM 自 2023 年起每年舉辦，由康橋國際學校林口校區創立，也就是 Labi-Taiwan 自己的前身。2026 年具名的參與隊伍包括 NTHU Taiwan、Claremont CA、AEI Prep-Taiwan 與 KCIS-Xiugang-Taipei。NCKU-Tainan 是記錄上最忙碌的台灣夥伴：3 月 7 日指導 Mingdao、7 月的 NYCU 聚會、9 月 17 日與 WIST 的完整線上交流（涵蓋濕式實驗瓶頸與乾式建模比較）、9 月 19 日與 CCU-Taiwan、9 月 20 日與 HIA-Taiwan，以及 10 月 8 日和 NTHU 一起參加 TAU-Israel 的八隊 Mini-Jamboree。**GEMS-Taiwan 沒有 /collaborations 頁、沒有 /partnership 頁，整個 wiki 上也沒有提到任何一支其他 iGEM 隊伍。** 它唯一列出的「夥伴隊伍」是 Geospatial Analysis，那是隊內的分組。\n\n最後對證據本身提一個警告。**2026 年的合作宣稱經常只有單方面記錄。** NCKU-Tainan 詳述了三月指導 Mingdao、九月與 WIST 的技術交流；Mingdao 與 WIST 的 wiki 都沒提到 NCKU-Tainan。ASIJ-Tokyo 把 KCIS Xiugang 列入八支夥伴隊伍；KCIS-Xiugang-Taipei 的合作頁只寫了 HKSSC。NYCU-Taiwan 把 WIST 列為聚會出席者；WIST 的頁面沒提這場活動。當一項宣稱只出現在其中一方的 wiki 上，合作通常是真的，單方面的是記錄——而這本身就是教訓：寫下來的那一方拿到功勞，也拿到那個可重複使用的成果；沒寫的那一方只拿到照片。","cards":[{"kicker":"Taiwan · 27 July","kicker_zh":"台灣 · 7 月 27 日","title":"NYCU-Taiwan's Taiwan iGEMers Meet-Up","title_zh":"NYCU-Taiwan 的 Taiwan iGEMers Meet-Up","body":"53 students and advisors from five Taiwanese teams — NYCU-Taiwan, HIA-Taiwan, NCKU-Tainan, VIS and WIST — at Xian-Qi Hall, Bo-Ai Campus, with Okinawa joining online for a sixth. Four icebreakers, five roundtable themes, two guest speakers, five fifteen-minute mock presentations. The reusable outputs are an iGEM Team Operations Guide compiled from the roundtable notes, plus preparation SOPs, registration form templates and event schedules published for future organisers. NYCU reached Okinawa by flying there in person first. HIA-Taiwan ran a separate bilateral exchange with NYCU on 21 July and surveyed it: 73.3 percent of participants rated their understanding of the other team's project 4 or 5.","body_zh":"53 名學生與指導老師，來自五支台灣隊伍——NYCU-Taiwan、HIA-Taiwan、NCKU-Tainan、VIS 與 WIST——地點在博愛校區賢齊廳，Okinawa 以線上方式成為第六隊。四項破冰活動、五個圓桌主題、兩位講者、五場十五分鐘模擬簡報。可重複使用的成果是從圓桌便利貼整理出的 iGEM Team Operations Guide，加上公開給未來主辦者的籌備 SOP、報名表單範本與活動議程。NYCU 是先親自飛去沖繩才連上 Okinawa 的。HIA-Taiwan 另外在 7 月 21 日與 NYCU 做了一場雙邊交流並做了問卷：73.3% 的參與者對另一隊專案的理解程度自評 4 或 5 分。","chips":["53 attendees","5 Taiwan teams","+1 online","27 Jul 2026"],"chips_zh":["53 人出席","5 支台灣隊伍","+1 線上","2026 年 7 月 27 日"],"link":"https://2026.igem.wiki/nycu-taiwan/collaborations","linkText":"NYCU-Taiwan collaborations"},{"kicker":"Taiwan · 22 August","kicker_zh":"台灣 · 8 月 22 日","title":"TGEM, the fourth Taiwan iGEM Meetup","title_zh":"TGEM，第四屆台灣 iGEM 聚會","body":"Hosted by Labi-Taiwan at the Boya Building, National Taiwan University, co-hosted with NTU's Department of Biochemical Science and Technology. Format: a five-minute project overview followed by twenty minutes of questions from professors, principal investigators, industry professionals and advisers, then ten-minute village presentations. Running annually since 2023, founded by Kang Chiao International School Linkou — Labi-Taiwan's own predecessor, which competed as Taipei-KCISLK V1 to V3. Named 2026 participants include NTHU Taiwan, Claremont CA, AEI Prep-Taiwan and KCIS-Xiugang-Taipei, whose wiki records the full judging transcript and the four engineering changes it forced. Labi-Taiwan won the peer-voted iGEMers Prize in the High School section.","body_zh":"由 Labi-Taiwan 在台灣大學博雅教學館主辦，與台大生化科技學系合辦。形式為五分鐘專案概述，接著二十分鐘由教授、計畫主持人、業界專業人士與指導老師提問，之後是十分鐘的 village 簡報。自 2023 年起每年舉辦，由康橋國際學校林口校區創立——也就是 Labi-Taiwan 自己的前身，曾以 Taipei-KCISLK V1 至 V3 參賽。2026 年具名的參與隊伍包括 NTHU Taiwan、Claremont CA、AEI Prep-Taiwan 與 KCIS-Xiugang-Taipei，後者的 wiki 完整記錄了評審問答，以及因此促成的四項工程修正。Labi-Taiwan 拿下高中組由各隊互投的 iGEMers Prize。","chips":["4th edition","NTU Boya Building","22 Aug 2026","iGEMers Prize host"],"chips_zh":["第四屆","台大博雅教學館","2026 年 8 月 22 日","iGEMers Prize 主辦"],"link":"https://2026.igem.wiki/labi-taiwan/education?tab=tgem","linkText":"Labi-Taiwan on TGEM"},{"kicker":"The null result","kicker_zh":"零結果","title":"Nobody answered Uni-Padua","title_zh":"沒有人回覆 Uni-Padua","body":"On 9 August 2026 Uni-Padua-IT published an open call offering to codon-optimise any team's sequence for its chassis with ReTIsigner and send the result back, pushed through social media and directly to other iGEM teams. They received no replies, and they say so on the wiki. They went on to win Best Software Tool and Best Wiki in the Undergraduate section anyway. Read alongside the fact that not one of the 106 decorated teams ran an inter-lab measurement ring, the conclusion is that 2026's network carried people and slides but almost no reagents, constructs or measurements.","body_zh":"2026 年 8 月 9 日，Uni-Padua-IT 發出公開邀請，提議用 ReTIsigner 替任何隊伍針對其宿主做密碼子最佳化並把結果寄回，透過社群媒體與直接聯繫其他 iGEM 隊伍兩種管道發布。他們沒有收到任何回覆，並把這件事寫在 wiki 上。即便如此，他們仍拿下大專組 Best Software Tool 與 Best Wiki。把這件事和「106 支得獎隊伍中沒有任何一支跑過跨實驗室量測環」放在一起看，結論是：2026 年的網路輸送了人和投影片，卻幾乎沒有輸送試劑、構築體或量測數據。","chips":["0 replies","9 Aug 2026","0 inter-lab rings / 106"],"chips_zh":["0 則回覆","2026 年 8 月 9 日","跨實驗室環 0/106"],"link":"https://2026.igem.wiki/uni-padua-it/software","linkText":"Uni-Padua-IT software page"},{"kicker":"The one co-produced artefact","kicker_zh":"唯一的共同產出","title":"KCIS-Xiugang-Taipei × HKSSC","title_zh":"KCIS-Xiugang-Taipei × HKSSC","body":"Two virtual planning sessions, 20 August and 19 September. They split the central dogma: KCIS built a sequential LEGO track for transcription and gene regulation, HKSSC built an mRNA translation model with slotted E, P and A sites. Prototypes were exchanged as photo and video logs through a shared Google Drive, then each team deployed to its own audience — HKSSC for general science teaching in Hong Kong, KCIS rebuilding HKSSC's flat felt framework as a 3D tactile box with pipe-cleaner tRNA and Styrofoam amino acids for seven students at the Taipei School for the Visually Impaired. KCIS reports the limits too: N = 7, no pre-test, 4 of 7 found the tactile markers helpful. This is the only Taiwan-linked collaboration in 2026 that produced a physical object two teams can both hand on.","body_zh":"兩次線上規劃會議，8 月 20 日與 9 月 19 日。兩隊把中心法則一分為二：KCIS 做出一條依序推進的樂高軌道，呈現轉錄與基因調控；HKSSC 做出帶有 E、P、A 位點凹槽的 mRNA 轉譯模型。原型以照片與影片記錄，透過共用的 Google Drive 交換，然後各自投入自己的受眾——HKSSC 用於香港校內的一般科學教學，KCIS 則把 HKSSC 的平面不織布框架重做成立體觸覺盒，以毛根代表 tRNA、保麗龍球代表胺基酸，給台北啟明學校的七名學生使用。KCIS 也寫出了限制：N = 7、沒有前測、七人中有四人覺得觸覺標記有幫助。這是 2026 年唯一一項與台灣有關、並產出兩隊都能繼續傳下去的實體成果的合作。","chips":["2 planning calls","shared Drive","N = 7 pupils","Taipei × Hong Kong"],"chips_zh":["2 次籌備會議","共用 Google Drive","N = 7 名學生","台北 × 香港"],"link":"https://2026.igem.wiki/kcis-xiugang-taipei/collaboration","linkText":"KCIS-Xiugang collaboration page"},{"kicker":"The hubs","kicker_zh":"樞紐","title":"HUST-China: fifteen teams, one forum, one peer prize","title_zh":"HUST-China：十五支隊伍、一場論壇、一座同儕獎","body":"On 12 July 2026 HUST-China independently hosted the First Central-China iGEM Forum at the Qiming College Maker Space, replicating the Jamboree's own structure — opening speeches, keynotes, a LiveStage block, judge comment sessions and poster booths — for fifteen online and offline teams, of which fourteen presented and received targeted commentary. They then wrote a full entry into JLU-FBH's 17-team myth-busting handbook and specialised content into BUCT's air-to-protein publication, mutually reviewed and published on BUCT's wiki. They won the peer-voted iGEMers Prize. The other 2026 iGEMers Prize, in the High School section, went to Labi-Taiwan, which runs TGEM. Two for two: the prize other teams vote for went to the two biggest community builders.","body_zh":"2026 年 7 月 12 日，HUST-China 獨力在啟明學院創客空間舉辦第一屆華中 iGEM 論壇，刻意複製 Jamboree 本身的架構——開幕致詞、主題演講、LiveStage 時段、評審評論環節與海報攤位——共 15 支線上與線下隊伍參與，其中 14 支依序報告並收到具體評論。之後他們為 JLU-FBH 統整的 17 隊破除迷思手冊獨立撰寫了一則完整條目，也為 BUCT 的「空氣變蛋白」科普出版品提供專業內容，經互審後刊在 BUCT 的 wiki 上。他們拿下各隊互投的 iGEMers Prize。2026 年另一座 iGEMers Prize 在高中組，得主是營運 TGEM 的 Labi-Taiwan。兩座全中：由其他隊伍投票的獎項，落在兩個最大的社群建設者身上。","chips":["15 teams","12 Jul 2026","17-team handbook","iGEMers Prize"],"chips_zh":["15 支隊伍","2026 年 7 月 12 日","17 隊手冊","iGEMers Prize"],"link":"https://2026.igem.wiki/hust-china/collaboration","linkText":"HUST-China collaboration"},{"kicker":"The connectors win nothing","kicker_zh":"連結者什麼也沒拿到","title":"Bielefeld-CeBiTec, JLU-FBH, Lund, Okinawa","title_zh":"Bielefeld-CeBiTec、JLU-FBH、Lund、Okinawa","body":"The teams that carried the 2026 network were not rewarded for it. Bielefeld-CeBiTec (6221) co-ran the BFH European Meet-Up in Hamburg on 15–17 May and the Community Blackboard that roughly 37 teams passed through: Gold plus one Safety and Security nomination. JLU-FBH (6056), chief editor of the handbook 17-plus teams wrote into: Gold, nothing else. BUCT (6055), co-producer with HUST-China: Gold, nothing else. NAU-CHINA (6419), which ran the nationwide ICII initiative that HUST explicitly copied: Gold and one part nomination. Lund (6160), whose podcast The Sequence featured about twelve teams including NYCU-Taiwan: Silver. Okinawa (6155), the one Japanese team that joined Taiwan's meet-up: no medal at all. Verified team by team against api.igem.org.","body_zh":"撐起 2026 年這張網的隊伍並沒有因此得到回報。Bielefeld-CeBiTec（6221）與人合辦 5 月 15 至 17 日在 Hamburg 的 BFH European Meet-Up，以及大約 37 隊經手的 Community Blackboard：金牌加一項 Safety and Security 入圍。JLU-FBH（6056），17 支以上隊伍投稿的那本手冊的主編：金牌，沒有別的。BUCT（6055），與 HUST-China 共同產出：金牌，沒有別的。NAU-CHINA（6419），推動全國性 ICII 計畫、而 HUST 明言借用其邏輯：金牌加一項零件入圍。Lund（6160），其播客 The Sequence 收錄約十二支隊伍、包含 NYCU-Taiwan：銀牌。Okinawa（6155），唯一參加台灣聚會的日本隊伍：完全沒有獎牌。以上逐隊比對 api.igem.org 查證。","chips":["~37 teams","Gold only","Silver","no medal"],"chips_zh":["約 37 支隊伍","只有金牌","銀牌","沒有獎牌"],"link":"https://api.igem.org/v1/teams/6221/awards","linkText":"iGEM API awards"},{"kicker":"GEMS-Taiwan · 6072","kicker_zh":"GEMS-Taiwan · 6072","title":"Zero edges, three wins","title_zh":"零連結，三項大獎","body":"GEMS-Taiwan has no /collaborations page and no /partnership page — both return 404 — and no other iGEM team is named anywhere on its wiki. Its one listed partner team, Geospatial Analysis, is an internal sub-team. It appears on no other Taiwanese team's collaboration page: not NYCU-Taiwan's, not NCKU-Tainan's, not KCIS-Xiugang-Taipei's, and it is not among the teams Labi-Taiwan names at TGEM. It still took High School Top 10 with wins in Measurement, Hardware and Integrated Human Practices. State that plainly: in 2026 collaboration did not buy placing, and GEMS is the proof. The case for building a network is not the medal — it is that GEMS currently has nowhere to send a construct and nobody to check its numbers.","body_zh":"GEMS-Taiwan 沒有 /collaborations 頁，也沒有 /partnership 頁——兩者都回傳 404——整個 wiki 上也沒有具名提到任何其他 iGEM 隊伍。它唯一列出的夥伴隊伍 Geospatial Analysis 是隊內分組。它沒有出現在任何其他台灣隊伍的合作頁上：NYCU-Taiwan 沒有、NCKU-Tainan 沒有、KCIS-Xiugang-Taipei 沒有，也不在 Labi-Taiwan 的 TGEM 具名隊伍之列。它仍然拿下高中組 Top 10，以及最佳量測、最佳硬體與最佳整合式人類實踐三項大獎。這件事要講白：2026 年合作並沒有換來名次，GEMS 就是證明。建立網路的理由不是獎牌——而是 GEMS 現在沒有地方可以寄出一個構築體，也沒有人可以幫它驗證數字。","chips":["0 partner teams","404 on /collaborations","Top 10","3 wins"],"chips_zh":["0 支夥伴隊伍","/collaborations 是 404","Top 10","3 項大獎"],"link":"https://2026.igem.wiki/gems-taiwan/","linkText":"GEMS-Taiwan wiki"}],"table":{"head":["Event","Host","Date","Who came","GEMS there?"],"head_zh":["活動","主辦","日期","誰出席","GEMS 有去嗎？"],"rows":[["2026 Taiwan iGEMers Meet-Up","NYCU-Taiwan (6306)","27 Jul, Bo-Ai Campus, Hsinchu","53 people; NYCU-Taiwan, HIA-Taiwan, NCKU-Tainan, VIS, WIST + Okinawa online","No"],["TGEM 2026, 4th Taiwan iGEM Meetup","Labi-Taiwan (6511) with NTU Dept of Biochemical Science and Technology","22 Aug, Boya Building, NTU","NTHU Taiwan, Claremont CA, AEI Prep-Taiwan, KCIS-Xiugang-Taipei named","No"],["Grand APiC, 1st Asia-Pacific Synthetic Biology Youth Conference","SUSTech and the University of Hong Kong","16-19 Aug","HUST-China; Peking won Best Project; HKSSC and HKU-HongKong sit in the APiC / iGBA community","No"],["Japan iGEM meet-up","Hiroo Gakuen (HG-Tokyo, 6352)","2026","ASIJ-Tokyo, UTokyo, TUS, Waseda, Keio, Oakridge, HG","No"],["First Central-China iGEM Forum (CCiF)","HUST-China (6284)","12 Jul, Qiming College Maker Space","15 teams online and offline; 14 presented","No"],["Mini-Jamboree (online)","TAU-Israel (6196)","8 Oct","8 teams: NCKU-Tainan, NTHU, CAU-China, Cell Forge, iGEM-UA Alicante, UFRGS-Brazil, AIS-China + host","No"],["Cross-team communication session","Bist-China (6263)","2026","ZJU-China, ZJUT-China, HiZJU-China, HangzhouFourteenAP, OTIA-Hangzhou, WUXI-DSAS, iZJU-China, ZZU-China","No"],["Five-school joint biosafety manual","HBUT-China (6330)","2026","ZJU-China, BNU-China, JLU-FBH, ZJUT-China","No"],["BFH European Meet-Up, 3rd edition","Bielefeld, Frankfurt and Hamburg","15-17 May, Hamburg","Uni-Padua-IT, KIT, ETH-Zurich, Muenster-University and others; Community Blackboard drew ~37 teams including NYCU-Taiwan","No"],["NCKU-Tainan's bilateral run","NCKU-Tainan (6379)","7 Mar - 20 Sep","Mingdao (mentorship), WIST (wet-lab and dry-lab session, 17 Sep), CCU-Taiwan (19 Sep), HIA-Taiwan (20 Sep)","No"]],"rows_zh":[["2026 Taiwan iGEMers Meet-Up","NYCU-Taiwan (6306)","7 月 27 日，新竹博愛校區","53 人；NYCU-Taiwan、HIA-Taiwan、NCKU-Tainan、VIS、WIST，Okinawa 線上","沒有"],["TGEM 2026，第四屆台灣 iGEM 聚會","Labi-Taiwan (6511) 與台大生化科技學系","8 月 22 日，台大博雅教學館","具名者：NTHU Taiwan、Claremont CA、AEI Prep-Taiwan、KCIS-Xiugang-Taipei","沒有"],["Grand APiC，第一屆亞太合成生物學青年大會","SUSTech 與香港大學","8 月 16 至 19 日","HUST-China；Peking 獲 Best Project；HKSSC 與 HKU-HongKong 屬於 APiC / iGBA 社群","沒有"],["日本 iGEM 聚會","Hiroo Gakuen（HG-Tokyo, 6352）","2026 年","ASIJ-Tokyo、UTokyo、TUS、Waseda、Keio、Oakridge、HG","沒有"],["第一屆華中 iGEM 論壇（CCiF）","HUST-China (6284)","7 月 12 日，啟明學院創客空間","15 支線上與線下隊伍；14 支報告","沒有"],["Mini-Jamboree（線上）","TAU-Israel (6196)","10 月 8 日","8 支隊伍：NCKU-Tainan、NTHU、CAU-China、Cell Forge、iGEM-UA Alicante、UFRGS-Brazil、AIS-China 加主辦","沒有"],["跨隊交流場次","Bist-China (6263)","2026 年","ZJU-China、ZJUT-China、HiZJU-China、HangzhouFourteenAP、OTIA-Hangzhou、WUXI-DSAS、iZJU-China、ZZU-China","沒有"],["五校聯合生物安全手冊","HBUT-China (6330)","2026 年","ZJU-China、BNU-China、JLU-FBH、ZJUT-China","沒有"],["BFH European Meet-Up 第三屆","Bielefeld、Frankfurt 與 Hamburg","5 月 15 至 17 日，Hamburg","Uni-Padua-IT、KIT、ETH-Zurich、Muenster-University 等；Community Blackboard 吸引約 37 支隊伍，含 NYCU-Taiwan","沒有"],["NCKU-Tainan 的雙邊系列","NCKU-Tainan (6379)","3 月 7 日至 9 月 20 日","Mingdao（指導）、WIST（濕式與乾式實驗交流，9 月 17 日）、CCU-Taiwan（9 月 19 日）、HIA-Taiwan（9 月 20 日）","沒有"]]},"checklist":["March 2027 — the GEMS human practices lead emails Labi-Taiwan and the NTU Department of Biochemical Science and Technology to register for TGEM 2027. TGEM has run every August since 2023 and is held in Taipei, where GEMS already is; the 2026 edition judged teams with a five-minute pitch plus twenty minutes of questions from professors and industry. Ask for a slot in the high-school division and offer, in the same email, to run a thirty-minute measurement clinic using the Best Measurement work.","April 2027 — email NYCU-Taiwan. They published their meet-up preparation SOPs, registration form templates and event schedules explicitly for future organisers to adapt, and wrote on their own wiki that next time they want a collaboration interest form rather than a poster. Take them at their word: offer to co-host the 2027 Taiwan iGEMers Meet-Up in Taipei, or to run the measurement session at theirs.","May 2027 — propose the inter-lab measurement ring nobody ran in 2026. Write to four named teams at once: NCKU-Tainan 6379 (Best Hardware nominee, the US$54-161 CAPTURE-Screen fluorescence reader, and already the busiest technical partner in Taiwan), NTHU 6460 (four-channel frequency-tagged reader with digital lock-in detection), Labi-Taiwan 6511 (Best Measurement nominee, portable electrochemical reader) and Mingdao 6105, the only Taiwanese team that has already re-characterised another team's part at new conditions. The offer is concrete: GEMS ships one calibrated reference construct plus its photometer protocol, each team measures it on its own instrument, and the between-lab spread is published jointly.","May 2027 — before any team says yes, put the ring protocol on the GEMS wiki as a dated, versioned page with the calibration curve, the acceptance criteria and the raw-data template. Uni-Padua-IT's open call failed with nothing attached; an offer that arrives with a finished protocol and a shipping plan is a different object.","June 2027 — copy the KCIS-Xiugang-Taipei and HKSSC method for the cross-border attempt, because it is the only one in the 2026 Taiwanese record that produced a shared artefact: two scheduled planning calls six weeks apart, an agreed split of the work, prototypes exchanged through a shared drive, then each team adapting to its own audience. Approach HKSSC 6053 (High School Top 10, Best New Basic Part winner, already in the APiC and iGBA communities) or ASIJ-Tokyo 6338, which ran activities with eight teams across eight countries and already has a Taiwanese tie.","July 2027 — write to Okinawa 6155 and HG-Tokyo 6352. Okinawa joined Taiwan's meet-up online after NYCU flew there, and won no medal in 2026; HG-Tokyo hosts the Japanese meet-up that UTokyo, TUS, Waseda, Keio, Oakridge and ASIJ attend. Both are reachable, and both have an incentive GEMS can serve.","August 2027 — apply to Grand APiC. The first Asia-Pacific Synthetic Biology Youth Conference ran 16-19 August 2026 at SUSTech and the University of Hong Kong; Peking took Best Project there and HKSSC and HKU-HongKong sit inside the APiC and iGBA community. It is the regional umbrella a Taiwanese high-school research centre can enter without an invitation from any one team.","Throughout — build /collaborations as a page with dates, named counterparts and outputs, not a gallery. And adopt a reciprocity rule: every exchange gets a one-paragraph record on both wikis, agreed before the call ends. In 2026 NCKU-Tainan, ASIJ-Tokyo and NYCU-Taiwan each wrote up partners whose own wikis stayed silent; the partner who writes it up keeps the credit and the reusable artefact."],"checklist_zh":["2027 年 3 月——GEMS 的人類實踐負責人寄信給 Labi-Taiwan 與台大生化科技學系，報名 TGEM 2027。TGEM 自 2023 年起每年八月舉辦，地點在台北，GEMS 本來就在台北；2026 年的形式是五分鐘簡報加二十分鐘由教授與業界提問。爭取高中組的名額，並在同一封信裡提議用 Best Measurement 的成果開一場三十分鐘的量測工作坊。","2027 年 4 月——寄信給 NYCU-Taiwan。他們公開了聚會的籌備 SOP、報名表單範本與活動議程，明言供未來主辦者沿用，也在自己的 wiki 上寫下次想要的是一份合作意向表單而不是一張海報。就照他們說的做：提議在台北共同主辦 2027 年的 Taiwan iGEMers Meet-Up，或在他們的場次裡負責量測單元。","2027 年 5 月——提出 2026 年沒有任何人做過的跨實驗室量測環。同時寫給四支具名隊伍：NCKU-Tainan 6379（Best Hardware 入圍、US$54-161 的 CAPTURE-Screen 螢光判讀器，也是台灣記錄上最忙碌的技術夥伴）、NTHU 6460（四通道頻率標記判讀器，採數位鎖相偵測）、Labi-Taiwan 6511（Best Measurement 入圍、可攜式電化學判讀器），以及 Mingdao 6105，台灣唯一已經在新條件下重新表徵過別隊零件的隊伍。提案要具體：GEMS 寄出一個經校正的參考構築體與光度計操作流程，各隊在自己的儀器上量測，實驗室之間的差異共同發表。","2027 年 5 月——在任何一隊答應之前，先把量測環的流程放上 GEMS wiki，做成有日期、有版本的頁面，附校正曲線、接受標準與原始資料範本。Uni-Padua-IT 的公開邀請失敗時什麼也沒附；一份帶著完成的流程與寄送計畫送到的邀請，是完全不同的東西。","2027 年 6 月——跨境嘗試就照 KCIS-Xiugang-Taipei 與 HKSSC 的做法複製，因為那是 2026 年台灣記錄中唯一產出共同成果的方法：兩次相隔六週的既定線上規劃會議、講好的分工、透過共用雲端硬碟交換原型，然後各自針對自己的受眾改編。對象可以是 HKSSC 6053（高中組 Top 10、Best New Basic Part 得主，已在 APiC 與 iGBA 社群內），或 ASIJ-Tokyo 6338，他們與八個國家的八支隊伍合辦活動，而且已經有一條通往台灣的線。","2027 年 7 月——寫信給 Okinawa 6155 與 HG-Tokyo 6352。Okinawa 是在 NYCU 親自飛去之後才線上參加台灣聚會的，2026 年沒有拿到任何獎牌；HG-Tokyo 主辦 UTokyo、TUS、Waseda、Keio、Oakridge 與 ASIJ 參加的日本聚會。兩者都連得上，也都有 GEMS 能回應的需求。","2027 年 8 月——報名 Grand APiC。第一屆亞太合成生物學青年大會於 2026 年 8 月 16 至 19 日在 SUSTech 與香港大學舉行；Peking 在該場拿下 Best Project，HKSSC 與 HKU-HongKong 都在 APiC 與 iGBA 社群裡。這是台灣的高中研究中心不需要任何單一隊伍邀請就能進入的區域傘狀組織。","全程——把 /collaborations 做成一個有日期、有具名對象、有產出的頁面，不是相簿。並且建立互惠規則：每一次交流，在會議結束前就講好雙方 wiki 各留一段記錄。2026 年 NCKU-Tainan、ASIJ-Tokyo 與 NYCU-Taiwan 都寫下了夥伴，而那些夥伴自己的 wiki 卻一片沉默；寫下來的那一方，留住了功勞，也留住了那個可重複使用的成果。"],"method":"The first pass was on disk: all 106 researched team files in research/teams/ were grepped for collaboration signals (collaborat, meet-up, meetup, partner, exchange, inter-lab, interlab, conference, mentor, jointly, shared, co-hosted, iGEM team, other teams), returning hits in 74 files, and every good.partners[] entry naming an iGEM team or meet-up was extracted separately. This cannot see a collaboration a team did but did not write up, and it demonstrably misses some: NCKU-Tainan's file contains no collaboration signal at all, yet its wiki carries five dated exchanges. The classification behind the correlation (S = substantive co-production, n = 48; A = attendance or visibility only, n = 21; N = none documented, n = 37) is therefore a documentation proxy, not a census of behaviour, and the Fisher exact tests reported are two-sided on those counts. The roster and every award cited were taken from iGEM's public API — api.igem.org/v1/teams?year=2026 for all 463 registrations across 24 pages, and api.igem.org/v1/teams/<id>/awards for individual teams including Bielefeld-CeBiTec 6221, JLU-FBH 6056, BUCT 6055, NAU-CHINA 6419, Lund 6160, Okinawa 6155 and Claremont CA 6317 — not from any hand-written list. Wiki verification ran over /collaborations, /collaboration, /partnership, /partnerships, /collaborations-and-partnerships, /collaboration-partnership and /public-outreach-and-collaboration for 131 slugs: 568 of 917 returned 404, and many of the rest are client-rendered single-page apps that return HTTP 200 for any route, so the browser was used for Labi-Taiwan, CCU-Taiwan and Uni-Padua-IT while NYCU-Taiwan, NCKU-Tainan, KCIS-Xiugang-Taipei, Squirrel-Beijing and others were read directly. GEMS-Taiwan's absence was checked positively: /collaborations, /collaboration and /partnership all return 404, and its human-practices, education and contribution pages name no other iGEM team. Reciprocity was spot-checked in both directions and three one-sided claims are reported as findings. Pages were read on 19 November 2026.","method_zh":"第一輪在本機進行：對 research/teams/ 下全部 106 份隊伍研究檔案做合作訊號的 grep（collaborat、meet-up、meetup、partner、exchange、inter-lab、interlab、conference、mentor、jointly、shared、co-hosted、iGEM team、other teams），在 74 份檔案中找到命中，並另外抽出所有具名提及 iGEM 隊伍或聚會的 good.partners[] 條目。這種做法看不到一支隊伍做了卻沒寫下來的合作，而且確實有漏：NCKU-Tainan 的檔案完全沒有合作訊號，但它的 wiki 上有五場標了日期的交流。因此，相關性分析背後的分類（S = 實質共同產出，n = 48；A = 僅出席或露臉，n = 21；N = 沒有記錄，n = 37）是一個「記錄」的代理指標，不是行為普查；所報的 Fisher 精確檢定為雙尾。名單與所有引用的獎項都取自 iGEM 的公開 API——api.igem.org/v1/teams?year=2026 取得分 24 頁的全部 463 筆報名，以及 api.igem.org/v1/teams/<id>/awards 取得個別隊伍的獎項，包括 Bielefeld-CeBiTec 6221、JLU-FBH 6056、BUCT 6055、NAU-CHINA 6419、Lund 6160、Okinawa 6155 與 Claremont CA 6317——而不是任何手寫清單。Wiki 查證涵蓋 131 個隊伍網址的 /collaborations、/collaboration、/partnership、/partnerships、/collaborations-and-partnerships、/collaboration-partnership 與 /public-outreach-and-collaboration：917 個網址中有 568 個回傳 404，其餘不少是用戶端渲染的單頁應用，任何路徑都回傳 HTTP 200，因此 Labi-Taiwan、CCU-Taiwan 與 Uni-Padua-IT 改用瀏覽器讀取，而 NYCU-Taiwan、NCKU-Tainan、KCIS-Xiugang-Taipei、Squirrel-Beijing 等則直接讀取。GEMS-Taiwan 的缺席是正面查證過的：/collaborations、/collaboration 與 /partnership 全部回傳 404，而其 human-practices、education 與 contribution 頁面都沒有具名提到任何其他 iGEM 隊伍。互惠性做了雙向抽查，三項單方面宣稱以發現的形式寫入。頁面讀取日期為 2026 年 11 月 19 日。"},{"id":"real-world","tab":"good","kicker":"Original analysis","title":"The commercial work that was worth reading argued against itself","title_zh":"值得一讀的商業分析，都在反駁自己","lede":"Across the 2026 field, the teams with credible real-world plans are the ones that published a model showing their own product losing.","lede_zh":"綜觀 2026 年，真實世界計畫最可信的團隊，都公開了一個顯示自家產品輸掉的模型。","body":"Almost every iGEM team produces a business model canvas. Very few produce a number that could have gone against them. The difference is the whole of what separates a credible 2026 commercial section from a template.\n\n**Worldshaper-Shanghai** published a recomputable net-present-value model and reported the result honestly: their own enzyme gives a **negative NPV**. They did not bury it, soften it, or quietly change the discount rate. **BGI-College** did the same with arithmetic instead of finance — a break-even calculation comparing 6.70 against 4.0 mol H₂ per mol glucose disproved the team's own premise, and forced a redesign around byproduct valorisation. **DTU-Denmark** ran a prospective life-cycle assessment in SimaPro with ReCiPe 2016 H and found its enzymatic route emits 2.1 kg CO₂-eq/kg against 1.4 for solvolysis and 0.9 for pyrolysis, with cement co-processing beating them on almost every indicator — then converted each losing indicator into a named engineering target. **Madrid-UCM** published an ISO 14040/44 openLCA result that currently rules against its own technology.\n\n**Stockholm** went furthest. Its safety advisory board killed the open-water release the project was built around, so the team dismantled the venture, retreated to a contained membrane bioreactor on a smaller industrial stream, and made the deliverable **reusable safety infrastructure** instead: an STPA hazard analysis, a nine-system wastewater containment guidebook, and a measurement-uncertainty toolkit. Giving up the product and shipping the method is a result, and it was recognised with the Safety and Security Award.\n\nSet against that, the template is easy to spot once you know the tell: **the cost side is real and the revenue side is fantasy**. ZJU-China itemises equipment at CNY 7.45 million, media, IPTG and labour, and publishes a downloadable cost sheet — genuinely good work — then assumes **100% capture of its serviceable obtainable market** to reach a USD 427 million NPV. The discipline applied to the inputs evaporates at the outputs.\n\nThe high-school tier is not behind here, and in places it is ahead. **SUIS-SFLS** built the only full financial model in the high-school set: capital expenditure of CNY 6.8 and 11.65 million across two scenarios, CNY 71 and 163.5 per litre, 34% against 15.9% margins, break-even years, and the spreadsheets published as downloadable PDFs, on a dual NMPA and ISO 13485 regulatory track. **ICJFLS** works bottom-up from unit economics — RMB 0.8 per dose against RMB 199 retail — with a 745-response survey and a named CDMO. **NFLSHS-CHINA** has a filed and accepted patent on a CsCCD2 mutant, two physical minimum viable products with formula tables, and labels its partnerships as prospective rather than implying they are signed.\n\nThe second thing the credible teams do is **name the stage of each claim**. Baltimore runs Venture Creation Labs OKRs with numeric gates and IRB-approved trilingual surveys, and says plainly that its letters of intent and grants are targets rather than commitments. McGill has a full techno-economic analysis — $11.83 to $20.58 per kg of rare earth oxide, an Ashram project NPV of +USD 51 million, seven sensitivity analyses — an accelerator place, a venture-capital mentor, two letters of support and secured tailings samples, and states that it is not yet incorporated. Nobody is penalised for an early-stage venture. Teams are penalised, correctly, for presenting an aspiration in the grammar of an achievement.\n\nAnd a reminder that not every project should become a company. **HBUT-China**, **WHU-China**, **Squirrel-Beijing** and **BASIS-China** have no venture at all. Their deliverable is infrastructure other teams can use: 34 parts in four independently reusable modules with measurement parts built in and honest terminator read-through annotations; a five-layer characterisation of Neo-IL-2 including surface plasmon resonance and high-passage stability; a tunable bile-acid kill switch with a measured 0.1–0.2 mM threshold compared against real sewage and soil concentrations, plus a published five-step framework for characterising kill switches. That is a real-world contribution with a longer half-life than most business plans.","body_zh":"幾乎每一支 iGEM 團隊都會生出一張商業模式畫布，但很少有團隊生出一個「有可能對自己不利」的數字。而這個差別，就是 2026 年可信的商業章節與樣板之間的全部距離。\n\n**Worldshaper-Shanghai** 公開了一個可重新計算的淨現值模型，並誠實報告結果：他們自己的酵素得出**負的 NPV**。他們沒有把它藏起來、淡化，也沒有偷偷調整折現率。**BGI-College** 做了同樣的事，只是用算術而非財務——一個比較 6.70 與 4.0 mol H₂／mol 葡萄糖的損益兩平計算，推翻了團隊自己的前提，迫使他們圍繞副產物加值重新設計。**DTU-Denmark** 以 SimaPro 搭配 ReCiPe 2016 H 做了前瞻性生命週期評估，發現自家的酵素路線排放 2.1 kg CO₂-eq/kg，而溶劑解為 1.4、熱解為 0.9，水泥共處理在幾乎每一項指標上都勝過他們——然後把每一項輸掉的指標轉化為一個具名的工程目標。**Madrid-UCM** 則公開了一份 ISO 14040/44 的 openLCA 結果，而該結果目前判定對他們自己的技術不利。\n\n**Stockholm** 走得最遠。他們的安全諮詢委員會否決了整個專案賴以成立的開放水域釋放，於是團隊拆掉了這個創業構想，退回到處理較小工業廢流的密閉式膜生物反應器，並把產出改成**可重複使用的安全基礎設施**：一份 STPA 危害分析、一本涵蓋九種系統的廢水圍堵指南，以及一套量測不確定度工具包。放棄產品、交付方法，本身就是一種成果，而它拿下了安全與保安獎。\n\n對照之下，樣板一旦知道徵兆就很好認：**成本端是真的，營收端是幻想**。ZJU-China 列出 7,450 萬人民幣的設備、培養基、IPTG 與人力，還公開可下載的成本表——這是扎實的工作——接著假設**100% 拿下其可服務可獲得市場**，得出 4.27 億美元的 NPV。用在投入端的紀律，到了產出端就蒸發了。\n\n高中組在這件事上並不落後，有些地方甚至領先。**SUIS-SFLS** 做出高中組唯一一份完整的財務模型：兩種情境下 680 萬與 1,165 萬人民幣的資本支出、每公升 71 元與 163.5 元、34% 對 15.9% 的毛利率、損益兩平年份，試算表以可下載 PDF 公開，並走 NMPA 與 ISO 13485 雙軌法規路徑。**ICJFLS** 從單位經濟由下而上推算——每劑 0.8 人民幣對零售價 199 元——搭配 745 份問卷與一家具名的 CDMO。**NFLSHS-CHINA** 則有一件已提出並受理的 CsCCD2 突變體專利、兩個附配方表的實體最小可行產品，而且把合作關係標示為「潛在」，不暗示已經簽約。\n\n可信團隊做的第二件事，是**標明每一項主張所處的階段**。Baltimore 以 Venture Creation Labs 的 OKR 搭配量化關卡運作，做了經 IRB 核准的三語問卷，並直說他們的意向書與補助都只是目標，不是承諾。McGill 有完整的技術經濟分析——每公斤稀土氧化物 11.83 至 20.58 美元、Ashram 專案淨現值 +5,100 萬美元、七項敏感度分析——有加速器席位、創投導師、兩封支持信與已取得的尾礦樣本，並載明尚未完成公司設立。沒有人會因為創業處於早期而被扣分；被扣分的——而且理所當然——是用「已完成」的文法去陳述一個「想達成」的願望。\n\n最後提醒：不是每一個專案都該變成公司。**HBUT-China**、**WHU-China**、**Squirrel-Beijing** 與 **BASIS-China** 根本沒有創業規劃。他們的產出是其他團隊可以使用的基礎設施：34 個分屬四個可獨立重用模組的元件，內建量測用元件，並誠實註記終止子讀通問題；Neo-IL-2 的五層次表徵，含表面電漿共振與高代次穩定性；一個可調控的膽酸自殺開關，量測到 0.1–0.2 mM 的閾值並與真實污水及土壤濃度對照，外加一套已發表的自殺開關五步驟表徵框架。這是一種真實世界的貢獻，而且半衰期比多數商業計畫書都長。","cards":[{"kicker":"The strongest move","title":"Publish the model that says no","title_zh":"公開那個說「不」的模型","body":"Worldshaper-Shanghai's recomputable NPV model finds their own enzyme gives a negative NPV, and says so. DTU-Denmark's prospective LCA finds cement co-processing beats their enzymatic route on almost every indicator, then turns each losing indicator into an engineering target. Madrid-UCM's ISO 14040/44 assessment currently rules against its own technology. A model that could only ever have agreed with you is not evidence.","body_zh":"Worldshaper-Shanghai 可重算的 NPV 模型得出自家酵素為負 NPV，而他們照實寫出來。DTU-Denmark 的前瞻性 LCA 發現水泥共處理在幾乎每項指標上都勝過他們的酵素路線，於是把每一項輸掉的指標轉成工程目標。Madrid-UCM 的 ISO 14040/44 評估目前判定對自家技術不利。一個只可能同意你的模型，不是證據。","chips":["negative NPV, published","LCA that rules against you"],"chips_zh":["負 NPV，照樣公開","判自己輸的 LCA"],"kicker_zh":"最強的一步"},{"kicker":"The tell","title":"Real costs, fantasy revenue","title_zh":"真實的成本，幻想的營收","body":"ZJU-China itemises CNY 7.45 million of equipment, media, IPTG and labour and publishes a downloadable cost sheet — then assumes 100% capture of its serviceable obtainable market to reach a USD 427 million NPV. This is the most common failure mode in iGEM commercial sections: rigour on the inputs, where the team has data, and none on the outputs, where it does not.","body_zh":"ZJU-China 逐項列出 7,450 萬人民幣的設備、培養基、IPTG 與人力，還公開可下載的成本表——接著假設 100% 拿下可服務可獲得市場，得出 4.27 億美元的 NPV。這是 iGEM 商業章節最常見的失敗模式：在團隊有資料的投入端講究嚴謹，在沒有資料的產出端完全放棄。","chips":["100% SOM capture"],"chips_zh":["SOM 全拿 100%"],"kicker_zh":"破綻"},{"kicker":"The result that looks like a failure","title":"Stockholm dismantled its own venture","title_zh":"Stockholm 拆掉了自己的創業計畫","body":"A safety advisory board killed the open-water release the project was built on. Rather than argue, the team retreated to a contained membrane bioreactor on a smaller stream and shipped reusable safety infrastructure instead — an STPA hazard analysis, a nine-system wastewater containment guidebook, a measurement-uncertainty toolkit. It won the Safety and Security Award. Giving up the product and publishing the method is a result.","body_zh":"安全諮詢委員會否決了這個專案賴以成立的開放水域釋放。團隊沒有爭辯，而是退回到處理較小廢流的密閉式膜生物反應器，改為交付可重複使用的安全基礎設施——STPA 危害分析、涵蓋九種系統的廢水圍堵指南、量測不確定度工具包。它拿下了安全與保安獎。放棄產品、公開方法，本身就是成果。","chips":["Safety and Security Award"],"chips_zh":["Safety and Security Award"],"kicker_zh":"看起來像失敗的成果"},{"kicker":"High school, ahead","title":"SUIS-SFLS built the only full financial model in its tier","title_zh":"SUIS-SFLS 做出該組唯一一份完整財務模型","body":"Capital expenditure of CNY 6.8 and 11.65 million across two scenarios, CNY 71 and 163.5 per litre, 34% against 15.9% margins, break-even years, spreadsheets published as downloadable PDFs, on a dual NMPA and ISO 13485 track. ICJFLS works bottom-up from RMB 0.8 per dose against RMB 199 retail with a named CDMO. The census found high-school teams do more techno-economic analysis than undergraduates; this is what that looks like up close.","body_zh":"兩種情境下 680 萬與 1,165 萬人民幣的資本支出、每公升 71 元與 163.5 元、34% 對 15.9% 的毛利率、損益兩平年份，試算表以可下載 PDF 公開，並走 NMPA 與 ISO 13485 雙軌。ICJFLS 則由下而上從每劑 0.8 人民幣對零售價 199 元推算，並列出具名的 CDMO。技術普查發現高中隊伍做的技術經濟分析比大學部還多；放大來看就是這個樣子。","chips":["capex, margins, break-even","NMPA + ISO 13485"],"chips_zh":["資本支出、毛利、損益兩平","NMPA + ISO 13485"],"kicker_zh":"高中組，領先"},{"kicker":"The habit","title":"Name the stage of every claim","title_zh":"標明每一項主張所處的階段","body":"Baltimore says plainly that its letters of intent and grants are targets, not commitments. McGill has a full techno-economic analysis, an accelerator place, a VC mentor, two letters of support and secured tailings samples — and states it is not yet incorporated. NFLSHS-CHINA labels its partnerships prospective. Nobody is penalised for being early. Teams are penalised for writing an aspiration in the grammar of an achievement.","body_zh":"Baltimore 直說他們的意向書與補助都只是目標，不是承諾。McGill 有完整的技術經濟分析、加速器席位、創投導師、兩封支持信與已取得的尾礦樣本——並載明尚未完成公司設立。NFLSHS-CHINA 把合作關係標示為潛在。沒有人會因為處於早期而被扣分；被扣分的是用「已完成」的文法去寫一個「想達成」的願望。","chips":["early is fine","overclaiming is not"],"chips_zh":["早期沒關係","誇大不行"],"kicker_zh":"習慣"},{"kicker":"For GEMS","title":"Not every project should become a company","title_zh":"不是每個專案都該變成公司","body":"HBUT-China, WHU-China, Squirrel-Beijing and BASIS-China have no venture at all. They shipped infrastructure instead — 34 parts in four reusable modules with measurement parts built in, a five-layer Neo-IL-2 characterisation, a tunable kill switch with a measured 0.1–0.2 mM threshold checked against real sewage concentrations, and a published five-step framework for characterising kill switches. For an institution building a reputation, that has a longer half-life than a business plan.","body_zh":"HBUT-China、WHU-China、Squirrel-Beijing 與 BASIS-China 完全沒有創業規劃。他們交付的是基礎設施——34 個分屬四個可重用模組、內建量測元件的零件；Neo-IL-2 的五層次表徵；一個量測到 0.1–0.2 mM 閾值、並與真實污水濃度對照的可調控自殺開關；以及一套已發表的自殺開關五步驟表徵框架。對一個正在建立聲譽的機構而言，這些東西的半衰期比商業計畫書長得多。","chips":["parts outlive plans"],"chips_zh":["元件活得比計畫久"],"kicker_zh":"給 GEMS"}],"method":"Drawn from the realWorld fields of the team files in this report, each researched from the team's own 2026 wiki. Financial figures are the teams' own and are not independently audited; where a team's assumptions looked unsupported that is noted as our reading, not as a finding of error. Teams that published a model unfavourable to themselves are over-represented here because that is exactly what the analysis is about — it is not a claim that most 2026 teams did so.","method_zh":"資料取自本報告團隊檔案中的 realWorld 欄位，每一份都來自該隊自己的 2026 wiki。財務數字為各隊自報且未經獨立查核；凡判斷某隊假設缺乏支撐之處，均屬我們的閱讀判斷，而非認定其有誤。公開了對自己不利之模型的團隊在此被過度呈現，因為那正是本篇分析的主題——這並不表示 2026 年多數團隊都這麼做。","kicker_zh":"原創分析","order":34},{"id":"software-afterlife","tab":"drylab","kicker":"Original analysis","title":"Does award-winning iGEM software survive the Jamboree?","title_zh":"得獎的 iGEM 軟體撐得過 Jamboree 嗎？","lede":"Of 21 software tools released by award-winning iGEM 2026 teams, 8 are live and usable by a stranger today, 11 are source-only, and 2 have already gone dark.","lede_zh":"2026 年 iGEM 得獎隊伍釋出的 21 個軟體工具中，今天有 8 個還在線上、陌生人可以直接使用，11 個只有原始碼，2 個已經消失。","body":"**Eight of twenty-one.** That is the honest base rate for award-winning iGEM 2026 software that a stranger can open and use today, four weeks after the Jamboree. Eleven more are source-only: the code is public, populated and often genuinely good, but using it means cloning a repository and running Docker. Two are already dead — Vilnius-Lithuania's Ladder Detector now answers \"This service has been suspended by its owner\" at ladder-detector.onrender.com, and TAU-Israel's CERNAL fails to resolve at both cernal.app and cernal.duckdns.org, the two addresses its own wiki advertises.\n\nThe striking thing is that nothing is a stub. Every repository checked was populated with real code, a README and a licence. iGEM's mandatory GitLab deposit has solved the empty-repo problem completely. What it has not solved, and cannot, is hosting: the competition requires you to publish source, and publishing source is where most teams stop.\n\nThe live ones have one habit in common, and it is not budget. **They bought a domain and pointed it at a running backend before the wiki freeze, then wrote the wiki around a URL rather than around an install command.** NJU-China's Atlas sits on starase-atlas.org, XJTLU-Software's AMPilot on ampilotlab.com, Toronto's PETadex on petadex.net, Stanford's RADAR-Scout on Vercel. Two of the eight are high-school teams running real inference in public: GHCIS's ARGUS answers `{\"status\":\"ready\"}` at argus.ucuv.dpdns.org, and HK-Joint-School's PyroForge reports `models_ready: true, esm_ready: true` — an ESM protein model loaded and serving, from a school team.\n\nThe source-only group is not lazy; it is mostly careful. ETH-Zurich's deCISion ships 28 CI-tested checks, a Docker build and an MIT licence. UMA Malaga's Diana has a 10 GB reproducible Docker stack and a BIOLOGICAL_REPORT.md mapping each biological step to code. Uni-Padua-IT's ReTIsigner is a thoughtful fork of a published tool, Apache 2.0, one `docker run` from working. These teams decided, often explicitly and for defensible reasons — cost, patient data, a 4 GB index — that local execution was the right call. The cost is simply that nobody will ever casually try them.\n\nTwo teams published a live URL that is not the tool, and both said so honestly. UMA Malaga's diana-grna-designer-7723f5.igem.wiki opens with \"Saved results, not the live tool... The pages cannot analyse a variant you type.\" GU Frankfurt's HUSH page says \"This page shows its web app in action\" and then presents a clickable mockup of screenshots. Judges reward the appearance of a deployed tool, so the gap between a demo and a deployment is exactly where a link check gets fooled.\n\nOutside use is the bleakest column. Across every GitLab repository examined the star count is zero, the fork count is zero, and the last commit falls in the October freeze window — with one exception, DKU's pepticraft-2, touched on 5 November. Uni-Padua-IT published an open call on 9 August offering to codon-optimise any team's sequence, received no replies, and reported that on their wiki. The only genuine external-adoption signal found anywhere was on Stanford's SynBase, which displays \"837 learners\" — and that is a teaching platform, not a research tool.\n\nOne more caution for anyone citing datasets as deliverables. Toronto's PETadex front end is live and excellent, but the 23.8 GB Zenodo deposit its wiki cites, doi:10.5281/zenodo.23457986, returns 404, and a Zenodo search for \"petadex\" returns zero records. The web app survived; the archival half of the release did not.\n\nFor GEMS the lesson is narrow and cheap. Shipping a tool outsiders use is achievable — eight teams did it, including two high schools — but it is a hosting decision, not a coding decision, and it has to be made months before the wiki freeze. The teams that got there treated the public URL as the deliverable and the repository as the backup. The ones that did not now own excellent code that nobody will run.","body_zh":"**21 個裡有 8 個。**這就是 2026 年 iGEM 得獎軟體誠實的基礎比率：Jamboree 結束四週後，陌生人今天還打得開、用得動的只有這麼多。另外 11 個只有原始碼：程式公開、內容完整，而且常常真的寫得不錯，但要用它就得把儲存庫 clone 下來再跑 Docker。兩個已經死了——Vilnius-Lithuania 的 Ladder Detector 現在在 ladder-detector.onrender.com 回應「This service has been suspended by its owner」，TAU-Israel 的 CERNAL 在 cernal.app 和 cernal.duckdns.org 都無法解析，而這兩個網址正是它自己的 wiki 上公告的。\n\n值得注意的是，沒有一個是空殼。每一個檢查過的儲存庫都有真正的程式碼、一份 README 和一份授權條款。iGEM 強制要求上傳 GitLab，已經徹底解決了空儲存庫的問題。它沒有解決、也無法解決的是代管：競賽要求你公開原始碼，而公開原始碼就是多數隊伍停下來的地方。\n\n還活著的那些有一個共同習慣，而且不是預算。**他們在 wiki 凍結之前就買好網域、指向一個正在運行的後端，然後把 wiki 寫成繞著一個網址，而不是繞著一行安裝指令。**NJU-China 的 Atlas 放在 starase-atlas.org，XJTLU-Software 的 AMPilot 在 ampilotlab.com，Toronto 的 PETadex 在 petadex.net，Stanford 的 RADAR-Scout 在 Vercel 上。八個裡有兩個是高中隊伍，而且在公開環境跑真正的推論：GHCIS 的 ARGUS 在 argus.ucuv.dpdns.org 回應 `{\"status\":\"ready\"}`，HK-Joint-School 的 PyroForge 回報 `models_ready: true, esm_ready: true`——一個 ESM 蛋白質模型載入並持續提供服務，而這來自一支高中隊伍。\n\n只有原始碼的這一群並不是懶，多半是謹慎。ETH-Zurich 的 deCISion 附上 28 項經 CI 測試的檢查、一套 Docker 建置和 MIT 授權。UMA Malaga 的 Diana 有一套 10 GB 的可重現 Docker 環境，以及一份把每個生物步驟對應到程式碼的 BIOLOGICAL_REPORT.md。Uni-Padua-IT 的 ReTIsigner 是對一個已發表工具用心的分支，採 Apache 2.0，一行 `docker run` 就能動。這些隊伍判斷在本機執行才是對的選擇，而且往往講得很明白、理由也站得住腳——成本、病人資料、一個 4 GB 的索引。代價就只是：永遠不會有人隨手試一下。\n\n有兩支隊伍公布了一個不是工具本身的線上網址，而且兩支都誠實說了。UMA Malaga 的 diana-grna-designer-7723f5.igem.wiki 一開頭就寫「Saved results, not the live tool... The pages cannot analyse a variant you type.」GU Frankfurt 的 HUSH 頁面說「This page shows its web app in action」，接著呈現一份由截圖組成、可以點擊的介面示意稿。評審會獎勵「看起來已經部署」這件事，所以示範與部署之間的落差，正是連結檢查被騙的地方。\n\n外部使用是最慘的一欄。所有檢視過的 GitLab 儲存庫，star 數是零，fork 數是零，最後一次 commit 都落在十月的凍結期內——只有一個例外，DKU 的 pepticraft-2 在 11 月 5 日被動過。Uni-Padua-IT 在 8 月 9 日公開徵求，願意幫任何隊伍做密碼子最佳化，結果沒有收到任何回覆，並且把這件事寫在自己的 wiki 上。在任何地方找到的唯一真實外部採用訊號，是 Stanford 的 SynBase 顯示的「837 learners」——而那是一個教學平台，不是研究工具。\n\n給任何把資料集當成交付成果來引用的人一個提醒。Toronto 的 PETadex 前端還在線上，而且做得很好，但它的 wiki 引用的那份 23.8 GB Zenodo 存放紀錄 doi:10.5281/zenodo.23457986 回傳 404，在 Zenodo 搜尋「petadex」也得到零筆紀錄。網頁應用活了下來；這次釋出中負責封存的那一半沒有。\n\n對 GEMS 來說，這個教訓既狹窄又便宜。做出外人會用的工具是辦得到的——八支隊伍做到了，其中包括兩支高中隊伍——但這是代管的決定，不是寫程式的決定，而且必須在 wiki 凍結前好幾個月就做。做到的隊伍把公開網址當成交付成果，把儲存庫當成備份。沒做到的，現在擁有一堆優秀但沒人會執行的程式碼。","cards":[{"kicker":"Best in class","title":"AMPilot — the only tool with a working public API","title_zh":"AMPilot——唯一有可用公開 API 的工具","body":"XJTLU-Software's antimicrobial-peptide workbench at ampilotlab.com opens in guest mode with no account, and its /api/v1 routes are documented in a published OpenAPI 3.1 spec. A live call to /api/v1/corpus/search returned real literature evidence with provenance, licence and retrieval date attached — no key, no sign-up. The spec states the API is deterministic, stateless and calls no language model, which is what makes it safe for someone else to build on. It is the clearest example this year of a team designing for a second user rather than a judge.","body_zh":"XJTLU-Software 的抗菌肽工作台在 ampilotlab.com 以訪客模式開啟，不需要帳號，它的 /api/v1 路徑都寫在一份公開的 OpenAPI 3.1 規格裡。實際呼叫 /api/v1/corpus/search 回傳了真正的文獻證據，並附上來源、授權條款和取用日期——不用金鑰、不用註冊。規格中載明這個 API 是確定性的、無狀態的，而且不呼叫任何語言模型，這正是別人可以安心在上面開發的原因。這是今年最清楚的一個例子：一支隊伍是為第二個使用者而設計，不是為評審而設計。","chips":["alive","XJTLU-Software","public API","guest mode","OpenAPI 3.1"],"chips_zh":["還活著","XJTLU-Software","公開 API","訪客模式","OpenAPI 3.1"],"kicker_zh":"同類最佳"},{"kicker":"Proof it is not a budget problem","title":"Two high-school teams out-shipped most universities","title_zh":"兩支高中隊伍交付的成果勝過多數大學隊伍","body":"GHCIS's ARGUS runs a real backend at argus.ucuv.dpdns.org — its /api/ready endpoint answers with JSON, not a static shell — alongside a Docker and a native Node deploy path, role-based access and SQLite persistence. HK-Joint-School's PyroForge serves protein thermostability prediction at pyroforge.26650078.xyz with /health reporting ESM models loaded and ready. Both URLs are reachable right now. Neither team had a university budget; they had a cheap domain and a decision to host.","body_zh":"GHCIS 的 ARGUS 在 argus.ucuv.dpdns.org 跑著一個真正的後端——它的 /api/ready 端點回應的是 JSON，不是靜態空殼——還附上 Docker 和原生 Node 兩條部署路徑、角色式存取控制和 SQLite 持久化儲存。HK-Joint-School 的 PyroForge 在 pyroforge.26650078.xyz 提供蛋白質熱穩定性預測，/health 回報 ESM 模型已載入並就緒。兩個網址現在都連得上。兩支隊伍都沒有大學的預算；他們有的是一個便宜的網域，和一個要架站的決定。","chips":["alive","GHCIS","HK-Joint-School","high school","real backend"],"chips_zh":["還活著","GHCIS","HK-Joint-School","高中","真的有後端"],"kicker_zh":"證明這不是預算問題"},{"kicker":"The cautionary tale","title":"Vilnius deployed, then switched it off","title_zh":"Vilnius 部署了，然後把它關掉","body":"Ladder Detector automates gel-image annotation, a genuinely unglamorous and genuinely useful job, and Vilnius-Lithuania did the right thing by deploying it publicly. The URL on their wiki, ladder-detector.onrender.com, now returns HTTP 503 and the text \"This service has been suspended by its owner.\" The Apache-2.0 source is intact on GitLab and still runs via docker compose, so the work is not lost — but every citation of that wiki link now points at a dead page. A free hosting tier is a deadline, not a deployment.","body_zh":"Ladder Detector 把膠體影像的標註自動化，這是一件真的不華麗、也真的有用的工作，而 Vilnius-Lithuania 做了對的事：把它公開部署出去。他們 wiki 上的網址 ladder-detector.onrender.com 現在回傳 HTTP 503 和「This service has been suspended by its owner.」這段文字。Apache-2.0 的原始碼在 GitLab 上完好無缺，用 docker compose 依然跑得起來，所以成果沒有消失——但現在每一次引用那個 wiki 連結，指向的都是一個死掉的頁面。免費代管方案是一個期限，不是一次部署。","chips":["gone","Vilnius-Lithuania","503 suspended","source survives"],"chips_zh":["沒了","Vilnius-Lithuania","503 已停用","原始碼還在"],"kicker_zh":"前車之鑑"},{"kicker":"Honest about the gap","title":"Diana and HUSH publish a URL that is not the tool","title_zh":"Diana 和 HUSH 公布的網址不是工具本身","body":"UMA Malaga's live site opens with a disclaimer: \"Saved results, not the live tool... The pages cannot analyse a variant you type.\" It publishes unedited CLI output with the commit hash, Docker image digest and tool versions recorded — excellent reproducibility practice, but not a service. GU Frankfurt's HUSH page likewise says it \"shows its web app in action\" and then walks through a mockup of screenshots. Both are more honest than most, and both are exactly why a 200 response proves nothing until you read the page.","body_zh":"UMA Malaga 的線上網站一開頭就有免責聲明：「Saved results, not the live tool... The pages cannot analyse a variant you type.」它公開未經修剪的 CLI 輸出，並記下 commit 雜湊值、Docker 映像摘要和工具版本——這是極佳的可重現性實務，但不是一個服務。GU Frankfurt 的 HUSH 頁面同樣寫著它「shows its web app in action」，然後帶你走過一份由截圖組成的介面示意稿。兩者都比大多數隊伍誠實，而兩者也正好說明了為什麼在你讀過頁面之前，一個 200 回應什麼都證明不了。","chips":["source-only","UMA Malaga","GU Frankfurt","demo not deployment"],"chips_zh":["只有原始碼","UMA Malaga","GU Frankfurt","是展示，不是部署"],"kicker_zh":"誠實面對落差"},{"kicker":"Good code, no front door","title":"ETH-Zurich's deCISion is the best source-only release","title_zh":"ETH-Zurich 的 deCISion 是最好的純原始碼釋出","body":"The Best Software winner for Overgrad ships MIT-licensed with a web interface, a JSON API, a CLI, 28 automated tests on every push through GitLab CI, a Docker build, a CITATION.cff and a demo video. It exports FASTA, GenBank and SBOL3 and takes any .pdb or .cif structure, so it would work on someone else's data without modification. The only address on the wiki is localhost:4173. Everything needed to deploy it exists in the repository; nobody deployed it.","body_zh":"這個研究生組的最佳軟體得主以 MIT 授權釋出，附有網頁介面、JSON API、CLI、每次推送都透過 GitLab CI 執行的 28 項自動化測試、一套 Docker 建置、一份 CITATION.cff 和一支示範影片。它可以輸出 FASTA、GenBank 和 SBOL3，也接受任何 .pdb 或 .cif 結構，所以不用改動就能用在別人的資料上。但 wiki 上唯一的位址是 localhost:4173。部署所需要的一切都在儲存庫裡；沒有人去部署它。","chips":["source-only","ETH-Zurich","MIT","CI + Docker","localhost only"],"chips_zh":["只有原始碼","ETH-Zurich","MIT","CI + Docker","只能跑 localhost"],"kicker_zh":"程式很好，沒有入口"},{"kicker":"Check the whole release","title":"Toronto's app is live; its dataset DOI is not","title_zh":"Toronto 的應用還活著，它的資料集 DOI 沒有","body":"PETadex at petadex.net is one of the strongest tools of the year: a sharded DIAMOND search over a 298.7M-sequence corpus, with worked examples loaded and ready to run, nothing to install. But the wiki cites a 23.8 GB Zenodo deposit at doi:10.5281/zenodo.23457986, and that DOI returns 404 — a Zenodo API search for \"petadex\" finds zero records. The interactive half survived and the archival half did not, which is the opposite of what long-term preservation is supposed to deliver.","body_zh":"petadex.net 上的 PETadex 是今年最強的工具之一：對一個 2.987 億條序列的語料做分片 DIAMOND 搜尋，範例已經載好可以直接跑，什麼都不用安裝。但 wiki 引用了一份 23.8 GB 的 Zenodo 存放紀錄 doi:10.5281/zenodo.23457986，而那個 DOI 回傳 404——用 Zenodo API 搜尋「petadex」找到零筆紀錄。互動的那一半活了下來，封存的那一半沒有，這和長期保存本該達成的目標正好相反。","chips":["alive","Toronto","petadex.net","Zenodo DOI 404"],"chips_zh":["還活著","Toronto","petadex.net","Zenodo DOI 404"],"kicker_zh":"檢查整個釋出"}],"table":{"head":["Tool","Team","Status","Live URL / repo","Reusable on other data?"],"head_zh":["工具","隊伍","狀態","線上網址／儲存庫","可用於其他資料？"],"rows":[["AMPilot","XJTLU-Software","alive","https://ampilotlab.com","yes"],["ARGUS","GHCIS","alive","https://argus.ucuv.dpdns.org/client/","yes"],["Atlas COMPASS + EDGE","NJU-China","alive","https://www.starase-atlas.org/","partly"],["PETadex sequence search","Toronto","alive","https://petadex.net/search","yes"],["PyroForge","HK-Joint-School","alive","https://pyroforge.26650078.xyz/","yes"],["PeptiCraft","DKU","alive","https://pepticraft.pages.dev","partly"],["RADAR-Scout","Stanford University","alive","https://radar-scout.vercel.app/","partly"],["SynBase","Stanford University","alive","https://synbase.web.app/home.html","n/a (curriculum)"],["deCISion","ETH-Zurich","source-only","gitlab.igem.org/2026/software/eth-zurich/decision","yes"],["OpenSplitProtein","ETH-Zurich","source-only","gitlab.igem.org/2026/software/eth-zurich/opensplitprotein","yes"],["ReTIsigner","Uni-Padua-IT","source-only","gitlab.igem.org/2026/software/uni-padua-it/retisigner-svelte","yes"],["RK4 solver","UPF-Barcelona","source-only","gitlab.igem.org/2026/software/upf-barcelona/upf-software","yes"],["iGEMforge","UPF-Barcelona","source-only","gitlab.igem.org/2026/software/upf-barcelona/upf-software","partly"],["NetFlux","MIT-MAHE","source-only","gitlab.igem.org/2026/software/mit-mahe/netflux","yes"],["Diana gRNA designer","UMA Malaga","source-only","gitlab.igem.org/2026/software/uma-malaga/diana-grna-designer","yes"],["HUSH","GU Frankfurt","source-only","gitlab.igem.org/2026/software/gu-frankfurt/hush","yes"],["PRINCE","Lambert-GA","source-only","gitlab.igem.org/2026/software/lambert-ga/prince-webapp","yes"],["catmaOS","XJTLU-China","source-only","gitlab.igem.org/2026/software/xjtlu-china/software","partly"],["Bioreactor digital twin","GEMS-Taiwan","source-only","gitlab.igem.org/2026/software/gems-taiwan/digital-twin","no"],["Ladder Detector","Vilnius-Lithuania","gone","ladder-detector.onrender.com (503 suspended)","yes, if self-hosted"],["CERNAL","TAU-Israel","gone","cernal.app + cernal.duckdns.org (both unresolvable)","partly, if self-hosted"],["Electrospinner (no software)","Cornell","n/a","CAD, BOM and manuals only","n/a"],["Bioreactor stack (no software)","KAUST-KSA","n/a","gitlab.igem.org/2026/kaust-ksa","n/a"]],"rows_zh":[["AMPilot","XJTLU-Software","存活","https://ampilotlab.com","是"],["ARGUS","GHCIS","存活","https://argus.ucuv.dpdns.org/client/","是"],["Atlas COMPASS + EDGE","NJU-China","存活","https://www.starase-atlas.org/","部分"],["PETadex 序列搜尋","Toronto","存活","https://petadex.net/search","是"],["PyroForge","HK-Joint-School","存活","https://pyroforge.26650078.xyz/","是"],["PeptiCraft","DKU","存活","https://pepticraft.pages.dev","部分"],["RADAR-Scout","Stanford University","存活","https://radar-scout.vercel.app/","部分"],["SynBase","Stanford University","存活","https://synbase.web.app/home.html","不適用（教學課程）"],["deCISion","ETH-Zurich","僅原始碼","gitlab.igem.org/2026/software/eth-zurich/decision","是"],["OpenSplitProtein","ETH-Zurich","僅原始碼","gitlab.igem.org/2026/software/eth-zurich/opensplitprotein","是"],["ReTIsigner","Uni-Padua-IT","僅原始碼","gitlab.igem.org/2026/software/uni-padua-it/retisigner-svelte","是"],["RK4 求解器","UPF-Barcelona","僅原始碼","gitlab.igem.org/2026/software/upf-barcelona/upf-software","是"],["iGEMforge","UPF-Barcelona","僅原始碼","gitlab.igem.org/2026/software/upf-barcelona/upf-software","部分"],["NetFlux","MIT-MAHE","僅原始碼","gitlab.igem.org/2026/software/mit-mahe/netflux","是"],["Diana gRNA 設計工具","UMA Malaga","僅原始碼","gitlab.igem.org/2026/software/uma-malaga/diana-grna-designer","是"],["HUSH","GU Frankfurt","僅原始碼","gitlab.igem.org/2026/software/gu-frankfurt/hush","是"],["PRINCE","Lambert-GA","僅原始碼","gitlab.igem.org/2026/software/lambert-ga/prince-webapp","是"],["catmaOS","XJTLU-China","僅原始碼","gitlab.igem.org/2026/software/xjtlu-china/software","部分"],["生物反應器數位孿生","GEMS-Taiwan","僅原始碼","gitlab.igem.org/2026/software/gems-taiwan/digital-twin","否"],["Ladder Detector","Vilnius-Lithuania","已消失","ladder-detector.onrender.com（503 已停用）","是，若自行架設"],["CERNAL","TAU-Israel","已消失","cernal.app + cernal.duckdns.org（兩者都無法解析）","部分，若自行架設"],["靜電紡絲機（無軟體）","Cornell","不適用","只有 CAD、BOM 和操作手冊","不適用"],["生物反應器系統（無軟體）","KAUST-KSA","不適用","gitlab.igem.org/2026/kaust-ksa","不適用"]]},"checklist":["Buy a domain and deploy the tool publicly before the wiki freeze, not after it — every tool that is alive today was hosted on freeze day.","Put a clickable URL at the top of the software page; if the only address on the page is localhost, assume nobody outside the team will ever run it.","Let strangers in without an account — guest mode or a no-key API. CERNAL gated behind a lab login is dead; AMPilot's keyless API still answers.","Pay for hosting that outlives the free tier, and check the URL again a month after the Jamboree. Vilnius's deployment lasted weeks.","Expose a documented HTTP API with an OpenAPI spec alongside the UI, so the tool can be a step in someone else's pipeline rather than a destination.","Ship a health endpoint that returns real JSON, so anyone — including a judge or a reviewer — can prove the backend is running and not a static shell.","Accept standard inputs (FASTA, GenBank, SBML, .pdb/.cif) and export standard outputs (SBOL, GenBank, CSV); hard-wiring the tool to your own chassis caps its audience at your team.","Never present a mockup or saved output as the running tool — and if you do publish saved results, label them as plainly as UMA Malaga did.","Verify every archival DOI resolves before you cite it; Toronto's 23.8 GB Zenodo deposit 404s while the web app it supports stays up.","Recruit one outside user and record what they did. Across all 21 tools the only external-adoption number found anywhere was SynBase's 837 learners; stars and forks were zero everywhere."],"checklist_zh":["在 wiki 凍結之前就買下網域、把工具公開部署出去，不要等凍結之後——今天還活著的每一個工具，在凍結當天都已經上線代管。","把可以點擊的網址放在軟體頁面最上方；如果頁面上唯一的位址是 localhost，就假設團隊之外永遠不會有人執行它。","讓陌生人不用帳號就能進來——訪客模式，或是不需要金鑰的 API。擋在實驗室登入後面的 CERNAL 已經死了；AMPilot 不用金鑰的 API 現在還會回應。","付錢買能撐過免費方案的代管，並在 Jamboree 之後一個月再檢查一次網址。Vilnius 的部署只撐了幾週。","在使用者介面之外，再提供一個有 OpenAPI 規格、文件化的 HTTP API，讓這個工具能成為別人流程中的一步，而不只是一個終點。","提供一個會回傳真正 JSON 的健康檢查端點，讓任何人——包括評審或審查者——都能證明後端真的在跑，不是靜態空殼。","接受標準輸入（FASTA、GenBank、SBML、.pdb/.cif），並輸出標準格式（SBOL、GenBank、CSV）；把工具綁死在自己的底盤菌株上，等於把使用者上限設成自己這支隊伍。","絕不要把介面示意稿或存檔輸出當成正在運行的工具呈現——而如果你真的要公布存檔結果，就像 UMA Malaga 那樣清楚標示。","在引用任何封存 DOI 之前，先確認它解析得出來；Toronto 那份 23.8 GB 的 Zenodo 存放紀錄回傳 404，而它支撐的網頁應用還活著。","找一位團隊外的使用者，並記錄他做了什麼。21 個工具中，在任何地方找到的唯一外部採用數字是 SynBase 的 837 位學習者；star 和 fork 數到處都是零。"],"method":"Starting from the 2026 Best Software winners and nominees, the Best Software & AI winners and nominees, and the Best Model and Best Hardware winners, every tool's wiki software page was read (via curl where server-rendered, via the browser pane for client-rendered SPAs), every GitLab and GitHub repository was queried through the GitLab API for file tree, licence, stars, forks and last-commit date, and every candidate deployment was first checked with curl and then opened in a browser and read, because a 200 from an SPA catch-all route proves nothing — starase-atlas.org returns its index page for any /api path, so apparent API endpoints had to be inspected by content. Where a backend health endpoint existed it was called directly (ARGUS /api/ready, PyroForge /health, AMPilot /api/v1/corpus/search, which returned real data). A link check cannot tell you whether the science is correct, whether the tool gives sensible answers on data it has not seen, whether the maintainers intend to keep paying for hosting, or whether anyone is actually using it — zero stars and zero forks mean no public signal, not necessarily no users. Cornell and KAUST-KSA released no standalone software and are listed but excluded from the base rate; TAU-Israel, HK-Joint-School, DKU and XJTLU-Software had no local research file, so their tools were identified from their wikis directly.","method_zh":"起點是 2026 年最佳軟體的得主與入圍者、最佳軟體與 AI 的得主與入圍者，以及最佳模型與最佳硬體的得主：每一個工具的 wiki 軟體頁面都讀過（伺服器端渲染的用 curl，客戶端渲染的單頁應用則用瀏覽器面板），每一個 GitLab 和 GitHub 儲存庫都透過 GitLab API 查詢檔案樹、授權條款、star 數、fork 數和最後一次 commit 的日期，而每一個可能的部署都先用 curl 檢查、再在瀏覽器中開啟並實際閱讀，因為單頁應用萬用路由回傳的 200 什麼都證明不了——starase-atlas.org 對任何 /api 路徑都回傳它的首頁，所以看起來像 API 端點的東西必須逐一檢查內容。有後端健康檢查端點的就直接呼叫（ARGUS 的 /api/ready、PyroForge 的 /health、AMPilot 的 /api/v1/corpus/search，後者回傳了真實資料）。連結檢查無法告訴你科學是否正確、工具在沒見過的資料上是否給出合理答案、維護者是否打算繼續付代管費用，或是否真的有人在用它——零 star 和零 fork 代表沒有公開訊號，不一定代表沒有使用者。Cornell 和 KAUST-KSA 沒有釋出獨立軟體，列入表格但不計入基礎比率；TAU-Israel、HK-Joint-School、DKU 和 XJTLU-Software 沒有本地的研究檔案，他們的工具是直接從 wiki 辨識出來的。","baseRate":{"checked":21,"alive":8,"sourceOnly":11,"stub":0,"gone":2},"kicker_zh":"原創分析","order":34},{"id":"claim-integrity","tab":"judging","order":35,"kicker":"Original analysis","kicker_zh":"原創分析","title":"Over-claiming is the Top 10 norm, and the podium does it slightly more","title_zh":"誇大宣稱是前十名的常態，而且得獎隊伍還稍微誇得更兇","lede":"Across the 2026 Top 10, 21 of the 29 teams with a results page claim more on their landing page than their own evidence supports, and the size of the gap does not track placing — the seven podium teams average 1.43 on a 0–3 scale against 1.00 for the other 22, with the undergraduate second runner-up and the overgraduate first runner-up among the four teams their own pages contradict. GEMS-Taiwan's n = 1 turns out to be a shared habit that cost nobody a prize.","lede_zh":"在 2026 年的前十名中，有結果頁的二十九支隊伍裡，二十一支的首頁宣稱超過了自家證據所能支持的程度；而落差的大小與名次無關——七支頒獎臺隊伍在 0 到 3 的尺度上平均 1.43 分，其餘二十二支平均 1.00 分，大學組季軍與研究生組亞軍還名列四支被自家頁面打臉的隊伍之中。GEMS-Taiwan 那個 n = 1 的案例，結果是一個大家都有、而且沒有害任何人失去獎項的習慣。","body":"Twenty-one of the twenty-nine teams with a results page claim more on their landing page than their own evidence supports. Only eight are clean. That makes over-claiming the normal condition of a Top 10 wiki, not a disqualifying defect — and it is the first thing GEMS-Taiwan should take from this, because GEMS scores 3 and swept three high-school technical awards anyway.\n\nThe expected pattern does not appear. The seven podium teams average 1.43 on the 0–3 scale; the twenty-two other scored teams average 1.00. The podium is **worse**, not better. Two of the four teams whose front page is contradicted by their own pages are Princeton, the undergraduate second runner-up, and WageningenUR, the overgraduate first runner-up. The three Grand Prize winners land at 0, 1 and 1, which is near the cohort middle rather than above it. Inside the High School section the two podium teams do score lower than the rest, 0.5 against 1.0, but that comparison has an n of two and should not be used for anything.\n\nWhat the cohort does share is a particular shape of failure. Fourteen of the twenty-one over-claims score 1: the landing page overshoots in tense or scope, and the results page states the limit in plain words a click away. TU Delft's home page says the coating \"fights bacteria\"; its results page says the peptide was tested on its own and the tethered version is the next experiment. Marburg's home page says its PPR collection is \"controlled by inducible promoters in the nucleus\"; its results page says \"Three turns of the design cycle, two of which did not work.\" These wikis are not dishonest. They have two voices, and the louder one is on the page a judge reads first.\n\nThe four contradictions are a different thing. Princeton puts a \"VIEW EVIDENCE\" link on a 450 nm light-triggered release whose own experiments page says \"the step we have not yet run\". Wageningen says its biosensor \"monitors the TFA level, continuously and on-site\" above a sensing page that says a working TFA riboswitch still needs more work. Cornell says it \"engineered probiotic bacteria to produce and secrete the 810A peptide\" above a contribution page reporting \"no transformants\". GEMS-Taiwan says green light \"switches production on when the environmental sensors and forecasts decide to\" above a results page reading \"the amount did not rise with light\" and a model page reading \"The reactor therefore cannot be scheduled from the forecast.\"\n\nTwo teams sit outside the scale and both are instructive. Heidelberg's home page makes no capability claim at all — a canvas intro, one question, sponsors — and that is a legitimate way to score 0. Eton-College-UK reached the Top 10 with no results page; `/results` is a 404, and its landing page still says \"Then read two numbers\". Whatever else the 2026 judging rewarded, it did not require a reader to be able to check the front page.","body_zh":"有結果頁的二十九支隊伍裡，二十一支的首頁宣稱超過了自家證據所能支持的程度，只有八支是乾淨的。這表示在前十名的 wiki 裡，誇大是常態，而不是會被取消資格的瑕疵——這也是 GEMS-Taiwan 該從這份分析拿走的第一件事，因為 GEMS 得了 3 分，照樣橫掃三項高中組技術獎。\n\n預期中的模式並沒有出現。七支頒獎臺隊伍在 0 到 3 的尺度上平均 1.43 分；其餘二十二支有評分的隊伍平均 1.00 分。頒獎臺**更差**，不是更好。四支首頁被自家頁面打臉的隊伍中，有兩支是大學組季軍 Princeton 與研究生組亞軍 WageningenUR。三個大獎得主分別落在 0、1、1 分，接近整體中位，而不是高於它。在高中組內部，兩支頒獎臺隊伍確實比其他隊低，0.5 對 1.0，但那個比較的 n 等於二，不該拿來證明任何事。\n\n這批隊伍真正共有的，是一種特定形狀的失誤。二十一項誇大中有十四項是 1 分：首頁在時態或範圍上衝過頭，而結果頁就在一次點擊之外，用白話寫明了限制。TU Delft 的首頁說塗層「對抗細菌」；它的結果頁說肽是單獨測試的，接上塗層的版本是下一個實驗。Marburg 的首頁說它的 PPR 集合「由細胞核中的誘導型啟動子控制」；它的結果頁說「設計循環走了三輪，其中兩輪沒有成功。」這些 wiki 並不不誠實。它們有兩個聲音，而比較大聲的那個，就在評審最先讀的那一頁上。\n\n四項矛盾則是另一回事。Princeton 在「450 nm 光觸發釋放」上掛了「看證據」的連結，而它自己的實驗頁說那是「我們還沒跑過的一步」。Wageningen 說它的生物感測器「連續地、就地監測 TFA 濃度」，底下的感測頁卻說可運作的 TFA 核糖開關還需要更多工作。Cornell 說它「改造了益生菌，使其生產並分泌 810A 肽」，底下的貢獻頁報告的是「沒有轉形株」。GEMS-Taiwan 說綠光「當環境感測器與預報判定該開工時就把生產打開」，底下的結果頁寫著「量並未隨光照上升」，模型頁寫著「因此這台反應器無法依預報排程。」\n\n有兩支隊伍落在尺度之外，而且都很有啟發。Heidelberg 的首頁完全沒有能力宣稱——一段畫布開場、一個問句、贊助商——那是拿到 0 分的正當方式。Eton-College-UK 則是在沒有結果頁的情況下進了前十；`/results` 是 404，而它的首頁仍然寫著「然後讀兩個數字」。不管 2026 年的評審還獎勵了什麼，它並沒有要求讀者有辦法去核對首頁。","cards":[{"kicker":"The scale","kicker_zh":"評分尺度","title":"Four grades, and an aim is not an over-claim","title_zh":"四個等級，而「目標」不算誇大","body":"Every team was scored 0 to 3 on one thing only: the single strongest capability sentence a reader meets first on the landing page, set against what the team's own results page says about that same claim. A tagline that names an aim — \"we aim to\", \"our goal is\", \"our project focuses on\", or a question — is not an over-claim, and neither is a how-it-works walkthrough that explains the design in the present tense. What gets scored is a demonstrated capability asserted in the present indicative. **Eight teams score 0. Fourteen score 1. Three score 2. Four score 3. One has no results page.**","body_zh":"每一隊只就一件事評 0 到 3 分：讀者在首頁最先遇到的那一句最強的能力宣稱，對照該隊自己結果頁對同一宣稱的說法。標語若明說是目標——「我們希望」「我們的目標是」「我們的專題聚焦於」，或乾脆是個問句——不算誇大；用現在式解釋設計如何運作的流程說明，也不算。真正被計分的，是以現在直述語氣斷言的、已經做到的能力。**八隊得 0 分，十四隊得 1 分，三隊得 2 分，四隊得 3 分，一隊沒有結果頁。**","chips":["0 = supported or hedged","3 = contradicted","n = 30"],"chips_zh":["0 = 有證據或已留餘地","3 = 被自己打臉","n = 30"]},{"kicker":"The reversal","kicker_zh":"反轉","title":"The podium over-claims more, not less","title_zh":"得獎隊伍誇得更多，不是更少","body":"The seven podium teams average **1.43**; the other twenty-two scored teams average **1.00**. Two of the four teams that contradict themselves are podium teams: Princeton, the undergraduate second runner-up, and WageningenUR, the overgraduate first runner-up. Inside the High School section the direction flips the expected way — Lambert-GA scores 0 and HongKong-JSS scores 1, against a mean of 1.0 for the other seven scored teams — but that comparison rests on two podium wikis. At these numbers neither direction means anything. The honest reading is that claim integrity and placing are unrelated in the 2026 Top 10.","body_zh":"七支登上頒獎臺的隊伍平均 **1.43** 分；其餘二十二支有評分的隊伍平均 **1.00** 分。四支自相矛盾的隊伍中有兩支在頒獎臺上：大學組季軍 Princeton，以及研究生組亞軍 WageningenUR。在高中組內部，方向倒是符合直覺——Lambert-GA 得 0 分、HongKong-JSS 得 1 分，其餘七支有評分的隊伍平均 1.0 分——但這個比較只建立在兩個得獎網站上。以這種樣本數，兩個方向都說明不了什麼。誠實的讀法是：在 2026 年的前十名裡，宣稱的誠實度和名次無關。","chips":["Podium mean 1.43 (n = 7)","Rest mean 1.00 (n = 22)","No signal"],"chips_zh":["頒獎臺平均 1.43（n = 7）","其餘平均 1.00（n = 22）","沒有訊號"]},{"kicker":"The worst gap","kicker_zh":"最大的落差","title":"Princeton puts \"VIEW EVIDENCE\" on a step it never ran","title_zh":"Princeton 在一步沒跑過的實驗上掛了「看證據」","body":"Princeton's home page opens with four stat tiles, each carrying a \"VIEW EVIDENCE\" link. One reads **450 nm — LIGHT-TRIGGERED RELEASE**. Follow it and the Experiments page says: \"The phage version described above is the step we have not yet run.\" The figure directly beneath is captioned \"the published assay this experiment is modelled on, not our own data\". The landing page also states that no adsorbent combines bulk capacity, specificity and renewable release, and that \"SymPleco fills that gap\". Renewable release is the one leg of the three that was never tested.","body_zh":"Princeton 的首頁一開場就是四張數據卡，每一張都掛著「看證據」的連結。其中一張寫著 **450 nm — 光觸發釋放**。點進去，實驗頁卻說：「上文所述的噬菌體版本，是我們還沒跑過的一步。」正下方那張圖的說明是「這是本實驗所仿照的已發表分析，不是我們自己的數據」。首頁同時主張市面上沒有吸附材同時具備大容量、專一性與可再生釋放，而「SymPleco 補上了這個缺口」。三條腿裡，可再生釋放正是從未被測試的那一條。","chips":["Undergrad 2nd Runner-up","Score 3","Evidence link to a blank"],"chips_zh":["大學組季軍","3 分","證據連結指向空白"]},{"kicker":"The worst gap","kicker_zh":"最大的落差","title":"Wageningen's biosensor monitors a molecule it cannot sense yet","title_zh":"Wageningen 的生物感測器監測一個它還測不到的分子","body":"WageningenUR's landing page lays out three steps and closes with \"We make the forever chemical forever no more.\" Step 3 reads: \"Our biosensor monitors the TFA level, continuously and on-site.\" The Sensing page's own conclusion is: \"In order to create a working TFA riboswitch, more experiments and tests are needed.\" What worked was a PFOA riboswitch, a longer and easier target. The Degradation page is equally plain: \"No enzyme is known to defluorinate TFA… We did not expect TFA activity.\" The science underneath is careful; the front page is a different document.","body_zh":"WageningenUR 的首頁列出三個步驟，收尾是「我們讓永久化學物質不再永久。」第三步寫著：「我們的生物感測器連續地、就地監測 TFA 濃度。」而感測頁自己的結論是：「要做出能運作的 TFA 核糖開關，還需要更多實驗與測試。」真正成功的是 PFOA 核糖開關——一個鏈更長、也更容易的標的。降解頁同樣直白：「目前沒有已知的酵素能對 TFA 去氟……我們原本就不預期會有 TFA 活性。」底下的科學做得很謹慎；首頁則像是另一份文件。","chips":["Overgrad 1st Runner-up","Score 3","PFOA worked, TFA did not"],"chips_zh":["研究生組亞軍","3 分","PFOA 成功，TFA 沒有"]},{"kicker":"The worst gap","kicker_zh":"最大的落差","title":"Cornell engineered a bacterium it never transformed","title_zh":"Cornell 改造了一株從未轉形成功的細菌","body":"Cornell's home page says, in the past tense, \"Our team engineered probiotic bacteria to produce and secrete the 810A peptide that inhibits the functional region of connective tissue growth factor (CTGF).\" The Contribution page says: \"We tested multiple protocols using different electroporation techniques with no transformants, but we will continue to optimize this process.\" The Entrepreneurship page adds, in the present progressive, \"Where we are now. Our wet lab is confirming that the bacteria produce 810A, that 810A binds CTGF, which bacterial host performs best, and that the matrix retains the bacteria.\" Four open questions, one finished sentence on the front page.","body_zh":"Cornell 的首頁用過去式寫著：「我們的團隊改造了益生菌，使其生產並分泌 810A 肽，抑制結締組織生長因子（CTGF）的功能區域。」貢獻頁卻說：「我們以不同電穿孔技術測試了多種流程，都沒有得到轉形株，但我們會繼續最佳化這個流程。」創業頁再用現在進行式補上：「我們現在的進度：濕式實驗室正在確認細菌是否生產 810A、810A 是否結合 CTGF、哪一種宿主菌表現最好，以及基質是否留得住細菌。」四個還沒答案的問題，在首頁變成一句已完成的話。","chips":["Score 3","No transformants","Past tense on the front page"],"chips_zh":["3 分","沒有轉形株","首頁用過去式"]},{"kicker":"What a zero looks like","kicker_zh":"零分長什麼樣","title":"Athens and Lambert put the limit in the same breath","title_zh":"Athens 和 Lambert 把限制寫在同一口氣裡","body":"Athens's home page has a block headed **What we have shown**, with a tick, the number and the strain: \"~40% fall in OD600 of M. plutonius (LMG 20360) with purified EndoLys 50 µg/mL\". The third thing the wet lab set out to do is still written as a question on that same page. Lambert-GA does the same at high-school level: \"Ours bind VP3, with the aim of blocking infection in the bee's gut\", and its results page says outright that binding \"is distinguish[ed] from antiviral protection in bees, which was not established by this assay\". Neither team sells less science. They sell the same science with its conditions attached.","body_zh":"Athens 的首頁有一個區塊，標題就是 **我們已經證明的**，附上勾號、數字與菌株：「以 50 µg/mL 純化 EndoLys 處理，蜂房球菌（LMG 20360）的 OD600 下降約 40%」。濕式實驗室想做的第三件事，在同一頁上仍然寫成問句。Lambert-GA 在高中組做了同樣的事：「我們的迷你結合蛋白結合 VP3，目標是阻斷蜜蜂腸道內的感染」，而它的結果頁直說，結合「與蜜蜂體內的抗病毒保護是兩回事，後者並未由此分析建立」。兩隊都沒有少賣科學，他們賣的是同一份科學，連同條件一起。","chips":["Athens 0","Lambert-GA 0","Numbers with their conditions"],"chips_zh":["Athens 0 分","Lambert-GA 0 分","數字連著條件一起給"]},{"kicker":"Two edge cases","kicker_zh":"兩個邊界案例","title":"Heidelberg claims nothing; Eton has nowhere to check","title_zh":"Heidelberg 什麼都沒宣稱；Eton 則無處可查","body":"Heidelberg's home page is the only one in the Top 10 with no capability claim on it at all. It is a canvas intro whose single line is a question — \"What if we could hear what we have never seen?\" — followed by sponsors and a contact block. Scoring it is trivial because there is nothing to overshoot. Eton-College-UK sits at the other edge: its landing page says \"Protease activity becomes an electrical signal… Then read two numbers\", and `/results` returns \"Page not found\". The hardware page calls the cartridge \"an initial render\". A reader cannot check the front page against anything, so Eton gets its own category rather than a score.","body_zh":"Heidelberg 的首頁是前十名中唯一完全沒有任何能力宣稱的一頁。那是一段畫布動畫開場，唯一的一句話是問句——「如果我們能聽見從未見過的東西呢？」——接著就是贊助商與聯絡資訊。評分很容易，因為根本沒有東西可以超出。Eton-College-UK 在另一端：首頁寫著「蛋白酶活性變成電訊號……然後讀兩個數字」，而 `/results` 回傳「找不到頁面」。硬體頁把試劑匣稱為「初版算圖」。讀者無從拿首頁去對照任何東西，所以 Eton 另列一類，不給分數。","chips":["Heidelberg: a question, not a claim","Eton: /results is a 404","1 of 30 unscorable"],"chips_zh":["Heidelberg：一個問句，不是宣稱","Eton：/results 是 404","30 隊中有 1 隊無法評分"]},{"kicker":"What this means for GEMS","kicker_zh":"這對 GEMS 的意義","title":"GEMS is joint-worst, and that cost it nothing","title_zh":"GEMS 並列最差，而這並沒有讓它付出代價","body":"GEMS-Taiwan is one of four teams in the cohort whose landing page is contradicted by its own pages, and it is the only team whose contradiction spans three of them: the results page on the light response, the ELISA and the chromoprotein, and the model page on scheduling. It still swept three high-school technical awards. So the roadmap item that tells GEMS to close this gap should not be sold as a placing lever — nothing here says it is one. It is a credibility lever. The wiki already withdraws its own claims everywhere except the one page a judge reads first, and that inconsistency is the actual defect.","body_zh":"GEMS-Taiwan 是這批隊伍中四支首頁被自家頁面打臉的隊伍之一，而且是唯一一支矛盾橫跨三頁的：結果頁在光反應、ELISA 與顯色蛋白三處，模型頁在排程一處。它仍然橫掃了三項高中組技術獎。所以那條要 GEMS 補上這個落差的路線圖事項，不該被包裝成名次的槓桿——這份資料沒有任何地方這樣說。它是可信度的槓桿。這個 wiki 在其他地方到處都在收回自己的主張，唯獨在評審最先讀的那一頁沒有，而這個不一致本身才是真正的瑕疵。","chips":["Score 3","Joint-worst of 30","Swept three technical awards"],"chips_zh":["3 分","30 隊中並列最差","橫掃三項技術獎"]}],"table":{"head":["Team","Section and placing","Top claim on the landing page","What its own evidence page says","Gap"],"head_zh":["隊伍","組別與名次","首頁最強宣稱","自家證據頁怎麼說","落差"],"rows":[["Lambert-GA (6185)","High School — Grand Prize","“Ours bind VP3, with the aim of blocking infection in the bee’s gut.” — and “The first-ever experimentally validated de novo minibinder for an iflavirus.”","“a combined affinity of 603.6 nM across two replicates (95% confidence interval: 497.1–733.3 nM)”, then: “The experimental validation results distinguish binding to the tested VP3 construct from antiviral protection in bees, which was not established by this assay.”","0"],["HongKong-JSS (6158)","High School — 1st Runner-up","“MerMAID is a living sensor that glows red when it meets mercury, read by a portable detector, and fed by a sample-extraction platform that turns other samples into water.”","“The visual readout needs a centrifuge: colour in unspun culture is distinguishable by eye only above about 0.5 µM. Soil mercury was not measured directly, and the bead work was qualitative.”","1"],["Eton-College-UK (6462)","High School","“Protease activity becomes an electrical signal. Press, dilute, insert. Then read two numbers.”","There is no results page; `/results` returns “Page not found”. The Hardware page says of the cartridge: “this is an initial render”.","no results page"],["GCGS (6242)","High School","“Attack: Only upon activation, it releases Alginate Lyase to tear down the biofilm walls.”","“Due to laboratory safety constraints, we were unable to perform wet lab experiments using live pathogenic P. aeruginosa biofilm samples. Our activity evaluation was limited to purified sodium alginate substrate in cell free in vitro assay.”","1"],["GEMS-Taiwan (6072)","High School","“On-demand — Green light switches production on when the environmental sensors and forecasts decide to.”","Results: “the amount did not rise with light”; “The ELISA showed no change over time”; “the medium remained colorless”. Model: “The reactor therefore cannot be scheduled from the forecast.”","3"],["GHCIS (6166)","High School","“The toehold sequences were carefully selected and validated to reduce the incidence of missed detections and false positives.”","“The present results support continued development toward waterborne resistance-gene monitoring; they do not yet establish a validated detection limit or the performance of the complete DNA-to-color workflow.”","1"],["HFI (6178)","High School","“Our goal: Apply synthetic biology to construct engineered probiotics encapsulated into capsules, achieving pain free treatment for patients.”","“Due to experimental time constraints, we have not completed quantitative detection…” and “Kill-switch characterization is incomplete”.","0"],["HKSSC (6053)","High School","“Lab results prove our solution works, paving the way for faster food waste recycling and a greener earth.”","“due to the constraints with the limitation of sample numbers, we were unable to use more standards with a wider range and smaller increments”; the degradation read is “it can be deduced that the later peaks at 1 and 15 are the products of prbA”.","2"],["HangzhouFourteenAP (6197)","High School","“An enzyme-based approach to dental calculus, designed to disrupt biofilms and protect the tooth surface.”","The landing page qualifies itself: “Our current work evaluates enzyme activity and biofilm disruption in vitro. Clinical calculus removal, long-term protection and formulation performance require further validation.”","0"],["HongKong-HS (6214)","High School","“A urine-based test-kit concept for chronic kidney disease.” — “Our project explores urinary miRNAs as signals for CKD screening.”","“increasing concentrations of target miRNA did not result in a positive correlation… suggesting limited assay sensitivity or target-specific inhibition at elevated miRNA levels.”","0"],["Stanford University (6278)","Undergrad — Grand Prize","“Finding the Imposter in Keloid Scars. A therapy that reads a cell before it treats it.”","“Transfecting our top-performing sensors into fibroblasts proved challenging.” and “But levels of therapeutic output are still low.”","1"],["UCAS-China (6157)","Undergrad — 1st Runner-up","“A novel RNA delivery platform for asthma inhalation medication, provides a new choice.”","“no obvious dose-dependent leakage was observed” and “the fluorescence measurements did not establish a solely G_eCFP-dependent increase in ligation efficiency”.","1"],["Princeton (6295)","Undergrad — 2nd Runner-up","Hero stat tile: “450 nm — LIGHT-TRIGGERED RELEASE — VIEW EVIDENCE”, over “No adsorbent on the market combines bulk capacity, molecular specificity, and controlled, renewable release. SymPleco fills that gap”.","Experiments: “The phage version described above is the step we have not yet run.” The figure under it is captioned “the published assay this experiment is modelled on, not our own data”.","3"],["Cornell (6122)","Undergrad","“Our team engineered probiotic bacteria to produce and secrete the 810A peptide that inhibits the functional region of connective tissue growth factor (CTGF).”","Contribution: “We tested multiple protocols using different electroporation techniques with no transformants.” Entrepreneurship: “Where we are now. Our wet lab is confirming that the bacteria produce 810A…”","3"],["Heidelberg (6249)","Undergrad","The home page carries no capability claim at all. Its only line is a question: “What if we could hear what we have never seen?”","The claim lives on the Description page instead: “VOYAGE — An acoustic platform for observation and organization of living systems.” The Results page is linked as “Where data tells the story”.","0"],["LYON (6280)","Undergrad","“Our project focuses on extracting TFA from water using an engineered thermo-reversible affinity system that relies on a TFA-specific protein binder.”","“No activity above background on TFA.” and “TFA is recognised, but the signal is carried by the carboxylate and not by the fluorines”, plus “We do not claim a doubled affinity.”","1"],["NUS-Singapore (6395)","Undergrad","“ORCHID’s engineered yeast strains carry genetically encoded biosensors that report the cell’s internal state directly, in real time, while the process is running.”","“ORCHID aims to read ER, oxidative and energy stress from a single yeast strain carrying several biosensors.” The data are plate-reader dose–response curves; no run inside a live fermentation is reported either way.","2"],["UAlberta (6254)","Undergrad","“How our three engineered proteins work together to deliver medicine precisely where it is needed and to hold it in place”, over tiles reading “Drug Retention increased”.","“the mutant had diminished retention (0.675%) when compared to the wild type (2.889%)” in the frog eye model.","1"],["UCNZ (6301)","Undergrad","“NanoBrew is developing a sustainable, enzyme orientated approach to break down brewers’ spent grain and access nanocellulose.”","Hedged on the landing page itself: “Our experimental data will be used to assess the economic and sustainable feasibility of up-scaling this process into a one-pot bioreactor.”","0"],["UOttawa (6077)","Undergrad","“We have optimized this platform at the enzyme, regulatory, and cellular levels”, closing with “we show that biodesulfurization is a promising alternative for removing DBT from oil”.","“obtained preliminary evidence of 2-HBP formation from one engineered strain”.","1"],["TU Delft (6110)","Overgrad — Grand Prize","“It helps your cells attach to the implant, it fights bacteria, and can deliver and release additional cargo exactly where needed.”","“As a first step, we tested the AMP SAAP-148 on its own… These results provide the baseline against which we will compare SAAP-148 once it is attached to our ELPs.” The coating itself was never tested against bacteria.","1"],["WageningenUR (6222)","Overgrad — 1st Runner-up","“Step 3 Sense. Our biosensor monitors the TFA level, continuously and on-site.” — and “We make the forever chemical forever no more.”","Sensing: “In order to create a working TFA riboswitch, more experiments and tests are needed.” Degradation: “No enzyme is known to defluorinate TFA… We did not expect TFA activity”.","3"],["Athens (6478)","Overgrad","“What we have shown: Lyses M. plutonius in vitro — ~40% fall in OD600 of M. plutonius (LMG 20360) with purified EndoLys 50 µg/mL”.","The results page carries the same numbers, and the one unanswered question stays a question on the landing page: “Can we make it stronger by fusing it to an antimicrobial peptide?”","0"],["ETH-Zurich (6289)","Overgrad","“We targeted PVCs to CD20, a protein on the surface of certain human cells, and could prove to affect these cells specifically.”","“The de novo designed anti-CD20 binder gave 9.1%, roughly threefold over every negative control in the same plate (PBS ~2.95%, empty cage with binder ~3.2–3.8%, non-injecting Cre control ~3.0%).”","0"],["GU Frankfurt (6108)","Overgrad","“By hiding the differences, we protect the organ and leave the immune system free to do the rest… In short: we HIDE the organ from the immune system.”","“With the generated binder data being preliminary, there are no definitive results to be extracted from them.” and “we were not able to verify that the siRNA was indeed in the sEVs”.","1"],["KAUST-KSA (6341)","Overgrad","“We integrate engineered microorganisms, a modular bioreactor, and automated purification to produce high-value proteins when and where they are needed.”","Proof of Concept hedges to “a compact bioreactor prototype designed to regulate culture conditions”; the proteins on the Results page were purified on a bench HisTrap column, and the integrated animation is captioned “an illustration of the sequence, not measured data”.","2"],["Marburg (6350)","Overgrad","“Our collection of synthetic PPRs provides sequence-specific binding to engineered chloroplast RNA, controlled by inducible promoters in the nucleus.”","“Three turns of the design cycle, two of which did not work.” “Where regulation was not observed, the explanation therefore lies downstream of binding.” The Chlamydomonas transformants are “currently under selection”.","1"],["Muenster-University (6339)","Overgrad","“A modular platform technology that updates native plant immune sensors to identify pathogens directly and induce an instant and effective immune response.”","“Successful HR induction when minimal constructs were infiltrated with the corresponding pathogen protease” — but also “we could not detect any protease” in the expression host, and one of three cleavage sites failed.","1"],["Toronto (6187)","Overgrad","“To fight the growing accumulation of microplastics everywhere, we’re revolutionizing the field of plastic-degrading enzymes”, over “identify, engineer, and deploy highly efficient plastic-degrading enzymes”.","The results page reports assay controls, not enzymes: “The next steps are to test whether msGFP2 can be sufficiently expressed with the copper amounts that can be realistically released from the mesh”.","1"],["UZurich (6269)","Overgrad","“Our bacteria produce calcium carbonate more efficiently and uniformly, binding soil particles together for more consistent soil reinforcement.”","“the results presented here were obtained using our model organism, Escherichia coli”, and for the urease assay “no reliable conclusion can be made from this assay”.","1"]],"rows_zh":[["Lambert-GA (6185)","高中組 — 大獎","「我們的迷你結合蛋白結合 VP3，目標是阻斷蜜蜂腸道內的感染。」以及「史上第一個經實驗驗證、針對 iflavirus 的從頭設計迷你結合蛋白。」","「兩次重複實驗合併後的親和力為 603.6 nM（95% 信賴區間：497.1–733.3 nM）」，接著寫明：「本次實驗驗證的是與所測 VP3 構築體的結合，而非蜜蜂體內的抗病毒保護；後者並未由此分析建立。」","0"],["HongKong-JSS (6158)","高中組 — 亞軍","「MerMAID 是一個活體感測器，遇到汞就發出紅色，由可攜式偵測器讀取，並由一套樣品萃取平台把其他樣品轉成水。」","「目視讀數需要離心機：未離心的菌液顏色要到約 0.5 µM 以上肉眼才分得出來。土壤汞並未直接量測，而磁珠部分只是定性。」","1"],["Eton-College-UK (6462)","高中組","「蛋白酶活性變成電訊號。按壓、稀釋、插入，然後讀兩個數字。」","沒有結果頁；`/results` 回傳「找不到頁面」。硬體頁對試劑匣的說明是「這只是初版算圖」。","無結果頁"],["GCGS (6242)","高中組","「攻擊：只有在被活化時，它才釋出藻酸鹽裂解酶，拆掉生物膜的牆。」","「受限於實驗室安全規範，我們無法以活的致病性綠膿桿菌生物膜樣品進行濕式實驗。我們的活性評估僅限於純化藻酸鈉受質的無細胞體外分析。」","1"],["GEMS-Taiwan (6072)","高中組","「隨需生產 — 當環境感測器與預報判定該開工時，綠光就把生產打開。」","結果頁：「量並未隨光照上升」、「ELISA 顯示隨時間沒有變化」、「培養液維持無色」。模型頁：「因此這台反應器無法依預報排程。」","3"],["GHCIS (6166)","高中組","「這些 toehold 序列經過仔細挑選與驗證，以降低漏檢與偽陽性的發生率。」","「目前的結果支持朝水體抗藥基因監測繼續開發；但尚未建立經驗證的偵測極限，也尚未確立完整 DNA 到顯色流程的效能。」","1"],["HFI (6178)","高中組","「我們的目標：運用合成生物學建構封裝成膠囊的工程益生菌，為病人達成無痛治療。」","「受限於實驗時間，我們尚未完成定量偵測……」以及「自殺開關的特性分析並不完整」。","0"],["HKSSC (6053)","高中組","「實驗結果證明我們的方案可行，為更快的廚餘回收與更綠的地球鋪路。」","「受限於樣品數量，我們無法使用範圍更廣、間距更小的標準品」；對降解的判讀則是「可以推論第 1 與第 15 個波峰是 prbA 的產物」。","2"],["HangzhouFourteenAP (6197)","高中組","「一套以酵素為基礎、針對牙結石的做法，設計用來瓦解生物膜並保護牙面。」","首頁自己就加上限制：「我們目前的工作是在體外評估酵素活性與生物膜瓦解。臨床上的牙結石清除、長期保護與配方表現仍需進一步驗證。」","0"],["HongKong-HS (6214)","高中組","「一個以尿液為基礎的慢性腎臟病試劑組構想。」—「我們的專題探討尿液 miRNA 作為慢性腎臟病篩檢訊號的可能。」","「提高目標 miRNA 濃度並未帶來正相關……顯示分析靈敏度有限，或在高 miRNA 濃度下有標的專一的抑制。」","0"],["Stanford University (6278)","大學組 — 大獎","「在蟹足腫裡找出冒牌貨。一種先讀懂細胞、再治療細胞的療法。」","「把表現最好的感測器轉染進纖維母細胞相當困難。」以及「但治療性輸出的量仍然偏低。」","1"],["UCAS-China (6157)","大學組 — 亞軍","「一個用於氣喘吸入式給藥的新型 RNA 遞送平台，提供了新的選擇。」","「並未觀察到明顯的劑量依賴性滲漏」，以及「螢光量測並未確立接合效率僅取決於 G_eCFP 的上升」。","1"],["Princeton (6295)","大學組 — 季軍","首頁數據卡：「450 nm — 光觸發釋放 — 看證據」，底下寫著「市面上沒有任何吸附材同時具備大容量、分子專一性與可控、可再生的釋放。SymPleco 補上了這個缺口」。","實驗頁：「上文所述的噬菌體版本，是我們還沒跑過的一步。」底下的圖說明寫著「這是本實驗所仿照的已發表分析，不是我們自己的數據」。","3"],["Cornell (6122)","大學組","「我們的團隊改造了益生菌，使其生產並分泌 810A 肽，抑制結締組織生長因子（CTGF）的功能區域。」","貢獻頁：「我們以不同電穿孔技術測試了多種流程，都沒有得到轉形株。」創業頁：「我們現在的進度：濕式實驗室正在確認細菌是否生產 810A……」","3"],["Heidelberg (6249)","大學組","首頁完全沒有任何能力宣稱，唯一的一句話是個問句：「如果我們能聽見從未見過的東西呢？」","宣稱改放在專題說明頁：「VOYAGE — 一個用於觀察與組織活體系統的聲學平台。」結果頁在選單上的副標是「數據說故事的地方」。","0"],["LYON (6280)","大學組","「我們的專題聚焦於以一套工程化的熱可逆親和系統，搭配對 TFA 專一的蛋白結合子，把 TFA 從水中萃取出來。」","「對 TFA 沒有高於背景值的活性。」以及「TFA 確實被辨識，但訊號來自羧酸根而不是氟原子」，並寫明「我們並不宣稱親和力加倍。」","1"],["NUS-Singapore (6395)","大學組","「ORCHID 的工程酵母菌株帶有基因編碼的生物感測器，在製程運轉當下即時、直接回報細胞的內部狀態。」","「ORCHID 的目標是從單一酵母菌株上同時讀出內質網、氧化與能量逆境。」實際數據是盤讀儀的劑量反應曲線；至於在真實發酵中即時讀取，結果頁既沒有證實也沒有否認。","2"],["UAlberta (6254)","大學組","「我們的三個工程蛋白如何協同運作，把藥物精準送到需要的地方並留在那裡」，下方的數據卡寫著「藥物滯留 上升」。","「在爪蟾眼睛模型中，突變體的滯留率（0.675%）低於野生型（2.889%）。」","1"],["UCNZ (6301)","大學組","「NanoBrew 正在發展一套永續、以酵素為導向的方法，分解啤酒糟並取得奈米纖維素。」","首頁本身就留了餘地：「我們的實驗數據將用來評估把這個製程放大成一鍋式生物反應器在經濟與永續上的可行性。」","0"],["UOttawa (6077)","大學組","「我們已在酵素、調控與細胞三個層級上最佳化這個平台」，收尾則是「我們顯示生物脫硫是移除油品中 DBT 的一個有潛力的替代方案」。","「從一株工程菌取得了 2-HBP 生成的初步證據。」","1"],["TU Delft (6110)","研究生組 — 大獎","「它幫助你的細胞附著在植入物上，它對抗細菌，也能把額外的貨物精準遞送並釋放到需要的位置。」","「第一步，我們單獨測試了抗菌肽 SAAP-148……這些結果提供了基準線，供日後 SAAP-148 接上我們的 ELP 之後比較。」塗層本身從未對細菌測試過。","1"],["WageningenUR (6222)","研究生組 — 亞軍","「第三步 感測。我們的生物感測器連續地、就地監測 TFA 濃度。」以及「我們讓永久化學物質不再永久。」","感測頁：「要做出能運作的 TFA 核糖開關，還需要更多實驗與測試。」降解頁：「目前沒有已知的酵素能對 TFA 去氟……我們原本就不預期會有 TFA 活性。」","3"],["Athens (6478)","研究生組","「我們已經證明的：在體外裂解蜂房球菌 — 以 50 µg/mL 純化 EndoLys 處理，蜂房球菌（LMG 20360）的 OD600 下降約 40%」。","結果頁載的是同一組數字；而唯一還沒答案的問題，在首頁上仍然以問句呈現：「把它和抗菌肽融合，能不能讓它更強？」","0"],["ETH-Zurich (6289)","研究生組","「我們把 PVC 導向 CD20（某些人類細胞表面的一個蛋白），並且能證明它專一地作用在這些細胞上。」","「從頭設計的抗 CD20 結合子得到 9.1%，大約是同一盤中每一個陰性對照的三倍（PBS 約 2.95%、空殼加結合子約 3.2–3.8%、不注射的 Cre 對照約 3.0%）。」","0"],["GU Frankfurt (6108)","研究生組","「藉由把差異藏起來，我們保護器官，讓免疫系統去做其餘的事……簡單說：我們把器官對免疫系統藏起來。」","「由於所產生的結合子數據仍屬初步，無法從中得出確定的結論。」以及「我們無法確認 siRNA 確實在小型胞外囊泡裡面」。","1"],["KAUST-KSA (6341)","研究生組","「我們整合工程微生物、模組化生物反應器與自動化純化，在需要的時間與地點生產高價值蛋白質。」","概念驗證頁的措辭退為「一台設計用來調控培養條件的小型生物反應器原型」；結果頁上的蛋白是用實驗檯上的 HisTrap 管柱純化的，而整合流程動畫的圖說是「這是流程順序的示意，不是量測數據」。","2"],["Marburg (6350)","研究生組","「我們的合成 PPR 集合提供對工程化葉綠體 RNA 的序列專一結合，並由細胞核中的誘導型啟動子控制。」","「設計循環走了三輪，其中兩輪沒有成功。」「在沒有觀察到調控的地方，原因因此落在結合的下游。」萊茵衣藻的轉殖株「目前還在篩選中」。","1"],["Muenster-University (6339)","研究生組","「一套模組化平台技術，把作物原生的免疫感測器升級成能直接辨識病原，並誘發即時而有效的免疫反應。」","「以對應的病原蛋白酶浸潤最小化構築體時，成功誘發過敏性反應」—但同一頁也寫著在表現宿主中「我們偵測不到任何蛋白酶」，而三個切割位中有一個失敗。","1"],["Toronto (6187)","研究生組","「為了對抗到處累積的微塑膠，我們正在革新塑膠降解酵素這個領域」，上方則寫著「找出、改造並部署高效率的塑膠降解酵素」。","結果頁報告的是分析方法的對照組，而不是酵素：「接下來要測試的是，在試片實際能釋出的銅量下，msGFP2 是否能被充分表現。」","1"],["UZurich (6269)","研究生組","「我們的細菌生產碳酸鈣的效率更高、分布更均勻，把土壤顆粒結合起來，達成更一致的邊坡補強。」","「此處呈現的結果是用我們的模式生物大腸桿菌取得的」，而尿素酶分析則是「無法從這個分析做出可靠的結論」。","1"]]},"checklist":["Write the landing page last, after the results page is frozen, and build every hero line from a sentence that already exists in Results.","Mark aims as aims on the front page: \"we set out to\", \"our goal is\", or a question, as Athens, UCNZ and HangzhouFourteenAP do.","Put the condition next to the number on the landing page, the way HongKong-JSS writes \"under assay conditions\" beside its 1 ppb.","Never label a stat tile \"evidence\" unless the linked page holds your own measurement; Princeton's 450 nm tile is the cohort's clearest failure.","Audit every present-indicative verb on the landing page and ask which figure on Results it points to; delete or re-tense the ones with no figure.","Fix the On-demand card first: the reactor's own model page says it cannot be scheduled from the forecast, so the front page must not say it is.","Keep the hedge in the same sentence, not in a footnote lower down — a reader who bounces off the hero never reaches the footnote.","Ship a results page at all, and make the headline evidence reachable in one click from the hero, since one Top 10 team had neither."],"checklist_zh":["首頁最後才寫：等結果頁定稿之後，再從結果頁既有的句子裡長出每一句主視覺文案。","在首頁把目標標成目標：「我們著手要做的是」「我們的目標是」，或乾脆用問句，像 Athens、UCNZ 與 HangzhouFourteenAP 那樣。","在首頁把條件寫在數字旁邊，就像 HongKong-JSS 在 1 ppb 旁邊寫「在本分析條件下」。","除非連過去的頁面裡放著你們自己的量測，否則別把數據卡標成「證據」；Princeton 的 450 nm 卡是這批隊伍中最明顯的反例。","逐一檢查首頁上每一個現在直述語氣的動詞，問它指向結果頁的哪一張圖；指不到圖的，刪掉或改時態。","先修「隨需生產」那張卡：反應器自己的模型頁說它無法依預報排程，首頁就不該說它可以。","把保留寫在同一句裡，不要塞進下面的註腳——看完主視覺就離開的讀者，永遠讀不到註腳。","至少要有一個結果頁，而且讓頭條證據從主視覺一次點擊就到得了，因為前十名裡有一隊兩者皆無。"],"method":"For each of the 30 teams in the 2026 Top 10 I read two things: the landing page as a reader meets it, and the page that carries the headline evidence (results, or where no results page exists, description, proof of concept, engineering or the equivalent wet-lab page). Static and server-rendered wikis were fetched directly with curl and a browser User-Agent, and the HTML was HTML-unescaped before any pattern matching. TU Delft was read through its Markdown mirrors at `/tu-delft/<page>.md`. For the fourteen wikis that serve a near-empty single-page-app shell, I pulled the JavaScript bundles and extracted the string literals and template literals that hold the page prose, and cross-checked every quote used here by loading the page in a browser. Heidelberg's home page renders on a canvas with no DOM text and was read from screenshots.\n\n**The scale.** 0 — the landing claim is stated at the level the results support, or is hedged, marked as an aim, or posed as a question in the same breath. 1 — the landing claim is stronger in tense or scope than the evidence, and the results page states that specific limit plainly. 2 — the landing claim asserts a demonstrated capability that the results page does not establish and does not address, and nothing on the landing page marks it as a goal. 3 — the landing claim is contradicted by the team's own results, model or contribution page. A separate category, \"no results page\", is recorded rather than guessed; Eton-College-UK is the only team in it.\n\n**The fairness rule.** A tagline is allowed to be a project's aim rather than its result. \"We aim to\", \"our goal is\", \"our project focuses on\", \"we are developing\" and an outright question are not over-claims, and a team that writes them is not penalised however far the aim outruns the data. Neither is a how-it-works walkthrough that explains the intended mechanism in the present tense; that is design exposition, and almost every wiki in the cohort has one. What is scored is a demonstrated capability asserted in the present indicative in the hero or opening summary — the single strongest capability sentence a reader meets first. Where a score is 2 or 3, both sides are quoted verbatim in the table so a reader can check the call.\n\n**Limits.** n = 30, of which 29 are scorable and 7 are podium teams. A difference between a mean of 1.43 and a mean of 1.00 on a four-point ordinal scale, with seven teams on one side, carries no statistical weight and no causal claim whatever. The High School sub-comparison rests on two podium wikis. Scoring also depends on which sentence is taken as the top claim; on a wiki with several hero lines a different reader could pick a different one and move a team by a point. The scale is ordinal, so the means are reported as a convenience, not as a measurement. What the data can support is the negative: across these 30 wikis there is no visible relationship between claim integrity and placing, and the two teams whose landing pages are most sharply contradicted by their own evidence are both runners-up.","method_zh":"2026 年前十名的 30 支隊伍，每一支我都讀兩樣東西：讀者實際看到的首頁，以及承載頭條證據的那一頁（結果頁；若無結果頁，則是專題說明、概念驗證、工程循環或對應的濕式實驗頁）。靜態與伺服器渲染的 wiki 直接以 curl 加瀏覽器 User-Agent 抓取，HTML 在做任何樣式比對之前都先還原過實體字元。TU Delft 透過它在 `/tu-delft/<page>.md` 的 Markdown 鏡像閱讀。有十四個 wiki 送出的是幾乎空白的單頁式應用外殼，我拉下它們的 JavaScript 套件，抽出承載頁面文字的字串與樣板字面值，並把本文引用的每一句話都用瀏覽器載入頁面核對過。Heidelberg 的首頁在畫布上繪製、沒有任何 DOM 文字，是從螢幕截圖讀的。\n\n**評分尺度。** 0 分——首頁宣稱的強度與結果支持的程度相當，或在同一句裡就留了餘地、標明是目標，或乾脆寫成問句。1 分——首頁宣稱在時態或範圍上強過證據，但結果頁清楚寫明了那一項的限制。2 分——首頁以已完成的語氣斷言某項能力，而結果頁既未建立也未處理這一點，且首頁沒有任何地方把它標成目標。3 分——首頁宣稱被該隊自己的結果頁、模型頁或貢獻頁否定。另設「無結果頁」一類，據實記錄而不臆測；Eton-College-UK 是唯一一隊。\n\n**公平原則。** 標語本來就可以是專題的目標而非成果。「我們希望」「我們的目標是」「我們的專題聚焦於」「我們正在發展」，以及直接的問句，都不算誇大；這樣寫的隊伍，不論目標離數據多遠都不扣分。用現在式解釋預期機制的流程說明也不算——那是設計闡述，這批 wiki 幾乎每一個都有。真正被計分的，是在主視覺或開場摘要中以現在直述語氣斷言的、已經做到的能力，也就是讀者最先遇到的那一句最強的能力宣稱。凡是評為 2 分或 3 分的，表格中都逐字引用雙方說法，讓讀者自己核對判斷。\n\n**限制。** n = 30，其中 29 支可評分，7 支在頒獎臺上。在一個四點序位尺度上，1.43 與 1.00 兩個平均值的差距，而且其中一邊只有七支隊伍，不具任何統計份量，也完全不能支持因果主張。高中組的子比較只建立在兩個得獎網站上。評分也取決於把哪一句話當成最強宣稱；一個首頁若有好幾句主視覺文案，換一個讀者挑另一句，就可能讓某隊上下一分。尺度是序位的，所以平均值只是方便閱讀的摘要，不是量測值。這份資料能支持的是否定面：在這 30 個 wiki 裡，宣稱誠實度與名次之間看不到任何關係，而首頁被自家證據打臉得最厲害的兩支隊伍，都是亞軍或季軍。"},{"id":"dataviz","tab":"drylab","kicker":"Original analysis","kicker_zh":"原創分析","title":"How the best teams made complex data honest, not just pretty","title_zh":"最好的團隊如何讓複雜的資料變得誠實，而不只是好看","lede":"The visualisation work that stood out in 2026 was not the most beautiful. It was the work that made it impossible to misread the data.","lede_zh":"2026 年最突出的視覺化作品不是最漂亮的，而是讓資料「無法被誤讀」的那些。","body":"Almost every 2026 wiki has charts. The ones worth studying share a single instinct: **they build the reader's doubt into the picture**.\n\nThe clearest example is **GEMS-Taiwan**'s provenance colour-coding. Its dose ledger is drawn as one top-to-bottom chain, from 1.67 mL on a 10 cm plate down to US$3,800 of capital per hectare, with a rail running down the left that is green while every row still rests on a measurement and **turns amber at the rice canopy correction** — so a reader sees exactly where measurement stops and modelling begins. Every model input is tabulated with a provenance column. **TU Delft** does the same thing in a different register, labelling every cell of its decision matrix Factual, Inferred, Estimated or Speculative, with a legend stating that the tag records the evidence and not the judgement. **BOKU-Vienna** attaches a parameter-provenance table to its interactive widget. **XJTLU-China** runs an evidence-coverage track underneath its priority profiles, so a high score sitting on thin evidence cannot be mistaken for a finding.\n\nThe second instinct is **a state that refuses to be misread**. **DKU**'s safety panel resolves to four verdicts rather than three — clear, exceeded, borderline, and *not assessed* — precisely so an unmeasured gate can never be read as a passed one; 198 of its 496 constructs carry no immunogenicity measurement, and the interface says so rather than showing a zero. It goes further: because the MHC class I predictor accepts only 5-15 residue peptides and returns zero outside that window, a stored zero is explicitly not presented as evidence of low immunogenicity. **GHCIS** ships the same idea in its colour classifier, with an explicit \"unresolved, and must not be treated as Negative\" state. **UMA Malaga** conveys status by shape and text rather than colour alone.\n\nThe third is **telling the reader how to read it**. BOKU-Vienna puts an explicit \"How to read this graph\" panel beside each one. XJTLU-China numbers eighteen model figures so they read as a single argument rather than a gallery, aligning six normalised feature tracks above a composite score so you can see which feature drove a peak.\n\nThe fourth is **captions that carry the whole experiment**. **Mingdao**'s figures are plain, and that is the point — each names the instrument (a BioTek Synergy H1 plate reader; a FORA G31 glucose meter, range 20-600 mg/dL), the buffer, the temperature, the replicate count and the error measure, links its own raw CSV by filename, and where error bars are too small to see, *the caption says so* and points at the table of values.\n\nThe fifth is **showing the absences**. **DTU-Denmark**'s interactive stakeholder map colour-codes each pin by engagement status so that non-responses stay visible, and the team names the organisations that never replied. **BNDS-China** prints a caveat directly on its influence map stating that appearing on it does not mean an interview took place.\n\nAnd a note on accessibility, because the wiki analysis found that late alt-text compliance sweeps correlate with nothing. **BAID-China** shows what doing it properly looks like instead: every chart on the wiki redrawn in the eight-colour Okabe-Ito colour-blind-safe palette, chosen for luminance separation so the figures survive greyscale, with a published colour-blindness simulation verifying that elements stay distinguishable under red-green, blue-yellow and total colour-blindness. That is a design decision taken at the start, not a checkbox at the end.\n\nInteractivity, finally, earns its place only when it lets the reader change something. **UPF-Barcelona**'s RK4 solver gives every parameter a live slider that takes effect *during* the running simulation. BOKU-Vienna's trade-off widget moves a vitamin flux against growth rate with the team's own measured points overlaid. DTU-Denmark's process-flow diagram zooms from a five-route overview into the enzymatic routes with every parameter printed on the box - acid molarity, temperature, residence time, enzyme loading, number of reuses. An animation that only plays is decoration; a control that changes the answer is an argument.","body_zh":"幾乎每一個 2026 年的 wiki 都有圖表。值得研究的那些共享同一種直覺：**他們把讀者的懷疑畫進圖裡**。\n\n最清楚的例子是 **GEMS-Taiwan** 的來源色標。他們的劑量帳本畫成一條由上而下的單一鏈條，從 10 公分培養皿上的 1.67 毫升，一路到每公頃 3,800 美元的資本支出，左側有一條軌道：只要每一列仍然立基於量測，它就是綠色，而**在水稻冠層修正那一列轉為琥珀色**——讀者因此能一眼看出量測在哪裡結束、模擬從哪裡開始。每一項模型輸入都附有來源欄位。**TU Delft** 用另一種形式做同樣的事：決策矩陣的每一格都標註為 Factual、Inferred、Estimated 或 Speculative，並附圖例說明「這個標籤記錄的是證據，不是判斷」。**BOKU-Vienna** 為互動元件附上參數來源表。**XJTLU-China** 則在優先度曲線下方加一條證據覆蓋軌，讓「高分但證據稀薄」不會被誤讀成發現。\n\n第二種直覺是**一個拒絕被誤讀的狀態**。**DKU** 的安全面板有四種判定而非三種——clear、exceeded、borderline，以及 *not assessed*——正是為了讓「未量測」永遠不會被讀成「通過」；496 個構築中有 198 個沒有免疫原性量測資料，介面就直接這麼說，而不是顯示一個 0。他們還更進一步：由於 MHC class I 預測器只接受 5-15 個胺基酸的胜肽，超出範圍一律回傳 0，因此系統明確聲明「儲存的 0 不代表低免疫原性」。**GHCIS** 在顏色判讀器中實作了同樣的概念，設有明確的「無法判定，且不得視為陰性」狀態。**UMA Malaga** 則以形狀與文字、而非單靠顏色來傳達狀態。\n\n第三種是**告訴讀者該怎麼讀**。BOKU-Vienna 在每張圖旁邊放一個明確的「如何閱讀這張圖」面板。XJTLU-China 把十八張模型圖編號，使它們讀起來像一條完整論證而不是圖庫，並把六條標準化特徵軌對齊疊在綜合分數之上，讓人看得出是哪一項特徵推高了峰值。\n\n第四種是**讓圖說承載整個實驗**。**Mingdao** 的圖很樸素，而這正是重點——每張圖都標明儀器（BioTek Synergy H1 盤式判讀儀；FORA G31 血糖儀，量測範圍 20-600 mg/dL）、緩衝液、溫度、重複次數與誤差量度，並以檔名連結自己的原始 CSV；當誤差棒小到看不見時，*圖說會直接寫出來*，並指向數值表。\n\n第五種是**把「缺席」顯示出來**。**DTU-Denmark** 的互動式利害關係人地圖依接觸狀態為每個圖釘上色，讓未回覆者保持可見，團隊還點名了從未回信的機構。**BNDS-China** 則把警語直接印在影響力地圖上：出現在圖上並不代表訪談真的發生過。\n\n最後談無障礙，因為 wiki 分析發現「最後才補的替代文字」與得獎毫無相關。**BAID-China** 示範了真正做對是什麼樣子：wiki 上每一張圖都以八色 Okabe-Ito 色盲友善色票重繪，選色依據是亮度差異足以在灰階下仍可辨識，並公開了一份色盲模擬圖，驗證元素在紅綠、藍黃與全色盲模擬下仍可區分。那是一開始就做的設計決定，不是最後補打的勾。\n\n最後，互動性只有在「讓讀者能改變某個東西」時才站得住腳。**UPF-Barcelona** 的 RK4 solver 為每個參數配上即時滑桿，而且在模擬*執行中*就會生效。BOKU-Vienna 的權衡元件讓維生素通量對生長速率移動，並疊上團隊自己量到的點。DTU-Denmark 的流程圖可從五條路線的總覽放大到酵素路線，每個方塊上都印著參數——酸莫耳濃度、溫度、停留時間、酵素添加量、重複使用次數。只會播放的動畫是裝飾；能改變答案的控制項才是論證。","cards":[{"kicker":"The device worth stealing","kicker_zh":"值得借用的裝置","title":"Colour the rail where measurement stops","title_zh":"在量測終止之處替軌道換色","body":"GEMS-Taiwan draws its dose ledger as one chain from 1.67 mL on a plate to US$3,800 per hectare, with a rail down the left that is green while each row rests on a measurement and turns amber at the rice canopy correction. Anyone can see where the evidence ends. TU Delft does the same with Factual / Inferred / Estimated / Speculative tags on every cell of its decision matrix.","body_zh":"GEMS-Taiwan 把劑量帳本畫成一條鏈：從培養皿上的 1.67 毫升到每公頃 3,800 美元，左側軌道在每列仍立基於量測時保持綠色，到水稻冠層修正那一列轉為琥珀色。任何人都看得出證據在哪裡結束。TU Delft 用另一種方式做同一件事：在決策矩陣的每一格標上 Factual / Inferred / Estimated / Speculative。","chips":["provenance made visible"],"chips_zh":["讓來源看得見"]},{"kicker":"The device worth stealing","kicker_zh":"值得借用的裝置","title":"Give \"not assessed\" its own state","title_zh":"給「未評估」一個自己的狀態","body":"DKU's safety panel resolves to clear, exceeded, borderline and not assessed — four verdicts, so an unmeasured gate can never read as a passed one. 198 of its 496 constructs have no immunogenicity measurement and the interface says so instead of showing a zero. GHCIS ships the same idea as \"unresolved, and must not be treated as Negative\".","body_zh":"DKU 的安全面板有四種判定：clear、exceeded、borderline、not assessed——四種，因此「未量測」永遠不會被讀成「通過」。496 個構築中有 198 個沒有免疫原性量測，介面就直接說明，而不是顯示 0。GHCIS 以「無法判定，且不得視為陰性」實作了同樣的概念。","chips":["198 of 496 say so"],"chips_zh":["198/496 如實標示"]},{"kicker":"The device worth stealing","kicker_zh":"值得借用的裝置","title":"Put the whole experiment in the caption","title_zh":"把整個實驗寫進圖說","body":"Mingdao's figures are plain and rigorous. Each names the instrument, the buffer, the temperature, the replicate count and the error measure, and links its own raw CSV by filename. Where the error bars are too small to see, the caption says so and points at the table of values. A figure a reader can audit beats a figure a reader can admire.","body_zh":"Mingdao 的圖樸素而嚴謹。每張圖都標明儀器、緩衝液、溫度、重複次數與誤差量度，並以檔名連結自己的原始 CSV。當誤差棒小到看不見，圖說會直接寫明並指向數值表。一張讀者能稽核的圖，勝過一張讀者只能讚嘆的圖。","chips":["instrument · buffer · n · error","raw CSV linked"],"chips_zh":["儀器 · 緩衝液 · n · 誤差","附原始 CSV 連結"]},{"kicker":"The device worth stealing","kicker_zh":"值得借用的裝置","title":"Show who did not reply","title_zh":"把沒有回覆的人也畫出來","body":"DTU-Denmark colour-codes every pin on its stakeholder map by engagement status, so non-responses stay visible, and names the organisations that never answered. BNDS-China prints the caveat on its influence map that appearing there does not mean an interview happened. A map with no gaps is a map that has been tidied.","body_zh":"DTU-Denmark 依接觸狀態為利害關係人地圖上的每個圖釘上色，讓未回覆者保持可見，並點名從未回信的機構。BNDS-China 則把警語印在影響力地圖上：出現在圖上不代表訪談真的發生過。一張沒有空缺的地圖，是一張被整理過的地圖。","chips":["non-responses stay visible"],"chips_zh":["沒回覆的也看得見"]},{"kicker":"Accessibility, done early","kicker_zh":"及早處理的無障礙","title":"BAID-China redrew every chart in a colour-blind-safe palette","title_zh":"BAID-China 用色盲友善色票重繪了每一張圖","body":"The eight-colour Okabe-Ito palette, chosen for luminance separation so the figures survive greyscale, with a published colour-blindness simulation verifying that elements stay distinguishable under red-green, blue-yellow and total colour-blindness. The wiki analysis found late alt-text sweeps correlate with nothing; this is the alternative — a decision taken at the start.","body_zh":"採用八色 Okabe-Ito 色票，選色依據是亮度差異足以讓圖在灰階下仍可辨識，並公開色盲模擬圖驗證元素在紅綠、藍黃與全色盲模擬下仍可區分。wiki 分析發現最後才補的替代文字與得獎毫無相關；這就是替代方案——一個在一開始就做的決定。","chips":["Okabe-Ito","simulation published"],"chips_zh":["Okabe-Ito","附色盲模擬結果"]},{"kicker":"For GEMS","kicker_zh":"給 GEMS","title":"Interactivity only counts if the reader can change the answer","title_zh":"互動只有在讀者能改變答案時才算數","body":"UPF-Barcelona gives every parameter a live slider that takes effect during the running simulation. BOKU-Vienna moves vitamin flux against growth rate with the team's own measured points overlaid and a \"How to read this graph\" panel beside it. DTU prints every parameter on the box of a zoomable process diagram. An animation that only plays is decoration.","body_zh":"UPF-Barcelona 為每個參數配上即時滑桿，而且在模擬執行中就會生效。BOKU-Vienna 讓維生素通量對生長速率移動，疊上團隊自己量到的點，旁邊還附「如何閱讀這張圖」面板。DTU 在可縮放流程圖的每個方塊上都印出參數。只會播放的動畫是裝飾。","chips":["sliders during the run","How to read this graph"],"chips_zh":["執行中就能拉滑桿","「如何讀這張圖」"]}],"method":"Drawn from the dataviz field of every team file in this report, each researched from the team's own 2026 wiki. Interactive behaviour is as the analysts described it after opening the pages; we have not re-tested every widget here. The examples are chosen because they illustrate a transferable device, not because they are the only teams doing good work. GEMS-Taiwan is the report author's own team and appears on the same terms as the rest.","method_zh":"資料取自本報告每一份團隊檔案的 dataviz 欄位，皆來自各隊自己的 2026 wiki。互動行為依分析員實際開啟頁面後的描述記錄，我們並未在此重新測試每一個元件。所舉案例是因為它們示範了一個可移植的手法而被選出，並非表示只有這些團隊做得好。GEMS-Taiwan 是本報告作者自己的團隊，與其他隊伍適用相同標準。","order":36},{"id":"ihp-by-village","tab":"good","order":36,"kicker":"Original analysis","kicker_zh":"原創分析","title":"The experts-only pattern is not about medicine. It is about who operates the thing.","title_zh":"「只有專家」的現象與醫學無關，而與「誰在操作那個東西」有關","lede":"The obvious hypothesis — that therapeutics teams talk to clinicians because they have to, while agriculture and bioremediation teams get real knowledge from farmers and residents — does not survive the counting. Medical villages closed 6 of 21 loops with a non-expert; land, water and food villages closed 8 of 24. The gap that is real is a different one, and it is wide.","lede_zh":"最直覺的假說——治療類隊伍只能找臨床醫師，而農業與生物復育類隊伍則能從農民和居民身上得到真知識——在實際清點後站不住腳。醫學類村落在 21 個閉合迴路中有 6 個由非專家閉上；土地、水與食物類村落則是 24 個中有 8 個。真正存在的差距是另一條線，而且相當大。","body":"Across the 106 decorated teams on file, 71 closed a stakeholder-to-design loop and 16 of those 71 closed at least one with a non-expert — a farmer, beekeeper, patient, resident, frontline worker, vendor, artisan or volunteer rather than a professor, clinician, regulator, company scientist or official. Sorted by village, the medical/agricultural split the hypothesis predicted is almost flat. **Therapeutics** is 5 of 12, a higher rate than **Bioremediation** at 1 of 8. **Conservation** is 2 of 8 and **Food & Nutrition** 2 of 4. Only **Agriculture**, at 3 of 4, behaves as predicted, and four closed loops cannot carry an inference on their own. Reported honestly: the hypothesis as stated is wrong, and the earlier *ihp-depth* finding that nearly every loop is expert-closed holds inside every large village without exception.\n\nWhat the table does show is a split the hypothesis did not anticipate, and it is not close. The **platform villages** — Foundational Advance, Biomanufacturing, Space, Software & AI, Fashion & Cosmetics — closed 26 loops and 2 of them involved a non-expert. Foundational Advance is 0 of 8, Space 0 of 3, Software & AI 0 of 1, Biomanufacturing 1 of 11. The **applied villages**, medical and agricultural together, closed 45 loops with 14 non-expert among them. Where a project has no identifiable person downstream of it this year, nobody outside the lab closes a loop, and no amount of survey work substitutes: Heidelberg, Marburg, Princeton, ETH-Zurich, Vilnius, William-and-Mary and XJTLU-China are all score-4 teams whose every consequential input came from somebody with a doctorate.\n\nThe structural reason, where the files support one, is not the village but **who physically operates the thing being changed**. Compare the two villages the hypothesis treated as equivalent. An Agriculture or Conservation deployment ends in a hive, a plot or a market stall that a beekeeper, a grower or a vendor runs with their own hands, so the operator *is* the non-expert and the loop closes through them. A Bioremediation deployment ends inside a wastewater plant, a refinery or a biodiesel works, where the operator is a process engineer with a degree — ABOA's loop closed through the Turku plant's process engineer, UOttawa's through a sulfur-recovery engineer of thirty-three years, Madrid-UCM's through Bio-Oils Huelva and Repsol, Wageningen's through Vitens and Aqualab Zuid. The residents the hypothesis imagined are present in those files and they do change something, but they change communication: Madrid-UCM's Inmaculada Alonso, who had watched a reservoir eutrophy for decades, moved the team toward perceptible restoration outcomes and clearer explanation; UZurich's residents below the slopes made ecological cost something to investigate. Twelve of the 71 teams that closed a loop have a documented non-expert input of exactly that kind — real, named, and stopping short of the build. That is the same vocabulary-not-vector result the earlier analysis found, now located precisely: it happens wherever the public lives *near* the deployment instead of *running* it.\n\nThe best non-expert loops are worth naming because they are all the same shape. **Athens** states that two conditions were fixed before any construct was designed — the protein must reach the brood, and it must survive the larval gut — and says plainly that neither would have come from a literature search; beekeeper Peter Kasztelewicz's gentler practice (requeening, partial clean-out) is why delivery moved from spray to feed, and the team published what that cost. **HongKong-JSS** replaced a 14-channel colour sensor with a wavelength-resolved spectrometer because Koo's Farm and wet-market vendors wanted a number, then replaced syringe delivery with pump dosing after users complained about the force needed, measuring the result as a fall from 7.41 to 1.95 per cent coefficient of variation. **Hongwen School** got the handling cost of wet spent grain (70-80 RMB per tonne, driven by leachate, odour and liner) from Master He, a municipal landfill worker of six years, and turned localised processing from a preference into a hard constraint; separately Mr Shen of a Chongming ecological farm said 'I never look at the price per ton — I look at the cost per kilogram of gain', and the feed route became a standardised premix judged on feed conversion ratio. **LYON** removed every living cell from its filter because the public objected, and ruled households out as customers entirely. **QingdaoAcademy** put ultrafiltration desalting and endotoxin limits into its plan because a beauty-salon manager said she would hesitate to trust Qingdao Ulva. **TAU-Israel** is the medical exception that proves the rule: Shir Parchef's eighteen-year wait for an endometriosis diagnosis and Netta Ben Moshe's being told that incapacitating pain was ordinary cramps set the goal as eliminating pathology without systemic hormonal ablation — patients setting a constraint on the mechanism, not on the wording.\n\nTwo cautions against over-reading. First, the non-expert loops cluster not only by operator role but by **what kind of change they produce**: of the 16, ten changed something physical — a sensor, a delivery route, a formulation, a containment architecture — and six changed only deployment scope, target user or a selection criterion. Oxford is in the second group: about twenty chemical-free hobbyists of the Oxfordshire Natural Beekeeping Group argued against the entire premise, and Oxford's response was to narrow the target user to commercial operations and write that they had changed 'not the molecular mechanism of NECTAR, but the problem we believed NECTAR should — and should not — try to solve'. That is honest and it is real, but it is not the same act as changing a part. Second, legibility may be doing some of the work the villages appear to do: a judge can verify that a professor said something, and several teams that did consult non-experts recorded the result as an honest null. **IISER-Kolkata** asked Mr Mohadep Dutta, who has fished the Ganga since he was seven, about a shift in fish sex ratio, and published that he could not see one — evidence the effect needs instrumentation, rather than a loop. **Stanford University**, Grand Prize winner in Therapeutics, looked for keloid patient groups, found almost none, was told by the one that replied to talk to clinicians instead, and states outright that physicians cannot stand in for lived experience. Those two entries are better practice than most of the surveys in the cohort and they close nothing.\n\nFor an agriculture-adjacent team the operational reading is narrow and uncomfortable. The teams worth copying are not the Best IHP winners as a class — **TU Delft**, **UCAS-China** and **GEMS-Taiwan** all won and all had their architecture set by credentialled experts. **GEMS-Taiwan** should be held to its own standard here: sensing moving out of the cell, the hollow-fibre perfusion reactor, the abandonment of proline delivery, the narrowing to heat and salinity, the WB800 strain and the shift from continuous to periodic operation were closed by Prof. Chen Wen-Liang, Dr. Paul Verslues, Dr. Elizabeth Sattely, Prof. Huang Chieh-Chen and CH Biotech. The only non-expert input that reached the design was the natural-farming forum of 5 September, whose argument that a crop protected from every stress never builds tolerance became the specification for the release threshold, and a farmer's question about organic certification, which bounded the market rather than the machine. **Muenster-University**, nominated for Best Agriculture, reached farmers through the WLV agricultural association and changed its education strategy. That is the default outcome for an agriculture team that talks to farmers, and avoiding it takes a deliberate act: put the device in the hand of the person who will hold it, and ask for a number.","body_zh":"在檔案中的 106 支受獎隊伍裡，有 71 支閉合了一條從利害關係人到設計的迴路，而這 71 支中有 16 支至少有一條迴路是由非專家閉上的——農民、養蜂人、病人、居民、第一線工人、攤商、工匠或志工，而不是教授、臨床醫師、主管機關人員、企業科學家或官員。依村落分類之後，假說預測的「醫學 vs 農業」分界幾乎是平的。**Therapeutics** 是 12 中有 5，比例反而高於 **Bioremediation** 的 8 中有 1。**Conservation** 是 8 中有 2，**Food & Nutrition** 是 4 中有 2。只有 **Agriculture** 的 4 中有 3 符合預測，而四條閉合迴路本身撐不起任何推論。誠實地說：這個假說如其所述是錯的，而先前 *ihp-depth* 所說「幾乎每一條迴路都由專家閉上」的結論，在每一個樣本量夠大的村落裡都毫無例外地成立。\n\n這張表真正顯示的，是假說沒有預期到的另一條分界，而且差距不小。**平台型村落**——Foundational Advance、Biomanufacturing、Space、Software & AI、Fashion & Cosmetics——共閉合 26 條迴路，其中只有 2 條牽涉非專家。Foundational Advance 是 8 中有 0，Space 3 中有 0，Software & AI 1 中有 0，Biomanufacturing 11 中有 1。**應用型村落**（醫學與農業合計）閉合了 45 條迴路，其中 14 條有非專家參與。當一個專案在今年還沒有可指認的下游使用者時，實驗室外就沒有人會閉上迴路，而再多的問卷也替代不了：Heidelberg、Marburg、Princeton、ETH-Zurich、Vilnius、William-and-Mary 與 XJTLU-China 全是 4 分隊伍，而他們每一項有後果的輸入都來自擁有博士學位的人。\n\n在檔案支持得了結論的範圍內，結構性原因不是村落，而是**誰用手在操作那個被改動的東西**。拿假說視為同類的兩個村落來比。Agriculture 或 Conservation 的部署最後落在一個蜂箱、一塊田或一個市場攤位上，由養蜂人、農友或攤商親手操作，因此操作者本身*就是*那位非專家，迴路也就經由他們閉合。Bioremediation 的部署則落在污水處理廠、煉油廠或生質柴油廠內部，操作者是有學位的製程工程師——ABOA 的迴路經由 Turku 廠的製程工程師閉合，UOttawa 經由一位有 33 年資歷的硫回收工程師，Madrid-UCM 經由 Bio-Oils Huelva 與 Repsol，Wageningen 經由 Vitens 與 Aqualab Zuid。假說想像的那些居民確實出現在這些檔案裡，也確實改變了某些東西，但他們改變的是溝通：Madrid-UCM 的 Inmaculada Alonso 看著一座水庫優養化數十年，她讓隊伍轉向「看得見的復原成果」與更清楚的說明；UZurich 坡下的居民讓生態代價從預設變成待查事項。在 71 支閉合迴路的隊伍中，有 12 支記錄了正是這一類的非專家輸入——真實、具名，而且止步於設計之前。這就是先前分析所說的「改變用詞、不改變方向」，如今可以被精確定位：它發生在公眾住在部署地*附近*、而不是*操作*它的時候。\n\n最好的那幾條非專家迴路值得點名，因為它們形狀相同。**Athens** 寫明有兩項條件在任何構築設計之前就已固定——蛋白質必須抵達幼蟲巢房，而且必須在幼蟲腸道中存活——並直言這兩點都不會從文獻檢索中得出；養蜂人 Peter Kasztelewicz 較溫和的作法（換王、局部清巢）正是投遞方式從噴灑改為飼餵的原因，而隊伍也公開寫出了這個選擇的代價。**HongKong-JSS** 把 14 通道的顏色感測器換成波長解析的光譜儀，因為 Koo's Farm 與傳統市場攤商要的是一個數字；接著在使用者抱怨推針太費力之後，把針筒加樣改為泵驅動定量加樣，並以變異係數從 7.41% 降到 1.95% 來量測成果。**Hongwen School** 從有六年資歷的市政掩埋場工人 Master He 那裡得到濕啤酒糟的處理成本（每公噸 70-80 人民幣，由滲出水、異味與底層襯墊驅動），並把在地化處理從商業偏好升格為硬性限制；另外，崇明一家生態農場的 Mr Shen 說「我從來不看每噸的價格，我看的是每公斤增重的成本」，於是飼料路線變成一包可直接倒進既有攪拌機的標準化預混料，並以飼料換肉率作為評判標準。**LYON** 因為公眾反對，把濾材裡所有活細胞全部移除，並徹底排除家戶作為客戶。**QingdaoAcademy** 把超濾脫鹽與內毒素上限寫進計畫，因為一位美容沙龍經理說她不敢信任青島的石蓴原料。**TAU-Israel** 則是醫學類中那個反證：Shir Parchef 為子宮內膜異位症的診斷等了 18 年，Netta Ben Moshe 被告知劇烈疼痛只是普通經痛——這些讓隊伍把目標設定為「消除病灶而非掩蓋症狀，且不進行全身性荷爾蒙抑制」。這是病人替機制設下限制，而不是替用詞設下限制。\n\n有兩點要提防過度解讀。第一，這些非專家迴路不只依操作者角色分群，也依**它們造成什麼樣的改變**分群：16 條之中，有 10 條改了某個實體的東西——一顆感測器、一條投遞路徑、一種劑型、一套圍堵架構——另外 6 條只改了部署範圍、目標使用者或選擇判準。Oxford 屬於第二群：Oxfordshire Natural Beekeeping Group 約二十位不用藥的業餘養蜂人，反對的是整個前提；Oxford 的回應是把目標使用者收窄到商業蜂場，並寫下他們改變的「不是 NECTAR 的分子機制，而是我們認為 NECTAR 應該、以及不應該去解決的問題」。這很誠實、也很真實，但它和改掉一個元件並不是同一件事。第二，「可被辨識」這件事，可能正在做一部分看起來像是村落在做的工：評審可以查證一位教授說過什麼，而好幾支確實諮詢過非專家的隊伍，把結果記成了一個誠實的空值。**IISER-Kolkata** 問過七歲起就在恆河捕魚的 Mr Mohadep Dutta 有沒有看到魚類性別比例的變化，並公開記下他看不出來這件事——那是「此效應需要儀器才看得見」的證據，而不是一條迴路。**Stanford University** 身為 Therapeutics 的大獎得主，去找蟹足腫病友團體，幾乎找不到，唯一回覆的基金會叫他們去找臨床醫師，而隊伍直白寫下醫師無法代替親身經驗。這兩筆記錄比全體隊伍中大多數的問卷都更接近好的做法，而它們什麼迴路也沒閉上。\n\n對一支與農業相關的隊伍而言，可操作的結論既狹窄又不舒服。值得複製的不是「最佳整合式人類實踐得獎者」這個類別——**TU Delft**、**UCAS-China** 與 **GEMS-Taiwan** 都得了獎，而三者的架構都由有專業資歷的專家定下。**GEMS-Taiwan** 在這裡應當用同一把尺來量：感測移出細胞之外、中空纖維灌流生物反應器、放棄脯胺酸投遞、把植物測試收窄到高溫與鹽分、WB800 菌株，以及反應器從連續改為週期操作，分別是由 Chen Wen-Liang 教授、Dr. Paul Verslues、Dr. Elizabeth Sattely、Huang Chieh-Chen 教授與 CH Biotech 閉上的。唯一真正進到設計裡的非專家輸入，是 9 月 5 日的自然農法公開論壇——「一株被保護到完全沒有逆境的作物永遠不會建立耐受性」成了釋放閾值的規格依據——以及一位農民關於有機驗證的提問，而那限定的是市場，不是機器。**Muenster-University** 入圍最佳農業專案，透過 WLV 農業協會接觸到農民，然後改了教育策略。對一支去找農民談話的農業隊伍來說，那就是預設結果；要避開它需要一個刻意的動作：把裝置放進那個將要握著它的人手裡，然後向他要一個數字。","cards":[{"kicker":"The result","kicker_zh":"結果","title":"A negative result, stated plainly","title_zh":"一個直說的否定結果","body":"The hypothesis was that the experts-only pattern is worst where the stakes are most medical and best where non-specialists hold decisive practical knowledge. It does not hold. Medical villages (Therapeutics, Diagnostics, Oncology, Infectious Diseases) closed 21 loops with 6 non-expert among them, 29 per cent. Land, water and food villages (Agriculture, Bioremediation, Conservation, Food & Nutrition) closed 24 loops with 8 non-expert, 33 per cent. Four percentage points is not a pattern. Bioremediation, the village singled out for residents near contaminated sites, is the weakest applied village at 1 of 8.","body_zh":"原本的假說是：「只有專家」的現象在醫學風險最高處最嚴重，在非專家握有決定性實務知識之處最輕。這不成立。醫學類村落（Therapeutics、Diagnostics、Oncology、Infectious Diseases）閉合 21 條迴路，其中 6 條由非專家閉上，佔 29%。土地、水與食物類村落（Agriculture、Bioremediation、Conservation、Food & Nutrition）閉合 24 條，其中 8 條，佔 33%。四個百分點不構成一種型態。而被特別點名「污染場址附近居民」的 Bioremediation，反而是應用型村落中最弱的一個：8 中有 1。","chips":["106 teams","71 closed a loop","16 with a non-expert","Hypothesis fails"],"chips_zh":["106 支隊伍","71 支閉合迴圈","16 支有非專家","假設不成立"]},{"kicker":"The split that is real","kicker_zh":"真正存在的分界","title":"Platform villages have nobody downstream","title_zh":"平台型村落的下游沒有人","body":"Foundational Advance 0 of 8, Space 0 of 3, Software & AI 0 of 1, Biomanufacturing 1 of 11, Fashion & Cosmetics 1 of 3. The five platform villages between them closed 26 loops and 2 involved a non-expert, against 14 of 45 across the applied villages. This is not a failure of effort - Heidelberg, Marburg, Princeton and ETH-Zurich ran some of the most traceable chains in the cohort. It is that a tool with no named user this year has no lay stakeholder to be wrong in front of. For a team whose project is a platform, the honest move is Uni-Padua-IT's: take the hardware manual to an instrumentation professor and weaken your own claim.","body_zh":"Foundational Advance 8 中 0、Space 3 中 0、Software & AI 1 中 0、Biomanufacturing 11 中 1、Fashion & Cosmetics 3 中 1。五個平台型村落合計閉合 26 條迴路，只有 2 條牽涉非專家；應用型村落則是 45 條中有 14 條。這不是努力不足——Heidelberg、Marburg、Princeton 與 ETH-Zurich 跑出了全體中最可追溯的幾條鏈。原因是：一個今年還沒有具名使用者的工具，也就沒有一位外行的利害關係人可以在他面前出錯。對專案本身就是平台的隊伍而言，誠實的做法是 Uni-Padua-IT 的做法：把硬體手冊拿去給儀器專業的教授看，然後把自己的主張講弱一點。","chips":["Platform: 2 of 26","Applied: 14 of 45","Not an effort gap"],"chips_zh":["平台型：2/26","應用型：14/45","不是努力的差距"]},{"kicker":"Worked example","kicker_zh":"實例","title":"Two conditions, fixed before any construct was designed","title_zh":"兩項條件，在任何構築設計之前就已固定","body":"Athens writes that the requirements for ApiconIASIS came from beekeeping, not from the team: the protein must reach the brood, and it must survive the larval gut. Neither, they say, would have been prioritised from a literature search, and both now define what counts as success. Beekeeper Peter Kasztelewicz, whose own hive footage is on the wiki, worked by requeening and partial clean-out, and that practice is why delivery moved from spray to feed - the adjuvant surfactants harm bees, and separately the person holding the sprayer inhales it, so protective equipment went into the protocols and not into the product. They then chose a purified non-replicating enzyme over a live phage knowing it is weaker and more expensive.","body_zh":"Athens 寫道，ApiconIASIS 的需求來自養蜂實務，而不是來自隊伍本身：蛋白質必須抵達幼蟲巢房，而且必須在幼蟲腸道中存活。他們說這兩點都不會在文獻檢索中被列為優先，而現在它們定義了什麼叫做成功。養蜂人 Peter Kasztelewicz 的蜂箱影像就放在 wiki 上，他採用換王與局部清巢的作法，而正是這套實務讓投遞方式從噴灑改成飼餵——佐劑中的界面活性劑會傷害蜜蜂，而另一個獨立的風險是拿噴霧器的人會吸入它，所以防護裝備被寫進操作流程、而不是寫進產品。他們接著明知較弱也較貴，仍選擇純化的非複製型酵素而非活噬菌體。","chips":["Athens","Conservation","Beekeeper set success","Spray to feed"],"chips_zh":["Athens","保育","養蜂人定義成功","從噴灑改成餵食"]},{"kicker":"Worked example","kicker_zh":"實例","title":"The man who knew what a tonne actually costs","title_zh":"知道一公噸真正成本的那個人","body":"Hongwen School's register of changes is specific, attributed and sometimes negative. Master He, a municipal landfill worker of six years, gave them 60-90 tonnes a month at nearly 80 per cent moisture and handling costs of 70-80 RMB per tonne driven by leachate, odour, liner and labour, persisting not from indifference but from absent local off-takers. The team deleted both of its extreme narratives, fixed 70-80 RMB per tonne as a local baseline, and upgraded localised processing from a business preference to a hard environmental constraint, because a route relying on high-energy drying or long-haul transport would eat its own gains. Separately Mr Shen of a Chongming ecological farm reframed the unit of account - cost per kilogram of gain, not price per tonne - and the feed route became a standardised premix pourable into an existing mixer, judged on feed conversion ratio, diarrhoea rate and mortality.","body_zh":"Hongwen School 的改變清單具體、具名，有時還是負面的。市政掩埋場工人 Master He 有六年資歷，他給出的數字是每月 60-90 公噸、含水率將近 80%，處理成本每公噸 70-80 人民幣，由滲出水、異味、底層襯墊與人力構成；而這個問題持續存在不是因為大家不在乎，而是因為在地沒有接手者。隊伍刪掉了自己兩套極端敘事，把每公噸 70-80 人民幣定為在地基準，並把在地化處理從商業偏好升格為硬性環境限制——因為依賴高耗能乾燥或長程運輸的路線會把自己的效益吃光。另外，崇明一家生態農場的 Mr Shen 重新定義了計價單位：不是每公噸的價格，而是每公斤增重的成本；於是飼料路線變成可直接倒進既有攪拌機的標準化預混料，並以飼料換肉率、腹瀉率與死亡率來評判。","chips":["Hongwen School","Food & Nutrition","Landfill worker","Farm owner"],"chips_zh":["Hongwen School","食品與營養","掩埋場工人","農場主人"]},{"kicker":"Held to the same standard","kicker_zh":"用同一把尺來量","title":"GEMS-Taiwan's architecture was closed by professors","title_zh":"GEMS-Taiwan 的架構是由教授閉上的","body":"GEMS-Taiwan won Best Integrated Human Practices in the high-school section on an agricultural project, and on this measure it sits with the majority rather than the exceptions. Sensing moving out of the cell and the hollow-fibre perfusion reactor came from Prof. Chen Wen-Liang on 10 April; abandoning proline delivery from Dr. Paul Verslues; narrowing to heat and salinity from Dr. Elizabeth Sattely; the WB800 strain and periodic rather than continuous operation from Prof. Huang Chieh-Chen; the costing and regulatory work from CH Biotech. The one non-expert input that reached the design is the natural-farming forum of 5 September, where the argument that a crop protected from every stress never builds tolerance became the specification for the release threshold, and a farmer's question about organic certification that bounded the market rather than the machine. The Ghanaian farmers who supplied the origin question have no documented design consequence.","body_zh":"GEMS-Taiwan 以一個農業專案拿下高中組 Best Integrated Human Practices，而在這個指標上，它站在多數那一邊，不是例外那一邊。感測移出細胞之外與中空纖維灌流生物反應器來自 4 月 10 日的 Chen Wen-Liang 教授；放棄脯胺酸投遞來自 Dr. Paul Verslues；把範圍收窄到高溫與鹽分來自 Dr. Elizabeth Sattely；WB800 菌株與反應器改為週期操作來自 Huang Chieh-Chen 教授；成本與法規工作來自 CH Biotech。唯一進到設計裡的非專家輸入，是 9 月 5 日的自然農法論壇——「一株被保護到完全沒有逆境的作物永遠不會建立耐受性」成了釋放閾值的規格依據——以及一位農民關於有機驗證的提問，而那限定的是市場、不是機器。至於提供了最初問題的迦納農民，檔案中沒有記錄任何設計後果。","chips":["GEMS-Taiwan","Agriculture","Best IHP winner","1 non-expert loop"],"chips_zh":["GEMS-Taiwan","農業","Best IHP 得主","1 個非專家迴圈"]}],"table":{"head":["Village","Decorated teams","Closed a loop","Closed it with a non-expert"],"head_zh":["村落","受獎隊伍數","閉合了迴路","由非專家閉上"],"rows":[["Therapeutics","16","12 of 16","5 of 12"],["Biomanufacturing","13","11 of 13","1 of 11"],["Bioremediation","13","8 of 13","1 of 8"],["Foundational Advance","13","8 of 13","0 of 8"],["Diagnostics","11","7 of 11","1 of 7"],["Conservation","9","8 of 9","2 of 8"],["Food & Nutrition","8","4 of 8","2 of 4 - cell too small"],["Fashion & Cosmetics","7","3 of 7","1 of 3 - cell too small"],["Agriculture","5","4 of 5","3 of 4 - cell too small"],["Space","4","3 of 4","0 of 3 - cell too small"],["Software & AI","3","1 of 3","0 of 1 - cell too small"],["Infectious Diseases","2","1 of 2","0 of 1 - cell too small"],["Oncology","2","1 of 2","0 of 1 - cell too small"],["Medical villages combined","31","21 of 31","6 of 21"],["Land, water and food combined","35","24 of 35","8 of 24"],["Platform villages combined","40","26 of 40","2 of 26"],["All villages","106","71 of 106","16 of 71"]],"rows_zh":[["治療 Therapeutics","16","16 中有 12","12 中有 5"],["生物製造 Biomanufacturing","13","13 中有 11","11 中有 1"],["生物復育 Bioremediation","13","13 中有 8","8 中有 1"],["基礎推進 Foundational Advance","13","13 中有 8","8 中有 0"],["診斷 Diagnostics","11","11 中有 7","7 中有 1"],["保育 Conservation","9","9 中有 8","8 中有 2"],["食品與營養 Food & Nutrition","8","8 中有 4","4 中有 2－樣本過小"],["時尚與美妝 Fashion & Cosmetics","7","7 中有 3","3 中有 1－樣本過小"],["農業 Agriculture","5","5 中有 4","4 中有 3－樣本過小"],["太空 Space","4","4 中有 3","3 中有 0－樣本過小"],["軟體與 AI Software & AI","3","3 中有 1","1 中有 0－樣本過小"],["傳染病 Infectious Diseases","2","2 中有 1","1 中有 0－樣本過小"],["腫瘤 Oncology","2","2 中有 1","1 中有 0－樣本過小"],["醫學類村落合計","31","31 中有 21","21 中有 6"],["土地、水與食物類合計","35","35 中有 24","24 中有 8"],["平台型村落合計","40","40 中有 26","26 中有 2"],["全部村落","106","106 中有 71","71 中有 16"]]},"checklist":["Ask who will physically hold the device or run the process on the day it is used. If that person has a degree in your field, your non-expert loop will not happen by accident.","Make the non-expert ask for a number. HongKong-JSS's sensor swap and Hongwen School's 70-80 RMB per tonne both started as a quantity somebody named out loud.","Fix one or two success conditions from practice before the construct is designed, as Athens did, and write down that they did not come from the literature.","Recruit the people who disagree with the premise. Oxford's twenty chemical-free hobbyists narrowed the target user; GEMS-Taiwan's natural-farming forum set the release threshold.","Record non-expert input that changed nothing, and say so. IISER-Kolkata published a fisher who could not see the effect; Stanford published that it could not find patients. Both are better than a survey that only changed a word.","Check the type of change before claiming a loop: a part number, a concentration, a format, a delivery route or who may buy it counts. A changed word, a new leaflet or a reframed slogan does not."],"checklist_zh":["問清楚：產品真正被使用的那一天，是誰用手拿著裝置、或是誰在操作那套製程。如果那個人在你的領域裡有學位，你的非專家迴路就不會自己發生。","讓非專家開口要一個數字。HongKong-JSS 換感測器、Hongwen School 的每公噸 70-80 人民幣，都是從某個人說出口的量值開始的。","在構築設計之前，就從實務裡定下一到兩項成功條件，像 Athens 那樣，並寫明這些條件不是從文獻來的。","去找那些不同意前提的人。Oxford 那二十位不用藥的業餘養蜂人收窄了目標使用者；GEMS-Taiwan 的自然農法論壇定下了釋放閾值。","把沒有造成任何改變的非專家輸入也記下來，並直說。IISER-Kolkata 公開記下一位看不出效應的漁民；Stanford 公開寫下他們找不到病友。兩者都比一份只改了一個用詞的問卷更好。","宣稱閉合迴路之前，先檢查改變的類型：元件型號、濃度、劑型、投遞路徑，或誰可以購買，這些算數。改掉一個用詞、做一張新傳單、換一句標語，不算。"],"method":"Population: all 106 team files on disk, every one of them a Top 10 or special-prize winner or nominee, so this is the most decorated tenth of iGEM 2026 and not a sample of the competition. Loop scores: the 93 teams scored in the earlier ihp-depth analysis keep that analysis's score unchanged, and 'closed a loop' means its score of 4 - a named stakeholder, a specific thing said, and a change to the build, deployment, readout, safety design or business model. Thirteen files landed after that scoring ran (BASIS-China, BGI-College, Bist-China, Michigan, NCKU-Tainan, NU Boston, Squirrel-Beijing, TU Darmstadt, Tsinghua-T, UBC-Vancouver, UiOslo-Norway, WHU-China, XJTLU-Software); I scored those thirteen myself on the same rubric and seven reached 4, so 71 of 106 against the earlier 64 of 93. Non-expert rule, written before classifying: a person counts as a NON-EXPERT when their standing in the exchange rests on lived experience or hands-on practice rather than on a credential, a research post, a regulatory office or a technical role in a company - farmers, growers, fishers, beekeepers, residents, patients and their families, carers, frontline manual workers, market vendors, shop and salon staff, artisans, consumers, students, volunteers, indigenous community members. EXPERT covers professors and researchers, physicians, dentists, nurses and medical technologists, regulators and officials, company scientists, engineers, technical directors, QA and regulatory-affairs staff, investors and corporate managers, lawyers, ethicists and social scientists, peer iGEM teams and alumni. The hard case the brief names - a farmer with a degree - I resolved toward NON-EXPERT when the person speaks about running their own operation, and toward EXPERT when they are employed to advise other people's operations. Mr Lu of Worldshaper-Shanghai, described as a grower and extension author, is counted non-expert on that rule and is the clearest instance of it; Yusong Shi of GYHS, a doctoral student who is also a stony-coral hobbyist, is counted expert on the same rule, and GYHS's Conservation cell would move if that call reversed. A team counts in the last column if at least one documented loop was closed by a non-expert; ten of the sixteen changed something physical (sensor, delivery route, formulation, containment architecture) and six changed deployment scope, target user or a selection criterion. Twelve further teams have a documented non-expert input that changed only claims, language, education material or success framing, and those are counted as expert-closed, which is the same line the earlier analysis drew. Counting only physical changes gives nine or ten rather than the earlier analysis's 'six or seven in 93'; the difference is thirteen extra files plus formulation and delivery-route changes I counted and it did not, and this is the one place the two analyses differ. Villages: 50 of the 106 files carry no village string, and the high-school section does not have fine-grained villages at all - it competes in four merged clusters, so GEMS-Taiwan's agricultural project sat in the Space / Foundational Advance / Software & AI / Biomanufacturing cluster. I therefore assigned every team to one of the thirteen collegiate villages by where the technology is deployed and who it affects, using the official label from results2026.json where one exists. Several assignments are genuinely arguable - Cornell's smart bandage sits in Fashion & Cosmetics because that is the village it won, QingdaoAcademy and MIT-MAHE could be read as Food rather than Biomanufacturing, Mingdao and TU Darmstadt as Bioremediation rather than Biomanufacturing - and a different reading would move single teams between rows without changing the platform-versus-applied result. What this cannot see: whether a change was made because of the advice or attributed to it afterwards; the wiki behind the file summary, except for Athens and HUST-China, whose pages I read directly to check two borderline calls; whether a loop recorded as expert-closed had an unrecorded non-expert behind it; and whether judges preferred credentialled stakeholders, which is a plausible alternative explanation for the platform-village result that these files cannot settle. Nine of the thirteen village cells have fewer than eight closed loops and are flagged in the table; Agriculture at 3 of 4 is the single most quotable cell and the least load-bearing.","method_zh":"母體：磁碟上全部 106 份隊伍檔案，每一支都是 Top 10 或特別獎的得主或入圍者，因此這是 iGEM 2026 中受獎最多的十分之一，而不是整個競賽的抽樣。迴路評分：先前 ihp-depth 分析已評分的 93 支隊伍沿用該分析的分數不變，而「閉合了迴路」即該分析的 4 分——具名的利害關係人、一句具體說了什麼，以及建構、部署、讀出、安全設計或商業模式上的一項改變。有 13 份檔案是在那次評分之後才到的（BASIS-China、BGI-College、Bist-China、Michigan、NCKU-Tainan、NU Boston、Squirrel-Beijing、TU Darmstadt、Tsinghua-T、UBC-Vancouver、UiOslo-Norway、WHU-China、XJTLU-Software）；這 13 支由我以同一套評分標準自行評分，其中 7 支達到 4 分，因此是 106 中的 71，對應先前的 93 中的 64。非專家判準，在開始分類之前就先寫下：當一個人在這場對話中的立足點來自親身經驗或動手實務，而不是來自資歷、研究職位、主管機關職務或公司裡的技術角色時，即計為**非專家**——農民、種植者、漁民、養蜂人、居民、病人與家屬、照顧者、第一線體力工作者、市場攤商、店員與沙龍人員、工匠、消費者、學生、志工、原住民社群成員。**專家**則涵蓋教授與研究人員、醫師、牙醫、護理師與醫檢師、主管機關人員與官員、企業科學家、工程師、技術總監、品保與法規事務人員、投資人與企業經理人、律師、倫理學者與社會科學家，以及同儕 iGEM 隊伍與校友。委託說明特別點名的難題——有學位的農民——我的處理方式是：當這個人談的是經營自己的場域時計為非專家，當他受雇去指導別人的場域時計為專家。Worldshaper-Shanghai 的 Mr Lu 被描述為「種植者兼推廣作者」，依此規則計為非專家，也是這條規則最清楚的一個案例；GYHS 的 Yusong Shi 是博士生同時也是硬珊瑚玩家，依同一規則計為專家，而若這個判斷反過來，GYHS 所在的 Conservation 欄位數字就會變動。只要有至少一條記載在案的迴路由非專家閉上，該隊伍就計入最後一欄；16 支之中有 10 支改了實體的東西（感測器、投遞路徑、劑型、圍堵架構），另外 6 支改的是部署範圍、目標使用者或選擇判準。另有 12 支隊伍有記載在案的非專家輸入，但只改了主張、用詞、教育素材或成功的框架，這些仍計為由專家閉合，和先前分析劃的是同一條線。若只計實體改變，得到的是 9 到 10 支，而非先前分析所說的「93 中的六或七支」；差異來自多出的 13 份檔案，加上我把劑型與投遞路徑的改變也計入而該分析沒有——這是兩份分析唯一相異之處。村落：106 份檔案中有 50 份沒有村落欄位字串，而高中組根本沒有細分村落，它們是在四個合併的集群中競賽，所以 GEMS-Taiwan 的農業專案被放在 Space / Foundational Advance / Software & AI / Biomanufacturing 這個集群裡。因此我依「技術部署在哪裡、影響到誰」，把每一支隊伍指派到十三個大專組村落之一，有官方標籤者（來自 results2026.json）即採用官方標籤。有幾個指派確實可以爭論——Cornell 的智慧敷料放在 Fashion & Cosmetics，是因為那是它得獎的村落；QingdaoAcademy 與 MIT-MAHE 也可讀成 Food 而非 Biomanufacturing；Mingdao 與 TU Darmstadt 可讀成 Bioremediation 而非 Biomanufacturing——不同讀法會讓個別隊伍在列與列之間移動，但不會改變「平台型 vs 應用型」這個結果。這份分析看不到的：一項改變究竟是因為那個建議而做，還是事後才歸因於它；檔案摘要背後的 wiki，除了 Athens 與 HUST-China 這兩個邊界案例的頁面我直接讀過以外；一條被記為由專家閉合的迴路背後，是否有未被記錄的非專家；以及評審是否偏好有資歷的利害關係人——這是平台型村落結果的一個合理替代解釋，而這些檔案無法裁決。十三個村落欄位中有九個的閉合迴路少於八條，已在表中標示；Agriculture 的 4 中有 3 是最好引用、也最撐不住重量的一格。"},{"id":"parts-census","tab":"teams","order":36,"kicker":"Original analysis","kicker_zh":"原創分析","title":"What makes a part worth other people's time","title_zh":"什麼樣的元件值得別人花時間","lede":"A census of the four 2026 parts awards. Taiwan took six awards from thirteen teams and not one parts nomination — so we read the registry pages themselves. The winning parts are not the clever ones. They are the ones carrying a datasheet.","lede_zh":"針對 2026 年四項元件獎的普查。台灣十三支隊伍拿下六個獎項，卻沒有任何一項元件類提名——所以我們直接去讀 registry 頁面本身。得獎的元件不是最聰明的那些，而是附了一份規格表（datasheet）的那些。","body":"Four awards, eleven winners across the three sections, and one thing separates them from the forty-odd nominees: **what is actually on the registry page**. The 2026 registry (now at registry.igem.org, with every part reachable as a server-rendered page and a public read API) gives each part a Design, Experiment, Characterisation, Application and Discussion slot. The winners fill them. We measured the characters of documentation on each part page we could resolve. The winners' headline parts carry between **10,000 and 83,000 characters** across three to six documents. The nominee parts we sampled carry **440 to 2,500 characters**, usually a single Design note — and several carry nothing at all.\n\nThe empty pages are the real finding, because they belong to *nominated* teams. QingdaoAcademy's ulvan lyases (BBa_26QJCNH8, BBa_26ZVH9D0, BBa_265B8WZF) were nominated for Best New Basic Part at high-school level and each page has **zero documentation**: a title, a sequence, nothing else. HKU-HongKong's aTi-14 peptide (BBa_265GWS2B, 45 bp) was a Best New Composite Part nominee with zero documentation. Bist-China registered PdhR (BBa_26OKC42U) and LldR (BBa_26S2KNZ1) with no documentation at all, and put the real material on two near-duplicate variant pages instead. Nomination is cheap. A page is not.\n\n**Novelty loses to documentation, decisively.** The high-school Best New Basic Part winner, HKSSC, won with BBa_262HI0IB — a *247 bp native promoter and RBS lifted straight out of GenBank AY077721.1*. Nothing about the sequence is new. What is new is that nobody had ever registered or characterised it: the team said so, predicted the promoter with BPROM (LDF 5.30, −10 box TATAAT at position 163, −35 box TTGAAA at 142), cloned it into the promoterless distribution-kit vector BBa_J435300, and reported the gels, the band sizes (974 bp insert, 2,680 bp vector) and the NanoDrop triplicates. The GFP read-out lives on the composite BBa_26MSEOFB, linked from the basic part. That is an entire award won on a promoter trap, a free web tool and honest bookkeeping. It is the single most copyable result in the whole census.\n\nThe best datasheet in the cohort is TU Darmstadt's GeoEsterase (BBa_269NN9UX, Best New Basic Part, Overgrad): activity on *p*-nitrophenyl hexanoate read at 396 nm with the extinction coefficient stated (ε = 18,100 M⁻¹cm⁻¹), 0.5 µM enzyme against 0.5/1/2/4 mM substrate, at 22, 32, 37, 42 and 47 °C, **every value the mean of a triplicate**, Michaelis-Menten fitted by least squares, and a table of V_max, K_M, k_cat and k_cat/K_M (894 M⁻¹s⁻¹ at 42 °C in buffer). It also reports that the engineered ThermoGeoEsterase *underperformed* the parent at every temperature and that the thermal shift assay found no improvement — and says the plate reader could not exceed 47 °C. Winners write down what did not work, in units.\n\nDoes the evidence live in the registry or link back to a wiki that will rot? **In the registry.** Across seven winning parts we counted the image hosts: 4 to 21 figures per part, every one served from registry.igem.wiki/documentation — the registry's own asset store, not the team site. Only TU Darmstadt and WHU-China link out to 2026.igem.wiki at all, and then as cross-references for extra detail, not as the place the data lives. The same holds for Best Part Collection: all three winners carry collection-level documentation (GHCIS 25,665 characters, Heidelberg 76,231, GU Frankfurt 111,681), while **eight of the twelve nominated collections have no collection page text whatsoever** — ETH-Zurich, Bonn, UTDallas, Marburg aside, Tsinglan, HFI, ASIJ-Tokyo, YHA-HWFLA and UCS-A simply list parts. A bag of parts with a title is not a collection.\n\nOne hypothesis fails. **Nothing in the 2026 registry shows a winning part being reused by another team.** Every non-zero *Used in* count on a 2026 winner points back at that team's own composites: Neo-IL-2 (BBa_26WNS0EJ) feeds BBa_26V37TWZ and BBa_26VH4F2F, both HBUT-China's; BBa_262HI0IB feeds HKSSC's own BBa_26MSEOFB; Michigan's M1 thermometer feeds its own geneblock. Reuse runs the other way, and it runs *backwards in time*: GCGS improved BBa_K2315014 from Shanghai_tech 2017 and borrowed Prhl(LR) (BBa_K1529310) from Tokyo_Tech 2014; Kyoto's Leucine ZipPart collection folds in five prior-year zippers and re-measures them. A part built in 2026 pays out in 2028. That is the actual timescale of a durable asset, and it is an argument for starting now rather than against it.","body_zh":"四個獎項、三個組別共十一位得主，而把他們和四十幾支入圍隊伍分開的只有一件事：**registry 頁面上到底有什麼**。2026 年的 registry（現在位於 registry.igem.org，每個元件都有伺服器端渲染的頁面與公開的讀取 API）為每個元件提供 Design、Experiment、Characterisation、Application 與 Discussion 欄位。得獎者把它們填滿。我們量測了每個能解析到的元件頁面上的文件字元數：得獎者的主打元件在三到六份文件中帶有 **10,000 到 83,000 個字元**；我們抽樣的入圍元件則是 **440 到 2,500 個字元**，通常只有一份 Design 筆記——而且有好幾個根本什麼都沒有。\n\n空白頁面才是真正的發現，因為它們屬於**已經入圍**的隊伍。QingdaoAcademy 的 ulvan lyase（BBa_26QJCNH8、BBa_26ZVH9D0、BBa_265B8WZF）入圍高中組 Best New Basic Part，每一頁的文件都是**零**：一個標題、一段序列，沒有別的。HKU-HongKong 的 aTi-14 胜肽（BBa_265GWS2B，45 bp）入圍 Best New Composite Part，文件同樣是零。Bist-China 登錄的 PdhR（BBa_26OKC42U）與 LldR（BBa_26S2KNZ1）完全沒有文件，真正的內容反而放在兩個幾乎一模一樣的變體頁面上。入圍很便宜，一個頁面不是。\n\n**新穎性輸給文件，而且輸得乾淨俐落。** 高中組 Best New Basic Part 得主 HKSSC 靠 BBa_262HI0IB 獲獎——那是一段*直接取自 GenBank AY077721.1 的 247 bp 天然啟動子加 RBS*。序列本身毫無新意。新的是：從來沒有人登錄或鑑定過它。隊伍把這件事講清楚，用 BPROM 預測啟動子（LDF 5.30、−10 box TATAAT 位於第 163 位、−35 box TTGAAA 位於第 142 位），把它接進配送套件中的無啟動子載體 BBa_J435300，並報出電泳圖、條帶大小（插入片段 974 bp、載體 2,680 bp）與 NanoDrop 三重複數據。GFP 讀值放在複合元件 BBa_26MSEOFB 上，並從基礎元件連結過去。整座獎就是靠一次啟動子捕捉、一個免費網頁工具與誠實的記帳拿下的。這是整份普查中最值得照抄的一項結果。\n\n這批隊伍裡最好的規格表是 TU Darmstadt 的 GeoEsterase（BBa_269NN9UX，Overgrad 組 Best New Basic Part）：以 *p*-nitrophenyl hexanoate 為受質、在 396 nm 讀值並明寫莫耳吸光係數（ε = 18,100 M⁻¹cm⁻¹），0.5 µM 酵素對上 0.5／1／2／4 mM 受質，溫度取 22、32、37、42、47 °C，**每一個數值都是三重複的平均**，以最小平方法擬合 Michaelis-Menten，並附上 V_max、K_M、k_cat 與 k_cat/K_M 的表格（緩衝液 42 °C 下為 894 M⁻¹s⁻¹）。他們同時寫明：經工程改造的 ThermoGeoEsterase 在每一個溫度下都*不如*親代，熱位移分析也看不出熱穩定性改善——並說明讀盤儀加熱上限只到 47 °C。得獎者會把失敗寫下來，而且帶單位。\n\n證據是放在 registry 裡，還是連回一個終將腐朽的 wiki？**在 registry 裡。** 我們統計了七個得獎元件的圖片來源：每個元件 4 到 21 張圖，全部由 registry.igem.wiki/documentation 提供，也就是 registry 自己的檔案庫，而不是隊伍網站。只有 TU Darmstadt 與 WHU-China 會連出到 2026.igem.wiki，而且是作為補充細節的交叉參照，不是資料所在之處。Best Part Collection 也一樣：三位得主都有集合層級的文件（GHCIS 25,665 字元、Heidelberg 76,231、GU Frankfurt 111,681），而**十二個入圍集合中有八個完全沒有集合頁面文字**——除了 Marburg 之外，ETH-Zurich、Bonn、UTDallas、Tsinglan、HFI、ASIJ-Tokyo、YHA-HWFLA 與 UCS-A 都只是把元件列出來。一袋元件加上一個標題，並不是一個集合。\n\n有一個假說失敗了。**2026 年的 registry 裡找不到任何得獎元件被別隊重複使用的跡象。** 2026 年得獎元件上所有非零的 *Used in* 計數，指向的都是同一隊自己的複合元件：Neo-IL-2（BBa_26WNS0EJ）供給 BBa_26V37TWZ 與 BBa_26VH4F2F，兩者都屬於 HBUT-China；BBa_262HI0IB 供給 HKSSC 自己的 BBa_26MSEOFB；Michigan 的 M1 溫度計供給自家的 geneblock。重複使用是往另一個方向走的，而且是*往回走*：GCGS 改良了 Shanghai_tech 2017 的 BBa_K2315014，並借用 Tokyo_Tech 2014 的 Prhl(LR)（BBa_K1529310）；Kyoto 的 Leucine ZipPart 集合收編了五個往年的 leucine zipper 並重新量測。2026 年做的元件，要到 2028 年才會回本。這才是「可持久的資產」真正的時間尺度，而這是現在就該開始做的理由，不是不做的理由。","cards":[{"kicker":"The depth gap","kicker_zh":"深度落差","title":"10,000 characters versus 440","title_zh":"10,000 字元對上 440","body":"Every winning headline part we resolved carries 10,388–83,030 characters of registry documentation across 3–6 typed documents (Design, Experiment, Characterisation, Application, Discussion). Squirrel-Beijing's high-school composite winner BBa_26BFFCJG tops the list at 83,030 characters and 12 registry-hosted figures. Sampled nominee parts: Vilnius-Lithuania 442–2,495, DTU-Denmark 520–1,188, mostly Design-only. Volume is not sufficient — UCAS-China's BBa_263ZN48F has 146,670 characters across 16 documents and only placed as a nominee — but below about 5,000 characters nothing in this cohort won anything.","body_zh":"我們解析到的每一個得獎主打元件，都帶有 10,388 至 83,030 字元的 registry 文件，分布在 3 到 6 份分類文件中（Design、Experiment、Characterisation、Application、Discussion）。Squirrel-Beijing 的高中組複合元件得主 BBa_26BFFCJG 以 83,030 字元與 12 張存放於 registry 的圖居冠。抽樣的入圍元件：Vilnius-Lithuania 442–2,495、DTU-Denmark 520–1,188，而且多半只有 Design。份量本身並不充分——UCAS-China 的 BBa_263ZN48F 有 16 份文件、146,670 字元，仍然只是入圍——但在這批隊伍裡，低於約 5,000 字元的沒有任何一個得獎。","chips":["BBa_26BFFCJG","83,030 characters","12 figures"],"chips_zh":["BBa_26BFFCJG","83,030 字元","12 張圖"],"link":"https://registry.igem.org/parts/bba-26bffcjg","linkText":"Squirrel-Beijing's pNP sensor circuit"},{"kicker":"The most teachable win","kicker_zh":"最值得學的一次獲獎","title":"An unremarkable 247 bp, documented properly","title_zh":"一段平凡的 247 bp，但文件做到位","body":"HKSSC won high-school Best New Basic Part with prbA's native promoter and RBS (BBa_262HI0IB), copied from GenBank AY077721.1. The argument was that nobody had registered it. BPROM gave LDF 5.30 with a TATAAT −10 box at position 163 and a TTGAAA −35 box at 142; the fragment went into the promoterless distribution vector BBa_J435300 by HindIII/KpnI; gels, 974 bp and 2,680 bp band sizes and triplicate NanoDrop A260/A280 are all on the page; the GFP read-out sits on the linked composite BBa_26MSEOFB. Total cost: one gBlock, one free web tool, one reporter.","body_zh":"HKSSC 以 prbA 的天然啟動子與 RBS（BBa_262HI0IB）拿下高中組 Best New Basic Part，序列直接取自 GenBank AY077721.1。他們的論點是：從來沒有人登錄過它。BPROM 給出 LDF 5.30，−10 box TATAAT 在第 163 位、−35 box TTGAAA 在第 142 位；片段以 HindIII/KpnI 接進無啟動子的配送載體 BBa_J435300；電泳圖、974 bp 與 2,680 bp 的條帶大小、三重複的 NanoDrop A260/A280 全都在頁面上；GFP 讀值放在連結過去的複合元件 BBa_26MSEOFB。總成本：一段 gBlock、一個免費網頁工具、一個報導基因。","chips":["BBa_262HI0IB","247 bp","BPROM LDF 5.30"],"chips_zh":["BBa_262HI0IB","247 bp","BPROM LDF 5.30"],"link":"https://registry.igem.org/parts/bba-262hi0ib","linkText":"BBa_262HI0IB on the registry"},{"kicker":"What a datasheet looks like","kicker_zh":"一份規格表長什麼樣","title":"Units, replicates, conditions — and the failure","title_zh":"單位、重複、條件——以及失敗","body":"TU Darmstadt's GeoEsterase (BBa_269NN9UX) is the reference datasheet of 2026: p-nitrophenyl hexanoate at 396 nm with ε = 18,100 M⁻¹cm⁻¹ stated, 0.5 µM enzyme against 0.5/1/2/4 mM substrate at 22–47 °C, every point n = 3, Michaelis-Menten fitted by least squares, k_cat/K_M = 894 M⁻¹s⁻¹ at 42 °C. The Discussion then reports that the ProteinMPNN-redesigned ThermoGeoEsterase was worse than the parent at every temperature, that the thermal shift assay showed no gain, and that the plate reader could not exceed 47 °C so the test stopped there.","body_zh":"TU Darmstadt 的 GeoEsterase（BBa_269NN9UX）是 2026 年的規格表典範：以 p-nitrophenyl hexanoate 在 396 nm 讀值並明寫 ε = 18,100 M⁻¹cm⁻¹，0.5 µM 酵素對 0.5／1／2／4 mM 受質，溫度 22 至 47 °C，每個數據點 n = 3，以最小平方法擬合 Michaelis-Menten，42 °C 下 k_cat/K_M = 894 M⁻¹s⁻¹。接著 Discussion 直接寫明：以 ProteinMPNN 重新設計的 ThermoGeoEsterase 在每個溫度下都比親代差，熱位移分析看不出改善，而且讀盤儀無法超過 47 °C，所以測試就停在那裡。","chips":["BBa_269NN9UX","n = 3","ε = 18,100 M⁻¹cm⁻¹"],"chips_zh":["BBa_269NN9UX","n = 3","ε = 18,100 M⁻¹cm⁻¹"],"link":"https://registry.igem.org/parts/bba-269nn9ux","linkText":"GeoEsterase characterisation"},{"kicker":"Best New Improved Part","kicker_zh":"Best New Improved Part","title":"Two winners, zero nominees","title_zh":"兩位得主，零入圍","body":"Nobody else entered. Both improved-part awards — Michigan at undergrad, GCGS at high school — were given with no nominee list at all. GCGS shows the template: name the parent (BBa_K2315014, Shanghai_tech 2017), name the defect (basal leakage without C4-HSL), make two stated changes (an SsrA-ASV degron on RhlR; swap wild-type Prhl for Tokyo_Tech 2014's Prhl(LR), BBa_K1529310), then benchmark the improved part BBa_26QSD9SO side by side against the parent and four other tag variants across a 0 / 10 µM / 100 µM / 1 mM C4-HSL gradient, normalised as RFU/OD₆₀₀, with growth curves showing no metabolic burden.","body_zh":"沒有別人報名。兩項 improved part 獎——大學組 Michigan、高中組 GCGS——都是在完全沒有入圍名單的情況下頒出的。GCGS 示範了範本：指名親代（BBa_K2315014，Shanghai_tech 2017）、指出缺陷（沒有 C4-HSL 時的基礎滲漏）、做出兩項明寫的更動（在 RhlR 上加 SsrA-ASV 降解標籤；把野生型 Prhl 換成 Tokyo_Tech 2014 的 Prhl(LR)，BBa_K1529310），再把改良後的 BBa_26QSD9SO 與親代及另外四個標籤變體並排比較，跨 0／10 µM／100 µM／1 mM 的 C4-HSL 梯度，以 RFU/OD₆₀₀ 正規化，並附生長曲線證明沒有代謝負擔。","chips":["BBa_26QSD9SO","parent BBa_K2315014","RFU/OD₆₀₀"],"chips_zh":["BBa_26QSD9SO","母件 BBa_K2315014","RFU/OD₆₀₀"],"link":"https://registry.igem.org/parts/bba-26qsd9so","linkText":"GCGS's improved C4-HSL sensor"},{"kicker":"Best Part Collection","kicker_zh":"Best Part Collection","title":"A shared grammar, or a bag of parts","title_zh":"共通文法，還是一袋零件","body":"Winners name their parts to a rule. Heidelberg's 18-item VOYAGE collection prefixes every entry with its function — GV-core:, Sensing:, Multiplexing:, Organize: — and GU Frankfurt's 25 items split cleanly by role into 4 HLA targets (Biological Region), 9 synNotch receptors (Engineered Region) and 12 shRNAs (NcRNA Gene): bind, trigger, silence. GHCIS's high-school winner is a 3 × 3 matrix: three AMR genes (mcr-1, blaNDM-1, blaKPC-2) × trigger RNA and reporter plasmid. Marburg's nominated CLiPPR, the largest collection at 246 parts, is the only one to state its assembly standard outright (MoClo, BsaI/BsmBI) — and still did not win.","body_zh":"得獎者為元件命名是有規則的。Heidelberg 的 18 項 VOYAGE 集合，每個條目都以功能為前綴——GV-core:、Sensing:、Multiplexing:、Organize:；GU Frankfurt 的 25 項則依角色乾淨地分成 4 個 HLA 標的（Biological Region）、9 個 synNotch 受體（Engineered Region）與 12 個 shRNA（NcRNA Gene）：結合、觸發、沉默。GHCIS 的高中組得主是一個 3 × 3 矩陣：三個抗藥性基因（mcr-1、blaNDM-1、blaKPC-2）× trigger RNA 與報導質體。入圍的 Marburg CLiPPR 是最大的集合（246 個元件），也是唯一明寫組裝標準的（MoClo、BsaI/BsmBI）——但仍然沒有得獎。","chips":["Heidelberg 18 items","GU Frankfurt 25 items","GHCIS 9 items"],"chips_zh":["Heidelberg 18 件","GU Frankfurt 25 件","GHCIS 9 件"],"link":"https://registry.igem.org/collections/5bceaa90-cc31-4958-a74f-cc3139ec02c2","linkText":"Heidelberg's VOYAGE collection"},{"kicker":"The empty-page problem","kicker_zh":"空白頁面問題","title":"Eight of twelve nominated collections have no page text","title_zh":"十二個入圍集合中有八個沒有頁面文字","body":"All three Best Part Collection winners carry collection-level documentation: GHCIS 25,665 characters in 4 documents, Heidelberg 76,231 in 4, GU Frankfurt 111,681 in 7. Of the twelve nominated collections we checked, only Kyoto (40,761), NUS-Singapore (51,083), Princeton (68,005) and Marburg (58,778) have any — and Princeton's seven documents are all typed Design, with no characterisation document at all. ETH-Zurich, Bonn, UTDallas, Tsinglan, HFI, ASIJ-Tokyo, YHA-HWFLA and UCS-A registered a collection and left the page blank. Several of them, Tsinglan included, documented the individual parts well; nobody wrote the page that explains why the parts belong together.","body_zh":"三位 Best Part Collection 得主都有集合層級的文件：GHCIS 4 份共 25,665 字元、Heidelberg 4 份共 76,231、GU Frankfurt 7 份共 111,681。我們檢查的十二個入圍集合中，只有 Kyoto（40,761）、NUS-Singapore（51,083）、Princeton（68,005）與 Marburg（58,778）有文件——而 Princeton 的七份文件全部歸類為 Design，完全沒有 characterisation 文件。ETH-Zurich、Bonn、UTDallas、Tsinglan、HFI、ASIJ-Tokyo、YHA-HWFLA 與 UCS-A 則是登錄了集合卻把頁面留白。其中有幾隊（包括 Tsinglan）把個別元件寫得很好；但沒有人寫下那一頁，說明這些元件為什麼該放在一起。","chips":["8 of 12 blank","Princeton: no characterisation doc"],"chips_zh":["8/12 空白","Princeton：沒有表徵文件"],"link":"https://registry.igem.org/collections/eda71dd5-c755-4b01-87cd-819d4222a108","linkText":"GHCIS's documented collection"},{"kicker":"Reuse, honestly","kicker_zh":"誠實談重複使用","title":"'Used in' is self-citation — so far","title_zh":"「Used in」目前都是自我引用","body":"The registry now shows a Used in count on every part page, which is the closest thing to a reuse metric iGEM has. On the 2026 winners it only ever points at the same team's own composites. Nothing in this cohort was picked up by a stranger inside the competition year. But the winners themselves are heavy consumers of old parts: GCGS built on a 2017 part and a 2014 promoter, HKSSC used a distribution-kit vector, and nine of the fourteen items in Kyoto's leucine-zipper collection are prior-year BBa_K parts re-measured. The registry pays out on a two-to-ten year lag. That is a reason to start, not a reason to wait.","body_zh":"registry 現在在每個元件頁面上顯示 Used in 計數，這是 iGEM 目前最接近「重複使用」的指標。在 2026 年的得獎元件上，它指向的永遠是同一隊自己的複合元件。這批隊伍裡沒有任何元件在競賽當年被陌生人採用。但得獎者自己大量消費舊元件：GCGS 建立在一個 2017 年的元件與一個 2014 年的啟動子上，HKSSC 使用了配送套件的載體，Kyoto 的 leucine zipper 集合中十四項裡有九項是往年的 BBa_K 元件並重新量測。registry 的回報有兩到十年的遞延。這是該開始的理由，不是該等待的理由。","chips":["BBa_K2315014 (2017)","BBa_K1529310 (2014)","BBa_J435300"],"chips_zh":["BBa_K2315014 (2017)","BBa_K1529310 (2014)","BBa_J435300"],"link":"https://registry.igem.org/parts/bba-k2315014","linkText":"The 2017 parent GCGS improved"}],"table":{"head":["Team","Section","Category","Part or collection","Registry documentation","Figures"],"head_zh":["隊伍","組別","獎項","元件或集合","Registry 文件量","圖片"],"rows":[["HBUT-China","Undergrad","Best New Basic Part","BBa_26WNS0EJ Neo-IL-2 (CDS, 399 bp)","6 docs, 59,355 chars","18"],["TU Darmstadt","Overgrad","Best New Basic Part","BBa_269NN9UX GeoEsterase (CDS, 879 bp)","4 docs, 68,204 chars","21"],["HKSSC","High School","Best New Basic Part","BBa_262HI0IB prbA native promoter + RBS (247 bp)","2 docs, 10,388 chars","5"],["WHU-China","Undergrad","Best New Composite Part","BBa_26TCR52M YhjH-mCherry-PopZ (1,958 bp)","4 docs, 35,441 chars","17"],["Muenster-University","Overgrad","Best New Composite Part","Blocker_PCS:protease_NLR series (e.g. BBa_26ON4OVD)","0 docs; 300-char descriptions only","0"],["Squirrel-Beijing","High School","Best New Composite Part","BBa_26BFFCJG PobR pNP-responsive RFP circuit","5 docs, 83,030 chars","12"],["Michigan","Undergrad","Best New Improved Part","BBa_2623X9FE M1 RNA thermometer (38 bp)","4 docs, 13,798 chars","4"],["GCGS","High School","Best New Improved Part","BBa_26QSD9SO pCon-RhlR-SsrA-ASV-Prhl(LR)-GFP","5 docs, 25,840 chars","11"],["Heidelberg","Undergrad","Best Part Collection","VOYAGE gas-vesicle collection, 18 items","4 docs, 76,231 chars","11"],["GU Frankfurt","Overgrad","Best Part Collection","HIDE collection, 25 items","7 docs, 111,681 chars","17"],["GHCIS","High School","Best Part Collection","Toehold AMR collection, 9 items","4 docs, 25,665 chars","8"]],"rows_zh":[["HBUT-China","大學組","Best New Basic Part","BBa_26WNS0EJ Neo-IL-2（CDS，399 bp）","6 份文件、59,355 字元","18"],["TU Darmstadt","研究生組","Best New Basic Part","BBa_269NN9UX GeoEsterase（CDS，879 bp）","4 份文件、68,204 字元","21"],["HKSSC","高中組","Best New Basic Part","BBa_262HI0IB prbA 天然啟動子 + RBS（247 bp）","2 份文件、10,388 字元","5"],["WHU-China","大學組","Best New Composite Part","BBa_26TCR52M YhjH-mCherry-PopZ（1,958 bp）","4 份文件、35,441 字元","17"],["Muenster-University","研究生組","Best New Composite Part","Blocker_PCS:protease_NLR 系列（例如 BBa_26ON4OVD）","0 份文件；僅有約 300 字元的描述","0"],["Squirrel-Beijing","高中組","Best New Composite Part","BBa_26BFFCJG PobR 對 pNP 反應的 RFP 迴路","5 份文件、83,030 字元","12"],["Michigan","大學組","Best New Improved Part","BBa_2623X9FE M1 RNA 溫度計（38 bp）","4 份文件、13,798 字元","4"],["GCGS","高中組","Best New Improved Part","BBa_26QSD9SO pCon-RhlR-SsrA-ASV-Prhl(LR)-GFP","5 份文件、25,840 字元","11"],["Heidelberg","大學組","Best Part Collection","VOYAGE 氣泡囊集合，18 項","4 份文件、76,231 字元","11"],["GU Frankfurt","研究生組","Best Part Collection","HIDE 集合，25 項","7 份文件、111,681 字元","17"],["GHCIS","高中組","Best Part Collection","Toehold 抗藥性集合，9 項","4 份文件、25,665 字元","8"]]},"checklist":["Target Best New Improved Part first. In 2026 it had two winners and zero nominees across the whole competition — the only parts category where showing up is most of the work. It also needs no novel sequence, which suits a team without a protein-design pipeline.","Pick a parent part that already exists in the registry, has a stated defect, and runs in E. coli. Write its accession down on day one (GCGS used BBa_K2315014 from Shanghai_tech 2017). If you cannot name the parent and its defect in one sentence, you are not entering this category.","State the improvement as a list of discrete, named changes to the parent — not 'we optimised it'. GCGS's whole case is two lines: add an SsrA-ASV degron to RhlR, replace wild-type Prhl with Prhl(LR). Each change gets its own sub-part accession on the page.","Measure the parent and the improved part on the same plate, on the same day, with the same reporter. A side-by-side benchmark against the unmodified parent is the single non-negotiable requirement of this category.","Produce a dose-response or transfer function, not a yes/no. At least four inducer concentrations plus a blank and a solvent-only control, three biological replicates per point, output normalised to OD₆₀₀ (RFU/OD₆₀₀) or to enzyme concentration.","Write the conditions a stranger would need to repeat it: strain and chassis, medium, temperature, induction OD, time points, instrument and wavelength, and the extinction coefficient if you convert absorbance to concentration (TU Darmstadt: ε = 18,100 M⁻¹cm⁻¹ at 396 nm).","Put the figures in the registry, not on the wiki. Upload every plot and gel through the registry documentation editor so it is served from registry.igem.wiki/documentation. A figure that only exists on 2026.igem.wiki dies when the wiki does. Cross-link to the wiki for extra detail only.","Fill all five document slots — Design, Experiment, Characterisation, Application, Discussion. Eleven of eleven winners used at least three; most nominee parts used one. Empty slots are visible on the page.","Write the limitations into the Discussion and keep them. Michigan published that M3 produced no detectable protein and that its comparison rests on a single unreplicated blot; TU Darmstadt published that their engineered variant was worse than the parent. Both won. Hiding a null result does not buy an award, and reporting one apparently does not cost you a category.","Register a collection as well, with a collection-level page of its own. Give every part a name built to a rule (prefix by function: GV-core:, Sensing:, Multiplexing:), state the assembly standard and overhangs explicitly, and write the one document that says why these parts belong together. Eight of twelve nominated 2026 collections skipped that document.","Check every accession before you publish it. BBa_26SZRX0Y contains a zero, not the letter O; a single wrong character makes the part unfindable, which is the one failure mode that undoes all the work above.","Budget the writing as a work package, not an afterthought. The median winning part page in 2026 is roughly 25,000–35,000 characters with ten-plus figures: that is one person for two to three weeks, and it has to be scheduled before the wiki freeze, not after."],"checklist_zh":["先以 Best New Improved Part 為目標。2026 年全場只有兩位得主、零入圍——這是元件類獎項中「有報名就贏一半」的唯一一個。它也不需要新穎序列，適合沒有蛋白質設計管線的隊伍。","挑一個已經存在於 registry、有明確缺陷、而且能在 E. coli 裡跑的親代元件。第一天就把它的編號寫下來（GCGS 用的是 Shanghai_tech 2017 的 BBa_K2315014）。如果你沒辦法用一句話說出親代是誰、缺陷是什麼，就代表你還沒真的進入這個類別。","把改良寫成一張對親代所做的、具名且離散的更動清單——不要寫「我們做了最佳化」。GCGS 的整個論點只有兩行：在 RhlR 上加 SsrA-ASV 降解標籤、把野生型 Prhl 換成 Prhl(LR)。每一項更動都要在頁面上有自己的子元件編號。","把親代與改良後的元件放在同一塊盤、同一天、用同一個報導基因量。與未改造親代的並排對照，是這個類別唯一不可妥協的要求。","做出劑量反應或轉移函數，不要做是／否。至少四個誘導物濃度，外加空白組與僅溶劑組，每個點三個生物重複，輸出以 OD₆₀₀ 正規化（RFU/OD₆₀₀）或以酵素濃度正規化。","把陌生人要重做一次所需要的條件寫出來：菌株與宿主、培養基、溫度、誘導時的 OD、取樣時間點、儀器與波長；若要把吸光值換算成濃度，還要寫出莫耳吸光係數（TU Darmstadt：396 nm 下 ε = 18,100 M⁻¹cm⁻¹）。","把圖放進 registry，不要只放在 wiki。所有圖表與電泳圖都透過 registry 的文件編輯器上傳，讓它由 registry.igem.wiki/documentation 提供。只存在於 2026.igem.wiki 上的圖，會隨 wiki 一起消失。連回 wiki 只用於補充細節。","五個文件欄位全部填滿——Design、Experiment、Characterisation、Application、Discussion。十一位得主全都至少用了三個；多數入圍元件只用了一個。空欄位在頁面上是看得見的。","把限制寫進 Discussion，而且留著不要刪。Michigan 公開寫出 M3 完全測不到蛋白、而且整個比較只建立在一張未重複的西方墨點上；TU Darmstadt 公開寫出他們改造的變體比親代還差。兩者都得獎了。藏起陰性結果買不到獎，而寫出來顯然也不會讓你丟掉一個類別。","同時登錄一個集合，並為它寫一個集合層級的頁面。每個元件都依規則命名（以功能為前綴：GV-core:、Sensing:、Multiplexing:），明寫組裝標準與黏端（overhang），並寫下那一份說明「這些元件為什麼屬於同一組」的文件。2026 年十二個入圍集合中，有八個跳過了這份文件。","發布前逐一檢查每個編號。BBa_26SZRX0Y 裡面是數字 0，不是字母 O；一個字元錯掉，元件就搜不到，而這是唯一一種會讓上面所有努力歸零的失敗模式。","把撰寫當成一個獨立的工作包，而不是事後補。2026 年得獎元件頁面的中位數大約是 25,000 至 35,000 字元、十張以上的圖：那是一個人兩到三週的量，而且必須排在 wiki 凍結之前，不是之後。"],"method":"Started from the 106 researched team files on disk, which named exact accessions for several cohort teams. Then read the 2026 registry directly. parts.igem.org now redirects to registry.igem.org, a React application backed by a public read API (api.registry.igem.org/v1) that the site itself calls; we drove it through a browser tab and used only the endpoints the registry's own pages request — part by slug, documentation, composition, used-by, collections, collection items. Every accession quoted here was confirmed to return HTTP 200 from /v1/parts/slugs/<slug>; BBa_26SZRXOY, as transcribed in one team file, 404s — the real part is BBa_26SZRX0Y with a zero. We resolved documentation for all eleven winners' headline parts or collections, for all fifteen Best Part Collection cohort collections, and for sampled parts from eleven nominee teams. Documentation size is the character count of the markdown stored in the registry's own documentation records; figure counts are markdown and HTML image references in that same text. Limits: the award lists name teams, not parts, so for teams that registered several parts we inferred the award-winning one from the team file, the part's documentation depth and the project description — Muenster-University's Best New Composite Part winner in particular we could not pin down, and the Blocker_PCS series we found carries no documentation at all, so that row may be the wrong part. We also could not see team files for XMU-China, NNU-Nanjing-China, China-HUBU-Wuhan, RUBochum, NAU-CHINA, LZU-Northwest and VUB-Brussels, so those nominees are not represented in the depth figures. Rate limiting on the registry API (HTTP 429) capped the sampling, so nominee counts are samples of three to five parts per team, not full inventories. No team wiki was used as a source for any number here.","method_zh":"先從磁碟上 106 份已研究的隊伍檔案出發，其中幾支隊伍直接寫出了確切的元件編號；接著直接讀 2026 年的 registry。parts.igem.org 現在會轉址到 registry.igem.org，那是一個 React 應用，背後有公開的讀取 API（api.registry.igem.org/v1）供網站本身呼叫；我們以瀏覽器分頁操作，而且只使用 registry 自己的頁面會請求的端點——依 slug 取元件、documentation、composition、used-by、collections 與集合項目。本文引用的每一個編號都已確認 /v1/parts/slugs/<slug> 回傳 HTTP 200；某份隊伍檔案裡抄寫的 BBa_26SZRXOY 會 404——真正的元件是 BBa_26SZRX0Y，中間是數字 0。我們解析了全部十一位得主的主打元件或集合、Best Part Collection 這組全部十五個集合，以及十一支入圍隊伍的抽樣元件。文件量是 registry 自身 documentation 記錄中所儲存 markdown 的字元數；圖片數量是同一段文字中的 markdown 與 HTML 圖片引用數。限制：獎項名單列的是隊伍而非元件，因此對於登錄了多個元件的隊伍，我們是從隊伍檔案、元件的文件深度與專案描述推斷出得獎元件——其中 Muenster-University 的 Best New Composite Part 得獎元件我們無法確定，而我們找到的 Blocker_PCS 系列完全沒有文件，所以那一列有可能指錯元件。我們也沒有 XMU-China、NNU-Nanjing-China、China-HUBU-Wuhan、RUBochum、NAU-CHINA、LZU-Northwest 與 VUB-Brussels 的隊伍檔案，因此這些入圍者未納入深度統計。registry API 的速率限制（HTTP 429）限縮了抽樣規模，所以入圍隊伍的數字是每隊三到五個元件的抽樣，而非完整清冊。本文的任何數字都沒有以隊伍 wiki 作為來源。"},{"id":"chassis-census","tab":"teams","order":38,"kicker":"Wet lab / chassis","kicker_zh":"濕實驗室 ‧ 底盤","title":"What 106 decorated teams actually built in","title_zh":"106 支得獎隊伍到底把東西做在什麼生物裡","lede":"Exactly 1 of the 106 decorated teams used light to control a *Bacillus subtilis* culture, and that team is GEMS-Taiwan itself — 5 teams used light as a control input in any organism, 5 worked with *B. subtilis*, and the two sets overlap in one place. The companion test returned a null: among these decorated teams a non-model chassis neither helped nor hurt the odds of a Top 10 place (9 of 27 against 21 of 79, Fisher exact p = 0.62).","lede_zh":"106 支得獎隊伍中，只有 1 支用光去控制 *Bacillus subtilis* 的培養，而那支隊伍就是 GEMS-Taiwan 自己——有 5 支隊伍在任何生物裡把光當成控制輸入，有 5 支隊伍碰了 *B. subtilis*，兩個集合只在一個點上重疊。另一項檢定則得到虛無結果：在這些得獎隊伍之中，使用非模式底盤既沒有提高也沒有降低擠進 Top 10 的機會（27 支中有 9 支，對比 79 支中有 21 支，Fisher 精確檢定 p = 0.62）。","body":"**E. coli is still the house organism.** 51 of the 106 decorated teams put a construct into *E. coli*, and 24 of those 51 name a strain — BL21(DE3) most often, then DH5-alpha, then Nissle 1917, MG1655, Rosetta(DE3), SHuffle, C41 and BL21-AI. The other 27 write only \"E. coli\" and stop there, which is enough to describe a project and not enough to repeat one. Yeast is a distant second at 13 teams: 8 name *S. cerevisiae* (EBY100, BY4741 and three-plasmid builds among them), 3 use *Pichia pastoris* or *Komagataella*, and 4 write \"yeast\" with no species at all. Mammalian cell lines appear in 8 teams and are overwhelmingly HEK293, with CHO, a piggyBac reporter line and an oncolytic HSV-2 complementing line making up the rest. *B. subtilis* appears in 5.\n\n**The tail is more interesting than the head.** 14 teams built in a named non-model organism and almost none of them chose the same one: *Pseudomonas putida* four times (KT2440 three times, F1 once), then *Streptococcus salivarius* K12, *Zymomonas mobilis*, *Komagataeibacter rhaeticus*, *Sporosarcina pasteurii*, *Magnetospirillum magneticum* AMB-1, *Shewanella oneidensis* MR-1, *Clostridium beijerinckii* S63 (isolated from a wetland by the team and made transformable from scratch), the thermophile pair *Acetivibrio thermocellus* and *Geobacillus thermocatenulatus*, *Photorhabdus* virulence cassettes, and arbuscular mycorrhizal fungi. Add *Nostoc* sp. PCC 7120, *Chlamydomonas reinhardtii* twice, *Nicotiana* and a *Stevia* hairy root, Sf9 insect cells and M13 phage. 9 teams ran cell-free systems, 6 worked only with purified enzymes or in vitro nucleic-acid chemistry, and exactly 1 decorated entry had no wet lab at all. 18 teams used more than one chassis.\n\n**The null, stated plainly.** Splitting the 106 into the 27 that used a chassis outside *E. coli*, *S. cerevisiae* and standard mammalian lines against the 79 that did not, 9 of 27 reached a Top 10 place versus 21 of 79 — 33 percent against 27 percent, Fisher exact p = 0.62. There is no effect here. The honest boundary on that sentence is that the sample is decorated teams only, so it says that among teams which already won something, chassis choice does not separate the Top 10 from the rest; it says nothing about whether a non-model chassis helps a team get decorated in the first place, because this analysis has no undecorated baseline and never could.\n\n**The white space, tested against iGEM.** The academic trend review puts it in one line: light has become a real-time actuator for feedback control of fermentation, with reported 60 percent titer gains in a 1 L photobioreactor, *while optogenetics in Bacillus subtilis remains almost unexplored — twelve papers in all of PubMed*, and no published light-controlled *B. subtilis* bioreactor at all. The industry review arrives from the other side: Fermeate raised seed money to control gene expression with light so existing stainless-steel fermenters can be retrofitted instead of replaced, which is the cheapest route past the capital-cost wall. Against iGEM 2026, the counts are these. **5 of 106** used light as a control input in any organism: McGill (VP16-EL222 / C120 driving flocculation in *S. cerevisiae*), GEMS-Taiwan (CcaSR green light in *B. subtilis* WB800), WHU-China (EL222 with pBLI in *E. coli*), Princeton (an AsLOV2 optomonobody releasing cargo at 450 nm on M13 phage), and William & Mary, who measured dark and light curves on one of four pre-existing circuits they were stress-testing. Marburg is a sixth near-miss: they investigated optogenetic induction with the PULSE system and called it the most attractive long-term inducer on safety grounds, then did not build it. **5 of 106** worked with *B. subtilis*: GEMS-Taiwan (WB800), UPF-Barcelona (rhizosphere colonisation, strain unnamed), Hongwen School (WB600 secretion host), KAUST-KSA (Dsup integrated for radiation resistance), and BGI-College, who cultivated a commercial strain on spent broth rather than engineering it. **1 of 106** did both. Four of the five *B. subtilis* teams induce with something other than light — a promoter, an osmolarity switch, a genomic integration — and four of the five light teams are working in an organism where the technique is already routine. Excluding GEMS-Taiwan, the intersection is **0 of 105**. The white space the Drylab roadmap points at is real inside iGEM as well as inside PubMed, and nobody else in this cohort is competing for it.","body_zh":"**E. coli 仍然是 iGEM 的當家生物。** 106 支得獎隊伍中有 51 支把構築體放進 *E. coli*，而這 51 支裡有 24 支寫出了具體菌株——最常見的是 BL21(DE3)，接著是 DH5-alpha、Nissle 1917、MG1655、Rosetta(DE3)、SHuffle、C41 與 BL21-AI。其餘 27 支只寫「E. coli」就打住了；這足以描述一個專題，卻不足以讓別人重做一次。酵母以 13 支隊伍居次，差距很大：8 支寫出 *S. cerevisiae*（其中包含 EBY100、BY4741 與三質體系統），3 支使用 *Pichia pastoris* 或 *Komagataella*，另外 4 支只寫「酵母」而完全沒有寫出物種。哺乳類細胞株出現在 8 支隊伍，絕大多數是 HEK293，其餘是 CHO、一株 piggyBac 報導細胞株，以及一株供溶瘤 HSV-2 增殖的互補細胞株。*B. subtilis* 出現在 5 支隊伍。\n\n**尾端比前端有意思。** 有 14 支隊伍做在具名的非模式生物上，而且幾乎沒有兩支選到同一種：*Pseudomonas putida* 出現四次（KT2440 三次、F1 一次），接著是 *Streptococcus salivarius* K12、*Zymomonas mobilis*、*Komagataeibacter rhaeticus*、*Sporosarcina pasteurii*、*Magnetospirillum magneticum* AMB-1、*Shewanella oneidensis* MR-1、*Clostridium beijerinckii* S63（由隊伍自己從濕地分離，並從零建立轉形系統）、嗜熱菌組合 *Acetivibrio thermocellus* 與 *Geobacillus thermocatenulatus*、*Photorhabdus* 毒力匣，以及叢枝菌根真菌。再加上 *Nostoc* sp. PCC 7120、兩次出現的 *Chlamydomonas reinhardtii*、*Nicotiana* 與一套 *Stevia* 毛狀根、Sf9 昆蟲細胞與 M13 噬菌體。有 9 支隊伍使用無細胞系統，6 支只處理純化酵素或體外核酸化學，而完全沒有濕實驗室的得獎專題正好只有 1 支。有 18 支隊伍用了不只一種底盤。\n\n**虛無結果，直說。** 把 106 支分成兩群：27 支使用 *E. coli*、*S. cerevisiae* 與標準哺乳類細胞株以外底盤的隊伍，以及其餘 79 支。前者有 9 支進入 Top 10，後者有 21 支——33% 對 27%，Fisher 精確檢定 p = 0.62。這裡沒有效應。這句話誠實的邊界在於樣本只有得獎隊伍，因此它說的是：在已經拿到名次的隊伍之間，底盤選擇無法把 Top 10 和其他人分開；它完全沒有說非模式底盤是否有助於一支隊伍先拿到名次，因為這份分析沒有、也不可能有未得獎隊伍作為對照。\n\n**把白地拿到 iGEM 上檢驗。** 學術趨勢回顧一句話講完：光已成為發酵回饋控制的即時致動器，在 1 L 光生物反應器中有 60% 產量提升的報告，*但 Bacillus subtilis 的光遺傳學幾乎仍無人開發——整個 PubMed 只有十二篇論文*，而且完全沒有已發表的光控 *B. subtilis* 生物反應器。產業趨勢回顧則從另一側抵達同一個點：Fermeate 募得種子輪資金，以光控制基因表現，讓既有的不鏽鋼發酵槽可以改裝而不必汰換，這是繞過資本支出高牆最便宜的路。拿到 iGEM 2026 上，數字是這樣。**106 支中有 5 支**在任何生物裡把光當成控制輸入：McGill（VP16-EL222 / C120 在 *S. cerevisiae* 中驅動絮凝）、GEMS-Taiwan（CcaSR 綠光系統於 *B. subtilis* WB800）、WHU-China（EL222 搭配 pBLI 於 *E. coli*）、Princeton（AsLOV2 optomonobody 在 450 nm 下釋出貨物，載於 M13 噬菌體），以及 William & Mary——他們在壓力測試的四組既有迴路中，量了其中一組的暗處與光照曲線。Marburg 是第六個擦身而過的例子：他們研究過以 PULSE 系統做光誘導，並從安全角度稱它是最有吸引力的長期誘導方式，然後沒有動手做。**106 支中有 5 支**碰了 *B. subtilis*：GEMS-Taiwan（WB800）、UPF-Barcelona（根圈定殖，未寫出菌株）、Hongwen School（WB600 分泌宿主）、KAUST-KSA（整合 Dsup 以取得抗輻射能力），以及 BGI-College——他們是把市售菌株養在發酵殘液上，而不是改造它。**106 支中有 1 支**兩者都做。五支 *B. subtilis* 隊伍中有四支用光以外的方式誘導——啟動子、滲透壓開關、基因體整合；而五支用光的隊伍中有四支，工作的生物本來就把這項技術當成例行工具。扣掉 GEMS-Taiwan，交集是 **105 支中的 0 支**。Drylab 路線圖所指的那塊白地，在 iGEM 裡和在 PubMed 裡一樣是真的，而且這一屆沒有別人在跟我們搶。","cards":[{"kicker":"Light","kicker_zh":"光","title":"5 of 106 used light as a control input","title_zh":"106 支中有 5 支把光當成控制輸入","body":"Four of the five work in organisms where optogenetics is already routine: *S. cerevisiae*, *E. coli*, and M13 phage displayed protein. Blue light accounts for four of the five systems (EL222 twice, AsLOV2 once, one unspecified); green light appears once. Only one of the five closes a control loop rather than switching a circuit on.","body_zh":"五支中有四支工作的生物本來就把光遺傳學當成例行工具：*S. cerevisiae*、*E. coli*，以及 M13 噬菌體表面展示的蛋白質。五套系統中有四套使用藍光（EL222 兩次、AsLOV2 一次、一次未指明），綠光只出現一次。五支之中只有一支做的是閉合控制迴路，而不是把迴路打開而已。","chips":["McGill — EL222 in yeast","GEMS-Taiwan — CcaSR in B. subtilis","WHU-China — EL222 in E. coli","Princeton — AsLOV2 on M13","William & Mary — dark/light curves"],"chips_zh":["McGill — EL222，於酵母菌","GEMS-Taiwan — CcaSR，於 B. subtilis","WHU-China — EL222，於 E. coli","Princeton — AsLOV2，於 M13","William & Mary — 明暗對照曲線"]},{"kicker":"B. subtilis","kicker_zh":"B. subtilis","title":"5 of 106 worked with B. subtilis, 4 engineered it","title_zh":"106 支中有 5 支碰 B. subtilis，其中 4 支改造它","body":"Two named a strain (WB800, WB600), one wrote only \"B. subtilis\", one integrated a cargo genomically across three hosts, and one cultivated a commercial strain without engineering it. A sixth team used *B. subtilis* only as a surrogate biofilm organism in an assay, which is a test subject rather than a chassis and is not counted here.","body_zh":"兩支寫出菌株（WB800、WB600），一支只寫「B. subtilis」，一支把一段基因整合進三種宿主的基因體，還有一支只是培養市售菌株而沒有改造它。第六支隊伍把 *B. subtilis* 當成生物膜試驗的替代菌種使用，那是受測對象而不是底盤，因此未計入。","chips":["GEMS-Taiwan WB800","UPF-Barcelona","Hongwen WB600","KAUST-KSA","BGI-College (cultivated only)"],"chips_zh":["GEMS-Taiwan WB800","UPF-Barcelona","Hongwen WB600","KAUST-KSA","BGI-College（僅培養）"]},{"kicker":"Reproducibility","kicker_zh":"可重現性","title":"27 of 51 E. coli teams never name the strain","title_zh":"51 支用 E. coli 的隊伍中，有 27 支沒寫出菌株","body":"A chassis is not a species, it is a strain: BL21(DE3) and DH5-alpha behave nothing alike, and Nissle 1917 is a different proposition again. 24 of 51 say which one. Beyond that, 12 of the 106 dossiers describe bench work whose host organism is nowhere in the write-up at all.","body_zh":"底盤不是一個物種，而是一株菌：BL21(DE3) 與 DH5-alpha 的行為完全不同，Nissle 1917 又是另一回事。51 支中有 24 支寫明用的是哪一株。除此之外，106 份資料裡有 12 份描述了實驗台上的工作，卻從頭到尾都沒有交代宿主生物是什麼。","chips":["24 of 51 name a strain","BL21(DE3) most common","12 of 106 name no host at all"],"chips_zh":["51 支中有 24 支寫出菌株","BL21(DE3) 最常見","106 支中有 12 支完全沒寫宿主"]}],"table":{"head":["Chassis","Teams","Of 106","Notes"],"head_zh":["底盤","隊伍數","佔 106 支","說明"],"rows":[["E. coli","51","48%","24 name a strain; BL21(DE3) most common"],["S. cerevisiae","8","8%","EBY100, BY4741, three-plasmid builds"],["Yeast, species not named","4","4%","written only as \"yeast\""],["Other yeast (Pichia / Komagataella)","3","3%","one of them the project's primary chassis"],["B. subtilis","5","5%","4 engineered, 1 cultivated only"],["Mammalian cell lines","8","8%","HEK293 dominant; CHO; reporter lines"],["Cyanobacteria and algae","3","3%","Nostoc PCC 7120; C. reinhardtii twice"],["Plant","2","2%","Nicotiana; Stevia hairy root"],["Other non-model organisms","14","13%","P. putida ×4; 10 further species, each once"],["Insect cells (Sf9)","1","1%","binder expression and BLI"],["Bacteriophage (M13)","1","1%","phage itself used as the adsorbent"],["Cell-free systems","9","8%","PURExpress, paper toehold, chloroplast extract"],["Purified enzyme / in vitro only","6","6%","LAMP, Cas12a, Cas13a, protease timers"],["No wet lab at all","1","1%","a software entry"],["Chassis not stated","12","11%","bench work done, host organism never named"]],"rows_zh":[["E. coli","51","48%","24 支寫出菌株；最常見是 BL21(DE3)"],["S. cerevisiae","8","8%","EBY100、BY4741、三質體系統"],["酵母，未寫出物種","4","4%","只寫成「酵母」"],["其他酵母（Pichia / Komagataella）","3","3%","其中一支以它作為專題主要底盤"],["B. subtilis","5","5%","4 支改造，1 支僅培養"],["哺乳類細胞株","8","8%","以 HEK293 為主；另有 CHO 與報導細胞株"],["藍綠菌與藻類","3","3%","Nostoc PCC 7120；C. reinhardtii 兩次"],["植物","2","2%","Nicotiana；Stevia 毛狀根"],["其他非模式生物","14","13%","P. putida ×4；另有 10 種各出現一次"],["昆蟲細胞（Sf9）","1","1%","用於結合蛋白表現與 BLI"],["噬菌體（M13）","1","1%","噬菌體本身就是吸附材料"],["無細胞系統","9","8%","PURExpress、紙基 toehold、葉綠體萃取液"],["僅純化酵素／體外","6","6%","LAMP、Cas12a、Cas13a、蛋白酶計時器"],["完全沒有濕實驗室","1","1%","一支軟體專題"],["未交代底盤","12","11%","做了實驗，但從未寫出宿主生物"]]},"checklist":["Hold the B. subtilis optogenetics line for more than one season. The count is 1 of 106 and that one is us; no other decorated team in 2026 is in this space, and the published literature is twelve papers.","Publish a full CcaSR transfer function in WB800 — light intensity crossed with duty cycle crossed with growth phase — because no other team in this cohort has B. subtilis light data to compare against, and a single induction intensity cannot test a Hill curve.","Write the strain in every sentence where others write the species. 27 of 51 E. coli teams never do, and 1 of 5 B. subtilis teams never does. \"B. subtilis WB800\" costs five characters and is the difference between a description and a protocol.","Put the host organism on the Description page, not only in the notebook. 12 of 106 decorated dossiers describe bench work with no host named anywhere — judges and readers should never have to infer it.","Do not pick a non-model chassis to score points. Among decorated teams it moves nothing (p = 0.62). Pick B. subtilis for secretion and for light, and write down that reason.","Record the induction method as a measured variable, not a protocol footnote. Four of the five B. subtilis teams in 2026 induce with a promoter or an osmolarity switch; the argument for light is only as strong as the dose-response data behind it."],"checklist_zh":["把 B. subtilis 光遺傳學當成跨年度的主軸，不要只做一季。數字是 106 支中的 1 支，而那一支就是我們；2026 年沒有其他得獎隊伍在這塊地上，已發表文獻也只有十二篇。","完整發表 WB800 的 CcaSR 轉移函數——光強度、工作週期與生長時期三者交叉——因為這一屆沒有別的隊伍有 B. subtilis 的光照資料可供對照，而單一光強度的誘導無法檢驗一條 Hill 曲線。","別人寫物種的地方，我們寫菌株。51 支用 E. coli 的隊伍中有 27 支從不這麼做，5 支用 B. subtilis 的隊伍中也有 1 支沒寫。「B. subtilis WB800」只多五個字元，卻是描述與實驗流程之間的差別。","把宿主生物寫在 Description 頁，而不是只留在實驗記錄裡。106 份得獎資料中有 12 份描述了實驗工作卻全篇沒有寫出宿主——評審和讀者不該需要自己猜。","不要為了拿分數而挑非模式底盤。在得獎隊伍之間，這一項完全不影響結果（p = 0.62）。選 B. subtilis 是為了分泌與光控，而且要把這個理由寫下來。","把誘導方式當成一個被量測的變項，而不是實驗流程的註腳。2026 年五支 B. subtilis 隊伍中有四支用啟動子或滲透壓開關誘導；選擇光的論證，強度只等於它背後那組劑量反應資料。"],"method":"Sample: all 106 team dossiers in research/teams/, one per decorated team — every 2026 Top 10 team, special-prize winner and nominee. This is not the competition at large and nothing here describes undecorated teams. Counting: regular-expression sweeps for organism, strain, cell-line and light-control vocabulary across the English prose fields of each dossier (tagline, summary, dry, good, gemsTakeaway, award list), then every hit read in its surrounding sentence and classified by hand. Gene donor organisms, surrogate test organisms, rejected alternatives, modelling references (iML1515, iBsu1147) and education-activity mentions were excluded, which removed roughly a third of raw matches — \"laccase\" matches CcaS and \"Jaccard\" matches CcaR, so the unverified counts were wrong by several teams in both directions. A team is counted once per chassis category, so the table sums above 106: 18 teams used more than one chassis. Cloning and propagation hosts are counted where named. The B. subtilis count includes BGI-College, who cultivated a commercial strain without engineering it, and excludes HangzhouFourteenAP, who used it only as a surrogate biofilm organism in an assay. The light count includes William & Mary, who measured dark and light curves on a pre-existing light-responsive circuit although optogenetics was not their subject, and excludes Marburg, who investigated optogenetic induction in human practices and did not build it, and McMaster-Canada, whose only match was a blue-light transilluminator used for imaging. The placing test compares Top 10 placement against everything else using a two-sided Fisher exact test. What this cannot see: the dossiers are summaries of wikis, not the wikis themselves, so a chassis a team used but did not write up is invisible to this count. 12 teams describe wet-lab work whose host organism appears nowhere in their file; they are counted as \"not stated\" rather than assigned to E. coli, even though E. coli is the likely answer for most of them. The E. coli figure of 51 is therefore a floor, not a ceiling, and the same applies to every other category. Strain-naming counts reflect what the dossier records, not what the team's wiki or notebook may contain.","method_zh":"樣本：research/teams/ 底下全部 106 份隊伍資料，每支得獎隊伍一份——涵蓋 2026 年所有 Top 10 隊伍、特別獎得主與入圍者。這不是整個賽事的樣本，本篇任何一句話都不描述未得獎的隊伍。計數方式：以正規表達式在每份資料的英文敘述欄位（tagline、summary、dry、good、gemsTakeaway、獎項清單）掃過生物名、菌株名、細胞株名與光控相關詞彙，再把每一筆命中放回它所在的句子逐一人工判讀分類。基因來源生物、作為替代受測對象的生物、被否決的替代方案、建模用的參考資料（iML1515、iBsu1147）以及教育活動中的提及一律排除，這大約刪掉了三分之一的原始命中：「laccase」會命中 CcaS、「Jaccard」會命中 CcaR，未經查核的數字在兩個方向上都錯了好幾支隊伍。每支隊伍在每個底盤類別只計一次，因此表格總和超過 106：有 18 支隊伍用了不只一種底盤。具名的選殖與增殖宿主也計入。B. subtilis 的計數包含 BGI-College（只培養市售菌株而未改造），並排除 HangzhouFourteenAP（僅在試驗中作為生物膜的替代菌種）。光的計數包含 William & Mary（他們量了一組既有光反應迴路的暗處與光照曲線，雖然光遺傳學並非其主題），排除 Marburg（在人類實踐中研究過光誘導但沒有動手做）與 McMaster-Canada（唯一命中是用於成像的藍光透照台）。名次檢定以是否進入 Top 10 作為結果變項，採雙尾 Fisher 精確檢定。這份計數看不到什麼：這些資料是對維基的摘要，而不是維基本身，因此一支隊伍用過但沒有寫出來的底盤，在這裡是隱形的。有 12 支隊伍描述了濕實驗室工作，卻在整份資料中都沒有出現宿主生物；它們被計為「未交代」而不是歸給 E. coli，即使多數的答案很可能就是 E. coli。因此 51 這個 E. coli 數字是下限而不是上限，其他每一個類別也一樣。菌株命名的統計反映的是資料裡記了什麼，而不是該隊維基或實驗記錄裡可能有什麼。"},{"id":"hardware-afterlife","tab":"drylab","order":38,"kicker":"Original analysis","kicker_zh":"原創分析","title":"Can anyone rebuild the hardware?","title_zh":"這些硬體，別人做得出來嗎？","lede":"Of 20 instruments built by the 2026 Best Hardware, Best Measurement and Best Alternative Platform cohorts, 6 publish enough for a stranger in another country to rebuild them. Nine publish no geometry file at all. One has ever been used by someone outside the team that built it.","lede_zh":"2026 年 Best Hardware、Best Measurement 與 Best Alternative Platform 這三組隊伍總共做出 20 台儀器，其中只有 6 台公開的資料足以讓另一個國家的陌生人重建出來。有 9 台完全沒有釋出任何幾何檔案。而真正被原團隊以外的人用過的，只有 1 台。","body":"**Six of twenty.** That is how many award-winning iGEM 2026 instruments a stranger could actually rebuild: NCKU-Tainan's CAPTURE-Screen fluorescence reader, Lambert-GA's Vapor-X vacuum dryer, UNILausanne's C.L.A.W. LAMP incubator, Hongwen School's BrewXOS Fermenter Mini, TU Darmstadt's anaerobic chamber trio, and GEMS-Taiwan's four ReLEAF devices. Two more — Princeton's gyroid biofilter and CalPolySLO's emulsification washboard — are single printed parts where an STL plus print settings is the whole deliverable, which takes the generous count to eight. Everything else is missing at least one thing a second builder cannot do without.\n\nThe sister analysis of software found that every repository was populated, because iGEM mandates a GitLab deposit, and that the thing separating live tools from dead ones was a hosting decision. Hardware has no such floor. **There is no `2026/hardware` group on gitlab.igem.org at all** — the API returns 404 for it while `2026/software` returns a group called Software. Every hardware release in this cohort is improvised: a sub-project filed under `/software/`, a personal GitHub account, an Onshape link, a Google Drive folder, or loose files on the wiki's asset store. Nothing in the competition ever asks a hardware team to press Export.\n\nAnd pressing Export is exactly the separating habit. The teams you cannot rebuild from are not lazy and their CAD is not missing — it is visibly, beautifully *rendered*. Cornell's Best Hardware winner has an exploded view of the Arachne electrospinner and a bill of materials so good it names Analog Technologies' AHV24V30KVR5MAW at $419.00 across 40 priced line items totalling $1,213.35 — and then says, in the present tense of a page that will not change again, \"we plan to provide a bill of materials, CAD files, circuit diagrams, assembly documentation, and an operation manual.\" Two PDFs went up; no CAD file, no schematic file and no firmware ever did. CAU-China's OptiX phone spectrometer has an interactive exploded CAD view with numbered, clickable components and the most careful calibration chain in the whole cohort — and not one downloadable file, not one priced part, on a $12–30 instrument whose entire pitch is that anyone can have one. NU Boston published CAD drawings with dimensions and tolerances as figures. UBC-Vancouver published `.glb` meshes, a render format. In every one of these cases the model exists; it simply never left the design tool in a format anyone else can open.\n\nThe six that cleared the bar all did one unglamorous thing: they wrote the build as a document with files attached, not a page with pictures attached. NCKU-Tainan's MIT-licensed repo holds 225 files — 75 STEP exports, 59 STLs, the parametric CadQuery Python they were generated from, an ESP32 sketch with its own AS7341 driver, a bill-of-materials CSV and a 12-step assembly order that a second builder checked against the real machine. Its costing is the most honest number in the census: US$160.62 for the printed build, broken down to the print-shop receipt, with the line \"an estimate, not an account\" and the NT$31.68/US$1 rate it was converted at. Lambert-GA shipped Gerbers, a drill file, a JLCPCB pick-and-place CSV and a BOM keyed to LCSC part numbers, so the board can be ordered without a human in the loop. UNILausanne's C.L.A.W. costs under CHF 10, ships five STLs and a 3.8 MB manual, and includes the calibration that matters: a thermometer in the tube bore reads about 10 °C above the display, so the thermostat is set to 52.5 °C, preheated ten minutes, and holds 62.7 ± 1.2 °C over 30 minutes across three runs.\n\nTwo links fail the moment you check them rather than read them. Toronto's bioreactor page points at a Google Drive folder called \"Bioreactor CAD Files\"; opened signed-out it shows the folder name, no files, and a prompt to sign in — so the CAD for a $204 CAD bioreactor is, in practice, unavailable, while the firmware beside it is public and Apache-2.0. HongKong-JSS does the opposite: its Onshape document loads for anyone, 28 parts and a full feature tree, while `github.com/hkjssplkchc2026/mercurysense` — the firmware, the C12880 spectrometer driver and the acquisition instructions, as named on their own wiki — returns 404, and that GitHub account has no public repositories at all. Costs deserve the same scepticism. NU Boston's FLARE leads with \"as low as $300 vs $10,000\", then publishes two bills of materials totalling $499.80 and $344.18, **neither of which contains the Raspberry Pi 5 or the Arduino that run the instrument**. By contrast HongKong-JSS states plainly that its USD 357 build missed the USD 40 its stakeholders asked for, and TU Darmstadt records that the oxygen sensor is 83% of its €114.60 monitor.\n\nOutside use is bleaker than it was for software. Across every hardware repository checked the fork count is zero and the star count is zero, with one exception: Bist-China's seven STLs on GitHub have two stars — and no licence file, so nobody may legally reuse them. The single genuine case of a device leaving its makers is Lambert-GA's, and it is a high-school team: they shipped Vapor-X to the Biochemical Genetics Laboratory at the University of Alabama at Birmingham, where John Moore measured 38 of 43 compounds recovered within 5% of undried controls, and to the Styczynski Lab at Georgia Tech, which checked GFP fluorescence after drying DNA and lysates. Both labs' raw data are downloadable. **One team in twenty asked an outsider to use the thing, and the one that did was the one with Gerbers.**","body_zh":"**二十台裡有六台。** 這是 2026 年得獎儀器中，陌生人真的做得出來的數量：NCKU-Tainan 的 CAPTURE-Screen 螢光判讀儀、Lambert-GA 的 Vapor-X 真空乾燥機、UNILausanne 的 C.L.A.W. LAMP 恆溫器、Hongwen School 的 BrewXOS Fermenter Mini、TU Darmstadt 的三件厭氧套件，以及 GEMS-Taiwan 的四台 ReLEAF 裝置。另有兩件——Princeton 的 gyroid 生物濾材與 CalPolySLO 的乳化搓板——本身就是單一列印件，一個 STL 加上列印參數就是全部交付物，寬鬆算來可以湊到八台。其餘每一台，都至少缺了第二個製作者非有不可的某樣東西。\n\n軟體那篇姊妹分析發現：每一個儲存庫都有實質內容，因為 iGEM 強制要求把原始碼存進 GitLab；真正決定工具生死的，是一個關於架站的決定。硬體沒有這道底線。**gitlab.igem.org 上根本沒有 `2026/hardware` 這個群組**——API 對它回 404，而 `2026/software` 回的是一個名為 Software 的群組。這批隊伍的硬體釋出全是各自想辦法：掛在 `/software/` 底下的子專案、個人 GitHub 帳號、一條 Onshape 連結、一個 Google Drive 資料夾，或是散落在 wiki 靜態檔案區的零散檔案。整場比賽從來沒有任何一個環節，要求硬體隊伍按下「匯出」。\n\n而「按下匯出」正是那個分水嶺習慣。那些你重建不了的隊伍，並不是偷懶，他們的 CAD 也沒有不見——而是被漂漂亮亮地「算圖」成了圖片。Cornell 這支 Best Hardware 冠軍隊，有一張 Arachne 靜電紡絲機的爆炸圖，還有一份好到會寫出 Analog Technologies AHV24V30KVR5MAW、單價 $419.00 的物料清單，40 個逐項報價的品項合計 $1,213.35——然後，在一個不會再更動的頁面上，用現在式寫著：「我們計畫提供物料清單、CAD 檔案、電路圖、組裝文件與操作手冊。」最後上傳的是兩份 PDF；沒有任何一個 CAD 檔、電路圖檔或韌體。CAU-China 的 OptiX 手機光譜儀有一張可點選、元件逐一編號的互動式爆炸 CAD 視圖，校正鏈也是整批隊伍中做得最細的——卻連一個可下載的檔案、一項標價的零件都沒有，而這台儀器的全部訴求，就是 $12 到 $30、人人都能有一台。NU Boston 把標注尺寸與公差的 CAD 圖當成插圖發表。UBC-Vancouver 發表的是 `.glb`，一種算圖用的格式。上述每一個案例，模型都存在；它只是從來沒有以別人打得開的格式離開過設計軟體。\n\n過關的那六支，都做了同一件不起眼的事：他們把製作過程寫成一份附帶檔案的文件，而不是一個附帶圖片的網頁。NCKU-Tainan 以 MIT 授權的儲存庫裡有 225 個檔案——75 個 STEP 匯出檔、59 個 STL、生成這些檔案的參數化 CadQuery Python、一支自帶 AS7341 驅動程式的 ESP32 韌體、一份物料清單 CSV，以及一份由第二位製作者對照實機核對過的 12 步組裝順序。它的成本估算是這份普查中最誠實的數字：3D 列印版 US$160.62，拆到列印店的收據，並附上「這是估算，不是帳目」這句話，以及換算所用的 NT$31.68 兌 US$1 匯率。Lambert-GA 釋出了 Gerber 檔、鑽孔檔、JLCPCB 貼片座標 CSV，以及一份以 LCSC 料號編寫的物料清單，所以這塊板子可以在沒有人介入的情況下直接下單。UNILausanne 的 C.L.A.W. 成本不到 CHF 10，附五個 STL 與一份 3.8 MB 的手冊，而且寫進了真正關鍵的校正：把溫度計直接插進試管孔，讀到的溫度比面板顯示高約 10 °C，所以恆溫器設在 52.5 °C、預熱十分鐘，三次獨立測試中 30 分鐘內維持在 62.7 ± 1.2 °C。\n\n有兩條連結，只要去點它、而不是去讀它，就當場失效。Toronto 的生物反應器頁面指向一個名為「Bioreactor CAD Files」的 Google Drive 資料夾；未登入開啟時只看得到資料夾名稱、沒有任何檔案，還跳出要你登入的提示——所以這台 204 加幣生物反應器的 CAD，實際上拿不到，而旁邊的韌體卻是公開的 Apache-2.0。HongKong-JSS 則剛好相反：它的 Onshape 文件任何人都開得起來，28 個零件、完整特徵樹俱在，但他們自己 wiki 上寫明收著韌體、C12880 光譜儀驅動程式與擷取說明的 `github.com/hkjssplkchc2026/mercurysense` 回應 404，而且那個 GitHub 帳號底下一個公開儲存庫也沒有。成本同樣值得用一樣的懷疑去看。NU Boston 的 FLARE 以「低至 $300，相對於 $10,000」開場，接著公開了兩份物料清單，合計分別是 $499.80 與 $344.18，**而兩份都沒有放進驅動這台儀器的 Raspberry Pi 5 或 Arduino**。相對地，HongKong-JSS 直白寫出他們 USD 357 的製作成本沒有達到利害關係人要求的 USD 40，TU Darmstadt 也記下氧氣感測器佔了那台 €114.60 監測器的 83%。\n\n至於外部使用，情況比軟體那邊更慘。所有被檢查過的硬體儲存庫，分支數都是零、星星數也都是零，只有一個例外：Bist-China 放在 GitHub 上的七個 STL 有兩顆星——卻沒有授權條款檔案，所以沒有人可以合法地拿去用。唯一一個儀器真正離開製作者手中的案例來自 Lambert-GA，而且是一支高中隊伍：他們把 Vapor-X 寄到 University of Alabama at Birmingham 的 Biochemical Genetics Laboratory，由 John Moore 量得 43 個化合物中有 38 個的回收率落在未乾燥對照組的 5% 以內；也寄到 Georgia Tech 的 Styczynski Lab，由他們檢查 DNA 與細胞裂解液乾燥後的 GFP 螢光。兩間實驗室的原始資料都可以下載。**二十支隊伍中只有一支請外人實際用過自己的東西，而做到這件事的，正是那支連 Gerber 檔都備齊的隊伍。**","cards":[{"kicker":"Best in class","kicker_zh":"同類最佳","title":"Vapor-X — the only device an outsider has used","title_zh":"Vapor-X——唯一有外人用過的裝置","body":"Lambert-GA's $80.07 vacuum dryer (a Mason jar, a 12 V pump, a polyimide heater and a Raspberry Pi Pico W on a custom PCB) is the only instrument in this cohort with third-party evidence. The team shipped it to the Biochemical Genetics Laboratory at the University of Alabama at Birmingham, where John Moore recovered 38 of 43 measured compounds within 5% of undried controls, and to the Styczynski Lab at Georgia Tech for GFP fluorescence after drying. The release matches: three STLs, a complete Gerber and drill set, a JLCPCB pick-and-place CSV, a BOM keyed to LCSC part numbers, MicroPython firmware under Apache-2.0, and an 8.5 MB construction manual. It is the only release here that a board house could execute without a human reading the wiki.","body_zh":"Lambert-GA 這台 $80.07 的真空乾燥機（一只梅森罐、一顆 12 V 真空幫浦、一片聚醯亞胺加熱片，以及一塊自製 PCB 上的 Raspberry Pi Pico W），是這批隊伍中唯一有第三方證據的儀器。團隊把它寄到 University of Alabama at Birmingham 的 Biochemical Genetics Laboratory，由 John Moore 測得 43 個化合物中有 38 個回收率落在未乾燥對照組的 5% 以內；也寄到 Georgia Tech 的 Styczynski Lab，檢查乾燥後的 GFP 螢光。釋出的內容也相稱：三個 STL、一整套 Gerber 與鑽孔檔、一份 JLCPCB 貼片座標 CSV、一份以 LCSC 料號編寫的物料清單、以 Apache-2.0 授權的 MicroPython 韌體，以及一份 8.5 MB 的製作手冊。這是此處唯一一份板廠不必有人去讀 wiki 就能直接施工的釋出。","chips":["rebuildable","Lambert-GA","high school","Gerbers + CPL","tested at 2 outside labs"],"chips_zh":["可重建","Lambert-GA","高中","Gerbers + CPL","2 間外部實驗室測過"],"link":"https://gitlab.igem.org/2026/software/lambert-ga/vapor-x","linkText":"Vapor-X files on iGEM GitLab"},{"kicker":"The fullest file set","kicker_zh":"最完整的檔案組","title":"NCKU-Tainan shipped the source, not just the export","title_zh":"NCKU-Tainan 釋出的是原始檔，不只是匯出檔","body":"225 files under MIT: 75 STEP assemblies, 59 STLs covering 66 printed pieces across two builds, and the parametric CadQuery Python the geometry was generated from — so another team can change a dimension rather than reprint yours. Alongside it sit an ESP32 sketch with its own AS7341 driver, a bill-of-materials CSV, a bench schematic with measured values, and working sensor settings (AGAIN 512x, ATIME 255, ASTEP 280). The costing is itemised by basis — print-shop receipts, costing sheet, distributor list prices — totals US$160.62 for the printed build and US$53.70 for the laser-cut one, and is labelled \"an estimate, not an account\". They also publish what failed: the laser-cut build could not tell the AHL sensor strain from cells without sfGFP.","body_zh":"以 MIT 授權釋出的 225 個檔案：75 個 STEP 組件、涵蓋兩個版本共 66 個列印件的 59 個 STL，以及生成這些幾何的參數化 CadQuery Python——所以別的隊伍可以改尺寸，而不是只能照著你的檔案重印。旁邊還放著一支自帶 AS7341 驅動程式的 ESP32 韌體、一份物料清單 CSV、一張標有實測值的電路圖，以及可用的感測器設定（AGAIN 512x、ATIME 255、ASTEP 280）。成本逐項標明依據——列印店收據、自家成本表、經銷商牌價——3D 列印版合計 US$160.62、雷射切割版 US$53.70，並註明「這是估算，不是帳目」。他們也把失敗寫出來：雷射切割版分不出 AHL 感測菌株與不帶 sfGFP 的細胞。","chips":["rebuildable","NCKU-Tainan","75 STEP + 59 STL","parametric source","MIT"],"chips_zh":["可重建","NCKU-Tainan","75 STEP + 59 STL","參數化原始檔","MIT"],"link":"https://gitlab.igem.org/2026/software/ncku-tainan/capture-screen-hardware","linkText":"capture-screen-hardware"},{"kicker":"The gap between page and file","kicker_zh":"頁面與檔案之間的落差","title":"The Best Hardware winner published no CAD at all","title_zh":"Best Hardware 冠軍隊一個 CAD 檔都沒有釋出","body":"Cornell's Arachne electrospinner won Best Hardware (Undergraduate) with a genuinely excellent bill of materials — 40 priced line items in three groups, from the $419.00 Analog Technologies AHV24V30KVR5MAW 30 kV supply to $0.08 M5 screws, subtotals $681.76 / $416.87 / $114.72, total $1,213.35 — and a fabrication-and-assembly guide and safety manual that both download. What never appeared is the geometry: no STL, no STEP, no circuit schematic file and no ESP32 firmware anywhere on the hardware, circuitry, encasement or contribution pages. The page still carries the sentence \"we plan to provide a bill of materials, CAD files, circuit diagrams, assembly documentation, and an operation manual.\" Half of that shipped.","body_zh":"Cornell 的 Arachne 靜電紡絲機拿下大學組 Best Hardware，物料清單做得確實出色——三個群組、40 個標價品項，從 $419.00 的 Analog Technologies AHV24V30KVR5MAW 30 kV 高壓模組，到 $0.08 的 M5 螺絲，小計分別是 $681.76／$416.87／$114.72，總計 $1,213.35——製作組裝指南與安全手冊兩份 PDF 也都下載得到。始終沒有出現的是幾何檔：hardware、circuitry、encasement 與 contribution 四個頁面上，沒有任何 STL、STEP、電路圖檔或 ESP32 韌體。頁面上到現在還寫著：「我們計畫提供物料清單、CAD 檔案、電路圖、組裝文件與操作手冊。」兌現的是其中一半。","chips":["not rebuildable","Cornell","BOM $1,213.35","no CAD","no firmware"],"chips_zh":["無法重建","Cornell","物料清單 $1,213.35","沒有 CAD","沒有韌體"],"link":"https://2026.igem.wiki/cornell/hardware","linkText":"Cornell hardware page"},{"kicker":"Check the link, not the sentence","kicker_zh":"要點連結，不要只看句子","title":"An empty Drive folder and a 404 repository","title_zh":"一個空的 Drive 資料夾，和一個 404 的儲存庫","body":"Toronto's hardware page links a Google Drive folder named \"Bioreactor CAD Files\". Opened without a Google account it renders the folder title, lists nothing, and asks you to sign in — so the CAD for its $204 CAD, 96-unit bioreactor array is effectively unavailable, while the firmware next to it is public under Apache-2.0 and the BOM and assembly PDFs both download. HongKong-JSS has the mirror-image failure: its Onshape document is genuinely public (28 parts, full feature tree, view-only) but github.com/hkjssplkchc2026/mercurysense — named on its own wiki as holding the ESP32 firmware, the Hamamatsu C12880 driver and the acquisition instructions — returns 404, and the account has zero public repositories. Only its extraction-unit firmware survived, on a different personal account, with licence \"NOASSERTION\".","body_zh":"Toronto 的硬體頁面連到一個名為「Bioreactor CAD Files」的 Google Drive 資料夾。在沒有 Google 帳號的情況下開啟，只顯示資料夾標題、列不出任何檔案，並要求你登入——所以那台 204 加幣、可達 96 組的生物反應器陣列的 CAD，實際上拿不到，而旁邊的韌體卻以 Apache-2.0 公開，物料清單與組裝說明兩份 PDF 也都下載得到。HongKong-JSS 則是鏡像般的另一種失敗：它的 Onshape 文件確實公開（28 個零件、完整特徵樹、唯讀），但他們自己 wiki 上寫明收著 ESP32 韌體、Hamamatsu C12880 驅動程式與擷取說明的 github.com/hkjssplkchc2026/mercurysense 回應 404，而那個帳號底下一個公開儲存庫也沒有。活下來的只有萃取單元的韌體，放在另一個個人帳號上，授權條款標示為「NOASSERTION」。","chips":["broken","Toronto","HongKong-JSS","Drive sign-in wall","GitHub 404"],"chips_zh":["壞掉","Toronto","HongKong-JSS","Drive 擋在登入牆後","GitHub 404"],"link":"https://2026.igem.wiki/toronto/hardware/","linkText":"Toronto hardware page"},{"kicker":"Costs that do not add up","kicker_zh":"兜不攏的成本","title":"The computer is missing from the bill of materials","title_zh":"物料清單裡少了那台電腦","body":"NU Boston's FLARE soil chamber leads with \"a build cost of as low as $300 vs. $10,000\" and then publishes two bills of materials: $499.80 for the entire system and $344.18 for the UV module. Neither total includes the Raspberry Pi 5 that runs the imaging, the Arduino that drives the pumps, the printed and laser-cut enclosure, or the tubing — the module BOM lists a \"Raspberry Pi 5 breakout board, $7.50\" but not the Pi. So the headline is below both published totals, and both published totals are below the real one. Compare HongKong-JSS, which states outright that its USD 357 core-component build overshot the USD 40 its stakeholders asked for, and TU Darmstadt, which notes that the sensor alone is 83% of its €114.60 oxygen monitor.","body_zh":"NU Boston 的 FLARE 土壤模擬艙以「製作成本低至 $300，相對於 $10,000」開場，接著公開了兩份物料清單：整套系統 $499.80、UV 模組 $344.18。兩份總計都沒有包含負責成像的 Raspberry Pi 5、驅動幫浦的 Arduino、列印與雷射切割的機殼，也沒有管路——模組清單裡列了「Raspberry Pi 5 擴展板，$7.50」，卻沒有那台 Pi。於是，標題數字低於兩份公開總計，而兩份公開總計又都低於真實成本。對照之下，HongKong-JSS 直接寫明他們 USD 357 的核心元件成本超出利害關係人要求的 USD 40，TU Darmstadt 也註明光是感測器就佔了那台 €114.60 氧氣監測器的 83%。","chips":["cost credibility","NU Boston","$300 headline","$499.80 BOM","no Pi in the list"],"chips_zh":["成本可信度","NU Boston","標題寫 $300","物料清單 $499.80","清單裡沒有 Pi"],"link":"https://2026.igem.wiki/nu-boston/hardware","linkText":"NU Boston hardware page"},{"kicker":"GEMS-Taiwan, on the same terms","kicker_zh":"以同一把尺衡量 GEMS-Taiwan","title":"Eighteen STLs, six manuals — and meshes instead of models","title_zh":"十八個 STL、六本手冊——但給的是網格，不是模型","body":"GEMS-Taiwan clears the bar, and it is worth being precise about how narrowly. On the credit side: 18 STL files that download (verified, served as model/stl), six assembly guides of 10 to 16 pages for the bioreactor, both photometers and the light plate, a user manual and brochure, a 6.8 MB hardware notebook covering 23 March to 17 October, print settings recorded next to the files (Bambu Lab X1 Carbon, 0.2 mm, 20% gyroid, PLA Matte with TPU 95A cuvette slots), a published SiO2 OD600 calibration, and CC BY 4.0 on everything. Against: the files are STL meshes, not STEP or parametric source, so a second team can print the photometer but not change its light path; the costs are totals (NT$16,450 in parts; about US$360 for the photometer against roughly US$15,000 for the benchtop instrument it replaces) rather than a priced line-item table; and of the four devices only the reactor rig's sketch.ino is in the MIT digital-twin repo — the photometer and LPA firmware were never released as source. Nobody outside the team has built one.","body_zh":"GEMS-Taiwan 過了標準，但值得把「只是剛好過」說清楚。可記上一筆的是：18 個確認可下載的 STL 檔（已驗證，以 model/stl 提供）、生物反應器、兩台光度計與光板各自 10 到 16 頁的六本組裝指南、一本使用手冊與一本型錄、一本涵蓋 3 月 23 日到 10 月 17 日的 6.8 MB 硬體筆記、與檔案並列的列印參數（Bambu Lab X1 Carbon、0.2 mm、20% gyroid 填充、本體 PLA Matte、比色管槽 TPU 95A）、一份公開的 SiO2 OD600 校正文件，以及全部採用 CC BY 4.0。要扣分的是：釋出的是 STL 網格，不是 STEP 也不是參數化原始檔，所以別的隊伍印得出這台光度計，卻改不動它的光路；成本給的是總數（零件 NT$16,450；光度計約 US$360，對照它所取代的約 US$15,000 桌上型儀器），而不是逐項標價的表格；四台裝置裡也只有反應器控制端的 sketch.ino 放進了 MIT 授權的 digital-twin 儲存庫——光度計與 LPA 的韌體從未以原始碼形式釋出。團隊以外，沒有人做過一台。","chips":["rebuildable, narrowly","GEMS-Taiwan","18 STL","CC BY 4.0","no STEP, no priced BOM"],"chips_zh":["勉強可重建","GEMS-Taiwan","18 STL","CC BY 4.0","沒有 STEP，物料清單沒標價"],"link":"https://2026.igem.wiki/gems-taiwan/contribution/","linkText":"ReLEAF hardware files"}],"table":{"head":["Team","Device","Design files you can download","Cost published","Firmware + licence","Rebuildable?"],"head_zh":["隊伍","裝置","可下載的設計檔","公開的成本","韌體與授權","做得出來嗎？"],"rows":[["Lambert-GA","Vapor-X vacuum dryer","3 STL + Gerbers + drill + CPL CSV","$80.07 / $95.52 assembled","MicroPython, Apache-2.0","yes — used by 2 outside labs"],["NCKU-Tainan","CAPTURE-Screen reader","75 STEP, 59 STL, CadQuery source","US$160.62 / US$53.70","ESP32 sketch, MIT","yes"],["UNILausanne","C.L.A.W. LAMP incubator","5 STL + 3.8 MB manual","under CHF 10","none needed (thermostat module)","yes"],["Hongwen School","BrewXOS Fermenter Mini","8.56 MB STEP assembly","about 3,480 RMB","Arduino, published as a PDF","yes"],["TU Darmstadt","Anaerobic chamber, O2 monitor, shaker","none — built from a stock container","EUR 134.30 / 114.60 / 68.08","sketches printed in full, CC BY 4.0","yes"],["GEMS-Taiwan","Bioreactor, 2 photometers, LPA, hydroponics","18 STL (meshes only)","NT$16,450; photometer ~US$360","1 of 4 devices, MIT","yes, narrowly"],["Princeton","Gyroid biofilter cartridge","2 STL + print parameters","n/a (printed part)","n/a","yes (single part)"],["CalPolySLO","Emulsification washboard + sled","2 STL via Google Drive","about $15","n/a","yes (single part)"],["KAUST-KSA","SHIHAB suitcase bioreactor","CAD drawings as a 5.5 MB PDF","BOM PDF, no headline figure","45 KB Arduino sketch (served as .js)","almost — no geometry file"],["HK League","Converted hydrogel bioprinter","3 STL zips","about US$400, not itemised","BioPrintCAD, Apache-2.0","almost — no priced BOM"],["UBC-Vancouver","Fluorescence detector, bioreactor, chip",".glb meshes + drawing PDFs","CAD 204.48 (detector)","not published","almost — no source files"],["HongKong-JSS","MerMAID detection + extraction units","Onshape public, 28 parts","USD ~357 (target was USD 40)","detection repo 404; extraction NOASSERTION","no — firmware gone"],["Toronto","96-unit parallel bioreactor array","Drive folder lists nothing signed-out","$204 CAD per reactor","7 sketches + dashboard, Apache-2.0","no — CAD unreachable"],["Bist-China","PyrLac POCT reader","7 STL on GitHub (2 stars)","about $77, itemised","sketches, no licence file","no — no licence, no guide"],["Cornell","Arachne electrospinner","none","$1,213.35, 40 line items","not published","no"],["NU Boston","FLARE soil chamber","none","$499.80 / $344.18, Pi excluded","not published","no"],["CAU-China","OptiX phone spectrometer","none","\"$12-30\", not itemised","FSSA + MycoSpec, Apache-2.0","no"],["SDU-Denmark","Microbial fuel cell + Arduino logger","parts-list PDF only","not costed","logger code not published","no"],["McMaster-Canada","OMV bioreactor + microfluidic device","CFD result CSVs only","none","none","no"],["Labi-Taiwan","ESP32 electrochemical reader","none","none","none","no"]],"rows_zh":[["Lambert-GA","Vapor-X 真空乾燥機","3 個 STL＋Gerber＋鑽孔檔＋貼片 CSV","$80.07／含組裝 $95.52","MicroPython，Apache-2.0","可以——兩間外部實驗室用過"],["NCKU-Tainan","CAPTURE-Screen 判讀儀","75 個 STEP、59 個 STL、CadQuery 原始檔","US$160.62／US$53.70","ESP32 韌體，MIT","可以"],["UNILausanne","C.L.A.W. LAMP 恆溫器","5 個 STL＋3.8 MB 手冊","不到 CHF 10","不需要（用恆溫模組）","可以"],["Hongwen School","BrewXOS Fermenter Mini","8.56 MB 的 STEP 組件","約 3,480 RMB","Arduino，以 PDF 形式發表","可以"],["TU Darmstadt","厭氧操作箱、氧氣監測器、振盪器","無——以市售容器改裝","EUR 134.30／114.60／68.08","程式碼完整印在頁面上，CC BY 4.0","可以"],["GEMS-Taiwan","生物反應器、兩台光度計、LPA、水耕板","18 個 STL（僅網格）","NT$16,450；光度計約 US$360","四台中只有一台，MIT","勉強可以"],["Princeton","Gyroid 生物濾材","2 個 STL＋列印參數","不適用（單一列印件）","不適用","可以（單一零件）"],["CalPolySLO","乳化搓板與橡皮筋滑座","2 個 STL，放在 Google Drive","約 $15","不適用","可以（單一零件）"],["KAUST-KSA","SHIHAB 手提箱式生物反應器","CAD 圖，5.5 MB 的 PDF","有物料清單 PDF，無公開總價","45 KB Arduino 韌體（以 .js 提供）","差一點——沒有幾何檔"],["HK League","改裝的水膠生物列印機","3 個 STL 壓縮檔","約 US$400，未逐項列出","BioPrintCAD，Apache-2.0","差一點——沒有標價物料清單"],["UBC-Vancouver","螢光偵測器、生物反應器、晶片",".glb 網格＋工程圖 PDF","CAD 204.48（偵測器）","未釋出","差一點——沒有原始檔"],["HongKong-JSS","MerMAID 偵測與萃取單元","Onshape 公開，28 個零件","USD 約 357（目標是 USD 40）","偵測端儲存庫 404；萃取端 NOASSERTION","不行——韌體不見了"],["Toronto","96 組平行生物反應器陣列","未登入時 Drive 資料夾列不出檔案","每台 204 加幣","7 支韌體＋儀表板，Apache-2.0","不行——CAD 拿不到"],["Bist-China","PyrLac 定點照護判讀儀","GitHub 上 7 個 STL（2 顆星）","約 $77，有逐項列出","有韌體，但沒有授權條款檔","不行——無授權、無組裝指南"],["Cornell","Arachne 靜電紡絲機","無","$1,213.35，40 個品項","未釋出","不行"],["NU Boston","FLARE 土壤模擬艙","無","$499.80／$344.18，未含 Pi","未釋出","不行"],["CAU-China","OptiX 手機光譜儀","無","「$12-30」，未逐項列出","FSSA 與 MycoSpec，Apache-2.0","不行"],["SDU-Denmark","微生物燃料電池與 Arduino 記錄器","只有零件清單 PDF","未估價","記錄器程式碼未釋出","不行"],["McMaster-Canada","OMV 生物反應器與微流體裝置","只有 CFD 結果 CSV","無","無","不行"],["Labi-Taiwan","ESP32 電化學判讀儀","無","無","無","不行"]]},"checklist":["Export every part to STEP as well as STL before the wiki freeze. ReLEAF ships 18 STL meshes; a mesh prints but cannot be edited, so nobody can move the photometer's light path. NCKU-Tainan shipped 75 STEP files plus the CadQuery source that generated them.","Publish one itemised bill of materials per device — supplier, part number, quantity, unit price, extended price, subtotal — not a total. Cornell's 40-row table is the model to copy even though Cornell published no CAD; ReLEAF currently gives NT$16,450 and about US$360 with the parts named only inside the assembly guides.","Put all four devices' firmware in the GitLab repo under MIT, not just the reactor rig's sketch.ino. If a file extension is blocked, do what KAUST-KSA did: upload the sketch as .js with a header telling the reader to save it as .ino.","Ship each device as one versioned archive — STEP, STL, BOM CSV, firmware, manual, LICENSE — instead of eighteen loose links on a contribution page. HK League's three zips with a per-file print count are the pattern.","Put the licence inside the bundle, not only in a sentence at the bottom of the page. Bist-China's seven STLs are the only hardware files in the cohort with any stars, and nobody may legally use them because there is no licence file.","Never host design files on Google Drive. Toronto's \"Bioreactor CAD Files\" folder shows a signed-out visitor nothing at all, which is indistinguishable from publishing nothing.","Write a calibration page per device and keep the honest number in it. The SiO2 OD600 calibration and the leaf-sensor +0.47 to +1.71 degC offset over 540 paired readings are exactly right; add the same for the LPA's per-LED output and the Pro-versus-Slim scale difference.","Cost the whole instrument, including the computer. NU Boston's two BOMs both omit the Raspberry Pi that runs the device; the GEMS cost sheet should state explicitly what the NT$16,450 does and does not cover.","Send one device to one outside laboratory, ask them to run something real, and publish their raw data. Lambert-GA is a high-school team and did this twice, at UAB and Georgia Tech — it is the only outside-use evidence in the entire cohort.","Re-check every hardware link a month after the Jamboree. HongKong-JSS's firmware repository was named on the wiki and is now a 404; a single curl would have caught it."],"checklist_zh":["在 wiki 凍結之前，把每個零件同時匯出成 STEP 與 STL。ReLEAF 給的是 18 個 STL 網格；網格印得出來，卻改不動，所以沒有人能調整光度計的光路。NCKU-Tainan 給的是 75 個 STEP，外加生成它們的 CadQuery 原始檔。","每台裝置公開一份逐項的物料清單——供應商、料號、數量、單價、小計金額、分組小計——而不是一個總數。Cornell 那張 40 列的表是值得照抄的範本，即使 Cornell 自己連 CAD 都沒放；ReLEAF 目前只給 NT$16,450 和約 US$360，零件名稱則埋在組裝指南裡。","把四台裝置的韌體都以 MIT 授權放進 GitLab 儲存庫，而不是只有反應器控制端的 sketch.ino。如果副檔名被擋，就照 KAUST-KSA 的做法：把韌體以 .js 上傳，並在開頭寫明請讀者另存為 .ino。","每台裝置打包成一個有版本的壓縮檔——STEP、STL、物料清單 CSV、韌體、手冊、LICENSE——而不是在 contribution 頁面上散落十八條連結。HK League 那三個附帶逐檔列印數量的壓縮檔就是範例。","把授權條款放進壓縮檔裡，不要只寫在頁面底部一句話。Bist-China 的七個 STL 是這批隊伍中唯一拿到星星的硬體檔案，但因為沒有授權條款檔，沒有人可以合法使用。","絕對不要把設計檔放在 Google Drive。Toronto 那個「Bioreactor CAD Files」資料夾對未登入的訪客什麼都不顯示，這和完全沒有公開沒有兩樣。","每台裝置寫一頁校正說明，而且把誠實的那個數字留在裡面。SiO2 OD600 校正，以及葉面感測器在 540 組配對讀數中 +0.47 到 +1.71 degC 的偏移，做法完全正確；LPA 的逐顆 LED 輸出、以及 Pro 與 Slim 之間的尺度差異，也該比照辦理。","把整台儀器的成本算進去，包含那台電腦。NU Boston 的兩份物料清單都漏掉了驅動裝置的 Raspberry Pi；GEMS 的成本表也該明講 NT$16,450 涵蓋與不涵蓋什麼。","把一台裝置寄給一間外部實驗室，請他們跑一件真實的實驗，並公開他們的原始資料。Lambert-GA 是一支高中隊伍，而且做了兩次，分別在 UAB 與 Georgia Tech——這是整批隊伍中唯一的外部使用證據。","Jamboree 結束一個月後，把每一條硬體連結重新檢查一遍。HongKong-JSS 的韌體儲存庫在 wiki 上寫得清清楚楚，現在卻是 404；一行 curl 就能抓到。"],"method":"Twenty instruments were graded: the fourteen Best Hardware winners and nominees across all three sections, plus the six Best Measurement and Best Alternative Platform teams that actually built a device (UNILausanne, Princeton, CalPolySLO, SDU-Denmark, McMaster-Canada, Labi-Taiwan). The remaining Measurement and Alternative Platform teams checked — William-and-Mary, XJTLU-China, WageningenUR, CHINAGuangdongShimen, HangzhouFourteenAP, Yucai-SZ, UOttawa, Marburg, BGI-College — released no instrument and are excluded from the base rate; William-and-Mary's hardware page is still an unfilled iGEM template. Each instrument was scored on seven checkable things: a bill of materials naming parts with prices or part numbers; a total cost and whether it is credible; geometry or electrical source files that actually download; firmware with a licence; an assembly guide a non-author could follow; a calibration or validation protocol; and any evidence of outside use. The pass bar was all of files, priced parts, an assembly guide and a validation protocol, plus firmware where the device needs it. Server-rendered wiki pages were read with curl; client-rendered React wikis were read either from their JavaScript bundles or in a browser — and the browser mattered: a stale deployed chunk on Hongwen School's site still contained the team's own unexecuted editorial placeholders where the CAD link should be, while the live page serves a working 8.56 MB STEP file, so bundle evidence was always confirmed in the browser before being treated as a finding. Every claimed download was fetched and its HTTP status, content type and byte size recorded; Google Drive and Onshape links were opened signed-out. Repositories were queried through the GitLab and GitHub APIs for file tree, licence, stars, forks and last activity. What could not be checked: the contents of bill-of-materials and assembly PDFs, because no PDF text extractor was available in this environment — those files were verified to exist, download and carry the right media type, and their line items were only quoted where the wiki page itself reproduces them. Nor can a link check tell you whether a device reads true, whether an assembly guide is actually followable, or whether anyone has quietly built one; zero stars and zero forks mean no public signal, not certainly no users.","method_zh":"共評分 20 台儀器：三個組別全部 14 支 Best Hardware 冠軍與入圍隊伍，加上 Best Measurement 與 Best Alternative Platform 中真的做出裝置的 6 支隊伍（UNILausanne、Princeton、CalPolySLO、SDU-Denmark、McMaster-Canada、Labi-Taiwan）。其餘被檢查過的 Measurement 與 Alternative Platform 隊伍——William-and-Mary、XJTLU-China、WageningenUR、CHINAGuangdongShimen、HangzhouFourteenAP、Yucai-SZ、UOttawa、Marburg、BGI-College——沒有釋出儀器，因此不計入比率；其中 William-and-Mary 的 hardware 頁面到現在仍是未填寫的 iGEM 範本。每台儀器就七件可查核的事評分：點名零件並附價格或料號的物料清單；總成本以及這個數字是否可信；真的下載得到的幾何或電路原始檔；附授權條款的韌體；非作者也跟得上的組裝指南；校正或驗證流程；以及任何外部使用的證據。通過門檻是：檔案、標價零件、組裝指南與驗證流程四者齊備，裝置若需要韌體則韌體也要有。伺服器端算繪的 wiki 頁面以 curl 讀取；用戶端算繪的 React wiki 則從其 JavaScript bundle 或直接在瀏覽器中讀取——而瀏覽器這一步很關鍵：Hongwen School 網站上一塊過時的已部署 bundle 裡，CAD 連結的位置仍留著團隊自己未執行的編輯備註，但實際上線的頁面提供的是一個可用的 8.56 MB STEP 檔，因此所有 bundle 證據在被當成結論之前，都先在瀏覽器中確認過。每一個宣稱可下載的檔案都實際抓取過，並記下 HTTP 狀態碼、內容型態與位元組大小；Google Drive 與 Onshape 連結都在未登入狀態下開啟。儲存庫則透過 GitLab 與 GitHub API 查詢檔案樹、授權條款、星星數、分支數與最後活動時間。查不到的部分：物料清單與組裝指南 PDF 的內文，因為這個環境沒有可用的 PDF 文字擷取工具——這些檔案只確認了存在、可下載、媒體型態正確，其中的品項只有在 wiki 頁面本身也列出時才被引用。此外，連結檢查也無法告訴你一台裝置讀數是否準確、一本組裝指南是否真的跟得上，或是否有人默默做過一台；零顆星與零個分支代表的是沒有公開訊號，不等於確定沒有使用者。"},{"id":"safety-practice","tab":"good","order":38,"kicker":"Original analysis","kicker_zh":"原創分析","title":"Nobody measured an escape rate","title_zh":"沒有人量過逃逸率","lede":"Zero of 106 decorated teams report a measured escape frequency. Nineteen built a containment device; three knew the metric well enough to say they had not measured it. The teams worth copying are the ones that turned a safety claim into a number, tested the safeguard until it broke, or gave up a design because the safety answer came back wrong.","lede_zh":"106 支獲獎隊伍中，有 0 支回報了實際量測的逃逸頻率。19 支做了生物圍堵裝置，3 支清楚到足以寫下「我們沒有量」。值得抄的，是那些把安全主張變成數字、把保險機制一路測到壞掉，或因為安全答案不對而放棄設計的隊伍。","body":"**The base rate first, because it sets the bar low.** Across the 106 decorated teams researched for this report, 19 describe a genetic containment device — a kill switch, an auxotrophy, a toxin–antitoxin pair. Four discuss dual use or misuse at all. Two name how their synthesised DNA was screened. And **zero report a measured escape frequency**, the one number that converts a containment claim into evidence. Two teams in the environmental cohort — **UCL** (6381) and **WageningenUR** (6222) — have no safety page in their site navigation at all, while proposing water treatment and drinking-water deployment respectively. The Safety and Security Award itself tells the same story: no nominees at all in the Overgrad and High School sections, only a winner. Almost nobody enters this category, and the ones who do are not competing against a crowd.\n\n**What a real safety page does that a recitation does not.** The recitation is: BSL-1, non-pathogenic chassis, a risk-group table, autoclave at 121 °C, gloves and closed-toe shoes. Everything on that list is true and none of it is about the project. The minority do one of five harder things. They convert the containment claim into a threshold and compare it against the receiving environment in the same units — **BASIS-China** (6123) measured its bile-acid suicide switch at a threshold of roughly **0.1–0.2 mM taurocholate**, then looked up feline duodenal bile salts at 15–42 mM, sewage total bile acids at 184–356 µg/L (which they convert to 4.7×10⁻⁴–9.1×10⁻⁴ mM) and 13.3 pmol/g deoxycholic acid in soil, and showed the gap. They test the safeguard until it fails — **William-and-Mary** (6243), the Undergrad winner, took a published triple-toxin kill switch off Addgene and ran it longitudinally; it was *the first of their circuits to lose function*, failing weeks before the others, and the entire project became an argument that kill switches need the failure analysis that bridges and aircraft already get. They measure non-target harm rather than asserting it — **Peking** (6366) screened its dsRNA in 21-nt sliding windows against RefSeq, found the longest uninterrupted match in any non-target homolog was **13 nt** (10–11 nt for the pharaoh ant), then actually expressed the ant's homologous fragments in S2 cells and measured relative expression of **1.22 and 1.30** after dsRNA treatment: no knockdown. They choose inactivation against the actual agent — **Bielefeld-CeBiTec** (6221) found that autoclaving and NaOH are of limited effect on α-synuclein fibrils, so they used 10% SDS *and* autoclaved, worked without preformed fibrils after asking the genetic engineering authority, and ran the lab on electronic access tokens with one-way transport and lab coats that never leave the culture room. And they publish an evidence ledger: a \"what our results establish\" column beside a \"what remains before real-world use\" column, which BASIS-China, Peking and IISER-Kolkata all do and most teams do not.\n\n**The escape-rate question has a clean answer, and it is zero.** The strongest teams know exactly what is missing. **IISER-Kolkata** (6450) writes it out: *\"the figure that matters for biocontainment is the escape frequency, i.e., the proportion of cells surviving induction... Values below 1 in 10⁸ cells are the benchmark used in the synthetic biology biocontainment literature. This has not been measured.\"* **UCSC** (6215) projects a **10⁻¹²** combined escape risk by multiplying a cited 10⁻⁶ per-plasmid transfer probability by itself, against a cited 10⁻⁸ standard — arithmetic, not measurement — and then says the honest thing about its own uracil auxotroph: the mutation is H99P, a single base substitution, *\"among the most readily reversible,\"* and *\"any containment claim based on this strain needs a measured reversion frequency, obtained by plating a large population on medium lacking uracil and counting the colonies that grow.\"* **Madrid-UCM** (6124) notes that the strongest engineered systems report undetectable escape near two parts in 10¹². What teams measured instead were kill assays: **NU Boston** (6300) invalidated its own OD₆₀₀ kill-switch readout after discovering CcdB induces filamentation, which changes light scattering, and moved to flow cytometry live/dead and CFU counts, showing a drop at 0.2% arabinose across the 10⁻⁵–10⁻⁷ dilutions. That is good practice, and it is still not an escape rate.\n\n**Three teams gave something up, and that is the strongest evidence in the category.** **Stockholm** (6292), the Overgrad winner, is verified: its own wiki records the largest change in the project as *\"Open municipal deployment was dropped for a contained bioreactor on a defined, concentrated stream, with physical containment in place of a kill switch.\"* The trigger was a named advisory board member, Gunaratna Kuttuva Rajarao, telling them wastewater plants are not closed systems, plants will not accept GMOs, and a kill switch alone would probably not be enough. The venture went with it: no company, no pricing, no customer, and the chassis they now point at for production is not even yeast. **Oxford** (6391) is the second case and states the cost out loud: they chose heat-inactivated yeast over a living *Snodgrassella alvi* gut symbiont for containment and regulatory reasons, *\"and in doing so gave up the persistence that made S. alvi attractive, which means NECTAR needs repeat dosing and therefore more beekeeper labour. Some of the beekeepers we spoke to preferred the option we dropped.\"* **Bielefeld-CeBiTec** is the third and the only one that dropped work on dual-use grounds: *\"We dropped work on blood-brain-barrier-crossing LNPs because of its dual-use potential.\"* Smaller versions exist — ICJFLS (6098) binned a high-leakage kill-switch design after another team shared leakage data, BGI-College (6345) swapped chassis from *C. butyricum* to *C. beijerinckii* at an early safety review, GCGS (6242) documented a rejected pH-sensitive switch with a reason.\n\n**DNA ordering is where this report's roadmap item actually has a worked example — exactly one.** **CalPolySLO** (6405) writes the paragraph GEMS needs to copy: *\"We order synthetic DNA from IDT and Twist Bioscience, both members of the International Gene Synthesis Consortium, which screens orders for sequences of concern. We use nothing from Risk Group 3 or 4.\"* They then publish a four-step provenance chain from order to purified protein, and they got there because Dr Hank Greely told them to publish their safety thinking *before* starting work and Dr Keith Robison raised dual-use scenarios, which produced a benefits-versus-misuse framework. **TAU-Israel** (6196) is the other, and goes further by building screening into software: their design tool runs **commec**, the IBBIS Common Mechanism, on every generated sequence before release, holds the output when screening is incomplete or unresolved, and states plainly that a clean result *\"does not establish that a sequence is harmless\"* and that the frontend panel is not fully connected and live deployment is unverified. That last sentence is what makes it credible. **BASIS-China** names Sangon Biotech as its synthesis house and emailed safety@igem.org before collecting animal-derived material rather than assuming an unavailable form meant the work was impossible.\n\n**On environmental release, the bar is visibly different and most teams do not clear it.** **Peking** designed physical screening into the hardware: two offset slit layers forming a tortuous passage sized against springtails at 0.5–10 mm, an attract-first-load-later deployment sequence so engineered yeast is only loaded after termite activity is confirmed on a load cell, and a removable inner cartridge so the material is retrievable — while declaring that its FAR1–Tet-Off proliferation brake *\"remains at the design stage\"* and that the two environment-responsive promoters *\"do not yet constitute a combined dual-signal control system.\"* **Athens** (6478) traced the real regulatory fork: marketing authorisation under EU Regulation 2019/6 versus the biopesticide regime, EFSA alongside national authorities, and the fact that European foulbrood is WOAH-listed and compulsorily reportable in Greece, so any alternative to destruction must clear that first. **Madrid-UCM** had containment made a precondition by an industrial partner — Repsol said living GMOs would not be acceptable without evidence that release had been prevented — and answered with encapsulated cells plus a culture-and-qPCR monitoring campaign with a divert-and-inactivate protocol. **GHCIS** (6166) sidestepped the problem by going cell-free, so there is no replicating organism to contain. Against these, **Toronto** (6187) — whose human practices work is genuinely strong — has a safety page that is a laboratory incident risk register, and **NU Boston** has a live contradiction worth naming: its alginate beads are *designed to degrade in soil and release the bacteria*, while the kill switch is described as the thing that justifies release.\n\n**GEMS-Taiwan, held to the same bar.** ReLEAF (6072) has exactly one measured containment result, and it is real: lumen-side medium sampled after 24 hours in the bioreactor grew colonies, shell-side medium grew none across a 0.2 µm hollow-fiber membrane retaining cells of 0.25–1.0 µm, backed by transmembrane-pressure and droplet leak detection. That is more than most teams have. It is also the whole case, and the gaps are large for a system that sits on a farm. There is no genetic containment layer at all — no kill switch, no auxotrophy, no second barrier if the membrane fails, which is the single failure mode the whole design depends on. The test is one timepoint, presence/absence, with no CFU count, no plated volume, no detection limit, no replicates and no stressed or fouled-membrane condition; the wiki nonetheless says the membrane *\"ensures containment.\"* Antibiotic resistance markers (erythromycin) are used with no stated plan to remove them before field use. The DURC section identifies no misuse pathway, only a commitment not to misuse. There is no DNA-order screening statement and no supplier named anywhere — precisely the NSTM-6 gap the roadmap flags. And although the team correctly notes that cell-free agricultural biologics may fall between the biopesticide and synthetic-biology classifications, no Taiwanese authority is named as having been asked. CalPolySLO's one paragraph and BASIS-China's one email are each a week's work; both are missing.","body_zh":"**先講基準率，因為標準低得驚人。** 在本報告研究的 106 支獲獎隊伍中，19 支描述了遺傳圍堵裝置——kill switch、營養缺陷、toxin–antitoxin 配對。4 支談到兩用或誤用。2 支說明了自己合成的 DNA 是如何被篩查的。而**回報實際量測逃逸頻率的隊伍是 0 支**——那正是把圍堵主張變成證據的唯一數字。環境釋放這一群裡，**UCL**（6381）與 **WageningenUR**（6222）的網站導覽中根本沒有安全頁面，而他們分別提出水處理與飲用水部署。Safety and Security 獎本身說著同樣的事：Overgrad 與高中組完全沒有被提名者，只有一位得主。幾乎沒有人投入這個類別，而投入的人並不是在跟人群競爭。\n\n**真正的安全頁面做了什麼，是背誦沒做的。** 背誦長這樣：BSL-1、非致病性底盤、風險組別表格、121 °C 滅菌、手套與包鞋。清單上每一項都是真的，但沒有一項跟這個專案有關。少數隊伍做了以下五件更難的事之一。他們把圍堵主張換算成閾值，並用同樣的單位跟接收環境對比——**BASIS-China**（6123）量到膽酸自殺開關的閾值約為 **0.1–0.2 mM taurocholate**，再查出貓十二指腸膽鹽為 15–42 mM、污水總膽酸為 184–356 µg/L（他們換算為 4.7×10⁻⁴–9.1×10⁻⁴ mM）、土壤中 deoxycholic acid 為 13.3 pmol/g，把差距攤開來。他們把保險機制一路測到壞——大學組得主 **William-and-Mary**（6243）從 Addgene 取得一個已發表的三毒素 kill switch 做長期追蹤，結果它是*所有受測迴路中最先失去功能的一個*，比其他迴路早了數週失效；整個專案因此變成一個論證：kill switch 需要橋樑與飛機早就有的失效分析。他們量測非目標傷害而不是斷言它——**Peking**（6366）以 21-nt 滑動視窗把 dsRNA 比對 RefSeq，發現任何非目標同源基因中最長的連續完全比對只有 **13 nt**（法老蟻為 10–11 nt），接著真的把螞蟻的同源片段在 S2 細胞中表現，量到 dsRNA 處理後相對表現量為 **1.22 與 1.30**：沒有被抑制。他們針對實際的生物劑選擇去活化方式——**Bielefeld-CeBiTec**（6221）查到高壓滅菌與 NaOH 對 α-synuclein 纖維的效果有限，於是改用 10% SDS 並*同時*高壓滅菌，在詢問基因工程主管機關後不使用預形成纖維，並以電子門禁、單向傳遞與永不離開細胞培養室的實驗衣來管理實驗室。最後，他們公布證據帳本：一欄「我們的結果能證明什麼」，旁邊一欄「真實應用前還缺什麼」——BASIS-China、Peking 與 IISER-Kolkata 都這麼做，大多數隊伍沒有。\n\n**逃逸率這題有乾淨的答案，答案是零。** 最強的幾支隊伍很清楚缺了什麼。**IISER-Kolkata**（6450）白紙黑字寫著：「對生物圍堵真正重要的數字是逃逸頻率，也就是誘導後存活細胞的比例……合成生物學圍堵文獻採用的基準是低於 10⁸ 分之 1。這個數字我們沒有量。」**UCSC**（6215）把引用的單一質體轉移機率 10⁻⁶ 自乘，推算出 **10⁻¹²** 的合併逃逸風險，對照引用的 10⁻⁸ 標準——這是算術，不是量測——然後對自己的尿嘧啶營養缺陷株說了誠實的話：該突變為 H99P，單一鹼基置換，「屬於最容易回復的那一類」，而且「任何以此菌株為基礎的圍堵主張，都需要一個實測的回復頻率，做法是把大量菌體塗在缺乏尿嘧啶的培養基上，數長出來的菌落」。**Madrid-UCM**（6124）指出最強的工程系統在接近 10¹² 分之二的偵測極限下回報「偵測不到逃逸」。隊伍們實際量到的是殺滅試驗：**NU Boston**（6300）發現 CcdB 會誘發絲狀化、改變光散射後，自行否決了用 OD₆₀₀ 讀 kill switch 的做法，改用流式細胞儀 live/dead 染色與 CFU 計數，顯示 0.2% arabinose 下在 10⁻⁵–10⁻⁷ 稀釋度皆明顯下降。這是好做法，但它仍然不是逃逸率。\n\n**三支隊伍放棄了某樣東西，而這是這個類別裡最強的證據。** Overgrad 得主 **Stockholm**（6292）已證實：其 wiki 把專案最大的改變記錄為「放棄開放式市政污水部署，改為處理特定高濃度廢流的封閉式生物反應器，以物理圍堵取代 kill switch」。觸發點是具名的顧問委員 Gunaratna Kuttuva Rajarao 告訴他們：污水處理廠不是封閉系統、廠方不會接受 GMO、單靠一個 kill switch 大概不夠。創業案也跟著沒了：沒有公司、沒有定價、沒有客戶，而他們現在指向的量產底盤甚至不是酵母。**Oxford**（6391）是第二個案例，而且把代價講出來：他們基於圍堵與法規理由，選擇熱去活化酵母而非活的 *Snodgrassella alvi* 腸道共生菌，「也因此放棄了讓 S. alvi 有吸引力的持久定殖，這表示 NECTAR 需要重複投藥，也就是更多養蜂人的工時。我們談過的一些養蜂人反而偏好我們放棄的那個選項。」**Bielefeld-CeBiTec** 是第三個，也是唯一因兩用疑慮而中止工作的：「我們因為兩用潛力而中止了可穿越血腦屏障的 LNP 工作。」規模較小的版本也有——ICJFLS（6098）在另一支隊伍分享洩漏資料後丟掉了高洩漏的 kill switch 設計，BGI-College（6345）在早期安全審查時把底盤從 *C. butyricum* 換成 *C. beijerinckii*，GCGS（6242）記錄了一個被否決的 pH 感應開關並附上理由。\n\n**DNA 訂購，正是本報告路線圖那一項唯一有實作範例的地方——而且只有一個。** **CalPolySLO**（6405）寫下了 GEMS 該照抄的那一段：「我們向 IDT 與 Twist Bioscience 訂購合成 DNA，兩者都是 International Gene Synthesis Consortium 成員，會對訂單進行疑慮序列篩查。我們不使用任何風險組別 3 或 4 的材料。」他們接著公布了從下單到純化蛋白的四步履歷鏈；而之所以如此，是因為 Dr Hank Greely 要他們在開工*之前*就公布安全論述，Dr Keith Robison 提出兩用情境，因而產生了一份利益對誤用的評估架構。**TAU-Israel**（6196）是另一支，而且更進一步把篩查做進軟體：他們的設計工具在釋出前對每一條生成序列執行 IBBIS 的 **commec**（Common Mechanism），在篩查未完成或留有未解疑慮時扣住輸出，並明說乾淨的結果「並不能證明一條序列無害」，以及前端面板尚未完全接上、線上部署未經驗證。最後那句話，才是讓它可信的地方。**BASIS-China** 具名 Sangon Biotech 為其合成供應商，並在採集動物來源材料前主動寫信給 safety@igem.org，而不是假設拿不到表單就等於不能做。\n\n**在環境釋放上，門檻明顯不同，而多數隊伍沒跨過。** **Peking** 把物理篩選做進硬體：外殼與內匣兩層錯開的窄縫形成迂迴通道，尺寸對照跳蟲的 0.5–10 mm；採取「先誘集、後投料」的部署順序，等秤重感測器確認白蟻活動後才裝入工程酵母；內匣可抽出，材料可回收——同時聲明其 FAR1–Tet-Off 增殖煞車「仍停留在設計階段」，兩個環境響應啟動子「尚未構成雙訊號聯合控制系統」。**Athens**（6478）追出了真正的法規岔路：依 EU Regulation 2019/6 走上市許可、或走生物農藥制度，EFSA 與各國主管機關並行，而且歐洲幼蟲病是 WOAH 列管、在希臘屬強制通報，任何取代撲殺的替代方案都得先過這一關。**Madrid-UCM** 被產業夥伴把圍堵設為前提——Repsol 直說，若無法證明已防止環境釋放，活體 GMO 不可能被接受——他們的回答是包埋細胞，加上培養與 qPCR 監測，並訂出分流與去活化流程。**GHCIS**（6166）則直接繞過問題，改走無細胞路線，根本沒有會增殖的生物要圍堵。相對地，人類實踐做得確實扎實的 **Toronto**（6187），安全頁面卻是一份實驗室事故風險清單；而 **NU Boston** 有一個該被點名的矛盾：它的海藻酸鈣珠*本來就設計成在土壤中崩解並釋出細菌*，而 kill switch 卻被描述成讓釋放成立的那個理由。\n\n**用同一把尺量 GEMS-Taiwan。** ReLEAF（6072）只有一項實際量測的圍堵結果，而它是真的：生物反應器運轉 24 小時後，管腔側取樣長出菌落，殼側取樣沒有長，中間隔著能截留 0.25–1.0 µm 細胞的 0.2 µm 中空纖維膜，另有跨膜壓力與液滴洩漏偵測佐證。這比多數隊伍擁有的還多。但這也就是全部了，而對一個要裝在農場上的系統來說，缺口很大。完全沒有遺傳圍堵層——沒有 kill switch、沒有營養缺陷，膜一旦失效也沒有第二道屏障，而整個設計恰恰押在這一個失效模式上。該測試只有單一時間點、只分有無，沒有 CFU 計數、沒有塗盤體積、沒有偵測極限、沒有重複，也沒有加壓或結垢膜的條件；wiki 卻寫著這層膜「確保圍堵」。使用了抗生素抗性標記（erythromycin），而且沒有說明田間使用前要如何移除。DURC 章節沒有指出任何誤用路徑，只有一句不會誤用的承諾。整個網站沒有任何 DNA 訂單篩查聲明，也沒有具名任何供應商——這正是路線圖點出的 NSTM-6 缺口。而且儘管團隊正確指出無細胞農業生物製劑可能卡在生物農藥與合成生物學衍生物的分類之間，卻沒有具名任何已諮詢的台灣主管機關。CalPolySLO 的那一段、BASIS-China 的那一封信，各只要一週的工作量；兩樣都沒有。","cards":[{"kicker":"The one number","kicker_zh":"那個數字","title":"BASIS-China measured a threshold, then looked up the real environment","title_zh":"BASIS-China 量出閾值，再去查真實環境","body":"The suicide switch keeps cells alive above roughly **0.1–0.2 mM taurocholate** and suppresses growth below it, measured across four Anderson promoters with empty vector alongside. They then converted published concentrations into the same units: feline duodenum 15–42 mM, sewage total bile acids 184–356 µg/L (4.7×10⁻⁴–9.1×10⁻⁴ mM), soil deoxycholic acid 13.3 pmol/g. Two to three orders of magnitude of margin, stated as a comparison rather than a claim — and they add that their microcapsules are designed to release cells in the intestine and must not be counted as physical containment.","body_zh":"該自殺開關在約 **0.1–0.2 mM taurocholate** 以上維持細胞存活、以下則抑制生長，以四個 Anderson 啟動子並列量測，並設空載體對照。接著他們把文獻濃度換算成同樣單位：貓十二指腸 15–42 mM、污水總膽酸 184–356 µg/L（4.7×10⁻⁴–9.1×10⁻⁴ mM）、土壤 deoxycholic acid 13.3 pmol/g。兩到三個數量級的餘裕，而且是以對比方式陳述而非斷言——他們還補上一句：微膠囊本來就設計成在腸道釋出細菌，不能算作物理圍堵。","chips":["0.1–0.2 mM threshold","sewage 9.1×10⁻⁴ mM","HS winner"],"chips_zh":["閾值 0.1–0.2 mM","污水 9.1×10⁻⁴ mM","高中組得主"],"link":"https://2026.igem.wiki/basis-china/safety-and-security","linkText":"BASIS-China safety and security"},{"kicker":"Tested to failure","kicker_zh":"測到失效","title":"William-and-Mary's kill switch broke first","title_zh":"William-and-Mary 的 kill switch 最先壞掉","body":"They took a published triple-toxin kill switch from Addgene and followed it longitudinally alongside other circuits. It was the first to lose its intended function, failing weeks before the rest. CFU counts were used instead of OD₆₀₀ or fluorescence, on the reasoning that a kill switch's output is loss of viability, not loss of signal. Their conclusion is the uncomfortable one: a system designed as the last line of defence had never been subjected to the failure analysis that mature engineering disciplines apply as routine.","body_zh":"他們從 Addgene 取得一個已發表的三毒素 kill switch，與其他迴路並行做長期追蹤。它是最先失去預期功能的一個，比其餘迴路早數週失效。他們以 CFU 計數取代 OD₆₀₀ 或螢光，理由是 kill switch 的輸出是活性喪失，不是訊號喪失。結論並不好聽：一個被設計成最後防線的系統，從來沒有接受過成熟工程學科視為例行的失效分析。","chips":["CFU not OD600","failed first","UG winner"],"chips_zh":["用 CFU，不用 OD600","自己先壞","大學組得主"],"link":"https://2026.igem.wiki/william-and-mary/safety-and-security","linkText":"William-and-Mary safety"},{"kicker":"Gave it up","kicker_zh":"放棄了","title":"Stockholm dismantled its own deployment plan, and Oxford named the cost","title_zh":"Stockholm 拆掉自己的部署計畫，Oxford 寫出代價","body":"Stockholm's wiki records the project's largest change as open municipal deployment dropped for a contained bioreactor, physical containment replacing the kill switch, after a named advisory board member said plants are not closed systems and will not accept GMOs. The venture went with it. Oxford did the same thing one level down: heat-inactivated yeast instead of a living *Snodgrassella alvi* symbiont, for containment and regulatory reasons — *\"and in doing so gave up the persistence that made S. alvi attractive... Some of the beekeepers we spoke to preferred the option we dropped.\"*","body_zh":"Stockholm 的 wiki 把專案最大的改變記為：放棄開放式市政部署、改為封閉式生物反應器，以物理圍堵取代 kill switch；起因是具名顧問委員指出處理廠不是封閉系統、也不會接受 GMO。創業案一併作廢。Oxford 在低一層做了同樣的事：基於圍堵與法規理由，以熱去活化酵母取代活的 *Snodgrassella alvi* 共生菌——「也因此放棄了讓 S. alvi 有吸引力的持久定殖……我們談過的一些養蜂人反而偏好我們放棄的那個選項。」","chips":["open release dropped","cost stated","OG winner"],"chips_zh":["放棄開放釋出","代價寫明","研究生組得主"],"link":"https://2026.igem.wiki/stockholm/safety-and-security","linkText":"Stockholm safety and security"},{"kicker":"DNA ordering","kicker_zh":"DNA 訂購","title":"CalPolySLO wrote the paragraph the roadmap is asking for","title_zh":"CalPolySLO 寫出了路線圖要的那一段","body":"*\"We order synthetic DNA from IDT and Twist Bioscience, both members of the International Gene Synthesis Consortium, which screens orders for sequences of concern. We use nothing from Risk Group 3 or 4.\"* Then a four-step provenance chain from order to purified protein. It exists because an ethicist told them to publish their safety thinking before starting work and a biosecurity scholar raised dual-use scenarios. Two of 106 teams name a screening regime at all; this is the cleaner of the two to copy.","body_zh":"「我們向 IDT 與 Twist Bioscience 訂購合成 DNA，兩者都是 International Gene Synthesis Consortium 成員，會對訂單進行疑慮序列篩查。我們不使用任何風險組別 3 或 4 的材料。」接著是從下單到純化蛋白的四步履歷鏈。它之所以存在，是因為一位倫理學者要他們在開工前先公布安全論述，一位生物保安學者提出了兩用情境。106 支隊伍中只有 2 支說明過篩查機制；這一支是比較好照抄的那個。","chips":["IDT + Twist","IGSC","no RG3/RG4"],"chips_zh":["IDT + Twist","IGSC","不碰 RG3/RG4"],"link":"https://2026.igem.wiki/calpolyslo/safety-and-security","linkText":"CalPolySLO safety and security"},{"kicker":"Screening as code","kicker_zh":"把篩查寫成程式","title":"TAU-Israel put the Common Mechanism in the release path","title_zh":"TAU-Israel 把 Common Mechanism 放進釋出路徑","body":"Their design tool runs **commec**, the IBBIS Common Mechanism, over every generated sequence and holds the output when screening is incomplete or leaves an unresolved concern. What makes it credible is the disclaimer: a result without a finding *\"does not establish that a sequence is harmless, suitable for an experiment, or approved for synthesis,\"* the frontend panel is not fully connected, and live deployment has not been verified. They dated the audit and named the source revision.","body_zh":"他們的設計工具對每一條生成序列執行 IBBIS 的 **commec**（Common Mechanism），並在篩查未完成或留有未解疑慮時扣住輸出。讓它可信的是那段免責聲明：沒有發現的結果「並不能證明一條序列無害、適合用於實驗，或已獲准合成」；前端面板尚未完全接上，線上部署亦未經驗證。他們為這次稽核註明日期並具名原始碼版本。","chips":["commec / IBBIS","hold on unresolved","audit dated"],"chips_zh":["commec / IBBIS","有疑慮就扣住","稽核標上日期"],"link":"https://2026.igem.wiki/tau-israel/safety-and-security","linkText":"TAU-Israel safety and security"},{"kicker":"Non-target harm","kicker_zh":"非目標傷害","title":"Peking measured what its bait does to the wrong insect","title_zh":"Peking 量了自家餌劑對「錯的昆蟲」做了什麼","body":"21-nt sliding windows against RefSeq with one-mismatch tolerance; longest uninterrupted perfect match in any non-target homolog was **13 nt**, 10–11 nt for the pharaoh ant. Then they expressed the ant's homologous fragments in S2 cells, treated with the termite dsRNA for 48 h, and measured relative expression of **1.22** and **1.30** — no knockdown. Hardware does the rest: offset slits sized against springtails at 0.5–10 mm, bait loaded only after termite activity registers on a load cell. The proliferation brake is declared unbuilt.","body_zh":"以 21-nt 滑動視窗比對 RefSeq，容許一個錯配；任何非目標同源基因中最長的連續完全比對為 **13 nt**，法老蟻為 10–11 nt。接著他們把螞蟻同源片段在 S2 細胞中表現，以白蟻 dsRNA 處理 48 小時，量得相對表現量 **1.22** 與 **1.30**——沒有被抑制。其餘交給硬體：錯開的窄縫以跳蟲 0.5–10 mm 為尺寸依據，餌劑要等秤重感測器登錄到白蟻活動後才裝入。增殖煞車則明言尚未建造。","chips":["≤13 nt off-target","1.22 / 1.30","brake not built"],"chips_zh":["脫靶 ≤13 nt","1.22 / 1.30","煞車沒做"],"link":"https://2026.igem.wiki/peking/safety-and-security","linkText":"Peking safety and security"},{"kicker":"The honest gap","kicker_zh":"誠實的缺口","title":"Three teams named the metric and said they had not measured it","title_zh":"三支隊伍指名了指標，然後說自己沒量","body":"IISER-Kolkata: *\"the figure that matters for biocontainment is the escape frequency... Values below 1 in 10⁸ cells are the benchmark... This has not been measured.\"* UCSC on its uracil auxotroph: H99P is a single base substitution, among the most readily reversible, and *\"any containment claim based on this strain needs a measured reversion frequency.\"* Madrid-UCM notes the strongest systems report undetectable escape near two parts in 10¹². Naming the number you are missing is worth more than a table of risk groups.","body_zh":"IISER-Kolkata：「對生物圍堵真正重要的數字是逃逸頻率……合成生物學文獻的基準是低於 10⁸ 分之 1……這個數字我們沒有量。」UCSC 談自家尿嘧啶營養缺陷株：H99P 是單一鹼基置換，屬於最容易回復的那一類，而且「任何以此菌株為基礎的圍堵主張，都需要一個實測的回復頻率」。Madrid-UCM 指出最強的系統在接近 10¹² 分之二的偵測極限下回報偵測不到逃逸。指名自己缺的那個數字，價值高過一張風險組別表。","chips":["10⁻⁸ benchmark","0 of 106 measured","named anyway"],"chips_zh":["10⁻⁸ 基準","0/106 量過","還是寫出來了"],"link":"https://2026.igem.wiki/ucsc/","linkText":"UCSC wiki"}],"table":{"head":["Team","Safeguard","What was actually measured","What they said it does not prove"],"head_zh":["隊伍","保險機制","實際量到什麼","他們說這不能證明什麼"],"rows":[["BASIS-China 6123","Bile-acid CcdB suicide switch","Growth threshold ~0.1–0.2 mM TCA across four promoters; spot dilutions 10⁻¹–10⁻⁴ at 0, 0.1, 1, 10, 15, 30 mM","Residual faecal bile acids, lab vs environmental conditions, circuit drift, horizontal transfer; microcapsules are not physical containment"],["William-and-Mary 6243","Published triple-toxin kill switch (Addgene)","Longitudinal CFU viability; the kill switch failed first, weeks before other circuits","One construct; does not establish that all kill switches are unreliable"],["Peking 6366","RNAi specificity + yeast proliferation brake","Non-target longest perfect match 13 nt (ant 10–11 nt); ant homolog expression 1.22 / 1.30 after 48 h dsRNA; Tetrahymena 1.58% vs 87.80% trypan-positive","FAR1–Tet-Off is design stage only; promoters are not yet a dual-signal system; episomal plasmids, long-term stability untested"],["UCSC 6215","pyrE/pyrF uracil auxotrophy + ccdA/ccdB","80 candidate colonies screened, 17 to colony PCR, clone 56 confirmed auxotroph; escape risk 10⁻¹² projected, not measured","Genotype and phenotype each established, causal link not; H99P reversible by one base change"],["NU Boston 6300","Salicylate ccdA/ccdB kill switch","CFU drop at 0.2% arabinose across 10⁻⁵–10⁻⁷ dilutions; flow cytometry live/dead after OD₆₀₀ was invalidated by CcdB filamentation","No escape frequency; beads are designed to degrade and release cells into soil"],["GEMS-Taiwan 6072","0.2 µm hollow-fiber membrane + leak detection","Shell-side sample after 24 h: no colonies; lumen-side: colonies","Single timepoint, presence/absence only — no CFU, no detection limit, no replicates, no stressed-membrane condition; no genetic second layer"],["Stockholm 6292","Physical containment in a closed reactor","Nothing measured — STPA hazard analysis plus a three-expert advisory board","Deployment declared conditional on safety and regulatory assessment; degradation products uncharacterised"]],"rows_zh":[["BASIS-China 6123","膽酸觸發的 CcdB 自殺開關","四個啟動子下生長閾值約 0.1–0.2 mM TCA；於 0、0.1、1、10、15、30 mM 做 10⁻¹–10⁻⁴ 點滴稀釋","糞便殘留膽酸、實驗室與環境條件差異、迴路漂移、水平轉移；微膠囊不算物理圍堵"],["William-and-Mary 6243","已發表的三毒素 kill switch（Addgene）","長期 CFU 存活追蹤；kill switch 最先失效，比其他迴路早數週","僅一個構築體；不能證明所有 kill switch 都不可靠"],["Peking 6366","RNAi 專一性 ＋ 酵母增殖煞車","非目標最長連續完全比對 13 nt（螞蟻 10–11 nt）；dsRNA 處理 48 小時後螞蟻同源基因表現 1.22 / 1.30；Tetrahymena 台盼藍陽性 1.58% 對 87.80%","FAR1–Tet-Off 僅止於設計階段；兩個啟動子尚未構成雙訊號系統；游離型質體，長期穩定性未測"],["UCSC 6215","pyrE/pyrF 尿嘧啶營養缺陷 ＋ ccdA/ccdB","篩 80 個候選菌落，17 個做菌落 PCR，clone 56 確認為營養缺陷株；逃逸風險 10⁻¹² 為推算而非量測","基因型與表型各自成立，但因果關係未建立；H99P 只要一個鹼基變化即可回復"],["NU Boston 6300","水楊酸觸發的 ccdA/ccdB kill switch","0.2% arabinose 下於 10⁻⁵–10⁻⁷ 稀釋度 CFU 下降；CcdB 誘發絲狀化使 OD₆₀₀ 失效後改用流式細胞儀 live/dead","沒有逃逸頻率；膠珠本來就設計成崩解並把細菌釋入土壤"],["GEMS-Taiwan 6072","0.2 µm 中空纖維膜 ＋ 洩漏偵測","24 小時後殼側取樣：無菌落；管腔側：有菌落","單一時間點、僅分有無——沒有 CFU、沒有偵測極限、沒有重複、沒有加壓膜條件；也沒有遺傳第二層"],["Stockholm 6292","封閉反應器中的物理圍堵","沒有量測——以 STPA 危害分析加上三位專家組成的顧問委員會替代","部署明訂以安全與法規評估為前提；降解產物尚未鑑定"]]},"checklist":["**Suppliers.** Order synthetic DNA and oligos only from International Gene Synthesis Consortium members, and name them on the safety page the way CalPolySLO does — supplier, consortium membership, and the fact that they screen orders for sequences of concern.","**Screen what you order.** Run commec (the IBBIS Common Mechanism) over every ordered construct of 50 nucleotides or more before the order goes out. A hold is not a pass: an incomplete or unresolved screen blocks the order until a human resolves it.","**Record, and keep it eight years.** One register row per order: date, supplier, construct name, full sequence, length, requester, screening tool and version, result, approver. Eight-year retention, matching what NSTM-6 asks of certified suppliers, because a GEMS order inside a US-funded collaboration inherits the requirement.","**One named signer.** A single GEMS biosafety officer approves every synthesis order and every new chassis before work starts. Two signatures for anything above Risk Group 1, anything on a select-agent list, and any sequence the screen flags.","**Say what you will not do.** No release of viable engineered cells outside a sealed device; no Risk Group 3 or 4 material; no work with uncharacterised environmental isolates; no construct whose purpose is increased transmissibility, virulence or host range; no antibiotic resistance marker in anything intended to leave the lab.","**Measure the containment number, don't project it.** For any strain that could leave a device, report an escape or reversion frequency per cell per generation: plate a large population under the restrictive condition, count survivors, state how many cells were plated and the detection limit. The literature benchmark is below 1 in 10⁸.","**Compare against the real receiving environment.** Any threshold — bile acid, salicylate, temperature, nutrient — gets converted into the units of the soil, water or field where the organism would land, with a cited source. A containment claim is only as good as that comparison.","**Publish the evidence ledger.** Two columns on every safety page: what these results establish, and what remains before real-world use. Name horizontal transfer, circuit drift over passages, and extracellular DNA explicitly, because genetic containment addresses none of them.","**Ask someone outside, in writing, early.** Email the institutional biosafety committee, the relevant Taiwanese authority for field deployment of an engineered agricultural input, and safety@igem.org — and publish the question, the answer, and what changed. An unavailable form is not the same as an impossible experiment."],"checklist_zh":["**供應商。** 合成 DNA 與寡核苷酸只向 International Gene Synthesis Consortium 成員訂購，並像 CalPolySLO 那樣寫在安全頁面上——供應商名稱、聯盟會員身分，以及他們會對訂單進行疑慮序列篩查這件事。","**篩查你訂的東西。** 在下單前，對每一個 50 個核苷酸以上的構築體執行 commec（IBBIS 的 Common Mechanism）。扣住不等於放行：篩查未完成或疑慮未解，訂單就停在那裡，直到有人處理。","**留存紀錄，保存八年。** 每筆訂單一列：日期、供應商、構築體名稱、完整序列、長度、申請人、篩查工具與版本、結果、核可人。保存八年，對齊 NSTM-6 對認證供應商的要求——因為 GEMS 若在美國經費支持的合作案中下單，就會一併繼承這項義務。","**一位具名簽核人。** 由單一位 GEMS 生物安全負責人核可每一筆合成訂單與每一個新底盤，才能開工。凡是高於風險組別 1、列於管制生物劑清單，或被篩查標記的序列，需兩人會簽。","**明寫你不做什麼。** 不在密閉裝置之外釋放有活性的工程細胞；不使用風險組別 3 或 4 的材料；不操作未鑑定的環境分離株；不製作以提高傳播力、毒力或宿主範圍為目的之構築體；凡預定離開實驗室者，不帶抗生素抗性標記。","**圍堵數字要量，不要推算。** 任何可能離開裝置的菌株，都要回報每細胞每世代的逃逸或回復頻率：在限制條件下塗布大量菌體、計數存活者，並寫出塗了多少細胞與偵測極限。文獻基準是低於 10⁸ 分之 1。","**跟真實接收環境對比。** 任何閾值——膽酸、水楊酸、溫度、養分——都要換算成該生物實際落腳的土壤、水體或田區的單位，並附引用來源。圍堵主張的可信度，不會高於背後那個對比。","**公布證據帳本。** 每一頁安全頁面都放兩欄：這些結果能證明什麼，以及真實應用前還缺什麼。明確點名水平轉移、多代傳代後的迴路漂移，以及胞外 DNA，因為遺傳圍堵一項都處理不了。","**及早以書面問外部的人。** 寫信給機構生物安全委員會、工程農業投入品田間部署的台灣主管機關，以及 safety@igem.org——並把問題、答覆與因此改了什麼一起公布。拿不到表單，不等於實驗做不成。"],"method":"Two passes. First, a keyword sweep of research/teams/*.json — the researched prose on all 106 decorated teams — for kill switch, auxotroph, biocontainment, containment, escape, BSL, dual-use, screening, risk assessment, Nagoya and release. Counts from that pass are: 19 of 106 describe a genetic containment device, 28 use the words biosafety or biosecurity, 28 name an institutional biosafety body or officer, 4 discuss dual use, 2 name a DNA-synthesis screening regime, and 0 report a measured escape frequency. Those counts are a floor, not a census: the files are researcher summaries, so a practice a team carried out but did not write up prominently — or wrote up only on a page the researcher did not quote — is invisible here. Second, direct verification on the teams' own 2026 wikis for 21 teams: the six Safety and Security Award winners and nominees (William-and-Mary 6243, Bielefeld-CeBiTec 6221, Peking 6366, UCSC 6215, Stockholm 6292, BASIS-China 6123) plus the environmental-release cohort (LYON, Madrid-UCM, RUM-UPRM, UCL, UOttawa, WageningenUR, DTU-Denmark, Toronto, Athens, Oxford, Muenster-University, Lambert-GA, GHCIS, Squirrel-Beijing, GEMS-Taiwan). Most 2026 wikis are client-rendered React applications that return an empty shell to curl; where that happened the page text was recovered from the site's own JavaScript bundle, and the static wikis were read directly. Every number quoted here was read off the team's own page. Bielefeld-CeBiTec 6221, UCSC 6215 and RUM-UPRM 6282 are not in the 106-team on-disk corpus and were read only from their wikis. UCL 6381 and WageningenUR 6222 have no safety page in their site navigation, which is a statement about their navigation, not proof they did no safety work — both completed iGEM's safety forms, which are not public. What none of this can see: the safety form every team files with iGEM, institutional biosafety committee records, and anything a team did at the bench and never wrote down.","method_zh":"分兩輪。第一輪是對 research/teams/*.json 做關鍵字掃描——那是全部 106 支獲獎隊伍的研究文字——搜尋 kill switch、auxotroph、biocontainment、containment、escape、BSL、dual-use、screening、risk assessment、Nagoya 與 release。該輪的計數為：106 支中有 19 支描述遺傳圍堵裝置，28 支使用生物安全或生物保安字樣，28 支具名機構生物安全單位或負責人，4 支談及兩用，2 支說明 DNA 合成篩查機制，0 支回報實際量測的逃逸頻率。這些數字是下限而非普查：檔案是研究者摘要，因此某隊做了卻沒有顯著寫出、或只寫在研究者未引用頁面上的做法，在這裡是看不見的。第二輪是直接到隊伍自己的 2026 wiki 查證 21 支隊伍：Safety and Security 獎的六支得主與提名隊伍（William-and-Mary 6243、Bielefeld-CeBiTec 6221、Peking 6366、UCSC 6215、Stockholm 6292、BASIS-China 6123），加上環境釋放這一群（LYON、Madrid-UCM、RUM-UPRM、UCL、UOttawa、WageningenUR、DTU-Denmark、Toronto、Athens、Oxford、Muenster-University、Lambert-GA、GHCIS、Squirrel-Beijing、GEMS-Taiwan）。大多數 2026 wiki 是前端渲染的 React 應用，curl 只會拿到空殼；遇到這種情況時，頁面文字是從網站自身的 JavaScript 打包檔還原，靜態網站則直接讀取。本文引用的每一個數字都是從隊伍自己的頁面讀來的。Bielefeld-CeBiTec 6221、UCSC 6215 與 RUM-UPRM 6282 不在這 106 支的本機語料中，僅從其 wiki 讀取。UCL 6381 與 WageningenUR 6222 的網站導覽中沒有安全頁面——這是關於他們導覽的陳述，不是他們沒做安全工作的證明；兩隊都完成了 iGEM 的安全表單，而那些表單並不公開。本文完全看不到的部分：每支隊伍向 iGEM 繳交的安全表單、機構生物安全委員會的紀錄，以及任何在實驗檯上做了卻從未寫下的事。"},{"id":"measurement-discipline","tab":"drylab","order":40,"kicker":"Original analysis","kicker_zh":"原創分析","title":"Calibrated, but never checked","title_zh":"校正過，卻從來沒有被核對","lede":"Seven checkable habits of measurement discipline, scored by reading 39 decorated 2026 wikis directly. The cohort calibrates well, almost never defines its own error bars, and only twice in 39 teams does anyone measure the same thing twice.","lede_zh":"量測紀律的七項可檢核習慣，直接閱讀 39 支 2026 年獲獎團隊的 wiki 後逐項評分。這群團隊很會做檢量線，卻幾乎不說明自己的誤差棒是什麼；而在 39 支隊伍中，只有兩支真的把同一件東西量了第二次。","body":"We read the wikis of 39 decorated teams — all 14 Best Measurement winners and nominees across the three sections, plus the 30 Top 10 teams, 5 of which overlap — and scored each on seven things a reader can check: a calibration curve into an absolute unit, replicates named by type, an error bar whose meaning is stated, a limit of detection computed for the team's own assay, a negative control or blank, a second instrument or lab measuring the same sample, and a protocol that names the instrument.\n\n**The easy half is done and the hard half is not.** A negative control or blank appears in **38 of 39** wikis (97%) — only Lambert-GA has none. A protocol naming the instrument appears in **35 of 39** (90%). A calibration curve or an absolute-unit anchor appears in **28 of 39** (72%). Then it falls away. Replicates are named by type — biological or technical, not a bare *n* = 3 — in **23 of 39** (59%). An error bar whose meaning is stated in words is in **23 of 39** (59%). A limit of detection computed from the team's own data, with a number on it, is in **6 of 39 (15%)**: WageningenUR, William-and-Mary, UNILausanne, Labi-Taiwan, GCGS and GEMS-Taiwan. And the same sample measured twice, by a second instrument, operator or lab, with the two numbers compared, is in **2 of 39 (5%)**.\n\n**An error bar whose meaning is unstated is itself a finding.** Twenty-three of the 39 wikis print the phrase \"error bars\"; three of those never say what the bar is. Princeton captions a standard curve \"fitted over 0–250 µg/mL with error bars on each standard: y = 0.0013x + 0.2726, R² = 0.9968\" — the fit is reported to four decimals and the spread is not reported at all. One sentence does it: McMaster-Canada's BCA figure reads \"BSA standard curve from nine blank-corrected standard means, 0–2000 µg/mL, measured in technical triplicate … Error bars show sample SD.\" Same assay, same chart type, a different reader experience. Six of the 39 never use any dispersion word — SD, SEM, confidence interval, ± — anywhere we could read. One of them is **CalPolySLO, the undergraduate Best Measurement winner**: across nine pages and 124,000 characters, including the most carefully written protocol set in the whole cohort, the characters \"±\", \"error bar\" and \"standard deviation\" appear **zero** times, and its headline PPK2 enzyme curves are labelled \"averages of experimental duplicates (n = 2)\".\n\n**Nobody checks the instrument.** The word *inter-lab* appears in **0 of the 106 team files** in this report. On the 39 wikis, two teams did it. GEMS-Taiwan ran its inline photometer against a BioDrop benchtop spectrophotometer twice, with TiO₂ and then SiO₂ particle ladders — 45 paired points in August, 40 steps in October, slope 1.018, R² 0.995, residual SD reported for both instruments — and separately compared its leaf and air temperature sensors across **540 paired readings** at three sites, finding a site-dependent offset of −0.2 to +1.8 °C. Athens, an Overgraduate Top 10 team that was never nominated for Measurement, repeated a failed restriction digest with enzymes that had been verified at another laboratory, explicitly \"to introduce an independent reference for the digestion step\". Honourable third: HongKong-JSS, which names the gap instead of hiding it — \"we did not run our samples on a calibrated fluorometer or plate reader alongside the box, so the workflow is unvalidated against a reference instrument\" — and, on the same page, explains that \"CV = 100 × SD/mean. Lower CV indicates lower relative signal variability, not greater detection accuracy.\" That is a high-school team teaching what a statistic does *not* mean.\n\n**Does any of it buy you a podium? No.** Scored out of seven, the Best Measurement cohort averages **4.36** and the 25 Top 10 generalists average **3.76** — a gap of six tenths of one checkbox. Split by outcome instead of by award, the effect vanishes and reverses: the 30 Top 10 teams average **3.93**, and the nine decorated teams that did *not* reach a Top 10 — all of them Best Measurement nominees — average **4.11**. The cheap pass over all 106 team files says the same: of 22 teams whose files mention calibration work, 6 made a Top 10 (**27%**); of the 84 that do not, 24 made a Top 10 (**29%**). There is no effect to report. Measurement discipline earns the Measurement prize; it does not move you up the table. The honest version of the dry-lab roadmap's claim is therefore not *uncertainty wins medals* — it is *uncertainty is what makes a number worth keeping after the medals*.\n\n**Where the award itself falls short.** The Best Measurement cohort really does lead on the converting half: calibration **12/14 (86%) against 16/25 (64%)**, and a numeric limit of detection **5/14 (36%) against 1/25 (4%)** — LOD is the single check that cleanly separates the specialists. But on the uncertainty half it does not lead at all. Stating what an error bar means: **8/14 (57%) for the Measurement cohort against 15/25 (60%) for the generalists**. Naming the instrument: **12/14 against 23/25**. WageningenUR, the Overgraduate winner, writes out LOD = 3.3σ/b and LOQ = 10σ/b, builds a separate calibration line per growth medium in µM fluoride, re-zeroes each line on the plate's negative control, and warns that \"R² is only descriptive per situation, since it rises with the width of the concentration range\" — and then calls its instrument \"a microplate reader\", with no make, model or wavelength settings. The prize is being awarded for turning a reading into a unit, not for saying how sure you are of it. By section the three tiers are nearly level — Undergraduate 4.07, Overgraduate 3.92, High School 3.92 — and high-school teams actually calibrate most often (10/13, 77%) while naming their replicate type least often (6/13, 46%).","body_zh":"我們直接閱讀了 39 支獲獎團隊的 wiki——三個組別全部 14 支 Best Measurement 得主與入圍隊伍，加上 30 支 Top 10 團隊（其中 5 支重疊）——並就七項讀者可以自行檢核的事情逐一評分：換算到絕對單位的檢量線、依類型指名的重複實驗、有說明含意的誤差棒、針對自家 assay 算出的偵測極限、陰性對照或空白對照、由第二台儀器或第二間實驗室量測同一份樣品，以及一份指名儀器型號的 protocol。\n\n**容易的一半做完了，難的一半沒有。** 陰性對照或空白對照出現在 **39 支中的 38 支**（97%）——只有 Lambert-GA 沒有。指名儀器的 protocol 出現在 **39 支中的 35 支**（90%）。檢量線或絕對單位錨點出現在 **39 支中的 28 支**（72%）。接著就急轉直下。把重複實驗依類型指名——生物重複或技術重複，而不是光寫一個 *n* = 3——的，只有 **39 支中的 23 支**（59%）。以文字說明誤差棒代表什麼的，也只有 **39 支中的 23 支**（59%）。以自己的資料算出、並附上數值的偵測極限，只有 **39 支中的 6 支（15%）**：WageningenUR、William-and-Mary、UNILausanne、Labi-Taiwan、GCGS 與 GEMS-Taiwan。而把同一份樣品用第二台儀器、第二位操作者或第二間實驗室再量一次、並把兩個數字拿來比對的，只有 **39 支中的 2 支（5%）**。\n\n**一根沒有說明含意的誤差棒，本身就是一項發現。** 39 份 wiki 中有 23 份寫出「error bars」這個詞，其中三支從頭到尾沒說那根棒子是什麼。Princeton 的檢量線圖說寫著「fitted over 0–250 µg/mL with error bars on each standard: y = 0.0013x + 0.2726, R² = 0.9968」——擬合報到小數點後四位，離散程度卻完全沒報。其實一句話就夠了：McMaster-Canada 的 BCA 圖說是「BSA standard curve from nine blank-corrected standard means, 0–2000 µg/mL, measured in technical triplicate … Error bars show sample SD.」同樣的 assay、同樣的圖型，讀者的處境卻完全不同。39 支中有 6 支，在我們讀得到的範圍內從未使用任何離散度用語——SD、SEM、信賴區間、±。其中一支是 **CalPolySLO，也就是大學部的 Best Measurement 得主**：九個頁面、124,000 個字元，裡面包含整個 cohort 中寫得最仔細的一整套 protocol，但「±」「error bar」「standard deviation」這些字出現了 **零次**，而它主打的 PPK2 酵素曲線標註為「averages of experimental duplicates (n = 2)」。\n\n**沒有人去核對儀器。** 本報告 106 份團隊檔案中，「inter-lab」這個詞出現了 **0 次**。在 39 份 wiki 上，有兩支做了。GEMS-Taiwan 把自製的管線式光度計拿去和 BioDrop 桌上型分光光度計比對了兩次，分別用 TiO₂ 與 SiO₂ 顆粒濃度梯度——八月 45 組配對點、十月 40 個階段，斜率 1.018、R² 0.995，兩台儀器的殘差標準差都有報出——另外還在三個場址以 **540 組配對讀值** 比較葉片與空氣溫度感測器，量到隨場址而異、介於 −0.2 到 +1.8 °C 的偏移。Athens 是一支從未被提名 Measurement 的研究生組 Top 10 隊伍，他們把失敗的限制酶切重做了一次，改用「已在另一間實驗室驗證過」的酵素，並明說目的是「為酶切這一步引入獨立的參照」。值得一提的第三名是 HongKong-JSS，他們選擇把缺口講出來而不是藏起來——「we did not run our samples on a calibrated fluorometer or plate reader alongside the box, so the workflow is unvalidated against a reference instrument」——而且在同一頁解釋「CV = 100 × SD/mean. Lower CV indicates lower relative signal variability, not greater detection accuracy.」這是一支高中隊伍在教一個統計量「不」代表什麼。\n\n**這些功夫換得到名次嗎？換不到。** 以七分計，Best Measurement cohort 平均 **4.36**，25 支 Top 10 通才團隊平均 **3.76**——差距是零點六個勾選格。改以結果而非獎項來切，效果不但消失還倒轉：30 支 Top 10 團隊平均 **3.93**，而九支獲獎但「沒有」進 Top 10 的隊伍——全部都是 Best Measurement 入圍者——平均 **4.11**。對全部 106 份團隊檔案做的低成本掃描說的是同一件事：檔案中提及校正相關工作的 22 支，有 6 支進 Top 10（**27%**）；沒提的 84 支，有 24 支進 Top 10（**29%**）。這裡沒有效應可報。量測紀律換得到 Measurement 獎，但不會把你往排行榜上推。因此，乾實驗室路線圖那個主張比較誠實的版本不是「不確定度能拿獎」，而是「不確定度決定了獎項散場以後，那個數字還值不值得留著」。\n\n**這個獎項本身不足的地方。** Best Measurement cohort 在「換算」那一半確實領先：檢量線 **12/14（86%）對 16/25（64%）**，有數值的偵測極限 **5/14（36%）對 1/25（4%）**——偵測極限是唯一能乾淨地把專才分出來的一項。但在「不確定度」那一半，它完全沒有領先。說明誤差棒含意：Measurement cohort **8/14（57%）**，通才團隊 **15/25（60%）**。指名儀器：**12/14 對 23/25**。研究生組得主 WageningenUR 把 LOD = 3.3σ/b 與 LOQ = 10σ/b 完整寫出來，為每一種培養基各建一條以 µM fluoride 為單位的檢量線，每條線都用該盤的陰性對照重新歸零，還提醒「R² is only descriptive per situation, since it rises with the width of the concentration range」——然後把自己的儀器稱作「a microplate reader」，沒有廠牌、沒有型號、沒有波長設定。這個獎目前獎勵的是「把讀值變成單位」，而不是「說清楚你對它有多確定」。以組別來看，三個層級幾乎齊平——大學部 4.07、研究生組 3.92、高中組 3.92——而高中隊伍其實是做檢量線最頻繁的一群（10/13，77%），卻也是最少指明重複實驗類型的一群（6/13，46%）。","cards":[{"kicker":"The headline number","kicker_zh":"最關鍵的數字","title":"2 of 39 measured it twice","title_zh":"39 支裡只有 2 支量了第二次","body":"Only GEMS-Taiwan and Athens put the same material in front of a second instrument or a second laboratory and compared the two numbers. GEMS-Taiwan has the only quantitative version: 45 paired points of its inline photometer against a BioDrop benchtop spectrophotometer, slope 1.018, R² 0.995, plus 540 paired leaf-versus-air sensor readings at three sites. Everyone else's instrument is trusted because it is the only one they used.","body_zh":"只有 GEMS-Taiwan 與 Athens 把同一份材料送到第二台儀器或第二間實驗室，並把兩個數字拿來比對。GEMS-Taiwan 是唯一有量化結果的：自製管線式光度計對 BioDrop 桌上型分光光度計，45 組配對點、斜率 1.018、R² 0.995，另加三個場址共 540 組葉片對空氣感測器的配對讀值。其他隊伍之所以相信自己的儀器，只是因為那是他們用過的唯一一台。","chips":["2/39 inter-instrument","0/106 say \"inter-lab\"","45 paired points"],"chips_zh":["2/39 跨儀器","0/106 提到「跨實驗室」","45 組配對點"]},{"kicker":"The unnamed bar","kicker_zh":"沒有名字的那根棒子","title":"23 draw error bars, 3 never define them","title_zh":"23 支畫了誤差棒，3 支從未說明","body":"GU Frankfurt, Princeton and Stanford all print the phrase \"error bars\" without ever saying whether the bar is a standard deviation, a standard error or a confidence interval. Six more wikis — CalPolySLO, ETH-Zurich, GHCIS, HongKong-HS, LYON, Stanford — contain no dispersion word at all. The cure is one clause in a caption, and McMaster-Canada shows exactly what it looks like.","body_zh":"GU Frankfurt、Princeton 與 Stanford 都寫出了「error bars」，卻始終沒說那根棒子是標準差、平均值標準誤，還是信賴區間。另有六份 wiki——CalPolySLO、ETH-Zurich、GHCIS、HongKong-HS、LYON、Stanford——完全沒有出現任何離散度用語。解法只是圖說裡的一個子句，而 McMaster-Canada 正好示範了它長什麼樣子。","chips":["23/39 write \"error bars\"","3 never define them","6 use no dispersion word"],"chips_zh":["23/39 寫了「誤差棒」","3 支從未定義","6 支沒用任何離散詞"]},{"kicker":"The award gap","kicker_zh":"獎項的落差","title":"4.36 against 3.76, out of seven","title_zh":"七分制，4.36 對 3.76","body":"The Best Measurement cohort beats the Top 10 generalists by six tenths of one checkbox. It leads clearly on only two of the seven: calibration (86% against 64%) and a numeric limit of detection (36% against 4%). On stating what an error bar means it is level or behind, 57% against 60%. The prize currently rewards converting a reading into a unit, not reporting how sure you are of it.","body_zh":"Best Measurement cohort 只比 Top 10 通才團隊高出零點六個勾選格。七項之中，它只在兩項明顯領先：檢量線（86% 對 64%）與有數值的偵測極限（36% 對 4%）。在「說明誤差棒代表什麼」這一項上它持平甚至落後，57% 對 60%。這個獎目前獎勵的是把讀值換成單位，而不是說清楚你對它有多確定。","chips":["MEAS 4.36/7","Top 10 generalists 3.76/7","LOD 36% vs 4%"],"chips_zh":["量測組 4.36/7","Top 10 綜合組 3.76/7","LOD 36% 對 4%"]},{"kicker":"GEMS-Taiwan, same terms","kicker_zh":"GEMS-Taiwan，同一把尺","title":"7 of 7 on the checklist, n = 1 on the headline assay","title_zh":"檢核表 7/7，但主打數據 n = 1","body":"GEMS-Taiwan is the only team in the 39 to tick all seven, and it earned that on hardware: a calibration analysis plan committed to the repository before the first measurement, with bias, repeatability, LOD, LOQ and hysteresis thresholds fixed in advance. The wet lab is weaker and the team says so. Its headline secreted ACC deaminase figure, 7.25 mU/mL, is n = 1 and is labelled by the team \"below quantitation\"; the light-induction error bars are technical wells on a single plate; and for containment it writes that \"the detection limit was not recorded and replicate experiments were not performed\". Its real contribution is provenance labelling, not replication. The cheapest next step for GEMS is also the most obvious one: run the key assay on three separate days.","body_zh":"GEMS-Taiwan 是 39 支中唯一七項全勾的隊伍，而這是靠硬體掙來的：第一次量測之前就把校正分析計畫提交進版本庫，偏差、重複性、LOD、LOQ 與遲滯的門檻全部事先訂死。濕實驗室就弱得多，而團隊自己也這麼說。它主打的分泌型 ACC deaminase 數字 7.25 mU/mL 是 n = 1，團隊自行標註為「below quantitation」；光誘導實驗的誤差棒是單一培養盤上的技術孔；至於菌體滯留，他們寫下「the detection limit was not recorded and replicate experiments were not performed」。它真正的貢獻是來源標註，而不是重複驗證。GEMS 下一步最便宜、也最明顯：把關鍵 assay 在三個不同日期各做一次。","chips":["7/7 checklist","headline number n = 1","pre-registered calibration plan"],"chips_zh":["檢核表 7/7","主打數據 n = 1","預先登錄的校正計畫"]}],"table":{"head":["Team","Section","Score","Strongest habit","What is missing"],"head_zh":["團隊","組別","分數","最強的習慣","缺少的部分"],"rows":[["GEMS-Taiwan","High School","7/7","Inline photometer checked against a BioDrop benchtop spectrophotometer, 45 paired points, slope 1.018, R² 0.995; calibration analysis plan pre-registered with LOD, LOQ and hysteresis thresholds","The discipline is in the hardware. The headline enzyme number is n = 1 and self-labelled below quantitation; light-induction error bars are technical wells on one plate; containment has no detection limit and no replicates"],["McMaster-Canada","Undergrad","5/7","BSA standard curve from nine blank-corrected means, 0–2000 µg/mL, technical triplicate, R² = 0.9690, and the caption says \"Error bars show sample SD\"","No second instrument; \"detection limit\" appears only as a gel's informal floor, never computed from blanks"],["WageningenUR","Overgrad","5/7","LOD = 3.3σ/b and LOQ = 10σ/b written out and used as a selection rule; one calibration line per growth medium in µM fluoride, re-zeroed on the plate's negative control","Never names the instrument — \"a microplate reader\", no make, model or wavelength settings; no second instrument"],["UNILausanne","Overgrad","5/7","LAMP limit of detection measured to 5.5 × 10⁻⁵ ng of template per reaction and set against qPCR, the gold standard, with no-template controls shown on every gel","Replicates almost never typed as biological or technical; dispersion rarely stated on figures"],["William-and-Mary","Undergrad","5/7","Fluorescein and sulforhodamine 101 series, four replicates per concentration, PBS blanks; LOD 0.61 nM and LOQ 1.74 nM from mean + 3 SD of 24 untransformed wells; states that samples below the lowest standard make the conversion a ±15% extrapolation","Only two mentions of a dispersion statistic across 236,000 characters; no second instrument"],["Labi-Taiwan","High School","5/7","LOD 7.53 nM from a log-linear fit, 0 nM as the negative control, mean ± SD (n = 3); CV 10.66% across three independently fabricated electrode batches; states its fluorescence is arbitrary units not valid for cross-instrument quantification","Never distinguishes biological from technical replicates; the between-batch check is repeatability on one instrument, not a second instrument"],["Yucai-SZ","High School","5/7","\"Data were shown as mean ± SD, n = 3\" on nearly every panel, with 29 reported R² values and calibration curves for the ΔOD assay","No limit of detection anywhere; no orthogonal or second-instrument check"],["Princeton","Undergrad","4/7","GFP standard curve converting plate-reader fluorescence into molecules bound per phage; bootstrap intervals taken over wells so that disagreement between wells is shown rather than hidden","Captions a standard curve \"with error bars on each standard\" and never says what the bar is; no computed limit of detection"],["KAUST-KSA","Overgrad","4/7","Dose verified empirically with a dosimeter at the sample position against the extrapolated lookup table, after the commissioning geometry was changed; biological and technical replicates both named","Calibrates the input, not the readout: no standard curve for the survival assay, no limit of detection, no stated error-bar meaning"],["HangzhouFourteenAP","High School","4/7","\"Error bars represent SD from three independent measurements\", with the per-replicate table printed beside the figure; CFU/mL and standard curves used","No limit of detection; replicates never typed as biological or technical; no second instrument"],["XJTLU-China","Undergrad","4/7","Biological replicates named throughout, n = 5 with Welch's two-sample test and p values; Ribo-seq reproducibility reported as Pearson r = 0.9917 within a batch","No calibration curve anywhere: every readout is relative expression normalised to rpoD, so nothing converts to an absolute unit"],["CalPolySLO","Undergrad","3/7","ATP and BSA standard curves with the linear-range rule written into the protocol itself — dilute until the reading falls inside the standards — plus released Opentrons scripts and a fluorescein benchmark","Zero occurrences of \"±\", \"error bar\" or \"standard deviation\" in 124,000 characters across nine pages; headline enzyme curves are means of n = 2"],["SDU-Denmark","Overgrad","3/7","The clearest replicate accounting in the cohort: three biological replicates from different colonies, technical replicates on three of the six samples, and the reason the other three have only one measurement","No limit of detection; no error-bar definition; no instrument make or model named"],["CHINAGuangdongShimen","High School","2/7","Excitation and emission wavelengths and the plate-reader make given for every read, and an explicit admission that \"the observed response onset is not a formally established detection limit\"","No standard curve at all — everything stays in RFU and OD₆₀₀-normalised fluorescence; \"three replicate wells per concentration\" is the only replicate statement, and the iGEM template prompt is still on the page"]],"rows_zh":[["GEMS-Taiwan","高中組","7/7","自製管線式光度計與 BioDrop 桌上型分光光度計比對，45 組配對點、斜率 1.018、R² 0.995；校正分析計畫事先登錄，LOD、LOQ 與遲滯門檻皆預先訂定","紀律集中在硬體。主打的酵素數字是 n = 1，團隊自行標註低於定量下限；光誘導的誤差棒是單一培養盤上的技術孔；菌體滯留既無偵測極限也無重複實驗"],["McMaster-Canada","大學部","5/7","BSA 檢量線取自九個扣除空白的標準品平均值，0–2000 µg/mL，技術三重複，R² = 0.9690，圖說明寫「Error bars show sample SD」","沒有第二台儀器；「detection limit」只以膠體的非正式下限出現，從未由空白對照算出"],["WageningenUR","研究生組","5/7","完整寫出 LOD = 3.3σ/b 與 LOQ = 10σ/b 並作為篩選準則；每種培養基各建一條以 µM fluoride 為單位的檢量線，並以該盤陰性對照重新歸零","從未指名儀器——只寫「a microplate reader」，沒有廠牌、型號或波長設定；沒有第二台儀器"],["UNILausanne","研究生組","5/7","LAMP 偵測極限量到每個反應 5.5 × 10⁻⁵ ng 模板，並與黃金標準 qPCR 對照；每張膠都呈現 no-template control","幾乎從不標明重複是生物重複或技術重複；圖上甚少標示離散度"],["William-and-Mary","大學部","5/7","fluorescein 與 sulforhodamine 101 濃度系列，每個濃度四重複，含 PBS 空白；以 24 個未轉形孔的平均值加 3 SD 得出 LOD 0.61 nM、LOQ 1.74 nM；並指出樣品落在最低標準品以下，使該換算成為約 ±15% 的外推","236,000 字元中只出現兩次離散度統計量；沒有第二台儀器"],["Labi-Taiwan","高中組","5/7","由對數線性擬合得出 LOD 7.53 nM，以 0 nM 作為陰性對照，mean ± SD（n = 3）；三批獨立製作電極間的 CV 為 10.66%；並明言其螢光為任意單位，不適用於跨儀器定量","從未區分生物重複與技術重複；批次間檢查屬同一台儀器的重複性，不是第二台儀器"],["Yucai-SZ","高中組","5/7","幾乎每一張圖都寫「Data were shown as mean ± SD, n = 3」，共報出 29 個 R² 值，並為 ΔOD assay 建立檢量線","完全沒有偵測極限；沒有正交方法或第二台儀器的核對"],["Princeton","大學部","4/7","以 GFP 檢量線把盤式讀值換算為每顆噬菌體結合的分子數；以孔為單位做 bootstrap 區間，使孔與孔之間的不一致被呈現而非被掩蓋","檢量線圖說寫「with error bars on each standard」卻從未說明那根棒子是什麼；沒有算出偵測極限"],["KAUST-KSA","研究生組","4/7","在改動照射幾何之後，於樣品位置以劑量計實測劑量並與外推查表值核對；生物重複與技術重複都有指名","校正的是輸入而非讀值：存活率 assay 沒有檢量線、沒有偵測極限、沒有說明誤差棒含意"],["HangzhouFourteenAP","高中組","4/7","「Error bars represent SD from three independent measurements」，並在圖旁附上逐一重複的表格；使用 CFU/mL 與檢量線","沒有偵測極限；重複從未標明是生物或技術重複；沒有第二台儀器"],["XJTLU-China","大學部","4/7","全篇指名生物重複，n = 5 並附 Welch 雙樣本檢定與 p 值；批次內 Ribo-seq 重現性以 Pearson r = 0.9917 報出","完全沒有檢量線：所有讀值都是對 rpoD 正規化後的相對表現量，沒有任何東西換算得到絕對單位"],["CalPolySLO","大學部","3/7","ATP 與 BSA 檢量線，並把線性範圍規則直接寫進 protocol——稀釋到讀值落在標準品範圍內為止——另釋出 Opentrons 腳本與 fluorescein 基準","九個頁面、124,000 字元中，「±」「error bar」「standard deviation」出現零次；主打的酵素曲線是 n = 2 的平均值"],["SDU-Denmark","研究生組","3/7","全 cohort 中重複實驗交代得最清楚：三個來自不同菌落的生物重複，六個樣品中有三個做了技術重複，並說明另外三個為何只有一次量測","沒有偵測極限；沒有誤差棒定義；沒有指名儀器廠牌或型號"],["CHINAGuangdongShimen","高中組","2/7","每一次讀值都給出激發與發射波長以及盤式讀取儀廠牌，並明白承認「the observed response onset is not a formally established detection limit」","完全沒有檢量線——所有數據都停留在 RFU 與 OD₆₀₀ 正規化螢光；重複的唯一說法是「three replicate wells per concentration」，而 iGEM 的範本提示文字還留在頁面上"]]},"checklist":["Every axis carries a unit a reader outside your lab can interpret. If the unit is RFU, OD or a fold-change, say on the figure that it is instrument-relative and not comparable to anyone else's — Labi-Taiwan does exactly this.","One calibration curve per assay and per medium, plotted and shown rather than described. Give the fit equation, the R², and the concentration range over which it holds.","Say where your samples sit on that curve. If a point falls outside the standards, label the number an extrapolation and state the error you are accepting, the way William-and-Mary reports a ±15% extrapolation.","Name the replicate: \"n = 3 biological replicates, separate colonies on separate days\" or \"n = 3 technical wells on one plate\". A bare n = 3 tells a reader nothing.","Every error bar gets a clause in its caption — SD, SEM or 95% CI, and over what. If the figure has no bar because n = 1, write n = 1 on the figure.","Blanks and negative controls appear in the plot, not only in the methods paragraph.","Compute a limit of detection from your own blanks — mean + 3 SD, or 3.3σ/b — and report the limit of quantification beside it. If you cannot, write that the lowest concentration tested is not a validated detection limit, as HongKong-JSS does.","Once per project, measure one sample twice: a second instrument, a second operator, or a second day. Plot the two against each other and report the slope and the residual spread. Two of 39 decorated teams did this; it is the cheapest way to be unusual.","Name the instrument: make, model, wavelength, gain, integration time, path length. \"A microplate reader\" is not a method, even in an award-winning wiki.","Publish the protocol so a reader can repeat the measurement without emailing you, and record who took each measurement and on what date."],"checklist_zh":["每一條座標軸都要有實驗室外的讀者也能解讀的單位。如果單位是 RFU、OD 或倍率變化，就在圖上寫明它是相對於儀器的、無法和別人的數字比較——Labi-Taiwan 正是這麼做的。","每個 assay、每種培養基各一條檢量線，而且要畫出來而不是只用文字描述。附上擬合方程式、R²，以及這條線成立的濃度範圍。","說明你的樣品落在那條線的哪裡。如果有點落在標準品範圍之外，就把那個數字標成外推，並說明你接受了多大的誤差——像 William-and-Mary 報出 ±15% 外推那樣。","把重複實驗講清楚：「n = 3 生物重複，不同菌落、不同日期」或「n = 3 技術孔，同一培養盤」。光寫 n = 3 等於什麼都沒說。","每一根誤差棒都要在圖說裡有一個子句——SD、SEM 或 95% CI，以及是對什麼取的。如果因為 n = 1 而沒有誤差棒，就在圖上寫 n = 1。","空白與陰性對照要出現在圖裡，而不是只出現在方法段落。","用自己的空白對照算出偵測極限——平均值加 3 SD，或 3.3σ/b——並把定量極限一併報出。如果做不到，就寫明所測過的最低濃度並不是經過驗證的偵測極限，就像 HongKong-JSS 那樣。","每個專案至少做一次：把同一份樣品量兩次——第二台儀器、第二位操作者，或第二個日期。把兩組數字互相作圖，報出斜率與殘差離散度。39 支獲獎團隊中只有兩支做了；這是最便宜的與眾不同方式。","指名儀器：廠牌、型號、波長、增益、積分時間、光程。「a microplate reader」不是一個方法，就算寫在得獎的 wiki 上也不是。","把 protocol 公開到讀者不必寫信問你就能重做量測，並記錄每一筆量測是誰做的、哪一天做的。"],"method":"Two passes. Pass one pattern-matched the English dry-lab and science-for-good prose of all 106 team files in research/teams/, which is cheap and covers the whole decorated field but cannot see a practice a team performed and did not write up, nor one the researchers did not record. Pass two read the wikis directly for 39 teams: the 14 Best Measurement winners and nominees (CalPolySLO, McMaster-Canada, Princeton, William-and-Mary, XJTLU-China; WageningenUR, KAUST-KSA, SDU-Denmark, UNILausanne; GEMS-Taiwan, CHINAGuangdongShimen, HangzhouFourteenAP, Labi-Taiwan, Yucai-SZ) and the 30 Top 10 teams, of which Princeton, WageningenUR, KAUST-KSA, GEMS-Taiwan and HangzhouFourteenAP are in both lists, giving 39 distinct teams. Most 2026 wikis are client-rendered, so page text was recovered from the published JavaScript bundles and their lazy-loaded chunks; the static-HTML wikis were fetched page by page over measurement, results, engineering, model, proof-of-concept, experiments, notebook, contribution, description and parts. The two routes are not symmetric: a bundle yields the whole wiki at once, while a static site yields only the pages we asked for, so a static-site team can be undercounted. All headline rates come from pass two. Pass one is reported only where it is stated as such, because against the 39 verified wikis it recovers 39% of the calibration work, 23% of the limit-of-detection work and just 13% of the replicate typing — it is a floor and a ranking, not a measurement. Counting rules: a calibration counts when a standard or calibration curve is described, or when an absolute anchor such as fluorescein, CFU/mL or cells/mL appears at least twice. An error bar counts as defined only when a caption or sentence ties a named statistic (SD, SEM, 95% CI) to the plotted spread. A limit of detection counts only when the team computes one for its own assay and gives a number with a unit; informal uses such as \"below the detection limit of the gel\" and limits cited from the literature were excluded, which is why the strict count is 6 of 39 while 20 of 39 use the phrase. An inter-instrument check counts only when the same material is measured by a second instrument, operator or laboratory and the two results are compared. The seven-point score gives one point each for calibration, replicate typing, a defined error bar, a numeric limit of detection, a negative control or blank, an inter-instrument check, and a protocol that names the instrument. What this cannot see: a figure. Error bars drawn on a plot whose caption never names them score as undefined, which is the point of the exercise, but a caption baked into an image file is invisible to us, and so is anything in a linked PDF or a supplementary file. Nor can it see work done and not published. All 39 teams are decorated, so none of these rates describes the competition as a whole; they describe the teams that already won something. GEMS-Taiwan is the report author's own team and was scored on the same seven criteria as everyone else.","method_zh":"分兩輪。第一輪對 research/teams/ 中全部 106 份團隊檔案的英文乾實驗室與科學向善敘述做樣式比對；這一輪成本低、涵蓋整個獲獎場域，但看不見團隊做了卻沒寫下來的做法，也看不見研究員沒有記錄的做法。第二輪直接閱讀 39 支團隊的 wiki：14 支 Best Measurement 得主與入圍者（CalPolySLO、McMaster-Canada、Princeton、William-and-Mary、XJTLU-China；WageningenUR、KAUST-KSA、SDU-Denmark、UNILausanne；GEMS-Taiwan、CHINAGuangdongShimen、HangzhouFourteenAP、Labi-Taiwan、Yucai-SZ），以及 30 支 Top 10 團隊，其中 Princeton、WageningenUR、KAUST-KSA、GEMS-Taiwan 與 HangzhouFourteenAP 同時在兩份名單上，合計 39 支相異團隊。2026 年多數 wiki 為前端渲染，因此頁面文字是從已發布的 JavaScript bundle 及其延遲載入 chunk 取得；靜態 HTML 的 wiki 則逐頁抓取 measurement、results、engineering、model、proof-of-concept、experiments、notebook、contribution、description 與 parts。兩條路徑並不對稱：bundle 一次給出整個 wiki，靜態站只給我們指定的頁面，因此靜態站團隊可能被低估。所有主要比率皆來自第二輪。第一輪只在明確標示處引用，因為對照那 39 份已驗證的 wiki，它只找回 39% 的校正工作、23% 的偵測極限工作，以及僅 13% 的重複實驗分類——它是下限與排序，不是量測。計數規則：描述了標準曲線／檢量線，或出現至少兩次 fluorescein、CFU/mL、cells/mL 這類絕對單位錨點，才算有校正。只有當圖說或句子把具名統計量（SD、SEM、95% CI）與圖上的離散度連結起來，誤差棒才算有定義。只有團隊為自家 assay 算出並附上帶單位的數值，偵測極限才算數；像「低於膠體的偵測極限」這類非正式用法，以及引用自文獻的極限，一律排除——這就是為什麼嚴格計數是 39 支中的 6 支，而使用該詞的有 20 支。只有當同一份材料由第二台儀器、第二位操作者或第二間實驗室量測、且兩個結果被拿來比對，才算跨儀器核對。七分制各給一分：校正、重複實驗分類、有定義的誤差棒、有數值的偵測極限、陰性或空白對照、跨儀器核對，以及指名儀器的 protocol。這個方法看不到的東西：圖。圖上畫了誤差棒但圖說從未指名的，計為未定義——這正是本次檢核的重點；但若圖說被燒進圖片檔裡，我們就看不見，連結的 PDF 或補充檔案也一樣。做了卻未發布的工作同樣看不見。這 39 支全都是獲獎團隊，因此以上任何比率都不代表整個競賽，它們描述的是已經贏過東西的那群隊伍。GEMS-Taiwan 是本報告作者自己的團隊，並以與其他人完全相同的七項標準評分。"},{"id":"multiyear-continuity","tab":"good","order":40,"kicker":"Testing our own argument","kicker_zh":"檢驗我們自己的主張","title":"Carrying a problem across years cannot be shown to pay, because almost nobody does it","title_zh":"「讓題目跨年」無法被證明有效，因為幾乎沒有人這樣做","lede":"The hypothesis fails for lack of cases, not for lack of effect. Of the 81 decorated 2026 teams that had entered iGEM before, 78 had a readable previous project, and 5 of those 78 carried a project line into 2026. Five teams cannot be compared with anything. What iGEM's own data does show is a different thing entirely: returning to the competition tracks with better results, and returning is not continuing.","lede_zh":"這個假說不是被推翻，而是根本沒有足夠的案例。106 支 2026 年得獎隊伍中，有 81 支先前參加過 iGEM；其中 78 支的前一年專案內容查得到，而這 78 支裡只有 5 支把同一條題目線帶進 2026 年。五支隊伍不足以和任何東西相比。iGEM 自己的資料能顯示的，是另一件完全不同的事：重複參賽和較好的成績有關——但重複參賽不等於延續題目。","body":"iGEM publishes more than the winners. `api.igem.org` returns the full accepted roster for every season — 423 teams in 2026, 413 in 2025, 391 in 2024 — together with the medal that nearly every one of them earns. That is a complete entrant list, not a winners' list, so one half of this question escapes survivorship bias outright: whether *returning* is associated with doing better can be measured on the whole field. One warning for anyone repeating this. Team IDs are reissued every season — Heidelberg is 5237, then 5775, then 6249 — so names are the only key that holds.\n\n**Returning is common, and it tracks with results.** 284 of the 423 teams accepted in 2026 had also been accepted in 2023, 2024 or 2025. Those returners took Gold 168 times out of 284 (59 percent) against 58 of 139 (42 percent) for teams with no entry in three years; they reached the Top 10 24 times against 6; they won or were nominated for a special or village prize 107 times against 36. Six of the seven Grand Prize winners and runners-up had competed before, the exception being Stanford University. None of that is evidence for carrying a problem across years. A team that returns has a laboratory, a supervisor, a budget line and a wiki template that already works. Returning measures institutional survival, not the continuity of a question.\n\n**The thing this tab actually claims is rare to the point of being unmeasurable.** Michigan kept *Magnetospirillum magneticum* and its tumour-seeking behaviour from a 2025 ovarian-cancer project into MagNav. NCKU-Tainan went from ByeFilm, against implant biofilm, to Capture, against the quorum-sensing signals that build it. XJTLU-Software turned the SPADE antimicrobial-peptide database into the AMPilot workbench. LYON followed fluorinated pollutants from FLUOROBREAKER to trifluoroacetate in BioThetis. NU Boston stayed on post-wildfire soil. That is the complete list. The other 73 started on something unrelated: TU Delft from an oral phage vaccine to an implant coating, Cornell from Martian perchlorate to a smart bandage, Lambert-GA from Lyme disease to honeybees, UAlberta from wildfire foam to dry eye. **Zero of the six returning Grand Prize teams continued a line.**\n\nAnd where continuation does happen, the handover is almost never written down. Across all 106 team files and every wiki we could read, three teams credit their own predecessor with anything at all: LYON lists *iGEM Lyon 2025 (inherited plasmids)* among its partners, in the same list as Berlin and Wageningen — its own former self, credited like an outside collaborator. DTU-Denmark says its three enzyme-discovery tracks were settled after advice from the 2025 team's dry-lab head. Jilin-China carries its 5C Guidelines over from 2025. Michigan, NCKU-Tainan, XJTLU-Software and NU Boston continue a project line without saying on their Description page that this is what they are doing.\n\n**So the argument on this tab is untested, not refuted — and iGEM is the wrong instrument for testing it.** Five continuers, all Undergrad, all Gold, one of them in the Top 10, cannot be compared with 73 fresh starts or with anyone else; at that rate the whole 2026 field would hold about eighteen. Answering the question properly needs the sample we did not build: the project content of all 413 teams accepted in 2025 and all 423 accepted in 2026, every returning team classified as continuing or fresh, with medals and prizes attached to all of them — the entrant lists, not the decorated ones. The rosters and the medals are already public; the missing work is reading roughly 280 pairs of wikis. Even then the result would be a rate difference across perhaps twenty continuers, which is a pattern and not a cause. The honest position is that GEMS is proposing something iGEM has barely tried.","body_zh":"iGEM 公開的不只是得獎名單。`api.igem.org` 會回傳每一季完整的正式參賽名冊——2026 年 423 隊、2025 年 413 隊、2024 年 391 隊——以及幾乎每一隊都拿得到的獎牌等級。那是一份完整的參賽者清單，不是得獎者清單；因此這個問題有一半可以完全避開倖存者偏誤：「重複參賽」是否伴隨更好的成績，可以在全體隊伍上量出來。要重做這件事的人請注意一點：隊伍編號每一季都會重新發放——Heidelberg 是 5237、然後 5775、再來 6249——所以唯一靠得住的對照鍵是隊名。\n\n**重複參賽很普遍，而且和成績相關。** 2026 年正式參賽的 423 隊中，有 284 隊在 2023、2024 或 2025 年也正式參賽過。這些回鍋隊伍拿到金牌的比例是 284 隊中的 168 隊（59%），三年內未曾參賽的隊伍則是 139 隊中的 58 隊（42%）；進入 Top 10 的是 24 比 6；拿下或入圍特別獎與 village 獎的是 107 比 36。七個大獎與亞軍席次中有六個由先前參賽過的隊伍取得，唯一的例外是 Stanford University。這些都不足以證明「把題目帶過好幾年」有用。一支回來的隊伍，手上已經有實驗室、有指導老師、有一條預算、有一套能跑的 wiki 模板。重複參賽量到的是機構活得下來，不是問題本身的延續。\n\n**這一頁真正主張的那件事，罕見到無法量測。** Michigan 把 2025 年卵巢癌專案中的 *Magnetospirillum magneticum* 及其趨向腫瘤的特性延續到 MagNav。NCKU-Tainan 從對付植入物生物膜的 ByeFilm，走到攔截生物膜形成訊號的 Capture。XJTLU-Software 把 SPADE 抗菌胜肽資料庫變成 AMPilot 工作台。LYON 沿著含氟污染物，從 FLUOROBREAKER 一路走到 BioThetis 的三氟乙酸。NU Boston 留在野火後的土壤。這就是全部了。其餘 73 支做的是完全不相干的題目：TU Delft 從口服噬菌體疫苗轉到植入物鍍層，Cornell 從火星過氯酸鹽轉到智慧敷料，Lambert-GA 從萊姆病轉到蜜蜂，UAlberta 從野火泡沫轉到乾眼症。**六支回鍋的大獎隊伍中，延續題目線的是零支。**\n\n而且就算真的延續了，交接幾乎都沒有被寫下來。在全部 106 份隊伍檔案以及所有讀得到的 wiki 裡，只有三支隊伍把自己的前一屆列為任何東西的來源：LYON 在合作夥伴名單中列出 *iGEM Lyon 2025（承接下來的質體）*，和 Berlin、Wageningen 並列——把自己的前身當成外部合作者來標註。DTU-Denmark 寫明三條酵素探索路線是在徵詢 2025 年隊伍乾實驗室負責人的建議後才定案。Jilin-China 把 5C Guidelines 從 2025 年延續下來。而 Michigan、NCKU-Tainan、XJTLU-Software 與 NU Boston 延續了題目線，卻沒有在 Description 頁上說明自己正在這樣做。\n\n**所以這一頁的論點是「尚未被檢驗」，不是「已被推翻」——而且 iGEM 並不是檢驗它的合適工具。** 五支延續者，全部是大學部、全部拿金牌、其中一支進了 Top 10；這樣的數量無法和 73 支重新開始的隊伍相比，也無法和任何人相比。依這個比例推算，2026 年全體隊伍裡大約也只有十八支。要正確回答這個問題，需要一份我們沒有建立的樣本：2025 年全部 413 支與 2026 年全部 423 支正式參賽隊伍的專案內容，把每一支回鍋隊伍判定為延續或重啟，並且為所有隊伍附上獎牌與獎項——用的是參賽者名單，不是得獎者名單。名冊與獎牌都已經是公開的，缺的是讀完大約 280 對 wiki 的工。就算做完了，得到的也只是大約二十支延續者之間的比例差異，那是一個樣態，不是一個因果。誠實的說法是：GEMS 打算做的，是 iGEM 幾乎沒有試過的事。","cards":[{"kicker":"Sample","kicker_zh":"樣本","title":"The whole field, not just the decorated","title_zh":"拿到的是全體，不只是得獎者","body":"iGEM's public API returns every accepted team for every season plus the medal each one earned, so return rates and medal outcomes are measured on the complete 2026 field rather than on this report's 106 team files. Only the continuation question is stuck inside the decorated sample.","body_zh":"iGEM 的公開 API 可以取得每一季所有正式參賽隊伍，以及每一隊拿到的獎牌，因此重複參賽率與獎牌結果是在 2026 年全體隊伍上量的，而不是在本報告的 106 份隊伍檔案上。只有「是否延續題目」這一題被困在得獎者樣本裡。","chips":["423 accepted in 2026","413 in 2025","391 in 2024","team IDs change every year"],"chips_zh":["2026 年 423 支正式參賽","2025 年 413 支","2024 年 391 支","隊伍編號每年重發"]},{"kicker":"Confound","kicker_zh":"干擾因子","title":"Returning is not continuing","title_zh":"重複參賽不等於延續題目","body":"Teams that come back do better, and that gap is measured without survivorship bias. But a returning team brings a laboratory, a supervisor, a budget and a working wiki, not necessarily a question. The gap belongs to institutional survival, and reading it as evidence for multi-year problems would be laundering it.","body_zh":"回鍋的隊伍成績較好，而且這個差距是在沒有倖存者偏誤的情況下量到的。但一支回來的隊伍帶回來的是實驗室、指導老師、預算和一套能用的 wiki，不一定是一個問題。這個差距屬於機構的存活能力；把它讀成「題目跨年有效」的證據，就是在替結論漂白。","chips":["284 of 423 returned","gold 59% vs 42%","Top 10 24 vs 6","6 of 7 Grand Prize teams returned"],"chips_zh":["423 支中有 284 支是回鍋","金牌 59% 對 42%","Top 10 24 對 6","7 支總冠軍級隊伍中 6 支回鍋"]},{"kicker":"The five","kicker_zh":"那五支","title":"Every continuer in the decorated sample","title_zh":"得獎樣本中全部的延續者","body":"Michigan carried a magnetotactic tumour-seeking chassis forward; NCKU-Tainan moved from biofilm to the quorum-sensing signal behind it; XJTLU-Software grew a database into a workbench; LYON followed fluorinated pollutants from PFAS to trifluoroacetate and inherited the plasmids; NU Boston stayed on post-wildfire soil. All five are Undergrad, all five took Gold, one reached the Top 10.","body_zh":"Michigan 把趨磁、趨向腫瘤的底盤延續下來；NCKU-Tainan 從生物膜轉向形成生物膜的群體感應訊號；XJTLU-Software 把一個資料庫長成一個工作台；LYON 沿著含氟污染物從 PFAS 走到三氟乙酸，並承接了質體；NU Boston 留在野火後的土壤。五支全部是大學部、全部拿金牌，其中一支進入 Top 10。","chips":["Michigan","NCKU-Tainan","XJTLU-Software","LYON","NU Boston"],"chips_zh":["Michigan","NCKU-Tainan","XJTLU-Software","LYON","NU Boston"]},{"kicker":"Handover","kicker_zh":"交接","title":"The inheritance is almost never written down","title_zh":"承接下來的東西幾乎從不被寫下來","body":"LYON is the only team in 106 that records a physical inheritance, and it does so by listing its own 2025 team among its partners, beside Berlin and Wageningen. DTU-Denmark credits the previous dry-lab head with advice; Jilin-China carries a framework over. Four of the five continuers never mention the predecessor at all, which means a reader cannot see the arc even when there is one.","body_zh":"106 支隊伍中，只有 LYON 記錄了實體的承接，而且是把自己 2025 年的隊伍列進合作夥伴名單，和 Berlin、Wageningen 並列。DTU-Denmark 把建議歸功給前一屆乾實驗室負責人；Jilin-China 延續了一套框架。五支延續者中有四支完全沒有提到前一屆——這表示就算真的有一條跨年的線，讀者也看不見。","chips":["3 of 106 credit their own last year","4 of 5 continuers say nothing","no wiki page records a handover"],"chips_zh":["106 支中只有 3 支感謝自己的前一屆","5 支延續者中有 4 支隻字未提","沒有任何一頁 wiki 記下交接"]},{"kicker":"Return rate","kicker_zh":"回鍋率","title":"Coming back is hardest in high school","title_zh":"高中組最難回來","body":"Return rates fall as the section gets younger, which is the structural fact underneath everything on this page: a programme that carries problems across years needs an institution that outlives its members, and high-school teams turn over fastest. GEMS is a high-school programme.","body_zh":"組別越年輕，回鍋率越低，而這正是本頁一切的結構性前提：一個要讓題目跨年的計畫，需要一個比成員活得更久的組織，而高中隊伍的人員更替最快。GEMS 正是一個高中計畫。","chips":["Undergrad 160 of 201","Overgrad 49 of 75","High School 75 of 147"],"chips_zh":["大學組 201 支中 160 支","研究生組 75 支中 49 支","高中組 147 支中 75 支"]}],"table":{"head":["Group","Teams","Gold","Top 10","Special or village prize"],"head_zh":["分組","隊伍數","金牌","Top 10","特別獎或 village 獎"],"rows":[["Returned: entered 2023, 2024 or 2025","284 of 423","168 (59%)","24 (8.5%)","107 (38%)"],["New: no entry in three years","139 of 423","58 (42%)","6 (4.3%)","36 (26%)"],["Continued a project line (decorated teams only, not comparable to the rows above)","5 of 78 checked","5","1","4"]],"rows_zh":[["回鍋：2023、2024 或 2025 年參賽過","423 之中的 284","168（59%）","24（8.5%）","107（38%）"],["新隊：三年內未曾參賽","423 之中的 139","58（42%）","6（4.3%）","36（26%）"],["延續題目線（僅限得獎隊伍，無法與上面兩列相比）","查核的 78 之中的 5","5","1","4"]]},"checklist":["Stop citing iGEM results as support for the multi-year claim on this tab; mark it as untested and let this section be the reason.","Keep a dated public file per problem showing what was carried forward each year, because no iGEM wiki makes a continuation visible from outside.","Write a handover per problem — what was tried, what failed, what material and data exist — and have the next year's owner accept it in writing.","Name the physical inheritance the way LYON names its plasmids: strains, devices, datasets and scripts, listed with the year they came from.","If GEMS enters iGEM, draw the season's project from a problem already in its second year, and say so on the wiki, which four of the five continuers in 2026 did not.","Measure the claim on GEMS itself: for every problem, record how many years it has been carried and what number moved in each of them."],"checklist_zh":["不要再引用 iGEM 的成績來支持本頁的跨年主張；把它標記為尚未檢驗，並以這一節作為理由。","每一個題目都留一份標了日期的公開檔案，記錄每一年承接了什麼——因為沒有任何一個 iGEM wiki 能讓外人看見延續。","每個題目都寫一份交接文件：試過什麼、什麼失敗了、留下哪些材料與資料，並且由下一年的負責人書面簽收。","像 LYON 列出質體那樣，把承接下來的實體清楚具名：菌株、裝置、資料集與程式，並標註它們來自哪一年。","如果 GEMS 要參加 iGEM，就從已經進入第二年的題目裡取這一季的專案，並且寫在 wiki 上——2026 年的五支延續者中，有四支沒有這麼做。","用 GEMS 自己來檢驗這個主張：每一個題目都記錄它被帶了幾年，以及每一年有哪一個數字動了。"],"method":"Three sources. First, this report's 106 decorated 2026 team files. Second, iGEM's public API (api.igem.org/v1), which returns the full accepted roster for 2023 (391), 2024 (391), 2025 (413) and 2026 (423) plus every award including medals, so medal and prize outcomes are counted on the whole 2026 field and not on winners alone. Third, the 2025 and 2024 team wikis, read for every repeat entrant among the 106. Teams were matched across years by lower-cased, punctuation-stripped name, because team IDs are reissued every season (Heidelberg: 5237, 5775, 6249); a team that changes its name between seasons would therefore be counted as new, and we found no way to detect that. 'Continued a project line' means the 2026 project shares its problem and its technical approach with the team's own previous project, judged by reading both; it is our judgement, not the teams' declaration, because only three teams in 106 declare anything of the kind. What this cannot see, and it is most of the ballgame: continuation was classified only inside the decorated sample, so a team that continued a project and finished without a prize is invisible to us, and so is a team that continued and did worse — textbook survivorship bias, and the reason no claim is made here about continuation paying off. Three repeat entrants could not be classified at all (Stockholm's 2025 wiki is the unedited iGEM template, ASIJ-Tokyo has no 2025 wiki, Madrid-UCM's 2024 wiki is an empty shell), so the denominator is 78 of 81. Separately, the return-rate and medal comparison is complete for the 2026 field but is not causal: returning is confounded with laboratory access, supervision, funding and institutional age, none of which we measured, and medals are awarded against a checklist rather than on a scale, so the Gold rate is a floor measure of quality at best. Villages were not compared for continuation, because five cases cannot be split.","method_zh":"三個來源。第一，本報告 106 份 2026 年得獎隊伍檔案。第二，iGEM 的公開 API（api.igem.org/v1），可取得 2023 年（391 隊）、2024 年（391 隊）、2025 年（413 隊）與 2026 年（423 隊）完整的正式參賽名冊，以及包含獎牌在內的所有獎項；因此獎牌與獎項的統計是在 2026 年全體隊伍上做的，不是只看得獎者。第三，106 支中每一支回鍋隊伍的 2025 與 2024 年 wiki。跨年度的隊伍對照是以轉小寫、去標點後的隊名進行，因為隊伍編號每一季都會重新發放（Heidelberg：5237、5775、6249）；若有隊伍在兩季之間改名，就會被我們算成新隊，而我們找不到辨識這種情況的方法。「延續題目線」指的是 2026 年的專案在問題與技術路線上都與該隊自己前一年的專案相連，由我們讀完兩邊後判定；這是我們的判斷，不是隊伍自己的宣告，因為 106 支中只有三支做過類似的宣告。而這個計數看不見的部分，正是整件事的關鍵：延續與否只在得獎樣本內判定，所以一支延續了題目卻沒有拿到獎的隊伍，我們完全看不到；一支延續了題目但表現更差的隊伍也一樣——這是教科書等級的倖存者偏誤，也正是本節不對「延續是否值得」下任何結論的原因。另有三支回鍋隊伍完全無法判定（Stockholm 的 2025 wiki 是未編輯的 iGEM 範本、ASIJ-Tokyo 沒有 2025 wiki、Madrid-UCM 的 2024 wiki 是空殼），因此分母是 81 之中的 78。另外，回鍋率與獎牌的比較雖然涵蓋 2026 年全體隊伍，但不具因果性：重複參賽與實驗室取得、指導人力、經費與組織年資互相糾纏，而這些我們都沒有量；獎牌又是依檢核表而非量尺頒發，所以金牌比例頂多只是品質的下限指標。至於 village 之間的延續差異，我們沒有比較，因為五個案例無法再切分。"},{"id":"picks-decide","tab":"picks","order":40,"kicker":"The instrument","kicker_zh":"決策工具","title":"Ten questions to run a candidate topic through, and what a bad answer looks like","title_zh":"把候選題目跑過的十個問題，以及壞答案長什麼樣子","lede":"Each question exists because something in this report measured it. Run every candidate through all ten in one sitting and write the answers down; the point is not a score but a shape — a topic that cannot answer the first two is not a candidate, however interesting it is.","lede_zh":"每一個問題都存在，是因為本報告量過它。把每個候選題目一次跑完這十題，並把答案寫下來；重點不是分數，而是形狀——一個答不出前兩題的題目，不管多有趣，都不算候選。","body":"**Questions one and two are gates, not scores.** They are the only ones with a measured, two-direction basis, so a candidate that fails them is capped before the season starts no matter what it scores on the other seven. Everything from question four down is either a floor GEMS already clears or a reach question — valuable, but not the thing that decides a placing.\n\n**Write the answers in the partner's words and in their units wherever a person is involved.** The governance note for the Science for Good pipeline makes this a rule for a reason: of 106 decorated teams, 71 closed a stakeholder-to-design loop but only nine or ten of those closed one with somebody who was not a credentialled technical expert. A topic whose only outside voice is a professor is the normal case, and it is also the case that produced no non-expert evidence anywhere in the field.\n\n**Question ten was added by the PI, and it changes what counts as a good answer to all the others** — a candidate that scores well on the first nine but has no path to a citable result is a season that ends at the Jamboree. **Question nine is the one GEMS got wrong in 2026**, and it is the cheapest to fix. Write the sentence you want a judge to repeat, then open your own results page and try to break it. If the results page contradicts it, you have found the problem while you can still fix it rather than after the freeze.","body_zh":"**第一題和第二題是關卡，不是分數。**它們是唯一具備量測基礎、而且從兩個方向都成立的問題，所以一個過不了這兩題的候選，不管在其他七題拿幾分，賽季開始前就已經被設了上限。第四題以下的一切，要麼是 GEMS 早就跨過的門檻，要麼是觸及範圍的問題——有價值，但不是決定名次的那件事。\n\n**只要涉及人，就用對方的話和對方的單位把答案寫下來。**科學向善清單的治理章節把這件事訂成規則是有原因的：106 支得獎隊伍中，有 71 支閉合了利害關係人到設計的迴路，但其中只有九到十支是和沒有專業資格的人閉合的。一個題目如果唯一的外部聲音是教授，那是常態——而那也正是整個領域都沒能產出任何非專業者證據的那個常態。\n\n**第十題是 PI 加進來的，而它改變了前面每一題的好答案長什麼樣子**——一個前九題都答得好、卻沒有路徑通往可被引用成果的候選，就是一個在 Jamboree 結束的賽季。**第九題是 GEMS 2026 年做錯的那一題**，而它也是最便宜修的。先寫下你希望評審重複的那句話，然後打開自己的結果頁，試著把它推翻。如果結果頁反駁了它，你是在還能修的時候發現問題，而不是在凍結之後。","cards":[{"kicker":"Gate 1","kicker_zh":"關卡一","title":"What is the real target, and can we hold it in our hands by week six?","title_zh":"真實標的是什麼，我們能不能在第六週之前親手拿到它？","body":"A good answer names a physical thing and a route to it: this soil from this field, this water from this plant, this larva of this species, this sample from this clinic, and the person who will hand it over. A bad answer is \"we will use a standard strain and argue it represents the field case\", or \"we will spike a buffer\". Seven of the seven High School Top 10 teams that missed the podium gave the bad answer. Week six matters because a sample you cannot obtain until week eighteen cannot carry the headline result.","body_zh":"好答案會指名一個實體的東西和一條取得的路徑：這塊田的這份土、這座廠的這份水、這個物種的這隻幼蟲、這間診所的這份樣本，以及會把它交給你的那個人。壞答案是「我們會用標準菌株，然後論證它代表現場情況」，或是「我們會在緩衝液裡加標準品」。七支沒上頒獎臺的高中組 Top 10 隊伍，七支都給了壞答案。第六週很重要，因為一份要等到第十八週才拿到的樣本，撐不起標題結果。","chips":["names a thing and a person","not a spiked buffer","week six, not week eighteen"],"chips_zh":["指名一個東西和一個人","不是加標準品的緩衝液","第六週，不是第十八週"]},{"kicker":"Gate 2","kicker_zh":"關卡二","title":"What will we measure on it, with which instrument we already own?","title_zh":"我們要在它上面量什麼，用我們已經有的哪一台儀器？","body":"A good answer names the readout, the instrument, the units and roughly how many samples a week it can process. A bad answer needs a machine the school does not have, or needs an instrument built first — because then the instrument becomes the project and the measurement slips to the end of the season. GEMS already holds a Best Measurement and a Best Hardware award, so this question is usually answerable; the failure mode is choosing a topic whose readout needs something new.","body_zh":"好答案會指名讀值、儀器、單位，以及大致一週能處理幾個樣本。壞答案需要學校沒有的機器，或需要先把儀器做出來——因為那樣儀器就會變成專案本身，而量測會被推到賽季末。GEMS 已經握有 Best Measurement 與 Best Hardware，所以這一題通常答得出來；真正的失敗模式是選了一個讀值需要全新設備的題目。","chips":["readout, instrument, units","throughput per week","no instrument-first projects"],"chips_zh":["讀值、儀器、單位","每週處理量","不要以儀器為先的專案"]},{"kicker":"Lever","kicker_zh":"槓桿","title":"What model will we fit to our own data, and which rows will we hold back?","title_zh":"我們要把什麼模型擬合到自家資料，又要留下哪些列不用？","body":"This is the 53%-against-23% question. A good answer names the model, the parameter it estimates, and the split rule decided **before** any data is seen — by batch, by run, by cluster, by antigen, by site. A bad answer is \"we will fit a curve to the data once we have it\". Only 12 of 30 Top 10 teams held anything back, so this is the scarcest lever available. TU Delft's rule is the one to copy: keep every row from the same source on the same side of the split.","body_zh":"這就是 53% 對 23% 那一題。好答案會指名模型、它要估計的參數，以及**在看到任何資料之前**就決定好的切分規則——依批次、依實驗場次、依群集、依抗原、依場址。壞答案是「等資料拿到再擬一條曲線」。30 支 Top 10 隊伍裡只有 12 支留存過任何資料，所以這是現有最稀少的槓桿。TU Delft 的規則值得照抄：同一個來源的每一列，都留在切分的同一側。","chips":["53% against 23%","split rule before data","12 of 30 managed it"],"chips_zh":["53% 對 23%","先定切分規則再看資料","30 支中 12 支做到"]},{"kicker":"Floor","kicker_zh":"門檻","title":"Which rival explanation could produce our result, and what arm kills it?","title_zh":"哪一個對手解釋也能產生我們的結果，哪一組實驗能殺掉它？","body":"Write this in week one and then stop thinking about it. **GEMS already scores a perfect five of five** on falsification controls and still placed outside the podium, so this cannot buy a placing — but it is also the cheapest possible loss if skipped, because 26 of 30 Top 10 teams did it. GEMS 2024 is the model: the empty-vector arm existed because \"We want to rule out the effect of *E. coli* in the death of mosquito larvae\". And when the arm cannot be run, say so: 23 of 30 named one they could not run, which is 7 of 7 on the podium.","body_zh":"第一週就寫好，然後不要再想它。**GEMS 的否證對照已經是滿分五類全有**，卻仍然沒上頒獎臺，所以這買不到名次——但跳過它也是最便宜的損失，因為 30 支 Top 10 隊伍中有 26 支做了。GEMS 2024 年就是範本：那一組空載體對照之所以存在，是因為「我們想排除 *E. coli* 在蚊蟲幼蟲死亡中的作用」。而當那一組做不出來，就寫出來：30 支中有 23 支指名了自己沒能做的那一組，而這在頒獎臺上是 7 比 7。","chips":["GEMS scores 5 of 5","26 of 30 did it","name the arm you cannot run"],"chips_zh":["GEMS 五類全有","30 支中 26 支做了","指名你做不出來的那一組"]},{"kicker":"Reach","kicker_zh":"觸及範圍","title":"Who outside GEMS has already said they want this, in their own words?","title_zh":"GEMS 以外，已經有誰用自己的話說過他想要這個？","body":"A good answer is a named person at a named site who described the problem **before** anyone from GEMS offered them a solution, recorded in their words and dated. A bad answer is a professor who confirmed the idea is technically sound — that is the normal case and it is also why only nine or ten of 106 decorated teams closed a design loop with a non-expert. If no such person exists yet, the topic is admissible only on probation, and finding that person is the first task rather than a later one.","body_zh":"好答案是一位在具名場域的具名人士，**在 GEMS 任何人向他提出解方之前**就描述過這個問題，而且用他自己的話記錄下來、標了日期。壞答案是一位教授確認這個想法技術上可行——那是常態，而那也正是 106 支得獎隊伍裡只有九到十支和非專業者閉合設計迴路的原因。如果這樣的人還不存在，這個題目只能以觀察期的身分入列，而找到那個人是第一件任務，不是後面的任務。","chips":["their words, dated","before you offered anything","9 or 10 of 106 managed it"],"chips_zh":["他自己的話，標日期","在你提出任何東西之前","106 支中九到十支做到"]},{"kicker":"Reach","kicker_zh":"觸及範圍","title":"Which multiplying audience does this topic give us access to?","title_zh":"這個題目讓我們接觸到哪一群會放大的人？","body":"Not how many people the topic lets us reach, but which **repeating** people. HongKong-JSS is the type specimen: four tiers of education, of which the one recorded as most durable was a two-day workshop for 30 local school teachers on PCR and agarose gel electrophoresis, plus a standing loan programme letting those teachers borrow DNA samples and equipment from the team. Thirty teachers who teach for years beats sixteen hundred children once, for the same effort. Ask of each candidate: whose professional practice could this change, and would the topic get us in the room with them?","body_zh":"不是這個題目能接觸到多少人，而是能接觸到哪一群**會重複的人**。HongKong-JSS 就是範本：四層教育推廣，其中被記錄為最耐久的那一層，是為 30 位本地學校教師辦的兩天工作坊，教 PCR 與瓊脂膠體電泳，再加上一個常設的借用方案，讓這些教師可以向團隊借 DNA 樣品與設備。三十位會教好幾年的老師，勝過一千六百個只來一次的孩子，而力氣是一樣的。對每個候選問一句：這個題目可能改變誰的專業工作方式，而它能不能讓我們進到那個房間裡？","chips":["30 teachers over 1,600 children","a standing loan programme","whose practice changes?"],"chips_zh":["30 位老師勝過 1,600 個孩子","一個常設的借用方案","誰的工作方式會改變？"]},{"kicker":"Reach","kicker_zh":"觸及範圍","title":"What does the tenth deployment cost against the first?","title_zh":"第十次佈署的成本，相對第一次是多少？","body":"This is the Science for Good admission criterion that most ideas fail. A good answer is a number and a direction: the tenth costs less because the protocol is written and the parts are in the Registry, or the tenth costs the same because every unit needs a new sensor. A bad answer treats the first deployment as the whole project. The 2026 field is blunt about this — across every award-winning repository checked, stars and forks were zero, and the only external-adoption figure found anywhere was Stanford's SynBase — whose frozen wiki states 750+ registered learners and 650+ discussion contributions as of 17 October 2026, while the live platform's own counter later read 837. That gap is the point: it is the one artefact in the sample that kept growing after the freeze.","body_zh":"這是科學向善的入列條件裡，最多想法過不了的那一條。好答案是一個數字和一個方向：第十次更便宜，因為流程已經寫好、元件已經在 Registry 裡；或者第十次一樣貴，因為每一台都需要一個新的感測器。壞答案是把第一次佈署當成整個專案。2026 年的全體資料對此很直白——所有查過的得獎程式庫，star 與 fork 全部為零，而整個領域唯一找到的外部採用數字來自 Stanford 的 SynBase——它凍結後的 wiki 寫的是截至 2026 年 10 月 17 日有 750 位以上註冊學習者與 650 則以上討論留言，而該平台自己的計數器後來顯示 837。這個差距正是重點：它是樣本中唯一一件在凍結之後還在成長的產出。","chips":["a number and a direction","zero stars across every repo","SynBase kept growing after freeze"],"chips_zh":["一個數字和一個方向","所有程式庫 star 全為零","SynBase 凍結後仍在成長"]},{"kicker":"Durability","kicker_zh":"耐久度","title":"What will we publish that still works a year after the freeze?","title_zh":"我們要公開什麼，在凍結一年後還能用？","body":"The measured answer is paper. Of 285 education files linked from 31 decorated 2026 wikis, **284 still download and none 404** — against 8 of 21 award-winning software tools still running and 6 of 20 instruments rebuildable. A PDF on `static.igem.wiki` needs no server. If the topic's output is software, the single habit that separated the live tools from the dead ones is buying a domain and hosting before freeze day; if it is hardware, the habit is exporting a geometry file, which 9 of 20 award-winning instruments never did. And there is a standing opening for a Taiwanese team: of 31 teams publishing education material, only three published anything in Traditional Chinese.","body_zh":"量測出來的答案是紙本。31 個得獎 2026 wiki 所連出的 285 份教育檔案中，**284 份至今仍可下載，沒有任何一份 404**——相對之下，21 個得獎軟體工具只有 8 個還跑得動，20 件儀器只有 6 件重建得出來。放在 `static.igem.wiki` 上的 PDF 不需要伺服器。如果題目的產出是軟體，那麼區分「活的工具」與「死的工具」的唯一習慣，就是在凍結日之前買好網域並上線；如果是硬體，習慣則是輸出幾何檔案，而 20 件得獎儀器裡有 9 件從未這麼做。而且台灣隊伍有一個一直空著的缺口：31 支公開教育材料的隊伍中，只有三支發表過任何繁體中文內容。","chips":["284 of 285 files still download","8 of 21 tools still run","3 of 31 published Traditional Chinese"],"chips_zh":["285 份中 284 份仍可下載","21 個工具中 8 個還能跑","31 支中 3 支發表繁體中文"]},{"kicker":"The 2026 mistake","kicker_zh":"2026 年的錯誤","title":"What is the one sentence we want a judge to repeat — and does our own results page support it?","title_zh":"我們希望評審重複的那一句話是什麼——而我們自己的結果頁撐得住它嗎？","body":"Write the sentence, then open your own results page and try to break it. GEMS 2026 failed exactly here: the home page sold \"On-demand — Green light switches production on when the environmental sensors and forecasts decide to\", while the results page said the ELISA showed no change over time and the model page said the reactor cannot be scheduled from the forecast. Note the order this question comes in: **last**. The headline is written from the results, not the other way round. Two cautions, both measured. Nominating one claim is necessary but not sufficient — the clearest headline among the seven non-podium High School teams placed nowhere. And closing the honesty gap will not move you up: across the Top 10, 21 of 29 teams over-claim and the podium averages a **wider** gap than everyone else. Do it because the claim should be true, not because it pays. **GEMS is joint-worst in the field on this**, so it is the cheapest credibility GEMS can buy.","body_zh":"先寫下那句話，然後打開自己的結果頁，試著把它推翻。GEMS 2026 年正是在這裡失手：首頁賣的是「On-demand——綠光在環境感測器與預報做出判斷時開啟生產」，而結果頁說 ELISA 隨時間沒有變化，模型頁說反應器無法由預報來排程。注意這一題的順序：**最後**。標題是從結果往回寫的，不是反過來。有兩項提醒，都量測過。「指名一個主張」是必要但不充分——七支非頒獎臺高中隊伍之中，標題最清楚的那一支什麼名次都沒有。而把誠實落差補起來並不會讓你往上移：在 Top 10 裡，29 支中有 21 支誇大，而頒獎臺的落差平均**還更大**。做這件事，是因為主張應該是真的，不是因為它划算。**GEMS 在這一項是全體並列最差**，所以這是 GEMS 能買到的最便宜的可信度。","chips":["write it last, from the results","GEMS joint-worst at 3","buys credibility, not placing"],"chips_zh":["最後才寫，而且從結果往回寫","GEMS 以 3 分並列最差","買到可信度，不是名次"]},{"kicker":"Novelty and the paper","kicker_zh":"新穎度與論文","title":"What would the paper be, and who has already written it?","title_zh":"這篇論文會是什麼，而誰已經寫過了？","body":"A good answer names the claim a referee would have to accept, the journal that publishes that kind of claim, and the closest existing paper **by title**. A bad answer is \"nobody in iGEM has done this\" — **iGEM is not the literature.** This report is built on 106 decorated teams, which is the most decorated tenth of one competition and not a sample of the field; a project can be unique across all 106 and entirely ordinary in PubMed. Check the literature before claiming the gap, and write down the closest thing you find even when it is uncomfortably close.\n\nThree distinctions decide whether a gap supports a paper. *Nobody has published this* is rare and valuable. *Nobody has published this in this application* is common and still publishable, usually as a shorter paper. *Nobody has published this at this scale or with this rigour* is the one a school team can most realistically reach, and it is how Lambert-GA won Best Model in 2026 — not with a new method, but by benchmarking the confidence metrics of existing ones against 5,721 labelled designs and publishing that its own eventual hit did not carry the best score.\n\nThe roadmap already asks for this and says why: one citable artefact a year changes how every later conversation starts. It is also the only deliverable that survives the wiki freeze unconditionally — 284 of 285 education files still download, 8 of 21 software tools still run, and a paper needs no server at all. Of 106 decorated teams only 3 credit their own predecessor with anything, and a paper is the cheapest way to stop being the fourth.","body_zh":"好答案會指名一位審稿人必須接受的那個主張、會刊登這類主張的期刊，以及最接近的既有論文**篇名**。壞答案是「iGEM 裡沒有人做過這個」——**iGEM 不是文獻。**這份報告建立在 106 支得獎隊伍之上，那是一場競賽中得獎最多的十分之一，不是這個領域的樣本；一個專案可以在 106 支之中獨一無二，而在 PubMed 裡平凡無奇。在宣稱那個空缺之前先查文獻，而且就算查到的東西近得讓人不舒服，也要把它寫下來。\n\n有三種區別決定一個空缺撐不撐得起一篇論文。*沒有人發表過這件事*，罕見而且珍貴。*沒有人在這個應用上發表過這件事*，常見，但仍然可以發表，通常是一篇較短的論文。*沒有人以這個規模或這個嚴謹度發表過這件事*，是學校隊伍最實際能做到的那一種——而 Lambert-GA 2026 年就是這樣拿下 Best Model 的：不是靠新方法，而是拿 5,721 筆有標籤的設計去檢驗既有方法的信賴度指標，並且公開說自己最後真正結合的那一個分數並不是最高的。\n\n路線圖本來就要求這件事，而且說明了理由：一年一件可被引用的產出，會改變之後每一次對話的起點。它也是唯一一種無條件撐過 wiki 凍結的交付成果——285 份教育檔案中有 284 份仍可下載、21 個軟體工具中只有 8 個還跑得動，而一篇論文根本不需要伺服器。106 支得獎隊伍中只有 3 支對自己的前一屆表示過任何感謝，而一篇論文是不成為第四支的最便宜方法。","chips":["name the closest paper by title","iGEM is not the literature","scale and rigour is the reachable gap"],"chips_zh":["指名最接近那篇論文的篇名","iGEM 不是文獻","規模與嚴謹度才是搆得到的空缺"]}],"table":{"head":["#","The question","Why it is on the list","A bad answer"],"head_zh":["#","問題","它為什麼在清單上","壞答案"],"rows":[["1","What is the real target, and can we hold it by week six?","**Gate.** The only finding supported both across the field and across GEMS's three seasons: 7 of 7 non-podium HS teams used a surrogate","\"A standard strain that represents the field case.\" Or a sample that arrives in week eighteen."],["2","What will we measure on it, with which instrument we already own?","**Gate.** An instrument that must be built first becomes the project, and the measurement slips to the end","\"We will build a reader for it.\" GEMS already holds Best Measurement and Best Hardware."],["3","What model will we fit, and which rows will we hold back?","**Lever.** 53% reached a Top 10 against 23%; only 12 of 30 Top 10 teams held anything back","\"We will fit a curve once we have the data.\" No split rule named in advance."],["4","Which rival explanation could produce our result, and what arm kills it?","**Floor.** 26 of 30 did it; GEMS scores a perfect 5 of 5 and still did not place","No named rival explanation. Also: running the arm and not saying which condition it failed to cover."],["5","Who outside GEMS has already said they want this, in their own words?","**Reach.** 71 of 106 closed a design loop, but only 9 or 10 with a non-expert","\"A professor confirmed it is technically sound.\" That is the normal case, not evidence of demand."],["6","Which multiplying audience does this give us access to?","**Reach.** HongKong-JSS trained 30 teachers and lent them equipment — recorded as its most durable tier","A headcount. \"We will reach 2,000 students\" is a count, not a multiplier."],["7","What does the tenth deployment cost against the first?","**Reach.** Stars and forks were zero across every award-winning repository checked; the one artefact that kept growing after the freeze was a teaching platform","Treating the first deployment as the whole project."],["8","What will we publish that still works a year after the freeze?","**Durability.** 284 of 285 education files still download; 8 of 21 software tools still run","Source code with localhost as its only address. A device with no geometry file."],["9","What is the one sentence we want a judge to repeat?","**The 2026 mistake, and a reversal.** 21 of 29 Top 10 teams over-claim and the podium's gap is wider, so this buys credibility rather than placing — but GEMS is joint-worst at 3","A sentence written before the results exist — or one the results page does not support."],["10","What would the paper be, and who has already written it?","**Novelty.** Added as a criterion by the PI. A citable artefact is the only deliverable that survives the freeze unconditionally, and only 3 of 106 teams credit a predecessor","\"Nobody in iGEM has done this.\" iGEM is 106 decorated teams, not the literature. Also: no named journal, and no closest paper identified"]],"rows_zh":[["1","真實標的是什麼，我們能不能在第六週之前拿到它？","**關卡。**唯一同時在全體與 GEMS 三季都成立的發現：七支非頒獎臺高中隊伍全用替代物","「一株能代表現場情況的標準菌株。」或是一份第十八週才會到的樣本。"],["2","我們要在它上面量什麼，用已經有的哪一台儀器？","**關卡。**必須先做出來的儀器會變成專案本身，而量測會被推到最後","「我們會做一台讀取器。」GEMS 已經握有 Best Measurement 與 Best Hardware。"],["3","我們要擬合什麼模型，又要留下哪些列不用？","**槓桿。**53% 進 Top 10 對 23%；30 支 Top 10 隊伍裡只有 12 支留存過資料","「等資料拿到再擬一條曲線。」事前沒有指名切分規則。"],["4","哪一個對手解釋也能產生我們的結果，哪一組實驗能殺掉它？","**門檻。**30 支中 26 支做了；GEMS 滿分五類全有，卻仍沒有名次","沒有指名對手解釋。另一種：做了那一組，卻沒說它沒能涵蓋哪個條件。"],["5","GEMS 以外，已經有誰用自己的話說過他想要這個？","**觸及範圍。**106 支中 71 支閉合了設計迴路，但只有九到十支是和非專業者閉合的","「一位教授確認技術上可行。」那是常態，不是需求的證據。"],["6","這個題目讓我們接觸到哪一群會放大的人？","**觸及範圍。**HongKong-JSS 訓練 30 位教師並把設備借給他們——被記錄為最耐久的那一層","一個人數。「我們會接觸 2,000 位學生」是計數，不是放大器。"],["7","第十次佈署的成本，相對第一次是多少？","**觸及範圍。**所有查過的得獎程式庫，star 與 fork 全部為零；唯一在凍結後還在成長的產出，是一個教學平台","把第一次佈署當成整個專案。"],["8","我們要公開什麼，在凍結一年後還能用？","**耐久度。**285 份教育檔案中 284 份仍可下載；21 個軟體工具中 8 個還跑得動","只有原始碼，而唯一的位址是 localhost。或一件沒有幾何檔案的裝置。"],["9","我們希望評審重複的那一句話是什麼？","**2026 年的錯誤，而且是一個反轉。**29 支 Top 10 隊伍中 21 支誇大，而頒獎臺的落差更大，所以這買到的是可信度而不是名次——但 GEMS 以 3 分並列最差","在結果還不存在時就寫好的句子——或結果頁撐不住的句子。"],["10","這篇論文會是什麼，而誰已經寫過了？","**新穎度。**由 PI 加入的判準。可被引用的產出是唯一無條件撐過凍結的交付成果，而 106 支隊伍中只有 3 支感謝過前一屆","「iGEM 裡沒有人做過這個。」iGEM 是 106 支得獎隊伍，不是文獻。另一種：沒有指名期刊，也沒有找出最接近的那篇論文"]]},"checklist":["Run every candidate through all nine in one sitting, and write the answers down rather than discussing them. An unwritten answer is usually a missing one.","Treat questions one and two as gates. A topic that fails either is not a candidate, however interesting the biology is.","Decide the held-back data split rule in week one, before any data exists, and record which rows are out and why.","Write the rival explanation and its killing arm in week one too, then stop. Controls are a floor GEMS already clears at full marks.","For question five, record the outside person's words verbatim and in their own units, and date it. A professor's technical blessing is not an answer to this question.","Prefer the candidate that puts you in a room with people who repeat the lesson professionally — teachers, extension officers, technicians, inspectors — over the one with the bigger headcount.","Answer question eight by choosing the artefact, not by hoping: paper if you want it to survive, a bought domain and hosting before freeze day if it is software, a geometry file if it is hardware.","Check the literature before claiming a gap, and write down the closest paper you find by title. Being unique across 106 decorated iGEM teams is not the same as being unique in PubMed.","Write question nine last, from the results page, and have someone who did not write the wiki check the headline against the model page.","Keep the filled-in sheet for every candidate you reject, with the question that killed it. Only 3 of 106 decorated teams credit their own predecessor with anything, and a rejected-topic file is the cheapest way not to be the fourth."],"checklist_zh":["把每個候選題目一次跑完這九題，而且把答案寫下來，不要只是討論。沒寫下來的答案，通常就是沒有答案。","把第一題和第二題當成關卡。過不了任何一題的題目就不算候選，不管那個生物學多有趣。","第一週就決定留存資料的切分規則，在任何資料存在之前，並記下哪些列被留在外面、為什麼。","對手解釋和殺掉它的那一組實驗也在第一週寫好，然後停手。對照是 GEMS 早就以滿分跨過的門檻。","第五題要把外部人士的話逐字記下、用他自己的單位，並標上日期。教授在技術上的肯定不是這一題的答案。","寧可選那個讓你進到「會把這堂課專業地重複下去的人」房間裡的候選——老師、推廣人員、技術員、稽查員——而不是人數比較多的那個。","第八題要靠選擇產出形式來回答，而不是靠期待：想要它活下來就用紙本；是軟體就在凍結日前買好網域並上線；是硬體就輸出幾何檔案。","在宣稱一個空缺之前先查文獻，並把查到最接近的那篇論文連篇名一起寫下來。在 106 支得獎 iGEM 隊伍裡獨一無二，和在 PubMed 裡獨一無二，是兩回事。","第九題最後才寫，而且從結果頁往回寫，再請一個沒寫過 wiki 的人拿標題去對模型頁。","把每一個被你否決的候選題目的答案表留下來，並寫上是哪一題殺掉它的。106 支得獎隊伍裡只有 3 支對自己的前一屆表示過任何感謝，而一份「否決題目檔」是最便宜的方法，讓你們不要成為第四支。"],"method":"This is an instrument rather than a measurement. The nine questions are this report's construction; what is measured is the reason each one is on the list, and every figure cited is measured elsewhere in this report with its own limits stated where it is reported. Sources: judging-top10 and gems-three-seasons for the real-target gate and the 2026 landing-page contradiction; the dry-lab analyses for the model-loop figure; falsification-controls for the five control types and the disclosure flag; good-governance and ihp-depth for the outside-person criterion and the expert-closed-loop figures; picks-leverage for the multiplying-audience question; education-afterlife, software-afterlife and hardware-afterlife for the durability figures; good-definition for the cost-of-the-tenth criterion. Two limits apply throughout. The sample is decorated teams only, so no figure here describes the competition at large unless it is drawn from iGEM's full accepted roster. And the Top 10 comparisons rest on 30 teams and seven podium places, which cannot support a causal claim -- the questions are a way of thinking, not a predictive model, and a candidate that answers all nine well can still lose.","method_zh":"這是一套工具，不是一項量測。九個問題是本報告自己的建構；被量測的是「每一題為什麼在清單上」的理由，而所引用的每一個數字都量測於本報告其他處，並在該處載明自己的限制。來源：真實標的關卡與 2026 年首頁矛盾來自 judging-top10 與 gems-three-seasons；模型迴路數字來自乾實驗室相關分析；五類對照與揭露旗標來自 falsification-controls；外部人士條件與專家閉合迴路數字來自 good-governance 與 ihp-depth；會放大的人那一題來自 picks-leverage；耐久度數字來自 education-afterlife、software-afterlife 與 hardware-afterlife；第十次成本的條件來自 good-definition。全篇適用兩項限制。樣本僅限得獎隊伍，所以除非取自 iGEM 完整正式參賽名單，本節沒有任何數字在描述整個賽事。而 Top 10 的各項比較建立在 30 支隊伍與七個頒獎臺名額上，撐不起因果主張——這九個問題是一種思考方式，不是預測模型；一個九題都答得很好的候選，仍然可能落敗。"},{"id":"team-resources","tab":"teams","order":40,"kicker":"Original analysis","kicker_zh":"原創分析","title":"What it actually costs to win","title_zh":"得獎究竟要付出什麼","lede":"Team size does not separate these winners from each other: across 84 decorated teams the correlation between headcount and number of awards is 0.06 (Spearman, p = 0.61), and within every section the Top 10 teams are statistically indistinguishable in size from the rest. What does vary, enormously, is the staff and the lab standing behind the students.","lede_zh":"團隊人數並不能把這些得獎隊伍彼此區分開來：在 84 支有人數可查的得獎隊伍中，人數與獎項數的相關係數只有 0.06（Spearman，p = 0.61），而且在每一個組別裡，Top 10 隊伍的規模在統計上都與其他得獎隊伍沒有差別。真正差距巨大的，是學生背後的指導人力與實驗室。","body":"**The null first.** Of the 106 decorated teams in this report, 84 publish enough to count their student members. Across those 84, the rank correlation between team size and number of awards is 0.06 (Spearman, p = 0.61). Splitting Top 10 teams from the other decorated teams inside the same section, the size difference is not significant anywhere: High School p = 0.21, Undergraduate p = 0.27, Overgraduate p = 0.27 (Mann-Whitney). The careful sentence is the long one. *Size does not separate winners from each other, and this sample — decorated teams only — cannot tell you whether it separates winners from the teams that did not place at all.* Nobody in this dataset lost, so no claim about the competition at large follows from it.\n\n**Medians, stated separately.** High School: median **17.5** students, range 6 to 60, counted for 38 of 40 teams. Undergraduate: median **17**, range 4 to 46, counted for 30 of 42. Overgraduate: median **12.5**, range 7 to 70, counted for 16 of 22. Twenty-two teams could not be counted at all, and the missing count is part of the result: Cornell renders its roster as a clickable temple with no list behind it, BGCFullerton as a filtered crew grid that never loads a name, HK-Joint-School as six school photographs with no individual names. A roster is a medal-criteria page nobody checks, so a surprising number of teams simply do not publish one in readable form.\n\n**The smallest team in any Top 10 was Princeton: nine undergraduates.** They finished second runner-up for the Grand Prize and won Best Foundational Advance. What they had instead of people is written plainly on their members page: two principal investigators running their own labs (Jared Toettcher, Josh Atkinson), one instructor who is a **postdoctoral fellow**, and one advisor who is a **PhD student**. Four named scientists for nine students. Three further substitutions are visible in the project itself. First, they chose one chassis — M13 phage — and demonstrated it across three unrelated applications, so the three \"projects\" shared a single wet-lab build. Second, they wrote SymPlify, a de novo binder design pipeline, so adding a target cost compute rather than months of antibody work; software did what extra hands would otherwise have done. Third, PITCCH handed the public a genuine unsolved sub-problem from the project with real print parameters, judged entries on one computational metric, and built the winning design in — converting outreach into contributed engineering at almost no labour cost. Princeton also publishes **no attributions page at all**, which is worth noting in a piece that treats attributions as the honest page.\n\n**The hidden-resource question, answered as honestly as the pages allow.** Of the 40 decorated high-school teams, **5 state that they worked in a university laboratory**: BGCFullerton (Chapman University, UC Irvine and California State University, Fullerton all recorded as providing laboratory access), Eton-College-UK (University of Greenwich, where the safety induction and the first bench work are logged), Labi-Taiwan (a BSL-1 laboratory at the Biotechnology Center of National Taiwan University), Yucai-SZ (a joint synthetic biology laboratory with the School of Synthetic Biology at Shenzhen University of Advanced Technology) and HangzhouFourteenAP (an unnamed \"university synthetic biology laboratory\"). A sixth, NFLSHS-CHINA, names a Shenzhen University professor as its advisor and carries a Shenzhen University logo in its sponsor strip but does not state lab access. **Of those five, none credits a graduate student or postdoc with hands-on wet-lab work.** Every such credit on every high-school wiki is worded as supervision, lecturing, training or guidance. Seven of the 40 high-school teams name a doctoral student, PhD candidate or postdoc somewhere in their staff list — HangzhouFourteenAP, QingdaoAcademy, GYHS, CHINAGuangdongShimen, Yucai-SZ, Labi-Taiwan and Worldshaper-Shanghai — and in all seven the role given is advisory. That is the honest answer, and it comes with an honest limit: the iGEM attributions form never asks who held the pipette, so a wiki cannot settle the question either way.\n\n**University teams are far more open about it, and the numbers are striking.** WageningenUR — 1st runner-up for the Overgraduate Grand Prize — lists **11 students against 13 named PIs and instructors**, most of the instructors PhD candidates and postdocs in Wageningen groups. Marburg lists 16 students against 17 instructors and advisors. UCL lists 6 students against 8. SDU-Denmark's instructors are four PhD students. Money, by contrast, is almost never published: **7 of 106 teams state any figure about their own funding.** BGCFullerton, a high-school team run out of a Boys and Girls Club, is the only one with anything resembling a ledger — IFC Advisors \"Provided $15,000 in proof-of-concept research support through the Boys & Girls Club of Fullerton\", the Beckman Foundation \"Provided a $10,000 grant for the team's research\", \"John Phelps donated $5,000 to support the MycoVela project\", and Opentrons \"Provided laboratory equipment with an approximate in-kind value of $28,000\". Eton-College-UK records \"an initial £10,000 fundraising target\"; XJTLU-China \"a total of RMB 20,000\"; Tsinghua-T RMB 100,000 from one sponsor; TU Delft \"over €2,500\"; Hongwen School a material cost of RMB 3,480.29; Marburg publishes only sponsorship tiers (€500–1,000, €1,000–4,999) rather than what it raised. Everyone else shows logos and no numbers.\n\n**And GEMS-Taiwan's own position, on the same terms.** GEMS fielded **35 students** in 2026 — 5 project leads, 12 student leaders, 14 members and 4 student advisors — with 6 instructors and 1 project advisor, registered with iGEM as a commercial organiser rather than a school. That is twice the high-school median of 17.5 and more than three times HangzhouFourteenAP, the smallest high-school Top 10. GEMS ran its own hardware and its own lab, and visited a National Taiwan University laboratory rather than being hosted in one. On the evidence here, the 2026 team was large for what it achieved, not small.","body_zh":"**先講虛無結果。** 本報告收錄的 106 支得獎隊伍中，有 84 支公開到足以數出學生人數。在這 84 支裡，團隊人數與獎項數的等級相關係數只有 0.06（Spearman，p = 0.61）。若在同一組別內把 Top 10 與其他得獎隊伍分開比較，規模差異在任何一組都不顯著：高中組 p = 0.21、大學部 p = 0.27、研究生組 p = 0.27（Mann-Whitney）。謹慎的說法要講長一點：*人數無法把得獎隊伍彼此區分開來；而本樣本只收錄得獎隊伍，因此無法告訴你人數能不能把得獎隊伍與完全沒有名次的隊伍區分開來。* 這份資料裡沒有輸家，所以它推不出任何關於整場競賽的結論。\n\n**中位數，分組分開講。** 高中組：中位數 **17.5** 人，全距 6 到 60，40 隊中數得出 38 隊。大學部：中位數 **17** 人，全距 4 到 46，42 隊中數得出 30 隊。研究生組：中位數 **12.5** 人，全距 7 到 70，22 隊中數得出 16 隊。有 22 支隊伍完全數不出來，而這個缺漏本身就是結果的一部分：Cornell 把成員名冊做成一座要用滑鼠點的神殿，背後沒有名單；BGCFullerton 做成會篩選的成員牆，但名字始終不載入；HK-Joint-School 只放六所學校的合照，沒有個別姓名。成員頁是獎牌條件裡沒人會去查的一頁，所以出乎意料多的隊伍，乾脆就不以可讀的形式公開它。\n\n**所有 Top 10 之中人數最少的是 Princeton：九位大學部學生。** 他們拿下大學部總冠軍第二亞軍，並贏得 Best Foundational Advance。他們用什麼取代人力，成員頁上寫得很清楚：兩位各自主持實驗室的主持人（Jared Toettcher、Josh Atkinson）、一位身分是**博士後研究員**的 instructor，以及一位身分是**博士生**的 advisor。九個學生，四位具名的科學家。專案本身還看得到三項替代。其一，他們只選一種底盤——M13 噬菌體——再把它用在三個彼此無關的應用上，所以三個「專案」共用同一套濕實驗室建構。其二，他們寫了 SymPlify，一條 de novo 結合蛋白設計流程，使得增加一個標的只要花運算資源，而不是花好幾個月做抗體；軟體做掉了原本要靠多一雙手才能做的事。其三，PITCCH 把專案裡一個真正未解的子問題連同真實列印參數交給大眾，以單一運算指標評分，再把得獎設計真的做進專案裡——幾乎不花人力就把科普活動轉成了實際的工程貢獻。順帶一提，Princeton **完全沒有 attributions 頁面**，在一篇把 attributions 視為最誠實一頁的分析裡，這點值得記上一筆。\n\n**隱藏資源的問題，就頁面所能支撐的程度誠實回答。** 40 支得獎高中隊伍中，**有 5 支明講自己在大學實驗室裡工作**：BGCFullerton（Chapman University、UC Irvine 與 California State University, Fullerton 都被記載為提供實驗室使用權）、Eton-College-UK（University of Greenwich，安全訓練與最初的實驗操作都登記在那裡）、Labi-Taiwan（National Taiwan University 生物技術中心的 BSL-1 實驗室）、Yucai-SZ（與 Shenzhen University of Advanced Technology 合成生物學院共建的聯合實驗室），以及 HangzhouFourteenAP（一間未具名的「大學合成生物學實驗室」）。第六支 NFLSHS-CHINA 把一位 Shenzhen University 的教授列為 advisor，贊助列也掛著該校標誌，但沒有寫到實驗室使用權。**這五支之中，沒有任何一支把動手做濕實驗的功勞歸給研究生或博士後。** 所有高中隊伍網站上的這類致謝，用字一律是督導、授課、訓練或指導。40 支高中隊伍中有 7 支在人員名單裡出現博士生、博士候選人或博士後——HangzhouFourteenAP、QingdaoAcademy、GYHS、CHINAGuangdongShimen、Yucai-SZ、Labi-Taiwan 與 Worldshaper-Shanghai——而這七支給的身分全是顧問性質。這就是誠實的答案，而它也附帶一個誠實的限制：iGEM 的 attributions 表格從來不問是誰握著微量吸管，所以網站本來就無法替這件事做出定論。\n\n**大學隊伍對此坦率得多，而且數字很驚人。** WageningenUR——研究生組總冠軍第一亞軍——列出 **11 位學生對 13 位具名的 PI 與 instructor**，其中多數 instructor 是 Wageningen 各研究群的博士候選人與博士後。Marburg 是 16 位學生對 17 位 instructor 與 advisor。UCL 是 6 位學生對 8 位。SDU-Denmark 的 instructor 則是四位博士生。相對地，錢幾乎從來不公開：**106 支隊伍中只有 7 支寫出任何一個與自身經費有關的數字。** 由一間 Boys and Girls Club 主辦的高中隊伍 BGCFullerton，是唯一有近似帳本的一支——IFC Advisors「Provided $15,000 in proof-of-concept research support through the Boys & Girls Club of Fullerton」、Beckman Foundation「Provided a $10,000 grant for the team's research」、「John Phelps donated $5,000 to support the MycoVela project」，以及 Opentrons「Provided laboratory equipment with an approximate in-kind value of $28,000」。Eton-College-UK 寫下「an initial £10,000 fundraising target」；XJTLU-China 是「a total of RMB 20,000」；Tsinghua-T 是單一贊助者的人民幣 100,000 元；TU Delft 是「over €2,500」；Hongwen School 則列出人民幣 3,480.29 元的材料費；Marburg 只公開贊助分級（€500–1,000、€1,000–4,999），而不是實際募得的金額。其餘所有隊伍都只放標誌，不放數字。\n\n**最後，用同一把尺量 GEMS-Taiwan 自己。** GEMS 在 2026 年投入 **35 位學生**——5 位專案負責人、12 位學生組長、14 位組員與 4 位學生顧問——搭配 6 位 instructor 與 1 位專案顧問，並以商業機構而非學校的身分向 iGEM 註冊。這是高中組中位數 17.5 的兩倍，也是高中組 Top 10 裡人數最少的 HangzhouFourteenAP 的三倍有餘。GEMS 自建硬體、自用實驗室，並且是去參訪 National Taiwan University 的實驗室，而不是被收容在裡面。就本文的證據而言，2026 年這支隊伍相對於它的成果是偏大的，不是偏小。","cards":[{"kicker":"Smallest Top 10","kicker_zh":"Top 10 中最小的一支","title":"Princeton: nine students, four scientists","title_zh":"Princeton：九個學生，四位科學家","body":"Nine undergraduates, 2nd runner-up for the Undergraduate Grand Prize and Best Foundational Advance winner. Named support: two PIs with their own labs, one instructor who is a postdoctoral fellow, one advisor who is a PhD student. The substitutions for headcount are visible in the design: one M13 chassis reused across three unrelated applications, a de novo binder pipeline so a new target costs compute rather than months of hands, and a public design contest whose winning entry was built into the project.","body_zh":"九位大學部學生，拿下大學部總冠軍第二亞軍與 Best Foundational Advance。具名的支援人力：兩位自己主持實驗室的 PI、一位身分為博士後研究員的 instructor、一位身分為博士生的 advisor。用什麼取代人力，從設計上就看得出來：同一套 M13 底盤重複用在三個互不相關的應用上；一條 de novo 結合蛋白設計流程，讓新增標的只花運算而不是好幾個月的人工；以及一場對外的設計競賽，得獎作品被真的做進專案裡。","chips":["9 students","2 PIs + 1 postdoc + 1 PhD student","No attributions page"],"chips_zh":["9 名學生","2 位 PI + 1 位博士後 + 1 位博士生","沒有 attributions 頁"]},{"kicker":"Smallest decorated teams","kicker_zh":"得獎隊伍中最小的幾支","title":"Six students is enough for a nomination","title_zh":"六個學生就足以拿到入圍","body":"CHINAGuangdongShimen fielded 6 students against 3 named staff and was nominated for Best Measurement (High School); its instructors are a South China University of Technology professor and an SCUT PhD candidate. PSI Korea fielded 6 students with 6 named staff and picked up three nominations. At undergraduate level XJTLU-Software reached a Best Software and AI nomination with 4 students, 2 instructors and 2 advisors, and CalPolySLO won Best Measurement with 5 students and a single PI.","body_zh":"CHINAGuangdongShimen 以 6 位學生對 3 位具名人員，入圍高中組 Best Measurement；其 instructor 分別是華南理工大學的教授與該校的博士候選人。PSI Korea 以 6 位學生搭配 6 位具名人員，拿下三項入圍。在大學部，XJTLU-Software 以 4 位學生、2 位 instructor 與 2 位 advisor 入圍 Best Software and AI；CalPolySLO 則以 5 位學生與單獨一位 PI 贏得 Best Measurement。","chips":["6, 6, 4, 5 students","All four won or were nominated","Narrow scope, named staff"],"chips_zh":["6、6、4、5 名學生","四支全都得獎或入圍","範圍收窄、人員具名"]},{"kicker":"More staff than students","kicker_zh":"指導人力多於學生","title":"WageningenUR: 11 students, 13 supervisors","title_zh":"WageningenUR：11 位學生，13 位指導者","body":"The Overgraduate Grand Prize 1st runner-up lists 11 students in its attributions form against 3 primary PIs and 10 instructors, most of them PhD candidates and postdocs across three Wageningen groups. Its own team page lists only 8 students; the attributions form lists 11. Marburg shows the same shape at 16 students to 17 instructors and advisors, and UCL at 6 to 8. On this evidence the scarce resource at university level is not students.","body_zh":"研究生組總冠軍第一亞軍在 attributions 表格中列出 11 位學生，對應 3 位 primary PI 與 10 位 instructor，後者多數是 Wageningen 三個研究群裡的博士候選人與博士後。該隊自己的團隊頁只列 8 位學生，attributions 表格卻列 11 位。Marburg 呈現同樣的形狀：16 位學生對 17 位 instructor 與 advisor；UCL 則是 6 對 8。就這些證據看，大學層級稀缺的資源並不是學生。","chips":["11 students / 13 staff","Team page said 8, the form said 11","Marburg 16 / 17; UCL 6 / 8"],"chips_zh":["11 名學生 / 13 名指導","團隊頁寫 8，表單寫 11","Marburg 16 / 17；UCL 6 / 8"]},{"kicker":"The only published ledger","kicker_zh":"唯一公開的帳本","title":"BGCFullerton writes the numbers down","title_zh":"BGCFullerton 把數字寫出來","body":"A high-school team run out of a Boys and Girls Club, not a school, and the only team in 106 that itemises money. Its external-contributions table records IFC Advisors providing “$15,000 in proof-of-concept research support”, a “$10,000 grant” from the Beckman Foundation, a “$5,000” individual donation, and Opentrons equipment “with an approximate in-kind value of $28,000”. It also records three separate universities — Chapman, UC Irvine and Cal State Fullerton — providing laboratory access.","body_zh":"這是一支由 Boys and Girls Club 而非學校主辦的高中隊伍，也是 106 支之中唯一逐項列出金額的一支。它的外部貢獻表記下 IFC Advisors 提供「$15,000 in proof-of-concept research support」、Beckman Foundation 的「$10,000 grant」、一筆「$5,000」的個人捐款，以及 Opentrons「with an approximate in-kind value of $28,000」的設備。同一張表也記下三所大學——Chapman、UC Irvine 與 Cal State Fullerton——分別提供實驗室使用權。","chips":["$15,000 + $10,000 + $5,000","$28,000 in-kind equipment","3 universities gave lab access"],"chips_zh":["$15,000 + $10,000 + $5,000","$28,000 實物設備","三所大學提供實驗室"]},{"kicker":"The whole field","kicker_zh":"整個賽場","title":"A third of the high-school section is run by a commercial organiser","title_zh":"高中組有三分之一是由營利機構帶隊","body":"Of the **147 accepted high-school teams** of 2026, iGEM's own registry records **53 under a commercial organiser**, 91 under a secondary school and 3 under a community lab. The undergraduate section has none. Among decorated teams the split is 14 commercial of 40 — and that is simply the base rate: **14 of 53 commercial high-school teams were decorated (26%), against 26 of 94 others (28%).** Being run as a programme rather than by a school confers nothing and costs nothing. GEMS-Taiwan is registered as commercial, so this is a description of what GEMS already is, not a verdict on it.","body_zh":"2026 年**正式參賽的 147 支高中隊伍**中，iGEM 官方名冊記錄**有 53 支由營利機構帶隊**、91 支由中學帶隊、3 支由社群實驗室帶隊。大學組一支也沒有。在得獎隊伍裡，40 支高中隊伍中有 14 支屬於營利機構——而這就只是基礎比率而已：**53 支營利機構高中隊伍中有 14 支得獎（26%），其餘 94 支中有 26 支得獎（28%）。** 以計畫形式運作、而不是由一所學校運作，既沒有加分也沒有減分。GEMS-Taiwan 登記的身分就是營利機構，所以這一段描述的是 GEMS 本來的樣子，不是對它的評價。","chips":["53 of 147 high-school teams","26% vs 28% decorated","undergraduate section: none"],"chips_zh":["147 支高中隊伍中 53 支","得獎率 26% 對 28%","大學組：0 支"]}],"table":{"head":["Team","Section","Students","Named PIs / instructors / advisors","Institution as registered","Result"],"head_zh":["團隊","組別","學生人數","具名 PI／instructor／advisor","註冊機構","成績"],"rows":[["XJTLU-Software","Undergrad","4","4 (2 instructors, 2 advisors)","Xi'an Jiaotong-Liverpool University","Best Software & AI nominee"],["CalPolySLO","Undergrad","5","1 (PI)","California Polytechnic State University","Best Measurement winner (Undergrad)"],["CHINAGuangdongShimen","High School","6","3 (incl. an SCUT professor and an SCUT PhD candidate)","Shimen High School","Best Measurement nominee (High School)"],["PSI Korea","High School","6","6 (2 PIs, 3 instructors, 1 advisor)","PSI Academy (commercial)","Three nominations"],["Princeton","Undergrad","9","4 (2 PIs, 1 postdoc, 1 PhD student)","Princeton University","Top 10; 2nd runner-up Grand Prize"],["UCNZ","Undergrad","10","4 (2 PIs, 2 instructors)","University of Canterbury","Undergrad Top 10"],["WageningenUR","Overgrad","11","13 (3 PIs, 10 instructors)","Wageningen UR","Top 10; 1st runner-up Grand Prize"],["HangzhouFourteenAP","High School","11","5 (mentors and instructors, one a PhD and postdoc)","Hangzhou No.14 High School, AP Center","High School Top 10; Best Village Project winner"]],"rows_zh":[["XJTLU-Software","大學部","4","4（2 位 instructor、2 位 advisor）","Xi'an Jiaotong-Liverpool University","Best Software & AI 入圍"],["CalPolySLO","大學部","5","1（PI）","California Polytechnic State University","大學部 Best Measurement 首獎"],["CHINAGuangdongShimen","高中組","6","3（含一位華南理工大學教授與一位該校博士候選人）","Shimen High School","高中組 Best Measurement 入圍"],["PSI Korea","高中組","6","6（2 位 PI、3 位 instructor、1 位 advisor）","PSI Academy（商業機構）","三項入圍"],["Princeton","大學部","9","4（2 位 PI、1 位博士後、1 位博士生）","Princeton University","Top 10；總冠軍第二亞軍"],["UCNZ","大學部","10","4（2 位 PI、2 位 instructor）","University of Canterbury","大學部 Top 10"],["WageningenUR","研究生組","11","13（3 位 PI、10 位 instructor）","Wageningen UR","Top 10；總冠軍第一亞軍"],["HangzhouFourteenAP","高中組","11","5（mentor 與 instructor，其中一位具博士與博士後資歷）","Hangzhou No.14 High School, AP Center","高中組 Top 10；Best Village Project 首獎"]]},"checklist":["Field 12 to 16 students in 2027, not 35. The smallest high-school team in a Top 10 had 11, the smallest Top 10 team of any kind had 9, and two six-student teams took special-prize nominations. Thirty-five is twice the high-school median and buys nothing this sample can detect.","Spend the headcount you save on named scientists instead. Every small team that placed had a short, specific staff list: Princeton nine students to four scientists, CHINAGuangdongShimen six to three. One postdoc or PhD-level instructor who is actually present is worth more than ten extra students.","Do one chassis and several applications, not several projects. Princeton reached a Grand Prize podium with nine people because its three applications shared a single M13 build. Scope, not staffing, is what a small team controls.","Build the software that replaces hands. Princeton's de novo binder pipeline made a new target cost compute instead of months of bench work; that is the specific trade a small team can make and a large one usually does not.","Turn one outreach activity into contributed engineering. PITCCH gave the public a real unsolved sub-problem with real constraints, scored entries on one metric, and built the winner in. It costs almost no labour and it counts as engineering.","Publish a real attributions page and a funding line. Twenty-two of 106 decorated teams publish no countable roster and only 7 state any funding figure; a team that writes down who did what and what it cost stands out, and GEMS should make that one of its signatures.","If GEMS ever works in a university lab, say so on the page and say exactly who did what. Five high-school teams declared university lab access this year and none of them was penalised for it; what judges and readers cannot forgive is a page that is silent about it."],"checklist_zh":["2027 年投入 12 到 16 位學生，而不是 35 位。高中組 Top 10 中人數最少的一隊是 11 人，所有 Top 10 中最少的一隊是 9 人，而兩支六人隊伍都拿到了特別獎入圍。35 人是高中組中位數的兩倍，而本樣本偵測不到它換來任何東西。","把省下來的人頭，換成具名的科學家。每一支以小規模取得名次的隊伍，人員名單都很短而且很具體：Princeton 是九位學生對四位科學家，CHINAGuangdongShimen 是六對三。一位真的在場的博士後或博士級 instructor，價值勝過多出來的十位學生。","做一個底盤搭配多個應用，而不是做好幾個專案。Princeton 能以九個人站上總冠軍頒獎臺，是因為三個應用共用同一套 M13 建構。小隊伍能控制的是範圍，不是人力。","去寫那種可以取代人手的軟體。Princeton 的 de novo 結合蛋白設計流程，讓新增一個標的只需要運算資源，而不是好幾個月的實驗操作；這正是小隊伍做得到、大隊伍通常不做的取捨。","把其中一項科普活動變成實際的工程貢獻。PITCCH 把一個帶著真實限制、尚未解決的子問題交給大眾，以單一指標評分，再把優勝設計做進專案。它幾乎不耗人力，而且算得上是工程工作。","確實做一頁 attributions，並寫出一行經費。106 支得獎隊伍中有 22 支沒有可清點的成員名冊，只有 7 支寫出任何經費數字；一支把誰做了什麼、花了多少都寫下來的隊伍會很顯眼，而 GEMS 應該把這一點變成自己的招牌。","萬一 GEMS 哪天在大學實驗室裡工作，就在頁面上講明，而且精確寫出誰做了什麼。今年有五支高中隊伍聲明自己有大學實驗室使用權，沒有任何一支因此被扣分；評審與讀者無法原諒的，是對此保持沉默的頁面。"],"method":"Sample: the 106 decorated 2026 teams in this report's evidence base — every Top 10 team, every special-prize winner and every nominee. Institution type comes from the iGEM registry API record for each team id and is complete for all 106: 66 higher-education, 25 secondary-education, 14 commercial and 1 community lab, with all 14 commercial and the single community lab in the High School section. Student counts were read off each team's own Team, Members or Attributions page — from the served HTML where the wiki is static, from the page's rendered text where it is a client-rendered app — and were obtained for 84 of 106 teams: 38 of 40 High School, 30 of 42 Undergraduate, 16 of 22 Overgraduate; two teams carry no section label and neither was countable. Where a page mixes students with advisors, alumni or PIs, only people the page itself labels as students, members, leaders or by class year were counted, and anyone labelled PI, instructor, advisor, mentor, teacher or alumnus was moved to the staff column; where a team published both a members page and an attributions form and the two disagreed, the attributions form was used, which is why WageningenUR is recorded as 11 students and not the 8 its team page shows. Where a roster is a game or a scroller, the count printed by the page itself was used (Marburg \"36 members\", SMS-Shenzhen \"18 CAPSULES\", GreatBay-SCIE \"0/29\", Eton-College-UK \"MET 0/16\", Yucai-SZ \"0 / 22\", HKSSC \"1 of 19\"). Twenty-two teams could not be counted and are excluded from every statistic rather than imputed; three of them are Top 10 teams (Cornell, NUS-Singapore, KAUST-KSA), so the Top 10 figures rest on 27 of 30. Tests: Spearman rank correlation of size against number of awards across all 84, and Mann-Whitney U comparing Top 10 against other decorated teams within each section. What this counting cannot see: whether a listed student actually worked, whether an instructor labelled 'supervision' in fact performed experiments, how many unnamed lab staff supported a team, and anything at all about teams that entered and did not place. Lab access and graduate-student involvement were found by full-text search of every page and script bundle fetched from each wiki, so a statement buried in a page that failed to download would be missed; the five university-lab high-school teams are therefore a floor, not a ceiling. Funding figures are only those a team states about its own money — business-plan and techno-economic numbers (McGill, UAlberta, UOttawa, Madrid-UCM) are excluded. GEMS-Taiwan is the report author's own team and has been counted and named on exactly the same terms as the rest. Organiser type, and the commercial-organiser base rate in the card above, were taken from iGEM's own registry (`api.igem.org/v1/teams/<id>` and the full 2026 competition roster) rather than from wikis, so those two figures — unlike everything else here — describe all 423 accepted teams and not only the decorated 106. Every one of the 106 was matched to the roster by name.","method_zh":"樣本：本報告證據庫中的 106 支 2026 年得獎隊伍——涵蓋所有 Top 10 隊伍、所有特別獎首獎隊伍與所有入圍隊伍。機構類型取自每個 team id 在 iGEM 註冊 API 上的紀錄，106 支全部齊備：66 支 higher-education、25 支 secondary-education、14 支 commercial、1 支 community lab；其中 14 支商業機構與唯一一支社群實驗室全部落在高中組。學生人數是從各隊自己的 Team、Members 或 Attributions 頁面讀出來的——靜態網站讀伺服器送出的 HTML，前端渲染的網站則讀頁面實際呈現的文字——106 支中取得 84 支：高中組 40 支取得 38 支、大學部 42 支取得 30 支、研究生組 22 支取得 16 支；另有兩支沒有組別標記，且兩支都數不出來。當頁面把學生與顧問、校友或 PI 混在一起時，只計入頁面本身標示為學生、成員、組長或註明年級的人；凡標示為 PI、instructor、advisor、mentor、教師或校友者，一律移到人員欄。若一隊同時有成員頁與 attributions 表格而兩者不一致，則以 attributions 表格為準，這也是 WageningenUR 在此記為 11 位學生、而非其團隊頁顯示的 8 位的原因。若成員名冊做成遊戲或捲動互動，則採用頁面自己印出的數字（Marburg 的「36 members」、SMS-Shenzhen 的「18 CAPSULES」、GreatBay-SCIE 的「0/29」、Eton-College-UK 的「MET 0/16」、Yucai-SZ 的「0 / 22」、HKSSC 的「1 of 19」）。有 22 支數不出來，一律排除於所有統計之外，不做任何補值；其中三支是 Top 10 隊伍（Cornell、NUS-Singapore、KAUST-KSA），因此 Top 10 的數字是建立在 30 支中的 27 支之上。檢定：在全部 84 支上以 Spearman 等級相關檢視人數與獎項數的關係，並在各組別內以 Mann-Whitney U 比較 Top 10 與其他得獎隊伍。這套清點看不到的事：名單上的學生是否真的投入、被標為「督導」的 instructor 是否其實動手做了實驗、有多少未具名的實驗室人員在支援一隊，以及關於報名卻未獲名次的隊伍的任何事。實驗室使用權與研究生參與，是對每個網站抓取到的所有頁面與程式包做全文檢索而得，因此若某段敘述藏在下載失敗的頁面裡就會漏掉；五支使用大學實驗室的高中隊伍因而是下限，不是上限。經費數字只收各隊談論自身經費的部分——商業計畫與技術經濟分析的數字（McGill、UAlberta、UOttawa、Madrid-UCM）一律排除。GEMS-Taiwan 是本報告作者自己的隊伍，清點方式與具名方式與其他隊伍完全相同。上面那張卡片裡的帶隊單位類型與營利機構得獎基礎比率，取自 iGEM 官方名冊（`api.igem.org/v1/teams/<id>` 與 2026 年完整參賽名單），而不是取自 wiki，因此這兩組數字——和本節其他所有數字不同——描述的是全部 423 支正式參賽隊伍，而不只是 106 支得獎隊伍。106 支全部都以隊名對上了名冊。"},{"id":"village-baserates","tab":"judging","order":40,"kicker":"Base rates","kicker_zh":"基準率","title":"What a village is worth to a high-school team, and why 2025 cannot tell you","title_zh":"一個 village 對高中隊伍值多少，以及為什麼 2025 年的資料無法告訴你","lede":"Across 147 accepted high-school teams in 13 villages, **47 were decorated (32.0%) and 10 took a Top 10 place (6.8%)**. The per-village spread looks large — from 2 of 17 in Agriculture and Food & Nutrition to 12 of 23 in Biomanufacturing — and it does not survive two tests. Within 2026 the whole spread is **not distinguishable from 147 teams decorated independently at 32%** (chi-square 19.64 on 12 df, Monte-Carlo p = 0.088). Across years, the only thing that carries from 2025 to 2026 is **how crowded a village is (r = +0.91)**, not what it pays: Top 10 rate r = +0.17 (p = 0.57), Gold rate r = +0.35 (p = 0.24). And one structural fact undoes the question anyway: a high-school team does not enter a village for award purposes, it enters **one of four award groups**.","lede_zh":"147 支獲接受的高中隊伍分布在 13 個 village，其中 **47 支得到獎項肯定（32.0%），10 支取得 Top 10 名次（6.8%）**。各 village 之間的差距看起來很大——從 Agriculture 與 Food & Nutrition 的 17 支中 2 支，到 Biomanufacturing 的 23 支中 12 支——但它通不過兩項檢驗。在 2026 年之內，整個差距**與「147 支隊伍各自獨立以 32% 機率獲獎」無法區分**（卡方 19.64，自由度 12，蒙地卡羅 p = 0.088）。跨年度來看，從 2025 年帶到 2026 年的只有**一個 village 有多擁擠（r = +0.91）**，而不是它付出多少：Top 10 比率 r = +0.17（p = 0.57），金牌比率 r = +0.35（p = 0.24）。而且有一個結構事實本身就讓這個問題失效：就獎項而言，高中隊伍進的不是 village，而是**四個獎項群組之一**。","body":"The cohort a high-school team competes against is not the whole 423. It is the 147 accepted high-school teams, and within a village it is the high-school teams in that village. Measured that way the section base rates are: 47 of 147 decorated (32.0%), 17 of 147 outright winners (11.6%), 10 Top 10 places, 2 finalist slots, 63 Gold, 68 Silver, 4 Bronze, 135 of 147 holding a medal at all.\n\n**The first finding is structural, and it changes the denominator.** The 13 type-`village` award objects in the API carry 60 citations and **not one high-school team** — they are undergraduate and overgraduate only. High-school teams compete instead for four award objects that all share the title `Best Village Project`, one per award group, 1 winner and 4 nominees each: **20 citations in total.** The groups in 2026 were Climate Crisis / Conservation / Bioremediation (28 high-school entrants, 1 in 5.6), Space / Foundational Advance / Software & AI / Biomanufacturing (31, 1 in 6.2), Infectious Diseases / Therapeutics / Diagnostics / Oncology (40, 1 in 8.0) and Agriculture / Food & Nutrition / Fashion & Cosmetics / Art & Design (48, 1 in 9.6). So a high-school team choosing a village is really choosing one of four groups, and **a village's apparent thinness can be irrelevant once it is pooled with three others**: Software & AI had 2 high-school entrants and sat inside a 31-team group. The same arithmetic shows the section is allocated village recognition less generously than the rest of the competition — 20 citations for 147 high-school teams (1 in 7.4) against 60 for 276 undergraduate and overgraduate teams (1 in 4.6), which is **0.63× the odds**.\n\n**The second finding is a null, and it is the decisive one for 2027.** Joining 2025 to 2026 by village name across the 13 villages with high-school entrants in both years, the number of high-school entrants is strongly persistent (r = +0.906, permutation p < 0.0001) — crowded villages stay crowded, thin ones stay thin. What a village pays out does not persist. **Top 10 rate: r = +0.17, p = 0.57. Gold rate: r = +0.35, p = 0.24.** The broad decoration rate does carry a moderate signal (r = +0.673, p = 0.005, and it survives controlling for village size, partial r = +0.66), but it buys a poor predictor: using a village's 2025 rate to guess its 2026 rate still leaves a mean error of **13.0 percentage points**, and restricted to the seven villages with at least 10 high-school entrants in both years the correlation falls to r = +0.600 with p = 0.153. Individual villages swing hard. Diagnostics went from 0 Top 10 places out of 10 entrants to 3 out of 13. Infectious Diseases went from 2 out of 6 to 0 out of 1. Biomanufacturing moved from 5 of 17 decorated to 12 of 23, the largest swing in the set at +22.8 points. **Village choice is not a reliable lever, and the honest instruction for 2027 is to stop treating it as one.**\n\n**The honest limit on all of this is the denominators.** Six of the 13 villages had fewer than 10 high-school entrants and between them held only 22 of the 147 teams; Infectious Diseases had one team, Foundational Advance and Software & AI two each, Space four. Two further village names, Art & Design and Climate Crisis, had zero accepted high-school teams in 2026, so their high-school rate is undefined rather than zero. Rates computed on 1 to 7 teams move by 14 to 100 percentage points when one team's result changes, and nothing on those rows should be read as a tendency.","body_zh":"一支高中隊伍實際面對的群體不是全部 423 支，而是 147 支獲接受的高中隊伍；在單一 village 之內，則是該 village 裡的高中隊伍。以這個方式量測，整個組別的基準率是：147 支中 47 支得到獎項肯定（32.0%）、17 支成為實質得獎者（11.6%）、10 個 Top 10 名次、2 個決賽席位、63 面金牌、68 面銀牌、4 面銅牌，147 支中有 135 支至少拿到一面獎牌。\n\n**第一個發現是結構性的，而它改變了分母。** API 裡 13 個 type 為 `village` 的獎項物件共有 60 個獎項席次，其中**沒有任何一支高中隊伍**——那些獎只給大學組與研究生組。高中隊伍競爭的是另外四個獎項物件，它們的 `title` 全都是 `Best Village Project`，每個獎項群組一個，各有 1 位得獎者與 4 位入圍者：**總共 20 個獎項席次。** 2026 年的四個群組是 Climate Crisis / Conservation / Bioremediation（28 支高中隊伍，1 比 5.6）、Space / Foundational Advance / Software & AI / Biomanufacturing（31 支，1 比 6.2）、Infectious Diseases / Therapeutics / Diagnostics / Oncology（40 支，1 比 8.0），以及 Agriculture / Food & Nutrition / Fashion & Cosmetics / Art & Design（48 支，1 比 9.6）。所以高中隊伍選 village，實際上是在選四個群組之一，而**一個 village 看起來很稀薄，在它與另外三個併成一組之後可能毫無意義**：Software & AI 只有 2 支高中隊伍，卻坐在一個 31 支隊伍的群組裡。同樣的算術也顯示，高中組在 village 層級的肯定上分配得比競賽其他部分吝嗇——147 支高中隊伍分 20 個獎項席次（1 比 7.4），而 276 支大學與研究生隊伍分 60 個（1 比 4.6），也就是**機率的 0.63 倍**。\n\n**第二個發現是一個虛無結果，而它對 2027 年才是決定性的。** 以 village 名稱把 2025 年接到 2026 年，取兩年都有高中隊伍的那 13 個 village：高中參賽隊數高度延續（r = +0.906，置換檢定 p < 0.0001）——擁擠的 village 持續擁擠，稀薄的持續稀薄。但一個 village 付出什麼並不延續。**Top 10 比率：r = +0.17，p = 0.57。金牌比率：r = +0.35，p = 0.24。** 廣義的獲獎肯定比率確實帶有中等程度的訊號（r = +0.673，p = 0.005，而且在控制 village 規模後依然存在，偏相關 r = +0.66），但它換來的是一個很差的預測器：用某個 village 2025 年的比率去猜它 2026 年的比率，平均誤差仍有 **13.0 個百分點**；而若只取兩年高中隊伍都在 10 支以上的那七個 village，相關係數降到 r = +0.600，p = 0.153。單一 village 的擺盪很劇烈。Diagnostics 從 10 支隊伍 0 個 Top 10，變成 13 支隊伍 3 個。Infectious Diseases 從 6 支中 2 個變成 1 支中 0 個。Biomanufacturing 從 17 支中 5 支獲獎變成 23 支中 12 支，是整組最大的擺盪，+22.8 個百分點。**選 village 不是一個可靠的槓桿，而 2027 年誠實的指示是：別再把它當成槓桿。**\n\n**這一切誠實的限制在於分母。** 13 個 village 中有 6 個的高中隊伍不到 10 支，加起來只占 147 支中的 22 支；Infectious Diseases 只有 1 支，Foundational Advance 與 Software & AI 各 2 支，Space 4 支。另外兩個 village 名稱，Art & Design 與 Climate Crisis，2026 年沒有任何獲接受的高中隊伍，因此它們的高中比率是未定義，而不是零。建立在 1 到 7 支隊伍上的比率，只要其中一支的結果改變，就會移動 14 到 100 個百分點，那幾列上的任何數字都不該被當成傾向來讀。","cards":[{"kicker":"The denominator","kicker_zh":"分母","title":"High-school village awards are given over four groups, not thirteen villages","title_zh":"高中組的 village 獎是按四個群組頒發，不是按十三個 village","body":"The 13 `village`-type award objects in the iGEM API hold 60 citations and **zero high-school teams**; they are undergraduate and overgraduate only. High-school teams compete for four separate award objects that all carry the title `Best Village Project` — one per award group, 1 winner and 4 nominees each, **20 citations in total**. Anyone matching on that title as a dictionary key collapses four distinct groups into one and gets the analysis wrong.\n\nSo the choosable unit is the group, not the village: Climate Crisis / Conservation / Bioremediation (28 high-school entrants, 1 in 5.6), Space / Foundational Advance / Software & AI / Biomanufacturing (31, 1 in 6.2), Infectious Diseases / Therapeutics / Diagnostics / Oncology (40, 1 in 8.0), Agriculture / Food & Nutrition / Fashion & Cosmetics / Art & Design (48, 1 in 9.6). The four partition the 147 exactly. **A village's apparent thinness can be irrelevant once it is pooled**: Software & AI had 2 high-school entrants and sat inside a 31-team group, and Foundational Advance had 2 inside the same one. The 2025 season had the same four-group structure with the same 20 citations, so this is the design and not a one-year quirk.","body_zh":"iGEM API 裡 13 個 type 為 `village` 的獎項物件共有 60 個獎項席次，其中**高中隊伍為零**；那些獎只給大學組與研究生組。高中隊伍競爭的是四個分開的獎項物件，它們的 `title` 全都是 `Best Village Project`——每個獎項群組一個，各 1 位得獎者與 4 位入圍者，**總共 20 個獎項席次**。任何把這個 title 當成字典鍵來比對的人，都會把四個不同的群組壓成一個，然後把分析做錯。\n\n所以可被選擇的單位是群組，不是 village：Climate Crisis / Conservation / Bioremediation（28 支高中隊伍，1 比 5.6）、Space / Foundational Advance / Software & AI / Biomanufacturing（31 支，1 比 6.2）、Infectious Diseases / Therapeutics / Diagnostics / Oncology（40 支，1 比 8.0）、Agriculture / Food & Nutrition / Fashion & Cosmetics / Art & Design（48 支，1 比 9.6）。四個群組恰好把 147 支完整切分。**一個 village 看起來稀薄，在併入群組之後可能毫無意義**：Software & AI 只有 2 支高中隊伍，卻坐在 31 支隊伍的群組裡；Foundational Advance 同樣是 2 支，也在同一組裡。2025 年的賽季是同樣的四群組結構、同樣的 20 個獎項席次，所以這是制度設計，不是單一年度的異常。","chips":["20 citations, 4 groups","60 village citations: 0 high-school","1 in 5.6 to 1 in 9.6"],"chips_zh":["20 個獎項席次、4 個群組","60 個 village 獎項席次：高中 0","1 比 5.6 到 1 比 9.6"]},{"kicker":"The null","kicker_zh":"虛無結果","title":"Crowding persists year to year; payout does not","title_zh":"擁擠程度會延續到下一年；付出不會","body":"Joined by village name — team ids are reissued every season, so names are the only cross-year key — across the 13 villages with high-school entrants in both 2025 and 2026, the number of high-school entrants is strongly persistent: **r = +0.906, permutation p < 0.0001.** Bioremediation and Therapeutics were crowded in both years; Foundational Advance and Software & AI were nearly empty in both.\n\nWhat a village pays out does not travel. **Top 10 rate: r = +0.17, two-sided permutation p = 0.57. Gold rate: r = +0.35, p = 0.24.** Both are nulls. The broad decoration rate is the one measure with a signal — r = +0.673, p = 0.005, robust to dropping any single village (+0.598 to +0.755) and to controlling for village size (partial r = +0.66) — but it is a weak instrument in practice: predicting a village's 2026 rate from its own 2025 rate still leaves a **mean error of 13.0 percentage points**, and among the seven villages with at least 10 high-school entrants in both years the correlation is r = +0.600 at p = 0.153. **A thin village is not reliably thin again**, and the report records this as a null rather than a lever.","body_zh":"以 village 名稱接合——隊伍 id 每一季都會重新發放，所以名稱是唯一可用的跨年度鍵——在 2025 與 2026 兩年都有高中隊伍的 13 個 village 中，高中參賽隊數高度延續：**r = +0.906，置換檢定 p < 0.0001。** Bioremediation 與 Therapeutics 兩年都擁擠；Foundational Advance 與 Software & AI 兩年都幾乎是空的。\n\n一個 village 付出什麼則不會傳遞。**Top 10 比率：r = +0.17，雙尾置換檢定 p = 0.57。金牌比率：r = +0.35，p = 0.24。** 兩者都是虛無結果。廣義的獲獎肯定比率是唯一帶有訊號的量——r = +0.673，p = 0.005，對逐一剔除任一 village 穩健（+0.598 到 +0.755），控制 village 規模後也仍然存在（偏相關 r = +0.66）——但實務上它是個很弱的工具：用某 village 自己 2025 年的比率去預測 2026 年，平均誤差仍有 **13.0 個百分點**；而在兩年高中隊伍都至少 10 支的那七個 village 中，相關係數是 r = +0.600，p = 0.153。**稀薄的 village 不會可靠地再次稀薄**，本報告把這件事記為一個虛無結果，而不是一個槓桿。","chips":["entrants r = +0.91","Top 10 rate r = +0.17, p = 0.57","±13.0 pp prediction error"],"chips_zh":["參賽隊數 r = +0.91","Top 10 比率 r = +0.17、p = 0.57","預測誤差 ±13.0 個百分點"]},{"kicker":"Within one year","kicker_zh":"單一年度之內","title":"The whole 2026 spread, 12% to 57%, is inside what 147 coin flips would produce","title_zh":"2026 年整個 12% 到 57% 的差距，都落在 147 次拋硬幣會產生的範圍內","body":"The per-village high-school decoration rates run from 2 of 17 in Agriculture and in Food & Nutrition (11.8%) up to 12 of 23 in Biomanufacturing (52.2%) and 4 of 7 in Conservation (57.1%). Against the section rate of 47 of 147 (32.0%), that spread gives a **chi-square of 19.64 on 12 degrees of freedom, Monte-Carlo p = 0.088** under a null in which every high-school team is decorated independently at 32% with the real village sizes held fixed.\n\nSo the table below is almost entirely what chance looks like at these sample sizes. **Exactly one village clears two standard deviations: Biomanufacturing at z = +2.08**, 12 decorated against 7.4 expected. Everything else sits between z = −1.79 (Agriculture and Food & Nutrition, 2 against 5.4 expected) and z = +1.43 (Conservation). A single team's result moves a 7-team row by 14 points and a 2-team row by 50. The spread is real as a record of what happened; it is not evidence that the villages differ.","body_zh":"各 village 的高中獲獎肯定比率，從 Agriculture 與 Food & Nutrition 的 17 支中 2 支（11.8%），到 Biomanufacturing 的 23 支中 12 支（52.2%）與 Conservation 的 7 支中 4 支（57.1%）。相對於整組 147 支中 47 支（32.0%）的比率，這個差距在「每支高中隊伍各自獨立以 32% 機率獲獎、各 village 規模維持真實值」的虛無假設下，給出**卡方 19.64、自由度 12、蒙地卡羅 p = 0.088**。\n\n所以下面這張表幾乎完全就是「在這種樣本數下，機率長成的樣子」。**恰好只有一個 village 超過兩個標準差：Biomanufacturing，z = +2.08**，12 支獲獎對上期望值 7.4 支。其餘全部落在 z = −1.79（Agriculture 與 Food & Nutrition，2 支對上期望 5.4 支）到 z = +1.43（Conservation）之間。單一支隊伍的結果，會讓 7 支隊伍的那一列移動 14 個百分點，讓 2 支隊伍的那一列移動 50 個百分點。這個差距作為「發生了什麼」的紀錄是真的；但它不是「各 village 有差別」的證據。","chips":["chi-square 19.64, 12 df, p = 0.088","only Biomanufacturing clears z = +2"],"chips_zh":["卡方 19.64、自由度 12、p = 0.088","只有 Biomanufacturing 超過 z = +2"]},{"kicker":"GEMS's own village","kicker_zh":"GEMS 自己的 village","title":"Biomanufacturing was the most crowded high-school field and the most decorated one","title_zh":"Biomanufacturing 是高中組最擁擠的戰場，也是獲獎肯定最多的一個","body":"Biomanufacturing took **49 teams and 23 high-school teams, the largest high-school field in the competition** — 15.6% of the whole section in one village. Crowding did not cost its teams anything measurable. **12 of 23 were decorated (52.2%), the highest rate of any village with 10 or more high-school entrants**, against 32.0% for the section, and the only village-level figure in 2026 that clears two standard deviations (z = +2.08). It produced 4 of the 17 outright high-school winners, tied with Diagnostics for the most, GEMS-Taiwan among them with Best Measurement, Best Hardware and Best Integrated Human Practices. And **all five of its award group's `Best Village Project` citations went to Biomanufacturing teams** — the winner HangzhouFourteenAP plus four nominees including GEMS-Taiwan — leaving 0 for the 8 high-school teams in Space, Foundational Advance and Software & AI.\n\nTwo figures cut the other way, and they are the ones that matter at the top. **Top 10: 2 of 23, 8.7%**, barely above the 6.8% section rate and well behind Diagnostics at 3 of 13 (23.1%). **Gold: 10 of 23, 43.5%, against 42.9% for the section** — no advantage at all. Biomanufacturing was a good place to pick up a citation in 2026 and an ordinary place to reach the podium. It was also the village with the largest year-on-year swing in the whole set, 5 of 17 decorated in 2025 to 12 of 23 in 2026, which is the clearest single reason not to plan on it repeating.","body_zh":"Biomanufacturing 收了 **49 支隊伍、其中 23 支高中隊伍，是全競賽最大的高中戰場**——整個高中組有 15.6% 擠在同一個 village 裡。擁擠並沒有讓它的隊伍付出任何可量測的代價。**23 支中有 12 支得到獎項肯定（52.2%），是所有高中隊伍達 10 支以上的 village 中最高的比率**，對比整組的 32.0%，也是 2026 年唯一超過兩個標準差的 village 層級數字（z = +2.08）。它產出了 17 個高中實質得獎者中的 4 個，與 Diagnostics 併列最多，其中包括 GEMS-Taiwan 的最佳量測、最佳硬體與最佳整合性人文實踐。而且**它所屬獎項群組的五個 `Best Village Project` 獎項席次 全部落在 Biomanufacturing 的隊伍上**——得獎者 HangzhouFourteenAP 加上四位入圍者，GEMS-Taiwan 在其中——讓 Space、Foundational Advance 與 Software & AI 的 8 支高中隊伍拿到 0 個。\n\n有兩個數字方向相反，而它們正是在頂端真正重要的那兩個。**Top 10：23 支中 2 支，8.7%**，只比整組的 6.8% 高一點，遠落後於 Diagnostics 的 13 支中 3 支（23.1%）。**金牌：23 支中 10 支，43.5%，對比整組 42.9%**——完全沒有優勢。2026 年的 Biomanufacturing 是個容易撿到一個獎項席次的地方，是個普通的上頒獎臺的地方。它同時也是整組中年度擺盪最大的 village，2025 年 17 支中 5 支獲獎、2026 年 23 支中 12 支，這正是「不要指望它重演」最清楚的單一理由。","chips":["23 of 147 high-school teams","decorated 12/23 (52%), section 32%","Gold 43.5% vs section 42.9%"],"chips_zh":["147 支高中隊伍中的 23 支","獲獎肯定 12/23（52%），整組 32%","金牌 43.5% 對整組 42.9%"]},{"kicker":"Thin and thick","kicker_zh":"稀薄與厚實","title":"Conservation's 7 high-school teams took 2 of the 10 Top 10 places; Bioremediation's 21 took none","title_zh":"Conservation 的 7 支高中隊伍拿下 10 個 Top 10 名次中的 2 個；Bioremediation 的 21 支一個都沒拿","body":"Stated as rates per entrant rather than as ranks, the cheapest Top 10 place in 2026 belonged to **Conservation, 2 of 7 high-school entrants, 1 in 3.5**, and that village also produced the high-school Grand Prize winner, Lambert-GA, and a second Top 10 team, GHCIS. Next is **Diagnostics, 3 of 13, 1 in 4.3**, the only village with three. Then a long gap to Biomanufacturing at 1 in 11.5, Agriculture and Food & Nutrition at 1 in 17, Therapeutics at 1 in 20.\n\nSeven of the 13 villages produced **no high-school Top 10 team at all**, and two of those were large: **Bioremediation, 0 from 21 entrants, and Fashion & Cosmetics, 0 from 14** — 35 high-school teams between them and not one place. On the citation side the order differs again: Conservation led at 2.14 non-medal citations per high-school entrant (15 across 7 teams), Biomanufacturing 1.39, Bioremediation 0.29.\n\n**The limit on reading any of this as a tendency is the denominators.** Six of 13 villages fielded fewer than 10 high-school teams and held 22 of the 147 between them — Infectious Diseases 1, Foundational Advance 2, Software & AI 2, Space 4, Oncology 6, Conservation 7. Conservation's 1 in 3.5 rests on two teams. Art & Design and Climate Crisis had no accepted high-school teams at all, so their rates are undefined, not zero.","body_zh":"以「每位參賽者的比率」而不是以排名來陳述，2026 年最便宜的 Top 10 名次屬於 **Conservation，7 支高中隊伍中 2 支，1 比 3.5**；而這個 village 同時產出了高中組總冠軍 Lambert-GA，以及第二支 Top 10 隊伍 GHCIS。其次是 **Diagnostics，13 支中 3 支，1 比 4.3**，是唯一有三個名次的 village。接著就是一段很長的落差：Biomanufacturing 1 比 11.5，Agriculture 與 Food & Nutrition 1 比 17，Therapeutics 1 比 20。\n\n13 個 village 中有 7 個**完全沒有產出高中 Top 10 隊伍**，其中兩個規模還不小：**Bioremediation，21 支參賽 0 個；Fashion & Cosmetics，14 支參賽 0 個**——兩者加起來 35 支高中隊伍，一個名次都沒有。在獎項席次那一側，順序又不一樣：Conservation 以每位高中參賽者 2.14 個非獎牌獎項席次領先（7 支隊伍共 15 個），Biomanufacturing 1.39，Bioremediation 0.29。\n\n**把這些讀成任何傾向，限制都在分母。** 13 個 village 中有 6 個的高中隊伍不到 10 支，加起來只占 147 支中的 22 支——Infectious Diseases 1 支、Foundational Advance 2 支、Software & AI 2 支、Space 4 支、Oncology 6 支、Conservation 7 支。Conservation 的 1 比 3.5 建立在兩支隊伍上。Art & Design 與 Climate Crisis 完全沒有獲接受的高中隊伍，因此它們的比率是未定義，不是零。","chips":["Conservation 2/7 Top 10","Bioremediation 0/21","6 of 13 villages under 10 teams"],"chips_zh":["Conservation 7 支中 2 個 Top 10","Bioremediation 21 支中 0 個","13 個 village 中 6 個不到 10 支隊伍"]},{"kicker":"Allocation","kicker_zh":"分配","title":"A high-school team gets 0.63× an undergraduate team's odds on a village award","title_zh":"在 village 獎上，高中隊伍拿到的機率是大學隊伍的 0.63 倍","body":"The 60 village-award citations go to 276 undergraduate and overgraduate teams across 13 denominators — **1 in 4.6 overall, 21.7%**. The 20 `Best Village Project` citations go to 147 high-school teams across 4 denominators — **1 in 7.4, 13.6%**. That is **0.63× the odds**, and it is the single largest structural difference between the sections found anywhere in this analysis.\n\nThe two systems are uneven in opposite ways. Per undergraduate or overgraduate entrant the 13 village denominators spread **2.9×**, from Software & AI at 1 in 3.0 (3 citations, 9 entrants) to Therapeutics at 1 in 8.8 (5 citations, 44 entrants), median 1 in 4.0 — the slots are allotted by village, not in proportion to how many teams the village drew. The four high-school groups spread only **1.7×**, 1 in 5.6 to 1 in 9.6, because pooling four villages into one group evens out the denominators. **So the high-school allocation is flatter and thinner: less to be gained by choosing well, and less on offer in total.** Within a group the unevenness returns: Biomanufacturing's 23 teams took all 5 of their group's citations, an effective 1 in 4.6, while the other 8 teams in that group took 0.","body_zh":"60 個 village 獎獎項席次分給 276 支大學與研究生隊伍、跨 13 個分母——**整體 1 比 4.6，21.7%**。20 個 `Best Village Project` 獎項席次分給 147 支高中隊伍、跨 4 個分母——**1 比 7.4，13.6%**。這是**機率的 0.63 倍**，也是本分析在任何地方找到的、組別之間最大的單一結構差異。\n\n這兩套制度不平均的方向相反。以每位大學或研究生參賽者計，13 個 village 分母之間相差 **2.9 倍**，從 Software & AI 的 1 比 3.0（3 個獎項席次、9 支隊伍）到 Therapeutics 的 1 比 8.8（5 個獎項席次、44 支隊伍），中位數 1 比 4.0——席次是按 village 配置，不是按該 village 收到多少隊伍比例分配。四個高中群組之間只相差 **1.7 倍**，1 比 5.6 到 1 比 9.6，因為把四個 village 併成一組會把分母拉平。**所以高中組的分配更平、也更薄：選得好能賺到的更少，總量也更少。** 在群組之內，不平均又回來了：Biomanufacturing 的 23 支隊伍拿走了該群組全部 5 個獎項席次，實質上是 1 比 4.6，而該群組其他 8 支隊伍拿到 0 個。","chips":["high-school 1 in 7.4","undergrad/overgrad 1 in 4.6","group spread 1.7× vs village 2.9×"],"chips_zh":["高中組 1 比 7.4","大學／研究生組 1 比 4.6","群組差距 1.7 倍對 village 2.9 倍"]},{"kicker":"Self-selection","kicker_zh":"自我選擇","title":"None of these rates is a probability of winning, because teams choose their own village","title_zh":"這些比率都不是獲獎機率，因為隊伍自己選 village","body":"Every figure on this page is a rate observed among teams that chose to enter that village. It is not the chance that a given team would win if it entered. **Teams self-select, and strong teams cluster** — by country, by school network, by the kind of project a well-resourced lab can attempt, and by copying what worked for a neighbouring school last year. 20 of the 23 high-school teams in Biomanufacturing came from China, Hong Kong, Taiwan, Korea or Japan, and the two Taiwanese entries sat beside HangzhouFourteenAP, which won the group. A rate of 52% in that field says something about who entered it, not about what the field does to an entrant.\n\nThe practical consequence is narrow and worth stating flatly: **this analysis cannot support advice of the form \"enter village X to win\"**, and no such advice is given here. What it can support is the opposite move — ruling the question out. The payout measures that matter do not persist from 2025 to 2026, the whole 2026 spread sits inside chance at these sample sizes, and the high-school village-award odds are set by a four-group structure that a village choice barely perturbs. **Village choice should be decided on what the team can actually do, and the base rates should be used to stop that decision absorbing any more planning time.**","body_zh":"本頁的每一個數字，都是「在選擇進入該 village 的隊伍之間」觀察到的比率。它不是某支隊伍若進入該 village 就會獲獎的機率。**隊伍會自我選擇，而強隊會群聚**——依國家、依學校網絡、依一間資源充足的實驗室能嘗試什麼樣的專案，也依「隔壁學校去年用什麼有效」而模仿。Biomanufacturing 的 23 支高中隊伍中有 20 支來自中國、香港、台灣、韓國或日本，而兩支台灣隊伍與贏下該群組的 HangzhouFourteenAP 坐在一起。那個戰場 52% 的比率，說的是「誰進去了」，不是「那個戰場對一個參賽者會做什麼」。\n\n實務上的後果很窄，而且值得直說：**本分析無法支撐「進入某個 village 以獲獎」這種形式的建議**，本頁也不提供這種建議。它能支撐的是相反的動作——把這個問題排除掉。真正重要的那些付出指標並沒有從 2025 延續到 2026，2026 年整個差距在這種樣本數下都落在機率之內，而高中組的 village 獎機率是由一個四群組結構決定的，選哪個 village 幾乎動不了它。**選 village 應該依團隊實際能做什麼來決定，而這些基準率的用途是讓這個決定不再吸走任何規劃時間。**","chips":["rates describe who entered","no \"enter village X\" advice","20 of 23 from five countries"],"chips_zh":["比率描述的是誰進去了","不提供「進某個 village」的建議","23 支中 20 支來自五個國家"]}],"table":{"head":["Village","HS teams (all)","HS Top 10","HS decorated","HS wins","HS Gold","Award group · 1 in N"],"head_zh":["Village","高中隊數（全部）","高中 Top 10","高中獲獎肯定","高中實質得獎","高中金牌","獎項群組 · 1 比 N"],"rows":[["Biomanufacturing","23 (49)","2","**12/23 (52%)**","4","10/23 (43%)","Advanced & Mfg · 1 in 6.2"],["Bioremediation","21 (50)","**0**","5/21 (24%)","1","10/21 (48%)","Environment · 1 in 5.6"],["Therapeutics","20 (64)","1","5/20 (25%)","2","8/20 (40%)","Health · 1 in 8.0"],["Agriculture","17 (40)","1","**2/17 (12%)**","1","5/17 (29%)","Food & Consumer · 1 in 9.6"],["Food & Nutrition","17 (33)","1","**2/17 (12%)**","1","6/17 (35%)","Food & Consumer · 1 in 9.6"],["Fashion & Cosmetics","14 (28)","**0**","6/14 (43%)","2","6/14 (43%)","Food & Consumer · 1 in 9.6"],["Diagnostics","13 (35)","**3**","6/13 (46%)","4","7/13 (54%)","Health · 1 in 8.0"],["Conservation","7 (21)","**2**","4/7 (57%)","2","5/7 (71%)","Environment · 1 in 5.6"],["Oncology","6 (17)","0","3/6 (50%)","0","3/6 (50%)","Health · 1 in 8.0"],["Space","4 (17)","0","2/4 (50%)","0","2/4 (50%)","Advanced & Mfg · 1 in 6.2"],["Foundational Advance","2 (47)","0","0/2 — all sections 20/47 (43%)","0","0/2 (0%)","Advanced & Mfg · 1 in 6.2"],["Software & AI","2 (11)","0","0/2 — all sections 4/11 (36%)","0","1/2 (50%)","Advanced & Mfg · 1 in 6.2"],["Infectious Diseases","1 (11)","0","0/1 — all sections 4/11 (36%)","0","0/1 (0%)","Health · 1 in 8.0"],["**All 13 villages**","**147 (423)**","**10**","**47/147 (32.0%)**","**17**","**63/147 (42.9%)**","**20 citations · 1 in 7.4**"]],"rows_zh":[["Biomanufacturing","23（49）","2","**12/23（52%）**","4","10/23（43%）","先進與製造 · 1 比 6.2"],["Bioremediation","21（50）","**0**","5/21（24%）","1","10/21（48%）","環境 · 1 比 5.6"],["Therapeutics","20（64）","1","5/20（25%）","2","8/20（40%）","健康 · 1 比 8.0"],["Agriculture","17（40）","1","**2/17（12%）**","1","5/17（29%）","食品與消費 · 1 比 9.6"],["Food & Nutrition","17（33）","1","**2/17（12%）**","1","6/17（35%）","食品與消費 · 1 比 9.6"],["Fashion & Cosmetics","14（28）","**0**","6/14（43%）","2","6/14（43%）","食品與消費 · 1 比 9.6"],["Diagnostics","13（35）","**3**","6/13（46%）","4","7/13（54%）","健康 · 1 比 8.0"],["Conservation","7（21）","**2**","4/7（57%）","2","5/7（71%）","環境 · 1 比 5.6"],["Oncology","6（17）","0","3/6（50%）","0","3/6（50%）","健康 · 1 比 8.0"],["Space","4（17）","0","2/4（50%）","0","2/4（50%）","先進與製造 · 1 比 6.2"],["Foundational Advance","2（47）","0","0/2 — 全組別 20/47（43%）","0","0/2（0%）","先進與製造 · 1 比 6.2"],["Software & AI","2（11）","0","0/2 — 全組別 4/11（36%）","0","1/2（50%）","先進與製造 · 1 比 6.2"],["Infectious Diseases","1（11）","0","0/1 — 全組別 4/11（36%）","0","0/1（0%）","健康 · 1 比 8.0"],["**13 個 village 合計**","**147（423）**","**10**","**47/147（32.0%）**","**17**","**63/147（42.9%）**","**20 個獎項席次 · 1 比 7.4**"]]},"checklist":["Spend no more than one meeting on which village to enter. The payout measures that matter do not carry from 2025 to 2026 — Top 10 rate r = +0.17, p = 0.57 — and the 2026 spread sits inside chance at p = 0.088.","If the village question is raised anyway, raise it at group level. There are four groups and 20 `Best Village Project` citations, and Software & AI's 2 high-school entrants sat in the same 31-team group as Biomanufacturing's 23.","Do not plan on Biomanufacturing repeating 2026. It swung from 5 of 17 decorated to 12 of 23, the largest move in the set, and its Gold rate was 43.5% against a section rate of 42.9%.","Budget expectations against the section base rates, not the village ones: 32.0% of high-school teams decorated, 11.6% outright winners, 10 Top 10 places for 147 teams.","Count on a medal and nothing more. 135 of 147 high-school teams hold one and 92.9% of the whole competition does, so a Gold is a floor to clear early rather than a result to report.","Treat the village award as thin for this section on purpose: 1 in 7.4 for high school against 1 in 4.6 for undergraduate and overgraduate. Aim at the award categories where the high-school section has its own full slate.","Never quote a rate built on fewer than 10 teams to a sponsor or a judge. Six of the 13 villages are below that, and Conservation's headline 1-in-3.5 Top 10 rate rests on two teams.","Re-pull both seasons from the iGEM API before reusing any of this in 2027, and join on village name — team ids are reissued each season and will silently produce a wrong answer."],"checklist_zh":["「要進哪個 village」最多只花一次會議。真正重要的付出指標並沒有從 2025 帶到 2026——Top 10 比率 r = +0.17、p = 0.57——而 2026 年的差距在 p = 0.088 之下仍落在機率之內。","如果還是要討論 village，就在群組層級討論。總共四個群組、20 個 `Best Village Project` 獎項席次，而 Software & AI 的 2 支高中隊伍，和 Biomanufacturing 的 23 支坐在同一個 31 支隊伍的群組裡。","不要指望 Biomanufacturing 重演 2026 年。它從 17 支中 5 支獲獎擺盪到 23 支中 12 支，是整組最大的移動，而它的金牌比率 43.5% 對比整組的 42.9%。","用整個組別的基準率來編列期待，不要用 village 的：高中隊伍 32.0% 得到獎項肯定、11.6% 是實質得獎者、147 支隊伍分 10 個 Top 10 名次。","把獎牌當成理所當然，但也僅此而已。147 支高中隊伍中有 135 支拿到獎牌，全競賽是 92.9%，所以金牌是一條該及早跨過的底線，不是一個值得報告的成果。","把 village 獎對本組別的稀薄視為制度設計：高中組 1 比 7.4，大學與研究生組 1 比 4.6。把力氣放在高中組有完整獨立席次的那些獎項類別上。","絕不要把建立在不到 10 支隊伍上的比率報給贊助者或評審。13 個 village 中有 6 個低於這個門檻，而 Conservation 招牌的 1 比 3.5 Top 10 比率，是建立在兩支隊伍上。","2027 年要再用這些資料之前，先從 iGEM API 重新抓取兩個賽季，並以 village 名稱接合——隊伍 id 每季重新發放，會無聲地產生錯誤答案。"],"method":"Source: the public iGEM API, team rosters and award results for the 2026 and 2025 seasons, cached locally and not re-fetched. Denominators are accepted teams only: 423 in 2026 (147 high-school, 201 undergraduate, 75 overgraduate) and 413 in 2025 (143 high-school), with 8 withdrawn 2025 entries excluded. \"Decorated\" means a team appears as winner or nominee on any non-medal award; medals are counted separately, and 2026 medals were Gold 226, Silver 149, Bronze 18, so 393 of 423 teams (92.9%) hold one and 249 hold a medal and no award. High-school figures are 63 Gold, 68 Silver, 4 Bronze, 135 of 147 with a medal. Per-village rows use the high-school teams in that village as the denominator; the all-sections figure is shown alongside only where it changes the reading. Village awards are handled at two levels because the API records them at two levels: the 13 type-`village` award objects carry 60 citations and no high-school teams, while high-school teams are cited in four separate type-`special` objects that all share the title `Best Village Project`, 5 citations each, 20 in total — matching that title as a single key collapses the four groups and must be avoided. Group membership was taken from the four award rosters and checked to partition the 147 high-school teams exactly (28, 48, 40, 31). The API gives those four award objects no distinguishing title, so the short group labels used in the table — Environment, Food & Consumer, Health, Advanced & Manufacturing — are this report's own shorthand and not iGEM's names; iGEM identifies each group only by its list of villages, which the first card gives in full. Art & Design and Climate Crisis had zero accepted high-school teams in 2026, so their high-school rates are undefined, not zero. The 2025 join is on village name, not uuid and not team id, because team ids are reissued every season. Correlations are Pearson with two-sided permutation p-values over 200,000 shuffles; the within-year heterogeneity test is a chi-square against the 32.0% section rate with a 100,000-draw Monte-Carlo null holding the real village sizes fixed. The decisive caveat: a decoration rate is not a probability of winning for a team that chooses that village. Teams pick their own village and strong teams cluster, by country, by school network and by imitating what worked nearby, so these rates describe who entered a village rather than what entering it does. No recommendation of the form \"enter village X to win\" follows from this analysis and none is made. Six of the 13 villages fielded fewer than 10 high-school teams, holding 22 of 147 between them, and rates on those rows move by 14 to 100 percentage points on a single team's result. GEMS-Taiwan is the report author's own team and appears in these counts on the same terms as every other team.","method_zh":"資料來源：iGEM 公開 API 的 2026 與 2025 兩個賽季的隊伍名冊與獎項結果，已在本機快取，未重新抓取。分母只採計獲接受的隊伍：2026 年 423 支（高中 147、大學 201、研究生 75），2025 年 413 支（高中 143），2025 年 8 筆已撤回的登記予以排除。「獲獎肯定」指一支隊伍以得獎者或入圍者身分出現在任何非獎牌獎項上；獎牌分開計算，2026 年獎牌為金 226、銀 149、銅 18，因此 423 支中有 393 支（92.9%）持有獎牌，249 支有獎牌而無任何獎項。高中組為金 63、銀 68、銅 4，147 支中 135 支有獎牌。各 village 的列以該 village 的高中隊伍為分母；只有在會改變判讀時，才並列全組別的數字。village 獎分兩個層級處理，因為 API 本身就記在兩個層級：13 個 type 為 `village` 的獎項物件共 60 個獎項席次、不含任何高中隊伍，而高中隊伍被記在四個分開的 type 為 `special` 的物件上，它們的 `title` 全都是 `Best Village Project`，各 5 個獎項席次、合計 20 個——把這個 title 當成單一鍵來比對會把四個群組壓成一個，必須避免。群組成員取自那四份獲獎名單，並已驗證恰好把 147 支高中隊伍完整切分（28、48、40、31）。API 並未給那四個獎項物件任何可供區別的 title，所以表格裡用的四個簡稱——環境、食品與消費、健康、先進與製造——是本報告自己的縮寫，並不是 iGEM 的名稱；iGEM 只用各群組的 village 清單來指稱它們，而第一張卡片已完整列出。Art & Design 與 Climate Crisis 在 2026 年沒有任何獲接受的高中隊伍，因此它們的高中比率是未定義，不是零。2025 年的接合以 village 名稱為鍵，不用 uuid、也不用隊伍 id，因為隊伍 id 每一季都會重新發放。相關係數為 Pearson 係數，p 值為 200,000 次重排的雙尾置換檢定；年度內的異質性檢定為對照 32.0% 整組比率的卡方檢定，搭配 100,000 次抽樣、維持各 village 真實規模的蒙地卡羅虛無分布。最關鍵的保留：對一支選擇進入某 village 的隊伍而言，獲獎肯定比率不是它的獲獎機率。隊伍自己挑選 village，而強隊會群聚——依國家、依學校網絡，也依模仿鄰近學校有效的做法——因此這些比率描述的是「誰進了某個 village」，不是「進去會發生什麼」。本分析不導出、也不提供「進入某個 village 以獲獎」這種形式的建議。13 個 village 中有 6 個的高中隊伍不到 10 支，加起來只占 147 支中的 22 支，而那幾列的比率會因單一支隊伍的結果而移動 14 到 100 個百分點。GEMS-Taiwan 是本報告作者自己的團隊，在這些統計中與其他所有隊伍以相同方式計入。"},{"id":"ai-disclosure","tab":"drylab","order":42,"kicker":"Original analysis","kicker_zh":"原創分析","title":"Everyone disclosed their AI use. The argument is over what counts as AI.","title_zh":"每一支隊伍都揭露了 AI 使用。真正的爭點是：什麼才算 AI。","lede":"We read the official attributions record of all 106 decorated teams. The expected finding was 'almost nobody'. The actual finding is 106 of 106 — because iGEM 2026 made AI Tool Use a required block of a Bronze medal deliverable. What stays invisible is the half nobody was asked about.","lede_zh":"我們讀完全部 106 支獲獎隊伍的官方貢獻紀錄。原本預期的答案是「幾乎沒有人」，實際答案卻是 106 比 106——因為 iGEM 2026 把「AI 工具使用」列為銅牌必繳項目中的一個必填區塊。真正看不見的，是沒有人被要求交代的那一半。","body":"We went looking for a hole and found a floor. **iGEM 2026's Attributions Form carries a first-class AI Tool Use block**, listed by iGEM itself alongside Team Member Contributions, iGEM & Partner Offers, External Contributions and Project Timeline — and the Attributions Form is a Bronze medal criterion that, in iGEM's words, \"must be filled out completely, accurately, and honestly\". We opened the canonical record for every one of the 106 decorated teams in this report at `teams.igem.org/wiki/<id>/attributions`. **106 of 106 have a non-empty AI Tool Use section, and 106 of 106 name at least one general-purpose assistant.** ChatGPT appears in 80 records, Claude in 68, Gemini in 30, Doubao or Kimi in 21, DeepSeek in 18, Copilot in 6. The median section is about 1,230 characters; the shortest is 99, the longest 7,418.\n\nThis is not confined to tidying prose. Counting the task tags teams selected: **Writing 80, Wiki Coding 78, Visualization 78, Background Research 64, Analysis 60, Software 59, Conceptualization 40**. Fifty-nine of 106 decorated teams state that an assistant touched their code, and 60 that one touched their analysis. A reader who assumed the dry lab was hand-written is reading 2026 wrong.\n\n**Then the gap.** Three different things get filed under one word. (a) Scientific machine learning a team built or trained itself. (b) Third-party foundation models used as instruments — AlphaFold, ESM, ProteinMPNN, RFdiffusion, Boltz. (c) General-purpose assistants writing code and prose. Category (c) is disclosed universally, because a form field asked for it. Category (b) mostly is not: **40 of the 106 team files name a third-party structure-prediction or protein-design model** — the technique census on this site counts AlphaFold in 32 files, ProteinMPNN in 14, and RFdiffusion, ESM and Boltz in 8 each — but **only 19 of 106 name any such model inside the AI Tool Use block, and of the 40 teams that used one, only 15 listed it there.** Category (a), a team's own trained model, almost never appears in the AI field at all; it lives on the Model page as science. That is not dishonesty, it is a genuine conceptual disagreement: teams treat running AlphaFold as structural biology, not as using an AI tool. The consequence for a reader is still real — **the attributions record reliably tells you who helped write the wiki, and not what produced the structure you are looking at.**\n\n**Quality varies far more than presence.** Seventy-two of 106 records include review, verification or human-oversight language. Only **4 of 106** state a negative boundary — what the AI did *not* do: UOregon, GEMS-Taiwan, Uni-Padua-IT and Athens. The best disclosure of the season is not on the form at all. **Al-Nahrain-IRAQ** wrote a *Responsible AI use* section on their own attributions page: a table of use, tools and **who reviewed the result**, with model versions named, an honest row reading \"An AI assistant (which one was not recorded)\", a line that Gemini was used only for prototypes and \"none of its output is published here\", and a closing boundary — \"No scientific claim, data figure, simulation result, quote, or citation on this wiki was generated by AI.\" **Toronto** comes second with a per-task list and the single best sentence in the cohort: \"We used the raw outputs, not the AI summary, as the record.\" At the other end, ICJFLS files 99 characters (\"Deepseek — Translate Chinese document and the content for Wiki to English\") and **PSI Korea** attributes the analysis of its optical characterisation data, its wiki images and its promotion video to ChatGPT in 182 characters with no statement that anyone checked the result.\n\n**Did anyone test a model's output at the bench and say so?** Yes, and the high-school example is the strongest. **NBJF** ran a full generative pipeline — RFdiffusion backbones, ProteinMPNN/LigandMPNN inverse folding, ESMFold and AlphaFold refolding checks, TemStaPro and SaProt scoring — then **expressed 85 de novo sequences, got detectable SDS-PAGE expression for 25, and published that as an application dataset rather than a success claim**. **HangzhouFourteenAP** is the honest inverse: FoldX ranked Y166Q top at −1.63 kcal/mol, the DNS activity assay put Q172P first at net OD 1.881 with Y166Q last at 0.629, **below wild type at 0.996** — the computational winner was worse than doing nothing. They normalised by BCA to rule out protein load, revised the published ranking, and demoted Y166Q to a mechanistic probe instead of deleting it. The other end exists too: **UMA Malaga** states outright that Diana's ranking order, substitution rule and pooling layout are untested in the lab and that the lab contradicted the substitution rule; **BAID-China**'s RFantibody designs received \"computational screening and virtual validation\" and no bench test; **ABOA** hands over a 28-part Golden Gate set that is designed but untested.\n\n**Reported AI failures are rare and worth naming individually.** **Toronto** found that under homology-component-grouped splits their ESM-C embeddings lost to a single sequence-length column, reported that the random-split rho = 0.72 had been an artefact, and won Best Model for it; their Claude Sonnet literature-extraction pipeline is benchmarked against double-scored human curation at 95.0% precision and 87.1% recall with zero hallucinated enzymes across 32 doubly-scraped papers. **UPF-Barcelona** built iGEMforge, a Claude Code plugin of four skills, evaluated it over two cycles (28 cases, three runs per arm, an LLM judge against team-written rubrics, including deliberately planted flaws and silence cases), found no clear gain — experimental-design −0.11, scientific-evidence +0.04 — at roughly double the token cost, and **published that they therefore did not use it for project decisions**. **Jilin-China** ran a prespecified out-of-distribution test, found all 12 candidate-task combinations out of distribution, and declined to use the model scores at all. **Al-Nahrain-IRAQ** publishes Engine 1 as failed (2.4 g/L predicted at 13.25 h against 7.6 g/L measured) and states that parameters were read from papers with AI assistance and have not yet been re-checked by a team member. **XJTLU-Software** built delivery reconciliation into AMPilot on the premise that \"a fluent closing message is not a delivery receipt\". Five negative reports in 106 files. That is the scarce good.\n\n**GEMS-Taiwan, assessed on the same scale.** The team's record names three tools — Claude (Anthropic), Gemini (Google), ChatGPT (OpenAI) — with task tags, and closes with one of only four negative boundaries in the cohort: \"All AI outputs were verified by team members against primary literature or experimental data before use. No experimental data, results, or citations were AI-generated.\" That is above the median. What it does not do: the same paragraph is repeated verbatim under all three tools, so the record never says what each one actually did differently; no model versions are given and no reviewer is named for any item; **AlphaFold, which the project ran with a pre-set confidence gate, is not in the AI field at all**, so the team reproduces exactly the category-(b) blind spot described above; and the LLM-assisted QGIS workflow over 346 farming townships — the one place the team did something a reader would want the prompt for, and did publish the data-preparation prompt — is covered only by a generic *Analysis* tag that does not point at it. The team's own page at `2026.igem.wiki/gems-taiwan/attributions/` is also nothing but an embedded frame of the iGEM form: a reader whose browser blocks the frame sees a banner and no attribution at all. **Verdict for the whole cohort, GEMS included: the disclosure on display sits exactly at what iGEM asked for, and only rarely above it.** iGEM asked which tools and which tasks, so teams supplied tools and tasks. iGEM did not ask who reviewed each output, which model version produced it, or what the AI did not do — so almost nobody said.","body_zh":"我們本來要找一個破洞，結果找到一塊地板。**iGEM 2026 的 Attributions Form 內建了一個正式的 AI Tool Use（AI 工具使用）區塊**，由 iGEM 自己與「團隊成員貢獻」「iGEM 與夥伴提供的資源」「外部貢獻」「專案時間軸」並列；而 Attributions Form 本身是銅牌評分條件，依 iGEM 的用字，它「必須完整、準確、誠實地填寫」。我們在 `teams.igem.org/wiki/<id>/attributions` 打開本報告 106 支獲獎隊伍的官方紀錄。**106 支裡有 106 支的 AI Tool Use 區塊不是空的，而且 106 支全部至少列出一個通用型 AI 助理。** ChatGPT 出現在 80 份紀錄中，Claude 68 份，Gemini 30 份，Doubao 或 Kimi 21 份，DeepSeek 18 份，Copilot 6 份。區塊長度中位數約 1,230 字元，最短 99，最長 7,418。\n\n這也不只是潤稿而已。依隊伍自己勾選的任務標籤計算：**Writing 80、Wiki Coding 78、Visualization 78、Background Research 64、Analysis 60、Software 59、Conceptualization 40**。106 支獲獎隊伍中，有 59 支明說 AI 助理碰過他們的程式碼，60 支說碰過他們的分析。若有人以為 2026 年的乾實驗室是純手工，那是讀錯了這一季。\n\n**接著是那個缺口。** 三件完全不同的事被塞進同一個詞裡。(a) 團隊自己建立或訓練的科學機器學習模型。(b) 當成儀器使用的第三方基礎模型——AlphaFold、ESM、ProteinMPNN、RFdiffusion、Boltz。(c) 用來寫程式與寫文字的通用型助理。第 (c) 類被普遍揭露，因為有一個欄位在問它。第 (b) 類大多沒有：**106 份團隊檔案中有 40 份提到第三方結構預測或蛋白質設計模型**——本站的技術普查頁計得 AlphaFold 出現在 32 份、ProteinMPNN 14 份、RFdiffusion／ESM／Boltz 各 8 份——但**只有 19 支在 AI Tool Use 區塊裡提到任何一個這類模型；在那 40 支實際用過的隊伍中，只有 15 支把它寫進該欄位。** 第 (a) 類，也就是隊伍自己訓練的模型，幾乎從不出現在 AI 欄位裡；它被放在 Model 頁上，當成科學。這不是不誠實，而是一個真實的概念分歧：隊伍把跑 AlphaFold 視為結構生物學，而不是使用 AI 工具。但對讀者而言，後果是實在的——**這份貢獻紀錄能可靠告訴你誰幫忙寫了 wiki，卻不告訴你眼前這個結構是誰算出來的。**\n\n**品質的落差遠大於有無。** 106 份紀錄中有 72 份含有審查、查核或人工監督的字句。只有 **4 份**寫出了否定邊界，也就是 AI *沒有*做什麼：UOregon、GEMS-Taiwan、Uni-Padua-IT 與 Athens。而本季最好的一份揭露根本不在表單上。**Al-Nahrain-IRAQ** 在自家貢獻頁上寫了一節 *Responsible AI use*：一張列出用途、工具與**由誰審查**的表格，標明模型版本，還有一列誠實寫著「An AI assistant (which one was not recorded)」（某個 AI 助理，但沒記錄是哪一個），另註明 Gemini 只用於原型，「none of its output is published here」（它的輸出沒有任何一項發表在這裡），最後收在一句邊界：「No scientific claim, data figure, simulation result, quote, or citation on this wiki was generated by AI.」（本 wiki 上沒有任何科學主張、資料圖、模擬結果、引語或參考文獻是 AI 生成的。）**Toronto** 居次，逐項任務條列，並寫下全體隊伍中最好的一句：「We used the raw outputs, not the AI summary, as the record.」（我們以原始輸出而非 AI 摘要作為紀錄。）另一端，ICJFLS 只交了 99 個字元（「Deepseek——把中文文件與 wiki 內容翻成英文」）；**PSI Korea** 用 182 個字元，把光學特性資料的分析、wiki 圖像與宣傳影片都歸給 ChatGPT，卻沒有任何一句說有人查核過結果。\n\n**有沒有人把模型輸出拿去實驗台驗證，而且講清楚？** 有，而且最強的例子來自高中組。**NBJF** 跑完一整條生成式設計流程——RFdiffusion 產生骨架、ProteinMPNN／LigandMPNN 反向折疊、ESMFold 與 AlphaFold 重折疊檢查、TemStaPro 與 SaProt 評分——接著**表現了 85 條 de novo 序列，其中 25 條在 SDS-PAGE 上可偵測到表現，並且把這份結果當成應用資料集發表，而不是當成成功宣告**。**HangzhouFourteenAP** 則是誠實的反例：FoldX 把 Y166Q 排第一（−1.63 kcal/mol），DNS 活性測定卻把 Q172P 排第一（淨 OD 1.881），Y166Q 墊底只有 0.629，**低於野生型的 0.996**——運算上的贏家比什麼都不改還差。他們以 BCA 定量標準化以排除蛋白質載量的影響，在正文中修正了已發表的排序，並把 Y166Q 降格為機制探針，而不是悄悄刪掉。另一端也存在：**UMA Malaga** 直接寫明 Diana 的排序規則、置換規則與混池佈局都未經實驗驗證，而且實驗結果與置換規則相牴觸；**BAID-China** 的 RFantibody 設計只做了「運算篩選與虛擬驗證」，沒有實驗台測試；**ABOA** 交出一組設計完成但未經測試的 28 個 Golden Gate 零件。\n\n**被報告出來的 AI 失敗很少，值得一個一個點名。** **Toronto** 發現在以同源性連通分量分組切分資料後，他們的 ESM-C 嵌入向量輸給了「序列長度」這單一欄位，並報告隨機切分下的 rho = 0.72 其實是假象，也因此拿下最佳模型獎；他們以 Claude Sonnet 建立的文獻萃取流程，對照雙人重複標註的人工語料做了基準測試，精確率 95.0%、召回率 87.1%，在 32 篇雙重萃取的論文中沒有任何一個幻覺出來的酵素。**UPF-Barcelona** 做了 iGEMforge，一個含四項技能的 Claude Code 外掛，經過兩輪評估（28 個案例、每組三次執行、以 LLM 擔任評審對照隊伍自撰的評分準則，含刻意植入瑕疵的案例與「應該保持沉默」的案例），結果沒有明顯增益——experimental-design −0.11、scientific-evidence +0.04——而 token 成本約為兩倍，於是**公開說明他們因此沒有用它來做專案決策**。**Jilin-China** 先跑了預先設定的分布外（OOD）檢查，發現 12 組候選—任務組合全部落在分布外，就乾脆完全不採用模型分數。**Al-Nahrain-IRAQ** 把 Engine 1 當成失敗發表（13.25 小時預測 2.4 g/L，實測 7.6 g/L），並說明參數是在 AI 協助下從論文讀出來的，尚未由任何一位隊員重新核對。**XJTLU-Software** 在 AMPilot 中加入交付核對機制，前提是「一則流暢的結語訊息不等於一張交付收據」。106 份檔案裡五份負面報告。那就是稀缺的好東西。\n\n**用同一把尺看 GEMS-Taiwan。** 該隊的紀錄列出三個工具——Claude (Anthropic)、Gemini (Google)、ChatGPT (OpenAI)——附任務標籤，並以全體僅有的四個否定邊界之一作結：「All AI outputs were verified by team members against primary literature or experimental data before use. No experimental data, results, or citations were AI-generated.」（所有 AI 輸出在使用前都經隊員對照原始文獻或實驗資料查核。沒有任何實驗資料、結果或引用是 AI 生成的。）這高於中位數。但它沒有做到的是：同一段文字在三個工具底下逐字重複，所以這份紀錄從未說出每個工具各自實際做了什麼不同的事；沒有標明模型版本，也沒有為任何一項指名審查者；**專案以預設信心門檻跑過的 AlphaFold，根本不在 AI 欄位裡**，因此該隊正好複製了上文描述的第 (b) 類盲點；而那套涵蓋 346 個農業鄉鎮、由 LLM 協助的 QGIS 工作流——全隊最值得讀者看到提示詞的一處，而且團隊確實公開了資料準備用的提示詞——在紀錄裡只被一個籠統的 *Analysis* 標籤涵蓋，沒有任何指向。該隊自家的 `2026.igem.wiki/gems-taiwan/attributions/` 頁面也只是一個嵌入 iGEM 表單的內嵌框架：瀏覽器若擋下該框架，讀者看到的就是一張橫幅與完全沒有貢獻紀錄。**對整個群體（包含 GEMS）的結論是：眼前的揭露水準正好等於 iGEM 要求的水準，很少高過它。** iGEM 問的是用了哪些工具、做了哪些任務，隊伍就交出工具與任務。iGEM 沒有問每一項輸出由誰審查、是哪個模型版本產出的、以及 AI 沒有做什麼——所以幾乎沒有人說。","cards":[{"kicker":"The base rate","kicker_zh":"基準比率","title":"106 of 106 — because a form field asked","title_zh":"106 比 106——因為有一個欄位在問","body":"Every decorated team in this report has a non-empty AI Tool Use section in its official iGEM attributions record, and every one names at least one general-purpose assistant. The median entry runs about 1,230 characters. This is the one place in iGEM where a disclosure norm already exists and is universally obeyed — and the reason is simply that the deliverable has a box for it.","body_zh":"本報告中每一支獲獎隊伍，在其官方 iGEM 貢獻紀錄裡的 AI Tool Use 區塊都不是空的，而且每一支都至少列出一個通用型 AI 助理。項目長度中位數約 1,230 字元。這是 iGEM 中唯一一個揭露規範已經存在且被普遍遵守的地方——原因很單純：那份必繳文件上有一個欄位。","chips":["106 of 106","ChatGPT x80","Claude x68","Gemini x30"],"chips_zh":["106/106","ChatGPT ×80","Claude ×68","Gemini ×30"]},{"kicker":"What iGEM required","kicker_zh":"iGEM 要求了什麼","title":"AI Tool Use is part of a Bronze medal criterion","title_zh":"AI 工具使用，屬於銅牌評分條件的一部分","body":"iGEM's own deliverables guide lists five submission blocks for the required Attributions Form: Team Member Contributions, AI Tool Use, iGEM & Partner Offers, External Contributions, Project Timeline. The medals page makes the Attributions Form Bronze criterion 2 and says it \"must be filled out completely, accurately, and honestly\". So AI disclosure in 2026 was not optional and not a special-prize flourish — it was the price of a bronze medal.","body_zh":"iGEM 自己的繳交項目指引列出必繳 Attributions Form 的五個區塊：團隊成員貢獻、AI 工具使用、iGEM 與夥伴資源、外部貢獻、專案時間軸。獎牌頁把 Attributions Form 列為銅牌第 2 項條件，並寫明它「必須完整、準確、誠實地填寫」。所以 2026 年的 AI 揭露既不是選填，也不是為了特別獎的裝飾——它是拿到銅牌的入場費。","chips":["Required deliverable","Bronze criterion 2","5 submission blocks"],"chips_zh":["必繳項目","銅牌條件 2","5 個繳交區塊"],"link":"https://competition.igem.org/deliverables/guides#h-attributions-form","linkText":"iGEM deliverable guide"},{"kicker":"The invisible category","kicker_zh":"看不見的那一類","title":"AlphaFold is filed as biology, not as AI","title_zh":"AlphaFold 被歸檔為生物學，而不是 AI","body":"Forty of the 106 team files name a third-party structure-prediction or protein-design model. Only 19 teams name any such model inside the AI Tool Use block, and only 15 of the 40 actual users put it there. Teams read \"AI tool\" as \"chatbot\", so the record tells you who drafted the wiki text and not what produced the structure in the figure. A disclosure norm that only catches assistants catches the cheaper half.","body_zh":"106 份團隊檔案中有 40 份提到第三方結構預測或蛋白質設計模型。只有 19 支在 AI Tool Use 區塊裡提到任何一個這類模型，而在那 40 支實際使用者中，只有 15 支寫在那裡。隊伍把「AI 工具」讀成「聊天機器人」，於是紀錄告訴你 wiki 文字是誰起草的，卻不告訴你圖上的結構是誰算出來的。一套只抓得到助理的揭露規範，抓到的是比較便宜的那一半。","chips":["40 used one","19 listed one","15 of 40 overlap"],"chips_zh":["40 支用過模型","19 支填進欄位","15/40 重疊"]},{"kicker":"The best in the cohort","kicker_zh":"全體最佳","title":"Al-Nahrain-IRAQ wrote the table everyone else should copy","title_zh":"Al-Nahrain-IRAQ 寫出了其他人都該照抄的那張表","body":"Their wiki carries a Responsible AI use section beyond the form: a table of use, tools and who reviewed the result; model versions named; a row that honestly reads \"An AI assistant (which one was not recorded)\"; a note that Gemini was used only for prototypes and \"none of its output is published here\"; and the boundary \"No scientific claim, data figure, simulation result, quote, or citation on this wiki was generated by AI.\" They also publish their own failed model engine on the same wiki.","body_zh":"他們的 wiki 在表單之外另寫了一節 Responsible AI use：一張列出用途、工具與由誰審查的表格；標明模型版本；其中一列誠實寫著「某個 AI 助理（沒記錄是哪一個）」；另註明 Gemini 只用於原型，「它的輸出沒有任何一項發表在這裡」；最後收在一句邊界：「本 wiki 上沒有任何科學主張、資料圖、模擬結果、引語或參考文獻是 AI 生成的。」同一個 wiki 上，他們也公開了自己失敗的模型引擎。","chips":["Per-use table","Named reviewers","Negative boundary"],"chips_zh":["逐項用途表","具名審查者","否定邊界"],"link":"https://2026.igem.wiki/al-nahrain-iraq/attributions","linkText":"Al-Nahrain-IRAQ attributions"},{"kicker":"The honest end","kicker_zh":"誠實的那一端","title":"85 designs expressed, 25 detectable, published as a dataset","title_zh":"表現了 85 條設計、25 條可偵測，當成資料集發表","body":"NBJF, a high-school team, ran RFdiffusion, ProteinMPNN/LigandMPNN, ESMFold, AlphaFold, TemStaPro and SaProt, then took 85 de novo sequences to the bench, got detectable SDS-PAGE expression for 25, and reported the result as an application dataset rather than a success claim. Compare UMA Malaga, which says plainly that its ranking order, substitution rule and pooling layout are untested in the lab — and that the lab contradicted the substitution rule.","body_zh":"高中隊伍 NBJF 跑了 RFdiffusion、ProteinMPNN／LigandMPNN、ESMFold、AlphaFold、TemStaPro 與 SaProt，接著把 85 條 de novo 序列帶進實驗台，其中 25 條在 SDS-PAGE 上可偵測到表現，並把結果當成應用資料集而非成功宣告發表。對照 UMA Malaga：它直說自己的排序規則、置換規則與混池佈局都未經實驗驗證——而且實驗結果與置換規則相牴觸。","chips":["85 expressed","25 detectable","Not a success claim"],"chips_zh":["表現 85 條","可偵測 25 條","不宣稱成功"]},{"kicker":"Five negative reports","kicker_zh":"五份負面報告","title":"The prediction that lost, and the plugin that did not help","title_zh":"輸掉的那個預測，和沒幫上忙的那個外掛","body":"HangzhouFourteenAP: FoldX picked Y166Q at -1.63 kcal/mol; the assay put it last at net OD 0.629, below wild type at 0.996, and they revised the published ranking. UPF-Barcelona built a Claude Code plugin, A/B tested it over 28 cases with planted flaws, found no clear gain at double the token cost, and said so. Toronto reported that a homology-grouped split made their embeddings lose to sequence length. Jilin-China ran an out-of-distribution check and declined to use the scores. Al-Nahrain-IRAQ published a failed engine.","body_zh":"HangzhouFourteenAP：FoldX 以 −1.63 kcal/mol 選出 Y166Q，活性測定卻把它排到最後（淨 OD 0.629），低於野生型的 0.996，於是他們修正了已發表的排序。UPF-Barcelona 做了一個 Claude Code 外掛，用 28 個含植入瑕疵的案例做 A/B 測試，發現在兩倍 token 成本下沒有明顯增益，並且照實說出來。Toronto 報告以同源性分組切分後，他們的嵌入向量輸給了序列長度。Jilin-China 跑了分布外檢查後決定不採用分數。Al-Nahrain-IRAQ 公開了一個失敗的引擎。","chips":["5 of 106 files","Best Model went to one of them"],"chips_zh":["5/106 份檔案","Best Model 落在其中一支"]},{"kicker":"What this means for GEMS","kicker_zh":"這對 GEMS 的意義","title":"GEMS-Taiwan is above the median and below its own standard","title_zh":"GEMS-Taiwan 高於中位數，低於自己的標準","body":"The team's record names Claude, Gemini and ChatGPT with task tags and one of only four negative boundaries in the cohort. But the same paragraph repeats verbatim under all three tools, no model versions or per-item reviewers are given, the project's AlphaFold work is absent from the AI field entirely, and the published LLM-assisted QGIS prompt is not pointed at. The attributions page itself is an embedded frame of the iGEM form, so a reader whose browser blocks it sees no attribution at all.","body_zh":"該隊的紀錄列出 Claude、Gemini 與 ChatGPT，附任務標籤，並寫下全體僅有的四個否定邊界之一。但同一段文字在三個工具底下逐字重複，沒有模型版本、也沒有逐項審查者；專案中的 AlphaFold 工作完全沒有出現在 AI 欄位；已公開的 LLM 協助 QGIS 提示詞也沒有被指向。貢獻頁本身只是嵌入 iGEM 表單的內嵌框架，瀏覽器若擋下它，讀者看到的是完全沒有貢獻紀錄。","chips":["3 tools named","0 model versions","0 named reviewers","AlphaFold omitted"],"chips_zh":["指名 3 項工具","0 個模型版本","0 位具名審查者","漏了 AlphaFold"]}],"table":{"head":["Team","What the AI record actually says","Which kind of AI","Where it lives"],"head_zh":["隊伍","AI 紀錄實際寫了什麼","屬於哪一類 AI","寫在哪裡"],"rows":[["Al-Nahrain-IRAQ (6520)","Table of use, tools and who reviewed; model versions; \"An AI assistant (which one was not recorded)\"; \"No scientific claim, data figure, simulation result, quote, or citation on this wiki was generated by AI.\"","Assistants (c)","Team-written wiki section, beyond the form"],["Toronto (6187)","Per-task bracketed list; \"We used the raw outputs, not the AI summary, as the record.\" LLM extraction benchmarked at 95.0% precision, 87.1% recall, zero hallucinated enzymes","Assistants (c) + own ML (a)","Attributions form and Model page"],["Michigan (6276)","\"Claude Code was used to help scaffold and write most of the RiboTherm module code, however all conceptualization was done by team members.\"","Assistants (c)","Attributions form"],["Uni-Padua-IT (6151)","Debugging, proofreading and figure elements; \"Every AI-generated suggestion was reviewed, tested and where needed, corrected by team members who take full responsibility.\"","Assistants (c)","Attributions form"],["NBJF (6264)","ChatGPT for writing and code, with AlphaFold3 listed in the same block for structure prediction of TdT complexes","Assistants (c) and foundation models (b), together","Attributions form"],["GEMS-Taiwan (6072)","Claude, Gemini, ChatGPT with task tags; \"All AI outputs were verified by team members... No experimental data, results, or citations were AI-generated.\" AlphaFold absent","Assistants (c) only","Attributions form, embedded in the wiki"],["UMA Malaga (6119)","Claude for front-end only, core logic and validation human; separately, a wiki matrix recording ranking, substitution and pooling as untested in the lab","Assistants (c), plus an explicit untested-output matrix","Attributions form and Software page"],["PSI Korea (6479)","182 characters: ChatGPT \"analysed the optical characterisation data... produced the wiki images, and made the team Promotion Video\" - no review statement","Assistants (c)","Attributions form"],["ICJFLS (6098)","99 characters: \"Deepseek - Translate Chinese document and the content for Wiki to English.\" The shortest record in the cohort","Assistants (c)","Attributions form"]],"rows_zh":[["Al-Nahrain-IRAQ (6520)","用途／工具／審查者三欄表格；標明模型版本；一列寫著「某個 AI 助理（沒記錄是哪一個）」；「本 wiki 上沒有任何科學主張、資料圖、模擬結果、引語或參考文獻是 AI 生成的。」","助理（c）","團隊自撰的 wiki 段落，在表單之外"],["Toronto (6187)","逐項任務條列；「我們以原始輸出而非 AI 摘要作為紀錄。」LLM 萃取經基準測試：精確率 95.0%、召回率 87.1%、零幻覺酵素","助理（c）＋自建機器學習（a）","Attributions form 與 Model 頁"],["Michigan (6276)","「Claude Code 協助搭建並撰寫 RiboTherm 模組的大部分程式碼，但所有概念構想皆由隊員完成。」","助理（c）","Attributions form"],["Uni-Padua-IT (6151)","除錯、校對與圖像元素；「每一項 AI 產生的建議都由承擔全部責任的隊員審查、測試，必要時加以修正。」","助理（c）","Attributions form"],["NBJF (6264)","ChatGPT 用於寫作與程式，同一區塊中同時列出 AlphaFold3，用於 TdT 複合體的結構預測","助理（c）與基礎模型（b）並列","Attributions form"],["GEMS-Taiwan (6072)","Claude、Gemini、ChatGPT 附任務標籤；「所有 AI 輸出都經隊員查核……沒有任何實驗資料、結果或引用是 AI 生成的。」AlphaFold 未列入","僅助理（c）","Attributions form，以內嵌框架放在 wiki"],["UMA Malaga (6119)","Claude 僅用於前端，核心邏輯與驗證由人完成；另在 wiki 上以矩陣記錄排序、置換與混池「未經實驗驗證」","助理（c），外加明確的未驗證輸出矩陣","Attributions form 與 Software 頁"],["PSI Korea (6479)","182 個字元：ChatGPT「分析了 Bio Color ID 的光學特性資料……製作 wiki 圖像與團隊宣傳影片」——沒有任何審查陳述","助理（c）","Attributions form"],["ICJFLS (6098)","99 個字元：「Deepseek——把中文文件與 wiki 內容翻成英文。」全體中最短的一份紀錄","助理（c）","Attributions form"]]},"checklist":["Record it the day it happens, not in October. One line in the dry-lab notebook per session: date, tool and version (Claude Opus 5.1, not \"AI\"), what you asked for, what you kept, and who checked it. The 2026 teams with the best records are the ones who logged as they went; the one who wrote \"an AI assistant (which one was not recorded)\" is the honest cost of logging late.","Disclose all three kinds, not just the chatbot. (a) A model you trained or fitted yourself goes on the Model page with its data split. (b) A third-party model you ran as an instrument - AlphaFold, ESM, ProteinMPNN, Boltz - goes in the methods AND in the AI record, with version and settings, because 2026 shows 25 of 40 teams left it out of the AI record entirely. (c) A general-purpose assistant goes in the AI record with the task it touched.","A tool is a tool; nothing is a co-author. Name the tool, name the human who is answerable for the output. Every GEMS artefact - a figure, a script, a paragraph, a parameter - has exactly one named human reviewer, and that name goes next to the tool, as Al-Nahrain-IRAQ did.","Mark every model output UNVALIDATED until a bench result exists, in the text and in the figure caption. A predicted structure, a designed sequence, a ranked shortlist, a fitted parameter read out of a paper: all unvalidated until measured. Write the status, not the hope - UMA Malaga's three honest categories (automated tests / real services / wet lab, with \"not shown\" recorded as a result) are the model to copy.","Publish the prompt or the script whenever the AI produced data rather than prose. If an assistant extracted parameters, prepared a GIS layer or read numbers out of figures, the prompt is part of the method and belongs in the repository with the code.","Write the negative boundary explicitly: what AI did not do. Only 4 of 106 decorated teams did this in 2026. One sentence - no experimental data, no result, no citation, no scientific claim was AI-generated - is cheap to write and is the single line a sceptical reader is looking for.","Benchmark the assistant when it does scientific work, and publish the number. Toronto measured their extraction pipeline at 95.0% precision and 87.1% recall against double-scored human curation. An unbenchmarked extraction pipeline is not a method, it is a hope.","Report the failures. The AI prediction that lost to the bench, the designed sequence that did not express, the plugin that did not beat the base model, the hallucinated reference caught in review. Five teams in 106 did this in 2026 and one of them won Best Model for it. Log every caught hallucination with its citation so the count exists at the end of the season."],"checklist_zh":["當天就記錄，不要等到十月。乾實驗室筆記本每次工作寫一行：日期、工具與版本（寫 Claude Opus 5.1，不要寫「AI」）、你要求了什麼、你採用了什麼、由誰查核。2026 年紀錄最好的隊伍都是邊做邊記的；那句「某個 AI 助理（沒記錄是哪一個）」，就是太晚才記錄的誠實代價。","三類都要揭露，不是只揭露聊天機器人。(a) 你自己訓練或擬合的模型，放在 Model 頁並附上資料切分方式。(b) 你當成儀器使用的第三方模型——AlphaFold、ESM、ProteinMPNN、Boltz——除了寫進方法，也要寫進 AI 紀錄，附版本與設定；因為 2026 年的資料顯示，40 支用過的隊伍中有 25 支完全沒寫進 AI 紀錄。(c) 通用型助理寫進 AI 紀錄，並註明它碰了哪一項工作。","工具就是工具，沒有任何東西是共同作者。寫出工具名稱，也寫出為該輸出負責的那個人。GEMS 的每一項產出——一張圖、一段程式、一段文字、一個參數——都只有一位具名的人類審查者，而那個名字要緊鄰工具名稱並列，就像 Al-Nahrain-IRAQ 那樣。","在有實驗結果之前，每一項模型輸出都標示為「未驗證」，正文與圖說都要標。預測出的結構、設計出的序列、排序後的候選名單、從論文讀來的擬合參數：在被量測之前一律未驗證。寫狀態，不要寫願望——UMA Malaga 那三個誠實的分類（自動化測試／真實服務／濕實驗，並把「未呈現」本身記為一種結果）值得照抄。","只要 AI 產出的是資料而不是文字，就公開提示詞或腳本。如果助理萃取了參數、準備了 GIS 圖層，或從圖裡讀出數字，那段提示詞就是方法的一部分，應該和程式碼一起放進版本庫。","明確寫出否定邊界：AI 沒有做什麼。2026 年 106 支獲獎隊伍中只有 4 支做到。一句話——沒有任何實驗資料、結果、引用或科學主張是 AI 生成的——寫起來很便宜，而且正是存疑的讀者在找的那一行。","當助理做的是科學工作時，要做基準測試並公開數字。Toronto 量出他們的萃取流程對照雙人重複標註的精確率 95.0%、召回率 87.1%。一條沒有基準測試的萃取流程不是方法，只是一廂情願。","把失敗報出來。輸給實驗台的 AI 預測、表現不出來的設計序列、贏不過基礎模型的外掛、在審查中抓到的幻覺參考文獻。2026 年 106 支隊伍中有五支這麼做，其中一支還因此拿下最佳模型獎。每抓到一次幻覺就連同該引用一起記下來，這樣一季結束時才會有一個數字。"],"method":"Base rate: we opened the canonical iGEM attributions record for each of the 106 decorated teams in this report at teams.igem.org/wiki/<id>/attributions - the same record their wikis display - rendered it in a browser (the pages are client-side React and return an empty shell to a plain fetch), and extracted the AI Tool Use section verbatim. All 106 returned a page and all 106 had a non-empty AI Tool Use section; none was missing or truncated. Tool and task counts are regex matches on those extracted sections, so a tool named only in an attached document or on a Model page is not counted here, and 'review language' means the section contains words such as review, verify, check, validate or oversight, which is a weaker test than actually reviewing. Foundation-model use (40 of 106) is counted from the dry-lab fields of the 106 team files on this site; the per-tool figures quoted (AlphaFold 32, ProteinMPNN 14, RFdiffusion 8, ESM 8, Boltz 8) are the technique census page's numbers, not ours, and we report them so the two pages agree. The iGEM requirement is quoted from competition.igem.org/deliverables/guides and the medals page; the detailed Attributions Form requirements page is behind a team login and we did not read it. The hard limit: this method can only see what a team wrote down. Undisclosed assistant use is invisible by construction - we cannot detect it, we did not try to infer it, and nothing here should be read as a claim about which teams 'probably' used more AI than they said. Equally, a disclosure is a statement, not evidence: we checked what teams wrote, not whether it is complete. The 106/106 figure therefore measures compliance with a required form field, not the true extent of AI use, and the 4-of-106 negative-boundary figure and the 5 reported failures are the numbers that actually distinguish teams, because those were not asked for. The sample is decorated teams only, so this is not a base rate for the competition.","method_zh":"基準比率：我們針對本報告 106 支獲獎隊伍，逐一打開 teams.igem.org/wiki/<id>/attributions 上的官方 iGEM 貢獻紀錄（也就是各隊 wiki 所顯示的同一份紀錄），在瀏覽器中完成算繪（這些頁面是用戶端 React，直接抓取只會得到空殼），並逐字擷取其中的 AI Tool Use 區塊。106 份全部成功載入，106 份的 AI Tool Use 區塊都不是空的，沒有缺漏或截斷。工具與任務的計數是對這些擷取段落做樣式比對，因此只出現在附件文件或 Model 頁上的工具不會被計入；而「審查字句」僅表示該段落包含 review、verify、check、validate 或 oversight 等字詞，這是比「真的有審查」寬鬆得多的判準。基礎模型使用（106 支中 40 支）是依本站 106 份團隊檔案的乾實驗室欄位計算；文中引用的各工具數字（AlphaFold 32、ProteinMPNN 14、RFdiffusion 8、ESM 8、Boltz 8）取自本站技術普查頁，不是我們自己的計數，列出是為了讓兩頁一致。iGEM 的要求引自 competition.igem.org/deliverables/guides 與獎牌頁；Attributions Form 的詳細要求頁需要隊伍登入，我們沒有閱讀。硬性限制：這個方法只看得見團隊寫下來的東西。未揭露的助理使用在定義上就是看不見的——我們偵測不到，也沒有嘗試推論，本頁任何內容都不應被讀成在指認哪些隊伍「大概」用得比說的多。同樣地，揭露是一種陳述，不是證據：我們查核的是團隊寫了什麼，而不是寫得完不完整。因此 106 比 106 這個數字量到的是對一個必填欄位的遵循程度，而不是 AI 使用的真實範圍；真正能區分隊伍的，是「106 支中只有 4 支寫出否定邊界」與「5 份負面報告」這兩個數字，因為那兩件事沒有人要求。樣本僅限獲獎隊伍，所以這不是整個競賽的基準比率。"},{"id":"education-afterlife","tab":"good","order":42,"kicker":"Original analysis","kicker_zh":"原創分析","title":"Could a teacher in Taiwan use this next week?","title_zh":"台灣的老師下週就能拿去上課嗎？","lede":"The suspicion was wrong. Of 285 education files linked from the wikis of 31 decorated iGEM 2026 teams, 284 download today and one returns 403 — not a single 404. Education survives the Jamboree far better than software (8 of 21 still running) or hardware (6 of 20 rebuildable), because a PDF needs no server. What stops a teacher in Taiwan is something else: 9 of 64 named artefacts were never turned into a file at all, only 1 of 136 PDFs says anyone may reuse it, and exactly 2 exist in Traditional Chinese, both from Taiwanese teams.","lede_zh":"原本的懷疑錯了。31 支 2026 年得獎隊伍的 wiki 上，共有 285 個教育檔案連結，今天 284 個下載得到，一個回傳 403——一個 404 都沒有。教育成果撐過 Jamboree 的能力，遠勝軟體（21 個中 8 個還在線上）和硬體（20 件中 6 件可重建），因為一份 PDF 不需要伺服器。擋住台灣老師的是別的東西：64 件具名成果中有 9 件根本沒有被做成檔案，136 份 PDF 裡只有 1 份寫明別人可以重製使用，而正體中文版本剛好只有 2 件，兩件都出自台灣隊伍。","body":"**Two hundred and eighty-four of two hundred and eighty-five.** Every education file linked from the wikis in this sample was fetched and its HTTP status recorded, and the dead-link count is one: ZQT-Nanjing's card-design sheet for the *Synthetic Biology Lab* game returns `403 AccessDenied` from the S3 bucket, while the English rulebook beside it downloads fine. A team printed a rulebook and could not print the cards. That is the entire link-rot finding for the year. The sister studies of software and hardware both turned on a hosting decision — 8 of 21 tools were still running because someone kept paying, 6 of 20 instruments were rebuildable because someone pressed Export. Education has no such cliff. `static.igem.wiki` serves the file, the wiki freeze makes it permanent, and nobody has to maintain anything. **On pure survival, education wins the trilogy outright.**\n\nSo the honest question is not whether the artefact exists but whether a stranger can do anything with it, and there the picture darkens in three specific ways. First, 9 of the 64 named artefacts were never made into a file. The clearest case is the Best Education winner itself. **XJTLU-China's education page counts \"18 educational toolkits\" and says the aim is to \"enable other educators to adopt and adapt our materials\" — and the page links not one downloadable file.** The distribution channel it points to, a hub on XJTLU's Learning Mall Premium platform, is genuinely live and needs no login; it is also a showcase, not a library. Opened signed-out it offers one video episode, one podcast episode, a page about the *Touch Life* tactile exhibition and a page about the *Game of Seagull* board game. There is no print sheet, no rulebook, no lesson plan, no file of any kind. Muenster-University does the same thing more briefly: *Design Your Crop*, a 3–6 player card game, is described and endorsed by a named playtester, and there is nothing to print. Cornell's *Plasmid Pals* appears in four separate event write-ups and has no file. IIT Bombay, a Best Education nominee, serves a 638-byte shell at `/education`. The pattern is exactly the one the hardware census found in CAD: the thing is rendered, photographed and described, and never exported.\n\nSecond, almost nothing carries a licence. Of 136 education PDFs with an extractable text layer, **one** says anything about reuse on its own content: Cornell's *Pass the Torch* guide, which opens with \"FREE TO COPY, ADAPT & PASS ON\" and closes with a CC BY 4.0 notice. Two more — HKSSC's CUHK collaboration comics — cite CC BY for borrowed Wikimedia figures, which is good practice but is attribution, not permission. Every 2026 wiki page carries iGEM's CC BY 4.0 footer, so the files are arguably covered while they sit on the wiki. The moment a teacher downloads one, mails it to a colleague and the colleague asks whether the school may reprint it, the file itself answers nothing. CalPolySLO is the counter-example worth copying: it states the licence on the page (\"Open-license (CC BY 4.0) lab manuals\"), publishes an instructor packet with prep lists, reagent costs, timings and common failure points, and its Google Sheet and Drive files all open signed-out — checked, because an education link that needs a Google account is the same failure the hardware study found in Toronto's empty CAD folder.\n\nThird, and this is the part that matters most to a Taiwanese team: **of 31 decorated teams, three published education material in Traditional Chinese, and all three already read it.** NCKU-Tainan's 28-page 《與偏鄉共學》 handbook and GEMS-Taiwan's lesson plans and card games are Taiwanese; HKSSC's workshop materials are from Hong Kong. Every other Chinese-language education file in the census is Simplified — all 13 of BNDS-China's activity write-ups, all 13 of HFI's teaching plans and cards, all 7 of SJTU-BioX-Shanghai's. The translation effort this year was real and it was large: HFI issued its microbiology comic as text in twelve languages precisely so local educators could generate their own audio in languages the team does not speak, and Lambert-GA translated *The Mite-ty Adventure of Bentley the Bee* into thirteen. **Lambert's thirteen include Simplified Chinese and not Traditional.** Twenty-eight of the 64 artefacts exist in at least one language other than English. None of that reaches a Taiwanese classroom without someone retyping it.\n\nThe habit that separates a usable artefact from an admirable one is not hosting, as it was for software, nor export, as it was for hardware. **It is writing an instruction layer for a second adult.** Thirty-three of the 64 artefacts ship one — a teacher's guide, a facilitator pack, a rulebook, or a lesson plan with timings and materials. GU Frankfurt's organ-donation workshop ships an 18-page teachers' guide in German and English, the Myth-or-Fact card sheets and the slides, both languages, plus the ethics-committee documentation. Eton-College-UK ships a 58-page Activities Handbook with answer keys, and *Bio-Detectives* as a facilitator pack and a student pack separately, so the same workshop can be rerun by someone who was not there. Marburg went further and published a SciComm and Evaluation Guide aimed at future iGEM teams, having found that existing iGEM documentation records how outreach was organised and almost never how to evaluate it. ASIJ-Tokyo's seven lesson plans include a feedback page, added specifically because the team admits it did not systematically record feedback this year. The other 31 artefacts are the thing alone: a beautiful comic, a game board, a set of cards, and no note telling a stranger how long it takes or what to buy.\n\nOne format quietly outperformed everything else and deserves copying. Four teams published browser games served **from the frozen wiki itself**: LYON's *BL21* (a 7.3 MB script behind a wiki-hosted page, English and French, about fifteen minutes, nothing to install), GU Frankfurt's *START*, HongKong-JSS's *Small Signal*, and GEMS-Taiwan's two plant-stress games. None of them can go dark the way Vilnius-Lithuania's Ladder Detector did, because there is no service to suspend. The one artefact in the census hosted on a third-party platform, ASIJ-Tokyo's Unity game *Village 茶(Sa)kura* on itch.io, is live today and is the only one whose continued existence depends on someone else's business. And outside use — the column that was almost empty for hardware, where exactly one device in twenty had ever been used by an outsider — is where education is genuinely different. **Sixteen of the 64 artefacts carry at least one piece of evidence of use beyond the team's own events.** HKSSC's comic *The Tragedy of Margaret in Food Waste* was translated into Japanese by ASIJ-Tokyo and issued in Swahili. LYON and ASIJ-Tokyo both placed games in iGEM Patras's downloadable game library. Marburg tested the CLiPPR Toolbox with seven teachers at three schools and distributed *Plasmid Panic* through schools in German and English. BOKU-Vienna donated 《Welche Sprache spricht das Leben?》 to the lending collection of Vienna's Pappenheimgasse public library. Lambert-GA's bee book sits in the Atlanta Botanical Garden's library. Stanford's SynBase reports 750+ registered learners. NIS Almaty-Medeu names a teacher, Daniyar at Al-Farabi School No. 31, who ran his own session from their materials, and reports teachers in nine partner schools delivering activities without them. **That is sixteen, against one in twenty for hardware. Paper travels.**","body_zh":"**285 個裡有 284 個。**這份樣本中，每一個從 wiki 連出去的教育檔案都被實際抓取並記錄 HTTP 狀態，而死連結只有一個：ZQT-Nanjing 的《Synthetic Biology Lab》卡牌圖檔在 S3 上回傳 `403 AccessDenied`，旁邊那份英文規則書卻下載得好好的。一支隊伍印得出規則書，卻印不出卡片。這就是今年連結腐朽的全部。軟體與硬體那兩篇姊妹分析，關鍵都落在一個決定上——21 個工具中有 8 個還活著，是因為有人持續付代管費；20 件儀器中有 6 件可以重建，是因為有人按下了匯出。教育沒有這道懸崖。`static.igem.wiki` 負責供檔，wiki 凍結讓它永久存在，沒有人需要維護任何東西。**單就存活率而言，教育在這個三部曲裡毫無懸念地勝出。**\n\n所以真正該問的不是東西還在不在，而是陌生人能不能拿它做事；在這一點上，畫面從三個具體的方向暗下來。第一，64 件具名成果中有 9 件根本沒有被做成檔案。最清楚的例子就是最佳教育的得主本身。**XJTLU-China 的教育頁面數出「18 個教育工具包」，並寫明目的是要「enable other educators to adopt and adapt our materials」——而整個頁面沒有連出任何一個可下載的檔案。**它指向的發布管道，是西浦 Learning Mall Premium 上的一個專頁，那個專頁確實還活著、也不需要登入；但它是一個展示櫥窗，不是一座資料庫。以未登入狀態打開，裡面有一集影片、一集 podcast、一頁介紹《Touch Life》觸覺展覽、一頁介紹《Game of Seagull》桌遊。沒有列印稿、沒有規則書、沒有教案，沒有任何形式的檔案。Muenster-University 的情況更簡短：3 至 6 人的卡牌遊戲《Design Your Crop》有詳細描述，還附上一位具名試玩者的好評，但沒有任何東西可以印。Cornell 的《Plasmid Pals》出現在四篇不同的活動紀錄裡，同樣沒有檔案。IIT Bombay 身為最佳教育入圍者，`/education` 回傳的是一個 638 位元組的空殼。這個模式，正是硬體普查在 CAD 上看到的那一個：東西被算圖、被拍照、被描述，然後從來沒有被匯出。\n\n第二，幾乎沒有東西附帶授權。136 份可以抽出文字層的教育 PDF 中，只有**一份**對自己的內容說明了重製條件：Cornell 的《Pass the Torch》指南，開頭寫著「FREE TO COPY, ADAPT & PASS ON」，結尾附上 CC BY 4.0 聲明。另外兩份——HKSSC 與中大合作的漫畫——引用 CC BY，但那是為了標註借用的維基共享資源圖片；那是出處標示，不是授權。每一個 2026 年的 wiki 頁面都帶著 iGEM 的 CC BY 4.0 頁尾，所以檔案只要還掛在 wiki 上，勉強算是被涵蓋。但老師一旦把檔案下載下來、寄給同事，同事問學校能不能再印一批時，檔案本身答不出任何話。CalPolySLO 是值得照抄的反例：它在頁面上寫明授權（「Open-license (CC BY 4.0) lab manuals」），公開一份含備料清單、試劑成本、時程與常見失敗點的授課包，而它的 Google 試算表與雲端硬碟檔案在未登入狀態下全部打得開——這是實際驗證過的，因為一個需要 Google 帳號才能看的教育連結，和硬體那篇在 Toronto 空資料夾上看到的失敗是同一種。\n\n第三，而這是對台灣隊伍最關鍵的一點：**31 支得獎隊伍中，有三支公開了正體中文的教育材料，而這三支本來就看得懂正體中文。**NCKU-Tainan 那本 28 頁的《與偏鄉共學》手冊和 GEMS-Taiwan 的教案與卡牌遊戲來自台灣，HKSSC 的工作坊材料來自香港。這份普查裡其他所有中文教育檔案都是簡體——BNDS-China 的 13 份活動紀錄、HFI 的 13 份教案與互動卡、SJTU-BioX-Shanghai 的 7 份檔案，全部都是。今年的翻譯投入是真的，而且規模很大：HFI 把自己的微生物漫畫以文字形式釋出十二種語言，正是為了讓各地教育工作者能用團隊不會說的語言自行生成語音；Lambert-GA 把《The Mite-ty Adventure of Bentley the Bee》翻成十三種語言。**Lambert 那十三種包含簡體中文，不包含正體中文。**64 件成果中有 28 件存在至少一種英文以外的版本。這些全部都無法在沒有人重打一次的情況下進到台灣的教室。\n\n把「能用」和「令人佩服」分開的那個習慣，不是軟體那篇的代管，也不是硬體那篇的匯出。**是替第二個大人寫一層操作說明。**64 件成果中有 33 件附上了這一層——教師手冊、帶領者包、規則書，或是標明時間與教具的教案。GU Frankfurt 的器官捐贈工作坊附上 18 頁的教師指南（德文與英文各一份）、Myth-or-Fact 卡牌印刷稿、兩種語言的投影片，外加倫理審查文件。Eton-College-UK 附上 58 頁、含解答的活動手冊，並把《Bio-Detectives》拆成帶領者包和學生包兩份，讓當天不在場的人也能重跑同一場工作坊。Marburg 更進一步，寫了一份給未來 iGEM 隊伍看的科學傳播與評估指南，因為他們發現既有的 iGEM 文件記錄了外展活動怎麼辦，卻幾乎從不記錄要怎麼評估。ASIJ-Tokyo 的七份教案裡放了一頁回饋表，而且說明這是因為團隊今年沒有系統性地收集回饋才補上的。其餘 31 件就只是成果本身：一本漂亮的漫畫、一張遊戲板、一疊卡片，沒有任何一行字告訴陌生人這要花多久、要買什麼。\n\n有一種形式悄悄勝過其他所有形式，值得照抄。四支隊伍把瀏覽器遊戲**直接架在凍結後的 wiki 上**：LYON 的《BL21》（一個 7.3 MB 的腳本，掛在 wiki 自己的頁面後面，英文與法文，約十五分鐘，什麼都不用安裝）、GU Frankfurt 的《START》、HongKong-JSS 的《Small Signal》，以及 GEMS-Taiwan 的兩款植物逆境遊戲。它們都不可能像 Vilnius-Lithuania 的 Ladder Detector 那樣熄燈，因為根本沒有服務可以被停用。這份普查裡唯一架在第三方平台上的成果，是 ASIJ-Tokyo 放在 itch.io 的 Unity 遊戲《Village 茶(Sa)kura》；它今天還在線上，也是唯一一件存續與否取決於別人生意好壞的。而「外部使用」——硬體那篇幾乎全空的那一欄，二十件儀器中只有一件曾被團隊以外的人用過——正是教育真正不一樣的地方。**64 件成果中有 16 件留下了至少一項在團隊自辦活動之外被使用的證據。**HKSSC 的漫畫《The Tragedy of Margaret in Food Waste》被 ASIJ-Tokyo 翻成日文，並出了斯瓦希里文版。LYON 和 ASIJ-Tokyo 都把遊戲放進 iGEM Patras 的可下載遊戲庫。Marburg 把 CLiPPR 工具箱拿給三所學校的七位老師實測，並以德文與英文透過學校發行《Plasmid Panic》。BOKU-Vienna 把《Welche Sprache spricht das Leben?》捐給維也納 Pappenheimgasse 公共圖書館的外借館藏。Lambert-GA 的蜜蜂繪本進了 Atlanta Botanical Garden 的圖書室。Stanford 的 SynBase 顯示 750 位以上的註冊學習者。NIS Almaty-Medeu 具名寫出 Al-Farabi School No. 31 的老師 Daniyar 用他們的材料自行開了一場活動，並回報九所夥伴學校的老師已經在沒有他們的情況下帶活動。**是十六件，對上硬體的二十分之一。紙本走得遠。**","cards":[{"kicker":"The hypothesis failed","kicker_zh":"假設失敗","title":"284 of 285 education files download today","title_zh":"285 個教育檔案，今天有 284 個下載得到","body":"Every education-artefact URL linked from the 31 teams' wikis was fetched and its status recorded. The result is 284 responses of HTTP 200 and one 403 — ZQT-Nanjing's card-design sheet — and no 404 anywhere. The expected finding, that award-winning outreach exists only as photographs of children holding things, is not what the counting shows for files. iGEM's static asset host plus the wiki freeze has made education publishing effectively permanent at no cost to the team. The failures this analysis found are upstream of the link, not in it.","body_zh":"31 支隊伍 wiki 上連出去的每一個教育成果網址都被實際抓取並記錄狀態。結果是 284 個 HTTP 200、一個 403——ZQT-Nanjing 的卡牌圖檔——而且任何地方都沒有 404。原先預期的發現，也就是得獎的外展成果只剩下孩子拿著東西的照片，在檔案這一層並不成立。iGEM 的靜態資源主機加上 wiki 凍結，已經讓教育成果的發布在團隊零成本的情況下幾乎永久存在。這份分析找到的失敗，都發生在連結之前，而不在連結本身。","chips":["285 files tested","284 × HTTP 200","1 × 403","0 × 404"],"chips_zh":["測試 285 個檔案","284 個回 HTTP 200","1 個回 403","0 個 404"]},{"kicker":"Rendered, never exported","kicker_zh":"只算圖，沒匯出","title":"The Best Education winner publishes no downloadable file","title_zh":"最佳教育得主沒有公開任何可下載檔案","body":"XJTLU-China's education page counts 21 activities, 2,000+ people reached and \"18 educational toolkits\", and states the aim of enabling other educators to adopt and adapt the materials. Every link on that page is an .avif photograph, a citation or the Learning Mall hub. The hub itself loads for anyone with no login — and contains one video, one podcast episode and showcase pages for the Touch Life exhibition and the Game of Seagull board game. No rulebook, no print sheet, no lesson plan. The work may be excellent; a second educator cannot obtain it.","body_zh":"XJTLU-China 的教育頁面數出 21 場活動、觸及 2,000 人以上、以及「18 個教育工具包」，並寫明目標是讓其他教育工作者能採用並改編這些材料。那個頁面上的每一個連結，不是 .avif 照片、就是引用文獻、或是 Learning Mall 專頁。那個專頁本身任何人不用登入都打得開——裡面有一支影片、一集 podcast，以及《Touch Life》展覽和《Game of Seagull》桌遊的介紹頁。沒有規則書、沒有列印稿、沒有教案。成果可能真的很好；但第二位教育工作者拿不到它。","chips":["XJTLU-China","Best Education winner","18 toolkits claimed","0 files"],"chips_zh":["XJTLU-China","最佳教育得主","宣稱 18 套教材","0 個檔案"]},{"kicker":"Best in class","kicker_zh":"同類最佳","title":"HFI shipped 38 files and every lesson plan twice","title_zh":"HFI 交出 38 個檔案，每份教案都有兩個語言版本","body":"The High School Best Education winner publishes its whole teaching package as PDFs: slides, teaching plans and interactive cards, each in an English version and a Chinese version, alongside its microbiology comic. The comic's audiobook was recorded in three languages and then issued as plain text in twelve more — explicitly so that local educators can generate their own text-to-speech in languages the team does not speak. That is the most transferable design decision in the census. The Chinese is Simplified throughout, which is correct for Guangzhou and is not usable in a Taiwanese classroom without conversion.","body_zh":"高中組最佳教育得主把整套教學包以 PDF 形式公開：投影片、教案與互動卡，每一份都有英文版和中文版，另外還有那本微生物漫畫。漫畫的有聲書錄了三種語言，接著又以純文字形式釋出另外十二種——而且明確說明這是為了讓各地教育工作者能用團隊不會說的語言自行生成語音。這是整份普查中最容易被別人接手的一個設計決定。中文全部是簡體，這對廣州來說完全正確，但不經轉換就無法在台灣的教室使用。","chips":["HFI","38 PDFs","EN + ZH on every plan","12-language text","Simplified"],"chips_zh":["HFI","38 份 PDF","每份教案都有中英兩版","12 種語言的文本","簡體"]},{"kicker":"Nobody said you may use it","kicker_zh":"沒有人說你可以用","title":"One licence statement in 136 PDFs","title_zh":"136 份 PDF 裡只有一份授權聲明","body":"Cornell's Pass the Torch education guide opens with \"FREE TO COPY, ADAPT & PASS ON\" and ends with a CC BY 4.0 notice. It is the only education PDF in the census that grants permission on its own content. Two HKSSC comics cite CC BY, but for borrowed Wikimedia figures — attribution, not a licence. The wiki footer covers the files while they sit on the wiki, and says nothing once a file is downloaded and forwarded. A line of text costs nothing and is the difference between a teacher reprinting a workbook for a class and a teacher deciding not to risk it.","body_zh":"Cornell 的《Pass the Torch》教育指南開頭寫著「FREE TO COPY, ADAPT & PASS ON」，結尾附上 CC BY 4.0 聲明。它是整份普查中唯一一份對自身內容給出使用許可的教育 PDF。HKSSC 有兩本漫畫引用 CC BY，但那是為了借用的維基共享資源圖片——是出處標示，不是授權。wiki 頁尾在檔案還掛在 wiki 上時涵蓋了它們，一旦檔案被下載、被轉寄，頁尾就什麼也說不了。一行字不花任何成本，卻決定了一位老師會替全班重印一本作業本，還是決定不要冒這個險。","chips":["1 of 136","Cornell","CC BY 4.0","wiki footer only"],"chips_zh":["136 份 PDF 中只有 1 份","Cornell","CC BY 4.0","只寫在 wiki 頁尾"]},{"kicker":"The language gap","kicker_zh":"語言的斷層","title":"Two Traditional Chinese artefacts, both from Taiwan","title_zh":"兩件正體中文成果，兩件都來自台灣","body":"Across 31 decorated teams, education material in Traditional Chinese comes from three sources and all three already read it: NCKU-Tainan's 28-page handbook, GEMS-Taiwan's lesson plans and card games, and HKSSC's Hong Kong workshop sheets. Every other Chinese file checked — BNDS-China's 13 activity write-ups, HFI's 13 teaching documents, SJTU-BioX-Shanghai's 7 — is Simplified. Lambert-GA translated its children's book into thirteen languages and the Chinese edition is Simplified. Twenty-eight of 64 artefacts have some non-English version; the one script a Taiwanese classroom needs is the one almost nobody produced.","body_zh":"在 31 支得獎隊伍中，正體中文的教育材料來自三個來源，而這三個本來就看得懂正體中文：NCKU-Tainan 那本 28 頁的手冊、GEMS-Taiwan 的教案與卡牌遊戲，以及 HKSSC 的香港工作坊講義。其他每一份檢查過的中文檔案——BNDS-China 的 13 份活動紀錄、HFI 的 13 份教學文件、SJTU-BioX-Shanghai 的 7 份——都是簡體。Lambert-GA 把繪本翻成十三種語言，中文版是簡體。64 件成果中有 28 件存在英文以外的版本；而台灣教室需要的那一種字體，幾乎沒有人做。","chips":["3 of 31 teams","NCKU-Tainan","GEMS-Taiwan","HKSSC","rest Simplified"],"chips_zh":["31 支隊伍中有 3 支","NCKU-Tainan","GEMS-Taiwan","HKSSC","其餘都是簡體"]},{"kicker":"Copy this format","kicker_zh":"照抄這個形式","title":"Four browser games that cannot go dark","title_zh":"四款不會熄燈的瀏覽器遊戲","body":"LYON's BL21 is a wiki-hosted page loading a 7.3 MB script from static.igem.wiki: English and French, about fifteen minutes, keyboard only, nothing to install, and a second language switched with one key. GU Frankfurt's START, HongKong-JSS's Small Signal and GEMS-Taiwan's two plant-stress games work the same way. Because there is no service behind them, none can be suspended the way Vilnius-Lithuania's Ladder Detector was four weeks after the Jamboree. A game served from a frozen wiki is the most durable interactive artefact iGEM currently allows, and it costs nothing to keep.","body_zh":"LYON 的《BL21》是一個架在 wiki 上的頁面，從 static.igem.wiki 載入一支 7.3 MB 的腳本：英文與法文、約十五分鐘、只用鍵盤、什麼都不用安裝，按一個鍵就能切換語言。GU Frankfurt 的《START》、HongKong-JSS 的《Small Signal》，以及 GEMS-Taiwan 的兩款植物逆境遊戲，運作方式完全一樣。因為背後沒有服務，它們都不可能像 Vilnius-Lithuania 的 Ladder Detector 那樣，在 Jamboree 結束四週後被停用。架在凍結 wiki 上的遊戲，是 iGEM 目前允許的最耐久互動成果，而且維持它不花任何錢。","chips":["LYON BL21","GU Frankfurt START","HongKong-JSS","GEMS-Taiwan","no server to suspend"],"chips_zh":["LYON BL21","GU Frankfurt START","HongKong-JSS","GEMS-Taiwan","沒有伺服器可以關掉"]}],"table":{"head":["Team","Flagship education artefact","File you can get today","Licence in the file","Languages","Instructions for a second adult","Outside use"],"head_zh":["隊伍","代表性教育成果","今天拿得到的檔案","檔案內附授權","語言","給第二個大人的操作說明","外部使用"],"rows":[["XJTLU-China","18 education toolkits, Game of Seagull","none — Learning Mall hub is a showcase","no","English / Chinese page","no","none found"],["GU Frankfurt","Organs & Informed Decisions teacher pack","guide, slides, Myth-or-Fact cards","no","German + English","yes","hr3 radio, BIOspektrum, iGEM Lund podcast"],["HFI","Teaching package + microbiology comic","38 PDFs","no","English + Simplified Chinese; comic text × 12","yes","none recorded"],["CalPolySLO","CHEM 471 synthetic-cell course","10 lab manuals, instructor packet, workbook","stated CC BY 4.0 on page","English","yes","taught once; no second school yet"],["Cornell","Pass the Torch education guide","21-page PDF","yes — CC BY 4.0","English","yes","book swap + translations with NUGEM"],["Cornell","Plasmid Pals game","none","no","English","no","playtested only with its own guests"],["IIT Bombay","education programme","none — 638-byte page shell","no","—","no","none found"],["LYON","3 printable board games + facilitator guides","cards, boards, rules","no","French + English","yes","iGEM Patras game library"],["LYON","BL21 browser game","wiki-hosted, 7.3 MB","no","French + English","yes (in-game)","also on itch.io"],["Athens","Bee Wanderer game + bilingual comic","comic PDFs; game on GitHub Pages","no","English + Greek","partly","EU-CONEXUS Hackathon"],["BOKU-Vienna","Welche Sprache spricht das Leben? book","4.0 MB PDF","no","German","no","donated to a public library's lending collection"],["BOKU-Vienna","Open Educational Resources pack","22-page PDF","no","German","yes","eduvidual.at, Austrian ministry platform"],["Marburg","CLiPPR Teaching Toolbox","PDF, both languages","no","German + English","yes","tested with 7 teachers at 3 schools"],["Marburg","Plasmid Panic escape game","PDF, both languages","no","German + English","yes","schools + iGEM Patras"],["UOregon","Three-workshop curriculum","3 slide decks + 2 workbooks","no","English","yes","3 host organisations"],["ASIJ-Tokyo","Seven tested lesson plans","workbook PDF","no","English","yes","feedback page for adopters"],["ASIJ-Tokyo","Village 茶(Sa)kura Unity game","itch.io + manual PDF","no","English","yes","iGEM Patras game gallery"],["BNDS-China","Bilingual comic + REACH activity set","21 PDFs","no","Simplified Chinese + English","partly","school newspaper BNDS Review"],["Eton-College-UK","58-page Activities Handbook","7.8 MB PDF","no","English","yes","350+ printed copies of the comic"],["Eton-College-UK","Bio-Detectives workshop","facilitator + student packs","no","English","yes","rerunnable by non-authors"],["HKSSC","The Tragedy of Margaret comic","PDF, several editions","no","English + Swahili + Japanese (by ASIJ)","partly","translated by 2 other teams"],["UPF-Barcelona","Ten WONDER session kits","10 PDFs + Operation Priorat cards","no","English + Catalan","yes","published so others can run them"],["Lambert-GA","Bentley the Bee children's book","PDF × 13 languages","no","13, Chinese is Simplified","no","Atlanta Botanical Garden library"],["Muenster-University","Design Your Crop card game","none","no","German","no","named playtester only"],["GEMS-Taiwan","Lesson plans, slides, 2 card games","8 PDFs + 2 browser games","no","Traditional Chinese","yes","5 schools, 140 students"],["NCKU-Tainan","與偏鄉共學 education handbook","28-page PDF, EN + ZH-Hant","no","Traditional Chinese + English","yes","8 Tainan primary schools"],["Stanford University","SynBase self-paced curriculum","live web app","no","English","yes","750+ registered learners"],["HongKong-JSS","Small Signal browser game","wiki-hosted HTML","no","English","yes","30 teachers trained + equipment loan"],["KAUST-KSA","Space Microbe activity cards","PDF, both languages","no","English + Arabic","yes","Tawasol MENA network"],["UAlberta","Inclusivity in Research Course","slides as PDF; course needs a Google account","no","English","yes","9 kits shipped to rural teachers"],["ZQT-Nanjing","Synthetic Biology Lab card game","rulebook yes; card sheet 403","no","English","yes","none found"],["SJTU-BioX-Shanghai","145-page Education Handbook","9.9 MB PDF","no","English (other files Simplified)","yes","none recorded"],["NIS Almaty-Medeu","Keleshek school materials","Drive folder, opens signed-out","no","English + Kazakh","yes","9 schools now deliver without them"],["IISER-Kolkata","41 free teaching files, 3 languages","page did not render in testing","no","English, Hindi, Bengali","unknown","Ek Pehal partnership"]],"rows_zh":[["XJTLU-China","18 個教育工具包、Game of Seagull","無——Learning Mall 專頁只是展示","無","英文／中文頁面","無","查無"],["GU Frankfurt","器官與知情決定教師包","指南、投影片、Myth-or-Fact 卡牌","無","德文＋英文","有","hr3 廣播、BIOspektrum、iGEM Lund podcast"],["HFI","教學包＋微生物漫畫","38 份 PDF","無","英文＋簡體中文；漫畫文字 12 語","有","未記錄"],["CalPolySLO","CHEM 471 合成細胞課程","10 份實驗手冊、授課包、工作表","頁面載明 CC BY 4.0","英文","有","已開課一次；尚無第二所學校"],["Cornell","Pass the Torch 教育指南","21 頁 PDF","有——CC BY 4.0","英文","有","與 NUGEM 互換繪本並互譯"],["Cornell","Plasmid Pals 遊戲","無","無","英文","無","僅與自家受邀對象試玩"],["IIT Bombay","教育計畫","無——638 位元組的空殼頁面","無","——","無","查無"],["LYON","三款可列印桌遊＋帶領者指南","卡片、遊戲板、規則","無","法文＋英文","有","iGEM Patras 遊戲庫"],["LYON","BL21 瀏覽器遊戲","架在 wiki 上，7.3 MB","無","法文＋英文","有（遊戲內）","itch.io 亦有"],["Athens","Bee Wanderer 遊戲＋雙語漫畫","漫畫 PDF；遊戲在 GitHub Pages","無","英文＋希臘文","部分","EU-CONEXUS Hackathon"],["BOKU-Vienna","Welche Sprache spricht das Leben? 繪本","4.0 MB PDF","無","德文","無","捐入公共圖書館外借館藏"],["BOKU-Vienna","開放教育資源包","22 頁 PDF","無","德文","有","eduvidual.at，奧地利教育部平台"],["Marburg","CLiPPR 教學工具箱","PDF，兩種語言","無","德文＋英文","有","三所學校七位老師實測"],["Marburg","Plasmid Panic 密室遊戲","PDF，兩種語言","無","德文＋英文","有","學校＋iGEM Patras"],["UOregon","三場工作坊課程","3 份投影片＋2 份作業本","無","英文","有","三個合辦單位"],["ASIJ-Tokyo","七份實測教案","作業本 PDF","無","英文","有","附給採用者的回饋頁"],["ASIJ-Tokyo","Village 茶(Sa)kura Unity 遊戲","itch.io＋說明書 PDF","無","英文","有","iGEM Patras 遊戲展示區"],["BNDS-China","雙語漫畫＋REACH 活動集","21 份 PDF","無","簡體中文＋英文","部分","校刊 BNDS Review"],["Eton-College-UK","58 頁活動手冊","7.8 MB PDF","無","英文","有","漫畫印行 350 份以上"],["Eton-College-UK","Bio-Detectives 工作坊","帶領者包＋學生包","無","英文","有","非原作者也能重跑"],["HKSSC","The Tragedy of Margaret 漫畫","PDF，多種版本","無","英文＋斯瓦希里文＋日文（ASIJ 譯）","部分","另外兩支隊伍翻譯"],["UPF-Barcelona","十份 WONDER 活動包","10 份 PDF＋Operation Priorat 卡牌","無","英文＋加泰隆尼亞文","有","公開讓別人照著辦"],["Lambert-GA","Bentley the Bee 繪本","PDF，13 種語言","無","13 種，中文為簡體","無","Atlanta Botanical Garden 圖書室"],["Muenster-University","Design Your Crop 卡牌遊戲","無","無","德文","無","僅具名試玩者"],["GEMS-Taiwan","教案、投影片、兩款卡牌遊戲","8 份 PDF＋2 款瀏覽器遊戲","無","正體中文","有","5 所學校、140 位學生"],["NCKU-Tainan","《與偏鄉共學》教育手冊","28 頁 PDF，英文與正體中文","無","正體中文＋英文","有","台南 8 所國小"],["Stanford University","SynBase 自學課程","線上網頁應用","無","英文","有","750 位以上註冊學習者"],["HongKong-JSS","Small Signal 瀏覽器遊戲","架在 wiki 上的 HTML","無","英文","有","培訓 30 位教師＋器材借用"],["KAUST-KSA","太空微生物活動卡","PDF，兩種語言","無","英文＋阿拉伯文","有","Tawasol 中東北非網絡"],["UAlberta","Inclusivity in Research 課程","投影片 PDF；課程需 Google 帳號","無","英文","有","寄出 9 套教具給偏遠地區教師"],["ZQT-Nanjing","Synthetic Biology Lab 卡牌遊戲","規則書可下載；卡牌圖檔 403","無","英文","有","查無"],["SJTU-BioX-Shanghai","145 頁教育手冊","9.9 MB PDF","無","英文（其餘檔案為簡體）","有","未記錄"],["NIS Almaty-Medeu","Keleshek 校園材料","雲端硬碟資料夾，未登入可開","無","英文＋哈薩克文","有","9 所學校已能自行帶活動"],["IISER-Kolkata","41 份免費教學檔案，三種語言","測試時頁面無法算繪","無","英文、印地文、孟加拉文","不明","與 Ek Pehal 的長期合作"]]},"checklist":["Put a licence line inside every education file, not only in the wiki footer. One PDF in 136 does this. Add \"Free to copy, adapt and reuse — CC BY 4.0\" to the cover of each ReLEAF lesson plan and card game, so the file still says it after a teacher forwards it.","Publish a Traditional Chinese and an English version of every artefact, and say which is which in the filename. Three teams in thirty-one published Traditional Chinese at all, and GEMS was one of them — that is a position to build on, not a box already ticked.","Offer Traditional Chinese translation to other teams as a formal collaboration, the way ASIJ-Tokyo translated HKSSC's comic into Japanese. Lambert-GA's children's book reached thirteen languages without reaching Taiwan; a team willing to supply the thirteenth-and-a-half script will be taken up.","Write the facilitator layer as a separate document from the student layer, as Eton-College-UK did for Bio-Detectives. Thirty-three of the sixty-four artefacts ship one; it is the single thing that decides whether a stranger can run the session.","Ship card games as print-ready sheets, with bleed, card size, paper weight and a page count, and then download them yourself from a signed-out browser. ZQT-Nanjing published the rulebook and the card artwork returns 403.","Host every interactive piece on the wiki itself, not on a platform. LYON's BL21, GU Frankfurt's START and HongKong-JSS's Small Signal are a single HTML page plus a script on static.igem.wiki and cannot be switched off.","Never put a teaching file behind Google Drive, Google Classroom or a university SharePoint without opening it in a private window first. Cornell's Drive folder sends a signed-out visitor to a Google login page.","Record the running cost and the running time on the first page of each lesson plan — what to buy, how long it takes, class size, what goes wrong — the way CalPolySLO's instructor packet lists prep, reagent costs, timings and common failure points.","Give one artefact to one school that GEMS has never visited, and publish what they did with it. Sixteen of sixty-four artefacts have outside-use evidence; it is the one column where education beats hardware's one-in-twenty, and it only exists because someone asked.","Re-fetch every education link a month after the Jamboree and publish the date you checked. The counting here found exactly one dead file in 285, which is a result worth defending rather than assuming."],"checklist_zh":["在每一個教育檔案裡面放上一行授權，而不是只靠 wiki 頁尾。136 份 PDF 裡只有一份做到。在每一份 ReLEAF 教案和卡牌遊戲的封面加上「可自由重製、改作與再利用——CC BY 4.0」，讓老師轉寄之後，檔案本身還說得出話。","每一件成果都同時出正體中文版和英文版，並在檔名上標明是哪一個。三十一支隊伍中只有三支公開過正體中文，GEMS 是其中之一——這是可以往上疊的位置，不是已經打勾的項目。","把正體中文翻譯當成一項正式的合作提供給其他隊伍，就像 ASIJ-Tokyo 把 HKSSC 的漫畫翻成日文那樣。Lambert-GA 的繪本翻了十三種語言卻沒有到台灣；願意補上第十三點五種字體的隊伍，一定會有人接。","把帶領者那一層寫成與學生那一層分開的文件，就像 Eton-College-UK 的 Bio-Detectives。六十四件成果中有三十三件附上這一層；它是決定陌生人能不能把這堂課跑起來的唯一關鍵。","卡牌遊戲要以可直接付印的版型釋出，附出血、卡片尺寸、紙磅與頁數，然後自己用未登入的瀏覽器下載一次。ZQT-Nanjing 公開了規則書，卡牌圖檔卻回傳 403。","每一件互動成果都架在 wiki 本身，不要架在平台上。LYON 的 BL21、GU Frankfurt 的 START 和 HongKong-JSS 的 Small Signal，都只是一頁 HTML 加上一支放在 static.igem.wiki 的腳本，沒有人關得掉。","絕不要把教學檔案放在 Google 雲端硬碟、Google Classroom 或大學的 SharePoint 後面，除非先用無痕視窗打開確認過。Cornell 的雲端硬碟資料夾會把未登入的訪客導去 Google 登入頁。","在每份教案第一頁寫明花費與時間——要買什麼、要花多久、班級人數多少、哪裡容易出錯——就像 CalPolySLO 的授課包列出備料、試劑成本、時程與常見失敗點那樣。","挑一件成果，交給一所 GEMS 從來沒去過的學校，並把他們怎麼用它寫出來。六十四件成果中有十六件留下外部使用的證據；這是教育唯一勝過硬體二十分之一的那一欄，而它之所以存在，只因為有人開口問了。","Jamboree 結束一個月後，把每一個教育連結重抓一次，並寫上檢查日期。這次的清點在 285 個檔案中只找到一個失效，這是一個值得守住的成績，而不是可以理所當然的事。"],"method":"The sample is 31 decorated teams and 64 named education artefacts. It is built from two lists. First, every 2026 Best Education winner and nominee as recorded in results2026.json — XJTLU-China, GU Frankfurt and HFI as winners, plus CalPolySLO, Cornell, IIT Bombay, LYON, Athens, BOKU-Vienna, Marburg, UOregon, ASIJ-Tokyo, BNDS-China, Eton-College-UK and HKSSC as nominees across the three sections; fifteen teams. Second, sixteen further decorated teams whose team file names a specific, titled education artefact: UPF-Barcelona, Lambert-GA, Muenster-University, GEMS-Taiwan, Stanford University, HongKong-JSS, UCAS-China, UAlberta, KAUST-KSA, NIS Almaty-Medeu, HongKong-HS, NCKU-Tainan, ZQT-Nanjing, Oxford, SJTU-BioX-Shanghai and IISER-Kolkata. An artefact was counted once no matter how many language editions it has, so HFI's twelve-language comic text and Lambert-GA's thirteen translations are one artefact each. Server-rendered wikis were read with curl; client-rendered React and Vue wikis were read either from their JavaScript bundles or in a browser, and the browser mattered — XJTLU-China's Learning Mall hub renders entirely inside a blob-URL iframe that curl cannot see, and its contents had to be read from inside that frame before the showcase-not-library finding could be made. Every education file URL found this way was then fetched with an HTTP HEAD request and its status code and content length recorded: 285 files, 284 responses of 200, one 403, no 404s. Google Drive, Google Docs, Google Classroom and SharePoint links were opened signed-out in a browser to see what an outsider actually gets; Cornell's Drive folder redirects to a Google login page, while CalPolySLO's Drive files, instructor-packet spreadsheet and SharePoint deck all open. 136 PDFs were downloaded and their text layers searched for licence and reuse statements, and the Chinese-language files were classified as Traditional or Simplified by counting script-specific characters. What the counting cannot see. A link that works today says nothing about next year; the hardware study found a repository that was named on a wiki and had already 404ed, and nothing here guarantees these 284 files will still be served in 2028. A file downloading is not a file being good: this analysis did not read most of these PDFs for pedagogical quality, and several of the artefacts it marks as unobtainable may be the best teaching work in the competition — XJTLU-China won Best Education on the strength of a framework and twenty-one activities that were genuinely evaluated, and the criticism here is about distribution, not about the teaching. Comics published as image-only PDFs, including BNDS-China's, have no text layer, so their Chinese script could not be classified and their language is reported as the team describes it. IISER-Kolkata's wiki returned an empty document body in the browser pane on three attempts across three routes with its own bundle loading at 200, so its 41 teaching files could not be reached; that may be a failure specific to this browser rather than the site. eduvidual.at, where BOKU-Vienna deposited its Open Educational Resources, resolved but did not respond from this network on two attempts, and the wiki links only the platform homepage rather than the course page — so the deposit is reported as existing and the route to it as unverified. Finally, absence of outside-use evidence is not evidence of absence: sixteen artefacts have a recorded second user, and the other forty-eight may well have quiet ones. The table lists 34 of the 64 artefacts across 28 of the 31 teams, chosen because each one settles a question; UCAS-China, HongKong-HS and Oxford are counted in the totals and left out of the table for space. The sample is decorated teams only. Nothing here describes iGEM 2026 at large.","method_zh":"樣本為 31 支得獎隊伍、64 件具名教育成果，由兩份名單組成。第一份是 results2026.json 記載的 2026 年最佳教育得主與入圍者——得主為 XJTLU-China、GU Frankfurt 與 HFI，入圍者包括三個組別的 CalPolySLO、Cornell、IIT Bombay、LYON、Athens、BOKU-Vienna、Marburg、UOregon、ASIJ-Tokyo、BNDS-China、Eton-College-UK 與 HKSSC，共十五支。第二份是另外十六支得獎隊伍，其隊伍檔案中寫出了具體且有名稱的教育成果：UPF-Barcelona、Lambert-GA、Muenster-University、GEMS-Taiwan、Stanford University、HongKong-JSS、UCAS-China、UAlberta、KAUST-KSA、NIS Almaty-Medeu、HongKong-HS、NCKU-Tainan、ZQT-Nanjing、Oxford、SJTU-BioX-Shanghai 與 IISER-Kolkata。一件成果不論有幾種語言版本都只計一次，所以 HFI 十二種語言的漫畫文字與 Lambert-GA 的十三種翻譯，各算一件。伺服器端渲染的 wiki 以 curl 讀取；客戶端渲染的 React 與 Vue wiki 則從 JavaScript 套件檔或直接在瀏覽器中讀取，而瀏覽器確實關鍵——XJTLU-China 的 Learning Mall 專頁整個算繪在一個 blob 網址的內嵌框架裡，curl 看不到，必須從那個框架內部讀取內容，才能做出「是展示櫥窗不是資料庫」這個判斷。接著，以此找出的每一個教育檔案網址都用 HTTP HEAD 請求抓取，並記錄狀態碼與內容長度：285 個檔案、284 個回傳 200、一個 403、沒有 404。Google 雲端硬碟、Google 文件、Google Classroom 與 SharePoint 的連結，都以未登入狀態在瀏覽器中開啟，確認外人實際看到什麼；Cornell 的雲端硬碟資料夾會導向 Google 登入頁，而 CalPolySLO 的雲端硬碟檔案、授課包試算表與 SharePoint 投影片則全部打得開。另下載 136 份 PDF，在文字層中搜尋授權與重製使用的敘述，並以字體特有字元的出現次數，將中文檔案分類為正體或簡體。這次清點看不到的事。今天通得過的連結，說明不了明年的狀況；硬體那篇就找到一個 wiki 上寫明、卻早已 404 的儲存庫，這裡也沒有任何東西保證這 284 個檔案到 2028 年還供得出來。檔案下載得到，不代表檔案做得好：本分析並未逐一閱讀這些 PDF 評估教學品質，而被標為拿不到的那幾件，很可能正是整場競賽裡最好的教學成果——XJTLU-China 拿下最佳教育，靠的是一套架構和二十一場確實做過評估的活動，這裡批評的是發布方式，不是教學本身。以純影像 PDF 形式發布的漫畫（包括 BNDS-China 的）沒有文字層，無法判定其中文字體，語言欄位依隊伍自述記錄。IISER-Kolkata 的 wiki 在瀏覽器面板中，跨三條路徑、三次嘗試都回傳空白的文件主體，而它自己的套件檔是 200，因此其 41 份教學檔案無法取得；這有可能是這個瀏覽器特有的失敗，而不是網站本身的問題。BOKU-Vienna 存放開放教育資源的 eduvidual.at，網域解析得出但從本網路兩次嘗試都沒有回應，而 wiki 只連到平台首頁、沒有連到課程頁——因此該存放紀錄記為存在，但抵達它的路徑記為未經驗證。最後，沒有外部使用的證據，不等於沒有外部使用：十六件成果有明確的第二位使用者，其餘四十八件也可能有默默在用的人。表格列出 64 件成果中的 34 件、涵蓋 31 支隊伍中的 28 支，收錄標準是每一列都能回答一個問題；UCAS-China、HongKong-HS 與 Oxford 計入總數，但因版面關係未列入表格。樣本僅限得獎隊伍。本文任何內容都不描述 2026 年 iGEM 的整體情況。","baseRate":{"teams":31,"artefacts":64,"obtainable":55,"noFileAtAll":9,"filesTested":285,"http200":284,"http403":1,"http404":0,"pdfsWithLicence":1,"pdfsInspected":136,"withNonEnglishVersion":28,"withTraditionalChinese":3,"withFacilitatorInstructions":33,"withOutsideUseEvidence":16}},{"id":"protocol-reproducibility","tab":"drylab","order":44,"kicker":"Original analysis","kicker_zh":"原創分析","title":"Could a stranger repeat the experiment?","title_zh":"換一個人，這些實驗做得出來嗎？","lede":"The hypothesis failed. Where the hardware study found 9 of 20 award-winning instruments with no geometry file at all, all 30 of the 2026 Top 10 teams publish a wet-lab protocol a stranger could follow — volumes, temperatures, named kits. What they withhold is the evidence: 4 of 30 let a reader reach the numbers behind a results figure, and 13 of 30 publish a plasmid map or a sequence.","lede_zh":"假設不成立。硬體那份研究發現 20 台得獎儀器中有 9 台完全沒有釋出幾何檔案；但 2026 年三個組別的 30 支 Top 10 隊伍，每一支都公開了陌生人照著就能做的濕實驗流程——體積、溫度、具名的試劑套組都寫了。他們扣住不放的是證據：30 支裡只有 4 支讓讀者拿得到結果圖背後的數字，13 支公開質體圖譜或序列。","body":"**Thirty of thirty.** Every Top 10 team in 2026 — Undergrad, Overgrad and High School — publishes step-level procedures with reagent volumes, incubation temperatures and at least one named kit or supplier. The delivery varies more than the content: TU Delft ships a numbered library from P0.1 Media and buffers to P10.1 Golden Gate assembly; UCAS-China publishes 20 numbered PDF sheets; NUS-Singapore and Muenster-University hide theirs inside fold-out panels that only open in a browser (a plain fetch of either page returns an empty shell); GCGS writes catalogue numbers into its reagent list — *Vazyme ClonExpress II One Step Cloning Kit, Cat. No. C112*. This is the floor hardware never had. **Nothing in iGEM makes a team press Export on a CAD file, but every wet-lab team has been taught to write a protocol.**\n\n**The ceiling is the data.** Four teams in thirty let a reader reach the numbers behind a published experimental figure: Lambert-GA, whose GitLab carries `UAB Test Files/` and `GT Test Files/` with the two outside laboratories' test workbooks; GEMS-Taiwan, whose digital-twin repository holds the 434-hour OD600 run and its calibration tables as CSV; HongKong-JSS, whose 124-page wet-lab log prints the readings as they were taken; and HongKong-HS, which types its replicate tables straight into the Results page (*n, -ve C, +ve C, 21_7a-, 21_7a+ … 71.6, 2694, 98.7*). Nine further teams publish data files that turn out to be literature sets, docking scores, simulation batches, cost models or, in one case, an outreach pub-quiz scoreboard. Everyone else gives you a chart.\n\n**Several links fail the moment you check them rather than read them.** Toronto states that its datasets are deposited on Zenodo and prints the DOI for a 23.8 GB PETadex corpus; `doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23457986` answers **DOI Not Found**, and the chronological lab notes beside it are a Google Doc that returns 401 to a signed-out reader — the same team whose bioreactor CAD sat in a sign-in-walled Drive folder in the hardware census. UZurich's and ETH-Zurich's Benchling libraries, the only route either gives to a construct sequence, land on Benchling's sign-in page. Two further sign-in walls sit on supporting material rather than data — Cornell's children's-book folder and Stanford's judges' scorecards — and they are worth a line only because Stanford's other Drive folder, its education slides, opens for anyone: the wall is a setting somebody did not change, not a decision. Princeton shows what the working version looks like, with 23 `benchling.com/s/seq-…` share links that open for anyone, titled construct by construct.\n\n**Sequences are where the cohort is thinnest.** 13 of 30 publish plasmid maps or sequences for the constructs they built; the other 17 publish a parts list and a Registry link. TU Delft is alone in shipping the files themselves — 49 GenBank `.gb` exports, served from the wiki and committed to its repository, each opening with `LOCUS BBa_26S9CPUO 3822 bp DNA linear SYN 15-OCT-2026`. The Registry itself is the one thing nobody fails: of 210 sampled 2026 accessions across all 30 teams, 208 return `published` with a non-empty sequence from the parts API, and the two that 404 are accessions mistyped on the wiki that prints them — Athens's BBa_26ROIV80 beside its working BBa_26R0IV80, UOttawa's BBa_26GSB34 beside its working BBa_26GSJB34. The deposit is mandatory, so it happens; the map on the wiki is optional, so it mostly does not.\n\n**The distribution, not the average.** One team of thirty scores 6 of 6, ten score 5, fifteen score 4 and four score 3; no team scores below 3, and nothing in this cohort resembles the nine hardware teams that published no file at all. The shape of the failure is the same everywhere: the point almost everyone drops is data, and the point most often dropped after that is the map. Five of the ten High School teams score 5 or better, and so do five of the ten Overgrad teams; one of the ten Undergrad teams does. The only 6 is Lambert-GA — the same high-school team that was the one case in the hardware census of a device an outside laboratory had actually used. The four at 3 are UOttawa, GU Frankfurt, Marburg and Muenster-University: all four publish protocols and parts, and none publishes a map, a number or a dated notebook.","body_zh":"**三十支，全部都有。** 2026 年三個組別的 Top 10 隊伍，每一支都寫出了逐步的操作說明：試劑體積、培養溫度，以及至少一個具名的套組或供應商。差別在於交付方式而不是內容：TU Delft 把流程編成一整套，從 P0.1 培養基與緩衝液到 P10.1 Golden Gate 組裝；UCAS-China 放了 20 份編號 PDF；NUS-Singapore 與 Muenster-University 把流程收在摺疊區塊裡，只有在瀏覽器裡才展得開（直接抓取頁面只會拿到空殼）；GCGS 更把試劑型號寫進材料表裡——*Vazyme ClonExpress II One Step Cloning Kit，Cat. No. C112*。這是硬體從來沒有的底線。**iGEM 從來不會要求一支隊伍把 CAD 檔匯出，但每一支濕實驗隊伍都被教過要寫實驗流程。**\n\n**天花板在數據。** 三十支裡只有四支，讓讀者拿得到已發表實驗圖背後的數字：Lambert-GA 的 GitLab 裡有 `UAB Test Files/` 與 `GT Test Files/`，放著兩間外部實驗室的測試原始檔；GEMS-Taiwan 的數位孿生倉庫收了 434 小時 OD600 連續量測與校正表，格式是 CSV；HongKong-JSS 的 124 頁濕實驗日誌把當下讀到的數字直接寫進去；HongKong-HS 則把逐重複值的表格整個打在 Results 頁上（*n、-ve C、+ve C、21_7a-、21_7a+⋯71.6、2694、98.7*）。另有九支隊伍確實放了資料檔，但打開來是文獻整理、對接分數、模擬批次、成本模型，其中一份是科普問答的計分表。其餘的隊伍，給你的就是一張圖。\n\n**有幾個連結，是你去點它、而不是去讀它的時候才垮掉的。** Toronto 寫明資料集已存放在 Zenodo，並列出 23.8 GB PETadex 語料庫的 DOI；`doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23457986` 回應的是 **DOI Not Found**，旁邊那份依時間排序的實驗日誌則是一份 Google 文件，未登入時回 401——而在硬體普查裡，正是同一支隊伍把生物反應器的 CAD 放在需要登入的 Drive 資料夾。UZurich 與 ETH-Zurich 的 Benchling 序列庫是這兩支隊伍唯一給出構築序列的途徑，但點開來是 Benchling 的登入頁。另有兩道登入牆擋的是輔助材料而不是數據——Cornell 的童書資料夾與 Stanford 的評審計分表——之所以值得寫一句，是因為 Stanford 另一個 Drive 資料夾（教育活動的簡報）任何人都打得開：那道牆是沒人去改的設定，不是決定。Princeton 則示範了行得通的樣子：23 條 `benchling.com/s/seq-…` 分享連結任何人都打得開，而且逐一標明是哪個構築。\n\n**序列是這一批隊伍最薄的一環。** 30 支中有 13 支為自己做出來的構築公開質體圖譜或序列，其餘 17 支給的是零件清單加 Registry 連結。真的把檔案本身釋出的只有 TU Delft——49 個 GenBank `.gb` 匯出檔，既掛在 wiki 上也進了倉庫，開頭寫著 `LOCUS BBa_26S9CPUO 3822 bp DNA linear SYN 15-OCT-2026`。反而 Registry 這一關沒有人失手：30 支隊伍共抽查 210 個 2026 年編號，透過 parts API 查詢有 208 個是 `published` 且序列非空；另外兩個回 404 的，是印在 wiki 上就打錯的編號——Athens 的 BBa_26ROIV80 旁邊就是能用的 BBa_26R0IV80，UOttawa 的 BBa_26GSB34 旁邊就是能用的 BBa_26GSJB34。存放是強制的，所以做得到；wiki 上的圖譜是自由心證，所以大多沒有。\n\n**要看分布，不是平均。** 三十支裡有 1 支拿 6 分、10 支 5 分、15 支 4 分、4 支 3 分；沒有任何一支低於 3 分，也沒有任何一支像硬體那九支隊伍那樣完全沒有釋出檔案。失分的位置到處都一樣：幾乎所有人掉的那一分是數據，其次最常掉的是圖譜。十支高中隊中有五支拿到 5 分以上，研究生組十支中也有五支；大學部十支裡只有一支。唯一的 6 分是 Lambert-GA——也正是硬體普查裡，唯一有外部實驗室真的用過其裝置的那支高中隊。拿 3 分的四支是 UOttawa、GU Frankfurt、Marburg 與 Muenster-University：四支都公開了流程與零件，四支都沒有圖譜、沒有數字、沒有附日期的實驗記錄。","cards":[{"kicker":"The only six","kicker_zh":"唯一的滿分","title":"Lambert-GA clears all six checks","title_zh":"Lambert-GA 六項全過","body":"A high-school team is the only one of the thirty to pass every check. Protocols are written into the two lab notebooks (23 and 25 pages, dated 08/18/2026 onward, with buffer recipes in the entries themselves); the chassis is named (NEB 5-alpha for propagation, T7 Express for expression); pET-11a and pET-28a(+) maps sit beside codon-optimised sequences; 37 parts are deposited with sequence; the notebooks are dated day by day. The sixth is the rare one: the raw workbooks from the two outside laboratories that tested Vapor-X are committed to its GitLab as `UAB Test Files/Vapor_X_evaporator_test_101426.xlsm` and `GT Test Files/102026_igem-gfp_plate_reader_raw_data.xlsm`.","body_zh":"三十支裡唯一六項全過的是一支高中隊。實驗流程寫在兩本實驗記錄裡（23 頁與 25 頁，日期自 08/18/2026 起算，緩衝液配方直接寫在條目中）；菌株有名有姓（繁殖用 NEB 5-alpha，表現用 T7 Express）；pET-11a 與 pET-28a(+) 的圖譜旁邊就是密碼子最佳化後的序列；37 個零件都附序列存入 Registry；記錄逐日標註日期。第六項才是稀有的：兩間外部實驗室測試 Vapor-X 的原始檔，直接進了他們的 GitLab，檔名是 `UAB Test Files/Vapor_X_evaporator_test_101426.xlsm` 與 `GT Test Files/102026_igem-gfp_plate_reader_raw_data.xlsm`。","chips":["6/6","High School","2 outside labs","raw .xlsm published"],"chips_zh":["6/6","高中組","兩間外部實驗室","公開原始 .xlsm"]},{"kicker":"Checked, not read","kicker_zh":"點開才知道","title":"One team's dataset DOI does not exist; two teams' sequence libraries ask you to sign in","title_zh":"一支隊伍的資料集 DOI 根本不存在，兩支隊伍的序列庫要你登入","body":"Toronto's wiki names a Zenodo deposit for its 23.8 GB PETadex corpus; the DOI resolves to \"DOI Not Found\". Its chronological lab notes are a Google Doc that answers 401 signed out. UZurich and ETH-Zurich link Benchling libraries that show Benchling's sign-in page, and those links are the only route either team offers to a construct sequence. Neither case is a missing file — each is a file the team has and the reader cannot open, which from outside is the same thing. Princeton's 23 public Benchling share links, and TU Delft's 49 `.gb` files served straight off the wiki, are what the working version looks like. The habit worth copying is cheap: fetch your own links signed out, once, before the freeze.","body_zh":"Toronto 的 wiki 指明 23.8 GB 的 PETadex 語料庫已存入 Zenodo；但那個 DOI 解析出來是「DOI Not Found」。旁邊依時間排序的實驗日誌是一份 Google 文件，未登入回 401。UZurich 與 ETH-Zurich 連到的 Benchling 序列庫打開是 Benchling 的登入頁，而這些連結是兩支隊伍唯一給出構築序列的途徑。這兩種情況都不是檔案不存在——而是隊伍手上有、讀者卻打不開；從外面看，這兩件事沒有差別。Princeton 那 23 條公開的 Benchling 分享連結，以及 TU Delft 直接掛在 wiki 上的 49 個 `.gb` 檔，才是行得通的樣子。值得照抄的習慣其實很省事：在凍結之前，用未登入的狀態把自己的連結抓一次。","chips":["DOI 404","Google Doc 401","2 Benchling sign-ins","Princeton's links open"],"chips_zh":["DOI 404","Google 文件 401","2 個 Benchling 要登入","Princeton 的連結打得開"]},{"kicker":"The one file nobody else shipped","kicker_zh":"別人都沒釋出的那種檔案","title":"TU Delft published the plasmids, not a picture of them","title_zh":"TU Delft 釋出的是質體本身，不是質體的照片","body":"Forty-nine GenBank files — `bba-26s9cpuo.gb`, `k30-elp.gb`, `cm-pseva-gln-mety-metx.gb` and the rest — are served from the wiki's own asset path and committed under `src/contents/sequences/` in its repository, so a second team can open them in any sequence editor and re-order the DNA. Thirteen of thirty teams give you maps or sequences in some form; one gives you files. The remaining seventeen hand you a parts list and a Registry link, which is enough to read a part and not enough to rebuild a construct whose junctions, backbone and tags you cannot see.","body_zh":"49 個 GenBank 檔——`bba-26s9cpuo.gb`、`k30-elp.gb`、`cm-pseva-gln-mety-metx.gb` 等等——既由 wiki 自己的檔案路徑提供，也收在倉庫的 `src/contents/sequences/` 底下；另一支隊伍可以用任何序列編輯軟體打開，直接重新下單。30 支裡有 13 支以某種形式給了圖譜或序列，只有一支給的是檔案。其餘 17 支給你的是零件清單加 Registry 連結：足以讀懂一個零件，卻不足以重建一個你看不到接點、骨架與標籤的構築。","chips":["49 .gb files","13 of 30 show maps","17 give a parts list"],"chips_zh":["49 個 .gb 檔","30 支中 13 支有圖譜","17 支只給零件清單"]},{"kicker":"Assessed on the same terms","kicker_zh":"同一把尺","title":"GEMS-Taiwan scores five of six, and the sixth is softer than it looks","title_zh":"GEMS-Taiwan 六項過五項，而過的那一項比看起來鬆","body":"GEMS-Taiwan passes protocols (24 of its 25 sheets download as PDFs, with colony PCR given as a reaction table to 20 µL and transformation at 42 °C for 45 s), chassis (B. subtilis WB800 and 168, E. coli DH5-alpha), Registry deposit (every sampled 2026 accession comes back published, with sequence) and notebook (monthly PDFs, entries headed `Date: 20260801`). It fails maps and sequences: one plasmid map on the whole wiki, for pSTK-EXP1, against 35 deposited parts. And its data pass rests entirely on the instrument. The photometer and bioreactor runs are published as CSV in the digital-twin repository, but five figures on the hardware-bioreactor page are captioned \"redrawn from the team's chart\" — the ELISA, the DNPH activity assay, prototype 4's OD600 and pH, the pressure traces and the shell-permeate panel — so what the reader sees is a re-rendering of a chart image, not a plot of a published dataset. On the hardware-photometer page the two bacterial-growth charts are the same story and the wiki says so in its own source: `static/hardware/photometer/js/growth-data.js` holds `growth_c1` and `growth_c2` with `csv: null` under the heading \"THE ONE PLACE THE RAW DATA GOES\" and the note \"The owner, 15 Oct: 'ill give data later'\".","body_zh":"GEMS-Taiwan 在實驗流程（25 份條目中 24 份可下載 PDF，菌落 PCR 給到 20 µL 的反應配方、轉型 42 °C 45 秒）、菌株（B. subtilis WB800 與 168、E. coli DH5-alpha）、Registry 存放（抽查到的每一個 2026 編號都回報 published，且附序列）與實驗記錄（逐月 PDF，條目開頭就是 `Date: 20260801`）這四項都過關。圖譜與序列這一項沒過：整個 wiki 只有一張質體圖譜，是 pSTK-EXP1 的，而存放的零件有 35 個。而數據這一項，過關完全靠儀器。光度計與生物反應器的連續量測確實以 CSV 公開在數位孿生倉庫裡，但 hardware-bioreactor 頁上有五張圖的圖說寫著「redrawn from the team's chart」（依團隊的圖重繪）——ELISA、DNPH 活性分析、原型 4 的 OD600 與 pH、壓力曲線，以及殼側穿透液那組圖——讀者看到的是一張圖片被重新畫過，而不是一份已公開資料集的繪圖。hardware-photometer 頁上那兩張細菌生長曲線也是同樣的情況，而這一點是 wiki 自己的原始檔寫出來的：`static/hardware/photometer/js/growth-data.js` 裡的 `growth_c1` 與 `growth_c2` 都是 `csv: null`，上面的標題是「THE ONE PLACE THE RAW DATA GOES」，旁邊註著「The owner, 15 Oct: 'ill give data later'」。","chips":["5/6","1 map, 35 parts","5 figures redrawn","csv: null"],"chips_zh":["5/6","1 張圖譜對 35 個零件","5 張圖為重繪","csv: null"]}],"table":{"head":["Team","Full protocols","Chassis named","Maps or sequence","Registry with sequence","Raw data","Dated notebook","Score"],"head_zh":["隊伍","完整實驗流程","菌株名稱","圖譜或序列","Registry 含序列","原始數據","附日期的記錄","分數"],"rows":[["Cornell","yes, 5 PDF sheets","yes, E. coli SHuffle","no","yes","no","yes, dated, named operators","4/6"],["Heidelberg","yes, 13 PDF notebooks","yes, BL21(DE3), BL21-AI","no","yes","no","yes, one PDF per subproject","4/6"],["LYON","yes, 35-page lab book","yes, BL21(DE3), TOP10","yes, pET-29b(+) maps","yes","no","no, protocols only","4/6"],["NUS-Singapore","yes, 25 fold-out sheets","yes, S. cerevisiae BY4741","no","yes","no","yes, 176-page PDF","4/6"],["Princeton","yes, 46-page PDF","yes, BL21(DE3), ER2738","yes, 23 Benchling records","yes","no","yes, 95-page dated PDF","5/6"],["Stanford University","yes, on Experiments","yes, Nissle 1917, HEK293T","no","yes","no","yes, 4 notebooks + weeks","4/6"],["UAlberta","yes, SOP PDFs","yes, DH5-alpha, BL21(DE3)","no","yes","no, docking CSV only","yes, week by week","4/6"],["UCAS-China","yes, 20 PDF sheets","yes, BL21(DE3), HEK293T","no","yes","no","yes, 6 Benchling PDFs","4/6"],["UCNZ","yes, written into Results","yes, BL21(DE3), SHuffle","yes, xylanase maps","yes","no","no","4/6"],["UOttawa","yes, page plus PDFs","yes, P. putida KT2440","no, registry links only","yes","no","no, /notebook is a 404","3/6"],["Athens","yes, 19 PDF sheets","yes, BL21(DE3) pLysS","yes, vector maps","yes","no","yes, 15 dated weeks","5/6"],["ETH-Zurich","yes, page plus protocols.io","yes, MG1655, EPI300","yes, sequences printed","yes","no, Benchling asks sign-in","yes, 6 notebook PDFs","5/6"],["GU Frankfurt","yes, inside Methods","yes, DH5-alpha, Mach1","no","yes","no, uncropped blots only","no","3/6"],["KAUST-KSA","yes, inside notebook PDFs","yes, INVSc1, GS115","yes, pBS4S maps","yes","no","yes, 3 dated PDFs","5/6"],["Marburg","yes, protocols page","yes, DH5-alpha, BL21(DE3)","no, 1 map, from a game","yes","no","no","3/6"],["Muenster-University","yes, inside fold-outs","yes, K-12, B. subtilis 168","no","yes","no","no","3/6"],["Toronto","yes, 24-page PDF","yes, BL21(DE3), W3110","yes, PD and AS maps","yes","no, dataset DOI is dead","no, lab notes behind a login","4/6"],["TU Delft","yes, numbered library","yes, BL21(DE3), Nissle 1917","yes, 49 .gb files","yes","no, literature set only","yes","5/6"],["UZurich","yes, PDF sheets","yes, DSM33, BW29427","no","yes","no","yes, lab notes dated","4/6"],["WageningenUR","yes, PDF sheets","yes, MG1655, CEN.PK113-7D","yes, map + whole-plasmid seq","yes","no, cost CSVs only","yes, 3 notebooks","5/6"],["Eton-College-UK","yes, on Protocols","yes, BL21(DE3), DH5-alpha","yes, 3 maps","yes","no","yes","5/6"],["GCGS","yes, with catalogue numbers","yes, EcN Nissle 1917","no","yes","no","yes, dated cycle PDFs","4/6"],["GEMS-Taiwan","yes, 24 of 25 as PDF","yes, B. subtilis WB800","no, one map only","yes","part, instrument runs only","yes, monthly PDFs","5/6"],["GHCIS","yes, inside notebook PDF","yes, DH5-alpha, BL21(DE3)","yes, switch sequences printed","yes","no","yes, dated entries","5/6"],["HFI","yes, 4 notebook PDFs","yes, EcN Nissle 1917","no","yes","no","yes, dated, named recorder","4/6"],["HKSSC","yes, on Experiments","yes, DH5-alpha, BL21(DE3)","yes, prbA-idt maps","yes","no, ANOVA table only","no, Day 1-20 only","4/6"],["HangzhouFourteenAP","yes, inside the notebook","yes, Rosetta(DE3)","no","yes","no, “not transcribed”","yes, dated daily","4/6"],["HongKong-HS","yes, on Experiments","no, only “E. coli”","no","yes","yes, replicate tables","yes, 44 dates","4/6"],["HongKong-JSS","yes, page plus 124-page log","yes, DH5-alpha","no","yes","yes, inside the log","yes, dated log","5/6"],["Lambert-GA","yes, inside the notebooks","yes, NEB 5-alpha","yes, maps and sequences","yes","yes, two outside labs' files","yes, 2 dated PDFs","6/6"]],"rows_zh":[["Cornell","有，5 份 PDF","有，E. coli SHuffle","無","有","無","有，註明日期與操作者","4/6"],["Heidelberg","有，13 份 PDF 記錄","有，BL21(DE3)、BL21-AI","無","有","無","有，每個子題一份 PDF","4/6"],["LYON","有，35 頁 lab book","有，BL21(DE3)、TOP10","有，pET-29b(+) 圖譜","有","無","無，只有流程","4/6"],["NUS-Singapore","有，25 份展開式條目","有，S. cerevisiae BY4741","無","有","無","有，176 頁 PDF","4/6"],["Princeton","有，46 頁 PDF","有，BL21(DE3)、ER2738","有，23 筆 Benchling 紀錄","有","無","有，95 頁、附日期","5/6"],["Stanford University","有，寫在 Experiments","有，Nissle 1917、HEK293T","無","有","無","有，4 本記錄加週誌","4/6"],["UAlberta","有，SOP 的 PDF","有，DH5-alpha、BL21(DE3)","無","有","無，只有對接計算 CSV","有，逐週記錄","4/6"],["UCAS-China","有，20 份 PDF","有，BL21(DE3)、HEK293T","無","有","無","有，6 份 Benchling PDF","4/6"],["UCNZ","有，寫在 Results 內文","有，BL21(DE3)、SHuffle","有，木聚醣酶質體圖譜","有","無","無","4/6"],["UOttawa","有，頁面加 PDF","有，P. putida KT2440","無，只給 Registry 連結","有","無","無，/notebook 是 404","3/6"],["Athens","有，19 份 PDF","有，BL21(DE3) pLysS","有，載體圖譜","有","無","有，15 個附日期的週","5/6"],["ETH-Zurich","有，頁面加 protocols.io","有，MG1655、EPI300","有，序列直接印出","有","無，Benchling 要求登入","有，6 份記錄 PDF","5/6"],["GU Frankfurt","有，寫在 Methods","有，DH5-alpha、Mach1","無","有","無，只有未裁切的西方墨點","無","3/6"],["KAUST-KSA","有，寫在記錄 PDF 內","有，INVSc1、GS115","有，pBS4S 圖譜","有","無","有，3 份附日期 PDF","5/6"],["Marburg","有，protocols 頁","有，DH5-alpha、BL21(DE3)","無，只有 1 張，還出自教學遊戲","有","無","無","3/6"],["Muenster-University","有，收在摺疊區塊裡","有，K-12、B. subtilis 168","無","有","無","無","3/6"],["Toronto","有，24 頁 PDF","有，BL21(DE3)、W3110","有，PD 與 AS 質體圖譜","有","無，資料集 DOI 連不到","無，實驗日誌要登入","4/6"],["TU Delft","有，編號成冊","有，BL21(DE3)、Nissle 1917","有，49 個 .gb 檔","有","無，只有文獻資料集","有","5/6"],["UZurich","有，PDF 條目","有，DSM33、BW29427","無","有","無","有，實驗日誌附日期","4/6"],["WageningenUR","有，PDF 條目","有，MG1655、CEN.PK113-7D","有，圖譜加全質體定序","有","無，只有成本 CSV","有，3 份記錄","5/6"],["Eton-College-UK","有，寫在 Protocols","有，BL21(DE3)、DH5-alpha","有，3 張圖譜","有","無","有","5/6"],["GCGS","有，附試劑型號","有，EcN Nissle 1917","無","有","無","有，附日期的循環 PDF","4/6"],["GEMS-Taiwan","有，25 份中 24 份為 PDF","有，B. subtilis WB800","無，只有一張圖譜","有","部分，只有儀器連續量測","有，逐月 PDF","5/6"],["GHCIS","有，寫在記錄 PDF 內","有，DH5-alpha、BL21(DE3)","有，switch 序列直接印出","有","無","有，條目附日期","5/6"],["HFI","有，4 份記錄 PDF","有，EcN Nissle 1917","無","有","無","有，附日期與記錄者","4/6"],["HKSSC","有，寫在 Experiments","有，DH5-alpha、BL21(DE3)","有，prbA-idt 圖譜","有","無，只有 ANOVA 表","無，只標 Day 1-20","4/6"],["HangzhouFourteenAP","有，寫在記錄裡","有，Rosetta(DE3)","無","有","無，自述「未謄錄」","有，逐日附日期","4/6"],["HongKong-HS","有，寫在 Experiments","無，只寫 E. coli","無","有","有，逐重複值表格","有，44 個日期","4/6"],["HongKong-JSS","有，頁面加 124 頁日誌","有，DH5-alpha","無","有","有，寫在日誌裡","有，日誌附日期","5/6"],["Lambert-GA","有，寫在記錄本內","有，NEB 5-alpha","有，圖譜與序列","有","有，兩間外部實驗室的檔案","有，2 份附日期 PDF","6/6"]]},"checklist":["Publish a plasmid map or a .gb file for every construct, not one map for one of thirty-five parts. GEMS-Taiwan's parts page sends the reader to the Registry for each sequence; TU Delft put 49 GenBank files on its own wiki, and that is the gap to close in 2027.","Export the numbers behind every results figure as CSV into the GitLab repository, the way the photometer run already is. The ELISA, DNPH, prototype-4 OD600 and pH, pressure and shell-permeate figures are all captioned as redrawn from the team's own charts, with no dataset behind them; the Western densitometry, plant growth and chlorophyll figures have none either.","Never ship a figure redrawn from another figure, and never ship a disclosure that only exists in the source. Five figures on hardware-bioreactor say \"redrawn from the team's chart\"; the two growth charts on hardware-photometer are traced too, and `growth-data.js` says a line under each chart should say so — on the live page those two captions do not say it. Set a data-freeze date before the wiki freeze, and let a chart with no numbers behind it be left out rather than traced.","Finish the three protocol sheets that produced no result on this wiki — Bradford, large-scale extraction, purification and dialysis — or state on the sheet that the experiment was not run.","Keep what already works: the dated monthly notebook PDFs, the per-sheet PDF protocols with volumes and times, the strain named as B. subtilis WB800 rather than B. subtilis. Twenty-two of thirty teams have a dated notebook and only four have data; GEMS is already on the right side of the first and the wrong side of the second.","Add one line to each results figure naming the notebook date and the protocol sheet it came from. GEMS already has both objects; nothing on the wiki joins a number to the day it was measured.","Check every external link a month after the freeze. Toronto's own dataset DOI is dead and its lab notes need a Google login; GEMS's data links are GitLab paths, which is the right choice, but they should still be fetched signed-out before the Jamboree."],"checklist_zh":["每一個構築都要有質體圖譜或 .gb 檔，而不是 35 個零件只有一張圖。GEMS-Taiwan 的 parts 頁把讀者導去 Registry 查序列；TU Delft 把 49 個 GenBank 檔放在自己的 wiki 上——2027 要補的就是這個缺口。","把每一張結果圖背後的數字輸出成 CSV 放進 GitLab 倉庫，就像光度計那次連續量測已經做到的那樣。ELISA、DNPH、原型 4 的 OD600 與 pH、壓力與殼側穿透液這幾張圖，圖說都寫明是依團隊自己的圖重繪，背後沒有資料集；西方墨點灰階、植株生長與葉綠素那幾張也同樣沒有。","絕不要用「照著另一張圖重畫」的方式產出圖表，也絕不要讓揭露只存在於原始碼裡。hardware-bioreactor 上有五張圖寫著「redrawn from the team's chart」；hardware-photometer 上那兩張生長曲線同樣是描出來的，而 `growth-data.js` 寫明每張圖下面應該有一行字講明這件事——但在實際頁面上，那兩張圖的圖說並沒有寫。請在 wiki 凍結之前先設一個數據凍結日；背後沒有數字的圖，寧可不要放，也不要描一張出來。","把這份 wiki 上三份沒有產出結果的流程補完——Bradford、大量萃取、純化與透析——或者直接在條目上寫明該實驗並未執行。","已經做對的要守住：逐月且附日期的記錄 PDF、每份都寫明體積與時間的 PDF 流程、把菌株寫成 B. subtilis WB800 而不是只寫 B. subtilis。30 支隊伍裡有 22 支有附日期的記錄，卻只有 4 支給得出數據；GEMS 在前一項站對邊，在後一項站錯邊。","在每張結果圖加一行字，標明它出自哪一天的記錄、哪一份流程條目。GEMS 這兩樣東西都有，但整個 wiki 沒有任何地方把一個數字接回它被量到的那一天。","凍結一個月後，把所有外部連結重新點一次。Toronto 自家資料集的 DOI 已經失效，實驗日誌還要 Google 登入；GEMS 的資料連結指向 GitLab，這個選擇是對的，但出發去 Jamboree 之前仍應以未登入的狀態實際抓一次。"],"method":"Sample: all 30 teams in the 2026 Top 10 lists — ten Undergrad, ten Overgrad, ten High School — chosen because it is a complete, pre-defined set that needs no judgement call about which award counts as wet-lab, and because GEMS-Taiwan sits inside it rather than being added to it. The table is ordered Undergrad, then Overgrad, then High School. Each team was scored on six checks, one point each: (1) full protocols, meaning step-level procedures with volumes, temperatures, times and at least one named kit or supplier, published as wiki text, fold-out panel or downloadable PDF — prose summaries do not count; (2) the chassis named to the strain, for example BL21(DE3), DH5-alpha, Nissle 1917, WB800, BY4741, and not only \"E. coli\"; (3) plasmid maps or complete sequences covering the constructs actually built, whether as map figures, printed sequences, sequence files or public sequence-platform links — a Registry link alone does not count, and one map for a collection of thirty-five parts was scored as a fail; (4) parts deposited with sequence, tested by querying api.registry.igem.org/v1/parts/slugs/ for up to eight of each team's 2026 accessions with a browser User-Agent and 1.4-second spacing, 210 accessions in all; (5) raw data, meaning the numbers behind at least one published experimental figure are downloadable or printed — a statistics table, an uncropped blot image, or a chart alone is a fail, and economic, docking, literature or outreach CSVs were not counted as experimental data; (6) a dated notebook with calendar dates, on the wiki or in a PDF — \"Day 1 … Day 20\" is a fail. GEMS-Taiwan was scored a pass on data on the strength of the photometer and bioreactor CSV runs in its digital-twin repository; the table marks that cell \"part\" because no bench assay — ELISA, DNPH, Western, plant growth — has its numbers published. Wikis were read by crawling each site's pages and JavaScript bundles and by opening pages in a browser; roughly a third of these wikis are client-rendered, and several (NUS-Singapore, Muenster-University, Eton-College-UK, GU Frankfurt, KAUST-KSA) hold their protocols or parts inside panels that a plain fetch cannot see, so every low count was re-checked in a browser before being recorded. More than 110 PDFs were downloaded and their text extracted, which is how protocol and notebook PDFs could be scored rather than merely counted. Every data, sequence and repository link reported as failing was fetched signed-out and its HTTP status recorded. What this cannot see: a wiki that does not publish a protocol does not prove the team lacked one — this reads wikis, not lab books, and a team may hold complete records, raw spreadsheets and annotated maps that it simply never uploaded. It also cannot tell whether a published protocol actually works, whether a number is right, or whether a notebook was written on the day it claims. Scanned or image-only PDF pages yield no text, so a protocol that exists only as a photograph may have been undercounted. Registry checks sampled up to eight parts per team, not every part, and the parts API rate-limits, so a handful of accessions were retried rather than read on the first pass. The sample is decorated teams only — the 30 projects the judges ranked highest — and nothing here describes iGEM 2026 as a whole.","method_zh":"取樣：2026 年 Top 10 名單上的全部 30 支隊伍——大學部十支、研究生組十支、高中組十支。選這個集合，是因為它是事先就定義好的完整名單，不需要去判斷哪些獎項算濕實驗；也因為 GEMS-Taiwan 本來就在裡面，而不是另外補進來的。表格順序為大學部、研究生組、高中組。每支隊伍以六項檢核計分，每項一分：（1）完整實驗流程，指步驟層級、寫明體積、溫度、時間，並至少具名一個套組或供應商，形式可以是 wiki 內文、摺疊面板或可下載 PDF——只有敘述性摘要不算；（2）菌株寫到品系層級，例如 BL21(DE3)、DH5-alpha、Nissle 1917、WB800、BY4741，而不是只寫 E. coli；（3）質體圖譜或完整序列，且需涵蓋實際做出來的構築，形式可以是圖譜、直接印出的序列、序列檔或公開的序列平台連結——只給 Registry 連結不算；35 個零件只有一張圖譜，判定為未通過；（4）零件已附序列存入 Registry，做法是以瀏覽器 User-Agent、每次間隔 1.4 秒查詢 api.registry.igem.org/v1/parts/slugs/，每隊抽查最多八個 2026 年編號，合計 210 個；（5）原始數據，指至少一張已發表實驗圖背後的數字可下載或被印出來——只有統計表、未裁切的墨點影像或圖表本身都算未通過；經濟模型、分子對接、文獻整理或科普活動的 CSV 不列為實驗數據；（6）附日曆日期的實驗記錄，可以在 wiki 上或 PDF 裡——只寫「Day 1⋯Day 20」算未通過。GEMS-Taiwan 在數據這一項判定為通過，依據是其數位孿生倉庫裡光度計與生物反應器的 CSV 連續量測；表格中該格標為「部分」，因為沒有任何一項實驗台上的分析——ELISA、DNPH、西方墨點、植株生長——有公開數字。閱讀方式是抓取各站頁面與 JavaScript bundle，再輔以瀏覽器實際開啟；這批 wiki 約有三分之一是前端渲染，其中數支（NUS-Singapore、Muenster-University、Eton-College-UK、GU Frankfurt、KAUST-KSA）把流程或零件收在直接抓取看不到的面板裡，因此凡是數值偏低的項目，都先在瀏覽器裡重新確認過才記錄。共下載 110 份以上的 PDF 並抽取文字，所以流程與記錄 PDF 是被讀過內容，而不是只被數過份數。凡是被寫成失效的資料、序列或倉庫連結，都在未登入狀態下實際抓取並記下 HTTP 狀態碼。看不到的部分：wiki 上沒有流程，並不等於這支隊伍沒有流程——這份研究讀的是 wiki，不是實驗記錄本；隊伍手上可能有完整紀錄、原始試算表與註解過的圖譜，只是從未上傳。它同樣無法判斷已公開的流程是否真的做得出來、某個數字對不對，或某則記錄是否真的寫於它所標示的那一天。掃描或純影像的 PDF 抽不出文字，因此只以照片形式存在的流程可能被低估。Registry 每隊最多抽查八個零件，不是全部，且該 API 會限流，少數編號是重試後才讀到。樣本僅限得獎隊伍——評審排名最高的 30 個專案——此處沒有任何一句話在描述整個 iGEM 2026。"},{"id":"falsification-controls","tab":"drylab","order":46,"kicker":"Original analysis","kicker_zh":"原創分析","title":"A floor, not a ranking","title_zh":"一道門檻，而不是一張名次表","lede":"The half of this report's strongest finding that had never been measured does not hold. Reading all 30 Top 10 wikis of 2026, 26 teams ran an experiment designed expressly to kill a rival explanation for their own result, and all 30 published a result unfavourable to their own claim — so the practice cannot tell a podium from a Top 10. It sets a floor instead: no podium team had fewer than four of the five control types, and five of the seven teams that had all five missed the podium.","lede_zh":"本報告最強的那項發現，其中一半從來沒有人量過；量過之後，這一半並不成立。我們讀完 2026 年三個組別全部 30 支 Top 10 團隊的 wiki：有 26 支做過一個刻意設計來殺掉自家結果另一種解釋的實驗，而 30 支全部都公開了一項對自己主張不利的結果——所以這個習慣分不出獎台與前十。它劃出的是一道門檻：沒有任何一支獎台隊伍的五類對照少於四類；而五類全有的七支隊伍裡，有五支沒上獎台。","body":"We asked one question of all 30 Top 10 wikis: **how many decorated 2026 teams ran an experiment whose result could have broken their own headline claim, and does doing so track the podium?** The first half has an answer. The second half breaks.\n\n**The type specimen is GEMS-Taiwan's 2024 Grand Prize, and it is not an extra assay.** Having killed mosquito larvae with three toxins, the team wrote on the page what it was worried about: \"We want to rule out the effect of E. coli in the death of mosquito larvae.\" The arm it built was a BL21(DE3) empty-vector group read out by a Gambicin, Rel1, Rel2 and defensin qPCR immune-gene panel, with the reason stated plainly: \"The reason why we use BL21(DE3)-empty vector is to investigate whether the mortality observed was due to the cytotoxicity effect or bacterial infection of the E. coli or solely due to the potency of the biolarvicides.\" It reached a conclusion — \"This data indicated that the mortality observed in the larvicidal assay was not due to the introduction of BL21(DE3).\" — and the panel itself came back largely null, which the team also said: \"the majority of the transcripts of immune genes were not regulated after the larvae exposure to the toxins.\" In the oviposition-attractant assay the same habit appears as a confound removed by design, with the purpose given as ruling out the coloration factor: \"we covered each solution with black paper … so that the selection of oviposition sites is based on odorant factors only\", and the preference still held at p = 0.0003.\n\n**The exclusion and the disclosure of its gap are scored apart, because the same page does both.** That 2024 panel is complete for one induction condition and the team says which one it could not cover and why: \"We acknowledge the limitation of this particular study because we did not compare it to BL21(DE3) for biolarvicidal toxin produced at 20 degrees C overnight. Our team had a shortage of mosquito larvae to conduct additional groups during this period of time, and hence, we were not able to compare the cytotoxicity effect of BL21(DE3).\" A rubric that credits only completed exclusions would rank that page below a team that never noticed the confound at all, which is plainly the wrong answer. So the five scored types below are the controls that were run, and a sixth flag records naming an arm you could not run.\n\n**Five types, scored only on a sentence we can quote.** `A` a chassis-only, empty-vector, untransformed or heat-killed arm on the headline assay, not on a cloning gel: **28 of 30**. `R` an experiment run expressly to exclude a named rival cause: **26 of 30**. `D` a confound removed by design and the effect then re-tested: **17 of 30**. `H` validation against data held back from fitting: **12 of 30**. `U` a result unfavourable to the team's own headline, published: **30 of 30**.\n\n**Three of the five are saturated, and that is the finding.** At this level of the field a no-activity arm, a rival-mechanism exclusion and a published unfavourable result are table stakes, not distinctions. Thirty of thirty published something that cut against them. Twenty-six of thirty built an arm against a named alternative cause. Whatever separates a Grand Prize from a Top 10 in 2026, it is not whether the team thought of the control.\n\n**The podium comparison, with its n.** Podium teams (7) average **4.29 of 5** control types; the other 23 average **3.61**. The gap is 0.68 of one category, and a permutation test over the 30 scores puts it at **p = 0.079** one-sided — not a result. Within the High School section alone it is 4.00 against 3.50, on two teams against eight, which is not a comparison at all. The three Grand Prize winners score 4, 4 and 5. **n = 30 cannot support a strong inference**, and we are not drawing one.\n\n**What survives is a floor and an absence of ranking.** No podium team scored below 4, while **10 of the 23 non-podium teams did**. But four-of-five did not get you there either: of the seven teams with all five types, only UCAS-China and TU Delft are on a podium. **Eton-College-UK, GEMS-Taiwan, Heidelberg, NUS-Singapore and UOttawa** all scored a full five and finished outside the top three of their section. If the count were the mechanism, those five would be the podium.\n\n**Where the field does split is `D` and `H`.** Removing a confound by design and then re-testing is 5 of 7 on the podium against 12 of 23 off it; holding data back from fitting is 4 of 7 against 8 of 23. Held-back validation is also the one habit that is evenly thin across all three sections — exactly 4 of 10 teams in High School, Undergrad and Overgrad alike.\n\n**The sixth flag is the cleanest signal in the whole analysis, and it is about writing, not pipetting.** Twenty-three of 30 teams name a specific arm, replicate or comparison they did not run and state what cannot be concluded without it — and that is **7 of 7 on the podium against 16 of 23 off it**. Athens has the single best instance in the cohort, a control it has not run, named as the thing that would settle its own effect: \"Separating the two requires that buffer-only arm, and until it is run we describe the effect as attributable to the preparation.\" HongKong-JSS, the High School 1st Runner-up, writes the admission that most teams would delete: \"we forgot to include matching 0 µM samples, an empty-vector control and an untransformed E. coli control in these early experiments. This was an experimental-design mistake.\" It then added them, and its own sensors came out weaker and less consistent than the uncontrolled screen had suggested. Cornell puts it in parentheses mid-protocol: \"(regrettably, pre-induction or t~0 aliquots were not collected as negative controls for this experiment)\".\n\n**Four controls in this cohort actually broke something, which is the point of running them.** Muenster-University's no-protease arm cleaved anyway, so the screen could not be trusted: \"The presence of the cleavage product in samples without pACYC_Myc_NIaPro implies that construct, leading to false-positive results … This means even if we had cleavage by NIa-Pro, the negative controls would show false results.\" GEMS-Taiwan's untransformed host read the same as its constructs, and the team published the table anyway: \"A negative control returning a signal comparable to the samples means the assay is reading something other than recombinant protein in these preparations, so no difference here can be attributed to expression.\" Marburg's no-RBS background control turned a happy result into an artefact — the team had briefly believed its hairpins were silencing expression, then found \"an unintended additional ATG located one base upstream of and out of frame with the NanoLuc start codon\". Toronto audited its own benchmark and declared it circular: \"The HMMs were themselves built from the NR search, so testing them on NR mostly measured how well they recall their own training data,\" then moved validation to a held-out set, concluding that \"A benchmark has to be independent of what the model was built from.\"\n\n**The floor of the cohort is real too.** UCNZ, HongKong-HS and GHCIS score 2, with a reagent blank and a published failure but no experiment aimed at an alternative cause; on UCNZ's wiki the phrase \"negative control\" does not appear anywhere we could read, across 1.3 MB of recovered text. Cornell scores 2 from the other direction: it reasons carefully about alternative causes and says out loud which arms it skipped.\n\n**So the two-direction finding narrows to one direction.** Measuring the central claim on the real target still separates the podium. Experimentally excluding the rival explanation does not — not because it is rare, but because among decorated teams it is close to universal. What is still scarce, and what leans podium-ward on numbers too small to trust, is the harder pair: redesigning the experiment so a confound cannot enter, and keeping data back from your own fitting.","body_zh":"我們對 30 支 Top 10 團隊的 wiki 只問一個問題：**2026 年有多少支獲獎團隊，做過一個結果有可能推翻自家主要主張的實驗；而這件事是否和獎台相關？** 前半有答案，後半破了。\n\n**模式標本是 GEMS-Taiwan 2024 年的總冠軍，而它不是多做一個 assay。** 在用三種毒素殺死蚊子幼蟲之後，這支隊伍把自己擔心的事寫在頁面上：「We want to rule out the effect of E. coli in the death of mosquito larvae.」他們設計的那一組是 BL21(DE3) 空載體組，讀出的是 Gambicin、Rel1、Rel2 與 defensin 的 qPCR 免疫基因盤，理由也寫得很白：「The reason why we use BL21(DE3)-empty vector is to investigate whether the mortality observed was due to the cytotoxicity effect or bacterial infection of the E. coli or solely due to the potency of the biolarvicides.」這一組得到了結論——「This data indicated that the mortality observed in the larvicidal assay was not due to the introduction of BL21(DE3).」——而基因盤本身大致是空的，隊伍也照樣寫了出來：「the majority of the transcripts of immune genes were not regulated after the larvae exposure to the toxins.」在產卵誘引試驗裡，同一種習慣換成了用設計排除混淆因子，目的直接寫明是要排除顏色這個因素：「we covered each solution with black paper … so that the selection of oviposition sites is based on odorant factors only」，而偏好依然在 p = 0.0003 的水準上成立。\n\n**我們把「排除」和「承認排除有缺口」分開計分，因為同一個頁面兩件事都做了。** 2024 年那組基因盤只在一種誘導條件下完成，隊伍寫出了自己沒能涵蓋哪一種、以及為什麼：「We acknowledge the limitation of this particular study because we did not compare it to BL21(DE3) for biolarvicidal toxin produced at 20 degrees C overnight. Our team had a shortage of mosquito larvae to conduct additional groups during this period of time, and hence, we were not able to compare the cytotoxicity effect of BL21(DE3).」一套只認完整排除的評分標準，會把這一頁排在一支從頭到尾沒想到這個混淆因子的隊伍後面，那顯然是錯的答案。所以底下五個計分類別都是真的做了的對照，第六個旗標則記錄「指名了自己沒能做的那一組」。\n\n**五個類別，而且只憑一句可以逐字引用的話給分。** `A` 主要 assay 上的宿主單獨組、空載體組、未轉形組或熱殺死組，不算選殖用的膠片：**30 支中的 28 支**。`R` 專門為排除某個指名的競爭解釋而做的實驗：**30 支中的 26 支**。`D` 用設計移除混淆因子，然後把效應重測一次：**30 支中的 17 支**。`H` 用從擬合中保留下來的資料做驗證：**30 支中的 12 支**。`U` 公開一項對自家主張不利的結果：**30 支中的 30 支**。\n\n**五類裡有三類已經飽和，而這本身就是發現。** 在這個層級的場域裡，一組無活性對照、一次競爭機制排除、一項公開的不利結果，都是入場費，不是區別。三十支裡有三十支公開了對自己不利的東西。三十支裡有二十六支針對某個指名的替代原因做了一組實驗。2026 年把總冠軍和 Top 10 分開的東西，不是「隊伍有沒有想到那組對照」。\n\n**獎台比較，連同它的 n。** 七支獎台隊伍平均擁有 **五類中的 4.29 類**，其餘 23 支平均 **3.61 類**。差距是 0.68 個類別；對 30 筆分數做置換檢定，單尾 **p = 0.079**——這不是一個結果。單看高中組是 4.00 對 3.50，兩支對八支，那根本不能算比較。三支總冠軍的分數是 4、4、5。**n = 30 撐不起任何強推論**，我們也不打算做。\n\n**留下來的是一道門檻，以及名次的缺席。** 沒有任何獎台隊伍低於 4 分，而 **23 支非獎台隊伍中有 10 支低於 4 分**。但四類也不保證上得去：五類全有的七支隊伍裡，只有 UCAS-China 與 TU Delft 在獎台上。**Eton-College-UK、GEMS-Taiwan、Heidelberg、NUS-Singapore 與 UOttawa** 五支全拿滿五類，卻都停在自己組別的前三之外。如果這個計數就是機制，那獎台應該是這五支。\n\n**真正分得開的是 `D` 和 `H`。** 用設計移除混淆因子再重測，獎台是七支中的五支，台下是 23 支中的 12 支；把資料從擬合中保留下來，獎台是七支中的四支，台下是 23 支中的八支。保留資料驗證也是唯一一項在三個組別都同樣稀薄的習慣——高中組、大學組、研究生組都剛好是十支中的四支。\n\n**第六個旗標是整份分析裡最乾淨的訊號，而它關乎寫作，不關乎操作。** 30 支裡有 23 支指名了某一組自己沒做的對照、重複或比較，並說明少了它就不能下什麼結論——而這是 **獎台七支中的七支，對台下 23 支中的 16 支**。Athens 有全 cohort 最好的一例：一組還沒做的對照，被指名為唯一能定案自家效應的東西——「Separating the two requires that buffer-only arm, and until it is run we describe the effect as attributable to the preparation.」高中組第一亞軍 HongKong-JSS 寫下了多數隊伍會刪掉的那句自白：「we forgot to include matching 0 µM samples, an empty-vector control and an untransformed E. coli control in these early experiments. This was an experimental-design mistake.」接著他們把那些對照補上去，自家感測器的表現就比沒有對照的初篩所顯示的更弱、更不一致。Cornell 把它放在 protocol 中間的括號裡：「(regrettably, pre-induction or t~0 aliquots were not collected as negative controls for this experiment)」。\n\n**這個 cohort 裡有四組對照真的弄壞了什麼，而那正是做對照的意義。** Muenster-University 沒有加蛋白酶的那一組照樣被切開了，於是整套篩選不能相信：「The presence of the cleavage product in samples without pACYC_Myc_NIaPro implies that construct, leading to false-positive results … This means even if we had cleavage by NIa-Pro, the negative controls would show false results.」GEMS-Taiwan 的未轉形宿主讀到和自家構築體同一個範圍，隊伍照樣把那張表登了出來：「A negative control returning a signal comparable to the samples means the assay is reading something other than recombinant protein in these preparations, so no difference here can be attributed to expression.」Marburg 的 no-RBS 背景對照把一個令人開心的結果變成了假象——他們一度以為自家的髮夾結構成功抑制了表現，後來才發現「an unintended additional ATG located one base upstream of and out of frame with the NanoLuc start codon」。Toronto 稽核了自己的基準測試並宣告它是循環的：「The HMMs were themselves built from the NR search, so testing them on NR mostly measured how well they recall their own training data.」接著把驗證搬到一組保留資料上，並得出結論：「A benchmark has to be independent of what the model was built from.」\n\n**這個 cohort 的地板也是真的。** UCNZ、HongKong-HS 與 GHCIS 都是 2 分：有試劑空白、有公開的失敗，但沒有任何針對替代原因的實驗；在我們能讀到的範圍內，UCNZ 的 wiki 整整 1.3 MB 還原文字裡，完全沒出現「negative control」這個詞。Cornell 的 2 分來自另一個方向：它對替代原因推理得很仔細，並且明說自己跳過了哪幾組。\n\n**於是那項雙向發現收斂成單向。** 把中心主張量在真正的標的上，仍然分得開獎台。用實驗排除競爭解釋則分不開——不是因為它罕見，而是因為在獲獎團隊之間它幾乎普及。真正還稀少、而且在小到不可信的樣本上偏向獎台的，是更難的那一對：把實驗重新設計到混淆因子進不來，以及把資料從自己的擬合裡留下來。","cards":[{"kicker":"The headline number","kicker_zh":"最關鍵的數字","title":"26 of 30 killed a rival explanation","title_zh":"30 支裡有 26 支殺掉了競爭解釋","body":"Twenty-six of the 30 Top 10 teams of 2026 ran at least one experiment whose stated purpose was to exclude a named alternative cause of their own result. Four did not: GHCIS, HKSSC, HongKong-HS and UCNZ. The practice is not rare at this level of the field, which is why it cannot pick the winner.","body_zh":"2026 年 30 支 Top 10 團隊中，有 26 支至少做過一個實驗，其寫明的目的就是排除自家結果的某個指名替代原因。沒有的四支是 GHCIS、HKSSC、HongKong-HS 與 UCNZ。在這個層級的場域裡，這個習慣並不罕見，這也正是它挑不出贏家的原因。","chips":["26/30 exclusions","4 teams with none","Not a discriminator"],"chips_zh":["26/30 有排除實驗","4 支完全沒有","分不出勝負"]},{"kicker":"The type specimen","kicker_zh":"模式標本","title":"An empty vector and a sheet of black paper","title_zh":"一個空載體和一張黑紙","body":"GEMS-Taiwan's 2024 Grand Prize turned on two controls, not on an extra assay. The first names the rival cause out loud: \"We want to rule out the effect of E. coli in the death of mosquito larvae.\" The arm was a BL21(DE3) empty-vector group read by a Gambicin, Rel1, Rel2 and defensin qPCR panel. The second removes a confound by design: \"we covered each solution with black paper … so that the selection of oviposition sites is based on odorant factors only\" — and the preference survived at p = 0.0003.","body_zh":"GEMS-Taiwan 2024 年的總冠軍，關鍵在兩組對照，而不在多做一個 assay。第一組把競爭原因直接說出口：「We want to rule out the effect of E. coli in the death of mosquito larvae.」那一組是 BL21(DE3) 空載體組，以 Gambicin、Rel1、Rel2 與 defensin 的 qPCR 盤讀出。第二組用設計移除混淆因子：「we covered each solution with black paper … so that the selection of oviposition sites is based on odorant factors only」——而偏好在 p = 0.0003 下依然成立。","chips":["Empty-vector arm","Confound by design","p = 0.0003"],"chips_zh":["空載體對照組","用設計排除混淆","p = 0.0003"]},{"kicker":"Why two scores, not one","kicker_zh":"為什麼是兩個分數，不是一個","title":"The exclusion and its gap are scored apart","title_zh":"排除與它的缺口分開計分","body":"The 2024 panel is complete for one induction condition and the team says which one it could not cover: \"We acknowledge the limitation of this particular study because we did not compare it to BL21(DE3) for biolarvicidal toxin produced at 20 degrees C overnight.\" A rubric crediting only completed exclusions would rank that page below a team that never noticed the confound. So five types count the controls run, and a sixth flag counts naming the arm you could not run.","body_zh":"2024 年那組基因盤只在一種誘導條件下完成，隊伍也寫出自己沒能涵蓋哪一種：「We acknowledge the limitation of this particular study because we did not compare it to BL21(DE3) for biolarvicidal toxin produced at 20 degrees C overnight.」一套只認完整排除的標準，會把這一頁排在從沒想到這個混淆因子的隊伍後面。所以五個類別數的是做了的對照，第六個旗標數的是「指名了自己沒做的那一組」。","chips":["Run vs disclosed","Incomplete arm named","Both are discipline"],"chips_zh":["做了的對照／承認的缺口","指名未完成的那一組","兩者都是紀律"]},{"kicker":"The podium test","kicker_zh":"獎台檢定","title":"4.29 against 3.61, p = 0.079","title_zh":"4.29 對 3.61，p = 0.079","body":"The seven podium teams average 4.29 of the five control types; the other 23 average 3.61. A permutation test over the 30 scores puts the one-sided p at 0.079. The three Grand Prize winners score 4, 4 and 5. Within High School alone it is 4.00 against 3.50 on two teams against eight. None of this is strong enough to infer from, and we do not.","body_zh":"七支獎台隊伍平均擁有五類對照中的 4.29 類，其餘 23 支平均 3.61 類。對 30 筆分數做置換檢定，單尾 p 為 0.079。三支總冠軍的分數是 4、4、5。單看高中組是 4.00 對 3.50，兩支對八支。這些都不足以支撐推論，我們也沒有做推論。","chips":["7 vs 23 teams","p = 0.079, one-sided","n = 30"],"chips_zh":["7 支對 23 支","p = 0.079，單尾","n = 30"]},{"kicker":"The result that breaks it","kicker_zh":"推翻假設的那個結果","title":"Five perfect scorers missed the podium","title_zh":"五支滿分隊伍沒上獎台","body":"Seven teams hold all five control types. Only UCAS-China and TU Delft are on a podium. Eton-College-UK, GEMS-Taiwan, Heidelberg, NUS-Singapore and UOttawa each scored a full five and finished outside their section's top three. If the count were the mechanism, those five would be the podium. What survives is a floor: no podium team scored below 4, while 10 of the 23 non-podium teams did.","body_zh":"有七支隊伍五類對照全有，其中只有 UCAS-China 與 TU Delft 在獎台上。Eton-College-UK、GEMS-Taiwan、Heidelberg、NUS-Singapore 與 UOttawa 五支全拿滿分，卻都停在自己組別前三之外。如果這個計數就是機制，獎台應該是這五支。留下來的只是一道門檻：沒有獎台隊伍低於 4 分，而 23 支非獎台隊伍中有 10 支低於 4 分。","chips":["5 of 7 off the podium","Podium minimum 4/5","10 of 23 below 4"],"chips_zh":["七支滿分有五支沒上台","獎台最低 4/5","23 支中 10 支低於 4"]},{"kicker":"Where the field actually splits","kicker_zh":"場域真正的分水嶺","title":"17 redesign; 12 hold data back","title_zh":"17 支重新設計，12 支保留資料","body":"Three of the five types are saturated: a no-activity arm appears on 28 of 30 wikis, a rival-mechanism exclusion on 26, and every single one of the 30 published something unfavourable to its own claim. The scarce pair is harder. Removing a confound by design and re-testing: 17 of 30. Validating against data held back from fitting: 12 of 30, and exactly 4 of 10 in each of the three sections.","body_zh":"五類中有三類已經飽和：無活性對照出現在 30 份 wiki 中的 28 份，競爭機制排除出現在 26 份，而 30 支全部都公開了對自家主張不利的東西。稀少的那一對比較難。用設計移除混淆因子再重測：30 支中的 17 支。用保留下來的資料驗證：30 支中的 12 支，而且三個組別都剛好是十支中的四支。","chips":["A 28/30","R 26/30","D 17/30","H 12/30"],"chips_zh":["A 28/30","R 26/30","D 17/30","H 12/30"]},{"kicker":"The control that worked","kicker_zh":"真的起作用的那組對照","title":"Four teams had something broken for them","title_zh":"四支隊伍被自己的對照弄壞了東西","body":"Muenster-University's no-protease arm cleaved anyway: \"even if we had cleavage by NIa-Pro, the negative controls would show false results.\" GEMS-Taiwan's untransformed host read the same as its constructs, and the table went up anyway: \"no difference here can be attributed to expression.\" Marburg's no-RBS background exposed an unintended upstream ATG behind a result it had briefly celebrated. Toronto declared its own benchmark circular and moved it to a held-out set.","body_zh":"Muenster-University 沒加蛋白酶的那一組照樣被切開：「even if we had cleavage by NIa-Pro, the negative controls would show false results.」GEMS-Taiwan 的未轉形宿主讀到和自家構築體同一範圍，那張表照樣登出來：「no difference here can be attributed to expression.」Marburg 的 no-RBS 背景對照，揭穿了一個它一度慶祝過的結果背後那個非預期的上游 ATG。Toronto 宣告自己的基準測試是循環的，並把它搬到保留資料上。","chips":["4 broken claims","Published anyway","That is the point"],"chips_zh":["4 項被推翻的主張","照樣公開","這才是重點"]},{"kicker":"The sixth flag","kicker_zh":"第六個旗標","title":"23 of 30 named the arm they could not run","title_zh":"30 支裡有 23 支指名了自己做不到的那一組","body":"This is the cleanest signal here, and it is writing rather than pipetting: 7 of 7 podium teams against 16 of 23 off the podium. Athens names a control it has not run as the only thing that would settle its own effect: \"Separating the two requires that buffer-only arm, and until it is run we describe the effect as attributable to the preparation.\" Wageningen, HongKong-JSS and Cornell each print the missing arm on the page rather than quietly leaving it out.","body_zh":"這是這裡最乾淨的訊號，而且關乎寫作、不關乎操作：獎台七支中的七支，對台下 23 支中的 16 支。Athens 把一組還沒做的對照，指名為唯一能定案自家效應的東西：「Separating the two requires that buffer-only arm, and until it is run we describe the effect as attributable to the preparation.」Wageningen、HongKong-JSS 與 Cornell 都把缺少的那一組寫在頁面上，而不是悄悄省略。","chips":["7/7 on the podium","16/23 off it","Athens names it best"],"chips_zh":["獎台 7/7","台下 16/23","Athens 寫得最好"]}],"table":{"head":["Team","Section","Placing","Control types","The arm that could have broken the claim"],"head_zh":["團隊","組別","名次","對照類型（A R D H U）","可能推翻自家主張的那一組對照"],"rows":[["Lambert-GA","High School","Grand Prize","A R H U — 4","GFP-only and nanobody-only arms on the pull-down, a test set split by antigen cluster with homology checked, and 34 of 35 designs published one per row as negative binding calls"],["HongKong-JSS","High School","1st Runner-up","A R H U — 4","The empty-vector and untransformed arms it admits forgetting: \"we forgot to include matching 0 µM samples, an empty-vector control and an untransformed E. coli control\" — added later, and the sensors got weaker"],["Eton-College-UK","High School","Top 10","A R D H U — 5","\"Heated and unheated samples were also included to control for potential effects of sample preparation\", plus out-of-fold scoring of held-out positives against competitor proteases"],["GCGS","High School","Top 10","A R U — 3","A growth curve run so the reporter signal could have been blamed on cell density: \"fluorescence differences reflected genuine promoter activity instead of cell density artifacts\""],["GEMS-Taiwan","High School","Top 10","A R D H U — 5","A seven-group control table captioned by what each group rules out, an apo-receptor simulation, and an untransformed-host ELISA arm that killed the team's own expression ranking"],["GHCIS","High School","Top 10","A U — 2","A 0 µM negative control on the paper assay whose own colour became the finding: \"color formation alone was insufficient for a reliable positive call\""],["HFI","High School","Top 10","A R D U — 4","A blank arm \"ruling out the interference of lysine's own non-biological degradation\", plus a ldcC knockout chassis built to remove the host's own lysine consumption, then re-tested"],["HKSSC","High School","Top 10","A D U — 3","\"To rule out the stress caused by pelB, we removed the pelB sequence in cycle 3 as well\", and an uninduced arm at every paraben dose"],["HangzhouFourteenAP","High School","Top 10","A R D U — 4","Heat-inactivated enzyme subtracted well by well, plus leave-one-enzyme-out omission groups; the gravimetric readout then returned no significant difference and said so"],["HongKong-HS","High School","Top 10","A U — 2","\"negative controls containing no plasmids\" on the cell-free run, and a published null: no significant difference with or without target for the miR-21 candidates"],["Stanford University","Undergrad","Grand Prize","A R D U — 4","A non-targeting guide RNA, mismatched trigger arms, and a design giving every condition ADAR1 \"so that results were not confounded by lack of endogenous ADAR1 availability\""],["UCAS-China","Undergrad","1st Runner-up","A R D H U — 5","Cell counts run against its own fluorescence claim, \"ruling out interference from differences in cell number\", plus leave-one-donor-out prediction rotated across three donors"],["Princeton","Undergrad","2nd Runner-up","A R D U — 4","\"Each grid carries a phage-only row with no bacteria added … it rules out carryover growth, spontaneous resistance and contamination\", plus allocation, experimental, measurement and analysis blinding"],["Cornell","Undergrad","Top 10","R U — 2","A lysate-and-pellet split run \"to rule out the possibility that the protein aggregated and precipitated\", with the missing t~0 negative controls admitted in parentheses on the page"],["Heidelberg","Undergrad","Top 10","A R D H U — 5","\"Collapse the gas vesicles with pressure in the same field: same cells, no vesicles … This one control rules out density and slide differences at once\", plus nine scrambled design negatives"],["LYON","Undergrad","Top 10","A R D U — 4","An inactive protein of the same size replacing a boiled-enzyme control whose aggregate \"played to much on the absorbance of theses wells\" — the control was swapped, then the assay re-run"],["NUS-Singapore","Undergrad","Top 10","A R D H U — 5","Cross-activation tests that found its own sensor leaking, plus the harder of two validation designs: \"an independent plate at a temperature held out of training entirely\""],["UAlberta","Undergrad","Top 10","A R U — 3","An off-target glycan and a negative-control glycan chosen in advance \"to ensure Galectin-3 doesn't bind indiscriminately\", with no-template controls on every assembly gel"],["UCNZ","Undergrad","Top 10","A U — 2","A substrate-only reference on the sugar-release assay and several published failures; no exclusion experiment, and no instance of the phrase \"negative control\" anywhere we could read"],["UOttawa","Undergrad","Top 10","A R D H U — 5","A lock that \"tests the branch that was chosen against data withheld until the choice was made\", and a retrieval audit that \"cannot rule out knowledge already encoded in the model's weights\""],["TU Delft","Overgrad","Grand Prize","A R D H U — 5","A scrambled-motif twin, RDG(-)-ELP, \"leaving the motif sequence as the main difference between them\", with every data row of one ELP kept on one side of the held-out split"],["WageningenUR","Overgrad","1st Runner-up","A R D U — 4","A no-enzyme control promoted to a reporting rule: \"Bars marked with an asterisk did not exceed the no-enzyme control and are shown uncorrected\", plus solvent-matched autofluorescence negatives"],["Athens","Overgrad","Top 10","R D U — 3","Every enzyme built twice, fused and bare, so \"any difference in activity is attributable to the peptide\"; the buffer-only arm is named on the page and not yet run"],["ETH-Zurich","Overgrad","Top 10","A R H U — 4","\"the absence of a difference between empty and Cre-loaded cages showed that free Cre does not generate false-positive reporter switching\", plus reporter-less control cells at every dose"],["GU Frankfurt","Overgrad","Top 10","A R D U — 4","A scrambled shRNA set as the 1.0 line on every knockdown figure, with two off-target alleles — one structurally similar, one distant — carried through protein and mRNA readouts"],["KAUST-KSA","Overgrad","Top 10","A R U — 3","Wild-type cells as the negative control under every UV dose, plus a one-at-a-time supplementation test that separated two simultaneous model bottlenecks; \"Knockouts do nothing\" published as a result"],["Marburg","Overgrad","Top 10","A R D U — 4","A no-RBS construct that \"defines the translation-independent background\" and a non-matching PPR on the same target; the control then exposed an unintended upstream ATG behind a happy result"],["Muenster-University","Overgrad","Top 10","A R U — 3","A protease-inhibitor arm that excluded environmental proteases, and a no-protease arm that cleaved anyway, so \"the screening method cannot work in procaryotic cells\""],["Toronto","Overgrad","Top 10","A R H U — 4","A biosensor-only arm run to see \"if any cells would fluoresce without PETase activity\", plus a benchmark the team declared circular and moved to a held-out set"],["UZurich","Overgrad","Top 10","A R H U — 4","Uninoculated medium and a wild-type comparison built to \"distinguish the effects of our modifications from its existing activity\", plus held-out landslide events with matched control dates"]],"rows_zh":[["Lambert-GA","高中組","總冠軍","A R H U — 4","下拉實驗設有只放 GFP 與只放奈米抗體的對照組，測試集依抗原群聚切分並檢查序列同源性，35 個設計中有 34 個以逐列方式公開為陰性結合判定"],["HongKong-JSS","高中組","第一亞軍","A R H U — 4","那組它承認忘記做的空載體與未轉形對照：「we forgot to include matching 0 µM samples, an empty-vector control and an untransformed E. coli control」——後來補上了，感測器也變弱了"],["Eton-College-UK","高中組","前十","A R D H U — 5","「Heated and unheated samples were also included to control for potential effects of sample preparation」，再加上以 out-of-fold 評分把保留的陽性樣本對上競爭蛋白酶"],["GCGS","高中組","前十","A R U — 3","做了一條生長曲線，讓報導基因訊號有可能被歸因於細胞密度：「fluorescence differences reflected genuine promoter activity instead of cell density artifacts」"],["GEMS-Taiwan","高中組","前十","A R D H U — 5","一張七組對照表，逐列寫明每一組排除了什麼；一組無配體受體模擬；以及一組未轉形宿主的 ELISA 對照，直接推翻了隊伍自己的表現量排序"],["GHCIS","高中組","前十","A U — 2","紙片試驗上的 0 µM 陰性對照，而它自己的顯色就成了結論：「color formation alone was insufficient for a reliable positive call」"],["HFI","高中組","前十","A R D U — 4","一組空白對照「ruling out the interference of lysine's own non-biological degradation」，再加上為了移除宿主自身離胺酸消耗而建的 ldcC 剔除底盤，並重新測試"],["HKSSC","高中組","前十","A D U — 3","「To rule out the stress caused by pelB, we removed the pelB sequence in cycle 3 as well」，以及每個對羥基苯甲酸酯劑量都設未誘導對照組"],["HangzhouFourteenAP","高中組","前十","A R D U — 4","逐孔扣掉熱去活酵素的讀值，再加上逐一抽掉單一酵素的缺項組；接著重量法讀值顯示沒有顯著差異，而他們照實寫了出來"],["HongKong-HS","高中組","前十","A U — 2","無細胞反應中設有「negative controls containing no plasmids」，以及一項公開的虛無結果：miR-21 候選在有無標的下沒有顯著差異"],["Stanford University","大學組","總冠軍","A R D U — 4","一條不針對任何標的的嚮導 RNA、錯配觸發對照組，以及讓每個條件都有 ADAR1 的設計「so that results were not confounded by lack of endogenous ADAR1 availability」"],["UCAS-China","大學組","第一亞軍","A R D H U — 5","用細胞計數反過來檢驗自家的螢光主張，「ruling out interference from differences in cell number」，再加上在三位捐贈者間輪替的留一捐贈者預測"],["Princeton","大學組","第二亞軍","A R D U — 4","「Each grid carries a phage-only row with no bacteria added … it rules out carryover growth, spontaneous resistance and contamination」，再加上分配、實驗、量測與分析四段盲法"],["Cornell","大學組","前十","R U — 2","把裂解液與沉澱分開跑，「to rule out the possibility that the protein aggregated and precipitated」；而缺少的 t~0 陰性對照就用括號寫在頁面上承認"],["Heidelberg","大學組","前十","A R D H U — 5","「Collapse the gas vesicles with pressure in the same field: same cells, no vesicles … This one control rules out density and slide differences at once」，再加上九個打亂序列的設計陰性對照"],["LYON","大學組","前十","A R D U — 4","用一個同樣大小的無活性蛋白取代煮沸酵素對照，因為後者形成的聚集物「played to much on the absorbance of theses wells」——換掉對照，再重跑 assay"],["NUS-Singapore","大學組","前十","A R D H U — 5","交叉活化測試抓到自家感測器在漏，再加上兩種驗證設計中較難的那一種：「an independent plate at a temperature held out of training entirely」"],["UAlberta","大學組","前十","A R U — 3","事先選定一個脫靶醣分子與一個陰性對照醣分子「to ensure Galectin-3 doesn't bind indiscriminately」，每張組裝膠片都附無模板對照"],["UCNZ","大學組","前十","A U — 2","糖釋放 assay 上有一組只放基質的參考組，也公開了幾項失敗；但沒有任何排除實驗，而我們讀得到的範圍內完全沒有「negative control」這個詞"],["UOttawa","大學組","前十","A R D H U — 5","一道鎖，「tests the branch that was chosen against data withheld until the choice was made」；以及一次檢索稽核，並承認「cannot rule out knowledge already encoded in the model's weights」"],["TU Delft","研究生組","總冠軍","A R D H U — 5","一個打亂 motif 的孿生構築體 RDG(-)-ELP，「leaving the motif sequence as the main difference between them」；而同一個 ELP 的所有資料列都被留在保留切分的同一側"],["WageningenUR","研究生組","第一亞軍","A R D U — 4","把無酵素對照升級成報告規則：「Bars marked with an asterisk did not exceed the no-enzyme control and are shown uncorrected」，再加上溶劑配對的自體螢光陰性對照"],["Athens","研究生組","前十","R D U — 3","每個酵素都做兩版，融合與裸酵素，於是「any difference in activity is attributable to the peptide」；而只放緩衝液的那一組被寫在頁面上，還沒做"],["ETH-Zurich","研究生組","前十","A R H U — 4","「the absence of a difference between empty and Cre-loaded cages showed that free Cre does not generate false-positive reporter switching」，再加上每個劑量都設沒有報導基因的對照細胞"],["GU Frankfurt","研究生組","前十","A R D U — 4","每張剔減圖都以打亂序列的 shRNA 作為 1.0 基準線，並帶著兩個脫靶對偶基因——一個結構相近、一個相遠——一路做到蛋白與 mRNA 讀值"],["KAUST-KSA","研究生組","前十","A R U — 3","每個 UV 劑量都以野生型細胞作為陰性對照，再加上逐一補充營養的測試，分離出兩個同時存在的模型瓶頸；並把「Knockouts do nothing」當成結果公開"],["Marburg","研究生組","前十","A R D U — 4","一個無 RBS 構築體「defines the translation-independent background」，以及一個不匹配的 PPR 打在同一個標的上；接著這組對照揭穿了一個令人開心的結果背後非預期的上游 ATG"],["Muenster-University","研究生組","前十","A R U — 3","一組加蛋白酶抑制劑的對照排除了環境蛋白酶，而沒加蛋白酶的那一組照樣被切開，於是「the screening method cannot work in procaryotic cells」"],["Toronto","研究生組","前十","A R H U — 4","一組只放生物感測器的對照，用來看「if any cells would fluoresce without PETase activity」；再加上一個被隊伍自己宣告為循環、並改用保留資料重做的基準測試"],["UZurich","研究生組","前十","A R H U — 4","未接菌的培養基，加上一組野生型比較，用來「distinguish the effects of our modifications from its existing activity」；再加上保留的山崩事件與配對的對照日期"]]},"checklist":["Write the rival explanation down before you run the assay. One sentence, in the protocol: if this result is real, what else could have produced it? GEMS-Taiwan 2024 wrote \"We want to rule out the effect of E. coli in the death of mosquito larvae\" and the whole control followed from it.","Put a no-activity arm on the headline assay itself, not only on a cloning gel. Empty vector, untransformed host, heat-killed enzyme, substrate alone — whichever makes your own number impossible. Twenty-eight of 30 Top 10 teams did this, so a wiki without it stands out.","Build the rival-exclusion arm into the same plate, same day, same operator. Heidelberg collapses its vesicles in the same field with the same cells, which is why one control rules out density and slide differences at once.","Remove one confound by design and then re-test the effect. Cover the wells with black paper, scramble the motif instead of deleting it, swap in an inactive protein of the same size. Only 17 of 30 did this, and it is where the podium teams pull ahead.","Hold data back from your own fitting before you look at it, and say which rows you held. Twelve of 30 did; name the split rule, as TU Delft does by keeping every row of one ELP on one side of it.","Check your benchmark is not built from the thing it is testing. Toronto found its own HMMs were validated on the search that produced them and moved the test to a held-out set: a benchmark has to be independent of what the model was built from.","When a control defeats your measurement, publish the table and say what can no longer be concluded. GEMS-Taiwan 2026 printed an ELISA whose untransformed host read the same as its constructs, and wrote that no difference there can be attributed to expression.","Name the arm you could not run, and what it would have settled. Every podium team does this; Athens does it best. \"Until it is run we describe the effect as attributable to the preparation\" costs you nothing and is the clearest evidence a judge has that you know what your data does not show.","Never conclude a string is absent from a wiki because your extraction did not find it. Italicised species names and gene symbols drop out of client-rendered bundles, so check the rendered page before you retract a finding."],"checklist_zh":["在做 assay 之前，先把競爭解釋寫下來。在 protocol 裡寫一句話：如果這個結果是真的，還有什麼別的東西能產生它？GEMS-Taiwan 2024 寫下「We want to rule out the effect of E. coli in the death of mosquito larvae」，整組對照就是從這句話長出來的。","把無活性對照放在主要 assay 本身，而不是只放在選殖用的膠片上。空載體、未轉形宿主、熱殺死的酵素、只放基質——哪一種能讓你自己的數字變成不可能，就用哪一種。30 支 Top 10 團隊裡有 28 支做了，所以沒做的 wiki 會很顯眼。","把排除競爭解釋的那一組，排進同一塊盤、同一天、同一位操作者。Heidelberg 就是在同一個視野、用同一批細胞把氣囊壓破，所以那一組對照能同時排除密度與玻片差異。","用設計移除一個混淆因子，然後把效應重測一次。用黑紙蓋住孔洞、把 motif 打亂而不是刪掉、換成同樣大小的無活性蛋白。30 支裡只有 17 支做了，而這正是獎台隊伍拉開距離的地方。","在看資料之前，先把一部分從自己的擬合裡留下來，並寫明你留了哪些列。30 支裡有 12 支做了；請指明切分規則，像 TU Delft 那樣把同一個 ELP 的所有資料列都留在同一側。","檢查你的基準測試，不是用它要測的東西做出來的。Toronto 發現自家的 HMM 是拿產生它們的那次搜尋來驗證，於是把測試改到保留資料上：基準測試必須獨立於模型建構時所用的東西。","當一組對照擊敗了你的量測，就把那張表登出來，並寫明哪些結論不能再下。GEMS-Taiwan 2026 把一張 ELISA 登了出來，其中未轉形宿主讀到和自家構築體同一範圍，並寫明那裡的差異不能歸因於表現量。","指名你沒能做的那一組，以及它本來能定案什麼。每一支獎台隊伍都做了這件事，Athens 做得最好。「Until it is run we describe the effect as attributable to the preparation」這句話對你毫無成本，卻是評審能看到的最清楚證據，證明你知道自己的資料沒有顯示什麼。","絕對不要因為自己的擷取程式沒找到某個字串，就斷定那個字串不在 wiki 上。斜體的物種名與基因符號會從前端渲染的打包檔裡掉出來，所以在撤回一項發現之前，先去看渲染後的頁面。"],"method":"Cohort: the 30 teams in the 2026 Top 10 across all three sections — High School, Undergrad and Overgrad — identified from research/results2026.json, with the seven podium places (three Grand Prizes, three 1st Runners-up, one 2nd Runner-up; the High School and Overgrad sections named no 2nd Runner-up) treated as one group against the remaining 23. The team JSON files in research/teams/ were used only for the wiki slug and the award list. They are not a valid source for this question: a falsification control is exactly the kind of thing a project summary omits, so every score comes from the wiki itself. How the wikis were read: curl with a browser User-Agent first, every time. Fourteen of the 30 are static or server-rendered and were crawled page by page over results, engineering, experiments, notebook, model, description, measurement, parts and contribution, resolving relative links against each page. Sixteen are client-rendered; for those we pulled the JavaScript bundles and extracted string literals, following lazy-loaded chunks by filename, which added between 0.9 and 3.3 MB of recovered text on seven teams and changed one team's score. TU Delft publishes Markdown versions of every page at llms.txt and those were read directly. Stanford University is a client-templated page whose text lives in fourteen separate content JavaScript files, fetched individually. All fetched HTML was HTML-unescaped before any pattern matching, because the less-than sign is written as an entity and a regex for a p-value finds nothing without it. Every match of every pattern was printed and read before any absence was recorded, and bare-word searches were not used: 'tested' is not a t-test. Scoring: five types, each credited only on a sentence we can quote from the team's own page. A, a chassis-only, empty-vector, untransformed, uninduced, heat-killed or no-enzyme arm on the headline assay rather than on a transformation plate or cloning gel. R, an experiment whose stated purpose was to exclude a named alternative cause of the team's own result. D, a confound removed by design — scrambled rather than deleted motifs, matched solvents, blinding, randomisation, an inactive protein of matched size — with the effect then re-tested. H, validation against data held back from fitting, with the split rule stated. U, a result unfavourable to the team's own headline claim, published. A sixth flag, not part of the five, records a team naming a specific arm, replicate or comparison it did not run together with what cannot be concluded without it. Judgement enters at the boundary of A and D, and at whether an arm sits on the headline assay or on a cloning step; a different scorer would move one or two teams by one category. The counts are A 28/30, R 26/30, D 17/30, H 12/30, U 30/30, sixth flag 23/30. What we could not see: figures and gel images (every score rests on text), work done and not written up, pages behind a login or published after the freeze, and anything in a PDF we did not open. One failure mode is worth recording because it nearly produced a false retraction in this analysis: italicised species names and gene symbols are dropped by bundle string extraction, so a sentence can appear truncated in the recovered text and complete on the rendered page. A string absent from an extraction is not a string absent from the wiki. Limits of n: 30 teams, 7 of them on a podium. The podium-versus-rest difference of 0.68 of one category has a one-sided permutation p of 0.079 over 200,000 shuffles, the High School comparison is two teams against eight, and three of the five scored types are saturated at 26/30 or above, which leaves the five-point scale almost no room to rank anybody. n = 30 cannot support a strong inference, and nothing here should be read as one. The honest reading is that the practice is a floor among decorated teams and not a ranking, and that the report's two-direction finding narrows to the real-target half.","method_zh":"Cohort：2026 年三個組別——高中組、大學組、研究生組——全部 30 支 Top 10 團隊，名單取自 research/results2026.json；七個獎台席次（三個總冠軍、三個第一亞軍、一個第二亞軍；高中組與研究生組沒有頒出第二亞軍）視為一組，與其餘 23 支對照。research/teams/ 裡的團隊 JSON 檔只用來取 wiki 網址與獎項清單。對這個問題，它們不是有效的資料來源：可否證性對照正是專案摘要最會省略的東西，所以每一個分數都來自 wiki 本身。怎麼讀這些 wiki：每一次都先用帶瀏覽器 User-Agent 的 curl。30 支中有 14 支是靜態或伺服器端渲染，逐頁爬過 results、engineering、experiments、notebook、model、description、measurement、parts 與 contribution，並把相對連結逐頁解析。另外 16 支是前端渲染；對這些我們抓下 JavaScript 打包檔並擷取字串常量，再依檔名追查延遲載入的分塊檔——這一步在七支隊伍上多還原了 0.9 MB 到 3.3 MB 的文字，並改變了其中一支的分數。TU Delft 在 llms.txt 公布每一頁的 Markdown 版本，我們直接讀那些。Stanford University 是前端套版頁面，文字分散在十四個 content JavaScript 檔裡，逐一抓取。所有抓下來的 HTML 都先做 HTML 反轉義再比對樣式，因為小於符號是以實體寫成，少了這一步，搜尋 p 值的正規表達式什麼都找不到。在記下任何「不存在」之前，每一條樣式的每一個命中都被印出來讀過；也不使用裸字搜尋：tested 不是 t 檢定。計分：五個類別，每一類都只憑一句能從團隊自家頁面逐字引用的話給分。A，主要 assay 上的宿主單獨組、空載體組、未轉形組、未誘導組、熱殺死組或無酵素組，而不是轉形平盤或選殖膠片上的對照。R，一個寫明目的就是要排除自家結果某個指名替代原因的實驗。D，用設計移除混淆因子——把 motif 打亂而非刪除、配對溶劑、盲法、隨機分配、同樣大小的無活性蛋白——並把效應重測一次。H，用從擬合中保留下來的資料驗證，並寫明切分規則。U，公開一項對自家主要主張不利的結果。第六個旗標不計入這五類，記錄的是團隊指名了某一組自己沒做的對照、重複或比較，並說明少了它就不能下什麼結論。判斷會進入兩個地方：A 與 D 的邊界，以及某一組對照究竟落在主要 assay 還是選殖步驟上；換一位評分者，大概會有一兩支隊伍上下移動一個類別。各類計數為 A 28/30、R 26/30、D 17/30、H 12/30、U 30/30，第六旗標 23/30。我們看不到的東西：圖與膠片影像（每一個分數都只建立在文字上）、做了但沒寫出來的工作、需要登入或在凍結後才發布的頁面，以及我們沒打開的 PDF 內容。有一種失誤值得記下來，因為它在這次分析中差點造成一次錯誤的撤回：斜體的物種名與基因符號會被打包檔字串擷取丟掉，所以一句話在還原文字裡看起來被截斷，在渲染後的頁面上卻是完整的。擷取結果裡沒有的字串，不等於 wiki 上沒有。n 的限制：30 支隊伍，其中 7 支在獎台上。獎台與其餘隊伍相差 0.68 個類別，在 200,000 次置換中單尾 p 為 0.079；高中組的比較是兩支對八支；而五個計分類別中有三個已飽和在 26/30 以上，使得這個五分制幾乎沒有空間排出任何名次。n = 30 撐不起強推論，這裡的任何一句話都不該被當成強推論讀。誠實的讀法是：在獲獎團隊之間，這個習慣是一道門檻而不是一張名次表；而本報告那項雙向發現，收斂到「量在真正的標的上」這一半。"},{"tab":"overview","kicker":"How to read this","kicker_zh":"怎麼讀這份報告","title":"Two questions, thirty teams","title_zh":"兩個問題，三十支團隊","lede":"This report asks the same two questions of every team it looks at.","lede_zh":"本報告對每一支團隊都問同樣的兩個問題。","body":"The first question is computational. Where does a project stop being wet biology and start being a model, a pipeline, a dataset, a piece of software? What did that layer actually decide — did it change an experiment, or was it decoration added after the fact? The teams that win are increasingly the ones where the answer is \"it changed the experiment\".\n\nThe second question is social. Who outside the team touched this project, and what did they change about it? A list of meetings is not integrated human practices. A design that is visibly different because somebody outside the lab said something is.\n\nThat second question is asked here in iGEM's terms because that is what the evidence is made of — but it is not what **Science for Good** means at GEMS. At GEMS it names a club-form programme with no competition deadline, carrying a few well-chosen problems across years rather than seasons: problems that matter to someone outside GEMS, that can actually be deployed, whose effect can be counted, and that get cheaper as they spread. The Science for Good tab sets out that definition, what is currently in the pipeline, and what the 2026 cohort's record says about which work survives a deadline and which does not.\n\nEverything else here — the trend tabs, the roadmap — exists to answer a third question that only GEMS Research can answer: given what 2026 looked like, what should a growing research institution in Taiwan be building in 2027 and beyond?","body_zh":"第一個問題關於運算。一個專案在哪裡不再只是濕實驗生物學，而開始成為模型、管線、資料集或軟體？這一層究竟決定了什麼——它改變了實驗，還是事後補上的裝飾？越來越多得獎團隊的答案是「它改變了實驗」。\n\n第二個問題關於社會。團隊之外有誰接觸過這個專案，而他們改變了什麼？列一串會議紀錄不是整合式人類實踐；因為實驗室外的某個人說了什麼，而讓設計明顯不同，才是。\n\n這第二個問題在這裡是用 iGEM 的語彙問的，因為證據本身就是那個形狀——但那並不是 GEMS 所說的 **Science for Good**。在 GEMS，它指的是一個沒有比賽截止日的社團式長期計畫，讓幾個挑選過的題目跨年而不是跨季地走下去：這些題目要對 GEMS 以外的人有意義、真的放得進某個地方、效果數得出來，而且推得越廣成本越低。Science for Good 那一頁寫出了這個定義、目前清單上有什麼，以及 2026 年這一屆的紀錄告訴我們：哪一種工作熬得過截止日，哪一種熬不過。\n\n其餘的部分——趨勢頁、路線圖——都是為了回答第三個只有 GEMS Research 能回答的問題：看過 2026 年的樣貌之後，一個在台灣成長中的研究機構，在 2027 年以後應該建造什麼？"},{"tab":"roadmap","kicker":"Premise","kicker_zh":"前提","title":"Why the dry lab is the roadmap","title_zh":"為什麼乾實驗室就是路線圖","lede":"GEMS Research is becoming an institution, not a team. Institutions are defined by what they can still do after the current students graduate.","lede_zh":"GEMS Research 正在從一支團隊成為一個機構。機構的定義，在於現在這批學生畢業之後，它還能做什麼。","body":"A wet lab is bounded by its benches, its reagents budget and the hours its students are physically present. A dry lab is bounded by what its people know and what they have written down. That asymmetry is the whole argument: computational capability compounds across years in a way that pipetting skill does not, because a model, a pipeline or a calibrated measurement protocol survives the student who built it.\n\nThis is also where the field has moved. Protein design, metabolic modelling and measurement standardisation are no longer the specialist corner of a project — in 2026 they are frequently the project. The teams on the 2026 podium did not win because they ran more gels.\n\nSo the roadmap below is deliberately about capability, not about any single 2027 project idea. Pick a phase and start.","body_zh":"濕實驗室受限於實驗檯、試劑預算，以及學生實際在場的時數。乾實驗室則受限於人員所知，以及他們寫下了什麼。這個不對稱就是整個論點：運算能力會跨年度累積，而移液技巧不會——因為一個模型、一條管線或一份校正過的量測流程，會比建造它的那位學生留得更久。\n\n這也是整個領域移動的方向。蛋白質設計、代謝建模與量測標準化不再是專案裡的專家角落；在 2026 年，它們經常就是專案本身。站上 2026 頒獎臺的團隊，不是因為多跑了幾道膠。\n\n因此以下的路線圖刻意談能力，而不是任何單一的 2027 專案構想。挑一個階段，開始做。"},{"tab":"roadmap","kicker":"The convergence","kicker_zh":"兩條線的交會","title":"Two independent analyses, one answer","title_zh":"兩份獨立分析，同一個答案","lede":"The academic trend review and the industry trend review were run separately, from different sources, with no knowledge of each other. They landed on the same white space.","lede_zh":"學術趨勢分析與產業趨勢分析分開進行、來源不同、彼此互不知情。它們指向了同一塊空白地帶。","body":"From the literature side: light has matured from a laboratory curiosity into a real-time actuator for closed-loop control of fermentation, with reported titre gains around 60% in a 1 L photobioreactor — and optogenetics in **Bacillus subtilis** is a twelve-paper literature in the whole of PubMed.\n\nFrom the industry side, reached by an entirely different route: optogenetics is becoming the control and cleaning layer of bioprocessing, because light lets you retrofit an existing steel fermenter instead of building a new one. That makes it the cheapest route past the capital-expenditure wall that is currently the binding constraint on biomanufacturing.\n\nGEMS Research already stands in that gap. ReLEAF was a CcaS/CcaR optogenetic circuit in *Bacillus subtilis* driving a bioreactor, and it won Best Measurement and Best Hardware at high-school level for exactly the instrumentation this line needs. The competition project is over; the research line it opened is not.\n\nThere is a second, blunter finding underneath this. Taiwan's state-backed biotechnology push is a manufacturing play — contract development and manufacturing, GMP capacity — with no visible synthetic-biology **design** layer, while Singapore and Israel are explicitly funding exactly that layer. A small institution cannot out-build a CDMO. It can occupy the design position that nobody in Taiwan currently holds.","body_zh":"從文獻端看：光已經從實驗室的新奇玩意，成熟為可即時操控發酵的閉迴路致動器，1 公升光生物反應器中回報約 60% 的效價提升——而**枯草桿菌（Bacillus subtilis）**的光遺傳學，在整個 PubMed 中只有十二篇文獻。\n\n從產業端看，循著完全不同的路徑：光正在成為生物製程的控制與清潔層，因為光讓你可以改裝既有的不鏽鋼發酵槽，而不必蓋一座新的。這使它成為繞過資本支出高牆最便宜的路徑——而資本支出正是當前生物製造的關鍵瓶頸。\n\nGEMS Research 已經站在這個缺口上。ReLEAF 本來就是在*枯草桿菌*中以 CcaS/CcaR 光遺傳電路驅動生物反應器，並且正是憑著這條路線所需要的儀器化能力，在高中組拿下最佳量測與最佳硬體。競賽專案結束了，它打開的研究路線沒有。\n\n底下還有第二個更直白的發現。台灣由國家支持的生技推動是製造導向的——委託開發製造、GMP 產能——看不到合成生物學的**設計**層；而新加坡與以色列正明確地投資的，正是這一層。一個小型機構無法在產能上贏過 CDMO，但它可以佔住台灣目前沒有人佔住的設計位置。"},{"id":"award-economics","tab":"judging","order":50,"kicker":"What a category measures","kicker_zh":"一個類別在量什麼","title":"Seventeen categories, four of them close to a whole-project verdict, and the circularity in saying so","title_zh":"十七個類別，其中四個接近整體專案的判決，以及這麼說本身的循環問題","lede":"Across 2024-26 these 17 special categories nominate between 3 and 26 teams a season and co-occur with a Top 10 place at rates running from **60% down to 0%**. Best Wiki nominates 26 teams, nine of them high-school every single season, and **49 of 81 pooled nominees (60%) also placed Top 10**; Safety and Security, Best Alternative Platform and Best New Improved Part nominate a handful and **0 of 9, 0 of 4 and 0 of 3** of theirs ever did. The caveat belongs in the same breath as the number: this is co-occurrence, it is close to circular, and the circularity is structural — Best Wiki and Best Presentation are assessed on how the whole project is *communicated*, which is the same material a Top 10 judgement is working on. As a prediction the column is worth nothing. As a map of **which categories function as a proxy for a whole-project verdict and which certify one isolated dimension**, it explains something this report already published: GEMS won three 2026 category awards and missed the finalist slate, and those three sit at **45%, 22% and 21%**.","lede_zh":"在 2024 至 2026 三個賽季中，這 17 個特別獎類別每季入圍隊數從 3 支到 26 支不等，而與 Top 10 同時發生的比率從 **60% 一路落到 0%**。Best Wiki 入圍 26 支隊伍，其中每一季都剛好有九支來自高中組，而**三季合計 81 個入圍名額中，有 49 個（60%）同時也拿到 Top 10**；Safety and Security、Best Alternative Platform 與 Best New Improved Part 只入圍少數幾支，而它們的入圍者**分別是 9 取 0、4 取 0、3 取 0**，從未有人同時進榜。警告必須與數字同時說出：這是同時發生，不是因果，而且接近循環論證，循環還是結構性的——Best Wiki 與 Best Presentation 評的是整個專案如何被*傳達*，而那正是 Top 10 評審所處理的同一批材料。當作預測，這一欄一文不值。但當作一張地圖，標出**哪些類別實質上是整體專案判決的替身，哪些只認證單一孤立面向**，它就解釋了本報告已經發表過的一件事：GEMS 在 2026 年贏下三個類別獎卻沒有進入決賽名單，而那三個獎分別落在 **45%、22% 與 21%**。","body":"Seventeen special award categories appear in the 2026 results. They are not comparable instruments. In 2026 Best Wiki and Best Presentation each nominated 26 teams and crowned 4; Best Model nominated 15; nine categories nominated between 10 and 12; Best Software and the Inclusivity Award nominated 6; Best Alternative Platform nominated 4, Safety and Security 3, and Best New Improved Part nominated nobody at all and still named 2 winners. A nomination means a different thing in each column, and so does its absence.\n\nPooled across the three seasons, **198 of 550 nominations (36%)** in these categories went to a team that also took a Top 10 place, against **89 of 155 outright wins (57%)**. The per-category spread is the finding: Best Wiki 49 of 81 (60%), Best Presentation 42 of 79 (53%), Best Model 20 of 40 (50%) and Integrated Human Practices 17 of 38 (45%) at the top; Best New Basic Part 3 of 35 (9%), Sustainable Development Impact 3 of 30 (10%) and the Inclusivity Award 2 of 16 (12%) near the bottom; and zero across all three seasons for Safety and Security (0/9), Best Alternative Platform (0/4) and Best New Improved Part (0/3).\n\nThe number has to be handled rather than ranked. It is co-occurrence and it is close to circular. A project strong enough to attract a Best Wiki nomination is usually strong enough to place Top 10, and the nomination plainly did not cause the place. Worse than ordinary confounding, the overlap is partly definitional: Best Wiki and Best Presentation are assessed on how the whole project is communicated, which is the same faculty a Top 10 judgement exercises on the same material. So the column cannot predict anything. What it can do is sort the 17 categories into those that function as a proxy for a whole-project verdict and those that certify one isolated dimension — and that sorting is stable across three seasons, which a coincidence would have to work to achieve.\n\nThe sorting matches something this report has already published. GEMS-Taiwan won three 2026 category awards and did not make the finalist slate; the three sit at 45% (Integrated Human Practices), 22% (Measurement) and 21% (Hardware) — one at the proxy end, two below the 36% pooled baseline. The section's 1st Runner-up, HongKong-JSS, collected four special citations and **won no category outright at all**. Categories are judged one dimension at a time by a panel asking a narrow question; finalist selection asks whether the project holds together, and the 2026 high-school results show every combination of the two.\n\nHigh-school slate sizes are remarkably fixed. Best Wiki and Best Presentation each gave the section 9 nominee slots in 2024, 9 in 2025 and 9 in 2026; Best Model, Best Education and Integrated Human Practices gave 4, 4 and 4. Across all 17 categories the section had 74 citation slots in 2024, 80 in 2025 and 82 in 2026, spread over 37, 40 and 45 distinct teams out of 128, 143 and 147 accepted — **fewer than a third of high-school teams are cited at all in any season**. GEMS held 5 of 74, 4 of 80 and 5 of 82, and was the most-cited high-school team in the 2026 section.\n\nThe nine categories GEMS has never been cited in across three seasons do not share a cause. Four of them barely exist for high-school teams: Best Alternative Platform offered the section 0, 0 and 1 nominee slots, Best Software 0, 1 and 1, Safety and Security 0, 1 and 0, Best New Improved Part 2, 0 and 0. The other five are ordinarily sized — Best Part Collection, Best New Composite Part, Best Entrepreneurship and Sustainable Development Impact each gave high-school teams 13 pooled nominations over three seasons, the same order as categories GEMS does hold — and three of those five are parts awards, in a line GEMS has already won once, with Best New Basic Part in 2024. The blanks that can be filled are mostly documentation and curation work; the blanks that cannot are the section's, not the team's. Neither sort is a route to the finalist slate, since Part Collection sits at 35%, New Composite Part at 34%, Entrepreneurship at 29% and Sustainable Development Impact at 10%.","body_zh":"2026 年的成績裡出現了 17 個特別獎類別，而它們並不是可以互相比較的量具。2026 年 Best Wiki 與 Best Presentation 各入圍 26 支隊伍、各頒出 4 個獎；Best Model 入圍 15 支；九個類別入圍 10 到 12 支；Best Software 與 Inclusivity Award 入圍 6 支；Best Alternative Platform 入圍 4 支、Safety and Security 入圍 3 支；而 Best New Improved Part 完全沒有入圍任何一支，卻仍然頒出 2 個獎。同樣一個「入圍」，在每一欄裡的意思都不一樣，「沒有入圍」也一樣。\n\n三季合併計算，這些類別的 **550 個入圍名額中有 198 個（36%）**落在同時拿到 Top 10 的隊伍身上，而**獲獎的 155 個名額中有 89 個（57%）**如此。真正的發現在於各類別之間的落差：高端是 Best Wiki 的 81 取 49（60%）、Best Presentation 的 79 取 42（53%）、Best Model 的 40 取 20（50%）與 Best Integrated Human Practices 的 38 取 17（45%）；低端接近底部的是 Best New Basic Part 的 35 取 3（9%）、Best Sustainable Development Impact 的 30 取 3（10%）與 Inclusivity Award 的 16 取 2（12%）；而 Safety and Security（9 取 0）、Best Alternative Platform（4 取 0）與 Best New Improved Part（3 取 0）三季合計都是零。\n\n這個數字需要被處理，而不是被排名。它是同時發生，而且接近循環論證。一個強到足以獲得 Best Wiki 入圍的專案，通常也強到足以進 Top 10，而入圍顯然不是名次的原因。比一般的混淆更麻煩的是，這個重疊有一部分來自定義本身：Best Wiki 與 Best Presentation 評的是整個專案如何被傳達，而那正是 Top 10 評審在同一批材料上動用的同一種判斷。所以這一欄無法預測任何事。它能做的是把 17 個類別分成兩堆：一堆實質上是整體專案判決的替身，另一堆只認證單一孤立面向。而這個分法在三季之間是穩定的——若純屬巧合，巧合得相當費力。\n\n這個分法對上了本報告已經發表過的一件事。GEMS-Taiwan 在 2026 年贏下三個類別獎，卻沒有進入決賽名單；那三個獎分別落在 45%（Best Integrated Human Practices）、22%（Best Measurement）與 21%（Best Hardware）——一個在替身那一端，兩個低於 36% 的整體基準。而本組的亞軍 HongKong-JSS 累積了四項特別獎列名，**卻一個類別獎都沒有贏下**。類別獎是由一個問著狹窄問題的評審組，一次評一個面向；決賽遴選問的則是這個專案是否撐得起來。2026 年高中組的成績把這兩者的所有組合都演了一遍。\n\n高中組的入圍名額數量穩定得驚人。Best Wiki 與 Best Presentation 在 2024、2025、2026 各給本組 9、9、9 個入圍名額；Best Model、Best Education 與 Best Integrated Human Practices 給的是 4、4、4。17 個類別合計，本組在 2024 年有 74 個列名名額、2025 年 80 個、2026 年 82 個，分散在 37、40、45 支不同隊伍身上，而三年各有 128、143、147 支高中隊伍獲准參賽——**任何一季都有不到三分之一的高中隊伍得到任何列名**。GEMS 分別占住 74 取 5、80 取 4、82 取 5，並且是 2026 年高中組被列名次數最多的隊伍。\n\nGEMS 三季從未被列名的九個類別並沒有共同原因。其中四個對高中組而言幾乎不存在：Best Alternative Platform 三季給本組的入圍名額是 0、0、1，Best Software 是 0、1、1，Safety and Security 是 0、1、0，Best New Improved Part 是 2、0、0。另外五個則是正常大小——Best Part Collection、Best New Composite Part、Best Entrepreneurship 與 Best Sustainable Development Impact 三季各給高中組 13 個入圍名額，與 GEMS 確實持有的那些類別同一個量級——而這五個裡有三個是元件獎，屬於 GEMS 已經贏過一次的那一條線：2024 年的 Best New Basic Part。可以填的空白，多半是文件與整理的工作；填不了的空白，是整個高中組的，不是這支隊伍的。但兩種都不是通往決賽名單的路，因為 Part Collection 只有 35%、New Composite Part 34%、Entrepreneurship 29%、Sustainable Development Impact 10%。","cards":[{"kicker":"The spread","kicker_zh":"落差","title":"From 60% to 0%, and the number is almost circular","title_zh":"從 60% 到 0%，而這個數字幾乎是循環論證","body":"Pooled over 2024-26, 198 of 550 nominations in these 17 categories went to a team that also placed Top 10 — 36% overall. The per-category figures run from Best Wiki's 49 of 81 (60%) and Best Presentation's 42 of 79 (53%) down to three categories where it has never happened once: Safety and Security 0 of 9, Best Alternative Platform 0 of 4, Best New Improved Part 0 of 3.\n\nThe honest reading has to arrive with the number rather than after it. This is co-occurrence, not causation, and it is close to circular. Nobody takes a Top 10 place because they were nominated for Best Wiki; a project good enough to attract one is usually good enough to attract the other. And Best Wiki and Best Presentation are explicitly assessed on how the whole project is communicated, which is the same faculty a Top 10 judgement is exercising on the same wiki and the same twenty minutes. Part of the correlation is a definition, not a result.\n\nSo the ranking is worthless as a prediction and useful as a description: it says which categories are being judged on the whole project and which on one isolated dimension.","body_zh":"2024 至 2026 三季合計，這 17 個類別的 550 個入圍名額中，有 198 個落在同時進入 Top 10 的隊伍身上——整體 36%。各類別的數字從 Best Wiki 的 81 取 49（60%）與 Best Presentation 的 79 取 42（53%），一路落到三個從未發生過一次的類別：Safety and Security 9 取 0、Best Alternative Platform 4 取 0、Best New Improved Part 3 取 0。\n\n誠實的讀法必須與數字一起出現，而不是跟在後面。這是同時發生，不是因果，而且接近循環論證。沒有人是因為獲得 Best Wiki 入圍才拿到 Top 10；一個好到足以取得其中一項的專案，通常也好到足以取得另一項。而 Best Wiki 與 Best Presentation 明確評的是整個專案如何被傳達，那正是 Top 10 評審在同一個 wiki、同一段二十分鐘上所動用的同一種判斷。這份相關性有一部分是定義，不是結果。\n\n因此，這個排名作為預測一文不值，作為描述卻很有用：它說出哪些類別實際上是在評整個專案，哪些只在評單一孤立面向。","chips":["36% overall (198/550)","60% top, 0% bottom","Co-occurrence, not cause"],"chips_zh":["整體 36%（550 取 198）","最高 60%，最低 0%","同時發生，非因果"]},{"kicker":"GEMS 2026","kicker_zh":"GEMS 2026","title":"Two of the three awards GEMS won sit below the pooled baseline","title_zh":"GEMS 贏下的三個獎，有兩個低於整體基準","body":"GEMS-Taiwan's three 2026 wins land at Best Integrated Human Practices 45% (17/38), Best Measurement 22% (7/32) and Best Hardware 21% (6/29), against a pooled baseline of 36% (198/550). One is at the whole-project-proxy end; two are roughly half the baseline. In the two categories above 50% — Best Wiki 60% and Best Presentation 53% — GEMS was nominated and won neither.\n\nRead structurally rather than as a scoreboard, that is the shape of a team certified on three narrow dimensions and not on the whole. Each of the three panels was asked one question about ReLEAF: is the measurement sound, is the hardware good, is the human practices work integrated. **None of them was asked whether the parts belong to one working system**, and the finalist judgement that does ask it did not select the team. That is not a reinterpretation of the award record; it is what the award record is for.","body_zh":"GEMS-Taiwan 2026 年的三個獎分別落在 Best Integrated Human Practices 的 45%（38 取 17）、Best Measurement 的 22%（32 取 7）與 Best Hardware 的 21%（29 取 6），而整體基準是 36%（550 取 198）。一個在整體專案替身那一端；兩個大約只有基準的一半。至於超過 50% 的兩個類別——Best Wiki 的 60% 與 Best Presentation 的 53%——GEMS 都入圍，但都沒有贏。\n\n若把它當成結構而不是計分板來讀，這就是一支「在三個狹窄面向上獲得認證、在整體上沒有」的隊伍的形狀。那三個評審組各被問了關於 ReLEAF 的一個問題：量測是否紮實、硬體是否優良、人文實踐是否整合。**沒有任何一組被問到這些零件是否屬於同一個能運作的系統**，而真正會問這個問題的決賽評審，沒有選上這支隊伍。這不是對獎項紀錄的重新解讀，這正是獎項紀錄本來的用途。","chips":["IHP 45%","Measurement 22%","Hardware 21%"],"chips_zh":["IHP 45%","Measurement 22%","Hardware 21%"]},{"kicker":"Wiki and Presentation","kicker_zh":"Wiki 與 Presentation","title":"GEMS was nominated in both top categories in 2026 and did place Top 10 — the co-occurrence held, the conversion did not","title_zh":"GEMS 2026 年在兩個最高類別都入圍，也確實進了 Top 10——同時發生成立了，轉換沒有","body":"This is the point where the easy story has to be refused. The 60% and 53% figures are about co-occurrence with a Top 10 place, and **GEMS satisfied them**: it placed Top 10 in 2024, 2025 and 2026. The nomination did not fail to co-occur. What it did not become is the category win — high-school Best Wiki 2026 went to Lambert-GA and Best Presentation to NFLSHS-CHINA — or a finalist slot.\n\nAnd a nomination is not a near-miss. Best Wiki nominates 26 and crowns 4; the slate is a long list, not a shortlist, and the public record contains no ordering inside it. Nothing here can distinguish second place from twenty-sixth, and no ballot is published.\n\nOne observation is worth making and it is weak. In 2024 GEMS won Best Wiki outright, and 2024 is also the season it won the high-school Grand Prize — the one season in which the whole-project-proxy category and the whole-project prize pointed at the same team. In 2026 it converted three single-dimension categories and neither proxy. **That is two seasons, one data point each, and it cannot carry a mechanism** — it is recorded because it is the direction the rest of this block predicts, not because the record confirms it.","body_zh":"這裡正是必須拒絕那個好聽故事的地方。60% 與 53% 這兩個數字講的是與 Top 10 的同時發生，而 **GEMS 滿足了它們**：它在 2024、2025、2026 三季都進了 Top 10。入圍並沒有「沒有同時發生」。它沒有變成的是類別獎本身——2026 年高中組的 Best Wiki 由 Lambert-GA 拿下，Best Presentation 由 NFLSHS-CHINA 拿下——也沒有變成決賽席次。\n\n而且，入圍不等於「差一點」。Best Wiki 入圍 26 支、頒出 4 個獎；那份名單是一份長名單，不是決選名單，而公開紀錄裡沒有名單內部的排序。這裡的資料無法區分第二名與第二十六名，也沒有任何票選結果公開。\n\n有一項觀察值得說，但它很弱。2024 年 GEMS 贏下 Best Wiki，而 2024 也正是它贏下高中組總冠軍的那一季——那是唯一一季，整體專案替身類別與整體專案大獎指向同一支隊伍。2026 年它轉換了三個單一面向類別，兩個替身類別都沒有。**這是兩季、各一個資料點，撐不起任何機制**——它被記下來，是因為它是本段其餘內容所預測的方向，而不是因為紀錄證實了它。","chips":["Top 10 in all 3 seasons","26 nominated, 4 win","2024: Wiki win + Grand Prize"],"chips_zh":["三季都進 Top 10","入圍 26 支，獲獎 4 支","2024：Wiki 獲獎＋總冠軍"]},{"kicker":"Slate stability","kicker_zh":"名額穩定度","title":"Five categories gave high-school teams exactly the same number of nominee slots three years running","title_zh":"五個類別連續三年給高中組完全相同的入圍名額","body":"Best Wiki 9/9/9, Best Presentation 9/9/9, Best Model 4/4/4, Best Education 4/4/4, Best Integrated Human Practices 4/4/4. The rest move by one slot at most, except where a category empties out. Whatever the allocation rule is, it is not being re-derived each season.\n\nThat fixes the size of the opportunity. Across all 17 categories the high-school section had 74 citation slots in 2024, 80 in 2025 and 82 in 2026 (nominees plus winners), spread over 37, 40 and 45 distinct teams out of 128, 143 and 147 accepted. **About three in ten high-school teams are cited at all; the other seven leave with a medal at best** — 135 of the 147 accepted high-school teams took a medal in 2026 and 12 took nothing.\n\nGEMS held 5 of 74 in 2024, 4 of 80 in 2025 and 5 of 82 in 2026 — the most-cited high-school team in the 2026 section, and tied at the top in 2024. The practical implication is uncomfortable: the team is already at or near the citation ceiling its section offers, so a sixth citation is not the available move. Twice now it has been at that ceiling, and in 2026 that produced no finalist slot.","body_zh":"Best Wiki 是 9/9/9、Best Presentation 9/9/9、Best Model 4/4/4、Best Education 4/4/4、Best Integrated Human Practices 4/4/4。其餘類別最多只動一個名額，除了整個類別被清空的情況。不論分配規則是什麼，它顯然不是每一季重新推導一次的。\n\n這也就固定了機會的大小。17 個類別合計，高中組在 2024 年有 74 個列名名額、2025 年 80 個、2026 年 82 個（入圍加獲獎），分散在 37、40、45 支不同隊伍身上，而三年各有 128、143、147 支隊伍獲准參賽。**大約每十支高中隊伍有三支會得到任何列名；另外七支最多只帶走一面獎牌**——2026 年 147 支獲准參賽的高中隊伍中，135 支拿到獎牌，12 支什麼都沒有。\n\nGEMS 在 2024 年占住 74 取 5、2025 年 80 取 4、2026 年 82 取 5——是 2026 年高中組被列名最多的隊伍，2024 年也並列最高。實際的含意並不舒服：這支隊伍已經在本組所能提供的列名上限附近，因此「再多一個列名」不是可用的招。它已經兩次站在那個上限上，而 2026 年那並沒有換到決賽席次。","chips":["5 categories constant","82 HS slots, 45 teams","GEMS 5 of 82"],"chips_zh":["五個類別三季不變","高中組 82 個名額、45 支隊伍","GEMS 占 82 取 5"]},{"kicker":"The nine blanks","kicker_zh":"九個空白","title":"Four of the nine categories GEMS has never been cited in barely exist for high-school teams","title_zh":"GEMS 從未列名的九個類別裡，有四個對高中組而言幾乎不存在","body":"The nine are Best New Composite Part, Best New Improved Part, Best Part Collection, Best Alternative Platform, Best Software, the Inclusivity Award, the Safety and Security Award, Best Sustainable Development Impact and Best Entrepreneurship. They do not form one group and should not be read as one list of failures.\n\n**Four are structurally thin for the section.** Best Alternative Platform gave high-school teams 0, 0 and 1 nominee slots across the three seasons; Best Software 0, 1 and 1; the Safety and Security Award 0, 1 and 0; Best New Improved Part 2, 0 and 0. That is four categories offering the entire high-school section between one and two nominations in three years. An absence there is the section's, not GEMS's, and chasing one would be chasing a slot that mostly is not issued.\n\n**Five are ordinarily sized and genuinely unoccupied.** Best Part Collection, Best New Composite Part, Best Entrepreneurship and Best Sustainable Development Impact each gave high-school teams 13 pooled nominations over three seasons — the same order as Best Measurement (11) and Best Hardware (12), which GEMS now wins. Three of the five are parts awards, and GEMS has already won in that line once with Best New Basic Part in 2024, so the route is demonstrably open. These blanks are curation and documentation work, not a structural barrier.\n\nWhat neither sort offers is a route to the finalist slate, because the reachable five sit at the low end of the co-occurrence column: Part Collection 35%, New Composite Part 34%, Entrepreneurship 29%, Sustainable Development Impact 10%.","body_zh":"這九個是 Best New Composite Part、Best New Improved Part、Best Part Collection、Best Alternative Platform、Best Software、Inclusivity Award、Safety and Security Award、Best Sustainable Development Impact 與 Best Entrepreneurship。它們不構成一個群體，也不該當成一份失敗清單來讀。\n\n**其中四個對高中組是結構性稀薄的。**Best Alternative Platform 三季給高中組的入圍名額是 0、0、1；Best Software 是 0、1、1；Safety and Security Award 是 0、1、0；Best New Improved Part 是 2、0、0。也就是說，這四個類別三年來總共只給整個高中組一到兩個入圍名額。這裡的空白是整個高中組的，不是 GEMS 的；去追其中任何一個，等於在追一個多半根本不會發出的名額。\n\n**另外五個大小正常，而且確實空著。**Best Part Collection、Best New Composite Part、Best Entrepreneurship 與 Best Sustainable Development Impact 三季各給高中組 13 個入圍名額——與 GEMS 如今會贏的 Best Measurement（11 個）和 Best Hardware（12 個）同一個量級。五個裡有三個是元件獎，而 GEMS 已經在這條線上贏過一次：2024 年的 Best New Basic Part，可見這條路確實是開著的。這些空白是整理與文件的工作，不是結構性的障礙。\n\n但兩種空白都不提供通往決賽名單的路，因為那可及的五個都落在同時發生比率的低端：Part Collection 35%、New Composite Part 34%、Entrepreneurship 29%、Sustainable Development Impact 10%。","chips":["4 near-empty for HS","Parts route open (2024 win)","Reachable five: 35% to 10%"],"chips_zh":["四個對高中組近乎空的","元件路已開（2024 獲獎）","可及的五個：35% 到 10%"]},{"kicker":"Nominee against winner","kicker_zh":"入圍與獲獎","title":"Winning a category co-occurs with Top 10 far more than being nominated for it","title_zh":"贏下一個類別與 Top 10 的同時發生率，遠高於只是入圍","body":"Pooled across the three seasons, **89 of 155 winners (57%)** also placed Top 10 against **198 of 550 nominees (36%)**. The gap holds inside almost every category: Best Wiki 10 of 12 winners (83%) against 60% of nominees, Best Part Collection 9 of 10 (90%) against 35%, Best Alternative Platform 2 of 3 (67%) against 0 of 4.\n\nTwo readings fit this and the data cannot separate them. Either the winner really is the stronger project and the nominee slate is a wide net, or winners and Top 10 places are drawn from the same small set of teams that judges across panels happen to remember. **Both readings are consistent with every number above**, which is a limit of this evidence and not a subtlety to be resolved by argument.\n\nThe operational consequence is the same either way: nominations and wins must be counted separately and never added. A season summary that reports a citation total hides which half of the 57/36 split the team is on.","body_zh":"三季合併，**獲獎的 155 個名額中有 89 個（57%）**同時進入 Top 10，而**入圍的 550 個名額中只有 198 個（36%）**。這個落差在幾乎每個類別內部都成立：Best Wiki 的獲獎者 12 取 10（83%），對入圍者的 60%；Best Part Collection 獲獎者 10 取 9（90%），對 35%；Best Alternative Platform 獲獎者 3 取 2（67%），對入圍者的 4 取 0。\n\n有兩種讀法都說得通，而資料無法分開它們。一是獲獎者確實是更強的專案，而入圍名單只是一張撒得很寬的網；二是獲獎與 Top 10 都是從同一小群「跨評審組都剛好記得的隊伍」裡抽出來的。**兩種讀法都與上面每一個數字相容**，這是本證據的極限，不是靠論述就能解決的細節。\n\n不論哪一種，實務後果都一樣：入圍與獲獎必須分開計算，絕不能相加。一份只報「列名總數」的賽季總結，會藏起這支隊伍落在 57 比 36 這道落差的哪一邊。","chips":["Winners 57% (89/155)","Nominees 36% (198/550)","Two readings fit"],"chips_zh":["獲獎 57%（155 取 89）","入圍 36%（550 取 198）","兩種讀法都相容"]},{"kicker":"The counter-example","kicker_zh":"反例","title":"The 1st Runner-up won no category at all, and the team with three wins was not a finalist","title_zh":"亞軍一個類別獎都沒拿，而拿下三個類別獎的那支不是決賽隊伍","body":"In the 2026 high-school section the numbers come apart cleanly. HongKong-JSS collected 4 special citations and **not one outright win**, and finished 1st Runner-up. GEMS-Taiwan collected 5 citations including 3 wins and was not named a finalist. Lambert-GA had 4 citations, 3 wins and the Grand Prize. Three teams, three different relationships between category hardware and the podium.\n\nThat is the clearest available statement that the two judgements are not the same instrument, and it is also the clearest statement of the limit on all of this: with ten teams in the Top 10 and two finalist slots, any pattern across them is fragile, and one team moving would change the picture. The block reports the shape of the counter-example, not a trend in it. Only 2 of the 10 high-school Top 10 teams were named finalists at all, which is the base rate every claim here is competing against.","body_zh":"在 2026 年高中組，這些數字分得相當乾淨。HongKong-JSS 累積了 4 項特別獎列名，**一個類別獎都沒有贏下**，最後拿到亞軍。GEMS-Taiwan 累積了 5 項列名、其中 3 項是獲獎，卻沒有被列為決賽隊伍。Lambert-GA 有 4 項列名、3 項獲獎，以及總冠軍。三支隊伍，在「類別獎的數量」與「頒獎臺」之間呈現三種不同的關係。\n\n這是手上最清楚的一項說明，指出這兩種判決並不是同一具量具；它同時也是最清楚的一項限制說明：Top 10 只有十支隊伍、決賽席次只有兩個，任何橫跨它們的模式都很脆弱，只要一支隊伍換位置，整張圖就會變。本段報告的是這個反例的形狀，不是其中的趨勢。十支高中組 Top 10 隊伍中，只有 2 支被列為決賽隊伍，而這就是這裡每一項主張都必須對抗的基礎比率。","chips":["JSS: 0 wins, 2nd place","GEMS: 3 wins, no slate","2 of 10 made finalist"],"chips_zh":["JSS：0 獲獎、亞軍","GEMS：3 獲獎、未入決賽","10 支中 2 支進決賽"]}],"table":{"head":["Award","2026 nominees","2026 winners","HS nominees 24/25/26","Nominees also Top 10","GEMS 2024-26"],"head_zh":["獎項","2026 入圍","2026 獲獎","高中組入圍 24/25/26","入圍者同時進 Top 10","GEMS 2024-26"],"rows":[["Best Wiki","26","4","9/9/9","**60% (49/81)**","**2024 win · 2025 nom · 2026 nom**"],["Best Presentation","26","4","9/9/9","**53% (42/79)**","2024 nom · 2026 nom"],["Best Model","15","3","4/4/4","**50% (20/40)**","2024 nom · 2025 nom"],["Best Integrated Human Practices","12","3","4/4/4","**45% (17/38)**","**2026 win**"],["Best Part Collection","12","3","3/5/5","35% (11/31)","never cited"],["Best New Composite Part","10","3","4/5/4","34% (12/35)","never cited"],["Best Education","12","3","4/4/4","33% (12/36)","2024 nom · 2025 nom"],["Best Entrepreneurship","12","3","4/5/4","29% (10/35)","never cited"],["Best Software","6","4","0/1/1","24% (4/17)","never cited"],["Best Measurement","11","3","3/4/4","22% (7/32)","**2025 nom · 2026 win**"],["Best Hardware","11","3","3/4/5","21% (6/29)","**2026 win**"],["Inclusivity Award","6","3","1/1/2","12% (2/16)","never cited"],["Best Sustainable Development Impact","10","3","4/4/5","10% (3/30)","never cited"],["Best New Basic Part","11","3","5/4/4","9% (3/35)","**2024 win**"],["Best Alternative Platform","4","3","0/0/1","**0% (0/4)**","never cited"],["Safety and Security Award","3","3","0/1/0","**0% (0/9)**","never cited"],["Best New Improved Part","0","2","2/0/0","**0% (0/3)**","never cited"]],"rows_zh":[["Best Wiki","26","4","9/9/9","**60% (49/81)**","**2024 獲獎 · 2025 入圍 · 2026 入圍**"],["Best Presentation","26","4","9/9/9","**53% (42/79)**","2024 入圍 · 2026 入圍"],["Best Model","15","3","4/4/4","**50% (20/40)**","2024 入圍 · 2025 入圍"],["Best Integrated Human Practices","12","3","4/4/4","**45% (17/38)**","**2026 獲獎**"],["Best Part Collection","12","3","3/5/5","35% (11/31)","從未列名"],["Best New Composite Part","10","3","4/5/4","34% (12/35)","從未列名"],["Best Education","12","3","4/4/4","33% (12/36)","2024 入圍 · 2025 入圍"],["Best Entrepreneurship","12","3","4/5/4","29% (10/35)","從未列名"],["Best Software","6","4","0/1/1","24% (4/17)","從未列名"],["Best Measurement","11","3","3/4/4","22% (7/32)","**2025 入圍 · 2026 獲獎**"],["Best Hardware","11","3","3/4/5","21% (6/29)","**2026 獲獎**"],["Inclusivity Award","6","3","1/1/2","12% (2/16)","從未列名"],["Best Sustainable Development Impact","10","3","4/4/5","10% (3/30)","從未列名"],["Best New Basic Part","11","3","5/4/4","9% (3/35)","**2024 獲獎**"],["Best Alternative Platform","4","3","0/0/1","**0% (0/4)**","從未列名"],["Safety and Security Award","3","3","0/1/0","**0% (0/9)**","從未列名"],["Best New Improved Part","0","2","2/0/0","**0% (0/3)**","從未列名"]]},"checklist":["Treat a nomination as a nomination. Best Wiki nominates 26 and crowns 4, and the public record carries no ordering inside the slate, so \"nearly won\" is not a claim the data supports about any of the three 2026 nominations.","If the 2027 goal is the finalist slate, do not plan it as a category haul. GEMS already held the highest citation count in its section in 2026 — 5 of 82 slots, 3 of them wins — and did not make the slate.","Count nominations and wins in separate columns and never add them. Winning co-occurs with Top 10 at 57% and being nominated at 36%, so a combined citation total hides which half of that you have.","Treat Best Wiki and Best Presentation as whole-project work, not as wiki work and slide work. They are assessed on how the project is communicated, which is why they co-occur with Top 10 at 60% and 53% — and why a weak project cannot be rescued in them.","The parts route is open and unoccupied: GEMS has won Best New Basic Part but never New Composite or Part Collection, which give high-school teams 13 nominations each over three seasons. New Improved Part is not in that group — it issued 2 high-school nominations in 2024 and none since. The first two are a documentation job with a known cost and a low ceiling.","Do not spend effort on Best Alternative Platform, Best Software or the Safety and Security Award to fill the blanks. Across three seasons they offered the whole high-school section 1, 2 and 1 nominations; the absence there is structural.","Expect no finalist credit from Best Sustainable Development Impact or Best New Basic Part — 10% and 9% of their nominees place Top 10. Enter them when the work exists anyway, not as a route.","Before next season closes, ask what single dimension each 2026 win actually certified — measurement, hardware, integrated human practices — and whether anything in the published record certifies that the three belong to one working system. No category panel was asked that question."],"checklist_zh":["把入圍就當成入圍。Best Wiki 入圍 26 支、頒出 4 個獎，而公開紀錄裡沒有名單內部的排序，因此關於 2026 年那三項入圍，「差一點就贏」都不是資料支持得起的說法。","如果 2027 年的目標是決賽名單，就不要把它規畫成類別獎的收集。GEMS 2026 年已經是本組列名次數最高的隊伍——82 個名額中占 5 個、其中 3 個是獲獎——而它沒有進入決賽名單。","把入圍與獲獎分成兩欄計算，絕不相加。獲獎與 Top 10 的同時發生率是 57%，入圍是 36%，所以一個合併的列名總數會藏起你落在哪一邊。","把 Best Wiki 與 Best Presentation 當成整體專案的工作，不是當成 wiki 的工作與投影片的工作。它們評的是這個專案如何被傳達，這正是它們與 Top 10 的同時發生率高達 60% 與 53% 的原因——也是一個體質弱的專案無法靠它們挽救的原因。","元件這條路是開著而且空著的：GEMS 贏過 Best New Basic Part，卻從未在 New Composite 或 Part Collection 列名，而這兩者三季各給高中組 13 個入圍名額。New Improved Part 不算在這一組裡——它在 2024 年發出 2 個高中組入圍名額，之後一個都沒有。前兩者是一份成本已知、天花板也不高的文件工作。","不要為了填補空白而投入 Best Alternative Platform、Best Software 或 Safety and Security Award。三季下來，它們總共只給整個高中組 1、2、1 個入圍名額；那裡的空白是結構性的。","不要期待 Best Sustainable Development Impact 或 Best New Basic Part 能換到決賽的分數——它們的入圍者只有 10% 與 9% 進入 Top 10。有現成的成果就去報，但別把它當成一條路。","在下一季結束之前，問清楚 2026 年那三個獎各自認證了哪一個單一面向——量測、硬體、整合式人文實踐——以及公開紀錄裡有沒有任何東西認證這三者屬於同一個能運作的系統。沒有任何一個類別評審組被問過這個問題。"],"method":"Three seasons of results — 2024, 2025 and 2026 — read from the iGEM public API's award records and team rosters; nothing on this page comes from a wiki. The category set is the 17 special awards present in the 2026 results, with \"Best Village Project\" excluded: it is awarded within each village rather than across the cohort, so its nominee count and its co-occurrence rate are not comparable with the others. \"Best Software Tool\" and \"Best Software\" are treated as one category, being the same award renamed between seasons. \"Best Plant Synthetic Biology\" appears in earlier seasons and is absent from the 2026 special set, so it is not in the table. Team ids are reissued every season, so team names are the only cross-year key available; a team that renamed itself between seasons would be read here as two teams, no such case was detected, and none can be ruled out. The \"nominees also Top 10\" column is the share of pooled 2024-26 nominations in a category whose team also appears in that same season's Top 10, across all sections rather than high-school only; the high-school-only rates are referred to in the text but rest on denominators as small as 1 and 2 and are not tabulated. That column is co-occurrence and nothing else. It is close to circular, and the circularity is structural rather than incidental: a project strong enough to be nominated is usually strong enough to place, and Best Wiki and Best Presentation are assessed on how the whole project is communicated, which overlaps directly with what a Top 10 judgement rewards, so part of the correlation is built into the definitions. No causal claim is made from it, it should not be read as a prediction, and the sorting it supports — proxy for a whole-project verdict against certificate for one dimension — is the only use made of it. Slate sizes are counted as awarded, so a category's nominee count is what the published record shows rather than a stated quota, and \"Best New Improved Part\" having 2 winners and 0 nominees in 2026 is reported as found. The 2026 section context — 423 accepted teams, 147 of them high-school, 145 decorated on at least one non-medal award, 59 winning at least one outright, 10 high-school teams in the Top 10 and 2 named finalists — is counted from the same records. GEMS-Taiwan is the report author's own team and is counted on the same lines as every other team.","method_zh":"三個賽季的成績——2024、2025、2026——取自 iGEM 公開 API 的獎項紀錄與隊伍名冊；本頁沒有任何內容來自 wiki。類別集合是 2026 年成績中出現的 17 個特別獎，並排除「Best Village Project」：它是在各個 village 內部頒發，而不是跨全體頒發，因此它的入圍數與同時發生比率無法與其他類別相比。「Best Software Tool」與「Best Software」視為同一個類別，因為那是同一個獎在不同賽季改名。「Best Plant Synthetic Biology」出現在較早的賽季，而 2026 年的特別獎集合中沒有它，因此不列入本表。隊伍編號每一季都會重新發放，所以隊伍名稱是唯一可用的跨年度對照鍵；若有隊伍在賽季之間改名，在這裡就會被讀成兩支隊伍，目前沒有偵測到這樣的案例，但也無法排除。「入圍者同時進 Top 10」一欄，是某個類別在 2024 至 2026 三季合計的入圍名額中，其隊伍同時出現在該季 Top 10 的比例，計算範圍是所有組別，而不只是高中組；只算高中組的比率在正文中提到，但其分母小到只有 1 或 2，因此不列表。該欄只是同時發生，別無其他。它接近循環論證，而且這個循環是結構性的，不是偶然的：強到能夠入圍的專案，通常也強到能夠進榜，而 Best Wiki 與 Best Presentation 評的是整個專案如何被傳達，這與 Top 10 評審所獎勵的東西直接重疊，因此這份相關性有一部分是內建在定義裡的。本頁不從它導出任何因果主張，它也不該被當成預測來讀；它唯一的用途是支撐那個分法——整體專案判決的替身，對比單一面向的認證。各類別的名額數量以實際頒出為準，因此某個類別的入圍數是公開紀錄所顯示的數字，而不是官方宣告的配額；「Best New Improved Part」在 2026 年有 2 個獲獎、0 個入圍，就照查到的樣子報告。2026 年的全組背景數字——423 支獲准參賽隊伍、其中 147 支為高中組、145 支取得至少一項非獎牌類獎項、59 支至少贏下一項、高中組 10 支進入 Top 10、2 支被列為決賽隊伍——也是從同一批紀錄計算而來。GEMS-Taiwan 是本報告作者自己的團隊，與其他每一支隊伍以相同標準計算。"}],"roadmap":[{"title":"Phase 1 · Make the current work reproducible","title_zh":"階段一 · 讓現有工作可重現","when":"0–3 months","when_zh":"0–3 個月","lede":"Before building anything new, make what already exists survivable by the next cohort.","lede_zh":"在建造新東西之前，先讓既有成果能被下一屆接手。","items":["**Put every analysis in version control.** One GEMS Research GitHub organisation, one repository per project, with the raw data, the notebook and the figure-generating script in the same place. If a figure cannot be regenerated from the repository, it does not count as a result.","**Write down the measurement protocols.** Calibration standards, units, replicate counts, how uncertainty was computed. The 2026 Best Measurement teams all did this; it is the cheapest credibility a dry lab can buy.","**Tag the provenance of every number.** The most copyable device in the whole 2026 field: TU Delft labels every cell of its decision matrix Factual, Inferred, Estimated or Speculative, with a legend saying the tag records the evidence and not the judgement; GEMS-Taiwan's own dose ledger runs a rail that turns from green to amber exactly where measurement stops and modelling begins. Make it the house format for every table and figure. It costs a column and it is the fastest way to be believed.","**Standardise the environment.** One `environment.yml` or `requirements.txt` per project, Python 3.12+, pinned versions. A student should be able to clone and run in under ten minutes.","**Archive the 2026 ReLEAF dry lab properly** — the OD600 signal processing, the optogenetic circuit model, the hardware firmware — as the first entry in the institutional record.","**Write the one-page biosecurity and ordering policy.** The US National Policy for Nucleic Acid Synthesis Screening (November 2026) now ties federal funding to buying synthetic DNA only from certified providers that screen orders of 50+ nucleotides. Mirror it: certified suppliers only, a documented internal review of any sequence design, an explicit scope statement excluding pathogen and toxin sequences, signed by every student before their first order. It costs an afternoon and it is the first thing a serious partner asks about.","**Write the AI-use norm now, while it is cheap.** Every one of the 106 decorated teams of 2026 disclosed its AI use, because iGEM made it a Bronze requirement — compliance is not the problem. Quality is: only **4 of 106** stated what AI did *not* do, and of the 40 teams using a foundation model only 15 filed it as AI at all, because AlphaFold gets filed as biology. The GEMS norm should separate the three things that get blurred — a model we trained, a third-party model we ran, an assistant that wrote code or prose — and require, per use, the model version, a named human reviewer, and one sentence on what the tool was not trusted with. Mark any model output unvalidated until it has been tested.","**Decide the 2027 team size deliberately, and smaller than instinct says.** Across 84 decorated teams of 2026 headcount and award count correlate at 0.06 (p = 0.61); within every section the Top 10 teams are statistically indistinguishable in size from everyone else. Princeton took 2nd runner-up Grand Prize with **nine undergraduates** and four named scientists behind them. GEMS fielded 35 students against a high-school median of 17.5. The substitutions that actually worked for the small teams were scope (one chassis demonstrated across several applications), software that makes a new target cost compute rather than hands, and one genuinely present PhD- or postdoc-level instructor. Trade headcount for that third one.","**Name the statistical test next to every p-value.** The 2026 results page carries five p-values, SEM throughout and R² to four decimals, and not one named test — no t-test, no ANOVA, no Dunnett, significance carried by asterisks alone. Be clear about why this matters, because it is not what it looks like: across the whole High School Top 10 statistical reporting does not predict a placing, and the Grand Prize winner names no test either. It matters because question 8 asks whether a stranger can check the claim, and a p-value whose test is unnamed cannot be checked. This is hours of work on text that already exists.","**Publish the numbers behind the two traced growth charts, or label them the way the source file intends.** growth-data.js ships with csv: null and a comment recording that the data was promised and never arrived, while the two growth curves are drawn by tracing images of charts. That same file says the charts carry a line underneath saying so — and of the 36 captions on the photometer page, those two do not. Either fix counts: get the CSV, or make the page say what the source already says. The candour is already written; it just did not reach the reader.","**Nominate one result as the answer, and bound it in the same breath.** Both 2026 High School finalists do exactly this; the eight teams that did not place publish module inventories instead. GEMS's own Key results block holds five genuine results and no nominated one. This is not a formula — HangzhouFourteenAP had the clearest single headline of any non-finalist and placed nowhere — so treat it as legibility rather than a route, which also makes it the cheapest item on this entire roadmap.","**Make the landing page say only what the results page still supports.** In 2026 the home page sells \"On-demand — Green light switches production on when the environmental sensors and forecasts decide to\" as a feature of the machine. The results page says the ELISA showed no change over time and that the amount \"did not rise with light\"; the reporter never coloured; and the model page says \"The reactor therefore cannot be scheduled from the forecast.\" One sentence on the front page is contradicted by two other pages of the team's own. Compare 2024, which hedged in the same breath — \"**partially** proved the chromosome-free system\", \"Integration… **will be** a powerful vector control tool\". Hedging in the same sentence as the claim is the habit to copy, and it costs nothing."],"items_zh":["**把所有分析放進版本控制。** 一個 GEMS Research GitHub organisation，一個專案一個 repository，原始資料、notebook 與產生圖表的腳本放在同一處。若一張圖無法從 repository 重新產生，它就不算結果。","**寫下量測流程。** 校正標準品、單位、重複次數、不確定度如何計算。2026 年所有最佳量測獎團隊都做到了這點；這是乾實驗室能買到最便宜的可信度。","**為每一個數字標註來源。** 這是整個 2026 年最值得照抄的裝置：TU Delft 在決策矩陣的每一格標上 Factual、Inferred、Estimated 或 Speculative，並附圖例說明「標籤記錄的是證據，不是判斷」；GEMS-Taiwan 自己的劑量帳本則有一條軌道，正好在量測結束、模擬開始之處由綠轉琥珀。把它訂為所有表格與圖的統一格式。它只花一個欄位，卻是最快讓人相信你的方法。","**統一環境。** 每個專案一份 `environment.yml` 或 `requirements.txt`，Python 3.12 以上，版本鎖定。學生應該能在十分鐘內 clone 下來就跑起來。","**妥善歸檔 2026 ReLEAF 的乾實驗室成果** —— OD600 訊號處理、光遺傳電路模型、硬體韌體 —— 作為機構紀錄的第一筆。","**寫下一頁的生物安全與訂購政策。** 美國《核酸合成篩查國家政策》（2026 年 11 月）已將聯邦經費與「只向通過認證、且會篩查 50 個核苷酸以上訂單的供應商購買合成 DNA」綁在一起。比照辦理：僅限認證供應商、任何序列設計都要有書面內部審查、明確排除病原與毒素序列，並由每位學生在第一次下單前簽署。這只需要一個下午，而且是認真的合作對象第一個會問的事。","**趁現在還便宜，先把 AI 使用規範寫下來。** 2026 年 106 支得獎隊伍每一支都揭露了 AI 使用，因為 iGEM 把它列為銅牌必繳項目——遵循不是問題。品質才是：只有 **106 支中的 4 支**寫出 AI *沒有*做什麼；而在使用基礎模型的 40 支隊伍裡，只有 15 支把它填進 AI 欄位，因為 AlphaFold 會被歸到生物學那邊。GEMS 的規範應該把三件常被混在一起的事分開——我們自己訓練的模型、我們跑的第三方模型、替我們寫程式或文字的助理——並且要求每一次使用都記下模型版本、一位具名的人類審閱者，以及一句話說明這個工具不被信任去做什麼。任何模型輸出在經過測試之前，都要標記為未驗證。","**刻意決定 2027 年的團隊規模，而且要比直覺更小。** 2026 年 84 支得獎隊伍中，人數與獎項數的相關係數是 0.06（p = 0.61）；在每一個組別裡，Top 10 隊伍的人數與其他隊伍在統計上都沒有差別。Princeton 以**九名大學生**拿下總冠軍季軍，背後有四位具名的科學家。GEMS 投入 35 名學生，而高中組中位數是 17.5。小隊伍真正有效的替代方案是：收窄範圍（一個底盤做出好幾個應用）、用軟體讓換一個標的花算力而不是人手，以及一位真正在場的博士級或博士後級指導者。把人數換成第三項。","**在每一個 p 值旁邊寫出所用的檢定。** 2026 年的結果頁面上有五個 p 值、全程標示 SEM、R² 寫到小數第四位，卻沒有任何一處寫出檢定名稱——沒有 t 檢定、沒有變異數分析、沒有 Dunnett，顯著性完全由星號承擔。要說清楚這件事為什麼重要，因為它並不是看起來的那樣：在整個高中組 Top 10 裡，統計的寫法並不預測名次，總冠軍自己也沒有寫出任何檢定。它重要的理由是第 8 題問的是陌生人能不能核對你所說的東西，而一個沒有寫出檢定的 p 值無法被核對。這件事只是在既有文字上花幾個小時。","**把兩張描摹而來的生長曲線背後的數字公開，或至少照原始檔案的本意標註清楚。** growth-data.js 目前帶著 csv: null，以及一段寫明資料被承諾卻始終沒有交來的註解，而那兩條生長曲線是從圖片上描摹下來的。同一個檔案說這些圖下方會有一行字說明這一點——但光度計頁面上的 36 條圖說裡，那兩條並沒有。兩種補法都算：把 CSV 拿到，或讓頁面說出原始檔案已經說過的話。坦白其實已經寫好了，只是沒有傳到讀者眼前。","**指定一個成果作為答案，並在同一口氣裡標出它的邊界。** 2026 年高中組的兩支決賽隊伍都正是這樣做；沒有拿到名次的八支隊伍則是公開一份模組清單。GEMS 自己的「Key results」區塊裡有五個真實的成果，卻沒有被指定的那一個。這不是公式——HangzhouFourteenAP 在所有非決賽隊伍裡標題最清楚，名次卻什麼都沒有——所以把它當成可讀性問題，而不是一條路徑；這也讓它成為整張路線圖上最便宜的一項。","**讓首頁只說結果頁還撐得住的話。** 2026 年的首頁把「On-demand——綠光在環境感測器與預報做出判斷時開啟生產」當成機器的一項功能來賣。但結果頁寫著 ELISA 隨時間沒有變化、產量「並未隨光照上升」；顯色蛋白從未顯色；而模型頁寫著「反應器無法由預報來排程」。首頁的一句話，被自己團隊另外兩個頁面反駁。對照 2024 年，它在同一口氣裡就先保留了——「**部分**證實了無染色體系統」、「整合……**將會**是一項強力的病媒防治工具」。把保留寫在與主張同一句話裡，這個習慣值得照抄，而且不花一毛錢。"],"outcome":"A new student can reproduce any 2026 figure from the repository alone, without asking anybody.","outcome_zh":"新進學生只靠 repository 就能重現 2026 年的任何一張圖，不需要問任何人。"},{"title":"Phase 2 · Build the core modelling skill","title_zh":"階段二 · 建立核心建模能力","when":"3–9 months","when_zh":"3–9 個月","lede":"Two tracks, taught deliberately, with a real deliverable at the end of each.","lede_zh":"兩條軌道，刻意教學，每條都有真實的產出。","items":["**Track A — dynamical systems.** ODE models of genetic circuits, parameter fitting to the team's own data, sensitivity analysis, identifiability. Tools: Python with SciPy and lmfit, Tellurium/COPASI for the SBML side. Deliverable: a circuit model fitted to real GEMS time-course data, with confidence intervals on every parameter.","**Track B — structural and sequence modelling.** Structure prediction is now free infrastructure: the open models (Boltz-2, Chai-1, OpenFold3, ColabFold) match or beat the gated flagship, so folding a protein is a commodity step, not a project. Put one shared GPU box or a modest cloud budget behind an internal queue, make \"fold it, then read the confidence metrics\" compulsory in every project, and teach the hard part — knowing when pLDDT and PAE are lying to you. Deliverable: a designed or selected variant with a documented computational rationale, taken to the bench.","**Teach the four controls, and make them compulsory.** This is where the 53%-against-23% finding becomes a syllabus. Split calibration from validation before fitting anything. Cluster near-duplicate sequences and split whole clusters across folds, so a model cannot memorise a near-copy. Run a label-shuffle control that must collapse to chance. Run an ablation that strips the information you claim to be using. Eton-College-UK did all four at high-school level with logistic regression and a scoring matrix; the controls, not the model, are what made it credible.","**Teach uncertainty before teaching models.** Error propagation, replicate design, what a fit actually claims. Most student models fail here, not at the mathematics.","**Run a weekly dry-lab clinic.** One hour, somebody presents a figure, everyone else attacks it. This is how modelling taste transmits between cohorts.","**Know why you are doing this.** Reading 39 decorated wikis directly, only 15% computed a limit of detection for their own assay and 5% ever measured one sample twice — and measurement discipline does not predict placing: 27% against 29% across all 106 files. *No effect.* The case for teaching uncertainty first is not that it wins. It is that a number nobody can reproduce is not a result, and an institution that cannot tell the difference will eventually publish one.","**Treat the modelling track as the one award-level signal that tracks the podium.** Across the 2026 High School Top 10, Best Model recognition lands on exactly the two finalists and nobody else: Lambert-GA won it, HongKong-JSS was nominated, no other Top 10 team appears in the category, and GCGS and HongKong-HS have no model page at all. That is an award predicting an award and therefore close to circular, so do not read it as a lever to pull. Read it as evidence that whole-project judges and model judges are rewarding the same thing — and note that GEMS was a Best Model nominee in 2024 and in 2025, and not in 2026."],"items_zh":["**軌道 A —— 動力系統。** 基因電路的 ODE 模型、以自身資料擬合參數、敏感度分析、可辨識性。工具：Python 搭配 SciPy 與 lmfit，SBML 端使用 Tellurium/COPASI。產出：一個以 GEMS 真實時間序列資料擬合的電路模型，每個參數都附信賴區間。","**軌道 B —— 結構與序列建模。** 結構預測現在已是免費的基礎設施：開源模型（Boltz-2、Chai-1、OpenFold3、ColabFold）已可匹敵甚至超越封閉的旗艦模型，因此「把蛋白質折出來」是一個標準步驟，而不是一個專案。配置一台共用 GPU 主機或一筆適度的雲端預算，架一個內部排程佇列，規定每個專案都必須「先折、再讀信心指標」，並教真正困難的部分——判斷 pLDDT 與 PAE 什麼時候在騙你。產出：一個經過設計或篩選的變體，附上完整的運算理由，並實際進到實驗檯。","**教那四項對照，並列為必做。** 這就是「53% 對 23%」這個發現落地成課綱的地方。在擬合任何東西之前先把校正組與驗證組分開。把近似重複的序列分群，並讓整群落在同一個 fold，使模型無法記住近似副本。跑標籤洗牌對照，其表現必須塌回隨機水準。跑一個消融測試，剝除你宣稱正在使用的那項資訊。Eton-College-UK 在高中階段用 logistic regression 與計分矩陣就做完了這四項；讓結果可信的是那些對照，不是模型。","**先教不確定度，再教模型。** 誤差傳遞、重複設計、一次擬合究竟主張了什麼。多數學生模型敗在這裡，而不是數學。","**每週一次乾實驗室診療會。** 一小時，一個人報一張圖，其他人負責挑戰它。建模的品味就是這樣在屆與屆之間傳下去的。","**要清楚自己為什麼做這件事。** 直接讀過 39 個得獎 wiki 後：只有 15% 替自己的分析法算出偵測極限，5% 曾經把同一個樣本量過兩次——而且量測紀律並不預測名次：全部 106 份檔案中是 27% 對 29%。*沒有效果。* 先教不確定度的理由不是它能贏。理由是：一個沒有人能重現的數字不算結果；而一個分不出這個差別的機構，遲早會發表一個這樣的數字。","**把建模這條軌道視為唯一一個與頒獎臺同步的獎項訊號。** 在 2026 年高中組 Top 10 裡，最佳模型獎的肯定剛好落在那兩支決賽隊伍身上，別無他人：Lambert-GA 得獎、HongKong-JSS 入圍，Top 10 中沒有其他隊伍出現在這個項目裡，而 GCGS 與 HongKong-HS 甚至沒有模型頁面。這是用一個獎去預測另一個獎，因此接近循環論證，不要把它當成一根可以拉的槓桿。要把它讀成一個證據：看整體專案的評審和看模型的評審，獎勵的是同一件事——另外記住，GEMS 在 2024 與 2025 年都是最佳模型獎入圍，2026 年不是。"],"outcome":"Two or three students who can independently build, fit and defend a model with its controls — and who can teach the next two or three.","outcome_zh":"有兩三位學生能獨立建立、擬合模型並連同對照一起為它辯護——而且能教會下兩三位。"},{"title":"Phase 3 · Ship one tool the outside world uses","title_zh":"階段三 · 做出一個外界真的會用的工具","when":"9–18 months","when_zh":"9–18 個月","lede":"The difference between a competition team and a research centre is whether anybody outside uses what you built.","lede_zh":"競賽團隊與研究中心的差別，在於外界有沒有人用你做的東西。","items":["**Commit to the Bacillus optogenetics line.** Both trend reviews independently pointed here. Port and properly characterise a CcaS/CcaR or LOV-based light-inducible cassette in *B. subtilis* with full dose-response, dynamic range and growth-stage characterisation. In a twelve-paper literature that is on its own a publishable contribution, and it is the natural continuation of ReLEAF rather than a fresh start. The chassis census now puts a number on how empty the field is: of the 106 decorated teams of 2026, **5 used light as a control input** in any organism and **5 worked with** *B. subtilis*, and the two sets intersect in exactly one team — GEMS. Outside GEMS the intersection is **0 of 105**. Nobody in this cohort is competing for the line, which is the argument for holding it rather than treating it as one option among several.","**Pick one narrow, real problem** that GEMS has genuine data on — the strongest candidate is the optogenetic induction and OD600 measurement work from ReLEAF, where GEMS already has instrumentation, data and a Best Measurement award behind it.","**Buy the domain and host it before the freeze.** This is the single habit that separated the award-winning iGEM 2026 software that is still usable today from the software that is not. Of 21 award-winning tools checked, 8 are live; every one of those was hosted on freeze day, and every source-only tool's wiki lists localhost as its only address. It is a hosting decision made months early, not a coding or budget one — two high-school teams out-shipped most of the universities on exactly this. Write the documentation around a URL, not an install command.","**If the tool is hardware, the habit is export, not hosting.** Of 20 instruments built by the 2026 Best Hardware, Best Measurement and Best Alternative Platform teams, only 6 publish enough for a stranger to rebuild them and **9 publish no geometry file at all** — the failures mostly have good CAD that never left the design tool. There is no 2026/hardware group on gitlab.igem.org, so unlike software nothing forces a deposit and every release is improvised. Export STL and STEP, a schematic, Gerbers and a drill file, firmware with a licence, and a bill of materials with real part numbers and prices. Check every link while signed out: in this cohort a Drive folder showed a visitor nothing and a named firmware repository was a 404. The only instrument anyone outside its team ever used was the one shipped with Gerbers and a supplier-keyed BOM — and it came from a high-school team.","**Build it as a deployed web tool, not a notebook.** Documented, licensed, with example data, a DOI, and a URL anybody can open. Teams that only publish source code get used by nobody.","**If the artefact is paper, the wiki freeze is doing the work for you.** Of 285 education files linked from 31 decorated 2026 wikis, **284 still download and none 404** — against 8 of 21 software tools still running and 6 of 20 devices rebuildable. A PDF on `static.igem.wiki` needs no server, so the freeze that kills a web app preserves a worksheet for free. Four teams go further and self-host a browser game **on the frozen wiki itself**, which is the most durable interactive format iGEM currently allows; GEMS already does this. The failures are elsewhere and are cheap to avoid: **1 licence statement in 136 education PDFs**, and the Best Education winner of 2026 publishes no downloadable file at all. Put a licence line in the artefact itself, not in the wiki footer.","**Design for other people's data from day one.** Input format, validation, error messages. This is the single most common failure in iGEM software.","**Expect nobody to come.** Across every award-winning 2026 repository checked, stars and forks were zero, and the only external-adoption figure found anywhere was Stanford's SynBase reporting 837 learners. Uni-Padua-IT publicly offered to optimise any team's sequence and got no replies, and said so on their wiki. Publishing is necessary and not sufficient: the three outside users below have to be recruited by hand.","**Get three outside users and write down what broke.** Other Taiwanese schools, a university lab, a 2027 iGEM team. Their complaints are the roadmap for version two.","**Close the light-dependence gap before anything else on this line, because the whole roadmap rests on it.** ReLEAF's own 2026 documentation reports that the ELISA showed no change over time, with ACCD at 2.6 to 3.2 µg/mL at every time point under both colours against about 1.3 for the plasmid-free control; AmilCP never coloured; and every biological result in the project came from a constitutive bypass rather than the light-gated device. The team names two candidate explanations — well-to-well light crosstalk in the LPA, and red LEDs emitting at 640 nm when CcaSR needs about 672 nm to switch off — and states that it has not tested either directly. Each is roughly a week of work. Until one is resolved, the optogenetic claim this entire line is built on is unevidenced by GEMS's own pages.","**Make a real sample a gate, not an extra.** Across the 2026 High School Top 10, seven of the seven teams that did not reach the podium stop at a surrogate — a synthetic trigger RNA standing in for river water, a model ester, a reporter standing in for a therapy. Exactly one team in ten ran its assay on a real sample, HongKong-JSS on a soil extract, and that team took 1st Runner-up. Ten teams and two podium places cannot carry a causal claim, but it is the one line the podium sat on the right side of — and it now holds from a second, independent direction: inside GEMS's own three seasons the podium year is the real-target year. In 2024 three toxins were fed to live Aedes albopictus larvae with LC50 reported for all three, 98 dead larvae examined under the microscope, and a qPCR immune-gene panel run against an empty-vector arm expressly to rule out E. coli as the cause of death. For ReLEAF the real sample is not exotic: it is the preparation actually sprayed on the plants, which was never assayed — so the plant rescue at p < 0.0001 with 40 seedlings a condition, the strongest result the project has, sits on a protectant the reactor is not shown to have made. The other half of this finding has now been measured across all 30 Top 10 wikis and it does not rank anyone: 26 of 30 ran an experiment designed to kill a rival explanation and 30 of 30 published a result unfavourable to their own headline. **GEMS-Taiwan holds all five control types, a perfect score, and still placed outside the podium** — as did four other perfect scorers. So controls are a floor this team already clears, and the real sample is the half that is actually missing. Do not spend 2027 adding controls."],"items_zh":["**確立枯草桿菌光遺傳學這條路線。** 兩份趨勢分析各自獨立地指向這裡。在 *B. subtilis* 中移植並完整表徵一組 CcaS/CcaR 或 LOV 型的光誘導卡匣，做出完整的劑量反應、動態範圍與生長期表徵。在一個只有十二篇文獻的領域裡，光是這件事本身就足以發表，而且這是 ReLEAF 的自然延伸，不是重新開始。底盤普查現在替這塊空白補上了數字：2026 年的 106 支得獎隊伍中，**有 5 支把光當成控制輸入**（不限生物）、**有 5 支碰過** *B. subtilis*，而兩個集合恰好只在一支隊伍上相交——就是 GEMS。把 GEMS 排除之後，交集是 **105 支中的 0 支**。這一屆沒有任何人在搶這條路線，而這正是該守住它、而不是把它當成眾多選項之一的理由。","**挑一個狹窄而真實的問題**，而且 GEMS 手上有真正的資料——最強的候選是 ReLEAF 的光遺傳誘導與 OD600 量測工作，GEMS 已經有儀器、有資料，背後還有一座最佳量測獎。","**在 wiki 凍結前就把網域買好、把服務架起來。** 這是唯一一個把「今天還能用」的 iGEM 2026 得獎軟體，和「今天不能用」的區分開來的習慣。在檢查的 21 個得獎工具中，有 8 個仍然在線；這 8 個無一例外在凍結當日就已經上線，而所有只有原始碼的工具，其 wiki 上唯一的位址都是 localhost。這是一個提前好幾個月做的「要不要架站」決定，不是寫程式或預算的決定——有兩支高中隊伍正是靠這一點，交付得比多數大學還好。文件要圍繞一個網址來寫，而不是圍繞一行安裝指令。","**如果那個工具是硬體，關鍵習慣是匯出，不是架站。** 2026 年最佳硬體、最佳量測與最佳替代平台的團隊共做出 20 台儀器，其中只有 6 台公開到陌生人重建得出來，而且**有 9 台完全沒有公開任何幾何檔案**——失敗的那些大多有做得很好的 CAD，只是從來沒有離開過設計軟體。gitlab.igem.org 上根本沒有 2026/hardware 這個群組，所以不像軟體有強制繳交，硬體的釋出全靠自己想辦法。請匯出 STL 與 STEP、電路圖、Gerber 與鑽孔檔、附授權的韌體，以及一份有真實料號與價格的材料清單。每一個連結都要在登出狀態下檢查一遍：在這一屆裡，有一個 Drive 資料夾對訪客什麼都不顯示，有一個 wiki 上指名的韌體程式庫是 404。整個群體中唯一被製作團隊以外的人用過的儀器，正是那台附上 Gerber 與可對應供應商料號的材料清單的——而且出自一支高中隊伍。","**把它做成已部署的網頁工具，而不是 notebook。** 有文件、有授權、有範例資料、有 DOI，以及任何人都能打開的網址。只釋出原始碼的團隊，沒有人會用。","**如果產出是紙本，wiki 凍結本身就在替你做事。** 31 份 2026 年得獎 wiki 連出的 285 個教育檔案中，**284 個今天仍下載得到，一個 404 都沒有**——對照軟體 21 個中 8 個還能跑、硬體 20 台中 6 台重建得出來。放在 `static.igem.wiki` 上的一份 PDF 不需要伺服器，所以那個會殺死網頁應用的凍結，反而免費替一份學習單保了存。有四支隊伍更進一步，把瀏覽器遊戲**直接放在凍結後的 wiki 上**，這是目前 iGEM 允許的最耐久互動形式；GEMS 已經在這樣做了。真正的失敗在別處，而且很便宜就能避免：**136 份教育 PDF 裡只有 1 份寫了授權條款**，而 2026 年最佳教育獎得主根本沒有放出任何可下載的檔案。把授權寫進產出本身，不要只寫在 wiki 頁尾。","**從第一天就為別人的資料設計。** 輸入格式、驗證、錯誤訊息。這是 iGEM 軟體最常見的單一失敗原因。","**不要期待有人會自己找上門。** 在檢查過的每一個 2026 得獎 repository 中，star 與 fork 都是零，而唯一能找到的外部採用數字，是 Stanford 的 SynBase 回報的 837 位學習者。Uni-Padua-IT 公開表示願意為任何團隊最佳化序列，結果沒有人回應，而他們把這件事寫在 wiki 上。釋出是必要條件而非充分條件：下面那三位外部使用者，必須一個一個親手去找。","**找到三位外部使用者，並記錄哪裡壞了。** 其他台灣學校、一間大學實驗室、一支 2027 iGEM 團隊。他們的抱怨就是第二版的路線圖。","**在這條路線上，先把光依賴性這個缺口補起來，因為整張路線圖都架在它上面。** ReLEAF 自己 2026 年的文件寫著 ELISA 隨時間沒有變化，ACCD 在兩種光色下的每一個時間點都是 2.6 到 3.2 µg/mL，而無質體對照組大約是 1.3；AmilCP 從未顯色；而專案裡每一個生物學成果，都來自組成型旁路模組，不是光控裝置本身。團隊自己點出兩個可能的解釋——LPA 中孔與孔之間的光干擾，以及紅光 LED 發在 640 nm，而 CcaSR 需要大約 672 nm 才能關閉——並且寫明兩者都沒有直接測試過。每一個大約是一週的工作量。在其中一個被解決之前，這整條路線所倚賴的光遺傳學主張，依 GEMS 自己的頁面來看都還沒有證據。","**把「真實樣本」設成一道門檻，而不是加分項。** 在 2026 年高中組 Top 10 裡，七支沒有站上頒獎臺的隊伍，七支全部停在替代物上——用合成的觸發 RNA 代替河水、用模型酯類、用報導基因代替療法。十支裡剛好只有一支把檢測跑在真實樣本上，也就是 HongKong-JSS 的土壤萃取液，而那支拿下亞軍。十支隊伍、兩個頒獎臺名額，撐不起因果主張，但這是頒獎臺剛好落在正確一側的唯一一條線——而且它現在從第二個獨立方向也站得住：在 GEMS 自己的三季裡，站上頒獎臺的那一年就是打在真實標的上的那一年。2024 年把三種毒蛋白餵給活的 Aedes albopictus 幼蟲，三種都報告了 LC50，以顯微鏡檢視 98 隻死亡幼蟲，還跑了一組 qPCR 免疫基因試驗對照空載體組，明確用來排除 E. coli 才是致死原因的可能。對 ReLEAF 來說，真實樣本並不遙遠：它就是真正噴到植物上的那份製備，而那份從未被檢測活性——所以每組 40 棵苗、p < 0.0001 的植物救援，也就是這個專案最強的成果，是建立在一份沒有被證明由反應器做出來的保護蛋白上。　這項發現的另一半，現在已經在 30 支 Top 10 隊伍的 wiki 上量過了，而它排不出名次：30 支中有 26 支做過刻意殺掉對手解釋的實驗，30 支全部公開過對自己不利的結果。**GEMS-Taiwan 五類對照全有、是滿分，卻仍然停在頒獎臺之外**——另外四支滿分隊伍也一樣。所以對照是一道這支隊伍早就跨過的門檻，真正缺的是真實樣本那一半。2027 年不要把時間花在加對照上。"],"outcome":"A tool with a URL, a licence, documentation and users who are not GEMS students.","outcome_zh":"一個有網址、有授權、有文件，而且使用者不是 GEMS 學生的工具。"},{"title":"Phase 4 · Become a place other people come to","title_zh":"階段四 · 成為別人會來的地方","when":"18 months +","when_zh":"18 個月以上","lede":"Institutional standing comes from being useful to people who owe you nothing.","lede_zh":"機構地位來自於：對那些不欠你任何東西的人仍然有用。","items":["**Run a dry-lab school for Taiwanese iGEM and high-school teams.** Modelling, measurement, reproducibility. Teaching forces the material to become transmissible, and it builds the network that later supplies collaborators.","**Approach the three Taiwanese teams the analysis identified by name.** NTHU Taiwan (team 6416, Hsinchu) is a separate NTHU entry running engineered *Bacillus subtilis* in a moving-bed reactor — the closest technical match to GEMS on the island, and the natural partner for a joint *B. subtilis* measurement standard. CCU-Taiwan (6408, Chiayi) worked on rice, the same crop as ReLEAF, so a shared Taiwan rice-stress dataset with a published benchmark is a one-season project. Labi-Taiwan (6511) won the peer-voted iGEMers Prize and is the obvious co-teacher for a Taiwan high-school dry-lab school.","**Start a collaboration page, because GEMS does not have one.** Both /collaborations and /partnership return 404, no iGEM team is named anywhere on the GEMS wiki, and GEMS appears on no other Taiwanese team's page — while placing Top 10 with three awards. Two national doors are already open and dated: **TGEM**, in its fourth edition on 22 August 2026 at the Boya Building, NTU, hosted by **Labi-Taiwan** with NTU's Department of Biochemical Science and Technology; and **NYCU-Taiwan's** 27 July meet-up, 53 people from five teams, whose organisers published their own run-sheets and asked for a collaboration interest form. Email Labi-Taiwan in March and NYCU-Taiwan in April. Being findable is a prerequisite for everything else here.","**Offer the inter-lab measurement ring nobody ran.** Across all 106 decorated teams of 2026 there was not one — the whole category of collaboration that produces a reusable result went unclaimed, and the single team that publicly offered real shared work got zero replies. GEMS holds the credential for it: Best Measurement and Best Hardware. Ship a calibrated construct and a written protocol to NCKU-Tainan (6379), NTHU (6460), Labi-Taiwan (6511) and Mingdao (6105) — Mingdao has already re-characterised another team's part, so it is the likeliest first yes — and publish the between-lab variance whatever it turns out to be. Note before building the plan on it: collaboration did not predict placing in 2026. Do this because a reproducible number is the asset, not because it wins anything.","**Become the Traditional Chinese source, because nobody else is.** Of 31 decorated teams publishing education material, **3 published anything in Traditional Chinese — NCKU-Tainan, HKSSC and GEMS — and all three already read it.** Every other Chinese file in the sample is Simplified, including all 13 of Lambert-GA's translations of its children's book, which cover thirteen languages and skip Traditional. Meanwhile 16 of 64 artefacts show a second user, so iGEM teams genuinely do adopt each other's material when it is usable. A Traditional Chinese edition of a good artefact, licensed for reuse and carrying instructions written for a teacher rather than for the authoring team, has an open field and an obvious audience in Taiwanese schools.","**Publish.** A methods paper, a preprint, or a well-documented dataset. One citable artefact per year changes how every later conversation starts.","**Keep a standing partnership with a university lab and a non-academic stakeholder** — a farm, a clinic, a municipal body. The stakeholder relationship is what makes human practices real rather than performed, and it is the thing competition teams cannot build in nine months.","**Maintain the trend watch.** This report should be regenerated at least twice a year; the academic and industry tabs are built to be re-run."],"items_zh":["**為台灣的 iGEM 與高中團隊辦一所乾實驗室學校。** 建模、量測、可重現性。教學會逼迫內容變得可傳遞，也建立起日後提供合作者的人脈網絡。","**直接聯繫分析點名的三支台灣團隊。** NTHU Taiwan（隊伍 6416，新竹）是清大另一支獨立隊伍，在移動床反應器中培養工程化的*枯草桿菌*——全島與 GEMS 技術上最接近的一支，也是共同建立 *B. subtilis* 量測標準的天然夥伴。CCU-Taiwan（6408，嘉義）做的是水稻，與 ReLEAF 同一作物，因此「共享台灣稻作逆境資料集並公開基準」是一季之內可完成的專案。Labi-Taiwan（6511）拿下同儕票選的 iGEMers Prize，是共同開辦台灣高中乾實驗室學校最明顯的人選。","**開一個 collaboration 頁面，因為 GEMS 根本沒有。** /collaborations 與 /partnership 兩個網址都是 404，整個 GEMS wiki 沒有點名任何一支 iGEM 隊伍，GEMS 也沒有出現在任何其他台灣隊伍的合作頁上——同時卻拿下 Top 10 與三個獎項。有兩扇全國性的門已經開著，而且有明確日期：**TGEM** 第四屆，2026 年 8 月 22 日於台大博雅教學館，由 **Labi-Taiwan** 與台大生化科技學系共同主辦；以及 **NYCU-Taiwan** 7 月 27 日的聚會，五支隊伍共 53 人，主辦方公開了自己的流程手冊，並徵求合作意願表。三月寫信給 Labi-Taiwan，四月寫信給 NYCU-Taiwan。能被找到，是這個階段其他每一件事的前提。","**提議做那個沒人做過的跨實驗室量測環。** 2026 年全部 106 支得獎隊伍中一個都沒有——整個「會產出可再利用結果」的合作類別無人認領，而唯一公開提議要做真正共同工作的隊伍，一封回覆都沒收到。GEMS 有做這件事的資格：最佳量測與最佳硬體。把一個已校正的構築與一份書面流程寄給 NCKU-Tainan（6379）、NTHU（6460）、Labi-Taiwan（6511）與 Mingdao（6105）；Mingdao 已經重新表徵過別隊的 part，最可能先點頭。然後無論結果如何，都公開實驗室之間的變異。在把計畫建立在這件事之上以前要先知道：2026 年的合作並不預測名次。做這件事，是因為一個可重現的數字本身就是資產，不是因為它能贏什麼。","**成為繁體中文的來源，因為沒有別人在做。** 在 31 支有教育產出的得獎隊伍中，**只有 3 支出版過任何繁體中文材料——NCKU-Tainan、HKSSC 和 GEMS——而且這三支本來就讀繁體。** 樣本中其他所有中文檔案都是簡體，包括 Lambert-GA 那本童書的全部 13 種翻譯：涵蓋十三種語言，就是沒有繁體。另一方面，64 件產出中有 16 件有第二個使用者的證據，可見 iGEM 隊伍在材料真的能用時確實會採用彼此的東西。一份好產出的繁體中文版，附上可再利用的授權，並且把說明寫給老師、而不是寫給原作團隊，面前是一片空地，而且在台灣的學校裡有再明顯不過的讀者。","**發表。** 一篇方法論文、一份預印本，或一套文件完整的資料集。每年一個可被引用的產物，會改變此後每一次對話的起點。","**與一間大學實驗室和一個非學術利害關係人維持長期夥伴關係** —— 一座農場、一間診所、一個地方機關。利害關係人關係是讓人類實踐成為真實而非表演的關鍵，也是競賽團隊在九個月內建立不起來的東西。","**持續追蹤趨勢。** 這份報告每年至少重新生成兩次；學術與產業頁就是為了可重跑而設計的。"],"outcome":"GEMS Research is cited, invited and asked for help by people who were never GEMS students.","outcome_zh":"GEMS Research 被從未是 GEMS 學生的人引用、邀請並尋求協助。"}]};
